\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 One of the last US clinics for later abortions closes just as it\u8217\'20\'19s needed most: \u8216\'20\'18There\u8217\'20\'19s a lack of understanding of what people go through\u8217\'20\'19\b0\par\par\uc2 Carter Sherman \par \uc2 1,725 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 June 2025\par 14:00 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Since Colorado clinic that performed abortions past the second trimester is gone, procedure will be harder to obtain\par \par \uc2 One Tuesday morning in April, Alicia Moreno and the rest of the staff at Boulder \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic learned that the clinic\u8217\'20\'19s owner, Dr Warren Hern, was closing the clinic on Friday. One of the few {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  clinics in the US that performed abortions past the second trimester would, after 50 years, shutter its doors.\par \par \uc2 They sprang into action. Suddenly, multiple patients who had been scheduled for abortions had to go somewhere else.\par \par \uc2 Using secure lines, Moreno and other staffers called \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics across the country to see who could take the patients. Because Boulder \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Clinic typically helped patients schedule flights and hotels, they had to reschedule all those logistics \u8211\'20\'13 while ensuring that nothing cost too much, since more than 90% of the clinic\u8217\'20\'19s patients relied on outside funding to help pay for their abortions.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt was hardest on the patients that were already scheduled,\u8221\'20\'1D Moreno said. \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re already in a really shitty circumstance, and we\u8217\'20\'19re just like: \u8216\'20\'18Haha, just kidding. You\u8217\'20\'19re not coming to Colorado now. You\u8217\'20\'19re going to DC in four days.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jun/02/at-least-20-planned-parenthood-clinics-shutter-amid-political-turbulence"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 At least 20 Planned Parenthood clinics shutter amid political turbulence}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 Abortions that take place later on in pregnancy are rare: in 2022, the year the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  overturned Roe v Wade, about 1% took place at or after 21 weeks of pregnancy, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cdc.gov/mmwr/volumes/73/ss/ss7307a1.htm#:~:text=Discussion-,For%202022%2C%20a%20total%20of%20613%2C383%20abortions%20were%20reported%20to,abortions%20per%201%2C000%20live%20births."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to the latest data from the CDC}}}\uc2 . But later abortions may be on the rise. Before Roe fell, about 8% of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  patients living in states that today ban the procedure ended their pregnancies in the second trimester, according to not-yet-published research by a team involving Diana Greene Foster, the principal investigator behind {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2020/jun/20/abortion-denied-debt-bankruptcy-eviction"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the seminal Turnaway Study}}}\uc2 , which followed women denied abortions. After Roe fell, leading more than a dozen states to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , that rose to 17%.\par \par \uc2 While data suggests the post-Roe demand for later abortions is on the rise, the supply has not kept pace. Now that Boulder \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic is gone, later abortions will be even harder to obtain.\par \par \uc2 These procedures can make even people who support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights uneasy. The US \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  wars are always volatile, but later abortions remain a uniquely explosive third rail. While 70% of Americans believe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be legal in the first trimester of pregnancy \u8211\'20\'13 when a fetus tends to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/oct/18/pregnancy-weeks-abortion-tissue"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 resemble a feathery sea creature}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 just {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.gallup.com/poll/506759/broader-support-abortion-rights-continues-post-dobbs.aspx#:~:text=Most%20Americans%20oppose%20abortion%20later,found%20in%20trends%20since%201996."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 22% think it should be legal by the third}}}\uc2 , when a fetus looks much more like a baby.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe way that I conceptualize it is that, yes, if I didn\u8217\'20\'19t intervene, often, this pregnancy would continue,\u8221\'20\'1D said Dr Diane Horvath, medical director of Partners in \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Care, a Maryland clinic that performs abortions up until 34 weeks of pregnancy. Every week, her clinic sees between six and eight patients who are at least 26 weeks along. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a potential life that I am taking part in ending, and I am completely comfortable with that, because the life of the pregnant person and their needs are always more important to me.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Gross lack of understanding\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Only nine states even permit abortions after viability, the benchmark at which a fetus can survive outside the womb and which typically occurs around 24 weeks of pregnancy. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://laterabortion.org/sites/default/files/documents/lai_referrals_sheet_4.21.2025.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Just 17 clinics}}}\uc2  in the US provide abortions after that point. Only three routinely do abortions past 28 weeks; others do so on a case-by-case basis.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.kff.org/womens-health-policy/issue-brief/abortions-later-in-pregnancy-in-a-post-dobbs-era/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 little research that exists}}}\uc2  on people who get later abortions has found it tends to happen to people who have discovered some late-breaking news \u8211\'20\'13 such as receiving a diagnosis about a fetal anomaly, many of which cannot be confirmed until later in pregnancy, or realizing that they are pregnant later than normal. Young people and individuals who used contraception when they had sex are especially likely to miss early signs of pregnancy, Greene Foster said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s a really gross lack of understanding of what people go through and why they might make this decision to terminate a pregnancy later in pregnancy,\u8221\'20\'1D said Dr Jennefer Russo, executive director of DuPont Clinic LA, a Washington DC-based \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic that offers the procedure until 32 weeks of pregnancy. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve had patients whose partners have died during their pregnancy. There\u8217\'20\'19s lots of different decisions that people could make in response to that event. But even just at the basic level of finances, if you don\u8217\'20\'19t have the financial and emotional support of a partner, in this world being a single parent is really difficult.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s little room, however, for this kind of complexity in US politics. In the months leading up to the 2024 election, campaigners behind ballot measures to codify \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.motherjones.com/politics/2023/09/roe-v-wade-abortion-rights-amendment-missouri-pro-choice-ohio-arizona-planned-parenthood-viability-limits/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 drew the line at viability}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 and most of these measures {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/nov/05/abortion-ballot-results-tracker-ban-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 passed}}}\uc2 . Meanwhile, Democrats rushed to capitalize on voters\u8217\'20\'19 outrage over Roe\u8217\'20\'19s downfall \u8211\'20\'13 but still acted like later abortions don\u8217\'20\'19t happen. When Donald Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abcnews.go.com/Politics/harris-trump-presidential-debate-transcript/story?id=113560542"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 insinuated in a debate}}}\uc2  that \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  supported abortions in \u8220\'20\'1Cthe seventh month, the eighth month, the ninth month\u8221\'20\'1D of pregnancy, Harris fired back: \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s not true.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 On the other side of the political spectrum, Republicans have taken to equating later \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  with infanticide. \u8220\'20\'1CPresident Trump has told me that he wants to end late-term abortions,\u8221\'20\'1D Robert F Kennedy Jr, secretary of the \uc2 Department of Health and Human Services\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XiVkDC7gWic"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told senators during his confirmation hearings}}}\uc2  earlier this year. \u8220\'20\'1CI serve at the pleasure of the president. I\u8217\'20\'19m gonna implement his policies.\u8221\'20\'1D (\u8220\'20\'1CLate-term \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D is a medically inaccurate phrase, as \u8220\'20\'1Clate term\u8221\'20\'1D refers to pregnancies that continue past their due date.)\par \par \uc2 Horvath believes that more doctors and clinicians are now willing to perform later abortions; indeed, the overturning of Roe led to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/apr/09/doctors-mexico-abortion-training"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 surge in demand}}}\uc2  for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/13/abortion-access-healthcare-workers-democratic-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  training}}}\uc2 . However, advocates say it is too difficult to get later-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics off the ground. <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jun/03/trump-admin-emergency-abortion-emtala"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump rescinds guidance protecting women in need of emergency abortions}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPeople just don\u8217\'20\'19t have the resources to do it. We had to start a \uc2 GoFundMe\uc2  to begin this clinic. We solicited grants. We put in our own money to do this,\u8221\'20\'1D Horvath said.\par \par \uc2 Back in 2022, DuPont Clinic announced plans to open up another clinic in Beverly Hills, California. The wealthy city is deep-blue, but the announcement was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://calmatters.org/politics/2024/04/abortion-rights-california-beverly-hills-clinic/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 greeted by a ferocious uproar}}}\uc2 . Anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protests erupted, and \uc2 DuPont\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s landlord ultimately cancelled the clinic\u8217\'20\'19s lease.\par \par \uc2 California\u8217\'20\'19s attorney general, Democrat \uc2 Rob Bonta\uc2 , accused Beverly Hills of violating state laws that protect Californians\u8217\'20\'19 right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . A lawsuit filed by Bonta\u8217\'20\'19s office alleged that city officials had improperly delayed \uc2 DuPont\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s building permits as well as launched an \u8220\'20\'1Cintense pressure campaign\u8221\'20\'1D against the clinic\u8217\'20\'19s landlord, such as by claiming that the clinic would be so overwhelmed by violent protests and bomb threats that the city could not protect the public.\par \par \uc2 Beverly Hills settled with Bonta\u8217\'20\'19s office and agreed to train their employees in \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law. However, city officials maintain that they did nothing wrong and did not try to block the clinic from opening.\par \par \uc2 Russo is sympathetic to fears around harassment and violence. In 1988, somebody fired multiple shots into Boulder \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Clinic\u8217\'20\'19s waiting room; in recent years, the front of the clinic was blocked from the street by a thick wall, while staffers protected patients\u8217\'20\'19 privacy by using code words, referring to patients by numbers and placing phones in Faraday bags. In 2009, Dr George Tiller, perhaps the most famous later-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider in the US, was shot to death in his Wichita, Kansas, church by an anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activist.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m worried about violence myself,\u8221\'20\'1D Russo said. But, she added: \u8220\'20\'1CIf we all just decide that the Maga movement is violent, and we say we\u8217\'20\'19re scared of them, and then we don\u8217\'20\'19t stand up for civil rights or the rule of law, then they win.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Behind the scenes in Boulder\par \par \uc2 The events leading up to Boulder \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Clinic\u8217\'20\'19s closure are in dispute. Hern has said that the business had become unsustainable for several reasons, including patients\u8217\'20\'19 inability to afford later abortions.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a difficult situation, and I decided that I didn\u8217\'20\'19t want to continue with this,\u8221\'20\'1D Hern said. \u8220\'20\'1CI have other things that I need to do.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Moreno, the chief operations officer at Boulder \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Clinic, said that plans for Hern to retire had long been in the works, but recently sped up as clinic staffers and physicians grew increasingly concerned about the 86-year-old Hern\u8217\'20\'19s age and his ability to treat patients. Hern\u8217\'20\'19s decision to close the clinic came as a surprise to her.\par \par \uc2 Now, Moreno and other former staffers at Boulder \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Clinic are planning on setting up a new later-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic. There are two main obstacles, she said: they need to find real estateand the Trump administration has made donors skittish.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s a barrier that everybody in this space is up against,\u8221\'20\'1D Moreno said. Given Trump\u8217\'20\'19s animosity to later abortions, \u8220\'20\'1Cthey want to be able to donate their money safely, where they won\u8217\'20\'19t be audited, that their business licenses for their personal businesses won\u8217\'20\'19t be held because of their donations\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Still, Moreno hopes to open up the clinic within 60 to 90 days, as the national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights group the Brigid Alliance is helping fundraise. The need feels too great to wait too long.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe clinics that provide this kind of care were already overloaded,\u8221\'20\'1D Moreno said. Now that Boulder \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Clinic is gone, \u8220\'20\'1Cthey\u8217\'20\'19re absorbing as much as they can\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 This article was amended on 9 June 2025. An earlier version said that a dozen patients had to be rescheduled the week that Boulder \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Clinic closed; instead, patients set to receive abortions after that week had to be rescheduled. An earlier version also misstated Jennefer Russo\u8217\'20\'19s title. She is the executive director of DuPont Clinic LA, not the chief medical director of DuPont Clinic.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250609el69001mj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
