\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Women in West Virginia who miscarry could face criminal charges, prosecutor says\b0\par\par\uc2 Carter Sherman \par \uc2 504 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 June 2025\par 18:51 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Tom Truman of Raleigh county advised women to report their miscarriages to the police to protect themselves\par \par \uc2 Women in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/west-virginia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 West Virginia}}}\uc2  could face criminal charges if they miscarry, a county prosecutor told a local news outlet last week, urging {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/lifeandstyle/women"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 women}}}\uc2  who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/miscarriage"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 miscarry}}}\uc2  to contact law enforcement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe kind of criminal jeopardy you face is going to depend on a lot of factors,\u8221\'20\'1D the Raleigh county prosecuting attorney Tom Truman {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wvnstv.com/news/local-news/prosecutor-warns-of-potential-charges-against-women-who-miscarry-in-west-virginia/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told the outlet WVNS 59News}}}\uc2  in comments reported on Friday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat was your intent? What did you do? How late were you in your pregnancy? Were you trying to hide something, were you just so emotionally distraught you couldn\u8217\'20\'19t do anything else?\u8221\'20\'1D <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2024/jan/24/us-miscarriage-laws-abortion-rights-options"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18I didn\u8217\'20\'19t know what I was supposed to do\u8217\'20\'19: US women who miscarry are in dangerous legal limbo post-Roe}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 He added: \u8220\'20\'1CIf you were relieved, and you had been telling people, \u8216\'20\'18I\u8217\'20\'19d rather get ran over by a bus than have this baby,\u8217\'20\'19 that may play into law enforcement\u8217\'20\'19s thinking, too.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Truman said he was personally opposed to prosecuting women who miscarry, but other law enforcement officials in West Virginia had said they would be willing to do so under laws that dictate the disposal of human remains. Although West Virginia bans virtually all abortions, its ban \u8211\'20\'13 like other \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans in the US \u8211\'20\'13 does not penalize \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  patients but instead people who provide the procedure.\par \par \uc2 To protect themselves, Truman suggested that women call law enforcement after they have a miscarriage.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CCall your doctor. Call law enforcement, or 911, and just say, \u8216\'20\'18I miscarried. I want you to know,\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D Truman said.\par \par \uc2 The wave of state-level \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans that followed the 2022 overturning of Roe v Wade sparked fears among women and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  supporters that people who miscarry could face charges over their handling of fetal remains. As abortions and miscarriages \u8211\'20\'13 which are known in medical parlance as \u8220\'20\'1Cspontaneous abortions\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 can look deeply similar to medical professionals, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans can incentivize police to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2024/jan/24/us-miscarriage-laws-abortion-rights-options"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 treat pregnancy losses like crime scenes}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In 2023, a woman in Ohio was charged with felony abuse of a corpse after she miscarried into a toilet. A grand jury ultimately {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/jan/11/ohio-woman-miscarriage-not-indicted-abuse-corpse-brittany-watts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 decided not to indict}}}\uc2 . Earlier this year, after a Georgia woman suffered a miscarriage and was found bleeding in a parking lot, police charged her with concealing the death of another person and throwing away or abandoning a dead body. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/apr/04/georgia-miscarriage-charges-dropped"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Those charges were dropped}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere is no one-size-fits-all way to handle fetal remains in these situations \u8211\'20\'13 in fact, doctors often tell women to simply miscarry at home,\u8221\'20\'1D Dana Sussman, senior vice-president of the \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive-rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  organization Pregnancy Justice, said in a statement issued after news of the Georgia case broke.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNo one is taught how to handle fetal remains, and police and prosecutors should not be weighing in on how women in this situation respond.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250605el650038s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
