\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 White House boasts family of suspect in Boulder attack \u8216\'20\'18could be deported as early as tonight\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Robert Mackey (now); Lucy Campbell, L\u233\'00\'E9onie Chao-Fong and Tom Ambrose (earlier) \par \uc2 12,149 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 June 2025\par 02:20 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This liveblog is now closed\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 <a href="{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jun/03/boulder-colorado-attack-suspect-family-detention">Family"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jun/03/boulder-colorado-attack-suspect-family-detention">Family}}}\uc2  of suspect in Colorado fire attack taken into custody of US immigration</a>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-06-04T01:55:27.159Z">2.55am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 This ends our live coverage of the second Trump administration for the day, but we will be back at it on Wednesday. In the meantime, here are some of the day\u8217\'20\'19s developments:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  , who played a leading role in the Trump administration until last week, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2025/jun/03/boulder-colorado-flamethrower-attack-police-fbi-us-politics-live?page=with%3Ablock-683f36de8f085b7ae48dadde#block-683f36de8f085b7ae48dadde"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 denounced}}}\uc2  the massive spending and tax bill the president wants to sign as \u8220\'20\'1Ca disgusting abomination\u8221\'20\'1D. \u8220\'20\'1CShame on those who voted for it: you know you did wrong\u8221\'20\'1D, he added. One Republican who did vote for it, Scott Perry, quickly piped up to say that he agreed with Musk, even though his single vote could have stopped it from passing the House.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The White House {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2025/jun/03/boulder-colorado-flamethrower-attack-police-fbi-us-politics-live?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with%3Ablock-683f682f8f08ac24e654899f#block-683f682f8f08ac24e654899f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 gloated}}}\uc2  on social media about {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jun/03/boulder-colorado-attack-suspect-family-detention"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the arrests}}}\uc2  of the wife and five children of Mohamed Sabry Soliman , the suspected Boulder attacker, and joked about providing them with \u8220\'20\'1Csix one-way tickets\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 In the 48 hours since the firebomb attack in Boulder, Colorado, on a demonstration in support of Israelis held hostage in Gaza, Republicans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2025/jun/03/boulder-colorado-flamethrower-attack-police-fbi-us-politics-live?page=with%3Ablock-683f88d58f083ea789b91f04#block-683f88d58f083ea789b91f04"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 politicized the attack}}}\uc2 , attempting to blame Democrats, including the state\u8217\'20\'19s multiple Jewish leaders.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Democrats denounced the Trump administration\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Ccruel\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jun/03/trump-admin-emergency-abortion-emtala"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 decision}}}\uc2  to rescind {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.hhs.gov/sites/default/files/emergency-medical-care-letter-to-health-care-providers.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 health department guidance}}}\uc2  issued in the wake of the 2022 Dobbs decision, striking down the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , that required hospitals to provide abortions to women in medical emergencies even in state\u8217\'20\'19s with local bans on the procedure.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-06-04T02:01:21.766Z">at 3.01am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-06-04T01:55:14.545Z">2.55am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Law professor suggests spike in court orders against Trump might be because he is more 'lawless' than other presidents\par \par \uc2 At a Senate hearing on Tuesday, Senator \uc2 Josh Hawley\uc2 , a Missouri Republican, pressed Kate Shaw, a law professor and host of the liberal podcast Strict Scrutiny, to explain why so many more injunctions were issued against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  than against other presidents.\par \par \uc2 As Hawley had a chart displayed showing the comparison, and asked: \u8220\'20\'1CYou don\u8217\'20\'19t think this is a little bit anomalous?\u8221\'20\'1D Shaw {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://youtu.be/Py0q1uHkXi8?si=kCz5iJQ0Xy-A3fAp&t=237"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 replied}}}\uc2 : \u8220\'20\'1CA very plausible explanation, Senator, you have to consider, is that he is engaged in much more lawless activity than other presidents.\u8221\'20\'1D <figure class="element element-video" data-canonical-url="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Py0q1uHkXi8" > <figcaption>Senator \uc2 Josh Hawley\uc2 , a Missouri Republican, pressed Kate Shaw, a law professor, at a hearing on Tuesday.</figcaption> </figure>\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-06-04T02:00:39.659Z">at 3.00am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-06-04T01:31:16.314Z">2.31am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Democrats condemn 'cruel, dangerous' order to revoke emergency \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care\par \par \uc2 Democrats responded with anger to the Trump administration\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jun/03/trump-admin-emergency-abortion-emtala"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 decision}}}\uc2  on Tuesday to rescind {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.hhs.gov/sites/default/files/emergency-medical-care-letter-to-health-care-providers.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 health department guidance}}}\uc2  issued in the wake of the 2022 Dobbs decision, striking down the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , that required hospitals to provide abortions to women in medical emergencies even in state\u8217\'20\'19s with local bans on the procedure.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTrump\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 HHS\uc2  is erasing guidance that affirmed protections for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care during medical emergencies,\u8221\'20\'1D the Representative \uc2 Ayanna Pressley{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://bsky.app/profile/pressley.house.gov/post/3lqqct726ps2e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote on Bluesky}}}\uc2 . This is cruel, callous, and outright dangerous.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTrump just quietly erased guidance that told hospitals they had to save pregnant women\u8217\'20\'19s lives,\u8221\'20\'1D the Washington Senator \uc2 Patty Murray{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/PattyMurray/status/1930003212368785674"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 posted}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s right\u8212\'20\'14they don\u8217\'20\'19t care how many women die or are forced into health crises to advance their anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  agenda. I won\u8217\'20\'19t let this fly under the radar.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is cruel, dangerous, and puts lives at risk,\u8221\'20\'1D the Arizona Senator \uc2 Ruben Gallego{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/RubenGallego/status/1930065466925408688"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CRevoking emergency \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections means women in medical crisis could be told \u8216\'20\'18no\u8217\'20\'19 at the ER \u8212\'20\'14 just because they\u8217\'20\'19re pregnant.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Michigan\u8217\'20\'19s governor, \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2  , also called the policy cruel. \u8220\'20\'1CTaking away emergency \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care puts lives on the line and hands power to politicians, instead of medical professionals and patients,\u8221\'20\'1D she posted. \u8220\'20\'1CIn Michigan, we trust women. We trust doctors. And we\u8217\'20\'19ll never stop fighting to protect your health care.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-06-04T01:52:41.330Z">at 2.52am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-06-04T01:01:33.179Z">2.01am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Republicans blame Democrats for Boulder attack\par \par \uc2 In the 48 hours since the firebomb attack in Boulder, Colorado, on a demonstration in support of Israelis held hostage in Gaza, and the arrest of an Egyptian asylum seeker charged with hate crimes and attempted murder for wounding 12 people, Republicans have politicized the attack, attempting to blame Democrats for the attempted murders.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://truthsocial.com/@realDonaldTrump/posts/114614695646992423"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 claimed}}}\uc2  that the suspect, who arrived on a tourist visa in 2022 and asked for asylum six months later, \u8220\'20\'1Ccame in through Biden\u8217\'20\'19s ridiculous Open Border Policy\u8221\'20\'1D. The attack, Trump claimed, was \u8220\'20\'1Cyet another example of why we must keep our Borders SECURE, and deport Illegal, Anti-American Radicals\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Republicans in Congress even tried to use the attack as an argument to pass their massive spending and tax cut bill, which takes health insurance away from millions and cuts taxes for the rich, but also increases spending on deportations. \u8220\'20\'1CThis attack was preventable, but Democrats & Biden closed their eyes & created a national security nightmare\u8221\'20\'1D House Republicans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/HouseGOP/status/1929593196998185409"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 posted}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CIt doesn\u8217\'20\'19t have to be this way & House Republicans passed a solution: the One Big Beautiful Bill Act.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 As the 9News Denver anchor Kyle Clark {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://youtu.be/F2mNot1im4Q?si=RWihTxWU2JxOpQvA"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 observed}}}\uc2 , \u8220\'20\'1CColorado\u8217\'20\'19s elected leaders are responding to the terror attack in Boulder, with leading Democrats condemning antisemitic hate and violence and leading Republicans condemning Democrats.\u8221\'20\'1D <figure class="element element-video" data-canonical-url="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=F2mNot1im4Q" > <figcaption>A report from 9News Denver anchor Kyle Clark on Colorado Republicans blaming Democrats for the Boulder attack.</figcaption> </figure>\par \par \uc2 Colorado\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic governor, \uc2 Jared Polis\uc2  , who is Jewish, said: \u8220\'20\'1Can attack on any of us is an attack on all of us, it goes for Jews, Christians, Muslims, people of no faith at all; there\u8217\'20\'19s just no room in our state for these acts of terror\u8221\'20\'1D. The state\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic attorney general, \uc2 Phil Weiser\uc2  , condemned what he called a painful, \u8220\'20\'1Cantisemitic attack on fellow Jews\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Democratic Senator Michael Bennet , whose mother was born to a secular Jewish family in Poland in 1938 and smuggled out of the Warsaw ghetto, said he was horrified by \u8220\'20\'1Cthe terror attack in Boulder\u8211\'20\'13 targeting Jews peacefully marching\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Colorado\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic secretary of state, \uc2 Jena Griswold\uc2  , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://bsky.app/profile/jenagriswold.bsky.social/post/3lqlafznu6c27"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 posted on Bluesky}}}\uc2 : \u8220\'20\'1CMy heart goes out to those who were injured in the senseless and despicable attack that took place in Boulder. Violence is never the answer. Antisemitism has no place here.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Even so, two Colorado Republicans in Congress, \uc2 Lauren Boebert\uc2  and Gabe Evans , insisted Democrats were to blame.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen progressives allow and encourage hate speech toward Jews for their mere existence, people get hurt,\u8221\'20\'1D Boebert {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/RepBoebert/status/1929342607441969578"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 posted}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In a dozen posts, Evans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/GabeforColorado/status/1929357986935210477"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 repeatedly claimed}}}\uc2  that the attack was \u8220\'20\'1Ca direct result of failed sanctuary states like Colorado\u8221\'20\'1D, even though the state\u8217\'20\'19s unwillingness to cooperate with federal immigration officers had nothing to do with the suspected attacker, who had reportedly applied for asylum and so was legally allowed to remain in the US until that claim was adjudicated.\par \par \uc2 But the most inflammatory response came from Danielle Jurinsky , a conservative Aurora city council member, who called the Democratic party \u8220\'20\'1Ca demonic cult\u8221\'20\'1D, and attacked fellow Jews Polis, Bennet, Griswold and Weiser. \u8220\'20\'1CShame on every single one of you, who have made the Democratic party your religion. Shame on you! You\u8217\'20\'19re not Jewish, you\u8217\'20\'19re a Democrat!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 By contrast, the organizers of the movement for Israeli hostages, Run for Their Lives, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.instagram.com/p/DKYYLiXNSIw/?img_index=1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 thanked Weiser and Polis}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cfor their immediate and decisive responses\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Run for Their Lives is non-partisan but at least one its leaders, Shira Weiss, is a committed Democrat. Her \uc2 Facebook\uc2  page mixes posts about the plight of the Israeli hostages with denunciations of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CThank g-d no one in MY immediate family voted for this imbecile,\u8221\'20\'1D she wrote in April.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-06-04T02:20:30.399Z">at 3.20am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-06-03T23:14:09.098Z">12.14am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 During Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s Republican-led Senate judiciary subcommittee hearing, District Judges v Trump, there was an unusual degree of agreement among the senators and their panel of witnesses that nationwide injunctions have become problematic. They agreed that the sweeping rulings have been abused by both Republican and Democratic administrations, and that single judge divisions, which allow plaintiffs to guarantee their case will be heard by a particular judge they believe could be favorable to their case, known as forum shopping, are an \u8220\'20\'1Cenormous problem\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBoth sides,\u8221\'20\'1D Senator \uc2 John Kennedy\uc2 , a Louisiana Republican, declared loudly during the hearing. \u8220\'20\'1CThere are no clean hands here.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But there was also plenty of political posturing and goal-scoring. Several Republican senators spent their time assailing the Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 guest, law professor Kate Shaw , who hosts the podcast {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.crooked.com/podcast-series/strict-scrutiny/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Strict Scrutiny}}}\uc2 , part of the liberal Crooked Media empire.\par \par \uc2 On concerns over the rising threats to judges, Republicans sought to point the finger at Democrats, ignoring entirely Trump\u8217\'20\'19s attacks on the judiciary. At the end, Senator Adam Schiff , Democrat of California, highlighted some of the names Trump has used against the judges who have ruled against him: \u8220\'20\'1Ccommunist\u8221\'20\'1D, \u8220\'20\'1Clunatic\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cmonster\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In response, Cruz read aloud tweets posted by a liberal online commentator after the extraordinary supreme court leak that previewed the justices decision to overturn Roe v Wade. Declaring the left\u8217\'20\'19s rhetoric \u8220\'20\'1Cangry\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cunhinged\u8221\'20\'1D, he adjourned the hearing.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-06-04T00:23:30.341Z">at 1.23am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-06-03T23:10:19.879Z">12.10am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, Senator Ted Cruz , a Texas Republican, convened {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/live/chbQjFEG3ss?si=tQkUTLiwGuWjD7L5&t=608"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a hearing}}}\uc2  on a legal matter that has troubled judges and lawmakers of both parties: nationwide injunctions.\par \par \uc2 Cruz said the use of nationwide injunctions by a single judge to block large swaths of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s agenda from taking effect across the country amounted to \u8220\'20\'1Cjudicial tyranny\u8221\'20\'1D. But Democrats decried the hearing \u8211\'20\'13 titled {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.judiciary.senate.gov/hearings/the-supposedly-least-dangerous-branch-district-judges-v-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Supposedly \u8216\'20\'18Least Dangerous Branch\u8217\'20\'19: District Judges vs. Trump}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 as a political stunt designed to intimidate judges who rule against the president.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese district judges, they were not elected,\u8221\'20\'1D Cruz said. \u8220\'20\'1CThey were appointed by one individual and confirmed, not to legislate, not to govern, but to apply the law. And yet, far too many of them have abandoned that role. They stepped off the bench and into the political arena issuing sweeping edicts that impose their policy preferences on 340 million Americans.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He counted 40 universal injunctions issued against Trump in his second term so far, noting that it was \u8220\'20\'1Cmore than all of the nationwide injunctions issued against [presidents] Bush, \uc2 Obama\uc2  and Biden combined.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Senator Sheldon Whitehouse , a Rhode Island Democrat, said the rise in their use did not reflect judicial overreach but the necessary response to \u8220\'20\'1Cunprecedented lawlessness\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMany are flat out, on their face illegal as any first year law student could tell you,\u8221\'20\'1D Whitehouse said, pointing to several of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s executive orders that have triggered judges to issue nationwide injunctions, including his attempt to end birthright citizenship, a right enshrined in the 14th amendment of the US constitution.\par \par \uc2 Trump is \u8220\'20\'1Cbreaking the law and doing it a lot,\u8221\'20\'1D Whitehouse said. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd judges are doing their job.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-06-03T23:12:48.729Z">at 12.12am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-06-03T22:50:13.945Z">11.50pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 '\uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  is right' to criticize spending bill says House Republican who voted for spending bill\par \par \uc2 Representative Scott Perry , a Pennsylvania Republican and member of the far-right House Freedom caucus, just seconded \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s criticism of the massive spending bill that passed the House by a single vote as \u8220\'20\'1Ca disgusting abomination\u8221\'20\'1D and added that the billionaire Republican donor \u8220\'20\'1Cis right to call out House Leadership\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Perry, who voted for the bill last month, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/RepScottPerry/status/1930021722343751931"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shared Musk\u8217\'20\'19s post}}}\uc2  with that criticism on the billionaire\u8217\'20\'19s social media platform X along with a comment that he and his colleagues \u8220\'20\'1Cwere right all along\u8221\'20\'1D to object to the spending bill \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is eager to sign into law. Projections from non-partisan experts {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://budgetmodel.wharton.upenn.edu/issues/2025/5/23/house-reconciliation-bill-budget-economic-and-distributional-effects-may-22-2025"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 suggest}}}\uc2  that the spending bill, which includes massive tax cuts for the rich and could deprive 14 million people of health insurance, could add over $3tn to the federal debt in 10 years.\par \par \uc2 Aaron Fritschner , an aide to Representative \uc2 Don Beyer\uc2  , a Virginia Democrat, replied to the comment from Perry by pointing out that he could have defeated the bill himself by simply voting no. The House vote in favor of the bill, thanks to Perry\u8217\'20\'19s vote, was 215-214.\par \par \uc2 Perry reportedly played a key role in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s plot to subvert the result of the 2020 presidential election he lost to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://penncapital-star.com/campaigns-elections/unsealed-court-filing-shows-u-s-rep-scott-perry-contacted-pa-lawmakers-before-jan-6-attack/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 records obtained by special counsel }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://penncapital-star.com/campaigns-elections/unsealed-court-filing-shows-u-s-rep-scott-perry-contacted-pa-lawmakers-before-jan-6-attack/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jack Smith}}}\uc2  , and the testimony of former White House aide Cassidy Hutchinson.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-06-03T23:03:26.275Z">at 12.03am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-06-03T21:55:25.726Z">10.55pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 White House boasts family of suspect in Boulder attack 'could be deported as early as tonight'\par \par \uc2 The White House is boasting on its official social media accounts about {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jun/03/boulder-colorado-attack-suspect-family-detention"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the arrests}}}\uc2  of the wife and five children of Mohamed Sabry Soliman, the suspected Boulder attacker, who were taken into custody on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Soliman\u8217\'20\'19s six family members, \u8220\'20\'1Chave been captured and are now in ICE custody for expedited removal\u8221\'20\'1D, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.instagram.com/p/DKc79euxq3H/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a White House post}}}\uc2  says. It adds, in all caps: \u8220\'20\'1CTHEY COULD BE DEPORTED AS EARLY AS TONIGHT.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Thirty minutes later, the White House {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/WhiteHouse/status/1930002225860133080"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 added}}}\uc2 , in the gleeful, mocking tone that has distinguished posts gloating over deportations of even immigrants sent to foreign jails by mistake: \u8220\'20\'1CSix One-Way Tickets for Mohamed\u8217\'20\'19s Wife and Five Kids. Final Boarding Call Coming Soon.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 That timeline would appear to conflict with both court orders that people threatened with deportation should be given sufficient time to challenge their removals, and a statement from the homeland security secretary \uc2 Kristi Noem\uc2 , earlier on Tuesday, that authorities \u8220\'20\'1Care investigating to what extent his family knew about this horrific attack, if they had knowledge of it, or if they provided support to it\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 According to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.coloradojudicial.gov/sites/default/files/2025-06/2505040%20Arrest%20Warrant%20Signed_Redacted_Redacted.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a state arrest affidavit}}}\uc2 , Soliman told the Boulder police \u8220\'20\'1Cno one knew about his plans and he never talked to his wife or family about it\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 For its post on \uc2 Instagram\uc2 , the White House cropped an image of Soliman taken during the attack to include a rainbow Progress Pride Flag on the Boulder courthouse behind him.\par \par \uc2 Stephen Redfearn, the Boulder police chief, said on Tuesday that all of the victims of the firebomb attack are expected to survive, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dailycamera.com/2025/06/03/boulder-colorado-pearl-street-mall-attack-victims-survive/?utm_medium=social&utm_campaign=SocialFlowFeed&utm_source=twitter.com&utm_content=tw-dailycamera"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Denver Post reports}}}\uc2 . Three of the 12 victims are being treated at UCHealth\u8217\'20\'19s burn and frostbite center at the \uc2 University of Colorado\uc2  in Aurora.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-06-04T00:21:28.065Z">at 1.21am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-06-03T21:00:31.276Z">10.00pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Brazil's president resists Trump's threats to his supreme court\par \par \uc2 Brazil\u8217\'20\'19s president, Luiz In \u225\'00\'E1cio \uc2 Lula da Silva\uc2  , known as Lula, vowed on Tuesday to defend his country\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court against attacks from the United States, in a sharp rebuke of potential sanctions from Washington against one of the top court\u8217\'20\'19s justices.\par \par \uc2 US secretary of state \uc2 Marco Rubio{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www1.folha.uol.com.br/internacional/en/world/2025/05/brazilian-supreme-court-justice-could-face-us-visa-restrictions-for-censoring-americans.shtml"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told Congress}}}\uc2  last week that the Trump administration could impose economic sanctions on the judge overseeing the trial of Brazil\u8217\'20\'19s former president, \uc2 Jair Bolsonaro\uc2 , a Trump ally accused of plotting a January 6-style attack by his supporters on government buildings in Bras\u237\'00\'EDlia in 2023, to demand that the presidential election he lost be overturned.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is unacceptable for the president of any country in the world to comment on the decision of the supreme court of another country,\u8221\'20\'1D Lula {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/KriskaCarvalho/status/1929911341151584356"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told reporters}}}\uc2 , adding that the United States needs to understand the importance of \u8220\'20\'1Crespecting the integrity of institutions in other countries\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The Brazilian supreme court justice \uc2 Alexandre de Moraes\uc2  is under fire from the far-right in Brazil and the US as he leads the court\u8217\'20\'19s crackdown on what he has called threats to Brazil\u8217\'20\'19s democracy, both online and in an alleged coup plot.\par \par \uc2 His orders to social media companies to remove posts from Bolsonaro supporters that he considered threats to democratic institutions were called censorship by \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 , the owner of X, formerly known as \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , and \uc2 Rumble\uc2 , a right-wing alternative to \uc2 YouTube\uc2  backed by \uc2 Peter Thiel\uc2  and JD Vance .\par \par \uc2 The judge suspended Musk\u8217\'20\'19s social media platform in Brazil until it acquiesced to his orders.\par \par \uc2 Tensions have spiked between the two nations since Trump took office, according to reports in the Brazilian press. Last month, the country\u8217\'20\'19s leading newspaper, Folha de S.Paulo, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www1.folha.uol.com.br/internacional/en/world/2025/05/brazil-opposes-us-push-to-designate-criminal-factions-pcc-and-cv-as-terrorists.shtml"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  that a Trump administration diplomat, David Gamble, was rebuffed when he asked, during a visit to Brazil, for the Brazilian gangs PCC (Primeiro Comando da Capital) and CV (Comando Vermelho) to be designated terrorist organizations.\par \par \uc2 Two weeks later, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www1.folha.uol.com.br/internacional/en/world/2025/06/us-military-chiefs-visit-to-brazil-strained-by-tensions-and-poorly-attended-dinner.shtml"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to Folha}}}\uc2 , a visit to Bras\u237\'00\'EDlia by the head of the US Southern Command, Admiral Alvin Holsey, \u8220\'20\'1Ccaused discomfort among Brazilian military officials\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Ca dinner he hosted that ended up sparsely attended after key invitees failed to show\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The tension in that case was over the American\u8217\'20\'19s announcement that he planned to visit a military base along the border with Peru and Bolivia, to highlight illegal trafficking, without getting permission from Brazil\u8217\'20\'19s military.\par \par \uc2 The visit to the border was ultimately cancelled and Brazil\u8217\'20\'19s defense minister and the leaders of its army, navy and air force did not attend the dinner hosted by the visiting US admiral.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-06-03T21:26:33.067Z">at 10.26pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-06-03T20:23:37.327Z">9.23pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  would have voted against spending bill if she had read it, she says\par \par \uc2 Republican firebrand \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  has drawn widespread criticism from Democratic colleagues for admitting that not only did she not read \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s tax and spending bill before voting for it, but she would have voted against it had she read thoroughly.\par \par \uc2 Greene revealed she was unaware of a provision in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cone big beautiful bill\u8221\'20\'1D (OBBB) that would prevent states from regulating artificial intelligence systems for a decade. The Georgia representative said she would have voted against the entire bill if she had known about the AI language buried on pages 278-279.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFull transparency, I did not know about this section on pages 278-279 of the OBBB that strips states of the right to make laws or regulate AI for 10 years,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/RepMTG/status/1929946902566494653"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Greene wrote}}}\uc2  on X. \u8220\'20\'1CI am adamantly OPPOSED to this and it is a violation of state rights and I would have voted NO if I had known this was in there.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Democratic lawmakers, who all voted against the bill, responded with incredulity of Greene\u8217\'20\'19s admission.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou have one job. To. Read. The. Fucking. Bill,\u8221\'20\'1D Representative \uc2 Eric Swalwell\uc2  wrote in response.\par \par \uc2 Representative \uc2 Ted Lieu\uc2  said he had read the AI provision beforehand and \u8220\'20\'1Cthat\u8217\'20\'19s one reason I voted no on the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s big, ugly bill\u8221\'20\'1D, he posted on X. \u8220\'20\'1CPRO TIP: It\u8217\'20\'19s helpful to read stuff before voting on it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Representative \uc2 Mark Pocan\uc2  was more forward: \u8220\'20\'1CRead the f**king bill instead of clapping for it like a performing monkey. You should have done your job while it was written. You didn\u8217\'20\'19t. You own that vote.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Read more: <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jun/03/marjorie-taylor-greene-trump-tax-bill"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene criticized for not reading Trump\u8217\'20\'19s \u8216\'20\'18big beautiful\u8217\'20\'19 bill}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-06-03T20:02:11.406Z">9.02pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jun/03/elon-musk-trump-tax-bill-disgusting-abomination"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 online outburst}}}\uc2  could embolden fiscally conservative Republican senators \u8211\'20\'13 some of whom have already spoken out \u8211\'20\'13 to defy Trump as they continue crucial negotiations on Capitol Hill over the so-called \u8220\'20\'1Cbig, beautiful bill\u8221\'20\'1D, my colleague David Smith {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jun/03/elon-musk-trump-tax-bill-disgusting-abomination"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Musk drew immediate support from \uc2 Thomas Massie\uc2  , one of only two Republicans who last month voted against the bill in the House of Representatives. \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s right,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/RepThomasMassie/status/1929955746885624290"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Massie responded on X}}}\uc2  today.\par \par \uc2 Having narrowly passed the House, the bill is now under consideration in the Senate, which is aiming to pass a revised version by 4 July. Some Republican fiscal conservatives, such as senators Ron Johnson and \uc2 Rand Paul\uc2  , share Musk\u8217\'20\'19s concerns about the need for significant spending cuts.\par \par \uc2 Trump, who has been pressuring Republicans to pass his signature legislation to enact his domestic agenda, attacked Paul on Truth Social earlier today, writing: \u8220\'20\'1CRand Paul has very little understanding of the BBB, especially the tremendous GROWTH that is coming. He loves voting \u8220\'20\'1CNO\u8221\'20\'1D on everything, he thinks it\u8217\'20\'19s good politics, but it\u8217\'20\'19s not. The BBB is a big WINNER!!!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He then posted again: \u8220\'20\'1CRand votes NO on everything, but never has any practical or constructive ideas. His ideas are actually crazy (losers!). The people of Kentucky can\u8217\'20\'19t stand him. This is a BIG GROWTH BILL!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-06-03T19:54:53.605Z">8.54pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 House speaker Mike Johnson calls Musk \u8216\'20\'18terribly wrong\u8217\'20\'19 for slamming megabill\par \par \uc2 Politico {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/live-updates/2025/06/03/congress/mike-johnson-elon-musk-terribly-wrong-00382814"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2  that House speaker Mike Johnson said \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  is \u8220\'20\'1Cterribly wrong\u8221\'20\'1D after the tech billionaire \u8211\'20\'13 and, until last week, top Trump adviser - {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2025/jun/03/boulder-colorado-flamethrower-attack-police-fbi-us-politics-live?CMP=share_btn_url&page=with%3Ablock-683f36de8f085b7ae48dadde#block-683f36de8f085b7ae48dadde"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 blasted Trump\u8217\'20\'19s megabill}}}\uc2  as a \u8220\'20\'1Cdisgusting abomination\u8221\'20\'1D that will expand the \u8220\'20\'1Calready gigantic\u8221\'20\'1D budget deficit.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWith all due respect, my friend Elon is terribly wrong about the one big, beautiful bill,\u8221\'20\'1D Johnson told reporters.\par \par \uc2 Johnson said he spoke over the phone with Musk for what he described as a friendly conversation of more than 20 minutes yesterday about the \u8220\'20\'1Cvirtues\u8221\'20\'1D of the bill. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd he seemed to understand that,\u8221\'20\'1D Johnson said.\par \par \uc2 Johnson added that he discussed with Musk the accelerated repeal of many green energy tax credits in the House version of the bill, which Musk also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/policy/energy-environment/5323536-musk-trump-gop-budget-bill-biden-green-energy-tax-credits/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 voiced opposition to last week}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBut for him to come out and pan the whole bill, to me, is just very disappointing, very surprising in light of the conversation I had with him yesterday,\u8221\'20\'1D Johnson said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s not personal,\u8221\'20\'1D the speaker added. \u8220\'20\'1CI just deeply regret that he\u8217\'20\'19s made this mistake.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 House majority leader \uc2 John Thune\uc2 , according to Politico, simply said GOP senators \u8220\'20\'1Chave a difference of opinion\u8221\'20\'1D with Musk and that he hoped \u8220\'20\'1Che\u8217\'20\'19ll come to a different conclusion\u8221\'20\'1D after learning more about the bill.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-06-03T19:57:25.125Z">at 8.57pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-06-03T19:33:36.507Z">8.33pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Family of Colorado fire-bomb suspect taken into Ice custody\par \par \uc2 The family of the Egyptian national charged with attacking people with a makeshift flamethrower and other incendiary devices at an event for Israeli hostages in Boulder, Colorado, was taken into federal custody today, officials said.\par \par \uc2 The Homeland security secretary \uc2 Kristi Noem\uc2  said in a social media video post that Ice had taken into custody the family of Mohamed Sabry Soliman , who lived in Colorado Springs and who federal officials have said was in the US illegally, having overstayed a tourist visa and an expired work permit \u8211\'20\'13 though he had a pending asylum claim.\par \par \uc2 Noem said while Soliman will be prosecuted to the fullest extent of the law, federal agents were also \u8220\'20\'1Cinvestigating to what extent his family knew about this horrific attack \u8211\'20\'13 if they had any knowledge of it or if they provided any support for it\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Ice did not immediately respond to a Reuters request for more details about the detention of Soliman\u8217\'20\'19s family.\par \par \uc2 According to local media reports, Soliman\u8217\'20\'19s family included two teenagers and three younger children. \uc2 FBI\uc2  and police officials had said on Monday that the family has cooperated with investigators. The suspect told investigators he acted alone.\par \par \uc2 DHS officials said Soliman entered the US in August 2022 on a tourist visa, filed for asylum the following month, and remained in the country after his visa expired in February 2023.\par \par \uc2 A police affidavit filed in support of Soliman\u8217\'20\'19s arrest warrant said he was born in Egypt, lived in Kuwait for 17 years and moved three years ago to Colorado Springs, about 100 miles south of Boulder, where he lived with his wife and five children.\par \par \uc2 Federal and local authorities said at a news conference in Boulder yesterday that Soliman had done nothing to draw law enforcement attention before Sunday\u8217\'20\'19s attack. He was believed to have acted alone, they said.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-06-03T19:40:49.823Z">at 8.40pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-06-03T19:27:37.166Z">8.27pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 US announces visa restrictions for several central American government officials\par \par \uc2 Marco Rubio\uc2 , the secretary of state, has announced visa restrictions for several unnamed Central American government officials and their families for allegedly exploiting Cuban medical professionals, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 Rubio, who did not name the officials or the countries they are from, said the officials are responsible for Cuban medical mission programs that include elements of forced labor and the exploitation of Cuban workers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese steps promote accountability for those who support and perpetuate these exploitative practices,\u8221\'20\'1D he said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-06-03T19:42:56.447Z">at 8.42pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-06-03T19:22:30.330Z">8.22pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAttacks on the judiciary itself are dangerous to the rule of law and to the actual judges themselves,\u8221\'20\'1D says Dick Durbin , citing a spike in violence and threats against judges and their families in light of the president\u8217\'20\'19s rhetoric.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLet us recognise that violence begets violence,\u8221\'20\'1D he says. \u8220\'20\'1CThreats of violence \u8230\'20\'26 are never acceptable.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPeople are welcome to debate the merits of any particular judicial decision but we cannot condone personal attacks and threats against judges who rule against this administration, and we can\u8217\'20\'19t allow partisan politics or the latest outrage from the president to undermine the judicial branch and our constitutional order.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-06-03T19:26:08.700Z">at 8.26pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-06-03T19:21:06.745Z">8.21pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Durbin cites language used by Trump and his allies to attack the \u8220\'20\'1Cauthority and legitimacy\u8221\'20\'1D of the judiciary and to intimidate judges, including demanding impeachment {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/mar/20/white-house-impeachment-judge-james-boasberg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 of a judge who ruled against him}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 It is difficult to imagine either President Bush, President \uc2 Obama\uc2  or President Biden using such unhinged, bombastic and childish language, or calling for the impeachment of a judge simply for ruling against his administration.\par \par \uc2 The reason it\u8217\'20\'19s difficult is because \uc2 Obama\uc2  or Biden never did anything like this.\par \par \uc2 Durbin goes on to say that Trump and \u8220\'20\'1Chis allies go after anyone who dares to speak up because fear of political retribution is now at the core of this Maga world, and my Republican colleagues have been silent as the president has made the statements he has about judges\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-06-03T19:14:23.417Z">8.14pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Democratic senator Dick Durbin points out the \u8220\'20\'1Cflood the zone\u8221\'20\'1D context, saying Trump had \u8220\'20\'1Csigned more executive orders than any president in history, leading to more court challenges than any president in history\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSeems pretty logical to me,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-06-03T19:14:44.227Z">at 8.14pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-06-03T19:11:58.911Z">8.11pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 The Republican senator Ted Cruz highlighted that the number of nationwide injunctions during the second Trump administration so far is \u8220\'20\'1Cgreater than the entire 20th century and greater than all of those issued against Bush, \uc2 Obama\uc2  and Biden combined\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 However, among the factors contributing to this high number are the several executive orders signed by Trump and a high number of policies being challenged in court.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-06-03T19:26:21.189Z">at 8.26pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-06-03T18:54:49.379Z">7.54pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Democratic senator Dick Durbin has just posted about the hearing on X:\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his extreme allies keep using unhinged language to threaten judges \u8230\'20\'26 even calling for impeachment. Just imagine if President \uc2 Obama\uc2  had done that. Republicans would\u8217\'20\'19ve thrown a fit.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-06-03T18:56:32.660Z">at 7.56pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-06-03T18:43:28.055Z">7.43pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Senate judiciary committee hearing on judicial branch's oversight of executive authority\par \par \uc2 The senate judiciary subcommittees are holding a joint hearing on the judicial branch\u8217\'20\'19s check on executive power, amid federal judges halting several of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s orders with nationwide injunctions. I\u8217\'20\'19ll bring you any key lines here.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-06-03T18:56:36.271Z">at 7.56pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-06-03T18:26:22.895Z">7.26pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Trump was not informed of Ukraine drone attacks in advance, says White House\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was not informed in advance of Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s drone attacks on Russia , Karoline Leavitt said.\par \par \uc2 On Sunday, Ukraine said it launched 117 drones in an astonishing operation code-named \u8220\'20\'1C{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/jun/02/operation-spiderweb-visual-guide-ukraine-drone-attack-russian-aircraft"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Spider\u8217\'20\'19s Web}}}\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/jun/01/ukraine-launches-major-drone-attack-on-russian-bombers-security-official-says"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 attack Russian nuclear-capable long-range bomber planes}}}\uc2  at airfields in Siberia and the far north of the country.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-06-03T18:24:21.606Z">7.24pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Trump to sign order doubling metals tariffs, White House says\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will sign an executive order today making official his vow to double tariffs on steel and aluminum , Karoline Leavitt told reporters.\par \par \uc2 Last Friday Trump announced that he would increase tariffs on the two metals from 25% to 50%. Yesterday, Us steel and aluminum prices jumped while shares of foreign steelmakers fell.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-06-03T18:22:37.378Z">7.22pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 White House says it is aware of reports of Israelis firing on Palestinian people seeking aid in Gaza\par \par \uc2 The White House said that it is aware of reports of Israeli troops firing on Palestinian people seeking aid near a food distribution site in southern Gaza .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re going to look into reports before we confirm them from this podium or before we take action,\u8221\'20\'1D Karoline Leavitt told reporters.\par \par \uc2 At least 27 people were killed by Israeli fire as they waited for food at a distribution point set up by an Israeli-backed foundation in Gaza, according to health officials in the strip \u8211\'20\'13 the third such incident in three days. Israel admitted on Tuesday for the first time that its forces shot at individuals who were moving towards them. <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/jun/03/palestinians-killed-israeli-fire-aid-point-gaza-officials-say"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 At least 27 Palestinians killed by Israeli fire at food point, Gaza officials say}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-06-03T18:00:35.805Z">7.00pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 'A disgusting abomination': Musk tears into Trump budget bill days after leaving White House\par \par \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  has significantly upped the ante in his criticism of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cbig, beautiful\u8221\'20\'1D tax and spending cut bill, calling it a \u8220\'20\'1Cmassive, outrageous, pork-filled \u8230\'20\'26 disgusting abomination\u8221\'20\'1D that will expand the \u8220\'20\'1Calready gigantic\u8221\'20\'1D budget deficit.\par \par \uc2 The billionaire, who only {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/30/elon-musk-leaving-white-house-doge-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 formally left his top role in the White House}}}\uc2  last week, wrote on his X platform:\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m sorry, but I just can\u8217\'20\'19t stand it anymore. This massive, outrageous, pork-filled Congressional spending bill is a disgusting abomination. Shame on those who voted for it: you know you did wrong. You know it.\par \par \uc2 It will massively increase the already gigantic budget deficit to $2.5 trillion (!!!) and burden America citizens with crushingly unsustainable debt.\par \par \uc2 The broadside comes as Trump pressures Republicans in the Senate to approve the legislation, which narrowly passed in the House of Representatives.\par \par \uc2 Asked about Musk\u8217\'20\'19s criticism, White House press secretary Karoline Leavitt said: \u8220\'20\'1CLook, the president already knows where \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  stood on this bill. It doesn\u8217\'20\'19t change the president\u8217\'20\'19s opinion. This is one big, beautiful bill, and he\u8217\'20\'19s sticking to it,\u8221\'20\'1D she added.\par \par \uc2 Last week, Musk had sharply criticised Trump\u8217\'20\'19s spending plan, saying he was \u8220\'20\'1Cdisappointed\u8221\'20\'1D with the response to the federal cost-cutting efforts of his signature \u8220\'20\'1Cdepartment of government efficiency\u8221\'20\'1D (Doge ) that would increase the budget deficit.\par \par \uc2 In an interview with CBS News, he called the bill too expensive and a measure that would \u8220\'20\'1Cundermine\u8221\'20\'1D his work to make the government more \u8220\'20\'1Cefficient\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-06-03T18:51:12.365Z">at 7.51pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-06-03T17:50:14.525Z">6.50pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 White House says it's monitoring China's compliance with trade deal\par \par \uc2 The White House said that it is actively monitoring China\u8217\'20\'19s compliance with last month\u8217\'20\'19s tariff agreement, in response to questions on how it is handling Beijing\u8217\'20\'19s curbs on rare earth minerals.\par \par \uc2 Karoline Leavitt also reiterated that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  would soon be speaking with Chinese president Xi Jinping .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI can assure you that the administration is actively monitoring China\u8217\'20\'19s compliance with the Geneva trade agreement,\u8221\'20\'1D she told reporters. \u8220\'20\'1COur administration officials continue to be engaged in correspondence with their Chinese counterparts.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-06-03T17:40:44.030Z">6.40pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Fema 'taking hurricane season seriously', says White House after agency head 'joked' that he didn't know about it\par \par \uc2 The White House said that Fema (the \uc2 Federal Emergency Management Agency\uc2 ) is taking severe storms seriously, following a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/world/us/fema-staff-confused-after-head-said-he-was-unaware-us-hurricane-season-sources-2025-06-02/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Reuters report}}}\uc2  that the head of the agency said he was not aware of hurricane season.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe know that we are into hurricane season now, and I know Fema is taking this seriously, contrary to some of the reporting we have seen based on jokes that were made and leaks from meetings,\u8221\'20\'1D Karoline Leavitt told reporters.\par \par \uc2 Reuters reported that David Richardson , who has led Fema since early May, had told baffled staff he had not been aware that the US has a hurricane season. It was not clear to staff whether he meant it literally, as a joke, or in some other context.\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for the \uc2 Department of Homeland Security\uc2 , Fema\u8217\'20\'19s parent agency, told Reuters the comment was a joke and that Fema is prepared for hurricane season.\par \par \uc2 Trump has said Fema should be shrunk or even eliminated, arguing states can take on many of its functions, as part of a wider downsizing of the federal government. About 2,000 full-time Fema staff, one-third of its total, have been terminated or voluntarily left the agency since the start of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/trump-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump administration}}}\uc2  in January.\par \par \uc2 At the same time, data {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jun/02/trump-national-weather-service-hurricanes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 seen by the Guardian has showed}}}\uc2  that more than a dozen National Weather Service (NWS) forecast offices along the hurricane-prone Gulf of Mexico coast are understaffed as the US plunges into an expected active season for ruinous storms. There is a lack of meteorologists in 15 of the regional weather service offices along the coastline from Texas to Florida, as well as in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/puerto-rico"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Puerto Rico}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 an area that takes the brunt of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coast.noaa.gov/hurricanes/#map=4/32/-80"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 almost all}}}\uc2  hurricanes that hit the US. Several offices, including in Miami, Jacksonville, Puerto Rico and Houston, lack at least a third of all the meteorologists required to be fully staffed.\par \par \uc2 And the National Hurricane Center (NHC), the Miami-based nerve center for tracking hurricanes, is short five specialists, the \uc2 Guardian\uc2  has learned, despite assurances from the Trump administration that it is fully staffed ahead of what\u8217\'20\'19s anticipated to be a busy hurricane season that officially started on Sunday.\par \par \uc2 Experts have warned the turmoil unleashed by Trump upon the NWS and Fema, which has had multiple leadership changes and still {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/policy/fema-hurricane-season-no-plan-39042ee6?gaa_at=eafs&gaa_n=ASWzDAgY0aCCYONIknpW4SjCNtDr90lhy5Tp09vo0ssNmdQA52xNGQURu9gEWDf6EFQ%3D&gaa_ts=6835f746&gaa_sig=Waf8kf-S_d1bowXJ-UWhcXtOPJ--fxcT6DrL7WJEelhx8SCEU7bBzfRpMVqi57HEglEokl9QLYPg-D-GDhMcnQ%3D%3D"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 does not have a completed plan}}}\uc2  for this year\u8217\'20\'19s hurricane season, will dangerously hamper the response to a summer that will likely bring storms, floods and wildfires across the US. <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jun/02/fema-us-hurricane-season"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fema chief tells staff he did not know US has hurricane season}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-06-03T18:29:26.795Z">at 7.29pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-06-03T17:32:54.518Z">6.32pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Trump will attend Nato summit, White House says\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will attend a summit of the transatlantic Nato alliance at The Hague later this month, White House press secretary Karoline Leavitt said.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-06-03T18:30:34.720Z">at 7.30pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-06-03T17:28:42.428Z">6.28pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Defense secretary \uc2 Pete Hegseth\uc2  will testify before the Senate armed services commitee at a 18 June hearing on the administration\u8217\'20\'19s budget request, NBC is reporting, citing a source.\par \par \uc2 It will mark Hegseth\u8217\'20\'19s first time appearing publicly before Congress since his confirmation.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-06-03T17:19:52.240Z">6.19pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 A federal prosecutor who helped lead the Department of Justice\u8217\'20\'19s investigation into the January 6 attack on Congress has resigned \u8211\'20\'13 and, in a new interview, he criticized \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s decision to pardon or commute the sentences of about 1,500 people charged in connection with the Capitol attack, saying that it \u8220\'20\'1Csends a terrible message to the American people\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Longtime assistant US attorney Greg Rosen, the former chief of the justice department\u8217\'20\'19s Capitol siege section, sat down {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/justice-department-capitol-siege-section-greg-rosen-resigns/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 with CBS News}}}\uc2  after resigning over the weekend.\par \par \uc2 In the interview, Rosen said that he was \u8220\'20\'1Cshocked, if not stunned\u8221\'20\'1D by the breadth of the pardons Trump issued to those involved in the 6 January 2021 attack just hours after his second presidential inauguration.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think the message that they send is that political violence towards a political goal is acceptable in a modern democratic society,\u8221\'20\'1D Rosen said. \u8220\'20\'1CThat, from my perspective, is anathema to a constitutional republic.\u8221\'20\'1D <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jun/03/capitol-attack-prosecutor-trump-pardons"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Former Capitol attack prosecutor slams Trump pardons of January 6 defendants}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-06-03T18:02:31.734Z">at 7.02pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-06-03T17:06:59.795Z">6.06pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Laura Loomer, the far-right influencer behind some of the Trump administration\u8217\'20\'19s firings, met privately with JD Vance at the White House this morning, CNN is reporting, citing sources.\par \par \uc2 The vice president met alone with Loomer at the Eisenhower executive office building, the outlet reports. It is not known what the pair discussed.\par \par \uc2 After Loomer\u8217\'20\'19s last known visit to the White House in April, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  fired several national security council staffers whom she described as disloyal to the president.\par \par \uc2 The firings created the extraordinary situation where Loomer appeared to have more influence than \uc2 Mike Waltz\uc2 , who was the national security adviser at the time, over the NSC and undercut Waltz in having aides axed under him.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-06-03T16:50:16.249Z">5.50pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Ras Baraka , the mayor of Newark, has sued New Jersey\u8217\'20\'19s top federal prosecutor over his arrest on a trespassing charge at an immigration detention center.\par \par \uc2 Baraka, who is also running for the Democratic nomination for New Jersey governor, alleges that he was arrested for trespassing without cause and maliciously prosecuted following a tense confrontation last month at a privately run immigration detention center in Newark.\par \par \uc2 The lawsuit names as defendants Alina Habba, the acting US attorney in New Jersey and former personal lawyer to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , and Ricky Patel , a Homeland security department official who allegedly ordered the arrest.\par \par \uc2 The lawsuit seeks damages for \u8220\'20\'1Cfalse arrest and malicious prosecution,\u8221\'20\'1D and also accuses Habba of defamation for comments she made about his case, which was later dropped.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is not about revenge,\u8221\'20\'1D Baraka said during a news conference.\par \par \uc2 Ultimately, I think this is about them taking accountability for what has happened to me.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-06-03T16:30:17.485Z">5.30pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Trump seeks to reshape judiciary as first nominees face Senate\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s first batch of judicial nominees is set to go before a Senate panel as the president looks to further reshape a judiciary whose members have stymied parts of his agenda.\par \par \uc2 Five of the 11 judicial nominees Trump has announced so far are slated to appear tomorrow before the Republican-led Senate judiciary committee, which will weigh whether to recommend them for the full Senate\u8217\'20\'19s consideration.\par \par \uc2 Those nominees all have conservative bona fides that their supporters say will help Trump shift the ideological balance of the judiciary further to the right after making 234 appointments in his first term, which was a near-record for a president\u8217\'20\'19s first four years in office.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s first-term appointees included three members of the supreme court, which since gaining a 6-3 conservative majority has curtailed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, rejected affirmative action policies on university campuses and limited the power of administrative agencies.\par \par \uc2 White House spokesperson Harrison Fields said in a statement that Trump was committed to \u8220\'20\'1Crestoring integrity to the judicial system, which begins with appointing America First judges, not unelected politicians in robes\u8221\'20\'1D. Among Wednesday\u8217\'20\'19s nominees is Whitney Hermandorfer , who as a lawyer serving under Tennessee\u8217\'20\'19s Republican attorney general has defended the state\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban and challenged federal protections for transgender youth.\par \par \uc2 Hermandorfer, who is nominated to a seat on the Cincinnati-based 6th US circuit court of appeals, will appear before the Senate panel with four nominees to fill trial court vacancies in Missouri. Those include Joshua Divine , Missouri\u8217\'20\'19s solicitor general, who challenged \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s student loan forgiveness efforts and has defended \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and transgender healthcare restrictions.\par \par \uc2 Mike Davis\uc2  , whose conservative Article III Project backs Trump\u8217\'20\'19s judicial nominees, said that in his second term Trump \u8220\'20\'1Cdoesn\u8217\'20\'19t need to appease the DC establishment with weak and timid judges\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He is picking bold and fearless judges, like Emil Bove , who will follow the constitution instead of seeking establishment favor.\par \par \uc2 Bove, a justice department official who previously served as Trump\u8217\'20\'19s defense lawyer in the New York criminal trial over hush money paid to an adult film star, was nominated last week to join the Philadelphia-based 3rd US circuit court of appeals, which if approved by the Senate would be a lifetime tenure.\par \par \uc2 His nomination drew criticism from Democrats and \uc2 Ed Whelan\uc2  , a conservative legal commentator who in a piece in the National Review called Bove\u8217\'20\'19s nomination \u8220\'20\'1Cdisturbing\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-06-03T16:23:02.954Z">5.23pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Millions of legal immigrants\u8217\'20\'19 lives upended after social security freeze\par \par \uc2 Millions of legal immigrants may be left unable to work after the \uc2 Social Security Administration\uc2  quietly instituted a rule change to stop automatically issuing them {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-social-security"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 social security}}}\uc2  numbers.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://secure.ssa.gov/poms.nsf/lnx/0110205700"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Enumeration Beyond Entry program}}}\uc2  is an agreement between the SSA and the \uc2 Department of Homeland Security\uc2 , where \uc2 US Citizenship and Immigration Services\uc2  would provide social security with information from applicants for work authorization or naturalization.\par \par \uc2 The program {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.yahoo.com/news/trump-wants-terminate-legal-immigrants-002510588.html?guccounter=1&guce_referrer=aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuZ29vZ2xlLmNvbS8&guce_referrer_sig=AQAAACjChSZLARhSiHDKdJjzSEYc7Tb1pibRKvZ4jANxaEfG6GqBrjqhWtafpp-qySX__4Vxyo_pfmy8DojWXGuOnwzskam9vmi2t4U47G5vnss0Gr3xAghPX8EQrTxYTB8Diir_28YBR00sE88fM24A4t0VUmvNmfCkh06DdWQixG7h"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 began}}}\uc2  in 2017 under the first Trump Administration.\par \par \uc2 Without any public notice, on 19 March, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://popular.info/p/exclusive-secret-policy-shift-could"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 program was halted}}}\uc2 , impacting millions of immigrants every year and burdening \uc2 Social Security Administration\uc2  offices, as those applicants will now have to visit a \uc2 Social Security Administration\uc2  office and apply separately to receive a social security number.\par \par \uc2 Following the freeze, the Trump administration issued a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/presidential-actions/2025/04/preventing-illegal-aliens-from-obtaining-social-security-act-benefits/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 memo }}}\uc2 on 15 April aimed at preventing undocumented immigrants from receiving social security benefits, but provided no evidence of it being an issue.\par \par \uc2 Trump and \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  , billionaire former leader of the so-called \u8220\'20\'1Cdepartment of government efficiency\u8221\'20\'1D (Doge ) have falsely claimed these programs are being used to attract unauthorized immigrants to vote for Democrats.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CUnauthorized immigrants are not eligible for Medicare or social security retirement benefits. Nor does any evidence exist that unauthorized immigrants fraudulently receive benefits in large numbers,\u8221\'20\'1D wrote Geoffrey Sanzenbacher, an economics professor at Boston College, in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://crr.bc.edu/the-truth-about-immigrants-medicare-and-social-security/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 blog post}}}\uc2 . <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jun/03/social-security-program-quietly-frozen-musk-immigrant-claims"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Millions of legal immigrants\u8217\'20\'19 lives upended after social security freeze}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-06-03T15:39:21.672Z">4.39pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Republican senator Katie Britt asks about funding for charter school programs, which in the budget proposal is raised by $50m to $600m. She asks how these funds will be used to expand options particularly in rural and underserved communities so parents have \u8220\'20\'1Cmore choice\u8221\'20\'1D for their children.\par \par \uc2 McMahon says \u8220\'20\'1Cno child should be trapped in a failing school\u8221\'20\'1D, which led Trump to want to expand funding for charter schools. She says the \u8220\'20\'1Cfreedom of choice\u8221\'20\'1D you get with charter schools is important.\par \par \uc2 For context, as my colleague Marina Dunbar {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/22/supreme-court-religious-charter-schools-ruling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote}}}\uc2  last month: \u8220\'20\'1CCharter schools are set up as alternatives to traditional public schools. They typically operate under private management and often feature small class sizes, innovative teaching styles or a particular academic focus.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Last month the supreme court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/22/supreme-court-religious-charter-schools-ruling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 blocked an attempt}}}\uc2  led by two Catholic dioceses to establish in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/oklahoma"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Oklahoma}}}\uc2  the nation\u8217\'20\'19s first taxpayer-funded religious charter school in a major case involving religious rights in US education that challenged the constitutional separation of church and state.\par \par \uc2 Marina {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/22/supreme-court-religious-charter-schools-ruling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 writes}}}\uc2 : \u8220\'20\'1COpponents have said religious charter schools would force taxpayers to support religious indoctrination. Establishing them also could undermine non-discrimination principles, they argued, because religious charter schools might seek to bar employees who do not adhere to doctrinal teachings.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-06-03T15:40:24.745Z">at 4.40pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-06-03T15:17:53.467Z">4.17pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Democratic senator Dick Durbin grills McMahon on why they\u8217\'20\'19re cutting the borrower defense branch of the education department, which supports students who have been left \u8220\'20\'1Cexploited\u8221\'20\'1D and struggling to pay off debt after attending for-profit schools.\par \par \uc2 After stumbling over what the department is doing to address the problem, McMahon points to counsellors in schools who can provide support to those students, before Durbin cuts her off to point out that, as we\u8217\'20\'19ve just heard, the administration is reducing funding for those very counsellors too.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-06-03T15:06:58.016Z">4.06pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Republican senator, \uc2 Shelley Moore Capito\uc2 , asks how they plan to ensure that Jewish students are able to learn in an environment free from intimidation on college campuses given the budget proposes to decrease the office of civil rights.\par \par \uc2 Education secretary, Linda McMahon, says actions taken on \uc2 Columbia University\uc2  and also Harvard illustrate that the administration \u8220\'20\'1Cwill not tolerate antisemitism on campuses or discrimination of any kind\u8221\'20\'1D. Those actions include moves to prevent encampments and mask-wearing (a reference to pro-Palestine protests last year).\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are actively enforcing that and we have defunded [programs at Columbia and Harvard,\u8221\'20\'1D McMahon says. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re saying we mean business.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-06-03T15:14:35.138Z">at 4.14pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-06-03T14:52:25.581Z">3.52pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Democratic senator \uc2 Tammy Baldwin\uc2  asks McMahon if she does not believe that \u8220\'20\'1Cincreasing students\u8217\'20\'19 access to mental health support is not in the best interests of the federal government\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 McMahon says they\u8217\'20\'19re not looking to eliminate the funding, but plan to allow the states to rebid on a competitive grant basis.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-06-03T15:25:42.787Z">at 4.25pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-06-03T14:49:08.164Z">3.49pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Democratic senator presses McMahon on whether administration plans to spend Congress-appropriated funds\par \par \uc2 Baldwin says that during her confirmation hearing McMahon had said funds appropriated by Congress \u8220\'20\'1Cshould be disseminated\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNow we have a budget request that significantly cuts funding for public schools, students and educators,\u8221\'20\'1D Baldwin says, adding that $8bn remains \u8220\'20\'1Cunallocated\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAre you going to allocate all of the funding that Congress appropriated for students and schools \u8230\'20\'26 across the country this year?\u8221\'20\'1D she asks McMahon.\par \par \uc2 She interrupts as McMahon begins to answer to say that the question isn\u8217\'20\'19t \u8220\'20\'1Cnuanced\u8221\'20\'1D. \u8220\'20\'1CCongress passed a law appropriating this funding, you said in your confirmation hearing that you would spend funding Congress appropriated.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf the answer isn\u8217\'20\'19t simply \u8216\'20\'18yes\u8217\'20\'19, based on all the evidence before us that leads me to believe that you are planning to withhold funding and shortchange students and families across America.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-06-03T15:25:46.013Z">at 4.25pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-06-03T14:33:16.610Z">3.33pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 McMahon says the budget will take a significant step towards the goal of shrinking federal bureaucracy, cutting waste and giving education back to the states.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-06-03T14:27:58.350Z">3.27pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Democratic senator tells McMahon 'students will pay price' for plan to dismantle education department\par \par \uc2 Baldwin says she is \u8220\'20\'1Cdeeply concerned\u8221\'20\'1D the administration is planning to \u8220\'20\'1Cillegally impound [congressionally appropriated] funds and dismantle the department of education\u8221\'20\'1D adding: \u8220\'20\'1CIt will be students who pay the price.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBut if the executive branch is allowed to do that and ignore the laws we [Congress] pass, I\u8217\'20\'19m not sure what we\u8217\'20\'19re doing here,\u8221\'20\'1D Baldwin says.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-06-03T14:42:37.952Z">at 3.42pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-06-03T14:18:52.919Z">3.18pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 For this fiscal year, $13bn remain \u8220\'20\'1Cunallocated\u8221\'20\'1D Baldwin says, calling it \u8220\'20\'1Cflatly unprecedented and unacceptable\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe lack of transparency combined with this budget request raises serious questions about what are you trying to hide and why?\u8221\'20\'1D says Baldwin.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis administration seems focused above all else on dismantling the department of education to score political points regardless of the impact on tens of millions of public school students,\u8221\'20\'1D she goes on.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-06-03T15:30:20.595Z">at 4.30pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-06-03T14:12:47.861Z">3.12pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 There is a feed at the top of the blog if you would like to follow along.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-06-03T14:06:43.787Z">3.06pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Education secretary Linda McMahon testifies about education budget in Senate hearing\par \par \uc2 Secretary of education, Linda McMahon, is testifying before the Senate appropriations committee on the education department\u8217\'20\'19s budget 2026 request. I\u8217\'20\'19ll bring you all the key lines here.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-06-03T15:31:58.495Z">at 4.31pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-06-03T13:59:52.389Z">2.59pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Pentagon to redraw command map to more closely align Greenland with the US - Politico\par \par \uc2 The Pentagon is poised to shift its oversight of Greenland by putting it under \uc2 US Northern Command\uc2  , \u8220\'20\'1Ca symbolic gesture that would more closely align the island territory with the US\u8221\'20\'1D, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://url4027.email.politico.com/ss/c/u001.6g0Zd3AyneOViJYBXgbV65ZWHEH5gWGSDKLrcKzwr39yLaWrIHmycRa5iv8t_UvklMEZ9jiz_wdPRi4B6djqnSgIIqg1ujUSTo6_ZP1o6vOH0kAHifXLyRmjdg_THh2MrAGGGHFJg3YcMBt168IwUL0aCupE4CkMvGcHSH2nLSOQiKzoO2-jI2iBdhh2Bzt3pvHjYlt2lfj09gtnU7kgxUD-sK8dCxww8rCE7CNHkthkxrcfPwCu7R_zGiQCT8i8/4h1/GryM17-xQdCHrkOJwo938A/h25/h001.UDAI4IuWwrqb5ANnLIvgBdRrAHkvb1HggV5BtXTL3M8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Politico reports}}}\uc2 , adding: \u8220\'20\'1CThe switch is the most concrete step yet in the Trump administration\u8217\'20\'19s months-long effort to gain ownership over the autonomous island.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The shift in oversight would see Greenland moved from European Command \u8217\'20\'19s jurisdiction to Northern Command, which is responsible for overseeing the security of North America \u8211\'20\'13 and could come as soon as this week, a DOD official and two people familiar with the planning told Politico. Denmark and the semi-autonomous Faroe Islands , on the other hand, would remain under European Command, \u8220\'20\'1Ccreating a symbolic and operational split between those territories and Greenland\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 One of the people told Politico:\par \par \uc2 From the perspective of geography, the move makes some sense. From a political perspective, however, this clearly is going to worry Europe.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-06-03T15:35:29.294Z">at 4.35pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-06-03T13:39:00.472Z">2.39pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Trump privately complains about \uc2 Amy Coney Barrett\uc2  and other supreme court justices he nominated \u8211\'20\'13 CNN\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has privately complained that the supreme court justices he appointed have not sufficiently stood behind his agenda, CNN {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2025/06/03/politics/amy-coney-barrett-justice-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2 , citing multiple sources familiar with the conversations, with particular ire at Justice \uc2 Amy Coney Barrett\uc2  , his most recent appointee.\par \par \uc2 The president has also expressed frustration about Justices \uc2 Neil Gorsuch\uc2  and \uc2 Brett Kavanaugh\uc2  , the sources told CNN, and his complaints have gone on for at least a year.\par \par \uc2 According to the sources, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s private anger at Barrett \u8220\'20\'1Chas been fuelled by allies on the right who have told Trump privately that Barrett is \u8216\'20\'18weak\u8217\'20\'19 and that her rulings have not been in line with how she presented herself in an interview before Trump nominated her to the bench in 2020\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Causing anger in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s orbit was Barrett\u8217\'20\'19s vote in March to reject the president\u8217\'20\'19s plan to freeze nearly $2bn in foreign aid , her decision that allowed Trump to be sentenced in his New York hush money case last year, and her decision {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/22/supreme-court-religious-charter-schools-ruling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to recuse herself}}}\uc2  from a high-profile case questioning whether a Catholic charter school in Oklahoma should be entitled to taxpayer funding (she had ties to the attorneys representing the school).\par \par \uc2 CNN notes:\par \par \uc2 Much of the criticism from the right has overlooked the fact that Barrett remains a reliable vote for conservative outcomes at the supreme court . She did not dissent in recent cases allowing Trump to enforce his ban on transgender service members, end temporary deportation protections for Venezuelans, fire board members at independent agencies and cut millions in education grants.\par \par \uc2 And yet Barrett is nevertheless one of the most important justices to watch because she does, at times, break with the more rigid conservativism embraced by [Clarence] Thomas and [Samuel] Alito . A year ago, when the supreme court was hearing arguments about whether to grant Trump sweeping immunity from criminal prosecution, it was Barrett who was at the center of some of the most compelling exchanges with Trump\u8217\'20\'19s attorney. Barrett was one of several justices who prodded Trump\u8217\'20\'19s attorney to agree that a president\u8217\'20\'19s \u8216\'20\'18private\u8217\'20\'19 actions would not qualify for immunity.\par \par \uc2 But when the court\u8217\'20\'19s decision landed in July, Barrett ultimately sided with the court\u8217\'20\'19s conservatives to grant immunity to Trump.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-06-03T15:37:51.104Z">at 4.37pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-06-03T13:07:50.705Z">2.07pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 After \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  revealed his cancer diagnosis, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  offered an uncharacteristically empathetic and simple response.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMelania and I are saddened to hear about \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s recent medical diagnosis. We extend our warmest and best wishes to Jill and the family, and we wish Joe a fast and successful recovery,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.instagram.com/p/DJz8dAIuwZI/?hl=en"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote}}}\uc2  on social media.\par \par \uc2 But the compassion didn\u8217\'20\'19t last long. Trump soon reverted to type, dabbling in a burgeoning rightwing conspiracy theory about Biden\u8217\'20\'19s health and comparing the former president, who has stage four prostate cancer, to a corpse, as Trump\u8217\'20\'19s hangers-on and acolytes used the diagnosis to attack Biden and his wife.\par \par \uc2 Trump posted his well-wishing message on 18 May, after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/18/joe-biden-prostate-cancer-diagnosis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s office announced}}}\uc2  the 82-year-old had been diagnosed with an \u8220\'20\'1Caggressive form\u8221\'20\'1D of prostate cancer that has spread to his bones.\par \par \uc2 The president\u8217\'20\'19s tone changed quickly, however. Trump spent Memorial Day \u8211\'20\'13 which the \uc2 Department of Defense\uc2  describes as being intended to \u8220\'20\'1Chonor all those who died in service to the US during peacetime and war\u8221\'20\'1D, attacking his one time rival and his time in office. \u8220\'20\'1CHappy Memorial Day to all,\u8221\'20\'1D the president wrote on Truth Social.\par \par \uc2 Including the scum that spent the last four years trying to destroy our country through warped radical left minds, who allowed 21,000,000 million people to illegally enter our country, many of them being criminals and the mentally insane, through an open border that only an incompetent president would approve, and through judges who are on a mission to keep murderers, drug dealers, rapists, gang members, and released prisoners from all over the world, in our country so they can rob, murder, and rape again \u8211\'20\'13 all protected by these USA hating judges who suffer from an ideology that is sick, and very dangerous for our country.\par \par \uc2 It was clear that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cwarmest and best wishes\u8221\'20\'1D to Biden had been firmly retracted, and that became even more transparent as Trump went on to promote an emerging, fact-free, theory that Biden hid the cancer diagnosis while in office.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m surprised that the public wasn\u8217\'20\'19t notified a long time ago because to get to stage nine, that\u8217\'20\'19s a long time,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said \u8211\'20\'13 seemingly conflating the Gleason score, which measures how cancerous cells look compared with normal cells, with Biden\u8217\'20\'19s stage four cancer. <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jun/03/trump-biden-cancer-diagnosis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump extendss sympathy after Biden cancer diagnosis \u8211\'20\'13 but it doesn\u8217\'20\'19t last long}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-06-03T15:39:42.372Z">at 4.39pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-06-03T12:34:26.607Z">1.34pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Trump threatens 'large scale fines' over transgender athlete's participation in California high school competition\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has threatened to impose \u8220\'20\'1Clarge scale fines\u8221\'20\'1D on California over the participation of a transgender athlete taking part in a high school competition.\par \par \uc2 The president wrote on Truth Social:\par \par \uc2 A Biological Male competed in California Girls State Finals, WINNING BIG, despite the fact that they were warned by me not to do so. As Governor Gavin Newscum fully understands, large scale fines will be imposed!!!\par \par \uc2 He appeared to be referring to 16-year-old AB Hernandez , a transgender athlete who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2025/jun/01/teen-trans-athlete-ab-hernandez"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 took home gold}}}\uc2  in the girls high jump and the triple jump at the California high school track and field championship last weekend.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 California Interscholastic Federation\uc2  (\uc2 CIF\uc2 ), the governing board for California high school sports, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/27/california-trans-student-high-school-sports-rule-change"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 changed the rules ahead of the competition}}}\uc2  to allow more cisgender girls to compete and medal in events in which Hernandez competed. \uc2 CIF\uc2  announced the change after Trump threatened last week {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2025/may/28/us-politics-live-donald-trump-elon-musk-tax-doge-harvard-students-immigration-news-updates?CMP=share_btn_url&page=with%3Ablock-68370e7e8f084e71bb0de087#block-68370e7e8f084e71bb0de087"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to pull federal funding}}}\uc2  from California unless it bars transgender athletes from competing in girls\u8217\'20\'19 sports.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-06-03T13:08:21.120Z">at 2.08pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-06-03T11:45:37.923Z">12.45pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Millions of acres of Alaska wilderness will lose federal protection and be exposed to drilling and mining in the Trump administration\u8217\'20\'19s latest move to prioritize energy production over the shielding of the US\u8217\'20\'19s open spaces.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/dec/01/doug-burgum-trump-interior-secretary-drilling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Doug Burgum}}}\uc2 , the interior secretary, said on Monday that the government would reverse an order {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/04/19/climate/biden-alaska-drilling-mining-nrpa.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 issued by Joe Biden}}}\uc2  in December that banned drilling in the remote 23m-acre National Petroleum Reserve-Alaska (\uc2 NPR\uc2 -A), the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/live/2025/06/02/us/trump-news?partner=slack&smid=sl-share#national-petroleum-reserve-alaska-trump-drilling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York Times reported}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The former president\u8217\'20\'19s executive order was part of a package of protections for large areas of Alaska, some elements of which the state was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/08/alaska-biden-oil-drilling-lawsuit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 challenging in court}}}\uc2  when he left office in January.\par \par \uc2 Burgum was speaking in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/alaska"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Alaska}}}\uc2  on Monday accompanied by the \uc2 Environmental Protection Agency\uc2  administrator \uc2 Lee Zeldin\uc2 , and the energy secretary \uc2 Chris Wright\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 He said the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/biden-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden administration}}}\uc2  had prioritized \u8220\'20\'1Cobstruction over production\u8221\'20\'1D and Biden\u8217\'20\'19s order was \u8220\'20\'1Cundermining our ability to harness domestic resources at a time when American energy independence has never been more critical\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/SecretaryWright/status/1929560891416039684"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 post to Twitter/X}}}\uc2 , Wright said oil production was the \u8220\'20\'1Cengine of economic growth\u8221\'20\'1D in Alaska, funding more than 90% of the state\u8217\'20\'19s general revenue. \u8220\'20\'1CUnleashing American energy goes hand in hand with unleashing American prosperity,\u8221\'20\'1D he wrote. <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jun/02/trump-administration-alaska-drilling-mining"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump officials open up millions of acres in Alaska to drilling and mining}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-06-03T11:30:42.983Z">12.30pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has pardoned two south Florida shark divers convicted of theft for freeing 19 sharks and a giant grouper from a fisherman\u8217\'20\'19s longline several miles from shore.\par \par \uc2 Pardons for Tanner Mansell and John Moore Jr were signed on Wednesday. They had been convicted in 2022 of theft of property within special maritime jurisdiction.\par \par \uc2 The two men avoided prison time, but they were ordered to pay $3,343.72 in restitution, and the felony convictions prevented them from voting in Florida, owning firearms and traveling freely outside the US.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe never stopped fighting, and justice has finally prevailed,\u8221\'20\'1D Moore\u8217\'20\'19s attorney, Marc Seitles, said in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1CWe are thrilled the White House considered our arguments and determined this was an unjust prosecution. We could not be happier for John and Tanner.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Moore, who was captain of a shark-diving charter boat, and Mansell, a crew member, spotted the longline about 3 miles (5km) off the Jupiter Inlet in August 2020, according to court records. Believing it was an illegal fishing line, the men freed the sharks and grouper, reported it to state wildlife officials and brought the line back to shore. <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jun/02/trump-shark-divers-florida"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump pardons two divers convicted of theft for freeing sharks off Florida coast}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-06-03T11:19:39.909Z">12.19pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Trump administration uses Colorado suspect\u8217\'20\'19s status to push deportation agenda\par \par \uc2 The immigration status of the man who allegedly attacked people with a makeshift flame-thrower and other incendiary devices at an event for Israeli hostages in Boulder, Colorado, has become further fodder for the Trump administration\u8217\'20\'19s deportation agenda.\par \par \uc2 Mohamed Sabry Soliman, a 45-year-old who came to the US in 2022 from Egypt and overstayed his initial tourist visa, according to the \uc2 US government\uc2 , allegedly planned his attack on the event specifically to target Zionists, federal authorities said. He shouted \u8220\'20\'1CFree Palestine\u8221\'20\'1D while carrying out the attack, which the \uc2 FBI\uc2  has called an \u8220\'20\'1Cact of terrorism\u8221\'20\'1D, and he was charged on Monday with a federal hate crime.\par \par \uc2 The attack combines two frequent enemies of the right \u8211\'20\'13 anti-Israel speech and actions, and illegal immigration \u8211\'20\'13 and is already being used on the right to garner support for more deportations. The response stands in contrast to how the right has reacted to attacks against Palestinians and Muslims in the US and to the conservative response to the war in Gaza. The Trump administration has also used support for Palestinians as an underpinning for deportations among college students.\par \par \uc2 The Gateway Pundit, a rightwing outlet, is referring to Soliman as \u8220\'20\'1CBiden\u8217\'20\'19s Illegal Alien from Egypt\u8221\'20\'1D. \uc2 Stephen Miller\uc2 , \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s deputy chief of staff, said the \u8220\'20\'1Cterror attack\u8221\'20\'1D was committed by an \u8220\'20\'1Cillegal alien\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe was granted a tourist visa by the Biden Administration and then he illegally overstayed that visa. In response, the Biden Administration gave him a work permit,\u8221\'20\'1D Miller wrote on X. \u8220\'20\'1CSuicidal migration must be fully reversed.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In a post on Truth Social, Trump blamed the attack on Biden\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cridiculous Open Border Policy\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe must go out under \u8216\'20\'18TRUMP\u8217\'20\'19 Policy,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump wrote. \u8220\'20\'1CActs of Terrorism will be prosecuted to the fullest extent of the Law. This is yet another example of why we must keep our Borders SECURE, and deport Illegal, Anti-American Radicals from our Homeland.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-06-03T13:11:38.258Z">at 2.11pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-06-03T11:03:20.261Z">12.03pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 A Boston high school student who was detained by immigration agents on Saturday while he was on his way to volleyball practice must be kept in Massachusetts for at least 72 hours, a federal judge said on Monday.\par \par \uc2 Marcelo Gomes Da Silva, 18, entered the United States on a student visa, according to a lawsuit filed on his behalf after his arrest. While his student visa status has lapsed, he is eligible for and intends to apply for asylum.\par \par \uc2 US district judge Richard Stearns ordered the 72-hour stay on Monday to \u8220\'20\'1Cprovide a fair opportunity for the judge who will be randomly assigned to this case\u8221\'20\'1D to review merits and rule on any contested issues.\par \par \uc2 Nonetheless, the head of \uc2 US Immigration and Customs Enforcement\uc2  (Ice) on Monday defended his agency\u8217\'20\'19s actions, saying the teen in question was \u8220\'20\'1Cin this country illegally and we\u8217\'20\'19re not going to walk away from anybody\u8221\'20\'1D. Gomes\u8217\'20\'19s attorney asked for his immediate release.\par \par \uc2 Attorney Miriam Conrad, in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://media.wbur.org/wp/2025/06/1.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 filing}}}\uc2  on Sunday, said that Gomes \u8220\'20\'1Chas no criminal history anywhere in the world\u8221\'20\'1D in asking for his release.\par \par \uc2 Gomes was arrested on Saturday in Milford, Massachusetts, where he lives. <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jun/02/ice-arrest-boston-teen-marcelo-gomes-da-silva"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Judge orders 72-hour stay for Boston teen arrested by Ice on way to volleyball practice}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-06-03T10:40:17.254Z">11.40am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 European Union\uc2  did not receive a letter from the United States in which \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s administration made a demand for countries to submit their best offer on trade negotiations by Wednesday, according to a source familiar with the talks.\par \par \uc2 After a call with \uc2 European Commission\uc2  President \uc2 Ursula von der Leyen\uc2 , Trump restored a 9 July deadline to allow for talks between Washington and Brussels to continue.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-06-03T13:12:35.037Z">at 2.12pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-06-03T10:28:17.981Z">11.28am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Authorities said on Sunday they believed Soliman acted alone and that no other suspect was being sought, AP reported.\par \par \uc2 He was also injured and was taken to a hospital to be treated. Authorities did not give details of his injuries, but a booking photo showed him with a large bandage over one ear.\par \par \uc2 Soliman was living in the US illegally after entering the country in August 2022 on a B2 visa that expired in February 2023, \uc2 Department of Homeland Security\uc2  assistant secretary Tricia McLaughlin said.\par \par \uc2 She added that Soliman filed for asylum in September 2022 and was granted a work authorisation in March 2023 that had expired.\par \par \uc2 Public records listed him as living in a modest rented townhouse in Colorado Springs, where local media outlets reported federal law enforcement agents were on the scene on Sunday.\par \par \uc2 An online resume under Soliman\u8217\'20\'19s name said he was employed by a Denver-area healthcare company working in accounting and inventory control, with previous employers listed as companies in Egypt.\par \par \uc2 Under education, the resume listed \uc2 Al-Azhar University\uc2 , a historic centre for Islamic and Arabic learning in Cairo.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-06-03T13:25:59.439Z">at 2.25pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-06-03T10:12:30.536Z">11.12am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Video from the scene shows a witness shouting : \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s right there. He\u8217\'20\'19s throwing molotov cocktails\u8221\'20\'1D, as a police officer with his gun drawn advances on a bare-chested suspect holding containers in each hand.\par \par \uc2 Alex Osante, of San Diego, said he was having lunch when he heard the crash of a bottle breaking on the ground and a \u8220\'20\'1Cboom\u8221\'20\'1D sound followed by people yelling and screaming.\par \par \uc2 In video of the scene captured by Osante, people can be seen pouring water on a woman lying on the ground who Osante said had caught fire during the attack.\par \par \uc2 After the initial attack, Osante said the suspect went behind some bushes and then re-emerged and threw a petrol bomb, but apparently accidentally caught himself on fire as he threw it.\par \par \uc2 The man then took off his shirt and what appeared to be a bulletproof vest before the police arrived. The man dropped to the ground and was arrested without any apparent resistance in the video filmed by Osante.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-06-03T13:28:54.303Z">at 2.28pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-06-03T10:00:04.601Z">11.00am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Israeli prime minister \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  issued a statement on Monday saying he, his wife and the nation of Israel were praying for the full recovery of the people wounded in the \u8220\'20\'1Cvicious terror attack\u8221\'20\'1D in Colorado.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSadly, attacks like this are becoming too common across the country,\u8221\'20\'1D said Mark Michalek, the special agent in charge of the \uc2 FBI\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Denver field office.\par \par \uc2 In New York, the police department said it had upped its presence at religious sites throughout the city for Shavuot.\par \par \uc2 The eight victims who were wounded were between 52 and 88 years old and the injuries ranged from serious to minor, officials said.\par \par \uc2 The attack occurred as people with a volunteer group called Run For Their Lives was concluding a weekly demonstration to raise visibility for the hostages who remain in Gaza.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-06-03T13:31:40.478Z">at 2.31pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-06-03T09:47:44.067Z">10.47am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Suspect in Colorado flamethrower attack told police he targeted 'Zionist group'\par \par \uc2 Hello and welcome to the US politics live blog. I\u8217\'20\'19m Tom Ambrose and I will be bringing you all the latest news lines over the next few hours.\par \par \uc2 We start with the news that a man accused of using a makeshift flame-thrower and an incendiary device to attack a US group bringing attention to Israeli hostages in Gaza has been charged with a federal hate crime .\par \par \uc2 Mohammed Sabry Soliman, 45, told police he had planned it for a year and targeted what he described as the \u8220\'20\'1CZionist group\u8221\'20\'1D, the \uc2 FBI\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 CNN reviewed a \uc2 Facebook\uc2  account matching his name and date of birth. It {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://us.cnn.com/2025/06/02/us/boulder-colorado-antisemitic-attack-mohamed-soliman-invs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 On the account\u8217\'20\'19s page, which was last updated about 10 years ago, Soliman said he attended high school and college in Egypt and later moved to Kuwait, where he had an accounting job, according to the page. That account featured photos of \uc2 Mohamed Morsi\uc2 , the \uc2 Muslim Brotherhood\uc2  leader who served as Egypt\u8217\'20\'19s president from 2012 to 2013, when he was ousted in a military coup that triggered mass protests and sit-ins in Cairo.\par \par \uc2 Posts on the \uc2 Facebook\uc2  page expressed support for the \uc2 Muslim Brotherhood\uc2  protests against the removal of Morsi. One post from August 2013 featured a four-finger salute with a yellow background, a symbol supportive of the Rabaa al-Adawiya square encampment, which was violently dispersed by Egyptian security forces loyal to Egypt\u8217\'20\'19s then-defense minister and current president, \uc2 Abdel Fattah al-Sisi\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Twelve people were injured in the attack in Colorado, some with burns, as a group was concluding a weekly demonstration to raise visibility for the hostages who remain in Gaza, AP reported. Witnesses reported the man shouted \u8220\'20\'1CFree Palestine\u8221\'20\'1D during the attack.\par \par \uc2 An \uc2 FBI\uc2  affidavit says Soliman confessed to the attack after being taken into custody on Sunday and told the police he would do it again. The affidavit was released in support of a federal hate crime charged filed by the Justice Department on Monday.\par \par \uc2 The attack happened on the beginning of the Jewish holiday of Shavuot, which is marked with the reading of the Torah, and barely a week after a man who also yelled \u8220\'20\'1CFree Palestine\u8221\'20\'1D was charged with fatally shooting two Israeli embassy employees outside a Jewish museum in Washington.\par \par \uc2 Federal and state prosecutors filed separate criminal cases against Soliman, charging him with a hate crime and attempted murder, respectively. He faces additional state charges related to the incendiary devices, and more charges are possible in federal court, where the justice department will seek a grand jury indictment.\par \par \uc2 During a state court hearing on Monday, Soliman appeared briefly via a video link from the Boulder County Jail wearing an orange jumpsuit.\par \par \uc2 In other news:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The head of Ice defended his agency\u8217\'20\'19s decision to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2025/jun/02/donald-trump-tariffs-white-house-us-politics-live-news?CMP=share_btn_url&page=with%3Ablock-683debcd8f083f8602399484#block-683debcd8f083f8602399484"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 arrest an 18-year-old Massachusetts high school student}}}\uc2  on his way to volleyball practice. US district judge Richard Stearns later {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://media.wbur.org/wp/2025/06/095112988016.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ordered}}}\uc2  a 72-hour stay to \u8220\'20\'1Cprovide a fair opportunity for the judge who will be randomly assigned to this case\u8221\'20\'1D to review merits and rule on any contested issues in the case of Marcelo Gomes Da Silva .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Massachusetts Institute of Technology\uc2  (MIT) barred its 2025 class president from attending her graduation ceremony on Friday after she delivered a speech during a commencement event the day before condemning Israel\u8217\'20\'19s war in Gaza and criticizing the university\u8217\'20\'19s ties to Israel.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 China accused the US of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2025/jun/02/donald-trump-tariffs-white-house-us-politics-live-news?CMP=share_btn_url&page=with%3Ablock-683de6798f0830853c23d986#block-683de6798f0830853c23d986"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cseriously violating\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  and undermining the agreements reached in Geneva in May.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Prosecutors in Milwaukee charged a man on Monday with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://wcca.wicourts.gov/caseDetail.html?caseNo=2025CF002572&countyNo=40&index=0&mode=details#charges"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 four felonies}}}\uc2  for attempting to frame an undocumented immigrant he is accused of assaulting, by sending forged letters in the immigrant\u8217\'20\'19s name with a threat to kill \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 New York\u8217\'20\'19s lieutenant governor, Antonio Delgado , announced on Monday that he is running for governor, setting up a Democratic primary battle against the sitting governor, \uc2 Kathy Hochul\uc2  , who selected him for the job as her deputy.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  , the Senate\u8217\'20\'19s senior Democrat, released a social media video on Monday in which he seemed to taunt \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for supposedly being too \u8220\'20\'1Cchicken\u8221\'20\'1D in negotiations with Iran over its nuclear program.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-06-03T13:06:43.699Z">at 2.06pm BST</time> \par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250603el63001bc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
