\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Trump says he is doubling tariffs on imported steel to 50% \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Robert Mackey, Lucy Campbell, Marina Dunbar and Tom Ambrose \par \uc2 13,689 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 June 2025\par 01:15 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This liveblog is now closed.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-31T01:33:22.125Z">2.33am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 This concludes our live coverage of the second Trump administration for the day. Here are some of the day\u8217\'20\'19s leading developments:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  made a surprise announcement doubling tariffs on imported steel and aluminum {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2025/may/30/donald-trump-tariffs-elon-musk-us-politics-live-news-updates?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with%3Ablock-683a2a3d8f086f6030084e3a#block-683a2a3d8f086f6030084e3a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 from 25% to 50%}}}\uc2  during a speech in Pittsburgh celebrating a deal between \uc2 US Steel\uc2  and Japan\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Nippon Steel Corporation\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The exact nature of the \uc2 US Steel\uc2  deal Trump blessed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2025/may/30/donald-trump-tariffs-elon-musk-us-politics-live-news-updates?page=with:block-683a4f538f086f6030084ec7#block-683a4f538f086f6030084ec7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 remained unclear}}}\uc2 . Although the president insists that it is \u8220\'20\'1Ca partnership\u8221\'20\'1D, \uc2 Nippon Steel\uc2  has never withdrawn its bid to buy and control \uc2 US Steel\uc2  as a wholly owned subsidiary. The \uc2 US Steel\uc2  website still describes the deal as \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 US Steel\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s agreement to be acquired by NSC\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 If the deal is a purchase of \uc2 US Steel\uc2  by its Japanese rival, Trump would be breaking {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2025/may/30/donald-trump-tariffs-elon-musk-us-politics-live-news-updates?page=with%3Ablock-683a18038f085984c73673aa#block-683a18038f085984c73673aa"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a campaign promise}}}\uc2  to block any such sale.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump held {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2025/may/30/donald-trump-tariffs-elon-musk-us-politics-live-news-updates?page=with%3Ablock-6839fff38f086f6030084cb9#block-6839fff38f086f6030084cb9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a bizarre press conference}}}\uc2  in the Oval Office with \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  , during which the billionaire said farewell to his role as a special government employee and the president repeated false claims about government spending his donor-turned-aide had stopped.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Supreme Court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2025/may/30/donald-trump-tariffs-elon-musk-us-politics-live-news-updates?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with%3Ablock-6839c43d8f088b2f036eb305#block-6839c43d8f088b2f036eb305"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ruled}}}\uc2  that the Trump administration can, for now, revoke the temporary protected status of more than 500,000 refugees fleeing violence or persecution in Haiti, Cuba, Venezuela and Nicaragua. Those legal immigrants are now subject to deportation if they choose not to leave their new homes in communities like Springfield, Ohio, where they were falsely accused by the president of eating pets.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2025/may/30/donald-trump-tariffs-elon-musk-us-politics-live-news-updates?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with%3Ablock-683a13668f088b2f036eb744#block-683a13668f088b2f036eb744"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2  on social media that he had fired Kim Sajet , the first female director of the National Portrait Gallery. Legal experts suggested that Trump does not have the power to fire Sajet, an employee of the Smithsonian, which is not run by the executive branch.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-31T00:57:38.316Z">1.57am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Fox News points out \uc2 US Steel\uc2  describes deal blessed by Trump as an acquisition\par \par \uc2 Even pro-Trump commentators on Fox are baffled at the ongoing uncertainty over the exact nature of the deal between \uc2 US Steel\uc2  and its Japanese rival \uc2 Nippon Steel Corporation\uc2  celebrated by the president at his rally on Friday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is being described as \u8216\'20\'18a partnership\u8217\'20\'19, this deal between Nippon and \uc2 US Steel\uc2 ; but then its described as an acquisition on the \uc2 US Steel\uc2  website,\u8221\'20\'1D the Fox host Laura Ingraham {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/Acyn/status/1928600393401221487"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pointed out}}}\uc2  on her show Friday night.\par \par \uc2 She then asked a guest from another pro-Trump outlet, Breitbart, \u8220\'20\'1CWho owns the majority stake in this company?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 When the guest said that he did not know, Ingraham suggested that Trump himself might not be aware of the details. \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t know if he was fully informed about the terms of the deal. We just don\u8217\'20\'19t know.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It is indeed the case that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ussteel.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US Steel\u8217\'20\'19s website}}}\uc2  links to a standalone site with the combined branding of the two companies that features {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bestdealforamericansteel.com/transaction-benefits-for-all-stakeholders"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a statement}}}\uc2  describing the transaction as \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 U. S. Steel\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s agreement to be acquired by NSC.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The same site also features a statement praising \u8220\'20\'1CPresident Trump\u8217\'20\'19s leadership\u8221\'20\'1D that says: \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 U. S. Steel\uc2  will remain American, and we will grow bigger and stronger through a partnership with \uc2 Nippon Steel\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-31T01:28:15.632Z">at 2.28am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-30T23:58:26.818Z">12.58am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Candace Laing , the president and chief executive of the Canadian Chamber of Commerce is not happy with the new 50% tariffs on imported steel and aluminum Trump announced on Friday. Here is her statement:\par \par \uc2 Unwinding the efficient, competitive and reliable cross border supply chains like we have in steel and aluminum comes at a great cost to both countries. In 2018, under the last round of steel and aluminum tariffs, we saw significant net negative job loss in America. Doubling the steel aluminum tariffs to 50% is antithetical to North American economic security. The fact remains that Canada is a reliable and secure trading partner that supplies materials that sustain American jobs.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-31T00:09:38.875Z">at 1.09am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-30T23:23:35.931Z">12.23am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://truthsocial.com/@realDonaldTrump/posts/114599330494282325"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a post}}}\uc2  to his social media platform from Air Force One, as he flies back to Washington from Pittsburgh, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  just announced that his new 50% tariffs on steel also apply to imported aluminum and will take effect on Wednesday, 4 June.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-30T22:43:39.923Z">11.43pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Trump does have authority to raise steel tariffs\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  just wrapped up his speech to steelworkers in Pittsburgh, which closely resembled a campaign event, despite the fact that he is no longer eligible to run for the presidency again.\par \par \uc2 The main news of the speech, at a \uc2 US Steel\uc2  plant near Pittsburgh, celebrating the sale of the company to Japan\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Nippon Steel\uc2 , was Trump\u8217\'20\'19s announcement that he was doubling tariffs on imported steel, from 25% to 50%.\par \par \uc2 Despite a court ruling this week that Trump does not have the authority to impose tariffs at will, he does have the authority, as president, to unilaterally raise tariffs on steel imports, under a national security provision called Section 232 of the Trade Expansion Act.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-30T22:24:15.792Z">11.24pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Trump presented with jersey of \uc2 Pittsburgh Steelers\uc2  great who endorsed \uc2 Kamala Harris\par \par \uc2 Near the start of his rally at a \uc2 US Steel\uc2  factory outside of Pittsburgh, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was presented with a \uc2 Pittsburgh Steelers\uc2  jersey by the former Steeler Rocky Bleier.\par \par \uc2 The jersey had Trump\u8217\'20\'19s name and the No 47, in honor of his role as the 47th president. Bleier {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/01Funkytown/status/1928573372285464805"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 noted}}}\uc2  that a Steelers jersey with that number \u8220\'20\'1Changs in the National Football League Hall of Fame\u8221\'20\'1D. <figure class="element element-video" data-canonical-url="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6Zry_OAqdvM" > <figcaption>Rocky Bleier and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in Pittsburgh on Friday.</figcaption> </figure>\par \par \uc2 What Bleier did not say is that the hall-of-famer who wore that number for the Steelers was his teammate {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.profootballhof.com/search/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mel Blount}}}\uc2 , a great defensive back.\par \par \uc2 Blount, however, is not a Trump supporter. In 2024, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.unionprogress.com/2024/09/28/why-are-we-writing-about-mel-blount-its-news-we-promise/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he endorsed Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  in her campaign against Trump.\par \par \uc2 In 2016, Blount {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://web.archive.org/web/20161111162954/https://www.post-gazette.com/news/politics-nation/2016/11/05/Biden-praises-union-support-of-Clinton-McGinty/stories/201611050166"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appeared alongside Joe Biden}}}\uc2  at a campaign rally for Trump\u8217\'20\'19s opponent \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-31T00:11:16.316Z">at 1.11am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-30T22:04:58.979Z">11.04pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Trump says he is doubling tariffs on imported steel to 50%\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  just announced at his rally in Pittsburgh that he is increasing the tariff on imported steel from 25% to 50%.\par \par \uc2 The US president told steel workers: \u8220\'20\'1CWe are going to be imposing a 25% increase. We\u8217\'20\'19re going to bring it from 25% to 50% the tariffs on steel into the United States of America, which will even further secure the steel industry in the United States.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-30T22:21:05.028Z">at 11.21pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-30T21:50:36.940Z">10.50pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Trump claims \uc2 US Steel\uc2  will remain 'an American company' after deal with Japanese rival\par \par \uc2 Speaking to steelworkers in Pittsburgh, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  just insisted that \uc2 US Steel\uc2  will \u8220\'20\'1Cstay an American company\u8221\'20\'1D after what he is now calling \u8220\'20\'1Ca partnership\u8221\'20\'1D with \uc2 Nippon Steel\uc2 , the Japanese firm that offered $14.9bn for its US rival.\par \par \uc2 It remains unclear how the deal Trump initially opposed is different from a takeover by the Japanese firm.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-30T21:55:44.775Z">at 10.55pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-30T21:27:57.820Z">10.27pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 California legislature opens bribery investigation into Paramount over possible Trump settlement \u8211\'20\'13 report\par \par \uc2 Two powerful California state senators have invited the former leaders of CBS News and 60 Minutes to testify as part of an investigation into whether the network\u8217\'20\'19s parent company, Paramount, might have violated state laws against bribery and unfair competition.\par \par \uc2 As Semafor reports, a letter asking for testimony from the former 60 Minutes producer Bill Owens and the former CBS News president Wendy McMahon, who both recently resigned, comes as Paramount has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/business/media/paramount-has-offered-15-million-to-settle-cbs-lawsuit-trump-wants-more-861d857e?gaa_at=eafs&gaa_n=ASWzDAgeCtOvIRXSjt4ObgatgAemqoYbmUYtHhzopw8Ufn2jzDUzEPrFlLau4tyuDR4%3D&gaa_ts=6839f488&gaa_sig=zSdwN0F4TwaKn3KZ5SCEYgwXAu1ep0jybPG48Q8AWlNwPQbXEDT8wMl7DUiS8SZ2xykuuLaEEmAGImOddVPGEQ%3D%3D"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reportedly}}}\uc2  offered \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s 2024 campaign $15m to settle a lawsuit filed against \uc2 CBS\uc2  over the fairly standard editing of an interview with \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , the former vice-president, in October.\par \par \uc2 Trump has so far refused to settle and threatened to file an additional suit against the company, which needs federal approval for a merger with the entertainment company Skydance. The chief executive of Skydance, \uc2 David Ellison\uc2 , is the son of the pro-Trump billionaire \uc2 Oracle Corporation\uc2  co-founder and chairman, \uc2 Larry Ellison\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A copy of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cdn.sanity.io/files/ifn0l6bs/production/d4e57e647c63b4e8fe556009e792ef39ff826cce.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the letter,}}}\uc2  obtained by Semafor, shows that it was sent by the chair of the California state senate energy, utilities & communications committee, Josh Becker, and the judiciary committee chair, Thomas Umberg.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYour recent resignations from \uc2 CBS\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s leadership, amid public reports of internal concern about the editorial and ethical implications of the proposed settlement, suggest that you may possess important, first-hand knowledge relevant to our legislative oversight responsibilities,\u8221\'20\'1D the lawmakers wrote to the former CBS News leaders.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-30T21:57:25.631Z">at 10.57pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-30T21:00:26.333Z">10.00pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Before he was for the Japanese bid for \uc2 US Steel\uc2 , Trump was actually against it\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is about to speak at a rally in Pittsburgh to celebrate what he is calling a \u8220\'20\'1Cpartnership\u8221\'20\'1D between \uc2 US Steel\uc2  and \uc2 Nippon Steel\uc2 , after insisting for months last year that he was \u8220\'20\'1C{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2024/dec/03/trump-nippon-us-steel"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 totally against}}}\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D the $14.9bn bid by the Japanese firm for its US rival.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s predecessor, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/03/us-blocks-us-steel-nippon-steel"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 blocked}}}\uc2  Nippon\u8217\'20\'19s acquisition of \uc2 US Steel\uc2 , citing national security concerns, during his final weeks in office. The Trump administration undertook a review of the proposal this year.\par \par \uc2 While the White House has been vague about the exact terms of the deal, and what changed Trump\u8217\'20\'19s mind about it, he was extremely clear about his opposition to the takeover on the campaign trail last year.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey want to strip us of our wealth and seeing our \u8211\'20\'13 you\u8217\'20\'19ve seen our companies being sold off to foreign countries all the time,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump told voters in Saginaw, Michigan at a rally last October. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd how about \uc2 US Steel\uc2 ? I\u8217\'20\'19m not going to let them sell \uc2 US Steel\uc2 . I don\u8217\'20\'19t care, even if it\u8217\'20\'19s maybe good.\u8221\'20\'1D <figure class="element element-video" data-canonical-url="{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ctXd9jTTc90"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ctXd9jTTc90}}}\uc2 " > <figcaption>\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  told voters in Michigan in October that he would not let \uc2 US Steel\uc2  be sold to a Japanese rival.</figcaption> </figure>\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis was the most important, 65, 70 years ago, \uc2 US Steel\uc2  was the most important company in the world. Now, Japan wants to buy it. I would not let that happen,\u8221\'20\'1D the candidate said. \u8220\'20\'1CI hope it doesn\u8217\'20\'19t go through before I get there because if I get there and it\u8217\'20\'19s not done, we\u8217\'20\'19re not letting that \u8211\'20\'13 we\u8217\'20\'19ll help it. We\u8217\'20\'19ll help it get along. But we\u8217\'20\'19re not letting them buy \uc2 US Steel\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 After he won the November election, Trump reiterated his opposition to the deal in a social media post. \u8220\'20\'1CI am totally against the once great and powerful \uc2 U.S. Steel\uc2  being bought by a foreign company, in this case Nippon Steel of Japan,\u8221\'20\'1D he wrote in December. \u8220\'20\'1CAs President, I will block this deal from happening. Buyer Beware!!!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 After meeting Japan\u8217\'20\'19s prime minister at the White House in February, Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/Roshan_Rinaldi/status/1887963849233457612"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2  that Nippon, a company he repeatedly called \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Nissan\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D by mistake, would be investing in \uc2 US Steel\uc2  rather than buying it.\par \par \uc2 Then last week, Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://truthsocial.com/@realDonaldTrump/posts/114558783827880495"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced on social media}}}\uc2  that he would approve what he called \u8220\'20\'1Ca planned partnership between \uc2 United States Steel\uc2  and \uc2 Nippon Steel\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Asked by reporters about the deal on Sunday, Trump, again calling Nippon \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Nissan\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D by mistake, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/Acyn/status/1926769935822225557"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 insisted}}}\uc2  that it was an investment rather than a purchase or merger.\par \par \uc2 Among those unclear about how this was different from the sale Trump had promised to block were the leaders of the United Steel workers union.\par \par \uc2 The USW said in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://usw.org/bargaining-update/u-s-steel-partnership-announcements-more-questions-than-answers/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a statement}}}\uc2  on Wednesday that the terms of the \u8220\'20\'1Cpartnership\u8221\'20\'1D remained unknown to them.\par \par \uc2 At this time, we cannot say whether the \u8220\'20\'1Cplanned partnership\u8221\'20\'1D described in Friday\u8217\'20\'19s message on Truth Social or news reports since then represents any meaningful change from the merger proposed in 2023, under which \uc2 Nippon Steel\uc2  would acquire \uc2 U.S. Steel\uc2  and make it a wholly owned subsidiary.\par \par \uc2 Throughout recent months, as the public conversation has turned to Nippon \u8220\'20\'1Cinvesting\u8221\'20\'1D in \uc2 U.S. Steel\uc2  or \u8220\'20\'1Cpartnering with\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 U.S. Steel\uc2 , Nippon has maintained consistently that it would only invest in \uc2 U.S. Steel\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s facilities if it owned the company outright. We\u8217\'20\'19ve seen nothing in the reporting over the past few days suggesting that Nippon has walked back from this position.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-30T22:00:16.264Z">at 11.00pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-30T20:41:01.841Z">9.41pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Trump says he fired the first female director of the National Portrait Gallery\par \par \uc2 With {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://truthsocial.com/@realDonaldTrump/posts/114597966895334541"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a post}}}\uc2  on his social media platform, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  announced on Friday that he was firing Kim Sajet, the first female director of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.si.edu/museums/portrait-gallery"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the National Portrait Gallery}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Trump accused Sajet, who was born in Nigeria, raised in Australia and is a citizen of the Netherlands, of being \u8220\'20\'1Ca strong supporter of DEI\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Chighly partisan\u8221\'20\'1D. He cited no evidence for either claim.\par \par \uc2 Legal experts, including Eric Columbus, a former litigator for the January 6 select committee, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://bsky.app/profile/ericcolumbus.bsky.social/post/3lqfzpcmze22g"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 suggested}}}\uc2  Trump does not have the power to fire Sajet, since the gallery is part of the Smithsonian, which is not run by the executive branch.\par \par \uc2 As our colleague David Smith wrote in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/artanddesign/ng-interactive/2024/dec/31/kim-sajet-national-portrait-gallery-washington"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a profile of Sajet}}}\uc2 , after she arrived in the US with her family in 1997, she held positions at the \uc2 Philadelphia Museum of Art\uc2 , the Pennsylvania Academy of the Fine Arts and the Historical Society of Pennsylvania before she {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/story/2013/02/kim-sajet-named-us-portrait-gallery-chief-087204"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was appointed director}}}\uc2  of the National Portrait Gallery in 2013.\par \par \uc2 Sajet said the gallery tries \u8220\'20\'1Cvery hard to be even-handed when we talk about people and that\u8217\'20\'19s the key. Everyone has an opinion about American presidents, good, bad and indifferent. We hear it all but generally I think we\u8217\'20\'19ve done pretty well.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A description of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in the gallery of American presidents includes this text: \u8220\'20\'1CImpeached twice, on charges of abuse of power and incitement of insurrection after supporters attacked the US Capitol on January 6, 2021, he was acquitted by the Senate in both trials. After losing to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in 2020, Trump mounted a historic comeback in the 2024 election. He is the only president aside from Grover Cleveland (1837-1908) to have won a nonconsecutive second term.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-31T00:00:13.035Z">at 1.00am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-30T20:02:58.150Z">9.02pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18My stomach just dropped\u8217\'20\'19: foreign students in panicked limbo as Trump cancels visa interviews\par \par \uc2 Students around the world who were gearing up to study in the United States this fall face growing uncertainty after the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/trump-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump administration}}}\uc2  temporarily halted student visa appointments this week.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, a state department directive ordered US embassies globally to immediately stop scheduling {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/27/international-student-visa-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 visa interviews}}}\uc2  for foreign students while it prepares to implement expanded {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/social-media"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 social media}}}\uc2  screening for all international visa applicants.\par \par \uc2 While interview {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/world/us/trump-administration-halts-scheduling-new-student-visa-appointments-2025-05-27/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appointments}}}\uc2  that were already scheduled can proceed, the announcement sparked panic among students who have yet to secure interviews. Students who spoke with the Guardian expressed anxiety over delays in visa processing that could jeopardize scholarships, on-campus housing, their ability to start classes on time \u8211\'20\'13 and their very academic futures.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy stomach just dropped,\u8221\'20\'1D said Oliver Cropley, 27, a student at the \uc2 University of East Anglia\uc2  in the UK, who is meant to attend the \uc2 University of Kansas\uc2  beginning this August for a year abroad.\par \par \uc2 The directive came amid a series of recent policy shifts targeting international students at US universities. This week, the Trump administration issued new measures targeting Chinese students, announcing it would focus on the visas of those studying in \u8220\'20\'1C{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/29/us-revoke-chinese-student-visas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 critical fields}}}\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D and of students with ties to the Chinese Communist party, and implement heightened scrutiny for all future applicants from China and Hong Kong.\par \par \uc2 Last week, the \uc2 Department of Homeland Security\uc2  said it would immediately ban \uc2 Harvard University\uc2  from enrolling international students, forcing the university\u8217\'20\'19s international student body to either transfer or leave the country. A federal judge {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/29/trump-harvard-international-students"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 blocked that effort on Thursday}}}\uc2 , but its long-term outcome remains uncertain.\par \par \uc2 The changes have left many international students who are planning to come to the US for the 2025-2026 academic year scrambling and in limbo.\par \par \uc2 Cropley said that he paid all of the application fees for the US visa including the last administrative fee last week to schedule his visa interview, but he has been unable to schedule it or reach anyone at the US embassy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt has demoralized me,\u8221\'20\'1D Cropley said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a stressful enough process, and then to get this sort of knockback at this stage \u8230\'20\'26 I\u8217\'20\'19m supposed to be there on August 4.\u8221\'20\'1D <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/30/trump-international-students-visas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18My stomach just dropped\u8217\'20\'19: foreign students in panicked limbo as Trump cancels visa interviews}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-30T19:32:07.574Z">8.32pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Key takeaways from Trump-Musk press conference\par \par \uc2 Despite brief tangents about {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2025/may/30/donald-trump-tariffs-elon-musk-us-politics-live-news-updates?CMP=share_btn_url&page=with%3Ablock-6839fcfc8f088b2f036eb66f#block-6839fcfc8f088b2f036eb66f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 black eyes}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2025/may/30/donald-trump-tariffs-elon-musk-us-politics-live-news-updates?CMP=share_btn_url&page=with%3Ablock-6839f6688f088b2f036eb63d#block-6839f6688f088b2f036eb63d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 gold ceilings}}}\uc2  and autopens, that meeting basically consisted of Trump showering Musk with praise as his turbulent tenure at Doge comes to an end, at least officially. \u8220\'20\'1CElon\u8217\'20\'19s service to America is without comparison in modern history,\u8221\'20\'1D said Trump from behind the Resolute Desk, in a show of unity with the world\u8217\'20\'19s richest person, who stood to his right in a black Doge hat and \u8220\'20\'1CDogefather\u8221\'20\'1D T-shirt. \u8220\'20\'1CElon has worked tirelessly helping lead the most sweeping and consequential government reform program in generations,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said, adding that Musk had delivered a \u8220\'20\'1Ccolossal change\u8221\'20\'1D in how Washington does things.\par \par \uc2 But despite the fanfare, both men said that Musk isn\u8217\'20\'19t really going anywhere. He will continue to be \u8220\'20\'1Ca friend and adviser\u8221\'20\'1D to the president and will still be \u8220\'20\'1Cback and forth\u8221\'20\'1D to the White House, Musk said, with \u8220\'20\'1Cmost\u8221\'20\'1D Doge workers \u8220\'20\'1Cstaying on\u8221\'20\'1D to continue its work to cut \u8220\'20\'1Cwasteful\u8221\'20\'1D federal spending. As if anyone needed reminding, in the last 130 days Doge under Musk has caused chaos as it haphazardly eliminated thousands of jobs and billions of dollars in contracts \u8211\'20\'13 all without actually saving the country very much at all. Acknowledging that Doge had failed to deliver the $1tn savings promised, Musk defended his efforts and insisted he was confident it would get to that number \u8220\'20\'1Cin time\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The two glossed over questions pertaining to Musk\u8217\'20\'19s criticisms of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cbig, beautiful\u8221\'20\'1D tax bill, which will add massively to the national deficit and undermine Doge\u8217\'20\'19s mission to cut spending (though Trump did say {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2025/may/30/donald-trump-tariffs-elon-musk-us-politics-live-news-updates?CMP=share_btn_url&page=with%3Ablock-6839fbcc8f086f6030084c9c#block-6839fbcc8f086f6030084c9c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he wants to see bigger tax cuts}}}\uc2  in the bill), and to Musk\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/30/elon-musk-trump-drug-use"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 alleged intense drug use}}}\uc2  over the course of his chaotic tenure in the White House. They focused instead on previously {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2025/may/30/donald-trump-tariffs-elon-musk-us-politics-live-news-updates?CMP=share_btn_url&page=with%3Ablock-6839f59a8f085984c7367272#block-6839f59a8f085984c7367272"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 debunked}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2025/may/30/donald-trump-tariffs-elon-musk-us-politics-live-news-updates?CMP=share_btn_url&page=with%3Ablock-6839f4e08f086f6030084c43#block-6839f4e08f086f6030084c43"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 claims}}}\uc2  about Doge\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cachievements\u8221\'20\'1D, with the president saying his government plans to make many of Doge\u8217\'20\'19s cuts permanent, while the billionaire declared: \u8220\'20\'1CThis isn\u8217\'20\'19t the end of Doge, it\u8217\'20\'19s more the beginning \u8230\'20\'26 It\u8217\'20\'19s a way of life.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-31T04:50:49.148Z">at 5.50am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-30T19:01:18.934Z">8.01pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Trump says he had a \u8220\'20\'1Cgood meeting\u8221\'20\'1D with Federal Reserve chair \uc2 Jerome Powell\uc2 , in a hurried response as reporters are ushered out of the room.\par \par \uc2 And that\u8217\'20\'19s it, the briefing is over. I\u8217\'20\'19ll post a short summary soon.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-30T18:58:58.854Z">7.58pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  dodged a question about a New York Times {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2025/05/30/us/elon-musk-drugs-children-trump.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report}}}\uc2  published this morning about his alleged drug use while serving as one of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s closest advisers.\par \par \uc2 According to the report, Musk was using drugs far more intensely than previously known, regularly consuming ketamine, ecstasy and psychedelic mushrooms during his rise to political prominence.\par \par \uc2 His use of ketamine was so heavy that he told people it caused bladder problems, the report says. Sources told the paper that he had a serious ketamine habit, consuming the powerful anesthetic sometimes daily rather than the \u8220\'20\'1Csmall amount\u8221\'20\'1D taken \u8220\'20\'1Cabout once every two weeks\u8221\'20\'1D he claimed in interviews. <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/30/elon-musk-trump-drug-use"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Elon Musk allegedly took large amounts of drugs including ketamine while advising Trump \u8211\'20\'13 report}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-30T19:00:40.869Z">at 8.00pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-30T18:53:46.096Z">7.53pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Trump says both \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  and \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2  are stubborn as he tries to negotiate an end to the war in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Asked if he believes Putin is stubborn, Trump says he was surprised and disappointed by Russian bombing in Ukraine while he was trying to arrange a ceasefire.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-30T19:55:05.238Z">at 8.55pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-30T18:51:37.872Z">7.51pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Trump says he still wants foreign students to attend US colleges despite his fight with Harvard over how many students it enrolls from outside the country.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-30T19:55:25.083Z">at 8.55pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-30T18:49:39.702Z">7.49pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Musk says his bruised eye was caused by 'horsing around' with his son\par \par \uc2 Asked about his black eye, Musk claims he was punched in the face by his five-year-old son while they were \u8220\'20\'1Chorsing around\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-30T18:59:40.033Z">at 7.59pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-30T18:42:16.548Z">7.42pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Trump wants to see bigger tax cuts in the budget bill\par \par \uc2 Trump says he wants to see bigger tax cuts in the budget bill (which passed the House {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/22/house-vote-trump-tax-bill"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 by the skin of its teeth}}}\uc2 ).\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19d like to see a bigger cut in taxes,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump says. \u8220\'20\'1C The bill is a great bill. It\u8217\'20\'19s going to be jiggered around a little bit, it\u8217\'20\'19s going to be negotiated with the Senate.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Musk was also asked to chime in by the reporter about what changes he wants to see (following his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2025/may/28/trump-tax-bill-weakens-doge-cost-cutting-efforts-elon-musk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 criticisms}}}\uc2  this week) but Trump moves on.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-30T18:44:58.566Z">at 7.44pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-30T18:41:11.636Z">7.41pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Fact check: Trump claims Musk\u8217\'20\'19s Doge uncovered the Biden administration \u8220\'20\'1Cspent $8m on making mice transgender\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Trump made this claim during his address to Congress in March, and it\u8217\'20\'19s unclear where he got this figure from.\par \par \uc2 Multiple outlets have suggested that he was referring to health studies that involve \u8220\'20\'1Ctransgenic\u8221\'20\'1D mice, which are lab research mice that have been genetically modified to better model human disease response.\par \par \uc2 The White House released a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/articles/2025/03/yes-biden-spent-millions-on-transgender-animal-experiments/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement}}}\uc2  after Trump\u8217\'20\'19s initial comments in March that referenced studies on the effects of hormone therapy. None of the studies listed were specifically focused on \u8220\'20\'1Cmaking mice transgender\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-30T18:40:02.538Z">7.40pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Trump on Macron being shoved in face by his wife: 'make sure the door remains closed'\par \par \uc2 Trump says his advice for French president \uc2 Emmanuel Macron\uc2 , who has been shown on a video through an open plane door being pushed in the face by his wife, was \u8220\'20\'1Cmake sure the door remains closed\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Trump says he had spoken to Macron in the wake of the video that showed his wife, Brigitte, giving him a shove on their plane.\par \par \uc2 Macron has shrugged off the incident as a moment of playfulness. \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s fine,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump says.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-30T19:30:47.224Z">at 8.30pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-30T18:36:22.206Z">7.36pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Asked if he would consider pardoning {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/music/diddy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Diddy}}}\uc2 , Trump says nobody has asked him to, but: \u8220\'20\'1CI know people are thinking about it \u8230\'20\'26 I think people have been very close to asking.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI would look at the facts,\u8221\'20\'1D he adds.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-30T18:36:31.505Z">at 7.36pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-30T18:27:40.123Z">7.27pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Trump cites previously debunked claim in list of Musk's achievements\par \par \uc2 In support of his claim that \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  helped identify and cut wasteful government spending, Trump just cited the cutting of what he called \u8220\'20\'1C$45m for diversity, equity and inclusion scholarships in Burma\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn Burma\u8221\'20\'1D, the president added. \u8220\'20\'1CDoes anyone know about Burma?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 As we {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2025/mar/05/trump-congress-speech-address-latest-updates?page=with%3Ablock-67c7c1aa8f08806c689201d2#block-67c7c1aa8f08806c689201d2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 first reported in February}}}\uc2 , there is no evidence that any such scholarships were ever planned. As the former representative \uc2 Tom Malinowski{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/Malinowski/status/1884733902620668363"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pointed out}}}\uc2 , when this claim was first made by Musk\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cdepartment of government efficiency\u8221\'20\'1D, this appears to be a reference to a very kind of different program, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.iie.org/programs/usaid-lincoln-scholarship-program/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 USAid Lincoln Scholarships}}}\uc2 , which helped educate young people struggling for freedom against Burma\u8217\'20\'19s military dictatorship.\par \par \uc2 It is not clear why Trump or Musk wrongly thought that these were scholarships aimed at promoting \u8220\'20\'1Cdiversity, equity and inclusion\u8221\'20\'1D, but, as Malinowski noted, the \uc2 USAid\uc2  project description did specify that the scholars were Burmese students \u8220\'20\'1Cfrom diverse backgrounds\u8221\'20\'1D. In the context of that country, where a military dictatorship has exploited ethnic and religious divisions to stay in power, helping to educate young leaders from all of the country\u8217\'20\'19s ethnic groups seems like sound policy.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-30T18:27:28.554Z">7.27pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Fact check: Trump's claim about hotels housing migrants in New York\par \par \uc2 Fact check: Trump claims that \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Doge \u8220\'20\'1Ccancelled $59m for illegal alien hotel rooms in New York City\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Musk claimed in February that his team had discovered the \uc2 Federal Emergency Management Agency\uc2  (Fema) had sent $59m to \u8220\'20\'1Cluxury hotels\u8221\'20\'1D in New York City to house illegal migrants. He claimed the money had been \u8220\'20\'1Cmeant for American disaster relief\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Musk gave no evidence to support this claim. Multiple outlets have reported that the money was appropriated by Congress and allocated to the city \u8211\'20\'13 not directly to the hotels \u8211\'20\'13 last year by Fema.\par \par \uc2 Musk\u8217\'20\'19s claim likely referred to payments made by the Shelter and Services Program, which gives money to reimburse cities, towns or organizations for immigration-related expenses, according to Associated Press.\par \par \uc2 A New York City office spokesperson told the news agency that only some of the $59m was for hotel costs, and that the city has never paid luxury rates.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-30T18:35:05.177Z">at 7.35pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-30T18:27:22.809Z">7.27pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Musk again says he expects to continue to provide Trump with advice, to which Trump says: \u8220\'20\'1CI hope so.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-30T18:26:26.224Z">7.26pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Trump says he feels they\u8217\'20\'19re \u8220\'20\'1Cvery close\u8221\'20\'1D to an agreement on Gaza, and feels he\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cfairly close\u8221\'20\'1D to a deal with Iran also.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-30T19:58:01.646Z">at 8.58pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-30T18:25:06.300Z">7.25pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Trump says he's sure he will speak to China's Xi Jinping to hopefully work out trade dispute\par \par \uc2 Trump repeats his claim that China \u8220\'20\'1Cviolated a big part of\u8221\'20\'1D the agreement they made, but he doesn\u8217\'20\'19t expand on what he\u8217\'20\'19s alleging China did.\par \par \uc2 He says he\u8217\'20\'19s sure he\u8217\'20\'19ll speak to the Chinese president to work it out.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-30T19:58:27.461Z">at 8.58pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-30T18:20:40.962Z">7.20pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Musk dodges question about reported drug-taking\par \par \uc2 Musk was about to be asked about the \uc2 NYT\uc2  report that he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/30/elon-musk-trump-drug-use"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 allegedly took large amounts of drugs}}}\uc2  including ketamine while advising Trump, but he cuts the reporter off and dodges the incoming question entirely.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-30T18:34:32.324Z">at 7.34pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-30T18:18:50.524Z">7.18pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Musk says he\u8217\'20\'19ll continue visiting the White House as a \u8220\'20\'1Cfriend and adviser to the president\u8221\'20\'1D, before veering off to compliment the \u8220\'20\'1Cstunning\u8221\'20\'1D Oval Office, in particular \u8220\'20\'1Cthe gold on the ceiling\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-30T18:22:22.534Z">at 7.22pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-30T18:17:48.529Z">7.17pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Musk says his time as special government employee had to end, but this isn\u8217\'20\'19t the end of Doge, it\u8217\'20\'19s more the beginning, he says, adding: \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a way of life.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He says he\u8217\'20\'19s confident that \u8220\'20\'1Cover time\u8221\'20\'1D that Doge will reach $1tn of savings he promised (in the last 130 days it hasn\u8217\'20\'19t come close).\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-30T18:22:53.656Z">at 7.22pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-30T18:11:32.634Z">7.11pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CElon\u8217\'20\'19s service to America is without comparison in modern history\u8221\'20\'1D, says Trump, continuing to pile on the praise.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-30T18:10:49.628Z">7.10pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Trump says Musk will 'be back and forth' with most Doge staffers 'staying on'\par \par \uc2 Most of the Doge people are staying on, says Trump.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CElon\u8217\'20\'19s not really leaving,\u8221\'20\'1D says Trump, adding: \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s going to be back and forth, I think, I have a feeling. [Doge is] his baby.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-30T18:16:34.276Z">at 7.16pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-30T18:09:28.961Z">7.09pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Some of these cuts will be in the \u8220\'20\'1Cbig, beautiful bill\u8221\'20\'1D, Trump says (the same bill Musk that has criticised for undermining Doge\u8217\'20\'19s work).\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-30T18:08:40.733Z">7.08pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Trump says he\u8217\'20\'19s committed to making Doge\u8217\'20\'19s cuts permanent.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-30T18:07:01.828Z">7.07pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ll remember you,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump tells Musk when, he claims, his administration announces in the future that \u8220\'20\'1Cbillions of dollars\u8221\'20\'1D in waste, fraud and abuse in federal contracts has been eliminated.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-30T18:08:07.266Z">at 7.08pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-30T18:03:06.639Z">7.03pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Musk has delivered a \u8220\'20\'1Ccolossal change\u8221\'20\'1D in how Washington does things, Trump says.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-30T18:01:45.607Z">7.01pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Musk has \u8220\'20\'1Cworked tirelessly\u8221\'20\'1D, says Trump, to help lead \u8220\'20\'1Cthe most sweeping and consequential government reform program in generations\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-30T18:00:41.775Z">7.00pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 If you\u8217\'20\'19d like to follow along this press conference, there is a feed at the top of the blog.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-30T17:57:58.682Z">6.57pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 And here comes Trump and Musk from the Oval Office, with Musk sporting his \u8220\'20\'1CDogefather\u8221\'20\'1D t-shirt and black \u8220\'20\'1CDOGE\u8221\'20\'1D hat.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-30T18:02:22.176Z">at 7.02pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-30T17:49:04.201Z">6.49pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 State department ramps up Trump anti-immigration agenda with new \u8216\'20\'18remigration\u8217\'20\'19 office\par \par \uc2 The state department is seeking to create an \u8220\'20\'1COffice of Remigration\u8221\'20\'1D as part of a restructuring of the US diplomatic service to facilitate \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s rightwing anti-immigration policies.\par \par \uc2 The plan would in effect repurpose the Bureau of Population, Refugees, and Migration (PRM), which sought to manage and facilitate the flow of people into the US under previous administrations, into a bureau meant to help deport immigrants from the country.\par \par \uc2 A congressional notification from the state department obtained by the Guardian said the office would be involved in \u8220\'20\'1Crepatriation tracking\u8221\'20\'1D, would \u8220\'20\'1Cactively facilitate\u8221\'20\'1D the \u8220\'20\'1Cvoluntary return of migrants\u8221\'20\'1D to other countries, and would work with the \uc2 Department of Homeland Security\uc2  and other law enforcement to \u8220\'20\'1Cadvance the president\u8217\'20\'19s immigration agenda\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CReflecting core administration priorities, these offices will be substantially reorganized to shift focus towards supporting the administration\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to return illegal aliens to their country of origin or legal status,\u8221\'20\'1D the document read.\par \par \uc2 The overhaul is part of a broader restructuring of the state department under its secretary, \uc2 Marco Rubio\uc2  , to create a \u8220\'20\'1Cmore agile department, better equipped to promote America\u8217\'20\'19s interests and keep Americans safe across the world\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Under the plan, which was submitted to Congress this week, the state department would eliminate or consolidate more than 300 offices and bureaus, leading to the firing, or \u8220\'20\'1Creduction in force\u8221\'20\'1D, of more than 3,400 employees.\par \par \uc2 The firings would not target members of consular affairs or law enforcement and other key roles of state. <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/30/state-department-plans-office-of-remigration-to-support-trump-agenda"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 State department ramps up Trump anti-immigration agenda with new \u8216\'20\'18remigration\u8217\'20\'19 office}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-30T17:46:16.265Z">6.46pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 In California , the conservative enclaves of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/08/shasta-county-elections-redding-far-right-voting-covid"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Shasta County}}}\uc2  in the north and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/07/huntington-beach-california-voter-id-pride-flag"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Huntington Beach}}}\uc2  in the south have frequently sought to distance themselves from the liberal policies of the deeply Democratic state. Both jurisdictions have passed resolutions expressing their opposition to sanctuary policies \u8211\'20\'13 rejecting California law, which limits cooperation with federal immigration officials (although Shasta has previously {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.shastacounty.gov/media/25426#:~:text=2023%2D079%20which%20supports%20the,various%20ethnic%2C%20religious%2C%20and%20political"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 voted}}}\uc2  to declare itself a \u8220\'20\'1Csecond amendment sanctuary\u8221\'20\'1D).\par \par \uc2 Yet this week Shasta county and Huntington Beach found themselves on a list produced by the Trump administration identifying them as sanctuary jurisdictions that \u8220\'20\'1Cundermine the rule of law and endanger the lives of Americans and law enforcement\u8221\'20\'1D. Nearly every county in California was included, even those such as Shasta, which passed an anti-sanctuary resolution {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://krcrtv.com/news/local/shasta-county-supervisors-pass-resolution-blocking-sanctuary-for-non-citizen-migrants"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 last year}}}\uc2 , and Amador where the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://calmatters.org/justice/2025/02/sanctuary-state-amador-sheriff/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sheriff}}}\uc2  has said he would cooperate with immigration authorities. Huntington Beach found itself on the list even though the city council voted to identify the community as a non-sanctuary city.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe went out of our way to declare non-sanctuary status,\u8221\'20\'1D Pat Burns, the city\u8217\'20\'19s mayor, told the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://voiceofoc.org/2025/05/how-did-ocs-most-maga-city-council-end-up-on-trumps-sanctuary-city-list/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Voice of OC}}}\uc2 . He described Huntington Beach\u8217\'20\'19s inclusion as a \u8220\'20\'1Cmisprint\u8221\'20\'1D or \u8220\'20\'1Cgrave error\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The Department for Homeland Security said in a statement that it would notify each jurisdiction of its \u8220\'20\'1Cnon-compliance with federal statutes\u8221\'20\'1D and demand they immediately change their policies. It also noted the list can be \u8220\'20\'1Creviewed and changed at any time\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-30T17:27:52.020Z">6.27pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Biden "optimistic" on cancer diagnoses, proud of record\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  spoke with reporters after giving {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2025/may/30/donald-trump-tariffs-elon-musk-us-politics-live-news-updates?page=with%3Ablock-6839d1118f088b2f036eb401#block-6839d1118f088b2f036eb401"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 his first speech}}}\uc2  since being diagnosed with prostate cancer earlier this month.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAll the folks are very optimistic\u8230\'20\'26the expectation is we are going to be able to beat this,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Biden {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/18/joe-biden-prostate-cancer-diagnosis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has been diagnosed}}}\uc2  with an \u8220\'20\'1Caggressive form\u8221\'20\'1D of prostate cancer that has spread to his bones.\par \par \uc2 Moments ago, speaking at a memorial event in Delaware, the former US president said he was already undergoing treatment, which he said currently consisted of \u8220\'20\'1Cone particular pill\u8221\'20\'1D a day.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s not in any organs, my bones are strong,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. He also said he was under the care of a world class surgeon who had himself beat prostate cancer three decades ago.\par \par \uc2 He didn\u8217\'20\'19t mention \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  but said that the US is at \u8220\'20\'1Ca really difficult moment, not just Americans, the world\u8221\'20\'1D and that America is at \u8220\'20\'1Can inflection point where the decisions we make in the next little bit are going to determine what things look like for the next 20 years.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden also said: \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m very proud. I\u8217\'20\'19ll put my record as president against any president at all.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-30T17:24:47.179Z">6.24pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to give joint press conference\par \par \uc2 In about five minutes, \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  are to give a joint press conference from the Oval Office to mark the last of Musk\u8217\'20\'19s turbulent 130 days leading Doge as a special government employee.\par \par \uc2 He leaves without saving the federal government much money but he has succeeded in upending the lives of millions around the world from the resulting chaos of his haphazardly detrimental cuts to federal funding, as well as taking a chainsaw to his own international reputation.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis will be his last day, but not really, because he will, always, be with us, helping all the way,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://url4027.email.politico.com/ss/c/u001.tZBh-UKX-I3yMqqHCXLb8yfOydSt7swN-GhaAPY3eIN9MnYXvDYGv-VD-Gll-KXMHdwK-_MMLHOg0TIgbhQ7slZSUvhP5jTyIOVyT6hFoOw/4gx/J2QIX8qcQ6iLA4D93Non2A/h16/h001.5tcSKZef9wWJmRuz4jhwCjd7dTHrZx7C4CxUZsnOVbc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 posted on Truth Social}}}\uc2  yesterday in what is no doubt an attempt at unity amid rumours of a rift between the two men, in particular over Musk\u8217\'20\'19s criticisms of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cbig, beautiful\u8221\'20\'1D tax bill and his private opposition to the president\u8217\'20\'19s tariffs regime.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s sure to be interesting, we\u8217\'20\'19ll bring you any key news lines here.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-30T17:30:12.213Z">at 6.30pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-30T16:42:01.528Z">5.42pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Golden Dome missile defense program won\u8217\'20\'19t be done by end of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s term\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s so-called Golden Dome missile defense program \u8211\'20\'13 which will feature space-based weapons to intercept strikes against the US \u8211\'20\'13 is not expected to be ready before the end of his term, despite his prediction that it would be completed within the next three years.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/20/trump-appoints-michael-guetlin-golden-dome"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 In the Oval Office last week}}}\uc2 , when he announced that the US space force would oversee the project under Gen Michael Guetlein , the president said he was confident that it would be \u8220\'20\'1Cfully operational\u8221\'20\'1D before he left office.\par \par \uc2 But the implementation plan for the Golden Dome produced by the Pentagon, as described by two people familiar with the matter, envisions having the defense weapons being ready only for a demonstration and under perfect conditions by the end of 2028.\par \par \uc2 The Golden Dome program is effectively becoming operational in phases as opposed to it coming online all at once. Initially, the Pentagon is set to focus on integrating data systems before developing space-based weapons later, the people said.\par \par \uc2 What might be possible in 18 months is for the US to have the foundations of a fully operational Golden Dome, where a military network of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://media.defense.gov/2022/Mar/17/2002958406/-1/-1/1/SUMMARY-OF-THE-JOINT-ALL-DOMAIN-COMMAND-AND-CONTROL-STRATEGY.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 satellites and space-based communication systems}}}\uc2  could track hundreds of inbound missiles towards the US.\par \par \uc2 There would be no capability to take out the missiles using space-based weapons at that stage. The US has roughly 40 Patriot defense batteries in Alaska and California that could be used to kill potential intercontinental ballistic missiles.\par \par \uc2 By the end of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s term, instead, the Pentagon could have the network of space-based sensors and communications, and attempt to integrate it with untested space-based weapons to shoot them down.\par \par \uc2 The space-based network is likely to rely heavily on \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 SpaceX\uc2 , which has been developing a next-generation tracking system known as the \u8220\'20\'1Caerial moving target identifier\u8221\'20\'1D. The defense department acquired the first prototypes last year during the Biden administration.\par \par \uc2 But the flagship concept for Golden Dome, to identify and kill ballistic missiles in the first 30 seconds to two minutes of launch when their heat signature is greatest \u8211\'20\'13 known as \u8220\'20\'1Cboost phase\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 is not expected to be ready.\par \par \uc2 That {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://spacenews.com/booz-allen-unveils-brilliant-swarms-satellite-concept-for-missile-defense/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 technology remains in development}}}\uc2  and it may not be feasible for years for a counter-missile launched from space to cut through Earth\u8217\'20\'19s atmosphere with enough force to eliminate a ballistic missile, the people said. <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/30/trump-golden-dome-missile-defense"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Golden Dome missile defense program won\u8217\'20\'19t be done by end of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s term}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-30T16:36:09.498Z">5.36pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  allegedly took large amounts of drugs including ketamine while advising Trump \u8211\'20\'13 NYT\par \par \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  engaged in extensive drug consumption while serving as one of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s closest advisers, taking {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2025/jan/13/ketamine-move-club-to-chill-out-drug-troubling-culture-shift"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ketamine}}}\uc2  so frequently it caused bladder problems and traveling with a daily supply of approximately 20 pills, an investigation from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2025/05/30/us/elon-musk-drugs-children-trump.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the New York Times}}}\uc2  (paywall) has revealed.\par \par \uc2 The world\u8217\'20\'19s richest man regularly consumed ketamine, ecstasy and psychedelic mushrooms during his rise to political prominence, anonymous sources familiar with his activities told the Times. His drug use {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2025/05/30/us/elon-musk-drugs-children-trump.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reportedly}}}\uc2  intensified as he donated $275m to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s presidential campaign and later wielded significant power through his role spearheading the \u8220\'20\'1Cdepartment of government efficiency\u8221\'20\'1D, or Doge .\par \par \uc2 Musk announced his departure from government service on Wednesday evening, months after exhibiting erratic behavior including insulting cabinet members and making a Nazi-like salute at a political rally.\par \par \uc2 The Doge leader developed what sources described to the Times as a serious ketamine habit, consuming the powerful anesthetic sometimes daily rather than the \u8220\'20\'1Csmall amount\u8221\'20\'1D taken \u8220\'20\'1Cabout once every two weeks\u8221\'20\'1D he claimed in interviews. \u8220\'20\'1CIf you\u8217\'20\'19ve used too much ketamine, you can\u8217\'20\'19t really get work done, and I have a lot of work,\u8221\'20\'1D Musk previously told journalist Don Lemon in March 2024, downplaying his consumption.\par \par \uc2 However, by spring last year, the Times reports that Musk was telling associates his ketamine use was affecting his bladder \u8211\'20\'13 a known consequence of chronic abuse of the drug, which has psychedelic properties and can cause dissociation from reality, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dea.gov/factsheets/ketamine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to the DEA}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 His regular medication box contained pills bearing Adderall markings alongside other substances, according to sources with the Times who have seen photographs of the container.\par \par \uc2 It remains unclear whether Musk was under the influence during his time at the White House, where he attended sensitive meetings with foreign leaders and held power over federal spending cuts.\par \par \uc2 The White House did not return a request for comment on whether Musk underwent drug testing despite his access to classified information. <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/30/elon-musk-trump-drug-use"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Elon Musk allegedly took large amounts of drugs including ketamine while advising Trump \u8211\'20\'13 report}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-30T16:10:42.979Z">5.10pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 White House says US considering other actions on China amid trade spat\par \par \uc2 The Trump administration is preparing to take other actions targeting China , the White House deputy chief of staff for policy has said following \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s accusation that Beijing had \u8220\'20\'1Ctotally violated\u8221\'20\'1D its preliminary trade agreement with the US.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat opens up all manner of action for the United States to ensure future compliance,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Stephen Miller\uc2  told reporters.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere are measures that have already been taken, there are measures that are being taken, there are measures that are being considered,\u8221\'20\'1D he said separately on CNN. \u8220\'20\'1CIt would be incredibly unwise for China to continue down this path and not seek instead the path of cooperation.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s been a few hours since Trump\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2025/may/30/donald-trump-tariffs-elon-musk-us-politics-live-news-updates?CMP=share_btn_url&page=with%3Ablock-6839a1b98f085984c7366ce1#block-6839a1b98f085984c7366ce1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 post on Truth Social}}}\uc2  but he\u8217\'20\'19s yet to explain the action taken by China that has allegedly violated the agreement, but a US official told Reuters that it appears China was moving slowly on promises to issue export licenses for rare earths minerals.\par \par \uc2 The Geneva agreement called for China to lift trade countermeasures that restrict its exports of the critical metals needed for US semiconductor, electronics and defense production.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s trade representative Jamieson Greer also said this morning that critical minerals was one area of particular concern. He told CNBC earlier:\par \par \uc2 We haven\u8217\'20\'19t seen the flow of some of those critical minerals as they were supposed to be doing \u8230\'20\'26 China continues to, you know, slow down and choke off things like critical minerals and rare earth magnets.\par \par \uc2 It follows comments from treasury secretary Scott Bessent yesterday stating that trade talks between the US and China {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/30/trump-china-tariffs-trade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 were \u8220\'20\'1Ca bit stalled\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  and getting a deal over the finish line will likely need the direct involvement of Trump and Chinese president Xi Jinping .\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-30T16:54:33.763Z">at 5.54pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-30T16:03:45.585Z">5.03pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Max Planck Society , one of Europe\u8217\'20\'19s leading research bodies, has seen a threefold surge in applications from US researchers following the Trump administration\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/27/trump-harvard-federal-contracts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 attacks on higher education}}}\uc2  in the US, Reuters reported.\par \par \uc2 The German state-backed network of research centers received over triple the amount of applications from the US this spring compared to last year in its latest call for early-career scientists looking to set up their own research labs.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat\u8217\'20\'19s interesting is the number of applications from other parts of the world remained constant,\u8221\'20\'1D Patrick Cramer, president of the Max Planck Society, told Reuters. \u8220\'20\'1CIf you look at which institutions these applications are coming from, you see almost half are concentrated at five institutions: Harvard, Stanford, MIT, the \uc2 National Institutes of Health\uc2  and the University of California.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The flood of applicants comes at a time of concern over a potential American \u8220\'20\'1C{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2025/mar/24/french-university-scientific-asylum-american-talent-brain-drain"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 brain drain}}}\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D where scientists and researchers in the US are considering leaving the country to pursue foreign research opportunities.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-30T15:52:55.509Z">4.52pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Biden urges defense of democracy, in first speech since cancer reveal\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  just gave a speech in Delaware, his first since he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/18/joe-biden-prostate-cancer-diagnosis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was diagnosed}}}\uc2  earlier this month with an aggressive form of prostate cancer that has spread to his bones.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/joebiden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 former president}}}\uc2  was commemorating fallen members of the military, in a week that began with the Memorial Day holiday that is traditionally dedicated to remembering those killed in service. He drew a direct line between their sacrifice and what Americans need to do now.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey are not asking us to risk our lives, they are asking us to stay true to what America stands for. They are not asking us to do their jobs, they are asking us do our jobs - to protect our nation, in our time, now, to defend democracy.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden, a Democrat, did not mention his successor, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  , and the Republican president\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/26/trump-memorial-day-speech"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 self-referential}}}\uc2  Memorial Day address or his thrust to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2025/may/27/a-hidden-measure-in-the-republican-budget-bill-would-crown-trump-king"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 expand}}}\uc2  his presidential power in what critics say is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2025/may/28/trump-defy-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a threat}}}\uc2  to the rule of law and US democracy, but he did not need to.\par \par \uc2 Biden also did not refer to his cancer or any treatment. He sounded vigorous and impassioned. He delivered the speech in New Castle as his family also marked the 10-year anniversary of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2015/may/31/beau-biden-dies-of-brain-cancer"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 death of his son}}}\uc2  Beau , from brain cancer at the age of 46.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-30T15:41:00.932Z">4.41pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 The Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2  (CDC) has removed language that says healthy children should get COVID vaccines. The public health agency has posted new recommendations that healthy children may, but no longer should, get COVID-19 shots, the Associated Press reported.\par \par \uc2 The change comes days after US health secretary Robert F. Kennedy Jr. announced that COVID-19 vaccines will no longer be recommended for healthy children and pregnant women, though the CDC website did not appear to substantially change recommendations for pregnant women.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-30T15:19:53.053Z">4.19pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 The US has cut awards to 24 green energy projects , including to an \uc2 Exxon\uc2  refinery complex in Texas issued during former President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s administration that totaled more than $3.7 billion, the Energy Department confirmed on Friday to Reuters.\par \par \uc2 The Trump administration has said it is \u8220\'20\'1Creevaluating\u8221\'20\'1D publicly-funded awards and loans issued to emerging technology projects during Biden\u8217\'20\'19s administration. The administration has so far dismantled several of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s policies on climate and clean energy while pursuing a very pro-oil agenda.\par \par \uc2 The Office of Clean Energy Demonstration awards the department axed include nearly $332 million to a project at \uc2 Exxon Mobil\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Baytown, Texas refinery complex, $500 million to \uc2 Heidelberg Materials\uc2 , US in Louisiana, and $375 million to \uc2 Eastman Chemical Company\uc2  in Longview, Texas.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-30T15:01:04.722Z">4.01pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 In another case, the supreme court on 19 May also allowed the Trump administration to end a deportation protection called temporary protected status that had been granted by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  to about 350,000 Venezuelans living in the United States, while that legal dispute plays out.\par \par \uc2 In a bid to reduce illegal border crossings, Biden starting in 2022 allowed Venezuelans who entered the United States by air to request a two-year parole if they passed security checks and had a US financial sponsor. Biden expanded that process to Cubans , Haitians and Nicaraguans in 2023 as his administration grappled with high levels of illegal immigration from those nations.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-30T14:50:55.908Z">3.50pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Supreme court lets Trump administration strip 'parole' status from half a million migrants from four countries\par \par \uc2 The supreme court has allowed \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s administration to revoke the temporary legal status of hundreds of thousands of Venezuelan , Cuban , Haitian and Nicaraguan migrants living in the United States, Reuters reports, bolstering the president\u8217\'20\'19s drive to step up deportations.\par \par \uc2 The court put on hold Boston-based US district judge Indira Talwani order halting the administration\u8217\'20\'19s move to end the immigration \u8220\'20\'1Cparole\u8221\'20\'1D granted to 532,000 of these migrants under \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  , potentially exposing many of them to rapid removal, while the case plays out in lower courts.\par \par \uc2 As with many of the court\u8217\'20\'19s orders issued in an emergency fashion, the decision was unsigned and gave no reasoning. Two of the court\u8217\'20\'19s three liberal justices, \uc2 Ketanji Brown Jackson\uc2  and \uc2 Sonia Sotomayor\uc2  , publicly dissented.\par \par \uc2 The court botched its assessment of whether the administration was entitled to freeze Talwani\u8217\'20\'19s decision pending the litigation, Jackson wrote in an accompanying opinion. The outcome, Jackson wrote, \u8220\'20\'1Cundervalues the devastating consequences of allowing the government to precipitously upend the lives and livelihoods of nearly half a million noncitizens while their legal claims are pending \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Immigration parole is a form of temporary permission under US law to be in the country for \u8220\'20\'1Curgent humanitarian reasons or significant public benefit\u8221\'20\'1D, allowing recipients to live and work in the United States . Biden used parole as part of his administration\u8217\'20\'19s approach by to deter illegal immigration at the US-Mexican border.\par \par \uc2 Trump called for ending humanitarian parole programs in an executive order signed on 20 January, his first day back in office. The \uc2 Department of Homeland Security\uc2  subsequently moved to terminate them in March, cutting short the two-year parole grants. The administration said revoking the parole status would make it easier to place migrants in a fast-track deportation process called \u8220\'20\'1Cexpedited removal\u8221\'20\'1D .\par \par \uc2 The plaintiffs, a group of migrants granted parole and Americans who serve as their sponsors, sued administration officials claiming the administration violated federal law governing the actions of government agencies.\par \par \uc2 Talwani in April found that the law governing such parole did not allow for the program\u8217\'20\'19s blanket termination, instead requiring a case-by-case review . The Boston-based 1st US circuit court of appeals declined to put the judge\u8217\'20\'19s decision on hold.\par \par \uc2 In its filing, the justice department told the supreme court that Talwani\u8217\'20\'19s order had upended \u8220\'20\'1Ccritical immigration policies that are carefully calibrated to deter illegal entry\u8221\'20\'1D, effectively \u8220\'20\'1Cundoing democratically approved policies that featured heavily in the November election\u8221\'20\'1D that returned Trump to the presidency.\par \par \uc2 The plaintiffs told the supreme court they would face grave harm if their parole is cut short given that the administration has indefinitely suspended processing their pending applications for asylum and other immigration relief. They said they would be separated from their families and immediately subject to expedited deportation \u8220\'20\'1Cto the same despotic and unstable countries from which they fled, where many will face serious risks of danger, persecution and even death \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-30T15:03:59.989Z">at 4.03pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-30T14:43:26.544Z">3.43pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 China moving slow to approve exports of rare earth minerals - Reuters\par \par \uc2 While Trump did not provide an explanation to his allegation that China had \u8220\'20\'1Ctotally violated\u8221\'20\'1D the terms of the agreement reached with the US in Geneva, Reuters has been told by a US official that it appears China was moving slow on promises to issue export licenses for rare earth minerals .\par \par \uc2 Earlier US trade representative Jamieson Greer \u8217\'20\'19s told CNBC:\par \par \uc2 The Chinese are slow-rolling their compliance, which is completely unacceptable and it has to be addressed.\par \par \uc2 According to the Wall Street Journal, Greer said the flow of critical minerals from China, which had been cut off by Chinese trade countermeasures, has not resumed as called for by the Geneva agreement.\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for China\u8217\'20\'19s embassy in Washington did not immediately respond to a Reuters request for comment. Spokespersons for the White House, the \uc2 US Treasury\uc2  and the US Trade Representative\u8217\'20\'19s Office also did not respond to requests for comment.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-30T14:12:25.372Z">3.12pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Trump administration orders extra vetting of 'online presence' of all visa applicants linked to \uc2 Harvard University\par \par \uc2 The state department has ordered all its consular missions overseas to begin additional vetting of visa applicants looking to travel to Harvard for any purpose, according to an internal cable seen by Reuters on Friday, in a significant expansion of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s crackdown against the embattled elite university.\par \par \uc2 In a cable dated 30 May and sent to all US diplomatic and consular posts, secretary of state \uc2 Marco Rubio\uc2  instructed the immediate start of \u8220\'20\'1Cadditional vetting of any non-immigrant visa applicant seeking to travel to \uc2 Harvard University\uc2  for any purpose\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Such applicants include but are not limited to prospective students, students, faculty, employees, contractors, guest speakers, and tourists, the cable said. \uc2 Harvard University\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cfailed to maintain a campus environment free from violence and anti-Semitism \u8221\'20\'1D, the cable said, citing the \uc2 Department of Homeland Security\uc2  and therefore the enhanced vetting measures aim to help consular officers identify visa applicants \u8220\'20\'1Cwith histories of anti-Semitic harassment and violence\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The order also directs consular officers to consider questioning the credibility of the applicant if the individual\u8217\'20\'19s social media accounts are private and instruct them to ask the applicant to set their accounts to public.\par \par \uc2 The additional measures on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/education/harvard-university"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Harvard}}}\uc2  were first reported by Fox News, but the cable itself has not been previously reported.\par \par \uc2 The state department did not immediately respond to a Reuters request for comment.\par \par \uc2 The move is part of the Trump administration\u8217\'20\'19s intensifying immigration crackdown and follows Rubio\u8217\'20\'19s order to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/27/international-student-visa-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stop scheduling new appointments}}}\uc2  for student and exchange visitor visa applicants. The secretary of state also said earlier this week that Washington {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/29/us-revoke-chinese-student-visas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will start revoking the visas}}}\uc2  of Chinese students with links to the Chinese Communist Party and those who are working on critical areas.\par \par \uc2 The Trump administration has launched a multifront attack on the nation\u8217\'20\'19s oldest and wealthiest university, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/27/trump-harvard-federal-contracts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 freezing billions of dollars in grants and other funding}}}\uc2 , proposing to end its tax-exempt status and opening an investigation into whether it discriminated against white, Asian, male or straight employees or job applicants.\par \par \uc2 Trump alleges top US universities are cradles of \u8220\'20\'1Canti-American\u8221\'20\'1D movements. In a dramatic escalation, his administration last week {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/22/trump-harvard-international-students"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 revoked Harvard\u8217\'20\'19s ability}}}\uc2  to enrol foreign students, a move later {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/29/trump-harvard-international-students"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 blocked by a federal judge}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-30T14:14:55.789Z">at 3.14pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-30T14:06:15.063Z">3.06pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s the full Truth post from Trump earlier this morning, in which he claims he moved to make a trade deal with China not out of any US self-interest whatsoever \u8211\'20\'13 but \u8220\'20\'1Cto save them\u8221\'20\'1D from a \u8220\'20\'1Cdevastating\u8221\'20\'1D situation, factory closings and civil unrest caused by his tariffs of up to 145% on Chinese imports.\par \par \uc2 Two weeks ago China was in grave economic danger! The very high Tariffs I set made it virtually impossible for China to TRADE into the United States marketplace which is, by far, number one in the World. We went, in effect, COLD TURKEY with China, and it was devastating for them. Many factories closed and there was, to put it mildly, \u8220\'20\'1Ccivil unrest.\u8221\'20\'1D I saw what was happening and didn\u8217\'20\'19t like it, for them, not for us. I made a FAST DEAL with China in order to save them from what I thought was going to be a very bad situation, and I didn\u8217\'20\'19t want to see that happen. Because of this deal, everything quickly stabilized and China got back to business as usual. Everybody was happy! That is the good news!!! The bad news is that China, perhaps not surprisingly to some, HAS TOTALLY VIOLATED ITS AGREEMENT WITH US. So much for being Mr. NICE GUY!\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-30T14:26:42.926Z">at 3.26pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-30T14:03:03.055Z">3.03pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Greer says Trump administration 'very concerned' with and must address Chinese 'non-compliance'\par \par \uc2 Echoing Trump\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2025/may/30/donald-trump-tariffs-elon-musk-us-politics-live-news-updates?CMP=share_btn_url&page=with%3Ablock-6839a1b98f085984c7366ce1#block-6839a1b98f085984c7366ce1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 accusation this morning}}}\uc2  that China has \u8220\'20\'1Ctotally violated\u8221\'20\'1D the terms of its preliminary trade agreement with the US, US trade representative Jamieson Greer {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnbc.com/2025/05/30/trump-china-tariffs-trade-futures.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told CNBC}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cwe\u8217\'20\'19re very concerned with\u8221\'20\'1D China\u8217\'20\'19s purported non-compliance with the temporary trade deal.\par \par \uc2 Per his CNBC interview, Greer said the \u8220\'20\'1CUnited States did exactly what it was supposed to do, and the Chinese are slow rolling their compliance \u8221\'20\'1D. He called that \u8220\'20\'1Ccompletely unacceptable and has to be addressed \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Trump did not explain what China had done to violate the terms of the Geneva agreement or what action Washington would take against Beijing.\par \par \uc2 It comes a day after US treasury secretary Scott Bessent told Fox News that trade talks between the US and China were \u8220\'20\'1Ca bit stalled\u8221\'20\'1D and getting a deal over the finish line will likely need the direct involvement of Trump and Chinese president Xi Jinping .\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-30T14:28:09.166Z">at 3.28pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-30T13:51:37.016Z">2.51pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 From infamous {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/21/elon-musk-nazi-roman-salute-difference-trump-inauguration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 salutes}}}\uc2  and multiple Maga hats (sometimes worn {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2025/apr/30/donald-trump-100-days-michigan-rally-tariffs-ukraine-mandelson-us-politics-live-updates?CMP=share_btn_url&page=with%3Ablock-6812605c8f083cd6dad7f9ae#block-6812605c8f083cd6dad7f9ae"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 at the same time}}}\uc2 ) to the globally detrimental {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2025/may/01/trump-100-days-elon-musk-doge"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 mass layoffs}}}\uc2 , my colleagues have put together this timeline of \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s highly contentious tenure at Doge . <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2025/may/30/elon-musk-doge-timeline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Salutes, Maga hats and mass layoffs: Elon Musk at Doge \u8211\'20\'13 a timeline}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-30T13:53:41.481Z">at 2.53pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-30T13:21:51.447Z">2.21pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 As we reported earlier, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  are due to hold a joint press conference at 1.30pm ET on what is supposed to be officially the tech billionaire\u8217\'20\'19s final day working as part of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/trump-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump administration}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Trump used his own Truth Social website to describe the X owner as \u8220\'20\'1Cterrific\u8221\'20\'1D in what is clearly an attempt to quell rumours of a rift between the two men. \u8220\'20\'1CThis will be his last day, but not really, because he will, always, be with us, helping all the way,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump wrote.\par \par \uc2 But after arriving the White House 130 days ago vowing to slash federal spending by $2tn (spoiler: he didn\u8217\'20\'19t), \u8220\'20\'1Cthe thing that Musk has been most stunningly effective at slashing is his own reputation,\u8221\'20\'1D writes Guardian columnist Marina Hyde .\par \par \uc2 He arrived in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s orbit as a somewhat mysterious man, widely regarded as a tech genius, and a titan of the age. He leaves it with vast numbers of people woken up to the fact he\u8217\'20\'19s a weird and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2024/nov/19/he-has-already-fathered-many-children-now-musk-wants-all-of-the-us-to-embrace-extreme-breeding"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 creepy breeding fetishist}}}\uc2 , who desperately pretends to be good at video games, and wasn\u8217\'20\'19t remotely as key to Space X or \uc2 Tesla\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s engineering prowess as they\u8217\'20\'19d vaguely thought. Also, with a number of them apparently convinced he had a botched penile implant. Rightly or wrongly convinced \u8211\'20\'13 sure. I\u8217\'20\'19m just asking questions.\par \par \uc2 But look, it\u8217\'20\'19s good news for \uc2 Tesla\uc2  investors, who have managed to end Musk\u8217\'20\'19s practice of WFWH (working from White House), and are now demanding {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnbc.com/2025/05/28/tesla-investors-demand-musk-work-40-hour-week-at-ev-maker-amid-crisis.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he puts in a 40-hour week}}}\uc2  to save the company whose stock he has spent the past few months tanking. As the world order dramatically seeks to rearrange itself in the new era of US unreliability, no one should ever be able to unsee the president of the United States\u8217\'20\'19s decision to turn the White House lawn into a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2025/mar/14/trump-musk-white-house-tesla-boycott"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 car sales lot for his sad friend}}}\uc2 . Did it work? It seems not. Musk spent a lot of this week airing his hurt feelings about his brrm-brrm cars. \u8220\'20\'1CPeople were burning Teslas,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thedailybeast.com/musk-throws-an-epic-self-pity-party-about-everyone-being-mean-to-him/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he whined}}}\uc2  to \uc2 Jeff Bezos\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  this week. \u8220\'20\'1CWhy would you do that? That\u8217\'20\'19s really uncool.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Well, one thing we will no longer have to endure is this guy\u8217\'20\'19s decrees on what is or isn\u8217\'20\'19t cool. The timeworn thing about money and power is that they allow nerds to reinvent themselves as cool \u8230\'20\'26 What you rarely see is the alchemy of that process in reverse, live and in real time. But we got that with Elon, and we have to take our laughs where we can. In some other businesses, Musk could have convinced himself it wasn\u8217\'20\'19t happening, but politics is a place where pollsters literally ask real people what they think of public figures every single week. Elon\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abcnews.go.com/Politics/elon-musk-approval-low-reflecting-opposition-trump-cuts/story?id=121199149"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 approval ratings}}}\uc2  are underwater. <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2025/may/30/elon-musk-tesla-investors-doge"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 So long, Elon: the cuts didn\u8217\'20\'19t go to plan, but you completely shredded your reputation | Marina Hyde}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-30T13:24:01.881Z">at 2.24pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-30T12:58:23.737Z">1.58pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Division between US and China is the biggest risk confronting world now, France's Macron says\par \par \uc2 France\u8217\'20\'19s president \uc2 Emmanuel Macron\uc2  has said that division between the United States and China , is the main risk currently confronting the world, as he emphasized the need for building new coalitions between Paris and partners in the Indo-Pacific.\par \par \uc2 Macron is visiting the region as France and the \uc2 European Union\uc2  aim to strengthen their commercial ties in Asia to offset uncertainty over Donald Trum p\u8217\'20\'19s tariff measures.\par \par \uc2 Speaking at the Shangri-La Dialogue, Asia\u8217\'20\'19s premier defence forum, alongside a two-day state visit to Singapore, Macron said:\par \par \uc2 I will be clear, France is a friend and an ally of the United States, and is a friend, and we do cooperate - even if sometimes we disagree and compete - with China.\par \par \uc2 The French president said Asia and Europe have a common interest in preventing the disintegration of the global order.\par \par \uc2 You have to choose a side. If we do so, we will kill the global order, and we will destroy methodically, all the institutions we created after the Second World War in order to preserve peace.\par \par \uc2 The time for non-alignment has undoubtedly passed, but the time for coalitions of action has come, and requires that countries capable of acting together give themselves every means to do so.\par \par \uc2 Macron is following leaders of China, Japan and other European countries in visiting the region in recent weeks, in a sign of south east Asia\u8217\'20\'19s strategic importance amid uncertainties on global supply chains and trade.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-30T13:29:48.780Z">at 2.29pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-30T12:25:11.494Z">1.25pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Trump says China has 'totally violated' agreement with US on tariffs\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has said China had \u8220\'20\'1Cviolated\u8221\'20\'1D an agreement on tariffs with the United States reached in Geneva and threatened to take action in response.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CChina, perhaps not surprisingly to some, HAS TOTALLY VIOLATED ITS AGREEMENT WITH US. So much for being Mr. NICE GUY!,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://truthsocial.com/@realDonaldTrump/posts/114596705340367716"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in a post}}}\uc2  on his Truth Social platform.\par \par \uc2 Trump didn\u8217\'20\'19t explain how China had violated the agreement or what action he would take.\par \par \uc2 Trade talks between the US and China were \u8220\'20\'1Ca bit stalled\u8221\'20\'1D and getting a deal over the finish line will likely need the direct involvement of Trump and Chinese president Xi Jinping , US treasury secretary Scott Bessent told Fox News yesterday.\par \par \uc2 I think that given the magnitude of the talks, given the complexity, that this is going to require [the leaders of both countries] to weigh in with each other.\par \par \uc2 Two weeks after breakthrough negotiations in Geneva that resulted in a temporary truce in the trade war between the world\u8217\'20\'19s two biggest economies, Bessent said progress since then has been slow, but said he expects more talks in the next few weeks.\par \par \uc2 I believe that we will be having more talks with [China] in the next few weeks and I believe we may at some point have a call between the president and [Xi Jinping].\par \par \uc2 He added that the pair had \u8220\'20\'1Ca very good relationship\u8221\'20\'1D and he was \u8220\'20\'1Cconfident that the Chinese will come to the table when President Trump makes his preferences known\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The US-China agreement to dial back triple-digit tit-for-tat tariffs for 90 days prompted a massive relief rally in global stocks. But it did nothing to address the underlying reasons for Trump\u8217\'20\'19s tariffs on Chinese goods, mainly longstanding US complaints about China\u8217\'20\'19s state-dominated, export-driven economic model, leaving those issues for future talks.\par \par \uc2 US stock index futures dropped following Trump\u8217\'20\'19s post this morning. Reuters reports that at 8:16am ET, Dow E-minis were down 153 points, or 0.36%, S&P 500 E-minis were down 26.5 points, or 0.45%, and Nasdaq 100 E-minis were down 102.75 points, or 0.48%.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-30T14:25:58.397Z">at 3.25pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-30T11:45:13.671Z">12.45pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 The Republican nominee for governor of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/virginia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Virginia}}}\uc2  has recently tried to distance herself from her longstanding, hardline anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  record, declining recently to state whether she would support any restrictions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access if she is elected to lead the state this fall. But her record reveals a candidate staunchly opposed to the procedure.\par \par \uc2 Winsome Earle-Sears, now the state\u8217\'20\'19s lieutenant governor, supported a 15-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban and has previously said she wants to make \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  illegal in almost all cases. In audio obtained by the Guardian, Earle-Sears also suggested an equivalence between consenting to sex and consenting to pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Virginia is the only state in the US south without a strict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is legal in the state through the end of the second trimester of pregnancy. The state\u8217\'20\'19s current Republican governor, \uc2 Glenn Youngkin\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://19thnews.org/2023/11/virginia-voters-reject-republican-campaign-abortion-ban/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 previously failed}}}\uc2  to build support for a 15-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, a framework Earle-Sears {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wric.com/news/virginia-news/watch-live-lt-gov-winsome-earle-sears-on-abortion-rights-in-virginia/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 endorsed}}}\uc2 . While campaigning for lieutenant governor in January 2021, before {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade}}}\uc2  was overturned and support for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights rose among the US public, Earle-Sears told a reporter that she considered \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to be \u8220\'20\'1C{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.winchesterstar.com/winchester_star/stephenson-resident-seeking-gop-nomination-in-lieutenant-governors-race/article_20653dc1-0cd4-509e-b5cc-5da9717eadb5.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 genocide}}}\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D and that she wanted to make \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  illegal in all cases unless the mother\u8217\'20\'19s life was at risk.\par \par \uc2 But she has recently struck a different tone. In a local news {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wric.com/news/politics/capitol-connection/8news-exclusive-earle-sears-declines-to-say-if-shell-sign-a-bill-limiting-abortion-access-if-elected-governor/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 interview}}}\uc2  last week, a reporter with WRIC 8News asked Earle-Sears about her past support for limiting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access. She replied: \u8220\'20\'1CI never said limiting access.\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Sears\uc2 , who is Black, then referenced \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates among Black women and asked: \u8220\'20\'1CWho doesn\u8217\'20\'19t want us to have babies?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 When asked if she would sign a law banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 15 weeks or less, Earle-Sears said: \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re not limiting access at all. That\u8217\'20\'19s not what we\u8217\'20\'19re saying. As a matter of fact, what we really need to do is get together and try to figure out, where is the limit?\u8221\'20\'1D <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/30/abortion-winsome-earle-sears-virginia-governor-candidate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 GOP nominee for Virginia governor tries to distance herself from anti-\b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  past}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-30T11:28:07.179Z">12.28pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Twenty-two young Americans have filed a new lawsuit against the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/trump-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump administration}}}\uc2  over its anti-{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us/environment"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 environment}}}\uc2  executive orders. By intentionally boosting oil and gas production and stymying carbon-free energy, federal officials are violating their constitutional rights to life and liberty, alleges the lawsuit, filed on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The federal government is engaging in unlawful executive overreach by breaching congressional mandates to protect ecosystems and public health, argue the plaintiffs, who are between the ages of seven and 25 and hail from the heavily climate-impacted states of Montana, Hawaii, Oregon, California and Florida. They also say officials\u8217\'20\'19 emissions-increasing and science-suppressing orders have violated the state-created danger doctrine, a legal principle meant to prevent government actors from inflicting injury upon their citizens.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAt its core, this suit is about the health of children, it\u8217\'20\'19s about the right to life, it\u8217\'20\'19s about the right to form families,\u8221\'20\'1D said Julia Olson, attorney and founder of Our Children\u8217\'20\'19s Trust, the non-profit law firm that brought the suit. \u8220\'20\'1CWe all have constitutional rights, and if we don\u8217\'20\'19t use our constitution \u8211\'20\'13 if we walk away from it and we walk away from our youth \u8211\'20\'13 we will not have a democracy.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The lawsuit specifically targets three of the slew of pro-fossil fuel executive orders Trump has signed during his second term. Among them are two day-one Trump moves to declare a \u8220\'20\'1Cnational energy emergency\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cunleash American energy\u8221\'20\'1D, and another April order aimed at \u8220\'20\'1Creinvigorating\u8221\'20\'1D the domestic production of coal \u8211\'20\'13 the dirtiest and most expensive fossil fuel. <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/29/trump-administration-sued-anti-environment-orders"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump violating right to life with anti-environment orders, youth lawsuit says}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-30T11:12:32.440Z">12.12pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/trump-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump administration}}}\uc2  has set aggressive new goals in its anti-{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/usimmigration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 immigration}}}\uc2  agenda, demanding that federal agents arrest 3,000 people a day \u8211\'20\'13 or more than a million in a year.\par \par \uc2 The new target, tripling arrest figures from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/feb/12/ice-officials-reassigned-deportation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 earlier}}}\uc2  this year, was delivered to \uc2 Immigration and Customs Enforcement\uc2  (Ice) leaders by \uc2 Stephen Miller\uc2 , the White House deputy chief of staff, and \uc2 Kristi Noem\uc2 , the \uc2 Department of Homeland Security\uc2  (DHS) secretary, in a strained meeting last week.\par \par \uc2 The intense meeting, first reported by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2025/05/28/immigration-ice-deportations-stephen-miller"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Axios}}}\uc2  and confirmed by the Guardian, involved Ice officials from enforcement and removal operations (ERO) and homeland security investigations (HSI) \u8211\'20\'13 both separate offices within DHS. ERO is in charge of immigration enforcement, including arrests, detention and deportation, while HSI typically focuses on investigating transnational crime, such as drug trafficking, human smuggling and the spread of online child abuse.\par \par \uc2 The 21 May meeting in Washington DC is the latest example of the increasing pressure being placed on officials nationwide to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/mar/13/us-immigration-arrests-february-2025"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 increase the number of arrests}}}\uc2  of immigrants, as the administration doubles down on its anti-immigration agenda.\par \par \uc2 The latest phase of the crackdown includes new tactics, such as mandating federal law enforcement agents outside Ice to assist in arrests and transports, more deputizing of compliant state and local law enforcement agencies, and arresting people at locations that were once protected, like courthouses. <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/29/trump-ice-arrest-quota"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump administration sets quota to arrest 3,000 people a day in anti-immigration agenda}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-30T10:54:20.466Z">11.54am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/federal-reserve"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Federal Reserve}}}\uc2  issued a rare, strongly worded {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.federalreserve.gov/newsevents/pressreleases/other20250529a.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement}}}\uc2  on Thursday after chair \uc2 Jerome Powell\uc2  spoke with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  at the White House on Thursday morning, holding firm on the central bank\u8217\'20\'19s independence amid pressure from Trump to lower interest rates.\par \par \uc2 The three-paragraph statement emphasized the Fed\u8217\'20\'19s independent, non-partisan role in setting monetary policy based on economic data.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CChair Powell did not discuss his expectations for monetary policy, except to stress that the path of policy will depend entirely on incoming economic information and what that means for the outlook,\u8221\'20\'1D the statement read.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/jerome-powell"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Powell}}}\uc2  told Trump that he and other Fed officials \u8220\'20\'1Cwill set monetary policy, as required by law, to support maximum employment and stable prices and will make those decisions based solely on careful, objective, and non-political analysis\u8221\'20\'1D, according to the statement. <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2025/may/29/federal-reserve-chair-powell-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Federal Reserve issues rare statement asserting independence amid Trump pressure}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-30T10:39:25.470Z">11.39am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 The United States plans to ramp up weapons sales to Taipei to a level exceeding president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s first term as part of an effort to deter China as it intensifies military pressure on the democratic island, according to two US officials.\par \par \uc2 If US arms sales to Taiwan do accelerate, it could ease worries about the extent of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s commitment to the island, Reuters reported. It would also add new friction to the tense US-China relationship.\par \par \uc2 The US officials, who spoke on condition of anonymity, said they expect US approvals for weapons sales to Taipei over the next four years to surpass those in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s first term, with one of the officials saying arms sales notifications to Taiwan could \u8220\'20\'1Ceasily exceed\u8221\'20\'1D that earlier period.\par \par \uc2 They also said the United States is pressing members of Taiwan\u8217\'20\'19s opposition parties not to oppose the government\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to increase defense spending to 3% of the island\u8217\'20\'19s economic output.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-30T10:26:50.552Z">11.26am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Trump administration considers allowing tariffs of up to 15% for 150 days, WSJ reports\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s administration is considering a stopgap effort to impose tariffs on large parts of the global economy under an existing law that includes language allowing for tariffs of up to 15% for 150 days, the Wall Street Journal reported on Thursday, citing people familiar with the matter.\par \par \uc2 The administration has not made a final decision and it could wait to impose any plans after a federal appeals court on Thursday temporarily reinstated the most sweeping of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s tariffs after a trade court ruling to immediately block them, the report added.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-30T10:14:33.809Z">11.14am BST</time>\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/trump-tariffs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tariff}}}\uc2  policy was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/28/us-court-blocks-trump-tariffs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 derailed}}}\uc2  by a libertarian public interest law firm that has received money from some of his richest backers.\par \par \uc2 The Liberty Justice Center filed a lawsuit against the US president\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Creciprocal\u8221\'20\'1D tariffs on behalf of five small businesses, which it said were harmed by the policy.\par \par \uc2 The center, based in Austin, Texas, describes itself as a libertarian non-profit litigation firm \u8220\'20\'1Cthat seeks to protect economic liberty, private property rights, free speech, and other fundamental rights\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Previous {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.propublica.org/article/illinois-policy-institute-john-tillman-transactions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 backers}}}\uc2  of the firm include billionaires Robert Mercer and Richard Uihlein, who were also financial backers of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s presidential campaigns.\par \par \uc2 Mercer, a hedge fund manager, was a key backer of Breitbart News and Cambridge Analytica, pouring millions into both companies. He personally {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2017/may/07/the-great-british-brexit-robbery-hijacked-democracy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 directed}}}\uc2  Cambridge Analytica to focus on the Leave campaign during the UK\u8217\'20\'19s Brexit referendum in 2016 that led to the UK leaving the \uc2 European Union\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 For its lawsuit against Trump\u8217\'20\'19s tariffs, the Liberty Justice Center gathered five small businesses, including a wine company and a fish gear and apparel retailer, and argued that Trump overreached his executive authority and needed Congress\u8217\'20\'19s approval to pass such broad tariffs. <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/29/trump-tariffs-liberty-justice-center"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump tariffs derailed by law firm that received money from his richest backers}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-30T10:04:09.635Z">11.04am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Trump celebrates \uc2 Nippon Steel\uc2  'deal' with rally at Pennsylvania plant\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  heads to Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania on Friday to headline a rally to celebrate \uc2 Nippon Steel\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cplanned partnership\u8221\'20\'1D with \uc2 US Steel\uc2 , signaling final approval for the deal could be on the horizon.\par \par \uc2 Proponents of the transaction are hoping his visit to the state where \uc2 U.S. Steel\uc2  is headquartered will cap a tumultuous 18-month effort by \uc2 Nippon Steel\uc2  to buy the iconic American company, beset by union opposition and two national security reviews, Reuters reported.\par \par \uc2 But the deal is possibly not entirely done. Following Trump\u8217\'20\'19s post on Truth Social last Friday announcing the rally and appearing to endorse the merger, he sowed doubt on Sunday, describing the deal to reporters as an investment with \u8220\'20\'1Cpartial ownership,\u8221\'20\'1D with control residing with the US.\par \par \uc2 Trump will deliver remarks at a \uc2 US Steel\uc2  plant at 5pm ET on Friday in the political swing state, which he won in the 2024 election. The White House described his remarks as being about the \u8220\'20\'1CUS Steel Deal.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-30T09:52:50.033Z">10.52am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Trump attacks judges and accuses them of hating him\par \par \uc2 After a relatively long \u8211\'20\'13 for him \u8211\'20\'13 period of silence on his Truth Social platform, Trump resumed posting on Thursday, with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://truthsocial.com/@realDonaldTrump/posts/114593880455063168"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a 500-word screed}}}\uc2  attacking the three judges who ruled against him over his tariffs policy.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s post began by noting that the order to unwind the tariffs had been paused temporarily by an appeals court, but then turned to baseless speculation that the three judges on the federal trade court must have been motivated by hatred for him.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhere do these initial three Judges come from? How is it possible for them to have potentially done such damage to the United States of America? Is it purely a hatred of \u8216\'20\'18TRUMP?\u8217\'20\'19 What other reason could it be?\u8221\'20\'1D the president asked, without noting that he had appointed one of the judges himself in 2018.\par \par \uc2 He added:\par \par \uc2 It is only because of my successful use of Tariffs that many Trillions of Dollars have already begun pouring into the U.S.A. from other Countries, money that, without these Tariffs, we would not be able to get.\par \par \uc2 It is the difference between having a rich, prosperous, and successful United States of America, and quite the opposite. The ruling by the U.S. Court of International Trade is so wrong, and so political!\par \par \uc2 Hopefully, the Supreme Court will reverse this horrible, Country threatening decision, QUICKLY and DECISIVELY. Backroom \u8220\'20\'1Chustlers\u8221\'20\'1D must not be allowed to destroy our Nation!\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s curiosity as to what could possibly explain the decision did not, apparently, extend to reading any of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://storage.courtlistener.com/recap/gov.uscourts.cit.17080/gov.uscourts.cit.17080.55.0.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the 49-page explanation}}}\uc2  written by the court, because his post did not deal with any of the legal issues raised in the opinion.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-30T09:43:51.629Z">10.43am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Trump gets tariff reprieve ahead of Musk Oval Office press conference later today\par \par \uc2 Hello and welcome to the US politics live blog. I\u8217\'20\'19m Tom Ambrose and I will be bringing you all the latest news lines over the next couple of hours or so.\par \par \uc2 Let\u8217\'20\'19s start with the news that the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/trump-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump administration}}}\uc2  is racing to halt a major blow to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/16/trump-us-tariff-rates-trading-partners"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 president\u8217\'20\'19s sweeping tariffs}}}\uc2  after a US court ruled they \u8220\'20\'1Cexceed any authority granted to the president\u8221\'20\'1D .\par \par \uc2 A US trade court ruled {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/16/trump-us-tariff-rates-trading-partners"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the president\u8217\'20\'19s tariffs regime}}}\uc2  was illegal on Wednesday in a dramatic twist that could block Trump\u8217\'20\'19s controversial global trade policy.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, an appeals court agreed to a temporary pause in the decision pending an appeal hearing. The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/trump-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump administration}}}\uc2  is expected to take the case to the supreme court if it loses.\par \par \uc2 The ruling by a three-judge panel at the New York-based court of international trade came after several lawsuits argued Trump had exceeded his authority, leaving US trade policy dependent on his whims and unleashing economic chaos around the world.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s the full report: <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/28/us-court-blocks-trump-tariffs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump wins temporary reprieve as he fights against court block on tariffs}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the president is expected to hold a press conference with \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  on what is supposed to be the tech billionaire\u8217\'20\'19s final day working as part of the Trump administration.\par \par \uc2 Trump used his own Truth Social website to describe the X owner as \u8220\'20\'1Cterrific\u8221\'20\'1D in what is clearly an attempt to quell rumours of a rift between the two men.\par \par \uc2 He wrote:\par \par \uc2 I am having a Press Conference tomorrow at 1:30 P.M. EST, with \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 , at the Oval Office. This will be his last day, but not really, because he will, always, be with us, helping all the way. Elon is terrific! See you tomorrow at the White House.\par \par \uc2 We will have all the key news lines, should any actually emerge, from that Oval Office presser later on.\par \par \uc2 In other developments:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 One day after the nonprofit news site NOTUS {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.notus.org/health-science/make-america-healthy-again-report-citation-errors"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 discovered}}}\uc2  that at least seven of the studies cited in a new report from health secretary Robert F Kennedy \u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1CMake America Healthy Again\u8221\'20\'1D commission do not exist, the report was quietly edited to remove at least some of the fiction.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 China has lodged a formal protest over the US declaration that it will \u8220\'20\'1Caggressively\u8221\'20\'1D revoke the visas of Chinese students, with the foreign ministry saying it had objected to the announcement made a day earlier by \uc2 Marco Rubio\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/federal-reserve"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Federal Reserve}}}\uc2  issued a rare, strongly worded {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.federalreserve.gov/newsevents/pressreleases/other20250529a.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement}}}\uc2  on Thursday after chair \uc2 Jerome Powell\uc2  spoke with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  at the White House on Thursday morning, holding firm on the central bank\u8217\'20\'19s independence amid pressure from Trump to lower interest rates.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Twenty two young Americans have filed a new lawsuit against the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/trump-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump administration}}}\uc2  over its anti-environment executive orders. By intentionally boosting oil and gas production and stymying carbon-free energy, federal officials are violating their constitutional rights to life and liberty, alleges the lawsuit, filed on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/trump-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump administration}}}\uc2  has set aggressive new goals in its anti-immigration agenda, demanding that federal agents arrest 3,000 people a day \u8211\'20\'13 or more than a million in a year.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250530el5u0018q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
