\par\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 A dystopian surveillance fear has become reality in Texas\b0\par\par\uc2 Arwa Mahdawi \par \uc2 1,318 \uc2 words\par \uc2 31 May 2025\par 21:12 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Law enforcement used license-plate readers in several states to search for a woman who had an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 Texas\u8217\'20\'19s Flocked-up \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws\par \par \uc2 Hello and welcome to the latest edition of \u8220\'20\'1Clo and behold, the dystopian thing that women and activists warned would happen ends up happening\u8221\'20\'1D. This time the issue is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://sls.eff.org/technologies/automated-license-plate-readers-alprs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 automated license plate readers (ALPRs)}}}\uc2 , which capture (no prizes for guessing!) license plate data and allow law enforcement to build a picture of where a particular vehicle has been. There\u8217\'20\'19s no opting out of being tracked: if you drive, you should simply assume that these cameras, which are sometimes hidden in objects such as traffic cones, are logging your movements. And you should assume that this license plate data can be combined with other surveillance data to paint a very detailed picture of your life. Privacy only exists for our {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pcmag.com/news/good-news-for-billionaires-faa-to-let-them-block-tracking-of-their-private"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 billionaire overlords}}}\uc2  these days. The rest of us are just data points.\par \par \uc2 There are obviously plenty of legitimate uses to ALPRs. Their proponents will wax lyrical about how they can help solve carjackings and kidnappings. But, like all technology, they are ripe for abuse. They are particularly ripe for abuse in an increasingly authoritarian US, full of lawmakers who want to control women\u8217\'20\'19s bodies.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/oct/06/how-expanding-web-of-license-plate-readers-could-be-weaponized-against-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Back in 2022}}}\uc2 , a few months after Roe v Wade was overturned, the \uc2 Guardian\uc2  published a piece on ALPRs warning that \u8220\'20\'1Can expanding web of license plate readers could be \u8216\'20\'18weaponized\u8217\'20\'19 against \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D. It focused on a company called Flock, one of the big players in this space, which promises a \u8220\'20\'1C{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.flocksafety.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 holistic solution to crime}}}\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Flock\u8217\'20\'19s technology could be used to \u8220\'20\'1Ccriminalize people seeking \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive health\b0 \highlight\uc2  and further erode people\u8217\'20\'19s ability to move about their daily lives free from being tracked and traced\u8221\'20\'1D, one expert told the Guardian at the time. Another civil rights expert warned that Flock, which has stated that it is happy to provide technology to help enact whatever laws have been passed, \u8220\'20\'1Cillustrates how surveillance isn\u8217\'20\'19t actually about benefiting society or protecting people \u8211\'20\'13 it\u8217\'20\'19s about enforcing the political goals of those in power\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Unfortunately, all these experts have been proved right. This week 404 Media reported that a Texas police officer used Flock to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.404media.co/a-texas-cop-searched-license-plate-cameras-nationwide-for-a-woman-who-got-an-abortion/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 perform a nationwide search}}}\uc2  of more than 83,000 ALPR cameras while looking for a woman who had had an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is almost entirely illegal in Texas but law enforcement reportedly looked at cameras in states such as Washington and Illinois, where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is legal.\par \par \uc2 Anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  voices love to argue that they\u8217\'20\'19re not trying to control women, they\u8217\'20\'19re trying to protect women. Funnily enough this same talking point came up in this case. Sheriff Adam King of Johnson county, Texas, told 404 Media that the woman had self-administered the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cand her family was worried that she was going to bleed to death, and we were trying to find her to get her to a hospital.\u8221\'20\'1D He added: \u8220\'20\'1CWe weren\u8217\'20\'19t trying to block her from leaving the state or whatever to get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It was about her safety.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Perhaps this was true in this case. Many of the details are still unclear so it\u8217\'20\'19s hard to tell. But even if this was purely benevolent surveillance, you can certainly see where all this is headed. \u8220\'20\'1CThis incident is undeniably a harbinger of more AI-enabled reproductive surveillance and investigations to come,\u8221\'20\'1D Ashley Emery, a senior policy analyst in \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive health\b0 \highlight\uc2  and rights at the \uc2 National Partnership for Women & Families\uc2 , told 404 Media. \u8220\'20\'1CEspecially for women of color who are already over-surveilled and over-policed, the stakes couldn\u8217\'20\'19t be higher.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTexas is the land of freedom,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.facebook.com/watch/?v=1122915602814590"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Governor Greg Abbott}}}\uc2  recently proclaimed. If you\u8217\'20\'19re a woman in Texas, however, \u8220\'20\'1Cfreedom\u8221\'20\'1D seems to have quite a strange definition. Not only are you not allowed freedom over your reproductive decisions, a number of Texas city councils (some of which are composed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.texastribune.org/2023/12/19/amarillo-texas-abortion-travel-ban-vote/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 entirely of male lawmakers}}}\uc2 ) have been trying to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.texastribune.org/2024/02/09/texas-abortion-transgender-care-outside-state-borders/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pass travel bans}}}\uc2  that would stop Texans from driving to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  appointments in other states. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans, attempted {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thenation.com/article/society/sanctuary-for-the-unborn-abortion-travel-bans-amarillo/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 travel bans}}}\uc2 , and a network of surveillance technology that can be used to enforce these bans: this is what \u8220\'20\'1Cfreedom\u8221\'20\'1D for women in Texas looks like.\par \par \uc2 Sexual exploitation and domestic violence soared after Hawaii wildfire\par \par \uc2 In the weeks and months after the 2023 Lahaina fire, \u8220\'20\'1Cone in six female fire survivors surveyed felt forced to engage in sexual acts in exchange for basic necessities such as food, clothing and housing\u8221\'20\'1D, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/29/sexual-violence-lahaina-hawaii-wildfires"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports Nina Lakhani}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Women and girls in Sudan\u8217\'20\'19s Darfur region are at near-constant risk of sexual violence\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSexual violence has become so widespread in Darfur that many people chillingly speak about it as unavoidable,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 M\u233\'00\'E9decins Sans Fronti\u232\'00\'E8res\uc2  states {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.msf.org/sexual-violence-sudan-%E2%80%9Cthey-beat-us-and-they-raped-us-right-there-road-public%E2%80%9D"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in a horrifying update}}}\uc2  on the crisis.\par \par \uc2 Saudi Arabia\u8217\'20\'19s secretive rehabilitation \u8216\'20\'18prisons\u8217\'20\'19 for disobedient women\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhile Saudi Arabia celebrates being {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/football/2024/dec/11/saudi-arabia-confirmed-as-2034-world-cup-host-despite-human-rights-concerns"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 awarded the Fifa men\u8217\'20\'19s World Cup}}}\uc2  and meticulously promotes itself on the global stage as reformed, women who have dared to publicly call for more rights and freedoms have faced house arrest, jail and exile,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2025/may/28/saudi-arabia-women-girls-rehabilitation-prisons-dar-al-reaya"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Guardian reports}}}\uc2 . Saudi Arabia, it should be noted, has had a lot of help promoting itself as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2018/jun/26/saudi-arabia-is-not-driving-change-it-is-trying-to-hoodwink-the-west"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Creformed\u8221\'20\'1D by the US media}}}\uc2 , which has run numerous puff pieces on \uc2 Mohammed bin Salman\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 also known as the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.eu/article/emmanuel-macron-saudi-arabia-mohammed-bin-salman/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cbone saw\u8221\'20\'1D prince.}}}\par \par \uc2 Yaqeen Hammad, 11, Gaza\u8217\'20\'19s youngest social media influencer, killed by Israel\par \par \uc2 She was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/ng-interactive/2025/may/30/gaza-two-family-tragedies-childhoods-cut-short-israeli-airstrikes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 watering flowers}}}\uc2  when she was killed in an airstrike.\par \par \uc2 Israeli airstrike kills nine of Gaza doctor\u8217\'20\'19s 10 children\par \par \uc2 The charred bodies of seven of Dr Alaa al-Najjar\u8217\'20\'19s 10 children arrived at her hospital. Two others, including a seven-month-old, remain missing, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/may/24/israeli-airstrike-kills-nine-of-gaza-doctors-10-children-reports-say"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 presumably under the rubble}}}\uc2 . Despite pretending to be outraged about the slaughter in Gaza, the UK has sent its trade envoy to Israel to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2025/may/28/uk-trade-envoy-lord-austin-visit-israel-talks-suspended-sparks-criticism"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 boost commercial links}}}\uc2 . Meanwhile US lawmakers are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://truthout.org/articles/republican-calls-for-gaza-to-be-nuked-like-hiroshima-and-nagasaki/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cheering the killing on}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s been a decline in mental health among US mothers\par \par \uc2 The percentage of mothers reporting \u8220\'20\'1Cexcellent\u8221\'20\'1D mental health dropped from 38% in 2016 to 26% in 2023. This decline was observed across nearly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/policy/healthcare/5323540-maternal-mental-health-decline-jama-study/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 every socioeconomic subgroup examined.}}}\par \par \uc2 Criminology lecturer turned shoplifter calls herself the \u8216\'20\'18UK\u8217\'20\'19s poshest thief\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Pretty sure {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2025/may/30/uk-poshest-thief-fined-stealing-le-creuset-cookware?CMP=fb_gu&utm_medium=Social&utm_source=Facebook&fbclid=IwY2xjawKmrH5leHRuA2FlbQIxMQBicmlkETFaem03V2g0Z2JSWmRJVWE3AR4ECY9Y3hJLf7-du2mKiNe2h7XxFUhYTBwZ0wTUGy9fK7YDJmWAr0nG3Ll5Ag_aem_zxJzAiyMSiDGRlRu9DBB_g#Echobox=1748602322"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pauline Al Said}}}\uc2 , who has been fined for stealing more than \u163\'00\'A31,000-worth of \uc2 Le Creuset\uc2  cookware, steaks, wine and gin, has taken a page out of the high-society scammer Anna Delvey\u8217\'20\'19s book. If you can grift your way to viral fame and a \uc2 Netflix\uc2  series then crime really does pay! (This should not be read as encouragement to do crime.)\par \par \uc2 Kate Nash releases a feminist pro-trans anthem that shouts out the Guardian\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://genius.com/Kate-nash-germ-lyrics"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lyrics}}}\uc2  include the following: \u8220\'20\'1CKathryn Bromwich from the Guardian states that Trans people make up roughly 0.5% of the UK population and are twice as likely to be victims of crime than cis people.\u8221\'20\'1D Nash told Attitude that she came out with the song because of JK Rowling\u8217\'20\'19s anti-trans activism. \u8220\'20\'1CI just wanted it to be on record, in music history and in feminist history, for there to be somebody else in culture that is saying that I just don\u8217\'20\'19t believe that\u8217\'20\'19s feminism,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.attitude.co.uk/culture/music/kate-nash-germ-mighty-hoopla-484405/?fbclid=PAZXh0bgNhZW0CMTEAAacQjBlp0l8hCSIvLJL9uj19TM9o-oU1X5jxZs-j3bAwgW3LL3d4d0LqccR0bg_aem_njbXV05CrW_Kz04m6rskYw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nash told Attitude}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Sydney Sweeney is selling used bathwater\par \par \uc2 The Euphoria actor, who has spoken out about being objectified by fans, is now selling soap {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.the-independent.com/life-style/sydney-sweeney-soap-bathwater-dr-squatch-b2760489.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 made with her used bathwater}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Woman says \u8216\'20\'18I don\u8217\'20\'19t like cheese\u8217\'20\'19 after winning cheese rolling race\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bbc.com/news/live/cd0l2j51gygt"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Un-brie-lievable}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Would you like to see some beatboxing nuns?\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.indy100.com/video/beatboxing-nuns-viral-video-catholic-tv"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Here you go!}}}\uc2  You\u8217\'20\'19re welcome.\par \par \uc2 The week in pawtriarchy\par \par \uc2 Doug the Pug, a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://people.com/doug-the-pug-receives-unique-honorary-degree-11741828"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 canine influencer}}}\uc2  with millions of followers, has received an honorary degree from the University of New Haven in Connecticut in \u8220\'20\'1Cfurensic science\u8221\'20\'1D. He\u8217\'20\'19s already got an unofficial dogtorate in cuteness.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Arwa Mahdawi is a Guardian columnist\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250531el5v001jn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
