\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 RFK Jr defends downsizing health department as protesters disrupt Senate hearing \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Coral Murphy Marcos (now); L\u233\'00\'E9onie Chao-Fong, Lucy Campbell, Tom Ambrose and Tom Bryant (earlier) \par \uc2 13,813 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 May 2025\par 02:02 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This blog has now closed. You can read more of our US politics coverage <a href="{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-politics">here</a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-politics">here</a}}}\uc2 >\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-15T01:53:52.182Z">2.53am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 Our live coverage is ending now. In the meantime, you can find all of our live US politics coverage {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/series/us-politics-live"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 . Here is a summary of the key developments from today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  will not attend what may be the first direct peace talks between Moscow and Kyiv in three years, scheduled for Thursday, Reuters reports. Instead, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/may/14/kremlin-tight-lipped-for-third-day-on-whether-putin-will-meet-zelenskyy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kremlin will send a team of technocrats}}}\uc2 . A US official said the US president would not attend, despite earlier comments suggesting he was considering the trip.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Health secretary Robert F Kennedy Jr described the downsizing of his department as necessary cost-cutting measures as he defended his spending plans under \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s budget proposal. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/14/rfk-jr-kennedy-senate-house-hearings"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The plans include an $18bn cut to National Institutes of Health funding}}}\uc2  and $3.6bn from the \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2 . Kennedy\u8217\'20\'19s back-to-back testimonies before House and Senate committees were his first appearances before lawmakers since his confirmation in February.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Protesters interrupted Robert F Kennedy Jr\u8217\'20\'19s opening remarks before the Senate health committee this afternoon, shouting: \u8220\'20\'1CRFK kills people with Aids!\u8221\'20\'1D The health secretary was visibly startled and jumped from his chair when protesters began shouting, before being removed by \uc2 Capitol police\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Tulsi Gabbard\uc2 , the US director of national intelligence, has fired the two highest-ranking officials at the National Intelligence Council just weeks after the council released an assessment that contradicted \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s justification for using the Alien Enemies Act to deport alleged Venezuelan gang members without due process. \uc2 Mike Collins\uc2  was serving as acting chair of the National Intelligence Council before he was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/14/tuli-gabbard-trump-national-intelligence-firings"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dismissed}}}\uc2  alongside his deputy, Maria Langan-Riekhof. They each had more than 25 years of intelligence experience.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A Russian-born researcher at \uc2 Harvard University\uc2  who has been held for weeks in an immigration detention center in Louisiana has been criminally charged with attempting to smuggle frog embryo samples into the US . Federal prosecutors in Boston announced the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/14/russian-scientist-harvard-charged"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 smuggling charge against Kseniia Petrova}}}\uc2 , 31, hours after a federal judge in Vermont heard arguments in a lawsuit she filed that argues the Trump administration has been unlawfully detaining her.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Trump administration\u8217\'20\'19s commerce secretary, \uc2 Howard Lutnick\uc2 , and his family have had extensive business interests linked to El Salvador , whose authoritarian leader \uc2 Nayib Bukele\uc2  has grown close to the White House and who has courted controversy by imprisoning people deported from the US in an aggressive immigration crackdown. El Salvador also plays host to a booming cryptocurrency and new media industry, which has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/14/lutnick-el-salvador-crypto-immigration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 numerous ties to Donald Trump allies }}}\uc2 who are seeking to make money from various ventures which have sometimes drawn the attention of authorities or ethics watchdogs.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has doubled down on why he wants to accept a luxury \uc2 Boeing\uc2  747 from Qatar , a country where he traveled to today to negotiate business deals, with the US president portraying the $400m aircraft as an opportunity too valuable to refuse. \u8220\'20\'1CThe plane that you\u8217\'20\'19re on is almost 40 years old,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump told Fox News host \uc2 Sean Hannity\uc2  during an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/15/trump-administration-news-updates-today"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Air Force One interview on the Middle East trip}}}\uc2 , where he is also visiting Saudi Arabia and the UAE.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Congressional Republicans advanced elements of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s sweeping budget package on Wednesday after a debate that lasted through the night, as a key committee voted along party lines to approve tax cuts that would add trillions of dollars to the national debt. The 26-19 vote by the tax-writing House ways and means committee amounts to an initial victory for Republicans, who still have many hurdles to clear before they can get the sprawling package of tax cuts, spending hikes and safety-net reductions to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s desk to sign into law.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-15T01:58:05.279Z">at 2.58am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-15T01:30:04.504Z">2.30am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 A Russian scientist held in Ice jail was charged with smuggling frog embryos into US.\par \par \uc2 Cy Neff brings us the full story on the Harvard scientist facing smuggling charges and the possibility of being deported:\par \par \uc2 A Harvard scientist who has been held in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/usimmigration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US immigration}}}\uc2  detention for months was charged on Wednesday with smuggling frog embryos into the United States, and likely faces deportation.\par \par \uc2 Kseniia Petrova, a Russian scientist and research associate working at \uc2 Harvard University\uc2 , was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/mar/27/russian-scientist-harvard-medical-school-ice-detention"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 originally detained by immigration officials}}}\uc2  in February after attempting to enter the United States at Boston Logan international airport.\par \par \uc2 In a 14 May {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.justice.gov/usao-ma/pr/russian-national-charged-smuggling-biological-material-boston"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 press release}}}\uc2 , the US district attorney\u8217\'20\'19s Massachusetts office said smuggling charges can bring sentences of up to 20 years and fines up to $250,000. The press releases alleges that Petrova\u8217\'20\'19s text messages show she knew of the requirement to declare the embryos before entering the United States. Petrova has spent the last three months in a Louisiana detention facility.\par \par \uc2 Petrova\u8217\'20\'19s lawyer, Gregory Romanovsky, called the case \u8220\'20\'1Cmeritless\u8221\'20\'1D and questioned the timing of her being transferred into criminal custody, saying it happened after the judge in her lawsuit set a 28 May bail hearing to consider releasing her.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe charge, filed three months after the alleged customs violation, is clearly intended to make Kseniia look like a criminal to justify their efforts to deport her,\u8221\'20\'1D he said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 Petrova detailed her research and detention experience in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2025/05/13/opinion/ice-detention-russian-scientist.html?unlocked_article_code=1.HE8.zxRL.0b6kx0MlmN6c&smid=url-share"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York Times op-ed}}}\uc2  this week. Petrova said that she left Russia after being arrested for protesting against the Ukraine war, and found \u8220\'20\'1Ca paradise for science\u8221\'20\'1D at the \uc2 Harvard Medical School\uc2  in 2023. Petrova, who also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.facebook.com/permalink.php?story_fbid=pfbid02tHDWfNj6wH5GmGXSmXTauPVmSL9suvPD9nvKVVZr4f74noxi5wvTwwMxVLLSuFdvl&id=100022022832628"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shared Facebook posts}}}\uc2  supporting the impeachment of Russian president \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 , said that she fears deportation to Russia due to her political stances.\par \par \uc2 Read the full story here: <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/14/russian-scientist-harvard-charged"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Russian scientist held in Ice jail charged with smuggling frog embryos into US}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-15T01:34:22.681Z">at 2.34am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-15T01:04:02.347Z">2.04am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Avelo Airlines\uc2 , a budget carrier based in Texas, is under fire from both customers and employees for its new contract with the Trump administration to operate deportation flights, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 As part of his immigration crackdown, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has ordered the deportation of Venezuelan migrants \u8211\'20\'13 whom he accuses of gang affiliation \u8211\'20\'13 to a maximum-security prison in El Salvador.\par \par \uc2 Avelo\uc2 , which has been struggling financially, signed a contract with the \uc2 US Department of Homeland Security\uc2  last month to transport migrants to detention centers inside and outside the US.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Association of Flight Attendants-CWA\uc2 , which represents \uc2 Avelo\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s crew, has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.afacwa.org/afa_statement_on_ice_charters"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 urged the company}}}\uc2  to reconsider its decision, which it said would be \u8220\'20\'1Cbad for the airline\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHaving an entire flight of people handcuffed and shackled would hinder any evacuation and risk injury or death,\u8221\'20\'1D the union said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe cannot do our jobs in these conditions.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Anne Watkins , a New Haven, Connecticut, resident, said she has stopped flying with \uc2 Avelo\uc2 . She launched an online petition urging travelers to boycott the airline until it ends its Ice flight operations. The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.change.org/p/we-won-t-fly-avelo-until-they-stop-ice-flights-no-volaremos-con-avelo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 petition}}}\uc2  has garnered more than 38,000 signatures.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-15T01:13:58.493Z">at 2.13am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-15T00:41:12.888Z">1.41am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 California governor seeks to exclude undocumented from Medicaid program\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/california"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 California}}}\uc2  governor, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/gavin-newsom"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Gavin Newsom}}}\uc2  , wants his state to stop enrolling more low-income immigrants without legal status in a state-funded healthcare program starting in 2026 and begin charging a monthly premium the following year to those already enrolled.\par \par \uc2 It is one of several measures proposed by Newsom on Wednesday to help close an additional $12bn deficit, a budget shortcoming the Democratic governor squarely placed on the shoulders of the \u8220\'20\'1CTrump slump\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The decision to cut in the state insurance program is driven by a higher-than-expected price tag on the program and economic uncertainty from federal tariff policies, Newsom said in a Wednesday announcement. The Democratic governor\u8217\'20\'19s move highlights his struggle to protect his liberal policy priorities amid budget challenges in his final years on the job.\par \par \uc2 California was among one of the first states to extend free healthcare benefits to all poor adults regardless of their immigration status last year, an ambitious plan touted by Newsom to help the nation\u8217\'20\'19s most populous state inch closer to a goal of universal healthcare. But the cost for such expansion ran $2.7bn more than the administration had anticipated.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on the measure proposed by the California governor: <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/14/gavin-newsom-healthcare-low-income-immigration-status"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 California governor seeks to exclude undocumented from Medicaid program}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-15T00:48:40.949Z">at 1.48am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-15T00:20:44.539Z">1.20am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 RFK Jr orders a mifepristone review as anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups push for a ban.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/robert-f-kennedy-jr"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr}}}\uc2  said on Wednesday that he had directed the \uc2 FDA\uc2  to review the regulations around the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill mifepristone.\par \par \uc2 The review, he said, was necessary due to \u8220\'20\'1Cnew data\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 data that emerged from a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://factcheck.afp.com/doc.afp.com.444Z863"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 flawed}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.huffpost.com/entry/gop-lays-groundwork-to-pull-abortion-pill-access-with-new-junk-science-report_n_6812975be4b04cfa6e2b45e0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  analysis}}}\uc2  that top US anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups are now using to pressure the Trump administration to reimpose restrictions on the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill, if not pull it from the market entirely.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s alarming,\u8221\'20\'1D Kennedy told the Missouri senator \uc2 Josh Hawley\uc2  , a Republican, during a congressional hearing. \u8220\'20\'1CClearly, it indicates that, at very least, the label should be changed.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The analysis, which has not been peer-reviewed or published in a medical journal, came after the Food and Drug Administration commissioner said he was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.semafor.com/article/04/24/2025/fdas-marty-makary-no-plans-to-pull-abortion-pill-mifepristone"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 open}}}\uc2  to reviewing new safety data on the pills, which are used in nearly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/2024/03/medication-abortion-accounted-63-all-us-abortions-2023-increase-53-2020"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 two-thirds}}}\uc2  of abortions nationwide.\par \par \uc2 The conservative organizations are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2025/05/07/anti-abortion-pill-gameplan-rolling-thunder-00331933"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rallying}}}\uc2  behind a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://eppc.org/publication/insurance-data-reveals-one-in-ten-patients-experiences-a-serious-adverse-event/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 paper}}}\uc2  published on 28 April by a rightwing thinktank, the Ethics and Public Policy Center, which claims there are higher complication rates from taking mifepristone than previously known.\par \par \uc2 The paper has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://factcheck.afp.com/doc.afp.com.444Z863"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 attracted}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2025/may/13/republican-conservatives-abortion-pill-study-fda"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 scrutiny}}}\uc2  for appearing to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2025/05/12/abortion-pill-medication-abortion-study-mifepristone/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dramatically overstate}}}\uc2  what it characterizes as \u8220\'20\'1Cserious adverse effects\u8221\'20\'1D associated with the pill, according to medical experts. For example, it counts ectopic pregnancies \u8211\'20\'13 when an embryo implants somewhere other than the uterine lining \u8211\'20\'13 as a serious complication.\par \par \uc2 Read the full story by Susan Rinkunas here: <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/14/rfk-jr-fda-abortion-pill-mifepristone"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 RFK Jr orders mifepristone review as anti-\b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  groups push for ban}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-15T00:30:30.775Z">at 1.30am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-15T00:01:32.579Z">1.01am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and South African president \uc2 Cyril Ramaphosa\uc2  are scheduled to meet at the White House on 21 May, following the US president\u8217\'20\'19s allegations \u8211\'20\'13 denied by South Africa \u8211\'20\'13 that white farmers are facing \u8220\'20\'1Cgenocide\u8221\'20\'1D in the country.\par \par \uc2 The meeting, announced on Wednesday by the South African government, comes shortly after the US granted refugee status to 59 white South Africans, part of what the Trump administration describes as a broader resettlement effort for minority Afrikaner farmers it says are being persecuted.\par \par \uc2 South African officials reject the allegations, saying white citizens are not being targeted.\par \par \uc2 Ramaphosa will be in the US from Monday through Thursday, with the White House visit scheduled for Wednesday. His office said the trip aims to \u8220\'20\'1Creset the strategic relationship\u8221\'20\'1D between the two countries.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-15T00:08:22.951Z">at 1.08am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-14T23:43:00.817Z">12.43am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Trump, Putin to skip Ukraine's peace talks that Russian leader proposed, Reuters reports\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  will not attend what may be the first direct peace talks between Moscow and Kyiv in three years, scheduled for Thursday, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 Instead, the Kremlin will send a team of technocrats.\par \par \uc2 The Russian president had proposed the talks in Istanbul \u8220\'20\'1Cwithout any preconditions\u8221\'20\'1D but, as of late Wednesday, confirmed he would send presidential adviser Vladimir Medinsky and deputy defense minister, Alexander Fomin , to lead the Russian delegation.\par \par \uc2 A US official later said the US president would not attend, despite earlier comments suggesting he was considering the trip.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-14T23:45:37.391Z">at 12.45am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-14T23:29:45.572Z">12.29am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Missouri lawmakers have approved a referendum seeking to repeal an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/dec/23/missouri-abortion-rights-ruling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 -rights amendment}}}\uc2  passed by voters six months ago.\par \par \uc2 The newly proposed constitutional amendment would go back to voters in November 2026, or sooner, if Republican governor Mike Kehoe calls a special election before then.\par \par \uc2 Republican senators used a series of rare procedural moves to cut off discussion by opposing Democrats before passing the proposed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights revision by a 21-11 vote. The measure passed the Republican-led House last month.\par \par \uc2 Immediately after vote, protestors erupted with chants of \u8220\'20\'1CStop the ban!\u8221\'20\'1D and were ushered out of the Senate chamber.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-14T23:06:21.188Z">12.06am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Director of national intelligence \uc2 Tulsi Gabbard\uc2  has fired the two highest-ranking officials at the National Intelligence Council, just weeks after the council released an assessment that contradicted President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s justification for using the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/mar/16/alien-enemies-act-explainer-can-trump-apply-a-wartime-law-to-deport-gang-members"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Alien Enemies Act}}}\uc2  to deport alleged Venezuelan gang members without due process.\par \par \uc2 Gabbard fired \uc2 Mike Collins\uc2  , the acting chair, and his deputy, Maria Langan-Riekhof , on Tuesday, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2025/05/14/politics/gabbard-fires-senior-intelligence-officials"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CNN reported}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The dismissals come after the NIC {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cdn.factcheck.org/UploadedFiles/SOCM-2025-11374_Redacted.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 authored an assessment}}}\uc2  that found it unlikely that Nicol\u225\'00\'E1s Maduro, Venezuela\u8217\'20\'19s president, is helping the criminal activities of Tren de Aragua in the US.\par \par \uc2 The latest round of intelligence firings comes as Gabbard and her team aim to eliminate what they view as bias and inefficiency within the intelligence community. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/alexahenning/status/1922695680872665588"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 On X}}}\uc2 , Gabbard\u8217\'20\'19s deputy chief of staff, Alexa Henning, said the NIC officials, whom she referred to as \u8220\'20\'1CBiden holdovers\u8221\'20\'1D, were removed for \u8220\'20\'1Cpoliticizing intelligence.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-14T22:48:20.856Z">11.48pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Indian academic held over pro-Palestinian views released from Ice jail\par \par \uc2 The Georgetown academic Badar Khan Suri was released from Ice detention hours after after a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/virginia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Virginia}}}\uc2  federal judge\u8217\'20\'19s order on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Khan Suri was among {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/apr/28/trump-immigration-people-detained-deported-cases"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 several individuals legally studying}}}\uc2  in the US who have been targeted by the Trump administration for their pro-Palestinian activism. He has spent two months in detention.\par \par \uc2 US district judge Patricia Giles in Alexandria, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/virginia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Virginia}}}\uc2 , said that the ruling was effective immediately with no conditions and no bond. She added that Khan Suri\u8217\'20\'19s release was \u8220\'20\'1Cin the public interest to disrupt the chilling effect on protected speech\u8221\'20\'1D during the hearing. The judge explained in her ruling how the government did not submit sufficient evidence on several of its claims.\par \par \uc2 A large crowd of demonstrators outside the courthouse reportedly cheered upon hearing the news of the ruling.\par \par \uc2 Badar Khan Suri will go home to his family in Virginia while he awaits the outcome of his petition against the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/trump-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump administration}}}\uc2  for wrongful arrest and detention in violation of the first amendment and other constitutional rights.\par \par \uc2 He is also facing deportation proceedings in an immigration court in Texas.\par \par \uc2 Read the full story by Marina Dunbar: <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/14/judge-order-release-khan-suri-ice"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Indian academic held over pro-Palestinian views released from Ice jail}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-14T22:28:34.825Z">11.28pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  shows he still has the White House\u8217\'20\'19s ear on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Middle East trip\par \par \uc2 Over the course of an eight-minute interview, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/elon-musk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Elon Musk}}}\uc2  touted his numerous businesses and vision of a \u8220\'20\'1CStar Trek future\u8221\'20\'1D while telling the crowd that his Tesla Optimus robots had performed a dance for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  and the crown prince of Saudi Arabia, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/mohammed-bin-salman"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mohammed bin Salman}}}\uc2 , to the tune of YMCA. He also announced that Starlink, his satellite internet company, had struck a deal for use in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/saudiarabia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Saudi Arabia}}}\uc2  for maritime and aviation usage; looking to the near future, he expressed his desire to bring \uc2 Tesla\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s self-driving robotaxis to the country.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe could not be more appreciative of having a lifetime partner and a friend like you, Elon, to the Kingdom,\u8221\'20\'1D Saudi Arabia\u8217\'20\'19s minister of communications and IT, Abdullah Alswaha, told Musk.\par \par \uc2 Although Musk has pivoted away from his role as de facto leader of the so-called \u8220\'20\'1Cdepartment of government efficiency\u8221\'20\'1D and moved out of the White House, the Saudi summit showed how he is still retaining his proximity to the US president and international influence. As Musk returns to his businesses as his primary focus, he is still primed to reap the rewards of his connections and political sway over Trump.\par \par \uc2 Starlink diplomacy\par \par \uc2 Musk\u8217\'20\'19s Starlink announcement comes after a spate of countries have agreed to allow the satellite communications service to operate within their borders. Several countries that have approved Starlink did so after US state department officials mentioned the company by name or pushed for increased satellite services in negotiations over Trump\u8217\'20\'19s sweeping tariffs, according to internal memos {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/business/2025/05/07/elon-musk-starlink-trump-tariffs/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 obtained by the Washington Post}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Concerns over whether Musk and the Trump administration are leveraging their power to force countries into adopting Starlink has prompted calls for a state department inspector general investigation into whether there is undue influence at play in these agreements. On Wednesday, a group of Democratic senators {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.warren.senate.gov/imo/media/doc/warren_lawmakers_letter_to_ethics_investigators_on_starlink_and_trade_negotiations.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 issued a letter}}}\uc2  requesting a broad review of the state department\u8217\'20\'19s alleged efforts to assist Starlink.\par \par \uc2 Read the full analysis by \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Nick Robins-Early here: <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2025/may/14/trump-musk-saudi-arabia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Elon Musk shows he still has the White House\u8217\'20\'19s ear on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Middle East trip}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-14T21:59:19.626Z">10.59pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 US prosecutors charge detained Harvard scientist from Russia with smuggling offense\par \par \uc2 A Russian-born researcher at \uc2 Harvard University\uc2  who has been held for weeks in an immigration detention center in Louisiana has been criminally charged with attempting to smuggle frog embryo samples into the United States, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 Federal prosecutors in Boston announced the smuggling charge against Kseniia Petrova , 31, hours after a federal judge in Vermont heard arguments in a lawsuit she filed that argues the Trump administration has been unlawfully detaining her.\par \par \uc2 The Trump administration intends to deport Petrova back to Russia, a country she fled in 2022, despite her fear that she will be arrested there over her protest of Russia\u8217\'20\'19s war in Ukraine, the \uc2 New York Times{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2025/05/14/health/detained-russian-scientist-harvard.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-14T21:43:41.749Z">10.43pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 About a dozen labor unions have filed a lawsuit against the Trump administration in an effort to overturn sweeping cuts to the nation\u8217\'20\'19s occupational health agency.\par \par \uc2 The suit was brought by the \uc2 United Mine Workers of America\uc2  , the \uc2 American Federation of Teachers\uc2  , \uc2 National Nurses United\uc2  and 10 other unions.\par \par \uc2 The case centers on the \uc2 National Institute for Occupational Safety and Health\uc2 , which was massively downsized this year following layoffs that eliminated about 850 of its 1,000 employees, according to the Associated Press.\par \par \uc2 At a Congressional hearing on Wednesday, Robert F Kennedy Jr said he is reversing the firing of about 330 Niosh workers. But the lawsuit seeks to reinstate all Niosh staff and functions, arguing that the cuts flouted express directives from Congress and are illegal.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-14T21:45:46.868Z">at 10.45pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-14T21:24:55.222Z">10.24pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Republicans have propose prohibiting US states from regulating AI for 10 years.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans}}}\uc2  in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-congress"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US Congress}}}\uc2  are trying to bar states from being able to introduce or enforce laws that would create guardrails for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/artificialintelligenceai"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 artificial intelligence}}}\uc2  or automated decision-making systems for 10 years.\par \par \uc2 A provision in the proposed budgetary bill now before the House of Representatives would prohibit any state or local governing body from pursuing \u8220\'20\'1Cany law or regulation regulating artificial intelligence models, artificial intelligence systems, or automated decision systems\u8221\'20\'1D unless the purpose of the law is to \u8220\'20\'1Cremove legal impediments to, or facilitate the deployment or operation of\u8221\'20\'1D these systems.\par \par \uc2 The provision was a last-minute addition by House {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans}}}\uc2  to the bill just two nights before it was due to be marked up on Tuesday. The House energy and commerce committee voted to advance the reconciliation package on Wednesday morning.\par \par \uc2 The bill defines AI systems and models broadly, with anything from facial recognition systems to generative AI qualifying. The proposed law would also apply to systems that use algorithms or AI to make decisions including for hiring, housing and whether someone qualifies for public benefits.\par \par \uc2 Many of these automated decision-making systems have recently come under fire. The deregulatory proposal comes on the heels of a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.njoag.gov/ag-platkin-files-antitrust-lawsuit-against-software-company-realpage-and-10-nj-landlords-for-alleged-collusion-in-statewide-rent-raising-scheme/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lawsuit}}}\uc2  filed by several state attorneys general against the property management software \uc2 RealPage\uc2 , which the lawsuit alleges colluded with landlords to raise rents based on the company\u8217\'20\'19s algorithmic recommendations. Another company, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2024/dec/14/saferent-ai-tenant-screening-lawsuit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SafeRent}}}\uc2 , recently settled a class-action lawsuit filed by Black and Hispanic renters who say they were denied apartments based on an opaque score the company gave them.\par \par \uc2 Read the full story here: <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/14/republican-budget-bill-ai-laws"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans propose prohibiting US states from regulating AI for 10 years}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-14T21:27:46.078Z">at 10.27pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-14T21:05:55.040Z">10.05pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Harvard to allocate $250m of its own funds to support research impacted by the Trump administration\par \par \uc2 Harvard University\uc2  announced that it will allocate $250 million of its own funds to support researchers after the Trump administration froze nearly $3 billion in federal grants and contracts in recent weeks, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thecrimson.com/article/2025/5/15/harvard-central-research-funding/?utm_campaign=feed&utm_medium=referral&utm_source=later-linkinbio"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Harvard Crimson reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The elite Ivy League institution in Cambridge, Massachusetts, has become a frequent target of President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  , who has launched an aggressive campaign to reshape private colleges and universities across the country. He accuses them of promoting anti-American, Marxist, and \u8220\'20\'1Cradical left\u8221\'20\'1D ideologies.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe understand the uncertainty that these times have brought and the burden our community faces,\u8221\'20\'1D Harvard President \uc2 Alan M. Garber\uc2  wrote. \u8220\'20\'1CWe are here to support you.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Still, Garber acknowledged that the university would not be able to fully absorb the cost of the suspended or canceled federal awards. He warned that the funding freeze could disrupt long-running projects, delay scientific progress, and force unpopular decisions across Harvard\u8217\'20\'19s schools, according to the student-run outlet.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhile there will undoubtedly be difficult decisions and sacrifices ahead, we know that, together, we will chart a path forward to sustain and advance Harvard\u8217\'20\'19s vital research mission,\u8221\'20\'1D he wrote.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-14T21:06:10.078Z">at 10.06pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-14T20:50:03.261Z">9.50pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr said that the \u8220\'20\'1Ccentral focus\u8221\'20\'1D of the \uc2 National Institutes of Health\uc2  (\uc2 NIH\uc2 ) and the Food and Drug Administration (\uc2 FDA\uc2 ) will be on studying ultra-processed foods, sugars and food additives.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe central focus of \uc2 NIH\uc2 , is going to be looking at \u8211\'20\'13 and \uc2 FDA\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 looking at ultra-processed foods, and sugars, and the 10,000 additives that are in our food,\u8221\'20\'1D Kennedy said during a Senate committee on health, education, labor & pensions hearing.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-14T20:53:22.591Z">at 9.53pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-14T20:37:11.023Z">9.37pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Among those interrupting Robert F Kennedy\u8217\'20\'19s testimony at the Senate hearing were Aids activists, protesting mass terminations and cuts at the \uc2 Department of Health and Human Services\uc2 . The reductions have gutted programs that focus on child support services and international HIV treatment initiatives.\par \par \uc2 In a statement, Asia Russell of Health Gap said:\par \par \uc2 Kennedy and Trump are massacring America\u8217\'20\'19s global and domestic HIV responses \u8230\'20\'26 People will die as a result of their senseless decisions. Congress has a duty to intervene now and reject Kennedy\u8217\'20\'19s deadly budget proposal, and work urgently to reinstate what he is demolishing.\par \par \uc2 All federal experts on HIV prevention in children overseas were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2025/04/08/health/cdc-hiv-mothers.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fired last month}}}\uc2  as part of the reduction in force. At least {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://link.mediaoutreach.meltwater.com/ls/click?upn=u001.htKzrPBEm-2BgT3JlaDU8MFBK4lpoLd9WdohaBPZ8WLh7LOYlsrQR9CbNJbr-2Fm8oKJZLfnZYjJmpbSNkblikUPv70gkfyfp-2BZniol46oOcMr8-3DEPHm_ZLaVF4Uye-2FMZNh-2FFBJkpj5ytXUmFcLyR7XNOL-2BsTFLwYM3x7DfBWdlBPYNWOb73yB2a1QGk1TIr3x-2BoNnwaro7FzHqk7T9of6uDllx43d5Fc9q7eeYtQIUlHKjuZzjitBRnXKx7Rq9sGJ2qtCUMyp28jh3bIcBDy288TqGzTz8TS6Tlk7-2BaHv8Htgizu3NiMtFGoMrad9tnENuBcfFQpeAJy3mC-2BqDcaJzTSzFs6F97x5-2BWWHRL-2FhqHnsGltkEpVkWkP0Jwaeajph97lLP0o2LquU41SbtM12lkjEb4vRxtirTn4TUQrEcf9sII1YzMNeTA8b074aLA-2Bhh7wlBVBGTEr2VE04t7lySkM1dx7wQqALRas2X4Fwtv6sn0-2BRkpAznKw6aa4fkUAgoHZ5w7Yvw-3D-3D"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $759m worth of federal grants for HIV research have been cancelled}}}\uc2  so far.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-14T20:44:56.591Z">at 9.44pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-14T20:14:45.841Z">9.14pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 House Republicans are proposing lowering the SNAP dependent exemption age from 18 to 7, NOTUS {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.notus.org/congress/snap-work-requirement-dependent-age"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Under current SNAP rules, adults caring for children under 18 are exempt from work requirements. House Republicans are proposing to lower that age limit to 7, meaning caregivers of children aged 8 or older would no longer qualify for the exemption.\par \par \uc2 The proposed change, part of the agriculture section in the reconciliation bill, drew outrage from Democrats on the Agriculture Committee.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn the absence of a hearing or serious explanation, I suggest we give our 8-year-olds little tiny boots with little tiny bootstraps,\u8221\'20\'1D said Rep. Eugene Vindman of Virginia.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-14T19:48:11.624Z">8.48pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 A judge has temporarily blocked the justice department from cancelling $3.2m in grants to the \uc2 American Bar Association\uc2  (ABA) to train lawyers to represent victims of domestic and sexual violence.\par \par \uc2 The ABA sued the justice department in April, claiming it illegally terminated federal grants in retaliation for the organization\u8217\'20\'19s public criticism of the Trump administration.\par \par \uc2 US district judge Christopher Cooper granted the ABA\u8217\'20\'19s request for a preliminary injunction to stop the government from terminating the grants as the case moves forward.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe first amendment injury is concrete and ongoing,\u8221\'20\'1D Cooper wrote in his opinion on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The ABA regularly engages in protected expressive activity, and DOJ\u8217\'20\'19s termination of its grants directly punishes that activity.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-14T19:51:48.217Z">at 8.51pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-14T19:29:38.578Z">8.29pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Pennsylvania governor, Josh Shapiro , has warned that the Medicaid cuts Congress is considering would mean billions of dollars in lost federal aid to the state.\par \par \uc2 Hundreds of thousands of people could lose access to Medicaid, Shapiro told WILK-FM radio on Wednesday. He said:\par \par \uc2 I just need to stress: there is no back-filling at the state level. There are no dollars available at the state level to make up for these cuts at the federal level. So if they cut someone off Medicaid, they\u8217\'20\'19re off. We will not be able to fix that for them.\par \par \uc2 Billions of dollars in funding cuts would also accelerate the shuttering of rural hospitals \u8220\'20\'1Cwhich are teetering on the brink of closure\u8221\'20\'1D, he added.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-14T19:32:30.360Z">at 8.32pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-14T19:03:56.887Z">8.03pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 RFK Jr defends downsizing health department as part of Trump budget plan\par \par \uc2 Health secretary Robert F Kennedy Jr described the downsizing of his department as necessary cost-cutting measures as he defended his spending plans under \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s budget proposal.\par \par \uc2 The plans include an $18bn cut to \uc2 National Institutes of Health\uc2  funding and $3.6bn from the \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Kennedy, appearing before the House appropriations committee this morning, argued the proposed cuts would save taxpayers $1.8bn per year and make the department more efficient. He said in his opening statement:\par \par \uc2 Our reductions have focused on aligning \uc2 HHS\uc2  staffing levels to reflect the size of \uc2 HHS\uc2  prior to the Covid-19 pandemic, which saw around a 15% increase in the number of employees.\par \par \uc2 Asked about \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s involvement in the cuts and firings at his department, Kennedy said:\par \par \uc2 Ultimately, we executed the decisions, but \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  gave us help in trying and figuring out where there was fraud and abuse in the department. But it was up to me to make the decision, and there are many instances where I pushed back.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-14T20:31:01.189Z">at 9.31pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-14T18:43:01.414Z">7.43pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Protesters disrupt Kennedy at Senate hearing\par \par \uc2 Protesters interrupted Robert F Kennedy Jr \u8217\'20\'19s opening remarks before the Senate health committee this afternoon, shouting: \u8220\'20\'1CRFK kills people with Aids!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The health secretary was visibly startled and jumped from his chair when protesters began shouting, before being removed by \uc2 Capitol police\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat was a made for \uc2 C-Span\uc2  moment,\u8221\'20\'1D said senator \uc2 Bill Cassidy\uc2  , the Republican chair of the committee.\par \par \uc2 Dozens of federal health workers and offices dedicated to HIV/Aids research have been shuttered under Kennedy\u8217\'20\'19s watch.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-14T18:47:33.896Z">at 7.47pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-14T18:38:15.814Z">7.38pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 RFK Jr defends staff cuts, funding freezes and drastic policy changes\par \par \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr has spent the day defending deep staffing cuts, research funding freezes and drastic policy changes in his department during his first appearance on Capitol Hill as health secretary.\par \par \uc2 Kennedy appeared at a House appropriations hearing earlier this morning to defend the White House\u8217\'20\'19s requested budget for his agency, including a $500m boost for his \u8220\'20\'1Cmake America healthy again\u8221\'20\'1D initiative.\par \par \uc2 Since his confirmation, Kennedy has slashed 10,000 jobs including at the country\u8217\'20\'19s top food and drugs regulator, public health agency and biomedical research institute.\par \par \uc2 Asked if he would give his children the measles vaccine today, Kennedy sidestepped the question. He said:\par \par \uc2 Measles? Probably for measles. What I would say is my opinions about vaccines are irrelevant. I don\u8217\'20\'19t think people should be taking advice, medical advice, from me.\par \par \uc2 Asked if he would vaccinate his kids today against chickenpox and polio, Kennedy refused to answer, only saying: \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t want to give advice.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-14T18:57:19.658Z">at 7.57pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-14T18:20:27.159Z">7.20pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 newest tax bill threatens to exclude millions of families from a tax credit meant to ease household financial burdens, even as conservatives are increasingly claiming to tout policies designed to entice families to have more babies.\par \par \uc2 One provision in the bill, which runs nearly 400 pages, seeks to raise the child tax credit from the current $2,000 level to $2,500 per child \u8211\'20\'13 but an estimated 17 million children would be ineligible to receive the full credit because their parents do not make enough to qualify, according to a congressional estimate.\par \par \uc2 Another provision of the bill would require a US citizen child\u8217\'20\'19s parent or guardian to possess a social security number in order to claim the credit; if the child\u8217\'20\'19s parents are married and file their taxes together, both parents would need social security numbers.\par \par \uc2 This requirement would make undocumented immigrants and other immigrants who lack work authorization ineligible to claim the credit on behalf of children who are US citizens or legal permanent residents, stripping the benefit from a number of families who would otherwise receive it.\par \par \uc2 Under current requirements, families of children with social security numbers are eligible regardless of the parents\u8217\'20\'19 status. <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/14/republican-bill-child-tax-credits"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans push for bigger families \u8211\'20\'13 but their tax bill could exclude millions from child credits}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-14T17:42:29.247Z">6.42pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Here are some more photos from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s visit to Qatar where he is attending a state dinner at Lusail Palace. He will no doubt have been pleased by the abundance of marble and camels.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-14T17:43:40.140Z">at 6.43pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-14T17:05:06.629Z">6.05pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 US secretary of state \uc2 Marco Rubio\uc2  has left Doha and is en route to Antalya , Turkey , where he will meet \uc2 Nato\uc2  foreign ministers on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 It comes ahead of his planned travel onwards to Istanbul on Friday, where the state department says he will attend talks with European counterparts to discuss the war in Ukraine .\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-14T17:00:03.535Z">6.00pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Judge orders immediate release of Indian academic detained by Ice over pro-Palestinian views\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/virginia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Virginia}}}\uc2  federal judge has ordered the immediate release of Georgetown academic Badar Khan Suri from Ice detention during a hearing on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Khan Suri was among {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/apr/28/trump-immigration-people-detained-deported-cases"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 several individuals legally studying}}}\uc2  in the US who have been targeted by the Trump administration for their pro-Palestinian activism . He has spent two months in detention.\par \par \uc2 US district judge Patricia Giles in Alexandria, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/virginia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Virginia}}}\uc2 , said that the ruling is effective immediately with no conditions and no bond.\par \par \uc2 The Trump administration had ordered the detention of Khan Suri, a citizen of India, on 17 March. He was previously being held at an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/usimmigration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 immigration}}}\uc2  prison in Alvarado, Texas.\par \par \uc2 Immigration officials revoked his J-1 student visa, alleging his father-in-law was an adviser to \uc2 Hamas\uc2  officials more than a decade ago in addition to claims that he was \u8220\'20\'1Cdeportable\u8221\'20\'1D because of his posts on social media in support of Palestine .\par \par \uc2 Khan Suri, who is married to a Palestinian-American US citizen, Mapheze Saleh, is a senior postdoctoral fellow at the institution\u8217\'20\'19s Alwaleed Bin Talal Center for Muslim-Christian Understanding (ACMCU). Many students and alumni of the institution {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/apr/14/georgetown-professor-detained"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 signed a letter}}}\uc2  opposing his detention by Ice.\par \par \uc2 Giles prohibited federal officials in March from deporting the postdoctoral fellow after his wife filed an emergency court request to prevent deportation. <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/14/judge-order-release-khan-suri-ice"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Judge orders release of Indian academic detained by Ice over pro-Palestinian views}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-14T17:47:15.214Z">at 6.47pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-14T16:49:27.406Z">5.49pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 According to \uc2 Boeing\uc2  , the 747-8 can travel the length of \u8220\'20\'1Cthree FIFA soccer fields\u8221\'20\'1D in one second. It has a tail as tall as an average six-storey city building, is the \u8220\'20\'1Cworld\u8217\'20\'19s fastest commercial jet\u8221\'20\'1D and is capable, theoretically, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IR8i1vwtdKUbVswsqR3A48nsxzRW70mo038ZvUFQB83QGDeZP7oULJ-8X6CjqnlO1bxeSAzMiq4evNpxeF9gt3-rzmdHI0Hy54LVoAOH-TvLwevqHWTrTFBEeFeEar6bGhvTZ1WVTlmDXuB0TdyfBHEwlETPTr-bQEFZwTrARkoXUMGUfNEbu0QIv26DLX3NUQ6fcPnUg5RY4VglLUwUd_Ip5tOKmzLM7Vu_Br52Nbbd6PuWiNbncH2YdvysiYs1t5Mie6NjVB6PXtK0BvlRbe9-JhdchDr7T7lZzOALURq9cdFDtkJEh0lkAhjbq29OlDw/4gh/m1pAtDslT4uUpusVDX_pag/h19/h001.iJG8IiYtOSRKls5PLrr24twAeMFUpBc-X34tFyKjZVA"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 of transporting 10,767 solid gold bars}}}\uc2  from Fort Knox.\par \par \uc2 What \uc2 Boeing\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s marketing spiel doesn\u8217\'20\'19t mention is that the 747-8 is also capable of serving as a giant flying metaphor for corruption, after it emerged that Qatar {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHEAkCD247PEzzJghnkN7Siw6DdbVZhvzkJzsLjoVIPpy5F93Sbpou3GE76Fa3atJVfNBWouX9Creutv0qrb3lXEoJ9GFW_mHSYVpRxwy8SVlKlSKFjwwQ3xudz3B1Fgdg-bQYaHTTN2IcmpLVAkVYjiwzy8db-LU-10a3SIK_CEw6ot2pGs-EOFIEBM1Nexiu_9uk6TO5U9a1FqY0iRJEGfO65xYNWUxLAGcfcdfbCmAnR2tfKYnFbNQoX50S7SbmWvOs7tTnNDbb5PokcLAK9bRYSY_a2f-mjVADXzU-ac2ve3BenM_LCl9gj0WNZ9qHe0/4gh/m1pAtDslT4uUpusVDX_pag/h20/h001.dS29pgzv35brsRFYUnfBF3Ii8MgBf_9IYpQe49wnpIY"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 planned to gift one of the $400m planes}}}\uc2  to the Trump administration, with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  planning to use it as Air Force One before handing it over to his presidential library.\par \par \uc2 Amid criticism, the president initially defended the move as a money-saving effort. But in the days following it has become clear that another thing was on his mind: that other people have big planes, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/14/trump-plane-gift-qatar"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he wants one too}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The transaction actually makes little sense financially. Experts {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IR_rX2Um48LB606KYZ_c-OQ7hQo8j1atD674nZuqP2X5YkrdVWyJsW67yP9gumj5N6nxdGRFb38VaTf1nPPqgQ0v-dOm4Emz3qNYvo4c8scokLmv2ZYATiM-1iaYEvXQCkmeKCu_l-BVqHYrqjUmpQ2DIYgxoSCBOHqRMAW4jMvPAVwsXPEW166feP6P4AFeel7bKG6jcB7C9o0h7qAdu5qKSScIzAA7gdmSmB7kOqbgYOc3MCZFrc-lOyV8OXqMh_rTkxWpkTmQo-PfzaLhYDzylwzgFAA9igrlIoUykaSMC-RBNMiJIbM1Ik6A279weeo_VnHifdCckGF-SUUUI4Ez5xxc24Fxzyo3eTdARdgeBsYITjGNwwBv2hLm2PJdNBHr-qe0d8S-92HFXB2dC_wA/4gh/m1pAtDslT4uUpusVDX_pag/h28/h001.4okyRuIiKi59WQbY33dXzHdP0ZMquumHYox8otN5zns"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told NBC News}}}\uc2  that converting the 747 into Air Force One would cost more than $1bn and take \u8220\'20\'1Cyears\u8221\'20\'1D to complete \u8211\'20\'13 potentially not even being ready by the end of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s term.\par \par \uc2 You can sign up for Adam\u8217\'20\'19s weekly newsletter This Week in Trumpland {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/25/election-newsletter-sign-up-stakes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-14T16:29:50.460Z">5.29pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Commerce secretary \uc2 Howard Lutnick\uc2 's links to El Salvador crypto firm under scrutiny\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/trump-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump administration}}}\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s commerce secretary, \uc2 Howard Lutnick\uc2  , and his family have had extensive business interests linked to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/el-salvador"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 El Salvador}}}\uc2 , whose authoritarian leader \uc2 Nayib Bukele\uc2  has grown close to the White House and who has courted controversy by imprisoning people deported from the US in an aggressive {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/usimmigration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 immigration}}}\uc2  crackdown.\par \par \uc2 El Salvador also plays host to a booming {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/cryptocurrencies"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cryptocurrency}}}\uc2  and new media industry, which has numerous ties to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  allies who are seeking to make money from various ventures which have sometimes drawn the attention of authorities or ethics watchdogs.\par \par \uc2 Securities and Exchange Commission and Office of Government Ethics (OGE) filings, along with public records in the US and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/el-salvador"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 El Salvador}}}\uc2 , indicate that \uc2 Cantor Fitzgerald\uc2  , the firm Lutnick headed until weeks ago before handing off to a management team including two of his sons, holds an effective 5% stake in the cryptocurrency firm Tether , has negotiated several investments on behalf of the highly profitable company, and is custodian of the US treasury holdings from which those profits arise. <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/14/lutnick-el-salvador-crypto-immigration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump cabinet member\u8217\'20\'19s links to El Salvador crypto firm under scrutiny}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-14T16:25:43.050Z">5.25pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Trump doubles down on luxury $400m plane gift from Qatar\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has doubled down on why he wants to accept a luxury \uc2 Boeing\uc2  747 from Qatar , a country where he traveled to today to negotiate business deals, with the US president portraying the $400m aircraft as an opportunity too valuable to refuse.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe plane that you\u8217\'20\'19re on is almost 40 years old,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump told Fox News host \uc2 Sean Hannity\uc2  during an Air Force One interview on the Middle East trip, where he is also visiting {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/saudiarabia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Saudi Arabia}}}\uc2  and the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/united-arab-emirates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 UAE}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 When you land and you see Saudi Arabia, you see UAE and you see {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/qatar"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Qatar}}}\uc2 , and they have these brand-new \uc2 Boeing\uc2  747s, mostly. You see ours next to it \u8211\'20\'13 this is like a totally different plane.\par \par \uc2 Clearly irritated by questions about the ethical criticism of accepting such a lavish gift as president, Trump insisted American prestige was at stake .\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re the United States of America. I believe we should have the most impressive plane.\par \par \uc2 The timing of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s visit has raised eyebrows, coming just weeks after the \uc2 Trump Organization\uc2  secured a deal with Qatar for a luxury resort and golf course development outside the capital, Doha, called Trump International Golf Club & Villas .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy attitude is why wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t I accept a gift?\u8221\'20\'1D Trump continued. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re giving to everybody else, why wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t I accept a gift? Because it\u8217\'20\'19s going to be a couple years until the Boeings are finished.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump was referring to the incoming Air Force One fleet, a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.af.mil/News/Article-Display/Article/1579091/air-force-formalizes-air-force-one-replacement-deal-with-contract-to-boeing/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $3.9bn contract}}}\uc2  given to \uc2 Boeing\uc2  in 2018 with an original timetable of 2024 that has since been delayed by a number of years.\par \par \uc2 The US attorney general, Pam Bondi , who worked as a lobbyist for Qatar while at her previous employer Ballard Partners, has reportedly declared accepting the aircraft \u8220\'20\'1Clegally permissible\u8221\'20\'1D. <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/14/trump-plane-gift-qatar"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump doubles down on luxury aircraft gift from Qatar}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-14T16:19:33.086Z">5.19pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Toddler left behind in US last year after parents deported arrives in Venezuela\par \par \uc2 A Venezuelan toddler who was separated from her parents when they crossed the US-Mexico border a year ago and who remained in the US when they were deported arrived in Venezuela on a removal flight on Wednesday, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 Major figures in Venezuela\u8217\'20\'19s government, which is under extensive US sanctions, had repeatedly called for Maikelys Antonella Espinoza Bernal , aged 2, to be returned to her mother, Yorely Bernal, who was deported back to Venezuela in April. Last month the foreign ministry went as far as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2025/04/30/americas/venezuela-child-separated-mother-latam-intl"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 accusing the US of \u8220\'20\'1Ckidnapping\u8221\'20\'1D the child}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Images on state television showed first lady Cilia Flores holding the child in her arms at the international airport near Caracas.\par \par \uc2 The toddler\u8217\'20\'19s return has been \u8220\'20\'1Ca battle every day and today we have a great victory,\u8221\'20\'1D said interior minister \uc2 Diosdado Cabello\uc2 , who was also at the airport.\par \par \uc2 Her parents had entered the US in May 2024 seeking asylum, and had been in immigrant detention during their entire stay in the country after turning themselves in at the border. Meanwhile their little girl was placed in the care of a foster family via the Office of Refugee Resettlement in the US.\par \par \uc2 The baby\u8217\'20\'19s father, Maiker Espinoza, 25, was sent to Cecot , the notorious maximum security prison in El Salvador where the Trump administration has sent at least 137 Venezuelans under the 1798 Alien Enemies Act, in March.\par \par \uc2 The department of homeland security (DHS) denied that it had kidnapped the child and said she was removed from the deportation flight list \u8220\'20\'1Cfor her safety and welfare\u8221\'20\'1D, claiming without evidence in late-April that Espinoza is a member the Venezuela gang Tren De Aragua .\par \par \uc2 Espinoza\u8217\'20\'19s family roundly denied the claim to Reuters. \u8220\'20\'1CAt no time has my son been involved with [Tren de Aragua],\u8221\'20\'1D his mother, Maria Escalona, told Reuters this month. \u8220\'20\'1CI think this is political - they are using the case of my son to cover up the horror that is being committed against all these innocents.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 DHS said the child\u8217\'20\'19s mother Bernal recruited young women for drug smuggling and sex work, though it also provided no evidence. The family has also denied the claim. She was deported without her child \u8211\'20\'13 it is unclear if Bernal was given the choice to be deported with her daughter.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-14T15:56:57.848Z">4.56pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 The White House has published a \u8220\'20\'1Cfact sheet\u8221\'20\'1D detailing the agreements signed by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and Qatar\u8217\'20\'19s emir, Sheikh Tamim bin Hamad Al-Thani, on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The agreements will \u8220\'20\'1Cgenerate an economic exchange worth at least $1.2 trillion,\u8221\'20\'1D it claims.\par \par \uc2 They include a $96bn agreement with \uc2 Qatar Airways\uc2  to buy up to 210 \uc2 Boeing\uc2  787 Dreamliner and 777X planes, as well as a statement of intent that could lead to $38bn in investments at Qatar\u8217\'20\'19s Al Udeid Air Base and other air defense and maritime security capabilities. The fact sheet writes:\par \par \uc2 The landmark deals celebrated today will drive innovation and prosperity for generations, bolster American manufacturing and technological leadership, and put America on the path to a new Golden Age.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-14T15:47:15.467Z">4.47pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Qatar \u8217\'20\'19s central bank\uc2  governor, Sheikh Bandar bin Mohammed bin Saoud Al Thani, met with \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  in Doha on Wednesday to discuss developments in global finance and investment, the bank said.\par \par \uc2 The meeting was held on the sidelines of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s visit to Qatar.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-14T15:34:17.023Z">4.34pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Republican House speaker Mike Johnson declined to weigh in on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s plans to accept a luxury \uc2 Boeing\uc2  747 from Qatar.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s not my lane,\u8221\'20\'1D Johnson said during a press conference on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 He added that he\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cnot following all of the twists and turns\u8221\'20\'1D of the case as he focuses on passing a budget reconciliation bill.\par \par \uc2 The idea of accepting a plane from Qatar has triggered alarm across the political spectrum, including even staunch Trump allies.\par \par \uc2 Texas senator Ted Cruz warned that the aircraft deal \u8220\'20\'1Cposes significant espionage and surveillance problems\u8221\'20\'1D, while the West Virginia senator \uc2 Shelley Moore Capito\uc2  said bluntly she\u8217\'20\'19d \u8220\'20\'1Cbe checking for bugs\u8221\'20\'1D. Former US ambassador to the \uc2 UN\uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  , called the acceptance of foreign gifts \u8220\'20\'1Cnever a good practice\u8221\'20\'1D that \u8220\'20\'1Cthreatens intelligence and national security\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-14T15:26:02.492Z">4.26pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Here are some of the latest images from the newswires from Qatar, where its emir Sheikh Tamim bin Hamad Al Thani welcomed \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for his latest stage of his Middle East tour.\par \par \uc2 The two leaders signed a number of economic and defense agreements, including an order from Qatar for 160 \uc2 Boeing\uc2  jets worth more than $200bn.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-14T15:11:41.142Z">4.11pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Non-profit groups are sounding the alarm over an attempt by Republican lawmakers to insert a provision allowing the government to cancel the tax-exempt status of organizations it deems \u8220\'20\'1Cterrorist supporting\u8221\'20\'1D in a massive bill under negotiation in the House of Representatives.\par \par \uc2 The provision\u8217\'20\'19s potential inclusion in the spending and taxation legislation that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his allies refer to as \u8220\'20\'1C{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/apr/26/republicans-trump-budget-bill"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 one big, beautiful bill}}}\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D has sparked fears that the administration will wield it against groups who file lawsuits or organize voters against his policies.\par \par \uc2 Lia Holland, campaigns and communications director at tech policy non-profit \uc2 Fight for the Future\uc2 , described the provision as \u8220\'20\'1Ca five-alarm fire for non-profits nationwide\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAny organization with goals that do not line up with Maga can be destroyed with a wink from Trump to the treasury\u8221\'20\'1D, likely those that oppose his policies towards Israel, or advocate for causes like racial justice and the environment, they said.\par \par \uc2 Trump had made plain his desire for revenge against his enemies, and since taking office has sought to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/mar/25/pro-palestine-student-deportation-lawsuit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 deport foreign students}}}\uc2  who engaged in pro-Palestinian activism, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/02/trump-perkins-coie-unconstitutional"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 blacklisted law firms}}}\uc2  who have worked for his political opponents and backed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/apr/25/judge-hannah-dugan-milwaukee-arrest"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the arrest of a county judge}}}\uc2  on charges of obstructing immigration authorities. <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/14/tax-status-non-profits-terrorism-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republican tax bill could slap \u8216\'20\'18terrorism\u8217\'20\'19 label on non-profits opposed to Trump}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-14T14:46:25.073Z">3.46pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Republicans advance Trump's tax cut plan after all-night debate\par \par \uc2 Back in the US, Reuters reports that congressional Republicans advanced elements of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s sweeping budget package on Wednesday after a debate that lasted through the night, as a key committee voted along party lines to approve tax cuts that would add trillions of dollars to the national debt.\par \par \uc2 The 26-19 vote by the tax-writing House ways and means committee amounts to an initial victory for Republicans, who still have many hurdles to clear before they can get the sprawling package of tax cuts, spending hikes and safety-net reductions to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s desk to sign into law. The vote came after an all-night debate that saw at least one lawmaker fall asleep at his post.\par \par \uc2 Republicans rejected a series of proposed changes by opposition Democrats, who blasted the bill as a wasteful giveaway to the wealthy that would shred health and food benefits for the poor and worsen the nation\u8217\'20\'19s financial standing.\par \par \uc2 A separate House committee was still debating a GOP proposal to tighten eligibility for the Medicaid health plan, which covers 71 million low-income Americans, with a vote expected later in the day. That would save the federal government $715bn and kick 7.7 million people off the program, according to the nonpartisan \uc2 Congressional Budget Office\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Police escorted out at least five protesters, including three who were in wheelchairs, at the outset of that debate on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 A third panel was due to resume debate on a proposal to require some people who receive Snap food benefits to get a job and shift some costs to states.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cbig, beautiful bill\u8221\'20\'1D would add trillions of dollars to the nation\u8217\'20\'19s debt load, which at $36.2tn now equals 127% of GDP. The package calls for $4tn in additional borrowing, though the total cost is uncertain at this point.\par \par \uc2 Republicans will need to stay united to pass the bill out of the House, where they hold a narrow 220-213 majority. The proposal will also need to clear the Senate, which Republicans control 53-47.\par \par \uc2 The country\u8217\'20\'19s looming debt ceiling deadline this summer is also pushing Republicans to work fast. The package would raise the debt limit by $4tn and treasury secretary Scott Bessent has urged lawmakers to act by mid-July to avoid a default that would upend the global economy.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-14T15:01:37.406Z">at 4.01pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-14T14:11:56.576Z">3.11pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Looking around the room, Trump compliments the marble {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2025/may/14/donald-trump-syria-middle-east-gulf-latest-us-politics-news-updates-live?CMP=share_btn_url&page=with%3Ablock-68248e7f8f08426112ae2f3f#block-68248e7f8f08426112ae2f3f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 again}}}\uc2 : \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s the real deal, it\u8217\'20\'19s very hard to buy.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 And that\u8217\'20\'19s it, the ceremony is over.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-14T14:12:57.040Z">at 3.12pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-14T14:11:03.583Z">3.11pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 'We just like each other,' Trump says of Qatar's emir\par \par \uc2 Trump says the US has a \u8220\'20\'1Cvery special relationship\u8221\'20\'1D with Qatar, and then oddly compares the emir to the Saudi crown prince \uc2 Mohammed bin Salman\uc2  saying they\u8217\'20\'19re both \u8220\'20\'1Ctall handsome guys that happen to be very smart\u8221\'20\'1D. He spoke similarly of Syrian president Ahmed al-Sharaa {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2025/may/14/donald-trump-syria-middle-east-gulf-latest-us-politics-news-updates-live?CMP=share_btn_url&page=with%3Ablock-682489028f08426112ae2eea#block-682489028f08426112ae2eea"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 earlier}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 He thanks the emir for their friendship: \u8220\'20\'1CWe just like each other.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-14T14:52:58.581Z">at 3.52pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-14T14:07:41.581Z">3.07pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Trump says Qatar $200bn agreement is 'largest order of jets' in history of \uc2 Boeing\par \par \uc2 Trump says the two leaders have discussed Russia and Ukraine, as well as Iran, which he says Qatar has been \u8220\'20\'1Ca great help\u8221\'20\'1D with. He says he believes the Iran situation \u8220\'20\'1Cwill work out\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He then says the \uc2 Boeing\uc2  agreement is the \u8220\'20\'1Clargest order of jets\u8221\'20\'1D in the history of the company.\par \par \uc2 He says the deal is worth $200bn and includes 160 jets.\par \par \uc2 He says tomorrow there will be \u8220\'20\'1Csort of an air fair\u8221\'20\'1D that will show the \u8220\'20\'1Clatest\u8221\'20\'1D planes.\par \par \uc2 The leaders also signed a number of agreements in the field of defense, including a statement of intent on military cooperation between the US and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/qatar"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Qatar}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-14T14:22:06.140Z">at 3.22pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-14T14:07:06.230Z">3.07pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 The emir says that with the signing of these documents, the two countries\u8217\'20\'19 relationship is reaching \u8220\'20\'1Canother level\u8221\'20\'1D and thanks Trump for his \u8220\'20\'1Chistoric\u8221\'20\'1D visit.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-14T14:04:56.527Z">3.04pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 They are now signing a joint declaration of cooperation between the two countries. Trump\u8217\'20\'19s pen appeared to run out of ink and he was swiftly offered a fresh one from the emir.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-14T16:51:26.478Z">at 5.51pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-14T14:03:47.052Z">3.03pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 They are now signing a number of agreements in the field of defense, including a statement of intent on military cooperation between the US and Qatar.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-14T14:04:06.044Z">at 3.04pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-14T14:01:16.120Z">3.01pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 The leaders have arrived now for the signing ceremony relating to the purchase of aircraft from \uc2 Boeing\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-14T13:47:27.892Z">2.47pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and Sheikh Tamim bin Hamad al-Thani are expected to make statements shortly. I\u8217\'20\'19ll bring you the key lines when they do.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-14T13:33:42.830Z">2.33pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 'Something wrong with him': Trump attacks Schumer for obstructing justice department picks over Qatar jet gift\par \par \uc2 Earlier \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  said that there\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Csomething wrong\u8221\'20\'1D with Senate minority leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  , in response to the senator placing a blanket hold on all justice department political nominees until the White House provides answers about plans to accept a $4oom luxury jet from Qatar for presidential use, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/politics/live-news/trump-middle-east-news-05-14-25#cmanwisen001g3b6m3nn9rr0o"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CNN reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The New York senator {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/13/chuck-schumer-trumps-justice-department-nominees-qatar-aircraft"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 declared the hold}}}\uc2  amid growing controversy over the constitutional and security implications of accepting a foreign government\u8217\'20\'19s offer to provide what would become the new Air Force One.\par \par \uc2 During a gaggle on Air Force One en route to Doha, Trump said:\par \par \uc2 Something wrong with him, I don\u8217\'20\'19t know. I\u8217\'20\'19ve known him a long time and there\u8217\'20\'19s something wrong. He\u8217\'20\'19s lost his confidence totally. And there\u8217\'20\'19s something wrong with him. I don\u8217\'20\'19t know what it is with Schumer.\par \par \uc2 Though the procedural maneuver cannot completely block nominees, it forces Senate Republicans to use valuable floor time to overcome Democratic opposition through individual confirmation votes. <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/13/chuck-schumer-trumps-justice-department-nominees-qatar-aircraft"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Chuck Schumer says he\u8217\'20\'19ll obstruct Trump\u8217\'20\'19s justice department picks over Qatar jet gift}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-14T13:42:26.758Z">at 2.42pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-14T13:27:26.328Z">2.27pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a shot of the camels \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2025/may/14/donald-trump-syria-middle-east-gulf-latest-us-politics-news-updates-live?CMP=share_btn_url&page=with%3Ablock-68248e7f8f08426112ae2f3f#block-68248e7f8f08426112ae2f3f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 so impressed by}}}\uc2  earlier, via White House aide Margot Martin . <figure class="element element-tweet" data-canonical-url="https://twitter.com/MargoMartin47/status/1922621403007754506">\par \par \uc2 Scene in Qatar from President Trump\u8217\'20\'19s motorcade! {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/20I4DEQuZ6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/20I4DEQuZ6}}}\uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Margo Martin (@MargoMartin47) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MargoMartin47/status/1922621403007754506?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 14, 2025}}}\uc2  </figure>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-14T13:15:59.296Z">2.15pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 The foreign ministers of Turkey , the United States and Syria will meet in southern Turkey on Thursday to discuss details of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s pledge to lift sanctions on Syria, Turkish foreign minister \uc2 Hakan Fidan\uc2  has said.\par \par \uc2 Speaking to state broadcaster TRT Haber ahead of an informal Nato foreign ministers\u8217\'20\'19 meeting in the southern Turkish province of Antalya, Fidan said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/14/trump-meets-syria-president-after-lifting-us-sanctions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the leaders\u8217\'20\'19 meeting}}}\uc2  on Wednesday was of \u8220\'20\'1Chistoric importance\u8221\'20\'1D. He said the lifting of sanctions would enable financial flows, investment and infrastructure development in Syria, which was politically fractured and left in widespread ruins by the 14-year-long civil war.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNow tomorrow, we, as the three foreign ministers - Mr [Marco] Rubio, Mr [Assad] Al-Shibani, and myself - will come together after the Nato meeting in Antalya and we will work on how to carry forward the details of the agreement that the leaders set the framework for and agreed upon,\u8221\'20\'1D Fidan said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COf course, there is a [congressional] leg to this matter in the United States, there is an administration leg, but there is a will that Mr Trump has put forth from the start,\u8221\'20\'1D he added. \u8220\'20\'1CWithin the framework of this will, and the work we will do, we hope the majority of these sanctions will be lifted as soon as possible.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Removing US sanctions that cut Syria off from the global financial system will clear the way for greater engagement by humanitarian organisations working in the country, easing foreign investment and trade as the country rebuilds.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-14T12:55:09.202Z">1.55pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Here is the clip from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s meeting with Qatar\u8217\'20\'19s emir Sheikh Tamim bin Hamad al-Thani , who said the agenda for the president\u8217\'20\'19s visit will focus on investments, energy, military cooperation and security, as well as bringing peace to the region. <figure class="element element-atom"> <gu-atom data-atom-id="3e05caf9-3b14-4191-918a-6326ad995988" data-atom-type="media"> </gu-atom> </figure>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-14T12:45:10.986Z">1.45pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 'Perfecto' marble: Trump impressed with Qatari palace interiors\par \par \uc2 As Trump arrived in Doha earlier, a lavish welcome reception and brief remarks with the Qatari emir Sheikh Tamim bin Hamad al-Thani followed, according to a pool report.\par \par \uc2 Military officers were called into formation and a band played the Star-Spangled Banner, to which the US president stood in a salute.\par \par \uc2 The leaders then walked into a luxurious, incense-scented room, and the emir spoke about investments and cooperation between the two countries.\par \par \uc2 We are very excited. Mr President, I\u8217\'20\'19ve known you for many year. I know that you are a man of peace. I know that you want to bring peace to this region . I hope that this time we can do the right thing and bring peace here in the region.\par \par \uc2 He mentioned the US hosting the World Cup (\u8220\'20\'1Cfootball. As you guys call it, soccer\u8221\'20\'1D) and how Qatar hosted it previously. \u8220\'20\'1CThere wasn\u8217\'20\'19t one incident here,\u8221\'20\'1D he said of their event in 2022. \u8220\'20\'1CYou did a great job,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump responded.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve liked each other and worked with each other,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd now we can work in the highest capacity.\u8221\'20\'1D He said he appreciated their cooperation, including with Russia and Ukraine .\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ll bring peace, not only here, but I know you\u8217\'20\'19re very much involved in helping us in other regions like what\u8217\'20\'19s happening with Russia-Ukraine etc. And I think we\u8217\'20\'19re having some pretty good news coming out of there today and maybe tomorrow and maybe Friday frankly. But we\u8217\'20\'19ll see about that.\par \par \uc2 He paused and looked around, marveling at the architecture.\par \par \uc2 The job you\u8217\'20\'19ve done is second to none. You look at this, it\u8217\'20\'19s so beautiful. As a construction person, I\u8217\'20\'19m seeing perfect marble. This is what they call perfecto .\par \par \uc2 Trump also remarked about the camels he saw upon arrival.\par \par \uc2 We appreciate those camels. I haven\u8217\'20\'19t seen camels like that in a long time. And it was some greeting, we appreciate it very much.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-14T13:40:00.967Z">at 2.40pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-14T12:24:34.515Z">1.24pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Trump says he's still open to attending talks on Ukraine, but unsure about whether Putin will go\par \par \uc2 While en route to Qatar, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  also told reporters aboard Air Force One he was still considering whether to attend talks on the war in Ukraine planned for Thursday in Turkey but he does not know whether Russian president \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  will go.\par \par \uc2 [Putin would] like me to be there, and that\u8217\'20\'19s a possibility ... I don\u8217\'20\'19t know that he would be there if I\u8217\'20\'19m not there. We\u8217\'20\'19re going to find out.\par \par \uc2 Trump has said he may visit Turkey for the talks as part of his trip to the Middle East this week. He cited his next stop to the United Arab Emirates on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have a very full situation. Now that doesn\u8217\'20\'19t mean I wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t do it to save a lot of lives and come back,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said, according to a pool report from the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Yesterday Trump announced that secretary of state \uc2 Marco Rubio\uc2  would be attending Thursday\u8217\'20\'19s talks in Istanbul.\par \par \uc2 Ukrainian president \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskyy\uc2  on Tuesday said he would only attend if Putin was also there. On Wednesday, the Kremlin said it would send a delegation to Istanbul but did not say who would be representing Moscow.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-14T12:26:35.196Z">at 1.26pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-14T12:19:19.082Z">1.19pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 'Young, attractive guy, tough guy': Trump praises Syrian president Ahmed al-Sharaa\par \par \uc2 Before touching down in Qatar a little while ago, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  told reporters on Air Force One that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/14/trump-meets-syria-president-after-lifting-us-sanctions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 his brief meeting}}}\uc2  with the Syrian president in Saudi Arabia this morning went \u8220\'20\'1Cgreat\u8221\'20\'1D, saying of Ahmed al-Sharaa :\par \par \uc2 Young, attractive guy. Tough guy. Strong past. Very strong past. Fighter.\par \par \uc2 Trump added:\par \par \uc2 He\u8217\'20\'19s got a real shot at holding it together. I spoke with President Erdo\u287\'01\'1Fan, who is very friendly with him. He feels he\u8217\'20\'19s got a shot of doing a good job. It\u8217\'20\'19s a torn-up country.\par \par \uc2 The US president said he thought Syria would join {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2025/may/14/donald-trump-syria-middle-east-gulf-latest-us-politics-news-updates-live?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with%3Ablock-682467818f089320ecd28fb2#block-682467818f089320ecd28fb2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Abraham Accords}}}\uc2  at some point, to normalise relations with Israel .\par \par \uc2 I think they have to get themselves straightened up. I told him: \u8216\'20\'18I hope you\u8217\'20\'19re going to join when it\u8217\'20\'19s straightened out.\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 He said: \u8216\'20\'18Yes.\u8217\'20\'19 But they have a lot of work to do.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s the clip. <figure class="element element-atom"> <gu-atom data-atom-id="155c4f0c-925e-445d-a12b-1177221741cb" data-atom-type="media"> </gu-atom> </figure>\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-14T14:48:29.680Z">at 3.48pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-14T12:13:35.016Z">1.13pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Trump touches down in Qatar for day two in Middle East amid furore back home over gift of $400m luxury jet\par \par \uc2 Here are some photos from Trump\u8217\'20\'19s arrival in Qatar, the second stop on his three-day tour of the Middle East aimed at drumming up investment and economic deals.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-14T12:34:41.209Z">at 1.34pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-14T12:00:41.241Z">1.00pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 And, for those interested in revisiting just why \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s acceptance of the Qatari plane has proved so controversial, here is Ed Pilkington\u8217\'20\'19s analysis of the scandal.\par \par \uc2 Accepting a \u8220\'20\'1Cgift\u8221\'20\'1D of a luxury jet from Qatar is just the most eye-catching of the president\u8217\'20\'19s ethically questionable acts, he writes.\par \par \uc2 See the full piece here: <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/13/trump-quid-pro-quo-qatar-plane"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump 2.0 takes quid pro quo fears to new heights with $400m flying grift}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-14T12:22:29.623Z">at 1.22pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-14T11:50:06.131Z">12.50pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 With \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in Doha for his Qatari state visit , attention will turn to his acceptance of a $400m \u8216\'20\'18palace in the sky\u8217\'20\'19 airplane.\par \par \uc2 The gift has proven highly controversial not just among his political opponents \u8211\'20\'13 the Democrats are flying a protest banner over Mar-a-Lago today \u8211\'20\'13 but also his Maga allies.\par \par \uc2 Ben Shapiro\uc2 , the prominent rightwing commentator, led the charge on his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mediamatters.org/ben-shapiro/it-needs-stop-ben-shapiro-calls-out-trumps-skeezy-stuff-crypto-scheme-and-accepting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 daily podcast}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CPresident Trump promised to drain the swamp \u8211\'20\'13 this is not, in fact, draining the swamp,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Linking {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/qatar"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Qatar}}}\uc2  to the militant Palestinian group \uc2 Hamas\uc2  and Al Jazeera, the media network that is widely detested on the right and is partly funded by the Qatari government, he added: \u8220\'20\'1CTaking sacks of goodies from people who support \uc2 Hamas\uc2 , \uc2 Muslim Brotherhood\uc2 , Al Jazeera, all the rest, that\u8217\'20\'19s not America First \u8230\'20\'26 If you want President Trump to succeed this kind of skeezy stuff would be stopped.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The planned gift of the 13-year-old \uc2 Boeing\uc2  747-8 jumbo jet, which Trump would inherit personally after he leaves the White House, has achieved the seemingly impossible: it has united the president\u8217\'20\'19s most fervent fans with his most ardent opponents. Laura Loomer, the far-right Maga activist, warned that the proposed gift would put \u8220\'20\'1Csuch a stain on the administration\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Loomer said she loved Trump and would \u8220\'20\'1Ctake a bullet for him. But I have to call a spade a spade. We cannot accept a $400m \u8216\'20\'18gift\u8217\'20\'19 from jihadists in suits.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The conservative New York Post, meanwhile, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nypost.com/2025/05/12/opinion/no-pres-trump-qatars-palace-in-the-sky-jet-isnt-a-free-gift-and-you-shouldnt-accept-it-as-one/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 published}}}\uc2  an editorial headlined: \u8220\'20\'1CQatar\u8217\'20\'19s \u8216\'20\'18Palace in the Sky\u8217\'20\'19 jet is NOT a \u8216\'20\'18free gift\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 and Trump shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t accept it as one.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-14T12:06:04.246Z">at 1.06pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-14T11:44:50.175Z">12.44pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Justice department officials have asked civil rights division attorneys to reconsider their decision to leave the department in recent weeks, according to people familiar with the matter, a sign that the agency may have been caught off-guard by the wave of personnel leaving.\par \par \uc2 Officials have also asked attorneys, including {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/apr/28/trump-doj-voting-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 career managers}}}\uc2 , who were involuntarily detailed to low-level offices last month, if they would consider returning to their sections to handle civil rights work, the people said. The attorneys were removed in late April in what was widely understood as an effort to force them to accept a paid offer to leave the department.\par \par \uc2 Leadership had also encouraged employees to accept the paid offer to leave. As a 28 April deadline approached for accepting the paid leave offer, Michael Gates, a political appointee in the civil rights division, told section chiefs there would be a \u8220\'20\'1Ctightening of the belt\u8221\'20\'1D moving forward, a person familiar with the matter said.\par \par \uc2 More than 250 civil rights division attorneys have left since January or are planning to leave, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/01/civil-rights-division-doj-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an approximate 70% reduction}}}\uc2  in the division\u8217\'20\'19s personnel.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s unclear how many attorneys were asked to stay and how many, if any, accepted. \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  has confirmed that the request was made at least of attorneys in the educational opportunities section, which enforces anti-discrimination law in schools. Many of the Trump administration\u8217\'20\'19s priorities, including challenging DEI programs, investigating allegations of antisemitism on campuses and limiting the rights of transgender people, fall under the purview of the section. <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/14/justice-department-civil-rights-attorneys-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US justice department asks civil rights division attorneys to stay after mass exits}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-14T11:59:57.346Z">at 12.59pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-14T11:28:06.344Z">12.28pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  said on Wednesday that Israel was not sidelined by his trip to the Gulf and that good US relations with those countries is good for Israel.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is good for Israel,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump told reporters onboard Air Force One. \u8220\'20\'1CHaving a relationship like I have with these countries \u8230\'20\'26 I think it\u8217\'20\'19s very good for Israel.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-14T11:36:42.732Z">at 12.36pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-14T11:20:24.989Z">12.20pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 The Syrian foreign minister said in a statement on Wednesday that the meeting between \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and the Syrian president, Ahmed al-Sharaa, included discussions about combating terrorism and cooperation in eliminating the influence of non-state actors and armed groups that threaten Syrian stability, including the Islamic State.\par \par \uc2 This meeting will be followed by another between the Syrian foreign minister and his US counterpart, \uc2 Marco Rubio\uc2 , Reuters reported.\par \par \uc2 In a statement, the foreign ministry said the meeting also addressed ways to \u8220\'20\'1Cenhance Syrian-American partnership in the field of counter-terrorism and cooperation in eliminating the influence of non-state actors and non-Syrian armed groups that hinder stability, including Islamic State and other threats\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-14T11:38:35.514Z">at 12.38pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-14T11:09:03.657Z">12.09pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Democrats fly 'Qatar-a-Lago' banner over Trump's Florida resort\par \par \uc2 With president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  looking to accept a $4o0 million luxury plane for his personal use from the Qatari government, the Democrats are planning a protest today.\par \par \uc2 Democrats have arranged to fly a sky banner over Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Mar-a-Lago Club in Florida that reads: \u8216\'20\'18Qatar-a-Lago\u8217\'20\'19.\par \par \uc2 DNC chair Ken Martin said:\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is using the presidency to personally enrich himself while he bankrupts working families. His corruption is a slap in the face to the millions of Americans who are struggling to get by and put food on the table.\par \par \uc2 Today, the DNC is highlighting what foreign autocracies around the world already know: Trump has no loyalty to the American people, national security, or the constitution \u8211\'20\'13 his only allegiance is to his bank account and his billionaire buddies.\par \par \uc2 Whether it\u8217\'20\'19s billionaires at home or governments abroad, Trump won\u8217\'20\'19t hesitate to sell out America\u8217\'20\'19s working families to the highest bidder.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-14T11:39:17.589Z">at 12.39pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-14T11:08:41.525Z">12.08pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  on Wednesday said he does not know if Russian president \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  will show up for talks on the war in Ukraine planned for Thursday in Turkey.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19d like me to be there, and that\u8217\'20\'19s a possibility \u8230\'20\'26 I don\u8217\'20\'19t know that he would be there if I\u8217\'20\'19m not there. We\u8217\'20\'19re going to find out,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump told reporters traveling aboard Air Force One en route to Qatar.\par \par \uc2 He has said he may visit Turkey for the talks as part of his trip to the Middle East this week.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-14T10:53:05.478Z">11.53am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Turkish president \uc2 Tayyip Erdogan\uc2  on Wednesday expressed his thanks to US president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for the US announcement that it would lift all sanctions on the Syrian government.\par \par \uc2 In a speech to lawmakers from his AK Party in parliament, Erdogan also said he had trust in the support of \u8220\'20\'1Cmy friend Trump\u8221\'20\'1D for Turkey\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to end the humanitarian tragedy in Gaza.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-14T10:44:18.876Z">11.44am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Saudi foreign minister Prince Faisal bin Farhan Al-Saud said there will be many investment opportunities in Syria after the US lifts sanctions, a day after a surprise US announcement it would lift all sanctions on the Islamist-led government.\par \par \uc2 Bin Farhan added that there will be a breakthrough in the kingdom\u8217\'20\'19s support to Syria after the lifting of US sanctions.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-14T10:43:25.255Z">11.43am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Americans worry about president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s administration\u8217\'20\'19s ability to contain an ongoing outbreak of measles, while the vast majority of them believe that vaccines for the disease are safe, according to a new Reuters/\uc2 Ipsos\uc2  poll.\par \par \uc2 Just 31% of respondents in the two-day poll, which closed on Tuesday, agreed with a statement that the current administration is handling the measles outbreak responsibly, while 40% disagreed and the rest were unsure or did not answer the question.\par \par \uc2 The US is now facing its largest single outbreak of measles in 25 years, with the number of cases crossing the 1,000 mark last week, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 The measles, mumps and rubella vaccine prevents 97% of cases after two doses and high adoption of the MMR vaccine resulted in the disease being declared eliminated in 2000 by the \uc2 World Health Organization\uc2 . Nonetheless, vaccination rates among US children have fallen in recent years, which experts attribute to vaccine skepticism and misinformation.\par \par \uc2 The vast majority of Americans still see the MMR vaccine as safe. Some 86% of respondents in the latest Reuters/\uc2 Ipsos\uc2  poll said it was safe for children, a marginally higher share than the 84% who said the same in a Reuters/\uc2 Ipsos\uc2  poll conducted in May 2020, in the early months of the COVID pandemic. Some 13% of respondents in the latest poll said the vaccine was not safe for kids, up marginally from 10% five years earlier.\par \par \uc2 The latest poll, which surveyed 1,163 US adults nationwide, had a margin of error of 3 percentage points.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-14T10:12:03.285Z">11.12am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Brooke Rollins, US agriculture secretary, has been visiting London to finalise the details of the US-UK trade deal agreed last week.\par \par \uc2 She told reporters, as she visited the new \uc2 Whole Foods\uc2  supermarket in Chelsea, that she had convinced energy Secretary \uc2 Ed Miliband\uc2  to take more wood pellets from America.\par \par \uc2 These are used to power the \uc2 Drax\uc2  power station, which environmental experts have said is unsustainable because burning wood emits carbon and the pellets used to power it are shipped across the ocean.\par \par \uc2 The drax plant accounts for about 6% of the UK\u8217\'20\'19s electricity supply but it had its subsidies halved last year, and was directed by government to only use sustainable wood.\par \par \uc2 Last year, \uc2 Drax\uc2  was forced to pay \u163\'00\'A325m to the energy regulator \uc2 Ofgem\uc2  after it was found to have submitted inaccurate data on the sourcing of its wood pellets. There have been reports some of the pellets used in the power station have been from rare forests.\par \par \uc2 Rollins said:\par \par \uc2 We are 100% confident that [the wood pellets] does meet your sustainability requirements here in this country yesterday, that was one of the key things that I spoke to, Secretary Miliband and Under Secretary [Michael] Shanks about, is the one who\u8217\'20\'19s leading that specific issue for the Energy Department here.\par \par \uc2 And they agreed, I don\u8217\'20\'19t want to get ahead of them, but in that meeting, they felt fully assured that what we are doing in America does meet your sustainability requirements, and in fact, we could potentially be opening up more markets for our wood pellets into the UK, as other countries that you\u8217\'20\'19re importing here into this country are clearly not meeting those marks.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-14T10:00:08.634Z">11.00am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 What are the Abraham Accords Trump has urged Syria to agree?\par \par \uc2 It was reported earlier today that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  urged Syria to sign onto the Abraham Accords with Israel (see post {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2025/may/14/donald-trump-syria-middle-east-gulf-latest-us-politics-news-updates-live?page=with%3Ablock-682455a98f089320ecd28f1b#block-682455a98f089320ecd28f1b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 ).\par \par \uc2 The Abraham Accords are bilateral agreements that established formal diplomatic relations between Israel and two Arab nations \u8211\'20\'13 the United Arab Emirates and Bahrain \u8211\'20\'13 both of which officially recognized Israel\u8217\'20\'19s sovereignty as part of the accords.\par \par \uc2 These agreements were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2020/sep/15/uae-bahrain-and-israel-sign-historic-accords-at-white-house-event-formal-relations-trump-netanyahu"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 signed on 15 September 2020}}}\uc2 , and were mediated by the United States.\par \par \uc2 The first deal, announced on 13 August 2020, involved Israel and the UAE, followed by a similar agreement with Bahrain on 11 September 2020.\par \par \uc2 The accord with the UAE marked the first time Israel had normalized relations with an Arab country since the 1994 peace treaty with Jordan.\par \par \uc2 The name \u8216\'20\'18Abraham Accords\u8217\'20\'19 was chosen to reflect the shared religious heritage of Judaism and Islam through the figure of the prophet Abraham.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-14T10:14:31.247Z">at 11.14am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-14T09:41:07.999Z">10.41am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Trump on way to Qatar amid controversy over $400m plane gift\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  continues his visit to the Middle East with a Qatari state visit later today.\par \par \uc2 According to a schedule released by the White House, the president will arrive at Doha\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Hamad International Airport\uc2  within the next hour, before stopping off to visit Amiri Diwan.\par \par \uc2 He will then arrive at St Regis Doha for the state visit shortly before 4pm local time.\par \par \uc2 Trump is also scheduled to attend a state dinner at the Lusail Palace this evening at 8pm.\par \par \uc2 The visit comes amid growing controversy over Trump\u8217\'20\'19s plans to accept a luxury $400m aircraft from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/qatar"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Qatar}}}\uc2  for presidential use.\par \par \uc2 Democrats and Republicans have criticized the US president accepting the gift amid concerns over the security implications and ethics of the deal.\par \par \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , Senate Democrat leader, has called the proposed arrangement \u8220\'20\'1Cnot just naked corruption\u8221\'20\'1D, likening it to something so corrupt \u8220\'20\'1Cthat even [Russian president Vladimir] Putin would give a double take\u8221\'20\'1D. <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/13/chuck-schumer-trumps-justice-department-nominees-qatar-aircraft"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Chuck Schumer says he\u8217\'20\'19ll obstruct Trump\u8217\'20\'19s justice department picks over Qatar jet gift}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-14T11:42:34.145Z">at 12.42pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-14T09:04:49.718Z">10.04am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 In pictures: Trump\u8217\'20\'19s meeting with Gulf leaders\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-14T08:52:24.035Z">9.52am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 The meeting between \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and Syria\u8217\'20\'19s president, Ahmad al-Sharaa , in Saudi Arabia was the culmination of months of diplomacy by the Syrians, as well as their Turkish and Saudi allies, who believed face time with Trump would help end Syria\u8217\'20\'19s international isolation, writes William Christou.\par \par \uc2 Damascus had prepared a pitch to Trump that included access to Syrian oil, reassurances of Israel\u8217\'20\'19s security and a proposal to build a Trump tower in Damascus.\par \par \uc2 A meeting with Trump was seen as a key step towards recognition of the legitimacy of the new authority in Damascus after Bashar al-Assad was ousted as Syria\u8217\'20\'19s president in December.\par \par \uc2 The Trump administration had previously been wary of engaging with Sharaa, a former leader of the Islamist rebel group Hayat Tahrir al-Sham.\par \par \uc2 Though sanctions were originally imposed on Assad after his bloody crackdown on peaceful protesters in 2011, the US and other countries retained their economic embargo on Syria as they evaluated the new Islamist-led government in Damascus.\par \par \uc2 The US state department had handed the Syrians an extensive list of conditions to end sanctions and were in the process of negotiating when Trump suddenly announced the lifting of US sanctions on Tuesday night. <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/14/trump-meets-syria-president-after-lifting-us-sanctions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump meets Syria\u8217\'20\'19s president after lifting US sanctions on country}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-14T08:46:16.612Z">9.46am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 At the end of his speech to the \uc2 Gulf Cooperation Council\uc2  in Riyadh, Trump told leaders in the region that he wants them to forge a Middle East that is \u8220\'20\'1Cthriving\u8221\'20\'1D and the \u8220\'20\'1Cgeographic centre of the world\u8221\'20\'1D. He said the \u8220\'20\'1Cwhole world is talking about what you are doing\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He added that it had been a pleasure to spend time with \uc2 Mohammed bin Salman\uc2  before he criticised the \u8220\'20\'1Cfake news\u8221\'20\'1D media.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-14T08:39:41.798Z">9.39am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Saudi Arabia \u8217\'20\'19s crown prince \uc2 Mohammed bin Salman\uc2  has told \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  that Arab Gulf states were seeking to work with the US to de-escalate tensions in the region, as the Israel-\uc2 Hamas\uc2  war in Gaza continues to drag on and destabilise the Middle East.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-14T08:38:51.444Z">9.38am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 According to a White House spokesperson, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  called on Syria\u8217\'20\'19s Ahmed al-Sharaa to '\u8220\'20\'1Cdeport Palestinian terrorists\u8221\'20\'1D and to help the US to prevent the resurgence of Islamic State. He urged Syria to sign onto the Abraham Accords with Israel.\par \par \uc2 Al-Sharaa invited American companies to invest in Syrian oil and gas.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-14T08:34:16.465Z">9.34am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 During Trump\u8217\'20\'19s speech to Arab leaders, he said he wants a future of \u8220\'20\'1Csafety and dignity\u8221\'20\'1D for Palestinians but warned that was impossible if leaders in Gaza continued down a path of violence.\par \par \uc2 He praised the \u8220\'20\'1Cconstructive role that the leaders in this room have taken trying to bring this conflict to an end\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He also thanked those involved in helping secure the release of Israeli-American hostage Edan Alexander.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-14T08:26:19.971Z">9.26am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Lifting sanctions on Syria 'gives them a chance of greatness', \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  says\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has said that lifting sanctions on Syria \u8220\'20\'1Cgives them a chance of greatness\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe sanctions were really crippling, very powerful,\u8221\'20\'1D he added. He said the US will drop \u8220\'20\'1Call of the sanctions on Syria, which I think will be a good thing.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He said that he is looking to normalise relations with Syria.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-14T08:48:09.127Z">at 9.48am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-14T08:21:36.119Z">9.21am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Trump wants to make deal with Iran but tells them to 'stop sponsoring terror'\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has said he wants to make a deal with Iran , but it can only go ahead if the regime stops \u8220\'20\'1Csupporting terror\u8221\'20\'1D and abandons its nuclear plans .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMany are watching with envy,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump told assembled Arab leaders during a speech and said there \u8220\'20\'1Care incredible deals within reach for this region\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He accused the Biden administration of \u8220\'20\'1Ccreating bedlam by being incompetent\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The US president says \u8220\'20\'1Cpeople at this table know where my loyalties lie\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In related news, Iran\u8217\'20\'19s deputy foreign minister will meet with European diplomats for nuclear talks in Istanbul on Friday, Foreign Minister \uc2 Abbas Araqchi\uc2  said on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Reuters reported on Tuesday that Iran would hold talks on the now moribund 2015 nuclear deal with European parties, which include France, Britain and Germany.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-14T08:32:12.222Z">at 9.32am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-14T08:11:29.963Z">9.11am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Turkish president \uc2 Recep Tayyip Erdo\u287\'01\'1Fan\uc2  has said Donald Turmp\u8217\'20\'19s decision to lift sanctions on Syria is of historic importance, Turkish state-owned Anadolu news agency reported on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Erdo\u287\'01\'1Fan met online with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , \uc2 Mohammed bin Salman\uc2  and Syrian president Ahmed al-Sharaa.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-14T08:06:41.639Z">9.06am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Speaking at an investment forum on Tuesday, Trump said that he planned to lift sanctions on Syria after holding talks with Saudi Arabia\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Mohammed bin Salman\uc2  and Turkey\u8217\'20\'19s Recep \uc2 Tayyip Erdo\u287\'01\'1Fan\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CI will be ordering the cessation of sanctions against Syria in order to give them a chance at greatness,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said.\par \par \uc2 Ahmed al-Sharaa\u8217\'20\'19s pitch to woo the US president offered access to Syrian oil, reconstruction contracts and to build a Trump Tower in Damascus in exchange for the lifting of US sanctions on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/syria"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Syria}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Though the details of the sanctions relief were still unclear, Sharaa\u8217\'20\'19s team in Damascus was celebrating, writes William Christou in Beirut.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is amazing, it worked,\u8221\'20\'1D said Radwan Ziadeh, a Syrian writer and activist who is close to the Syrian president. He shared a picture of an initial mockup of Trump Tower Damascus. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is how you win his heart and mind,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, noting that Sharaa would probably show Trump the design during their meeting in Riyadh on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-14T08:00:41.173Z">9.00am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  meets Syrian president in Saudi Arabia before Gulf tour resumes\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has met Syrian president Ahmed al-Sharaa in Saudi Arabia after agreeing to lift sanctions on Syria.\par \par \uc2 Despite concerns within sectors of his administration over the Syria\u8217\'20\'19s leaders\u8217\'20\'19 former ties to Al Qaeda, Trump said on Tuesday during a speech in Riyadh he would lift sanctions on Syria . The onetime insurgent leader spent years imprisoned by US forces after being captured in Iraq.\par \par \uc2 The White House says Trump agreed to \u8220\'20\'1Csay hello\u8221\'20\'1D to al-Sharaa before the US leader wraps up his visit to Saudi Arabia and moves on to Qatar.\par \par \uc2 Trump is also scheduled to attend a meeting of the \uc2 Gulf Cooperation Council\uc2 , the grouping of Bahrain, Kuwait, Oman, Qatar, Saudi Arabia, and the United Arab Emirates. He then sets off for Qatar, the second stop in his Gulf tour. Trump will be honored with a state dinner in Qatar.\par \par \uc2 Al-Sharaa was named president of Syria in January, a month after a stunning offensive by insurgent groups led by al-Sharaa\u8217\'20\'19s Hayat Tahrir al-Sham, or HTS, stormed Damascus and ended the 54-year rule of the Assad family.\par \par \uc2 Trump said he decided to meet with al-Sharaa after being encouraged to do so by Saudi crown prince \uc2 Mohammed bin Salman\uc2  and Turkish president Recep \uc2 Tayyip Erdo\u287\'01\'1Fan\uc2 . The president also pledged to lift years-long sanctions on Syria.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere is a new government that will hopefully succeed in stabilizing the country and keeping peace,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said in a wide-ranging foreign policy address Tuesday in which he announced he was lifting the sanctions that have been in place in Syria since 2011. \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s what we want to see in Syria.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump also urged Iran to take a \u8220\'20\'1Cnew and a better path\u8221\'20\'1D as he pushes for a new nuclear deal and said he wanted to avoid conflict with Tehran.\par \par \uc2 The United States and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/saudiarabia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Saudi Arabia}}}\uc2  signed a $142bn arms deal touted by the White House as the \u8220\'20\'1Clargest defence sales agreement in history\u8221\'20\'1D in the first stop of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump\u8217\'20\'19s}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/11/trump-middle-east-gulf-israel"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 four-day diplomatic tour}}}\uc2  to the Gulf states aimed at securing big deals and spotlighting the benefits of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s transactional foreign policy. <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/13/us-saudi-arabia-arms-deal-trump-meeting-syria"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US and Saudi Arabia sign $142bn arms deal as Trump to meet Syrian leader}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-14T08:05:29.842Z">at 9.05am BST</time> \par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250514el5e000xj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
