\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 RFK Jr orders mifepristone review as anti- \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  groups push for ban\b0\par\par\uc2 Susan Rinkunas \par \uc2 1,099 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 May 2025\par 22:36 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Health secretary cites \u8216\'20\'18new data\u8217\'20\'19 that emerged from flawed study conservatives are using to pressure \uc2 US government\par \par \uc2 The US health secretary, Robert F Kennedy Jr, said on Wednesday that he had directed the \uc2 FDA\uc2  to review the regulations around the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill mifepristone.\par \par \uc2 The review, he said, was necessary due to \u8220\'20\'1Cnew data\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 data that emerged from a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://factcheck.afp.com/doc.afp.com.444Z863"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 flawed}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.huffpost.com/entry/gop-lays-groundwork-to-pull-abortion-pill-access-with-new-junk-science-report_n_6812975be4b04cfa6e2b45e0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  analysis}}}\uc2  that top US anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups are now using to pressure the Trump administration to reimpose restrictions on the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill, if not pull it from the market entirely.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s alarming,\u8221\'20\'1D Kennedy told the Missouri senator \uc2 Josh Hawley\uc2 , a Republican, during a congressional hearing. \u8220\'20\'1CClearly, it indicates that, at very least, the label should be changed.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The analysis, which has not been peer-reviewed or published in a medical journal, came after the Food and Drug Administration commissioner said he was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.semafor.com/article/04/24/2025/fdas-marty-makary-no-plans-to-pull-abortion-pill-mifepristone"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 open}}}\uc2  to reviewing new safety data on the pills, which are used in nearly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/2024/03/medication-abortion-accounted-63-all-us-abortions-2023-increase-53-2020"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 two-thirds}}}\uc2  of abortions nationwide.\par \par \uc2 The conservative organizations are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2025/05/07/anti-abortion-pill-gameplan-rolling-thunder-00331933"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rallying}}}\uc2  behind a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://eppc.org/publication/insurance-data-reveals-one-in-ten-patients-experiences-a-serious-adverse-event/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 paper}}}\uc2  published on April 28 by a rightwing thinktank, the Ethics and Public Policy Center, which claims there are higher complication rates from taking mifepristone than previously known.\par \par \uc2 The paper has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://factcheck.afp.com/doc.afp.com.444Z863"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 attracted}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2025/may/13/republican-conservatives-abortion-pill-study-fda"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 scrutiny}}}\uc2  for appearing to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2025/05/12/abortion-pill-medication-abortion-study-mifepristone/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dramatically overstate}}}\uc2  what it characterizes as \u8220\'20\'1Cserious adverse effects\u8221\'20\'1D associated with the pill, according to medical experts. For example, it counts ectopic pregnancies \u8211\'20\'13 when an embryo implants somewhere other than the uterine lining \u8211\'20\'13 as a serious complication.\par \par \uc2 Mifepristone {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://factcheck.afp.com/doc.afp.com.444Z863"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 does not cause}}}\uc2  an ectopic pregnancy and taking it will not harm someone with an ectopic. It also claims that needing an in-clinic procedure to complete the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a complication, when patients are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://jessica.substack.com/p/eppc-abortion-pills-study-debunked"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 counseled}}}\uc2  in advance about the pills\u8217\'20\'19 failure rate of about 3 to 4%.\par \par \uc2 The data, the authors say, means the \uc2 FDA\uc2  should reinstate earlier restrictions on mifepristone, including a ban on telemedicine and limiting use to the first seven weeks of pregnancy \u8211\'20\'13 but they do not intend to stop there.\par \par \uc2 The authors note that restoring the limits could lead to better monitoring that could help \u8220\'20\'1Cdetermine whether this drug should remain on the market\u8221\'20\'1D, statements that echo proposals found in Project 2025, the 900-page playbook published by \uc2 the Heritage Foundation\uc2  and for which the EPPC was an advisory board member.\par \par \uc2 Project 2025 calls to end telemedicine prescriptions of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills as an \u8220\'20\'1C{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/05/project-2025-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 interim step}}}\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D to revoking mifepristone\u8217\'20\'19s approval altogether.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2023/04/01/health/abortion-pill-safety.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 More than 100 scientific studies}}}\uc2  have found the medications cited in the paper are safe and effective for ending a pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Telehealth, plus blue-state \u8220\'20\'1C{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/apr/26/abortion-clinic-pills-shield-laws"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shield laws}}}\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D, have enabled thousands of people living in states where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is banned to continue to access mifepristone and misoprostol, which frustrates \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents. One in five abortions nationwide are done via telemedicine, and in spring 2024, mail providers facilitated more than {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/apr/26/abortion-clinic-pills-shield-laws"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 7,700 abortions per month}}}\uc2  in states with total or six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans.\par \par \uc2 Anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  leaders said during a private \uc2 Zoom\uc2  call that they intend to use the EPPC paper to pressure the \uc2 FDA\uc2  and lawmakers to dramatically roll back access to the drug, \u8220\'20\'1Cif not suspend\u8221\'20\'1D their approval entirely, Politico{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2025/05/07/anti-abortion-pill-gameplan-rolling-thunder-00331933"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  reported}}}\uc2 . It is part of a plan they are privately calling \u8220\'20\'1CRolling Thunder\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Activists on that call \u8211\'20\'13 which included representatives from \uc2 Americans United for Life\uc2 , Live Action, Students for Life, and Susan B Anthony Pro-Life America \u8211\'20\'13 stressed that they viewed ending telemedicine prescriptions only as a \u8220\'20\'1Cfirst step\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 According to the Politico report, the EPPC president, Ryan Anderson, argued on the call that this plan aligns with Donald Trump\u8217\'20\'19s stated desire to leave \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy to the states because, he said, \u8220\'20\'1Cyou\u8217\'20\'19re not leaving it to states if California can mail pills to Texas\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Activists tried to push back on criticism that the paper was not peer-reviewed by arguing that academia is \u8220\'20\'1Cbroken\u8221\'20\'1D and they could not trust journals or reviewers not to \u8220\'20\'1Csabotage\u8221\'20\'1D their effort or leak it to the press. Politico reported that one medical professional on the call, Christina Francis, the CEO of the American Association of Pro-Life OBGYNs, warned her colleagues not to misrepresent the paper, acknowledging that the report was \u8220\'20\'1Cnot a study in the traditional sense\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cnot conclusive proof of anything\u8221\'20\'1D. Still, Francis argued that it warranted government action and more research.\par \par \uc2 During his January confirmation hearing, Kennedy said that Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://19thnews.org/2025/01/rfk-jr-confirmation-hearing-health-abortion-medication/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 asked him}}}\uc2  to review mifepristone\u8217\'20\'19s safety data. The \uc2 FDA\uc2  commissioner, Marty Makary, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.semafor.com/article/04/24/2025/fdas-marty-makary-no-plans-to-pull-abortion-pill-mifepristone"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  in March that he, too, would \u8220\'20\'1Cdo a review of the data\u8221\'20\'1D, and would act if necessary. Hawley, the Missouri senator, later {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.hawley.senate.gov/hawley-calls-on-fda-to-reinstate-abortion-drug-safety-regulations-the-time-to-act-is-now/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote}}}\uc2  a letter to Makary asking him to review the paper the day it was published; Hawley also{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.huffpost.com/entry/josh-hawley-introduces-law-to-ban-mailing-of-abortion-pills-citing-junk-science-report_n_681b808ce4b01488b7bfa2a7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  introduced a bill}}}\uc2  to end telemedicine of mifepristone. It is not expected to pass Congress, but the \uc2 FDA\uc2  could take action on its own, especially under pressure from groups on the call.\par \par \uc2 While \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents have promoted research {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/apr/28/junk-science-papers-abortion-cases"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 linked}}}\uc2  to anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  thinktanks claiming that mifepristone is dangerous, some studies have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/mar/23/anti-abortion-junk-science-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 been retracted}}}\uc2 , including one cited heavily by a federal judge in a case seeking to roll back the pill\u8217\'20\'19s availability that went to the supreme court last term. The court ruled unanimously that the plaintiffs, anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  doctors, did not have legal standing to sue the \uc2 FDA\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 That case is still ongoing, with three Republican attorneys general suing the \uc2 FDA\uc2  on behalf of the states of Missouri, Idaho and Kansas.\par \par \uc2 The Trump administration made news last week when {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/05/trump-biden-defense-mifepristone-abortion-drug"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 it argued}}}\uc2  in a filing that the judge should dismiss the case, the same position taken by the Biden administration earlier this year. But the Trump administration did not defend the \uc2 FDA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s actions on mifepristone, instead saying only that the plaintiffs were not the right people to sue.\par \par \uc2 As a health law expert {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/06/abortion-pill-trump-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recently told}}}\uc2  the Guardian, the administration could use that argument in the future if it chooses to restrict the drug and Democratic-led states sue over the changes.\par \par \uc2 Kirsten Moore, director of the Expanding Medication \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Access Project, told the Guardian she was not surprised by either the existence of a plan to restrict the drugs or that the push is based on what she called \u8220\'20\'1Cmanufactured misinformation\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Moore said that \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  supporters had long known that anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  advocates \u8220\'20\'1Cwill stop at nothing to put mifepristone \u8211\'20\'13 a safe, effective \uc2 FDA\uc2 -approved medication that has been used for 25 years in this country to end a pregnancy at 10 weeks or less \u8211\'20\'13 back under lock and key\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Carter Sherman contributed to this report\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250514el5e003bh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
