\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 South Carolina supreme court upholds six-week  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  ban\b0\par\par\uc2 Carter Sherman \par \uc2 384 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 May 2025\par 17:58 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Justices rejected \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s argument over the definition of a \u8216\'20\'18fetal heartbeat\u8217\'20\'19 in loss for the health giant\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/south-carolina"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 South Carolina}}}\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s state supreme court upheld the state\u8217\'20\'19s six-week {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ban in a decision issued on Wednesday, in a disappointing loss for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/planned-parenthood"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Planned Parenthood}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Planned Parenthood South Atlantic, which operates clinics in South Carolina, sued over the state\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, which outlaws the procedure after the emergence of a \u8220\'20\'1Cfetal heartbeat\u8221\'20\'1D. Generally, these kinds of \u8220\'20\'1Cheartbeat\u8221\'20\'1D bans have been interpreted to prohibit \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after six weeks of pregnancy, when providers can detect cardiac activity from a fetus.\par \par \uc2 But because a fetus\u8217\'20\'19s heart is not formed until nine weeks of pregnancy, Planned Parenthood South Atlantic argued that such activity does not constitute a real \u8220\'20\'1Cheartbeat\u8221\'20\'1D. Instead of outlawing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after six weeks of pregnancy, the \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive health\b0 \highlight\uc2  organization said, South Carolina should permit the procedure until nine weeks. <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/jul/29/abortion-laws-bans-by-state"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tracking \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  laws across the United States}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 The South Carolina supreme court rejected that argument. Legislators, the justices wrote in a 5-0 ruling, clearly intended for the law to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after six weeks.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe count at least sixty separate instances during the 2023 legislative session in which a member of the House or Senate referred to the 2023 Act as a six-week ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D Justice John Few wrote in the majority opinion. Few added: \u8220\'20\'1CIn particular, we could find not one instance during the entire 2023 legislative session in which anyone connected in any way to the General Assembly framed the Act as banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after approximately nine weeks.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is banned at six weeks of pregnancy or at conception {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/jul/29/abortion-laws-bans-by-state"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 throughout the south-eastern US}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 South Carolina and Planned Parenthood South Atlantic are also at the center of another legal dispute around \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Last month, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/apr/02/planned-parenthood-medicaid-us-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the US supreme court heard arguments}}}\uc2  in a case over South Carolina\u8217\'20\'19s attempt to kick the group out of its state Medicaid program because \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  provides \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . If the supreme court sides with South Carolina, its decision could pave the way for other red states to cut \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  out of their Medicaid programs \u8211\'20\'13 and financially devastate the organization.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250514el5e002ea\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
