\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 Louisiana investigates New York doctor for allegedly mailing  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  pills\b0\par\par\uc2 Carter Sherman \par \uc2 603 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 May 2025\par 21:21 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Margaret Carpenter was previously indicted over reported \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill prescription in state with near-total ban\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/louisiana"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Louisiana}}}\uc2  is investigating a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/new-york"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York}}}\uc2  doctor over accusations that she mailed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  pills into the state, Liz Murrill, the state attorney general, said on Monday. The case marks the second investigation into the doctor, Margaret Carpenter, whom Louisiana had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/31/new-york-louisiana-abortion-pill-charges"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 indicted earlier this year}}}\uc2  for allegedly prescribing abortions pills via telehealth to a Louisiana resident.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe young woman was 20 weeks pregnant,\u8221\'20\'1D Murrill said. \u8220\'20\'1CShe and her boyfriend after she gave birth took the baby, wrapped it in a towel and threw it in a garbage can.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Murrill said that police in Shreveport, where the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  allegedly took place, were investigating the incident alongside her office. A spokesperson for Murrill\u8217\'20\'19s office did not immediately respond to a request for comment or documentation of the case. <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/31/new-york-louisiana-abortion-pill-charges"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York doctor indicted in Louisiana over alleged \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  pill prescription}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 The couple ultimately went to the hospital, according to Murrill. Medical experts widely agree that it is safe to \u8220\'20\'1Cself-manage\u8221\'20\'1D your own \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  using pills in the first trimester of pregnancy. However, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/28/arizona-abortion-clinic"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 these pills can also safely induce}}}\uc2  an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the second trimester of pregnancy. \uc2 Doctors Without Borders\uc2  offers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.doctorswithoutborders.org/latest/faq-safe-abortion-care"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 guidelines}}}\uc2  on how to use \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills through 22 weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Murrill made the comments while speaking at a state legislative hearing about a bill that would allow people to sue an individual or an entity that \u8220\'20\'1Cperforms, causes or substantially facilitates\u8221\'20\'1D an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Louisiana already {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/jul/29/abortion-laws-bans-by-state"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bans virtually all abortions}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis bill provides for civil liability and allows another mechanism \u8211\'20\'13 it is another tool in the toolbox for people who are harmed by somebody who is intent on violating our laws,\u8221\'20\'1D Murrill said.\par \par \uc2 Carpenter has so far avoided making public statements in the case. An organization that she co-founded, \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Coalition for Telemedicine, did not immediately respond to a request for comment.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMake no mistake, since Roe v Wade was overturned, we\u8217\'20\'19ve witnessed a disturbing pattern of interference with women\u8217\'20\'19s rights,\u8221\'20\'1D the organization said in a statement when news of the first Louisiana case against Carpenter broke. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s no secret that the United States has a history of violence and harassment against \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers, and this state-sponsored effort to prosecute a doctor providing safe and effective care should alarm everyone.\u8221\'20\'1D <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/mar/27/new-york-abortion-pill-lawsuit-texas-fine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York clerk refuses to enforce Texas effort to punish \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  provider}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 Jeff Landry\uc2 , Louisiana\u8217\'20\'19s Republican governor, has signed an extradition warrant for Carpenter, but she has not been extradited to Louisiana and New York\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic governor, \uc2 Kathy Hochul\uc2 , has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/feb/13/texas-abortion-pills-shield-laws-new-york-doctor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 vowed to never sign}}}\uc2  an extradition order for her. New York is one of a handful of blue states that, in the wake of the fall of Roe v Wade, have enacted so-called {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/apr/26/abortion-clinic-pills-shield-laws"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cshield laws\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 , which guard \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers such as Carpenter against out-of-state prosecutions and civil lawsuits. In spring 2024, such shield laws helped facilitate more than 7,700 monthly abortions in states with total or six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans, according to #WeCount, a research project by the Society of Family Planning.\par \par \uc2 Texas has also sued Carpenter for allegedly mailing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills into the state, in defiance of its \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans, but a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/mar/27/new-york-abortion-pill-lawsuit-texas-fine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York clerk has rejected a Texas request}}}\uc2  to force Carpenter to pay a fine. Legal analysts expect the issue to wind up in front of the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250513el5d0035x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
