\par\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 Conservatives are trumpeting a new  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2 -pill study. One problem: it\u8217\'20\'19s bogus\b0\par\par\uc2 Moira Donegan \par \uc2 1,115 \uc2 words\par \uc2 12 May 2025\par 14:12 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The \uc2 FDA\uc2  chief suggested he wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t crack down on mifepristone without new data. Conveniently, misleading research emerged within days\par \par \uc2 Almost {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2025/03/06/health/fda-marty-makary-abortion-pill-vaccines-confirmation.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 two-thirds}}}\uc2  of US {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 abortions}}}\uc2  are induced with pills. The drug mifepristone blocks the pregnancy hormone progesterone, ending the growth of the fetus. Mifepristone was designed for abortions: its primary purpose, from its development through its regulatory approval and now on the market, has always been to allow women to control their own bodies and lives by ending their pregnancies. Because it exists as a tool of women\u8217\'20\'19s independence, mifepristone has been the object of controversy, misinformation and intense scrutiny for the entirety of its existence. Originally synthesized by French pharmaceutical researchers in 1980, the drug went through a rigorous, prolonged and heavily politicized approval process in the US, and wasn\u8217\'20\'19t approved by the Food and Drug Administration (\uc2 FDA\uc2 ) for the US market until 2000.\par \par \uc2 The anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement \u8211\'20\'13 including several prominent Republican lawmakers \u8211\'20\'13 is looking to undo that. Since the 2022 Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization decision that eliminated the nationwide right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , women living in anti-choice states have relied increasingly on mifepristone, particularly pills {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/apr/26/abortion-clinic-pills-shield-laws"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shipped by mail from providers in pro-choice states}}}\uc2  who prescribe the drug via telehealth. It is estimated that as many as 20% of abortions in the US are now accessed via telehealth appointments, a technological marvel that has allowed many people living in anti-choice states to avert the worst consequences to their lives, health and dignity that were threatened by the Dobbs decision by circumventing the unjust \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans that their states have attempted to impose on them. Dobbs has already been devastating for American women, causing needless deaths, driving up maternal mortality, derailing women\u8217\'20\'19s lives, constraining their prospects, and injuring their standing as equal citizens. The post-2022 explosion of telehealth \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  using mifepristone is the reason why the consequences have not been even worse. <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2025/may/11/mothers-day-us-birth-rates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 This Mother\u8217\'20\'19s Day, lets talk about why birth rates are really declining | Katrina vanden Heuvel}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 Now, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s new \uc2 FDA\uc2  commissioner, Marty Makary, is under pressure to restrict access to the drug. Pressed by reporters at the Semafor World Economy Summit late last month, Makaray said that he had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pbs.org/newshour/show/what-the-new-fda-commissioner-says-about-possible-restrictions-on-abortion-medication"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cno plans\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  to review the status of mifepristone. But he added a crucial caveat: that he would reconsider the drug\u8217\'20\'19s accessibility if new information emerged about the drug\u8217\'20\'19s safety. \u8220\'20\'1CIf the data suggests something or tells us that there\u8217\'20\'19s a real signal, we can\u8217\'20\'19t promise that we\u8217\'20\'19re not going to act on that data,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 As if on cue, a conservative thinktank published a new study just days later that purported to find that mifepristone caused serious adverse effects in more than 10% of patients. The study \u8211\'20\'13 which contradicts all previous tests of the drug and the resounding consensus of the medical field \u8211\'20\'13 was published by the Ethics and Public Policy Center, a rightwing advocacy group {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://eppc.org/about/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 that aims to}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Capply the richness of the Jewish and Christian traditions to contemporary questions of law\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cpush back against the extreme progressive agenda while building a consensus for conservatives\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The study was rapidly amplified on conservative social media, and was pushed by several Republican senators who had previously called on Makaray to ban mifepristone at his March confirmation hearing. Missouri\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Josh Hawley\uc2 , the author of a book on \u8220\'20\'1Cmanhood\u8221\'20\'1D who once {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/mar/15/josh-hawley-january-6-fist-photo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 raised a fist}}}\uc2  in solidarity with the January 6 insurrectionists, declared in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.legistorm.com/stormfeed/view_rss/2505790/member/3348/title/hawley-op-ed-fda-commissioner-can8217t-ignore-damning-new-data-on-dangers-of-mifepristone.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement}}}\uc2  directed at Makaray: \u8220\'20\'1CWell, the new data is here. And it\u8217\'20\'19s a signal that can\u8217\'20\'19t be missed: Mifepristone is not safe.\u8221\'20\'1D Hawley went on to urge the \uc2 FDA\uc2  to restrict access to the drug and revert to pre-pandemic regulations, in which mifepristone could only be dispensed by a doctor after multiple in-person visits: a regulatory regime that would cut off \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access to millions of women in anti-choice states.\par \par \uc2 But the study that is being proposed as a pretext for restricting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access has come under scrutiny from doctors and statisticians for its {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mediamatters.org/medication-abortion/right-wing-media-and-anti-abortion-groups-are-using-seriously-flawed-study"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 questionable methodology}}}\uc2 . Drawing from insurance claim data from 2017 to 2023, the EPPC study claims that 10% of women who take mifepristone experience \u8220\'20\'1Csepsis, infection, hemorrhaging, an emergency room visit, or another serious adverse event within 45 days\u8221\'20\'1D. This would be alarming if it were true, but it isn\u8217\'20\'19t. <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2025/apr/06/jd-vance-may-disagree-but-this-anti-abortion-activist-isnt-a-brutally-censored-dissident-livia-tossici-bolt"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 JD Vance may disagree, but this anti-\b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  activist isn\u8217\'20\'19t a brutally censored dissident | Catherine Bennett}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 Instead, the study seems to have been designed to dramatically overstate the side-effects of mifepristone, in part by counting the normal and intended functioning of the drug \u8211\'20\'13 such as vaginal bleeding as the pregnancy terminates and post-medication doctor visits to confirm the completion of the miscarriage \u8211\'20\'13 as serious adverse effects. The study also claimed that a vast range of health experiences in the 45 days following the medication \u8211\'20\'13 such as mental health symptoms \u8211\'20\'13 were caused by the drug, a claim that the data does not support. The EPPC study also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://factcheck.afp.com/doc.afp.com.444Z863"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 seems to include}}}\uc2  those who were prescribed mifepristone for non-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  uses, such as miscarriage management, as well as those who took it alone, without the standard misoprostol dose that accompanies it. The study is not peer-reviewed and has not been published in a medical journal, because its authors could not meet the standards that such publication requires: their work is not up to snuff. Dr Stella Dantas, the president of the \uc2 American College of Obstetricians and Gynecologists\uc2 , called the paper \u8220\'20\'1Cseriously flawed\u8221\'20\'1D and said that it \u8220\'20\'1Cmanipulates data to drive a myth that medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  isn\u8217\'20\'19t safe\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The truth is that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills have a lower rate of serious complications {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://factcheck.afp.com/doc.afp.com.444Z863?utm_source=substack&utm_medium=email"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 than Tylenol}}}\uc2 , and that the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement is in fact a great danger to American women\u8217\'20\'19s health. It is because of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans \u8211\'20\'13 not \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access \u8211\'20\'13 that women in America are facing dramatically rising rates of \u8220\'20\'1Csepsis, infection, hemorrhaging\u8221\'20\'1D and death in pregnancy. In Texas alone, the rate of sepsis in pregnant women experiencing second-trimester miscarriages increased by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.propublica.org/article/texas-abortion-ban-sepsis-maternal-mortality-analysis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more than 50%}}}\uc2  in the years since the state\u8217\'20\'19s near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban went into effect, and experts say that the laws prohibiting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  are the cause. The adverse effects that the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement sees in mifepristone\u8217\'20\'19s availability is not a matter of women\u8217\'20\'19s health, which they are indifferent to. It is women\u8217\'20\'19s freedom.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Moira Donegan is a Guardian US columnist\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250512el5c00236\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
