\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 New pope\u8217\'20\'19s brother says he is \u8216\'20\'18middle of the road\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Helen Livingstone (now); L\u233\'00\'E9onie Chao-Fong, Marina Dunbar and Jakub Krupa (earlier) \par \uc2 13,353 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 May 2025\par 05:10 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This blog has now closed. Our <a href="{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2025/may/09/pope-leo-xiv-to-hold-first-mass-pontiff-catholics-celebrate-live">live"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2025/may/09/pope-leo-xiv-to-hold-first-mass-pontiff-catholics-celebrate-live">live}}}\uc2  updates coverage on Pope Leo XIV\u8217\'20\'19s first full day in office has moved here</a>.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-09T05:06:59.146Z">6.06am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 This blog is closing now and we\u8217\'20\'19re {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2025/may/09/pope-leo-xiv-to-hold-first-mass-pontiff-catholics-celebrate-live"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 moving our live coverage of Pope Leo XIV\u8217\'20\'19s first full day in office here}}}\uc2 . Here\u8217\'20\'19s a summary of the main news:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Robert Francis Prevost has been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/may/08/white-smoke-signals-election-of-new-roman-catholic-pope"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 elected by his fellow cardinals}}}\uc2  to be the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/may/08/new-pope-cardinal-robert-prevost-leo-reaction"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 first US-born pope}}}\uc2  and has chosen to take the name Leo XIV. With the choice of Prevost, experts say, the cardinals opted for continuity with the late Francis, a progressive from Argentina who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/apr/21/pope-francis-outsider-whose-reforming-mission-made-him-an-ally-of-progressives"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shook up the Church}}}\uc2  in his 12-year papacy.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Prevost will celebrate a private mass with cardinals at the Sistine Chapel on Friday at 11am (0900 GMT). In it, he will deliver his much anticipated first homily as pope. It will be broadcast live.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Vatican spokesperson Matteo Bruni said the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2025/may/08/what-will-the-new-pope-be-like-hes-chosen-to-be-called-leo-thats-no-accident"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 choice of the name Leo}}}\uc2  was a \u8220\'20\'1Cclear and deliberate\u8221\'20\'1D reference to the last pope named Leo . Leo XIII was elected in 1878 and was best known for his 1891 encyclical, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.vatican.va/content/leo-xiii/en/encyclicals/documents/hf_l-xiii_enc_15051891_rerum-novarum.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Rerum Novarum}}}\uc2 , which outlined workers\u8217\'20\'19 rights.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 In his first comments after his election , Pope Leo XIV preached a message of \u8220\'20\'1Cunity\u8221\'20\'1D and of \u8220\'20\'1Cmoving forward\u8221\'20\'1D . He said he wants this message of peace to \u8220\'20\'1Center your hearts, to reach your families and all people, wherever they are.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Many shared their excitement at having an American pope , and specifically a pope born in Chicago . City mayor Brandon Johnson tweeted \u8220\'20\'1CEverything dope, including the Pope, comes from Chicago\u8221\'20\'1D and former US president \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  congratulated the \u8220\'20\'1Cfellow Chicagoan\u8221\'20\'1D on social media.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The election of the 69-year-old was also celebrated in Peru, where he has spent much of his life . Peru\u8217\'20\'19s president, \uc2 Dina Boluarte\uc2  described him as a Peruvian \u8220\'20\'1Cby choice and conviction\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 US president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  said he was \u8220\'20\'1Csurprised\u8221\'20\'1D but that it is a \u8220\'20\'1Cgreat honour\u8221\'20\'1D to have an American pope . Leaders from countries around the world also offered their congratulations.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 An account on X widely believed to belong to the new pope shows him to be somewhat critical of the Trump administration. The account posted two articles that took issue with the stance by JD Vance , also a Catholic, on immigration. One article was headlined \u8220\'20\'1CJD Vance is wrong: Jesus doesn\u8217\'20\'19t ask us to rank our love for others.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Leo\u8217\'20\'19s brother, John Prevost, told US media that Leo, was not afraid to speak his mind and that he was currently very unhappy with \u8220\'20\'1Cwhat\u8217\'20\'19s going on with immigration\u8221\'20\'1D . He told the \uc2 New York Times\uc2 : \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t think he\u8217\'20\'19ll stay quiet for too long if he has something to say \u8230\'20\'26 I know he\u8217\'20\'19s not happy with what\u8217\'20\'19s going on with immigration. I know that for a fact.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 In a 2012 address to the world Synod of Bishops , Father Robert Francis Prevost, now Pope Leo XIV appeared to criticise homosexuality , saying \u8220\'20\'1CWestern mass media is extraordinarily effective in fostering within the general public enormous sympathy for beliefs and practices that are at odds with the Gospel \u8211\'20\'13 for example \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , homosexual lifestyle, euthanasia\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Like his predecessor, \uc2 Pope Francis\uc2 , Leo is also on the record as opposing the ordination of women . He told a 2023 synod that \u8220\'20\'1Cclericalizing women\u8221\'20\'1D would not solve problems in the Catholic Church and might create new ones, according to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.catholicnewsagency.com/news/255823/cardinal-at-synod-on-synodality-clericalizing-women-will-not-solve-problems"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Catholic news agency}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-09T05:10:50.983Z">at 6.10am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-09T04:40:39.020Z">5.40am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Stephen Cottrell, the archbishop of York and acting head of the Church of England , has said Anglicans \u8220\'20\'1Cshare in the great joy of our Roman Catholic sisters and brothers\u8221\'20\'1D in welcoming Pope Leo as \u8220\'20\'1Cthe Bishop of Rome\u8221\'20\'1D. He continued:\par \par \uc2 Pope Leo XIV\u8217\'20\'19s many years of pastoral experience, his commitment to justice, and his deep spirituality are an example of life lived in service to Jesus Christ.\par \par \uc2 As Anglicans, we give thanks for his call to Christians to be bridge-builders across the divisions of our world, and the divisions that continue to exist between churches. This is something Jesus asks of us. He prays that the church will be one.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-09T04:20:25.969Z">5.20am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Leo XIV is expected to hols his first mass as pope at the Sistine Chapel on Friday morning at 11am (0900 GMT), according to Vatican News.\par \par \uc2 It will be a private mass with his cardinals but will be broadcast live and in it he will give his much anticipated first homily as pope, which Catholics hope will give an indication of the kind of leader he will be.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-09T04:03:27.027Z">5.03am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 A few pictures are coming in now from Chiclayo , the Peruvian city where Prevost was bishop until 2023 when he was called to Rome by \uc2 Pope Francis\uc2 . Locals have been attending mass at Saint Mary\u8217\'20\'19s cathedral in Chiclayo:\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-09T03:43:51.483Z">4.43am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Friends of the new pope have also been speaking to US media. Father Mark Francis, who attended the same seminary as Pope Leo XIV in the 1970s, said Leo wasn\u8217\'20\'19t \u8220\'20\'1Ca showboat kind of person\u8221\'20\'1D and that he had never mentioned wanting to become pope. He told CNN:\par \par \uc2 He is a calm person who is not a careerist, is not just seeking a promotion \u8211\'20\'13 but someone who\u8217\'20\'19s there to serve.\par \par \uc2 He said the Chicago church was \u8220\'20\'1Cforward-looking\u8221\'20\'1D and had a strong desire for more women to be involved in the church.\par \par \uc2 I think that is a hallmark of my ministry, and I also believe of Pope Leo\u8217\'20\'19s ministry as well: a respect for women and a respect for their voice.\par \par \uc2 However, as we reported earlier, Leo {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2025/may/08/new-pope-conclave-vatican-white-black-smoke-papacy-catholic-cardinals?page=with%3Ablock-681d56848f082cdfc1dab316#block-681d56848f082cdfc1dab316"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 does not support}}}\uc2  the ordination of women.\par \par \uc2 Rev John Lydon, who was an undergraduate with Leo at Villanova, warned Americans against thinking of him as an American pope. He told CNN:\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s a way of thinking that\u8217\'20\'19s not the same way of thinking in other parts of the world, so that\u8217\'20\'19s one thing I caution Americans to think: He\u8217\'20\'19s not an American pope, he\u8217\'20\'19s a pope who happened to be born in the United States.\par \par \uc2 Peggy Wurtz, who went to school with the new pope, told the broadcaster his family had always been pious. She added:\par \par \uc2 He was super smart and super quiet. There isn\u8217\'20\'19t a bad thing you can say about him. He is pure, pure, this guy was destined to be pope.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-09T03:29:29.527Z">4.29am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a bit more from Pope Leo\u8217\'20\'19s brother, John Prevost , who has been speaking to the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  as he does the media rounds.\par \par \uc2 John says his brother is \u8220\'20\'1Cmiddle of the road\u8221\'20\'1D and that \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t think we\u8217\'20\'19ll see extremes either way.\u8221\'20\'1D However he also said that the new pope would not be afraid to speak out and that he was currently unhappy with \u8220\'20\'1Cwhat\u8217\'20\'19s going on with immigration\u8221\'20\'1D. He said:\par \par \uc2 I don\u8217\'20\'19t think he\u8217\'20\'19ll stay quiet for too long if he has something to say \u8230\'20\'26 I know he\u8217\'20\'19s not happy with what\u8217\'20\'19s going on with immigration. I know that for a fact.\par \par \uc2 How far he\u8217\'20\'19ll go with it is only one\u8217\'20\'19s guess, but he won\u8217\'20\'19t just sit back. I don\u8217\'20\'19t think he\u8217\'20\'19ll be the silent one.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-09T03:14:58.409Z">4.14am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Watch Americans react to the naming of the new pope: <figure class="element element-atom"> <gu-atom data-atom-id="a0297470-723b-4bb5-abc1-58f90d19fecb" data-atom-type="media"> </gu-atom> </figure>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-09T03:00:21.447Z">4.00am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Taiwan has congratulated the new pope.\par \par \uc2 AFP reports that President Lai Ching-te has sent his congratulations to Pope Leo on his appointment, saying Taiwan hopes to continue working with the Vatican to pursue peace, justice and religious freedom.\par \par \uc2 The Vatican is one of only 12 countries to retain formal diplomatic ties with Chinese-claimed Taiwan, though Lai did not attend \uc2 Pope Francis\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 funeral last month, sending instead former vice president Chen Chien-jen, a devout Catholic.\par \par \uc2 Francis had led a wide-ranging outreach to officially atheist China, including signing a deal on the appointment of Catholic bishops in that country, worrying Taiwan.\par \par \uc2 Taiwan\u8217\'20\'19s foreign ministry\uc2  said in a statement that Lai had sent his congratulatory message via its embassy to the Vatican.\par \par \uc2 Lai \u8220\'20\'1Cstressed that Taiwan looks forward to continuing to work with the Holy See to jointly pursue peace, justice, religious freedom, solidarity, fraternity, and human dignity\u8221\'20\'1D, the statement said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTaiwan will continue to promote various exchanges and co-operation with the Holy See, to further strengthen bilateral relations, and to make more contributions to the world together with the Holy See,\u8221\'20\'1D said the ministry statement.\par \par \uc2 The foreign ministry did not say whether Lai might attend Leo\u8217\'20\'19s inauguration. In 2013, then-president Ma Ying-jeou went to Francis\u8217\'20\'19 inauguration.\par \par \uc2 Helen Davidson in Taipei has written about how the inauguration could risk raising tensions between China and Taiwan: <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/may/01/papal-inauguration-pope-risks-raising-tensions-between-china-and-taiwan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Papal inauguration risks raising tensions between China and Taiwan}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-09T02:45:53.039Z">3.45am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Chicago White Sox\uc2  have welcomed the news that one of their fans has been elected pope, writing in a post on X \u8220\'20\'1CWell, would you look at that... Congratulations to Chicago\u8217\'20\'19s own Pope Leo XIV.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 They also posted a clip of Leo\u8217\'20\'19s brother, John Prevost , saying \u8220\'20\'1CYeah he was never, ever a Cubs fan so I don\u8217\'20\'19t know where that came from. He was always a Sox fan.\u8221\'20\'1D <figure class="element element-tweet" data-canonical-url="{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/whitesox/status/1920605400484712617"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://twitter.com/whitesox/status/1920605400484712617}}}\uc2 ">\par \par \uc2 Well, would you look at that... Congratulations to Chicago's own Pope Leo XIV {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/U5DJ7TOyDr"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/U5DJ7TOyDr}}}\uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Chicago White Sox\uc2  (@whitesox) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/whitesox/status/1920605400484712617?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 8, 2025}}}\uc2  </figure>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-09T02:27:06.210Z">3.27am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Australian Catholics and politicians have embraced the appointment of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/may/08/robert-francis-prevost-the-moderate-good-humoured-first-american-pope"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new pope, Leo XIV}}}\uc2 , with many hoping he will continue his predecessor\u8217\'20\'19s emphasis on peace and social justice.\par \par \uc2 Archbishop Timothy Costelloe, the president of the Australian Catholic Bishops Conference, offered Cardinal Robert Francis Prevost \u8211\'20\'13 now known as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/pope-leo-xiv"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pope Leo XIV}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 heartfelt congratulations on behalf of the Roman Catholic church in Australia.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Catholic Church in Australia assures Pope Leo XIV of our prayers, loyalty, and joyful anticipation of his spiritual leadership,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CMay his pontificate be marked by peace, unity, and a deepening of the Gospel message throughout the world.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Brother Mark O\u8217\'20\'19Connor, head of communications for the Catholic archdiocese of Parramatta, told Radio National he had met the new pope, describing him as a \u8220\'20\'1Chumble, gentle leader\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s not different from \uc2 Pope Francis\uc2  in terms of vision, but maybe in style,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s more low key.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He said Leo XIV had been to Australia and was not a fan of Vegemite but did like Tim Tams. <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2025/may/09/australian-catholics-welcome-pope-leo-xiv"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Australian Catholics welcome \u8216\'20\'18approachable\u8217\'20\'19 new pope in hope he will pursue peace}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-09T02:27:20.534Z">at 3.27am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-09T02:15:24.552Z">3.15am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 As white smoke billowed from the Vatican in Rome, yellow papal flags whipped in the crisp Lake Michigan breeze in front of Our Lady of Mount Carmel Academy on Chicago\u8217\'20\'19s North Side.\par \par \uc2 Screams of \u8220\'20\'1CHabemus Papam!\u8221\'20\'1D echoed throughout the cafeteria at the Catholic school on Thursday afternoon, when news broke that Chicago\u8217\'20\'19s Robert Prevost had become {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/pope-leo-xiv"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pope Leo XIV}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Prevost was born on Chicago\u8217\'20\'19s South Side and attended Catholic school at St Mary of the Assumption, a now defunct parish on the city\u8217\'20\'19s far south-east side. Prevost studied divinity at Catholic Theological Union in Chicago\u8217\'20\'19s Hyde Park neighborhood, and taught at a local Catholic high school, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://chicago.suntimes.com/religion/2025/05/03/robert-prevost-pope-francis-conclave-catholic-church-dolton-saint-mary-assumption-parish"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Chicago Sun-Times}}}\uc2  reported.\par \par \uc2 Despite spending his formative years in Peru, where he worked as a missionary and later archbishop of Chiclayo, Chicagoans celebrated their native son at churches and schools around the city.\par \par \uc2 Seventh-grader Vincent Wall and eighth-grader Ava Broz were in the cafeteria at Mount Carmel, where students were waving US and city of Chicago flags.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt really feels like a 2016 Cubs World Series,\u8221\'20\'1D said Wall, referring to the baseball team that endured a long drought before a triumphant victory in 2016. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s just like, a pope from Chicago is just global, and so is the World Series. It\u8217\'20\'19s crazy.\u8221\'20\'1D <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/08/pope-leo-chicago-home-town"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Chicago reacts to hometown Pope Leo: \u8216\'20\'18Like the Cubs winning the World Series\u8217\'20\'19 }}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-09T02:55:48.042Z">at 3.55am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-09T02:01:40.866Z">3.01am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 The Peruvian national football team, La Bicolor, has released a picture of its football strip with a tribute to the new pope. The name on the shirt reads \u8220\'20\'1CL\u233\'00\'E9on\u8221\'20\'1D over the number 14, while the caption reads \u8220\'20\'1CA new leader in hope \u8230\'20\'26. and his heart is Peruvian.\u8221\'20\'1D <figure class="element element-tweet" data-canonical-url="{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SeleccionPeru/status/1920574137405215095"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://twitter.com/SeleccionPeru/status/1920574137405215095}}}\uc2 ">\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\u54753\'D5\'E1\u54786\'D6\'02\u54770\'D5\'F2\u54787\'D6\'03\u54780\'D5\'FC \u54777\'D5\'F9\u54774\'D5\'F6\u769\'03\'01\u54769\'D5\'F1\u54770\'D5\'F2\u54783\'D5\'FF \u54770\'D5\'F2\u54779\'D5\'FB \u54777\'D5\'F9\u54766\'D5\'EE \u54770\'D5\'F2\u54784\'D6\'00\u54781\'D5\'FD\u54770\'D5\'F2\u54783\'D5\'FF\u54766\'D5\'EE\u54779\'D5\'FB\u54791\'D6\'07\u54766\'D5\'EE\u8230\'20\'26 \u54790\'D6\'06 \u54770\'D5\'F2\u54784\'D6\'00 \u54781\'D5\'FD\u54770\'D5\'F2\u54783\'D5\'FF\u54786\'D6\'02\u54766\'D5\'EE\u54779\'D5\'FB\u54780\'D5\'FC \u54769\'D5\'F1\u54770\'D5\'F2 \u54768\'D5\'F0\u54780\'D5\'FC\u54783\'D5\'FF\u54766\'D5\'EE\u54791\'D6\'07\u54780\'D5\'FC\u769\'03\'01\u54779\'D5\'FB\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/UnSentimientoQueNosUne?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #UnSentimientoQueNosUne}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Yvxug4zrcT"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Yvxug4zrcT}}}\uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 La Bicolor (@SeleccionPeru) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SeleccionPeru/status/1920574137405215095?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 8, 2025}}}\uc2  </figure>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-09T01:48:42.979Z">2.48am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Louis Prevost , the eldest of the three Prevost brothers, said he had been in bed feeling ill when the news came that his brother had been elected pope. He {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abcnews.go.com/International/destined-pope-brother-leo-xiv-wanted-priest/story?id=121617183"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told ABC News}}}\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 My wife called to tell me there\u8217\'20\'19s white smoke from the chapel \u8230\'20\'26 They started reading his name, and when he went, \u8216\'20\'18blah, blah, blah, Roberto,\u8217\'20\'19 immediately I knew \u8211\'20\'13 that\u8217\'20\'19s Rob \u8230\'20\'26 I was just thankful I was still in bed lying down, because I might have fallen down.\par \par \uc2 Louis said he got out of bed and started \u8220\'20\'1Cdancing around like an idiot.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He said the new Pope Leo was \u8220\'20\'1Cdown to earth\u8221\'20\'1D, \u8220\'20\'1Csmart as a whip\u8221\'20\'1D and had a good sense of humour. His brother had loved his work as a missionary, he said, and had travelled the world through his work. Louis continued:\par \par \uc2 I thought I had done travelling in the Navy, but, my God, he blew me away.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-09T01:34:31.942Z">2.34am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Pope Leo\u8217\'20\'19s older brother, John Prevost , has told US media that as a child his sibling \u8220\'20\'1Cplayed priest\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cthe ironing board was the altar.\u8221\'20\'1D He had always wanted to be a priest, John {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abcnews.go.com/International/destined-pope-brother-leo-xiv-wanted-priest/story?id=121617183"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told ABC News}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 He knew right away. I don\u8217\'20\'19t think he\u8217\'20\'19s ever questioned it. I don\u8217\'20\'19t think he\u8217\'20\'19s ever thought of anything else.\par \par \uc2 Leo is a \uc2 Chicago White Sox\uc2  fan, his brother added, \u8220\'20\'1Ca regular, run-of-the-mill person.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-09T01:49:47.147Z">at 2.49am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-09T01:23:12.281Z">2.23am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 The new Pope Leo said in 2023 that he was opposed to the ordination of women, arguing that \u8220\'20\'1Cclericalizing women\u8221\'20\'1D would not solve problems in the Catholic Church and might create new ones, according to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.catholicnewsagency.com/news/255823/cardinal-at-synod-on-synodality-clericalizing-women-will-not-solve-problems"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Catholic news agency}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Asked about the possibility at a synod, the then-cardinal Robert Prevost told reporters:\par \par \uc2 The apostolic tradition is something that has been spelled out very clearly, especially if you want to talk about the question of women\u8217\'20\'19s ordination to the priesthood ...\par \par \uc2 Something that needs to be said also is that ordaining women \u8211\'20\'13 and there\u8217\'20\'19s been some women that have said this interestingly enough \u8211\'20\'13 \u8216\'20\'18clericalizing women\u8217\'20\'19 doesn\u8217\'20\'19t necessarily solve a problem, it might make a new problem.\par \par \uc2 He said that although women might become political leaders there was \u8220\'20\'1Cno immediate parallel\u8221\'20\'1D in the Church and added:\par \par \uc2 Perhaps we need to look at a new understanding or different understanding of both leadership, power, authority, and service \u8211\'20\'13 above all service \u8211\'20\'13 in the Church from the different perspectives that can be, if you will, brought to the life of the Church by women and men.\par \par \uc2 Despite {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/may/05/pope-francis-mixed-legacy-women-catholic-church"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appointing women to top Vatican roles}}}\uc2 , \uc2 Pope Francis\uc2  was also opposed to the ordination of women.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-09T01:23:37.057Z">at 2.23am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-09T01:09:55.634Z">2.09am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Prime minister Anthony Albanese says the election of US Cardinal Robert Prevost as new Pope \u8220\'20\'1Ccomes at an important time for the Catholic Church and the world\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 His statement says:\par \par \uc2 Today is a momentous day for Catholics around the world and faithful in Australia, and I join them in congratulating their Holy Father, Pope Leo XIV , Bishop of Rome, on his election overnight.\par \par \uc2 As the first North American Pope, Pope Leo XIV\u8217\'20\'19s leadership comes at an important time for the Catholic Church and the world.\par \par \uc2 Australia will invite His Holiness Pope Leo to Australia for the International Eucharistic Congress being proudly hosted in 2028. My government looks forward to continuing Australia\u8217\'20\'19s strong relationship with the Holy See under Pope Leo XIV\u8217\'20\'19s pontificate.\par \par \uc2 May the papacy of Pope Leo advance the cause of peace and social justice for all humanity.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-09T00:59:12.148Z">1.59am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 The pope has been praying in the Sistine Chapel: <figure class="element element-atom"> <gu-atom data-atom-id="81843ef3-0a65-443a-924c-d5bcf9c5754a" data-atom-type="media"> </gu-atom> </figure>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-09T00:46:18.148Z">1.46am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Cardinal \uc2 Se\u225\'00\'E1n O\u8217\'20\'19Malley\uc2  , who at 80 was too old to vote but {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/may/03/rumours-rock-star-cardinals-rome-pope-conclave"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 had been considered a papal contender}}}\uc2  this time round, has welcomed the choice of Robert Prevost in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cardinalseansblog.org/2025/05/08/the-gift-of-a-new-holy-father/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 post on his blog}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 He said the name Leo was \u8220\'20\'1C widely associated with the social justice legacy of Pope Leo XIII, who was pontiff at a time of epic upheaval in the world, the time of the industrial revolution, the beginning of Marxism, and widespread immigration.\u8221\'20\'1D He added:\par \par \uc2 The new Pope\u8217\'20\'19s rich pastoral experience in Latin America and as leader of an international religious community, and the years spent in Rome, will all provide valuable preparation for his new ministry as Pope.\par \par \uc2 He also pointed to the new pope\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cfrequent references to peace in his opening remarks\u8221\'20\'1D writing that they emphasised \u8220\'20\'1Cthe mission of the Church to be a leaven for unity in the human family.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 O\u8217\'20\'19Malley, who retired as archbishop of Boston last year, leads a commission tasked with preventing clerical abuse against minors.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-09T00:48:35.785Z">at 1.48am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-09T00:29:44.033Z">1.29am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 The choice of the name Leo, is a \u8220\'20\'1Cclear and deliberate\u8221\'20\'1D reference to Pope Leo XIII, author of the 1891 encyclical Rerum Novarum, which marked the beginning of the Churchs\u8217\'20\'19s modern social doctrine, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.vaticannews.va/en/vatican-city/news/2025-05/matteo-bruni-holy-see-press-office-conference-leo-xiv-pope-elect.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Vatican News reports}}}\uc2  citing papal spokesperson Matteo Bruni. He said:\par \par \uc2 In this context, it is clearly a reference to the lives of men and women, to their work \u8211\'20\'13 even in an age marked by artificial intelligence.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-09T00:15:45.901Z">1.15am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 US media have reported that the new pope has voted in three Republican primaries in his home state of Illinois since 2012, but no Democratic primaries.\par \par \uc2 He did not vote in last year\u8217\'20\'19s presidential election, according to the \uc2 New York Times\uc2 , which cited records from Will County, in suburban Chicago. Nor did he vote in the 2020 election in Will Country, or the 2022 midterms. The last Republican primary he voted in was 2016.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-09T00:05:13.905Z">1.05am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 As we mentioned earlier, Pope Leo XIV appears to have criticised the stance by US vice-president \uc2 JD Vance\uc2  , also a Catholic, on immigration. One article was headlined \u8220\'20\'1CJD Vance is wrong: Jesus doesn\u8217\'20\'19t ask us to rank our love for others.\u8221\'20\'1D In 2020, in the wake of George Floyd\u8217\'20\'19s death, Leo{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/drprevost/status/1266783036953317377"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  tweeted}}}\uc2 , \u8220\'20\'1CWe need to hear more from leaders in the Church, to reject racism and seek justice.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 These tweets appear to have upset the Maga movement in the US. Far-right influencer Laura Loomer wrote in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/LauraLoomer/status/1920537118041854297"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 post on X}}}\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 He is anti-Trump, anti-MAGA, pro-open Borders, and a total Marxist like \uc2 Pope Francis\uc2 . Catholics don\u8217\'20\'19t have anything good to look forward to. Just another Marxist puppet in the Vatican.\par \par \uc2 She also claimed he supported illegal immigrants and open borders, though it is not clear why she thinks that.\par \par \uc2 Another influential Maga cheerleader, Charlie Kirk , wrote:\par \par \uc2 Pope Leo XIV: Registered Chicago Republican and pro-life warrior OR Open borders globalist installed to counter Trump?\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-08T23:50:18.896Z">12.50am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 For cardinals in the conclave pondering who the next leader of the Catholic church should be, they will have considered leadership skills, pastoral experience, knowledge of the Vatican and toughness. Robert Prevost has all this in spades.\par \par \uc2 He led his religious order as prior general, he has worked in a diocese, and since 2023 has been in charge of the Vatican department that chooses bishops. The view is that he has made having a compassionate or pastoral approach a priority for choosing who joins the episcopacy.\par \par \uc2 There will be some who will worry that Prevost blotted his copybook when it came to dealing with abuse crises in Peru. The sexual abuse of children and vulnerable people remains a stain on the Catholic church, and how he handles it will be one of his great tests.\par \par \uc2 While some LGBTQ+ organisations noted that, before \uc2 Pope Francis\uc2  was elected, Prevost expressed concerns about what he called \u8220\'20\'1Cthe homosexual lifestyle\u8221\'20\'1D, it is noticeable that one of the Catholic church\u8217\'20\'19s leading advocates for gay people, the American Jesuit priest, James Martin, has described Prevost\u8217\'20\'19s election as \u8220\'20\'1Ca brilliant choice\u8221\'20\'1D, and said that Prevost is \u8220\'20\'1Ckind, open and honest\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-08T23:39:40.356Z">12.39am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 The Workers' Pope?\par \par \uc2 What\u8217\'20\'19s in a name? When it comes to a pope \u8211\'20\'13 everything. The white smoke from the Sistine Chapel earlier this evening told the world that a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/may/08/white-smoke-signals-election-of-new-roman-catholic-pope"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new pope to succeed Francis}}}\uc2  had been elected \u8211\'20\'13 and for the first time the pontiff is from the US.\par \par \uc2 But if \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his Catholic convert Veep, JD Vance, are ready to cheer, then they should think again. Cardinal Robert Prevost has chosen the name Leo XIV \u8211\'20\'13 and if you\u8217\'20\'19re a papal Leo, you tend to be a reformer at the progressive end of Catholicism.\par \par \uc2 That Prevost has decided to become Leo XIV will make Catholics think immediately of the last Leo \u8211\'20\'13 Leo XIII \u8211\'20\'13 and his 1891 encyclical or teaching document, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.vatican.va/content/leo-xiii/en/encyclicals/documents/hf_l-xiii_enc_15051891_rerum-novarum.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Rerum Novarum}}}\uc2 , which outlined workers\u8217\'20\'19 rights to a fair wage, safe working conditions and the rights of workers to belong to trade unions. If \uc2 Pope Francis\uc2  was the People\u8217\'20\'19s Pope, then Leo XIV is all set to be the Workers\u8217\'20\'19 Pope. <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2025/may/08/what-will-the-new-pope-be-like-hes-chosen-to-be-called-leo-thats-no-accident"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 What will the new Pope be like? He\u8217\'20\'19s chosen to be called Leo: that\u8217\'20\'19s no accident | Catherine Pepinster}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-08T23:25:04.141Z">12.25am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Peru\u8217\'20\'19s president, \uc2 Dina Boluarte\uc2  , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/presidenciaperu/status/1920563009706954856"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hailed the \u8220\'20\'1Chistoric\u8221\'20\'1D election}}}\uc2  of Leo XIV , whom she described as a Peruvian \u8220\'20\'1Cby choice and conviction\u8221\'20\'1D who had devoted more than 20 years of service to the country. She added that Prevost, 69, \u8220\'20\'1Cchose to be one of us, to live among us and to carry in his heart the faith, culture and dreams of this country\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 She added: \u8220\'20\'1CThe pope is Peruvian; God loves {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/peru"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Peru}}}\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Even so, Prevost has spoken out against Boluarte\u8217\'20\'19s government in the past. In early 2023, he described his \u8220\'20\'1Csadness and pain\u8221\'20\'1D over the deaths of 49 protesters in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/feb/08/peru-protests-president-election-what-is-happening-explainer"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 anti-government demonstrations}}}\uc2  that erupted when President Boluarte took office in December 2022, replacing Pedro Castillo who was forced out for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/dec/07/peru-parliament-dissolved-impeachment-vote-coup-fears"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 attempting to suspend congress}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 At the time Prevost said the unrest reflected the historic neglect of Peru\u8217\'20\'19s poor, saying: \u8220\'20\'1CThis conflict does not represent the best of the country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Pope Leo also called on late former president \uc2 Alberto Fujimori\uc2  , who was jailed in 2009 for human rights abuses and corruption to ask for forgiveness from each of his government\u8217\'20\'19s victims in order to begin a process of reconciliation.\par \par \uc2 His suggestion came just two days after Fujimori was given a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2017/dec/25/perus-jailed-ex-president-alberto-fujimori-pardoned-sparking-protests"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 presidential pardon as part of a political deal }}}\uc2 and released a video with a half-hearted apology. Prevost pointedly suggested \u8220\'20\'1Cit would be more effective to ask for forgiveness, personally, for some of the great injustices that were committed and for which he was tried and sentenced\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/sep/14/transformative-for-better-and-for-worse-whats-the-legacy-of-perus-alberto-fujimori"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 controversial ex-leader }}}\uc2 was sent back to jail in 2018, only to be {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/dec/07/alberto-fujimori-peru-former-president-released-jail"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pardoned again in 2023}}}\uc2  amid street protests. He died in 2024 and was given a state funeral. <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/may/08/pope-leo-xiv-peru-latin-america"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18The pope is Peruvian\u8217\'20\'19: elation in country where pontiff served as bishop}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-08T23:11:25.985Z">12.11am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 As news of Leo\u8217\'20\'19s election began to sink in, social media in Peru was flooded with memes of the pope eating ceviche, Peru\u8217\'20\'19s flagship dish, and drinking Inca Kola, its bubblegum-flavoured soft drink.\par \par \uc2 Others showed him in Peru\u8217\'20\'19s red-and-white football shirt and another humorous image showed the popemobile refashioned as a three-wheeled motorcycle rickshaw, the principal mode of transport in much of the country.\par \par \uc2 Some {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/may/08/chicago-new-pope-leo-xiv-memes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 posts on social media jokingly}}}\uc2  claimed that the new pope was \u8220\'20\'1Cmore Latino than the entire cast of Emilia P\u233\'00\'E9rez\u8221\'20\'1D, referencing the French film that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/film/2025/jan/16/jacques-audiard-emilia-perez-director-apologises"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sparked controversy}}}\uc2  over its portrayal of Mexico.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-08T22:52:44.887Z">11.52pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Palestinian president Mahmoud Abbas has called on the new Pope Leo XIV to pursue the \u8220\'20\'1Cpeace efforts\u8221\'20\'1D of his predecessor Francis, in an official statement.\par \par \uc2 Abbas sent \u8220\'20\'1Cbest wishes for the success of Pope Leo XIV in the pursuit of his noble task and maintaining the legacy of the late \uc2 Pope Francis\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D said the statement.\par \par \uc2 Abbas highlighted the \u8220\'20\'1Cimportance of the moral, religious and political role of the Vatican in the defence of just causes\u8221\'20\'1D, adding that \u8220\'20\'1Cthe Palestinian people and their right to liberty and independence\u8221\'20\'1D should be at the top.\par \par \uc2 Pope Francis\uc2  had been a critic of Israel\u8217\'20\'19s war on Gaza and had called the Holy Family Church in Gaza City every day after the war began until his death.\par \par \uc2 Shortly after his death it was revealed that Francis had approved the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/may/05/francis-popemobile-mobile-clinic-children-gaza"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 conversion of his popemobile}}}\uc2  into a mobile health clinic to treat children in Gaza.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-08T23:04:57.762Z">at 12.04am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-08T22:17:08.191Z">11.17pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Pope Leo XIV fell in love with Peru and its signature dish of raw seafood, ceviche, over his nearly two decades in the country, his successor as bishop of the northern city of Chiclayo has said said. AFP reports:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe loved goat, duck with rice and ceviche, those were his favourite dishes,\u8221\'20\'1D Chiclayo\u8217\'20\'19s current bishop Edison Farfan told a press conference.\par \par \uc2 He added that there were photographs in Chiclayo of him riding a horse.\par \par \uc2 Farfan recalled Prevost\u8217\'20\'19s beginnings in Peru as a missionary in the northern town of Chulucanas, fresh out of university in the United States.\par \par \uc2 From there he moved to the coastal city of Trujillo, where he helped set up an Augustinian seminary, before finally winding up in the far northern city of Chiclayo, where he was ordained a bishop in 2015, Farfan said.\par \par \uc2 Leo gave \u8220\'20\'1Chis whole life to the mission in Peru,\u8221\'20\'1D Farfan said, adding that the new pontiff, like his Argentine predecessor Francis, was particularly driven by poverty and by people living on the \u8220\'20\'1Cperiphery\u8221\'20\'1D of society.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-08T22:41:14.940Z">at 11.41pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-08T22:04:42.938Z">11.04pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 The internet exploded with humor and Chicago pride on Thursday following the historic announcement that Robert Francis Prevost , a 69-year-old American clergyman from Chicago, has been named the new pope.\par \par \uc2 The Chicago mayor, Brandon Johnson, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/ChicagosMayor/status/1920533436248305771"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 celebrated the moment}}}\uc2  on social media, posting:\par \par \uc2 Everything dope, including the Pope, comes from Chicago! Congratulations to the first American Pope Leo XIV! We hope to welcome you back home soon.\par \par \uc2 Other users asked for \u8220\'20\'1Cphotos of the new pope at the Bean\u8221\'20\'1D Chicago\u8217\'20\'19s famous sculpture, while MSNBC\u8217\'20\'19s Chris Hayes {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://bsky.app/profile/chrislhayes.bsky.social/post/3loogsyrxic2w"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wondered }}}\uc2 whether the pope was a \uc2 Chicago Cubs\uc2  fan, as others asked if he was a \uc2 White Sox\uc2  fan.\par \par \uc2 One X {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/EmSheDoesIt/status/1920533972456448304"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 user joked}}}\uc2 : \u8220\'20\'1CIn honor of Chicago\u8217\'20\'19s own Pope Leo XIV, the \uc2 White Sox\uc2  announce the new \u8216\'20\'18White Smoke Shake\u8217\'20\'19 that will be served in a commemorative pope hat.\u8221\'20\'1D Another poked fun at the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/AnnieAgar/status/1920530001755025771"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Chicago Bears}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/AnnieAgar/status/1920530001755025771"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  American Football team, writing}}}\uc2 : \u8220\'20\'1CChicago produced a pope before a QB who throws for 4,000 yards.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Others referenced Chicago\u8217\'20\'19s famous deep dish pizza, joking about the pope {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/biz_socks/status/1920530168466002111"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 serving deep dish pizza}}}\uc2  and to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://bsky.app/profile/link.spacelawshitpost.me/post/3lookoioonk27"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ask whether the new pope thinks that Chicago or Rome have better pizza.}}}\uc2  <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/may/08/chicago-new-pope-leo-xiv-memes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Deep dish eucharist\u8217\'20\'19: internet reacts to US pope with jokes and Chicago pride}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-08T21:58:34.089Z">10.58pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 UN\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s secretary general, Ant\u243\'00\'F3nio Guterres , has offered his \u8220\'20\'1Cheartfelt\u8221\'20\'1D congratulations to Pope Leo XIV and Catholics around the world.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur world is in need of the strongest voices for peace, social justice, human dignity [and] compassion,\u8221\'20\'1D the \uc2 UN\uc2  chief posted to X.\par \par \uc2 I look forward to building on the long legacy of cooperation between the \uc2 UN\uc2  and the Holy See to advance solidarity, foster reconciliation & build a just and sustainable world for all.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-08T21:49:30.632Z">10.49pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Robert Francis Prevost: the moderate, good humoured first American pope\par \par \uc2 Robert Francis Prevost \u8211\'20\'13 who has chosen the papal name Leo XIV \u8211\'20\'13 may not be the Latin American Jesuit wildcard that his predecessor, \uc2 Pope Francis\uc2 , was, but his election is similarly historic.\par \par \uc2 In the figure of the 69-year-old former head of the Augustinian order, the Roman Catholic church has its very first US leader.\par \par \uc2 Until Thursday evening, the idea of the fisherman\u8217\'20\'19s ring being slipped on to a North American hand was seen as a fairly distant possibility.\par \par \uc2 The Vatican\u8217\'20\'19s longstanding opposition to a US pope stemmed largely from the optics of having a pontiff from a political superpower and a country with such a hegemonic cultural and secular global influence.\par \par \uc2 But all that changed after a short conclave that chose a man who had been a cardinal for only a little more than two years.\par \par \uc2 While his appointment is likely to be welcomed by progressive factions within the church, it was probably not the news that some of his more conservative, Trump-aligned US brother cardinals had been hoping for.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/may/08/robert-francis-prevost-the-moderate-good-humoured-first-american-pope"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Read the full profile: }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/may/08/robert-francis-prevost-the-moderate-good-humoured-first-american-pope"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Robert Francis Prevost: the moderate, good humoured first American pope}}}\uc2  <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/may/08/robert-francis-prevost-the-moderate-good-humoured-first-american-pope"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Robert Francis Prevost: the moderate, good humoured first US pope}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-08T21:40:51.056Z">10.40pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Canada \u8217\'20\'19s newly elected prime minister, Mark Carney, has called the pope\u8217\'20\'19s election a \u8220\'20\'1Chistoric day for Catholics and all who look to the Vatican for guidance\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 A practicing Catholic, Carney said he offered his \u8220\'20\'1Cprayers and best wishes\u8221\'20\'1D to Pope Leo XIV, adding:\par \par \uc2 At a time of global challenges, may his pontificate carry forward a mission of solidarity, compassion, and dignity for all.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-08T22:09:15.476Z">at 11.09pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-08T21:35:01.771Z">10.35pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 A London LGBT+ faith group has welcomed the election of Robert Francis Prevost as Pope Leo XIV and said it hopes he has \u8220\'20\'1Cmoved on\u8221\'20\'1D from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2025/may/08/new-pope-conclave-vatican-white-black-smoke-papacy-catholic-cardinals?page=with%3Ablock-681d07f78f087953796a09f4#block-681d07f78f087953796a09f4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 previous remarks where he criticised the \u8220\'20\'1Chomosexual lifestyle\u8221\'20\'1D.}}}\par \par \uc2 As we reported earlier, Prevost said in a 2012 address to the world Synod of Bishops that \u8220\'20\'1CWestern mass media is extraordinarily effective in fostering within the general public enormous sympathy for beliefs and practices that are at odds with the Gospel \u8212\'20\'14 for example \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , homosexual lifestyle, euthanasia\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe trust he will be open to listen to the lived experience of LGBT+ Catholics, their parents and families,\u8221\'20\'1D the statement by the LGBT+ Catholics Westminster Pastoral Council reads.\par \par \uc2 Opinions and ideas can change, and he supported \uc2 Pope Francis\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 change in pastoral practice to allow divorced and civilly remarried Catholics to receive Holy Communion, and he showed support for Fiducia Supplicans, allowing blessings for same-sex couples.\par \par \uc2 He has expressed openness to marginalized groups, though his stance on specific issues remains ambiguous, including the concerns of LGBT+ Catholics.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-08T21:24:14.766Z">10.24pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 In the early hours of 20 February 1878, following a third ballot, the door of the ground gallery of the Vatican Basilica was thrown open and Italian-born Cardinal Pecci was announced as the successor to Pope Pius IX.\par \par \uc2 According to our Special Correspondent, the new Pope\u8217\'20\'19s first appearance gave the signal for the \u8216\'20\'18most vociferous cheering\u8217\'20\'19, the Rome crowd taking up the shout and crying \u8220\'20\'1Clong live the Pope\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Readers were also told that the new Pope, who had chosen Leo out of admiration for Pope Leo XII, was a \u8220\'20\'1Cman of moderate views in religious matters, though of distinguished piety, combined with great energy and character...\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Leo XIII \u8217\'20\'19s papacy lasted until his death in 1903, making him one of the longest-serving Popes.\par \par \uc2 Biographers later {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.britannica.com/biography/Leo-XIII"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 noted}}}\uc2  that he \u8220\'20\'1Cbrought a new spirit to the papacy, expressed in more conciliatory positions toward civil governments, by less opposition to scientific progress, and by an awareness of the pastoral and social needs of the times.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-08T21:16:46.202Z">10.16pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Here are some images from the newswires showing how people from around the world cheered the election of Robert Francis Prevost, now known as Pope Leo XIV.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-08T21:17:57.242Z">at 10.17pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-08T21:03:16.266Z">10.03pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Summary of the day so far\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A new pope is elected. US cardinal Robert Francis Prevost , will be known as Pope Leo XIV . It\u8217\'20\'19s been a long while since we had a pope with this name: last Leo, Leo XIII, was elected in 1878 and served until his death in 1903.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 In his first comments after his election , Pope Leo XIV preached a message of \u8220\'20\'1Cunity\u8221\'20\'1D and of \u8220\'20\'1Cmoving forward\u8221\'20\'1D. He said he wants this message of peace to \u8220\'20\'1Center your hearts, to reach your families and all people, wherever they are.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Many shared their excitement at having an American pope , and specifically a pope born in Chicago. City mayor Brandon Johnson tweeted \u8220\'20\'1CEverything dope, including the Pope, comes from Chicago\u8221\'20\'1D and former US president \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  congratulated the \u8220\'20\'1Cfellow Chicagoan\u8221\'20\'1D on social media.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 US president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  said he was \u8220\'20\'1Csurprised\u8221\'20\'1D but that it is a \u8220\'20\'1Cgreat honor\u8221\'20\'1D to have an American pope. World leaders from several countries including Italy, Spain, Greece, Ukraine , Peru and the United Kingdom have offered their congratulations.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 An account on X widely believed to belong to the new pope shows him to be somewhat critical of the Trump administration. The account posted two articles that took issue with the stance by JD Vance , also a Catholic, on immigration. One article was headlined \u8220\'20\'1CJD Vance is wrong: Jesus doesn\u8217\'20\'19t ask us to rank our love for others.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 In a 2012 address to the world Synod of Bishops , Father Robert Francis Prevost, now Pope Leo XIV appeared to criticize homosexuality, saying \u8220\'20\'1CWestern mass media is extraordinarily effective in fostering within the general public enormous sympathy for beliefs and practices that are at odds with the Gospel \u8212\'20\'14 for example \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , homosexual lifestyle, euthanasia\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-08T20:52:42.905Z">9.52pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 The election of Pope Leo XIV is being celebrated across Latin America \u8211\'20\'13 particularly in Peru , where he lived and worked for more than 20 years and was granted citizenship in 2015 \u8211\'20\'13 as a kind of \u8220\'20\'1Csecond Latin American pope\u8221\'20\'1D, following his Argentine predecessor, Francis.\par \par \uc2 The president of Peru, \uc2 Dina Boluarte\uc2 , said that Leo\u8217\'20\'19s election was \u8220\'20\'1Cnot only the first time that an American has ascended to the throne of Saint Peter, but also the first occasion on which a Peruvian, with more than 20 years of service on our soil, leads the Catholic Church as Supreme Pontiff.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She added: \u8220\'20\'1CThe Pope is Peruvian; God loves Peru.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The new pope holds Peruvian citizenship, after having lived and worked in the country on at least three separate occasions since the 1980s \u8211\'20\'13 with a period back in Chicago in the early 2000s \u8211\'20\'13 and only left Peru in 2023, when he was appointed to a position at the Vatican.\par \par \uc2 In his first appearance from the Vatican balcony, Leo XIV briefly switched from Italian to Spanish to address the faithful \u8220\'20\'1Cfrom my beloved diocese of Chiclayo, in Peru,\u8221\'20\'1D where he served as bishop for over a decade.\par \par \uc2 In Colombia, the interior minister, Armando Benedetti, posted on social media that the years spent in Peru \u8220\'20\'1Cmean the new pope is once again a Latin American.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Some posts on social media jokingly claimed that the new pope is \u8220\'20\'1Cmore Latino than the entire cast of Emilia P\u233\'00\'E9rez,\u8221\'20\'1D referencing the French film that sparked controversy over its portrayal of Mexico.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-08T20:45:11.160Z">9.45pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Prime ministers of Spain and Greece react to the new pope\par \par \uc2 The prime minister of Spain Pedro S\u225\'00\'E1nchez has offered his congratulations on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/sanchezcastejon/status/1920529498488897753"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 social }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://media.he"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 media.}}}\uc2  He wrote: \u8220\'20\'1CCongratulations to the entire Catholic Church for the election of the new Pope Leo XIV as @Pontifex_es. May your pontificate contribute to strengthening dialogue and the defense of human rights in a world in need of hope and unity.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Greek prime minister \uc2 Kyriakos Mitsotakis\uc2  has also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/PrimeministerGR/status/1920556362569801990"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 added his voice}}}\uc2  to leaders welcoming the news of the election of the Chicago-born pontiff. He said: \u8220\'20\'1CCongratulations to Pope Leo XIV. Your leadership comes at a time when the world faces profound challenges but also great opportunities for unity, compassion, and dialogue among peoples and faiths.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Greece, like fellow Christian Orthodox Cyprus, have small but ancient Catholic communities that Pope Leo\u8217\'20\'19s predecessor, \uc2 Pope Francis\uc2 , made a point of visiting as part of his emphasis on the peripheries during his twelve-year tenure.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-08T20:56:37.387Z">at 9.56pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-08T20:31:34.461Z">9.31pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Share your views on Pope Leo XIV.\par \par \uc2 Robert Francis Prevost, from Chicago, has become the first American pope to lead the Roman Catholic church. We\u8217\'20\'19d like to hear your thoughts about the first clergyman from the US to lead the Roman Catholic church. <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/may/08/share-new-pope-leo-xiv-american"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Share your views on Pope Leo XIV}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-08T20:32:14.296Z">at 9.32pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-08T20:21:40.834Z">9.21pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 New pope criticized 'homosexual lifestyle' as 'at odds with the Gospel' in 2012 speech\par \par \uc2 In a 2012 address to the world Synod of Bishops, Father Robert Francis Prevost , who became Pope Leo XIV on Thursday, said that \u8220\'20\'1CWestern mass media is extraordinarily effective in fostering within the general public enormous sympathy for beliefs and practices that are at odds with the Gospel \u8212\'20\'14 for example \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , homosexual lifestyle, euthanasia\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In the remarks, which he also read portions of for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://youtu.be/WttXvZt3m6k?si=f0JSnB4X5XU4cLyN"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a video}}}\uc2  produced by the Catholic News Service, a news agency owned by the United States Conference of Catholic Bishops, the cleric added:\par \par \uc2 The sympathy for anti-Christian lifestyles choices that mass media fosters is so brilliantly and artfully engrained in the viewing public that when people hear the Christian message it often inevitably seems ideological and emotionally cruel by contrast to the humaneness of the anti-Christian perspective.\par \par \uc2 Catholic pastors who preach against the legalization of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  or the redefinition of marriage are portrayed as being ideologically driven, severe and uncaring. \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 Note for example how alternative families comprised of same-sex partners and their adopted children are so benignly and sympathetically portrayed in television programs and cinema today.\par \par \uc2 The video illustrates his criticism of the \u8220\'20\'1Chomosexual lifestyle\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Csame-sex partners and their adopted children\u8221\'20\'1D with clips from two US sitcoms, The New Normal and Modern Family.\par \par \uc2 The cleric also called for a \u8220\'20\'1Cnew evangelization to counter these mass media-produced distortions of religious and ethical reality\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-08T20:13:37.245Z">9.13pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  congratulates 'fellow Chicagoan'\par \par \uc2 Former US president \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  congratulated the \u8220\'20\'1Cfellow Chicagoan\u8221\'20\'1D Pope Leo XIV in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/BarackObama/status/1920551037632397447"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 social media}}}\uc2  post.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMichelle and I send our congratulations to a fellow Chicagoan, His Holiness Pope Leo XIV. This is a historic day for the United States, and we will pray for him as he begins the sacred work of leading the Catholic Church and setting an example for so many, regardless of faith.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-08T20:22:09.378Z">at 9.22pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-08T20:00:41.557Z">9.00pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Villanova University\uc2  , the Catholic institution in Pennsylvania where Pope Leo XIV is an alumnus, celebrated the pope\u8217\'20\'19s election in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www1.villanova.edu/university/media/press-releases/2025/pope.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a statement}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs an Augustinian Catholic institution, we celebrate this significant day for our University community and the global Church. Villanova, built on the teachings of St. Augustine, has always been grounded in advancing a deeper understanding of the fundamental relationship between faith and reason\u8212\'20\'14between spirituality and wisdom,\u8221\'20\'1D said University President the Rev \uc2 Peter M Donohue\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWith today\u8217\'20\'19s election of His Holiness, Pope Leo XIV, I cannot help but reflect on what his Augustinian papacy will mean to our University community and our world. Known for his humility, gentle spirit, prudence and warmth, Pope Leo XIV\u8217\'20\'19s leadership offers an opportunity to reaffirm our commitment to our educational mission,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-08T20:01:25.152Z">at 9.01pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-08T19:46:13.815Z">8.46pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 UK prime minister \uc2 Keir Starmer\uc2  says election of first US pope a 'momentous moment'\par \par \uc2 British prime minister \uc2 Keir Starmer\uc2  posted a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/Keir_Starmer/status/1920545025731043349?ref_src=twsrc%5Egoogle%7Ctwcamp%5Eserp%7Ctwgr%5Etweet"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement on X}}}\uc2 , calling it \u8220\'20\'1Ca momentous moment.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe election of Pope Leo XIV is a deeply profound moment of joy for Catholics in the United Kingdom and globally, and begins a new chapter for the leadership of the Church and in the world\u8220\'20\'1C the statement reads.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPope Leo is the first American Pope. This is a momentous moment. As \uc2 Pope Francis\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 papacy showed, the Holy See has a special role to play in bringing people and nations together to address the major issues of our time; especially on climate change, alleviating poverty and promoting peace and justice across the world\u8221\'20\'1D he adds.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-08T19:50:42.734Z">at 8.50pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-08T19:31:13.241Z">8.31pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 An{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/drprevost"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  account on X}}}\uc2  widely believed to belong to the new pope offers a short tour of his interests. He tweeted and retweeted posts in both Spanish and English, reflecting his American heritage and his missionary work in Peru. He was close with his predecessor, \uc2 Pope Francis\uc2  , and tweeted prayers for the former pontiff\u8217\'20\'19s health in recent months.\par \par \uc2 Leo also tweeted in disagreement with vice president \uc2 JD Vance\uc2  . In February of this year, Leo posted two articles that took issue with the stance by Vance, also a Catholic, on immigration. One article was headlined \u8220\'20\'1CJD Vance is wrong: Jesus doesn\u8217\'20\'19t ask us to rank our love for others.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In 2020 and 2021, he used his account to encourage followers to follow social distancing measures and get the covid-19 vaccine. Also in 2020, in the wake of George Floyd\u8217\'20\'19s death, Leo{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/drprevost/status/1266783036953317377"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  tweeted}}}\uc2 , \u8220\'20\'1CWe need to hear more from leaders in the Church, to reject racism and seek justice.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-08T19:18:16.435Z">8.18pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 JB Pritzker , the governor of Illinois, the US state where Pope Leo XIV was born, welcomed the new pope in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/GovPritzker/status/1920536345404965189"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 social media}}}\uc2  post.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA historic moment as we witness the first American leading the Catholic Church,\u8221\'20\'1D he wrote. \u8220\'20\'1CHailing from Chicago, Pope Leo XIV ushers in a new chapter that I join those in our state welcoming in at a time when we need compassion, unity, and peace.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-08T19:06:01.916Z">8.06pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Trump says 'surprise' and 'great honour' to have an American pope\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  said he was \u8220\'20\'1Csurprised\u8221\'20\'1D and called it a \u8220\'20\'1Cgreat honor\u8221\'20\'1D to have an American pope. He added that he is \u8220\'20\'1Chappy\u8221\'20\'1D with the choice when speaking with reporters.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-08T19:19:14.797Z">at 8.19pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-08T18:54:58.381Z">7.54pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 US vice president \uc2 JD Vance\uc2  congratulated the new pope in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/JDVance/status/1920550545061810261"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 post on X}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CCongratulations to Leo XIV, the first American Pope, on his election! I\u8217\'20\'19m sure millions of American Catholics and other Christians will pray for his successful work leading the Church. May God bless him!\u8221\'20\'1D Vance wrote.\par \par \uc2 As we reported earlier, Pope Leo XIV had criticized some members of the Trump administration on social media, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/drprevost/status/1886469097560719594"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 including JD Vance}}}\uc2 . The late \uc2 Pope Francis\uc2  also had a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2025/apr/23/pope-francis-jd-vance-meeting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 complicated relationship}}}\uc2  with the vice president.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-08T18:43:14.489Z">7.43pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 The prime minister of Italy \uc2 Giorgia Meloni\uc2  extended her wishes for Pope Leo XIV in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/GiorgiaMeloni/status/1920546271099531369"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 post on X}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI extend my most sincere wishes to Pope Leo XIV for the beginning of his pontificate. In a time marked by conflict and unrest, his words from the Loggia delle Benedizioni are a powerful call for peace, brotherhood and responsibility.\par \par \uc2 A spiritual legacy that follows the path traced by \uc2 Pope Francis\uc2 , and that Italy looks at with respect and hope.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-08T18:33:39.130Z">7.33pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 New Pope Leo XIV - what we know so far\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 69-year-old US cardinal Robert Francis Prevost has been elected as Pope Leo XIV , prompted celebration and delight among more than 100,000 pilgrims and tourists in St Peter\u8217\'20\'19s Square.\par \par \uc2 <figure class="element element-atom"> <gu-atom data-atom-id="f99fd3e7-55d7-4687-a119-6d070c1e4048" data-atom-type="media"> </gu-atom> </figure>\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2025/may/08/new-pope-conclave-vatican-white-black-smoke-papacy-catholic-cardinals?page=with%3Ablock-681cf2a68f082cdfc1daaff3#block-681cf2a68f082cdfc1daaff3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 moderate, Chicago-born cardinal}}}\uc2  was given senior roles by \uc2 Pope Francis\uc2 , and has significant missionary experience in Peru having served as bishop of the northern city of Chiclayo.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 He was elected on the second day of conclave, securing a majority of votes among 133 cardinal electors.\par \par \uc2 <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/may/08/white-smoke-signals-election-of-new-roman-catholic-pope"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Robert Prevost becomes Pope Leo XIV as cardinals elect first US pontiff}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Global leaders , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2025/may/08/new-pope-conclave-vatican-white-black-smoke-papacy-catholic-cardinals?page=with%3Ablock-681ceebf8f0835e2df499a38#block-681ceebf8f0835e2df499a38"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 including US president Donald Trump}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2025/may/08/new-pope-conclave-vatican-white-black-smoke-papacy-catholic-cardinals?page=with%3Ablock-681cf36a8f087953796a090d#block-681cf36a8f087953796a090d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 key European heads of state and government}}}\uc2 , offered their congratulations for the new head of the Roman Catholic church.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 But between wars, migration, the climate crisis and divisions in his church, the new leader has no shortage of challenges ahead.\par \par \uc2 <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/may/06/the-papal-in-tray-new-pontiff-will-have-to-hit-the-ground-running-on-so-many-urgent-issues"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pope Leo\u8217\'20\'19s in-tray: pontiff has many urgent issues to address}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s all from me, Jakub Krupa , but Marina Dunbar will guide you through the evening in Rome with the latest updates.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-08T18:34:52.308Z">at 7.34pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-08T18:25:48.956Z">7.25pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 "Habemus Papam!" - the moment Pope Leo XIV was presented to world\par \par \uc2 <figure class="element element-atom"> <gu-atom data-atom-id="f99fd3e7-55d7-4687-a119-6d070c1e4048" data-atom-type="media"> </gu-atom> </figure>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-08T18:14:59.944Z">7.14pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 First messages of congratulations from political leaders\par \par \uc2 Ukrainian president \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskyy\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CCongratulations to His Holiness Pope Leo XIV @Pontifex on his election to the See of Saint Peter and the beginning of his pontificate.\par \par \uc2 Ukraine deeply values the Holy See\u8217\'20\'19s consistent position in upholding international law, condemning the Russian Federation\u8217\'20\'19s military aggression against Ukraine, and protecting the rights of innocent civilians.\par \par \uc2 At this decisive moment for our country, we hope for the continued moral and spiritual support of the Vatican in Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to restore justice and achieve a lasting peace.\par \par \uc2 I wish His Holiness Leo XIV wisdom, inspiration, and strength\u8212\'20\'14both spiritual and physical\u8212\'20\'14in carrying out his noble mission.\par \par \uc2 Ad multos annos!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 French president \uc2 Emmanuel Macron\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA historic moment for the Catholic Church and its millions of faithful. To Pope Leo XIV, and to all Catholics in France and around the world, I extend a message of fraternity.\par \par \uc2 On this May 8th, may this new pontificate be one of peace and hope.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Russian president \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am confident that the constructive dialogue and cooperation established between Russia and the Vatican will continue to develop on the basis of the Christian values that unite us.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 European Council president Ant\u243\'00\'F3nio Costa:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI warmly welcome the election of the new Pope Leo XIV, a moment of hope for millions around the world. In times of division and uncertainty, his spiritual leadership can help inspire unity, compassion, and peace.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 European Union\uc2  and the Holy See share a deep commitment to human dignity. I\u8217\'20\'19m looking forward to working together in our shared pursuit of the common good.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 US state secretary \uc2 Marco Rubio\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe United States looks forward to deepening our enduring relationship with the Holy See with the first American pontiff.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Lots of other European leaders also published their best wishes, including Spain\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/sanchezcastejon/status/1920529498488897753"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pedro S\u225\'00\'E1nchez}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/donaldtusk/status/1920542472687530084"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Poland\u8217\'20\'19s Andrzej Duda and Donald Tusk,}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/PM_ViktorOrban/status/1920530877630595182"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hungary\u8217\'20\'19s Viktor Orb\u225\'00\'E1n}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/LMontenegro_PT/status/1920531886838808604"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Portugal\u8217\'20\'19s Lu\u237\'00\'EDs Montenegro}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/_CStocker/status/1920533429977837889"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Austria\u8217\'20\'19s Christian Stocker,}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/P_Fiala/status/1920540045557018999"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Czech Republic\u8217\'20\'19s Petr Fiala,}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/MinPres/status/1920540945289728367"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Netherlands\u8217\'20\'19 Dick Schoof}}}\uc2  and many, many others.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-08T18:22:35.764Z">at 7.22pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-08T18:09:06.303Z">7.09pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Key facts about the new pope\par \par \uc2 Vatican\u8217\'20\'19s news service has now posted {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.vaticannews.va/en/pope/news/2025-05/cardinal-elected-pope-papal-name.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a lengthy biography of the new pope.}}}\par \par \uc2 I have read it for you, so here are the key facts about Pope Leo XIV, Robert Francis Prevost:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 69-year-old American\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 first Augustinian Pope\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 born in Chicago, Illinois to parents of French, Italian and Spanish decent\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 has two brothers, Luis Martin and John Joseph\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 studied in the US and entered the notiviate in Saint Louis, US, before receiving theological education in Chicago\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 was sent to Rome at the age of 27 to study canon law, where he was ordained priest\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 his long-standing connection with Peru dates back to 1985, when he served in an Augustinian mission in Chulucanas, Peru\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 he later joined a separate mission in Trujillo, Peru\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 he was made bishop of Chiclayo, Peru in 2015\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 promoted to archbishop in 2023 and created cardinal in 2024\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-08T18:00:11.028Z">7.00pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 New pontiff will have to hit ground running on many urgent issues\par \par \uc2 From conflicts in Ukraine and the Middle East , to migration , the climate crisis and schisms in the church , the honeymoon period for the new pope will be short.\par \par \uc2 The Roman Catholic church has a new leader, the Chicago-born Robert Francis Prevost , now Pope Leo XIV. Once the prayers are over and the crowds have dispersed from St Peter\u8217\'20\'19s Square, what issues must the new pope grapple with?\par \par \uc2 Church unity\par \par \uc2 A key task will be to strengthen unity within the church amid growing polarisation in the world and different views and expectations within the church. Some observers believe there is a real risk of schism after 20 years in which there have been popes on either end of the spectrum: the traditional/conservative \uc2 Benedict XVI\uc2 , and the liberal/progressive Francis.\par \par \uc2 International diplomacy\par \par \uc2 The pope has an important role to play on the international stage, particularly to ensure that religion does not become a fault line. He will face ongoing conflicts in Ukraine, the Middle East and Sudan plus the politically divisive issues of migration, the climate crisis, religious freedom and human rights.\par \par \uc2 Sexual abuse\par \par \uc2 The legacy of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/apr/22/tragedy-child-sexual-abuse-scandal-cast-long-shadow-over-pope-franciss-papacy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sexual abuse cast a long shadow}}}\uc2  over Francis\u8217\'20\'19s papacy. He was slow to grasp the scale and systemic nature of the problem, and at first did not understand the pain and anger of survivors. That pain has not gone away, and the new pope\u8217\'20\'19s approach will inevitably come under intense scrutiny.\par \par \uc2 Governance\par \par \uc2 The new pope will need to take decisions on governance within the church, including the pace of change and levels of inclusion regarding laity and women. He will need to make key appointments within days to get the new papacy up and running.\par \par \uc2 Vatican finances\par \par \uc2 There are two aspects to this for the new pope\u8217\'20\'19s attention: general oversight and transparency, on which there was significant progress under \uc2 Pope Francis\uc2  but still more to do; and the unsustainable levels of deficit in the Vatican finances, which deteriorated during Francis\u8217\'20\'19s papacy.\par \par \uc2 Sexuality and identity\par \par \uc2 Francis shifted the church\u8217\'20\'19s dial on issues relating to sexuality and identity, condemning discrimination against LGBTQ+ people, meeting trans men and women and authorising the blessings of same sex couples. Francis\u8217\'20\'19s standpoint prompted a backlash among traditionalists, and the new pope will be watched closely for his views.\par \par \uc2 Read more about papal in-tray: <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/may/06/the-papal-in-tray-new-pontiff-will-have-to-hit-the-ground-running-on-so-many-urgent-issues"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pope Leo\u8217\'20\'19s in-tray: pontiff has many urgent issues to address}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-08T17:58:17.609Z">6.58pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 "Everything dope, including the Pope, comes from Chicago,' city mayor quips\par \par \uc2 Chicago mayor Brandon Johnson responded to the news about the new pope {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/ChicagosMayor/status/1920533436248305771"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 on social media}}}\uc2  saying:\par \par \uc2 Everything dope, including the Pope, comes from Chicago! Congratulations to the first American Pope Leo XIV! We hope to welcome you back home soon.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-08T17:56:15.641Z">6.56pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 It appears the new pope is active on social media.\par \par \uc2 Given what seems to be his previous criticism towards some members of the Trump administration, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/drprevost/status/1886469097560719594"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 such as this comment towards JD Vance}}}\uc2  or {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/drprevost/status/1889907998753173882"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 perhaps this one}}}\uc2 , their relationship will be one to watch.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-08T17:52:44.137Z">6.52pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 US president Trump congratulates Leo XIV, looks forward to meeting\par \par \uc2 First congratulations are in from the US president, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://truthsocial.com/@realDonaldTrump/posts/114473380014194441"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 who said on Truth Social:}}}\par \par \uc2 Congratulations to Cardinal Robert Francis Prevost, who was just named Pope. It is such an honor to realize that he is the first American Pope. What excitement, and what a Great Honor for our Country. I look forward to meeting Pope Leo XIV. It will be a very meaningful moment!\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-08T17:47:54.746Z">6.47pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 In his first comments, the new pope calls for the light of Christ to serve \u8220\'20\'1Cas the bridge\u8221\'20\'1D to God\u8217\'20\'19s love.\par \par \uc2 He recalls the words of St Augustine:\par \par \uc2 For you I am a bishop; but with you I am a Christian.\par \par \uc2 He also says a few words addressed to the church of Rome , and thanks his (now former) diocese in Chiclayo in Peru .\par \par \uc2 He leads the faithful in St Peter\u8217\'20\'19s Square in prayer, with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.vaticannews.va/en/prayers/the-hail-mary.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ave Maria.}}}\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-08T17:34:33.622Z">6.34pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Message of peace and unity from new pope\par \par \uc2 In his first comments in Italian, Pope Leo XIV says he wants this message of peace to \u8220\'20\'1Center your hearts, to reach your families and all people, wherever they are.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Paying tribute to \uc2 Pope Francis\uc2 , he urges faithful to \u8220\'20\'1Cmove forward, without fear, united, hand in hand with God and with each other.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He also thanks fellow cardinals for choosing him for the role.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-08T17:27:54.165Z">6.27pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPeace be with all of you\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 Pope Leo XIV addresses crowds\par \par \uc2 The newly elected Pope Leo XIV, Cardinal Robert Prevost of the United States, appears on the balcony of St Peter\u8217\'20\'19s Basilica.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-08T17:36:45.781Z">at 6.36pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-08T17:17:56.866Z">6.17pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Habemus Papam: Pope Leo XIV!\par \par \uc2 The new pope, US cardinal Robert Francis Prevost, will be known as Pope Leo XIV.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s been a long while since we had a pope with this name: last Leo, Leo XIII, was elected in 1878 and served until his death in 1903.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-08T17:19:53.868Z">at 6.19pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-08T17:14:47.329Z">6.14pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 It's Robert Francis Prevost!\par \par \uc2 We have an American pope!\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s our profile of Prevost from before the conclave:\par \par \uc2 Despite the Vatican\u8217\'20\'19s longstanding opposition to the idea of a pope from the US because of the country\u8217\'20\'19s superpower status and secular global influence, the moderate, Chicago-born Prevost is still one to watch.\par \par \uc2 Created a cardinal by Francis in 2023, the former leader of the Augustinian order was also appointed by the late pope to the powerful Dicastery for Bishops, which oversees the selection of new bishops from around the world.\par \par \uc2 Those senior roles, combined with the fact that he has significant missionary experience in Peru, having served as bishop of the northern city of Chiclayo, may go some way to redeeming him in the eyes of those who would not usually countenance the idea of an American pope.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-08T17:15:56.963Z">at 6.15pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-08T17:13:40.969Z">6.13pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 And here\u8217\'20\'19s the announcement\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-08T17:13:02.572Z">6.13pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s just over an hour now since the white smoke, so we should see the new pope for the first time fairly soon.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-08T17:03:49.892Z">6.03pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Who will announce next pope?\par \par \uc2 It will be the French cardinal protodeacon Dominique Mamberti who will announce the new pope to the world, with the historic phrase: \u8220\'20\'1CHabemus Papam!\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Unless, that it, he is the one who was elected!\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-08T17:01:49.112Z">6.01pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Daniel writes in to make a good point that \u8220\'20\'1Cthe baptismal name given in the announcement will be the latinized version of it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Jorge Mario was \u8220\'20\'1CGiorgium Marium\u8221\'20\'1D, Joseph was \u8220\'20\'1CJosefus\u8221\'20\'1D and Karol was \u8220\'20\'1CKarolum\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Let\u8217\'20\'19s see who is it now.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-08T17:00:22.145Z">6.00pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Joy in Vatican - in pictures\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-08T16:50:28.848Z">5.50pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 'Incredible moment in history' - first reactions from pilgrims\par \par \uc2 from St Peter\u8217\'20\'19s Square\par \par \uc2 Raul Paredes and his family, from Colombia, were dancing with flags of their home country draped over their shoulders as the bells of St Peter\u8217\'20\'19s Basilica confirmed that a new pope had been found.\par \par \uc2 The family had booked their visit to Rome in December and had been hoping to see the late \uc2 Pope Francis\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CBut then Francis got sick and suddenly died,\u8221\'20\'1D said Paredes. \u8220\'20\'1CBut still, we crossed the Atlantic to be here for this incredible moment in history.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Parades admired Francis because, as a divorced Catholic, he felt welcomed by the church. \u8220\'20\'1CI hope we now get someone similar.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-08T16:40:07.157Z">5.40pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 'Never seen anything like it' - joy inside St Peter's Square\par \par \uc2 from St Peter\u8217\'20\'19s Square\par \par \uc2 There was a huge rush of journalists from the Vatican\u8217\'20\'19s press centre who ran out on to the square to capture the immediate reaction.\par \par \uc2 The rumour, the feeling that it would happen today was starting to build throughout the day. That seems to have begun when Cardinal Battista Re said this morning that he hopes to see the white smoke today.\par \par \uc2 The atmosphere is absolutely incredible, I have never seen anything like it.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-08T16:48:04.747Z">at 5.48pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-08T16:31:09.038Z">5.31pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 White smoke signals new pope - video\par \par \uc2 <figure class="element element-atom"> <gu-atom data-atom-id="ba5433ce-dfd7-4b5d-b942-9b2d59766597" data-atom-type="media"> </gu-atom> </figure>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-08T16:29:07.931Z">5.29pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Who is the new pope?\par \par \uc2 Could it be any of the favourites we talked about? <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/may/07/who-next-pope-potential-candidates-conclave"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Who will be the next pope? Leading candidates for the conclave to consider}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 Or someone else?\par \par \uc2 Surely not too long now before we learn that.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-08T16:17:40.248Z">5.17pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 If you\u8217\'20\'19re wondering about the timing of that next steps, here\u8217\'20\'19s Angela Giuffrida and Harriet Sherwood:\par \par \uc2 When \uc2 Jorge Bergoglio\uc2 , who became \uc2 Pope Francis\uc2 , was elected in March 2013, his identity was revealed about 45 minutes after the white smoke when he appeared on the balcony above St Peter\u8217\'20\'19s Square. <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/may/08/white-smoke-signals-election-of-new-roman-catholic-pope"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 White smoke signals election of new Roman Catholic pope}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-08T16:15:11.396Z">5.15pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Once the new pope appears on the balcony of St Peter\u8217\'20\'19s Basilica, we will hear a simple message:\par \par \uc2 Annuntio vobis gaudium magnum:\u8232\'20\'28Habemus Papam!\par \par \uc2 Eminentissimum ac reverendissimum dominum,\u8232\'20\'28dominum [baptismal name],\u8232\'20\'28Sanct\u230\'00\'E6 Roman\u230\'00\'E6 Ecclesi\u230\'00\'E6 Cardinalem [surname],\u8232\'20\'28qui sibi nomen imposuit [papal name].\par \par \uc2 \u8230\'20\'26 which translates to:\par \par \uc2 I announce to you a great joy:\u8232\'20\'28We have a Pope! \u8232\'20\'28\par \par \uc2 The Most Eminent and Most Reverend Father,\u8232\'20\'28Lord [baptismal name],\u8232\'20\'28Cardinal of the Holy Roman Church [surname],\u8232\'20\'28who takes to himself the name [papal name].\par \par \uc2 But who is it?\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-08T16:12:38.828Z">5.12pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 What happens now?\par \par \uc2 Once the pope is elected, the dean of the College of Cardinals asks him: \u8220\'20\'1CDo you accept your canonical election as supreme pontiff?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 If he agrees, he must decide his papal name. The cardinals will pledge obedience to the new pope.\par \par \uc2 Then he will be taken into the adjacent Room of Tears , where he will change from his scarlet cardinal\u8217\'20\'19s outfit into a white papal cassock. Usually small, medium and large cassocks are made in advance.\par \par \uc2 This time it is thought the Vatican is recycling cassocks made for previous conclaves.\par \par \uc2 The new pope is then led to the main balcony of St Peter\u8217\'20\'19s Basilica to greet the crowds, where the famous words \u8220\'20\'1CHabemus Papam\u8221\'20\'1D will be said. <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/may/06/how-conclave-work-when-new-pope-chosen"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 How does the conclave work and when will a new pope be chosen?}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-08T16:12:35.299Z">5.12pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 And the bells are ringing now, too.\par \par \uc2 No ambiguity there: we have got a new pope!\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-08T16:09:04.706Z">5.09pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 White smoke!\par \par \uc2 It looks like we\u8217\'20\'19ve got a new pope, everyone!\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-08T16:13:09.188Z">at 5.13pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-08T16:07:54.869Z">5.07pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 As we wait, the entire gulls family is back on the roof!\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-08T15:46:45.908Z">4.46pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 The challenge with this afternoon session is the uncertainty \u8211\'20\'13 we understand that won\u8217\'20\'19t get any signal after the fourth round of voting unless a new pope is elected.\par \par \uc2 Or, to put it simply, we will either see white smoke or nothing.\par \par \uc2 And if it\u8217\'20\'19s nothing, the wait will stretch into the evening, with the fifth round expected to conclude around 7 p.m. local time.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-08T15:49:56.393Z">at 4.49pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-08T15:41:52.266Z">4.41pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 A quick reminder: our live stream at the top of this blog is still active, showing the chimney atop the Sistine Chapel.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-08T15:24:52.474Z">4.24pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 What's the story with Vatican (sea)gulls?\par \par \uc2 Right, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2025/may/07/new-pope-conclave-catholic-cardinals-papacy-vote-white-black-smoke-latest-live-news?page=with%3Ablock-681baa9a8f0835e2df498ced#block-681baa9a8f0835e2df498ced"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 I promised you yesterday}}}\uc2  that we would get back to the question of the Vatican (sea)gulls and how did they end up there , quite a way in-land.\par \par \uc2 Going by what you told me in your emails (thank you!), the explanation is fairly simple.\par \par \uc2 Alick very helpfully told me that:\par \par \uc2 The question is simply resolved if you use the correct term. These birds are \u8216\'20\'18gulls\u8217\'20\'19 not \u8216\'20\'18seagulls\u8217\'20\'19.\par \par \uc2 Gulls are not exclusively sea dwelling birds. Most species are coastal and at various times of the year various species, all across the world, venture inland to feed and breed. Several of the largest gull breeding colonies in the UK are on upland moors. I\u8217\'20\'19ve seen Pallas\u8217\'20\'19s Gull in Kazakhstan \u8211\'20\'13 several hundred miles from the sea.\par \par \uc2 Chris offered a similar answer:\par \par \uc2 Gulls (for they are officially this, not seagulls) are found not just at sea. Many range inland for food, though often they will roost together in huge numbers on the sea at night.\par \par \uc2 If you live in a coastal area one can see very early in the morning and again in the evening, the gulls, in large flocks, commuting back and forth between their inland feeding areas (cities, refuse dumps, ploughed fields etc) and their marine roosts, which vary according to wind and wave direction.\par \par \uc2 \u8230\'20\'26 and it turns out we have some good writing on this on the Guardian already \u8211\'20\'13 just not in the Roman context, but the answer is broadly the same. <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/article/2024/aug/14/birdwatch-herring-gulls-forced-to-move-to-urban-jungle"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Birdwatch: herring gulls forced to move to urban jungle}}}\uc2  </aside> <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2018/nov/16/gulls-gulls-gulls-how-the-seaside-birds-took-over-urban-britain"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Gulls! Gulls! Gulls! How the seaside birds took over urban Britain}}}\uc2  </aside> <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2024/apr/01/justice-for-gulls-they-steal-our-chips-but-also-deserve-our-love-empathy-and-respect"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Justice for gulls! They steal our chips \u8211\'20\'13 but also deserve our love, empathy and respect}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 Separately, there is a little plot twist as Guy spotted that the seagulls (or gulls, sorry!) on the roof could be\u8230\'20\'26 a little family!\par \par \uc2 My wife and I are sure that the two gulls seen near the famous chimney are a nesting pair.\par \par \uc2 We were quite mesmerised by them this afternoon (Wednesday) as we watched the live TV feed while waiting for the black smoke.\par \par \uc2 Some time around 6pm a small chick appeared, clearly silhouetted against the sky. One of the parents fed it and it disappeared again. We imagine the nest must be in some cavity under the roof tiles.\par \par \uc2 Did anybody else see that little chick?\par \par \uc2 Here is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/emzanotti/status/1920200199500165254"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the photo evidence.}}}\par \par \uc2 And that\u8217\'20\'19s the secret of the Roman gulls. Glad we cleared that up.\par \par \uc2 Give it another day and we will have to give them names.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-08T15:02:30.549Z">4.02pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Some people appear to be prepared for a long, long wait.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-08T14:35:59.363Z">3.35pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 We're back for afternoon votes\par \par \uc2 The cardinals were expected to be back in the Sistine Chapel at 4.30pm local time, and we understand that they have just gone in.\par \par \uc2 So the fourth vote should be now getting under way any moment now.\par \par \uc2 The next possible smoke would be probably around 5.30pm local time, but only if they elected a pope.\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s the round in which Benedict XVI was elected in 2005.\par \par \uc2 Otherwise, we will have to wait until the fifth round is done, around 7pm, when we will get a smoke signal, whatever the result.\par \par \uc2 But keep in mind that all these timings are purely for guidance: it may be earlier, may be later, and it\u8217\'20\'19s only up to the 133 cardinals to decide the timings.\par \par \uc2 I know, not very helpful. But I don\u8217\'20\'19t make the rules!\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-08T14:50:00.854Z">at 3.50pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-08T14:28:39.720Z">3.28pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 The factions lobbying to shape the conclave\par \par \uc2 There are thought to be a number of different factions seeking to shape the outcome of the conclave. Broadly speaking, they can be characterised as progressives, conservatives, unifiers and the Italian contingent .\par \par \uc2 Those involved in lobbying \u8211\'20\'13 including cardinal electors and cardinals ineligible to take part in the conclave as they are 80 or older \u8211\'20\'13 are hoping to sway newer, less experienced cardinals. About 80% of the 133 cardinal electors have not taken part in a conclave before ; 21 were appointed just four months before Francis\u8217\'20\'19s death. Some believe this means there is everything to play for.\par \par \uc2 The progressives include those who want to preserve Francis\u8217\'20\'19s legacy and push forward on his priorities. Issues such as inequality, marginalisation, the climate crisis and migration are important. They also want more lay people, including women, appointed to important {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/vatican"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Vatican}}}\uc2  positions; an orientation on the global south, where the Roman Catholic church is seeing its greatest growth; and an emphasis on a \u8220\'20\'1Cpoor church for the poor\u8221\'20\'1D rather than the pomp and rituals beloved of the traditionalists.\par \par \uc2 You can read the full piece here: <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/may/08/will-the-catholic-church-turn-right-or-left-the-factions-lobbying-to-shape-conclave"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Will the Catholic church turn right or left? The factions lobbying to shape conclave}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-08T13:53:55.980Z">2.53pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Activists belonging to a group who held a peaceful protest aimed at calling out the \u8220\'20\'1Cinjustice\u8221\'20\'1D against women in the Catholic church were detained by Vatican police, allegedly because they were deemed a \u8220\'20\'1Cthreat to security\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday afternoon, as the cardinals began voting for the next pope, women from the UK-based Catholic Women\u8217\'20\'19s Ordination (CWO) emitted pink smoke into the air on Rome\u8217\'20\'19s Gianicolo hill, which overlooks St Peter\u8217\'20\'19s Basilica.\par \par \uc2 Later, as they gathered in St Peter\u8217\'20\'19s square to wait for the outcome of the first conclave vote, they were surrounded by a group of police in plain clothes.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey swooped in and said, \u8216\'20\'18Okay, ladies, documents, please ,\u8221\'20\'1D said Miriam Duignan, who was dressed in pink. \u8220\'20\'1CI protested furiously.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The women, along with three nuns who just so happened to be talking to them, were taken to the Vatican\u8217\'20\'19s police station.\par \par \uc2 Duignan claimed that a police officer questioned her over the peaceful protest, for which the group had a permit. \u8220\'20\'1CBut he said \u8216\'20\'18you are still perceived as a security threat by the Vatican\u8217\'20\'19.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The activists, who for years have been battling for women to become priests, were let go but banned from entering Vatican city for the remainder of the conclave.\par \par \uc2 It is believed they were being watched after being arrested during a protest close to the Vatican in 2022.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-08T12:19:27.717Z">1.19pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Lunchbreak continues\par \par \uc2 As the lunchbreak continues, thousands of pilgrims in the Vatican are trying to kill some time with all sorts of games and activities \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 The cardinals are expected to be back in the Sistine Chapel around 4.30pm local time (3.30 BST).\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-08T11:13:35.554Z">12.13pm BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Global media interest in conclave\par \par \uc2 Vatican official has just told me there are 6,000 media representatives from 90 countries here to cover the conclave.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-08T10:21:52.299Z">11.21am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 No pope after three votes - lunchtime summary\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Black smoke billowed out of the Sistine Chapel chimney before lunch, indicating no decision on who should be the next pope after three rounds of votes.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 133 cardinal elects are now taking a lunch break after the two morning votes.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Two more rounds are scheduled for this afternoon/evening , starting from 4.30pm local time (3.30pm BST).\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Three out of last five popes were elected on the second day of conclave, but this year\u8217\'20\'19s vote has a record-high number of electors, making the process more complex than usual.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-08T10:17:07.044Z">11.17am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Wait continues in Vatican - in pictures\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-08T10:05:04.898Z">11.05am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 How many votes are usually needed to elect pope?\par \par \uc2 Historically, some of the conclaves were really drawn out: in 13th century, they needed three years, over 1,000 days, to choose Gregory X.\par \par \uc2 There was also one that ended on the first day, when Julius II in 1503 was elected after just 10 hours.\par \par \uc2 But looking at the last 150 years, these days it is usually a much shorter process : the longest election, of Pius XI in 1922, took 5 days.\par \par \uc2 Francis was elected on the second day in 2013, after five rounds of voting.\par \par \uc2 Benedict XVI needed just four rounds to be confirmed as the new pope in 2005, as did John Paul I in 1978.\par \par \uc2 A bit more time was needed to confirm \uc2 John Paul II\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 three days, eight rounds \u8211\'20\'13 in 1978, and John XXIII in 1958, with 11 votes over four days. But then his immediate predecessor, Pius XII was elected after just three rounds.\par \par \uc2 So, the recent history seems to suggest they usually need 2 or 3 days, and we could be close to that moment.\par \par \uc2 Or not: since the process is so secretive and there are so many moving elements with a record-high number of cardinals involved in the process this year, there\u8217\'20\'19s no way to predict what happens behind the closed doors.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-08T10:03:39.595Z">11.03am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Two more votes today\par \par \uc2 There will be two further votes this afternoon and into the evening.\par \par \uc2 But first, it\u8217\'20\'19s time for lunch!\par \par \uc2 The cardinals are expected to be back in the Sistine Chapel around 4.30pm local time (3.30pm London).\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-08T09:54:38.129Z">10.54am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Black smoke again after morning votes - snap analysis\par \par \uc2 As per earlier briefings, we were meant to see black smoke only if they failed to choose the pope before the lunch break, so at the conclusion of the two morning rounds.\par \par \uc2 That takes us to three votes so far, with no conclusion.\par \par \uc2 Interestingly, we got black smoke much earlier than we expected the morning rounds to conclude, which suggests the 133 cardinals have got the hang of it now and vote much more efficiently than last night.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-08T09:59:19.903Z">at 10.59am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-08T09:52:07.940Z">10.52am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Black smoke from Sistine Chapel chimney\par \par \uc2 No decision on the pope again.\par \par \uc2 Updated <time datetime="2025-05-08T09:55:03.715Z">at 10.55am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-08T08:53:42.585Z">9.53am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 The chimney cam is back (and so are the seagulls; I will come back to this later).\par \par \uc2 Our live stream at the top is showing the chimney, too \u8211\'20\'13 although, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2025/may/08/new-pope-conclave-vatican-white-black-smoke-papacy-catholic-cardinals?page=with%3Ablock-681c5b778f0835e2df499186#block-681c5b778f0835e2df499186"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 as explained earlier}}}\uc2 , there is no guarantee we are going to get any smoke after the first round of voting.\par \par \uc2 Let\u8217\'20\'19s wait and see.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-08T08:29:03.553Z">9.29am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Who are the favourites?\par \par \uc2 In yesterday\u8217\'20\'19s blog, we covered the profiles of most of the favourites, including the Italians \u8211\'20\'13 Vatican\u8217\'20\'19s secretary of state \uc2 Pietro Parolin\uc2  and Bologna archbishop Matteo Zuppi \u8211\'20\'13 but also Filipino prelate Luis Antonio Tagle , Peter Turkson of Ghana, P\u233\'00\'E9ter Erd\u337\'01\'51 of Hungary\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 But then remember the old saying: \u8220\'20\'1Che who enters the conclave as pope, leaves it as a cardinal,\u8221\'20\'1D as few frontrunners at the start of the process make it through the successive rounds of voting.\par \par \uc2 You can catch up on their profiles here: <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/may/07/who-next-pope-potential-candidates-conclave"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Who will be the next pope? Leading candidates for the conclave to consider}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 But the Italian media are digging ever deeper to get some new anecdotes and stories about the candidates.\par \par \uc2 Corriere della Sera reported today on rumours about the rising odds of the Latin patriarch of Jerusalem Pierbattista Pizzaballa, adding that \u8220\'20\'1Cuntil a month ago, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pierluigi_Pizzaballa"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 his cousin, a former footballer from the 70s and an unobtainable Panini [collection] sticker}}}\uc2 , was better known.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-08T08:02:45.131Z">9.02am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 If you want to see the latest scenes from the Vatican, there is now a live stream showing St Peter\u8217\'20\'19s Square and the chimney atop the Sistine Chapel pinned at the top of this page.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-08T07:45:26.741Z">8.45am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 What to expect today?\par \par \uc2 What makes today slightly more tricky to follow is that while we have four rounds of voting, we may not get smoke after every one of them.\par \par \uc2 As I said earlier, there will be up four rounds of voting today , expected roughly around 9.30am and midday local time, and then after a long lunch break, again at 5.30pm and 7pm local time.\par \par \uc2 But according to the Italian media, what we see will depend on the results of the votes inside the Sistine Chapel.\par \par \uc2 If the cardinals do elect a new pope, we should know straight away, with white smoke.\par \par \uc2 But if they don\u8217\'20\'19t, we will only see black smoke at the end of each voting session \u8211\'20\'13 morning or afternoon \u8211\'20\'13 and not after every vote.\par \par \uc2 This means we will have to spend even more time looking closely at the chimney to get an idea of what is happening inside.\par \par \uc2 <time datetime="2025-05-08T07:30:08.347Z">8.30am BST</time>\par \par \uc2 Morning opening: Is today the day?\par \par \uc2 After a good night sleep in the Santa Marta guesthouse in the Vatican and a morning mass, 133 cardinals electors will soon be back in the Sistine Chapel for another rounds of voting on who should be the next pope.\par \par \uc2 The electors met earlier to celebrate mass and pray in the Pauline Chapel, and are due to move to the Sistine Chapel for prayers and votes.\par \par \uc2 There will be up four rounds of voting today , expected roughly around 9.30am and midday local time, and then after a long lunch break, again at 5.30pm and 7pm local time.\par \par \uc2 If you look at recent history, three of the last five popes were elected on the second day , so it\u8217\'20\'19s fair to say we could see white smoke today . The majority required is 89 votes.\par \par \uc2 But then again this conclave is like no other , with the largest and most diverse electorate of 133 cardinals from 70 countries, many of whom never met before the events of the last few weeks.\par \par \uc2 We will bring you all the latest.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s Thursday, 8 May 2025 , it\u8217\'20\'19s Jakub Krupa here, and this is Europe Live.\par \par \uc2 Good morning. \par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250508el580012z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
