\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 The Trump administration is defending  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  pill access in court. What?\b0\par\par\uc2 Carter Sherman \par \uc2 925 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 May 2025\par 15:40 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 It may seem a victory to some, but experts worry a win will allow the government to be coy about future attacks\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/trump-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump administration}}}\uc2  on Monday asked a federal court to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/05/trump-biden-defense-mifepristone-abortion-drug"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dismiss a lawsuit}}}\uc2  that takes aim at the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill mifepristone \u8211\'20\'13 a move that stunned many observers for what seemed a defense of the drug by a president who has overseen the most dramatic rollback of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in modern US history.\par \par \uc2 At first blush, it may seem a victory for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access \u8211\'20\'13 but experts worry that, in reality, the move preserves the administration\u8217\'20\'19s ability to play coy about any future plans to attack {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 When {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  first returned to the White House earlier this year, US anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists had high hopes for the man who helped orchestrate the downfall of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade}}}\uc2 . They thought he might use a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/17/anti-abortion-groups-trump-2025"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 19th-century anti-vice law}}}\uc2  to in effect ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide. Failing that, they imagined that he might use the power of the Food and Drug Administration to roll back access to mifepristone or even yank it from the market entirely.\par \par \uc2 Instead, over the last few months, the Trump administration has attempted to dodge the issue entirely. The Monday request, to a Texas judge who has become a reliable vote for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents, continued that pattern.\par \par \uc2 The lawsuit seeks to roll back several \uc2 FDA\uc2  regulatory changes that have, over the last decade, considerably expanded access to mifepristone, one of two drugs typically used in US medication abortions. It revives a lawsuit that led to a stinging {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/jun/13/supreme-court-abortion-pill-mifepristone"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 9-0 defeat}}}\uc2  for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights opponents when the court ruled the lawsuit\u8217\'20\'19s plaintiffs, a group of anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  doctors, did not have the legal standing to sue in the first place.\par \par \uc2 Rather than let the matter die, the Republican attorneys general of Idaho, Kansas and Missouri moved to take over the case as its new plaintiffs. Judge Matthew Kacsmaryk of the US district court for the northern district of Texas, where the case is being heard, agreed to let the attorneys general move forward.\par \par \uc2 However, in its Monday filing, the Trump administration argued that there was no reason why the case should proceed in Texas.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAt bottom, the states cannot keep alive a lawsuit in which the original plaintiffs were held to lack standing, those plaintiffs have now voluntarily dismissed their claims, and the states\u8217\'20\'19 own claims have no connection to this district,\u8221\'20\'1D the administration wrote.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights supporters have long pointed to one reason why the case was filed in Texas: Kacsmaryk. A Trump appointee with a track record of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opposition, Kacsmaryk once took the unprecedented step of ruling to reverse the \uc2 FDA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s 2000 approval of mifepristone, which would lead to its removal from the market.\par \par \uc2 Nicole Huberfeld, a health law professor at Boston University\u8217\'20\'19s School of Public Health, found it \u8220\'20\'1Ca little funny\u8221\'20\'1D that the Trump administration\u8217\'20\'19s filing seemed to call out its own side for judge-shopping.\par \par \uc2 It is possible that Trump, who was never exactly a true believer in the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement, has now soured on it. While the movement helped propel him to the White House in 2016, it became something of an albatross for him in 2024, as outrage over Roe\u8217\'20\'19s collapse led \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights to become one of the election\u8217\'20\'19s top issues.\par \par \uc2 Yet Huberfeld found the filing more notable for what it did not say: namely, it shied away from revealing the Trump administration\u8217\'20\'19s plans for mifepristone. She believes the administration may try to change mifepristone access through the \uc2 FDA\uc2 , and that the legal reasoning in Monday\u8217\'20\'19s filing could be used against a future lawsuit by blue states against new restrictions.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re basically saying that the states don\u8217\'20\'19t get to just challenge \uc2 FDA\uc2  policy because they want to,\u8221\'20\'1D Huberfeld said. \u8220\'20\'1CWhich, in my view, is a set-up for anticipating that blue states may try to challenge any changes on mifepristone rules.\u8221\'20\'1D <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/apr/26/abortion-clinic-pills-shield-laws"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Volunteers rush to send \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  pills to US women in need as \u8216\'20\'18war between the states\u8217\'20\'19 looms}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 FDA\uc2  commissioner, Martin Makary, could, for example, move to reverse regulations that permit people to dispense \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills through telehealth \u8211\'20\'13 which accounts for about a fifth of all US abortions \u8211\'20\'13 or eliminate mifepristone\u8217\'20\'19s approval. Project 2025, the notorious playbook of policy proposals authored by the conservative thinktank \uc2 the Heritage Foundation\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/05/project-2025-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 urged the FDA}}}\uc2  to do exactly that.\par \par \uc2 Last month, Makary {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.semafor.com/article/04/24/2025/fdas-marty-makary-no-plans-to-pull-abortion-pill-mifepristone"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told the Semafor World Economy Summit}}}\uc2  that he had \u8220\'20\'1Cno plans to take action\u8221\'20\'1D on mifepristone. However, he added: \u8220\'20\'1CThere is an ongoing set of data that is coming into the \uc2 FDA\uc2  on mifepristone. So if the data suggests something or tells us that there\u8217\'20\'19s a real signal, we can\u8217\'20\'19t promise we\u8217\'20\'19re not going to act on that data.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Decades of studies, conducted in more than a dozen countries, have found that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2023/04/01/health/abortion-pill-safety.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 mifepristone is safe and effective}}}\uc2 . However, anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups have repeatedly pushed studies that claimed to find that mifepristone is dangerous. (Some of those {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/apr/28/junk-science-papers-abortion-cases"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 studies have been retracted}}}\uc2 .)\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy guess is that the Trump administration is trying to walk the fine line of not looking like it\u8217\'20\'19s threatening access to mifepristone while also, potentially, through the \uc2 FDA\uc2  trying to limit access to mifepristone,\u8221\'20\'1D Huberfeld said. \u8220\'20\'1CIn other words, I don\u8217\'20\'19t think the \uc2 FDA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s actually going to be hands-off.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250506el5600336\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
