\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Standing up for Christian values\u8217\'20\'19: US evangelicals keep the faith with Trump\b0\par\par\uc2 Eric Berger \par \uc2 1,238 \uc2 words\par \uc2 28 April 2025\par 11:01 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Evangelicals say president is in step on core issues such as \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Israel \u8211\'20\'13 and they\u8217\'20\'19re backing him all the way\par \par \uc2 When asked about {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump }}}\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Easter morning post wishing a happy holiday to \u8220\'20\'1Cthe {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://truthsocial.com/@realDonaldTrump/posts/114370361342759621"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Radical Left }}}\uc2  Lunatics \u8230\'20\'26 fighting and scheming so hard to bring Murderers, Drug Lords, Dangerous Prisoners\u8221\'20\'1D to the United States, Jackson Lahmeyer, an Oklahoma evangelical Christian pastor, said: \u8220\'20\'1CIsn\u8217\'20\'19t it terrible that they are wanting to do that?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Lahmeyer, the founder of the Pastors for Trump organization, was not bothered by Trump\u8217\'20\'19s extreme and divisive message on the Christian religious holiday, because, he said: \u8220\'20\'1CYou cannot unify with evil.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Lahmeyer\u8217\'20\'19s attitude appears typical of many white evangelical leaders who still strongly support Trump despite what \u8211\'20\'13 for many \u8211\'20\'13 is violent, extremist-laden language that many would see as unsuitable for any religious occasion, let alone one intimately connected to rebirth, forgiveness and peace. <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/apr/16/christian-nationalists-trump-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump has put Christian nationalists in key roles \u8211\'20\'13 say a prayer for free speech }}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 But those leaders in the US say Trump \u8211\'20\'13 unlike some past Republican presidents \u8211\'20\'13 has followed through on campaign promises concerning core issues such as \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , immigration, the location of the US embassy in Israel and, more generally, his pledge to \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2024/06/13/trump-christian-right-abortion-prayer/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bring back Christianity }}}\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 More good things could be in store for that demographic because in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://truthsocial.com/@realDonaldTrump/posts/114370637123886922"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 second Easter post }}}\uc2  on his platform Truth Social, Trump said he would make America \u8220\'20\'1Cmore religious, than it has ever been before!!!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe has moved the needle for the Christian agenda unlike anyone else, especially in modern times,\u8221\'20\'1D said Lahmeyer, who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zglfjLEDjGA"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 attended an Easter dinner }}}\uc2  at the White House. \u8220\'20\'1CAs a pastor, obviously, that is music to my ears.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 White evangelical voters also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/politics/2004/12/06/religion-and-the-presidential-vote/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 turned out in large numbers }}}\uc2  for \uc2 George W Bush\uc2  when he ran for president in 2000 and 2004, but they were disappointed because they felt he did not do enough to oppose {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtontimes.com/news/2004/feb/19/20040219-115609-3712r/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 same-sex marriage }}}\uc2  or to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nationalreview.com/2004/09/evangelicals-bush-steven-waldman/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ban \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 . Bush also, when compared to Trump, had a more liberal immigration policy, including supporting {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pbs.org/newshour/show/conservatives-liberals-take-aim-at-presidents-immigration-plan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 providing undocumented immigrants }}}\uc2  the chance to become citizens, according to John Fea, a history professor at Messiah College in Mechanicsburg, Pennsylvania, and the author of Believe Me: The Evangelical Road to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBush wasn\u8217\'20\'19t willing to give them everything that they wanted to be elected,\u8221\'20\'1D Fea said. \u8220\'20\'1CTrump will do what evangelicals tell him to do for the most part, in order to maintain power.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In addition to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-overturned-abortion-summary-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appointing supreme court justices }}}\uc2  who ruled that there is no constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Trump also moved the embassy from Tel Aviv to Jerusalem, which previous {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2016/dec/21/us-israel-embassy-jerusalem-peace-process"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 presidents }}}\uc2  had said they supported but did not implement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey all said it to get votes. They never did it. The president did it,\u8221\'20\'1D said Lahmeyer, who ran for Senate and lost in 2022.\par \par \uc2 During this term, Trump has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/feb/07/trumps-executive-order-anti-christian-bias"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 signed executive orders }}}\uc2  to establish a faith office and a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/presidential-actions/2025/02/eradicating-anti-christian-bias/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 taskforce }}}\uc2  to address \u8220\'20\'1Canti-Christian bias\u8221\'20\'1D in the federal government.\par \par \uc2 To evangelical leaders, that emphasis on Christian values stands in contrast to how they perceive the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s actions, including in 2024 declaring 31 March Transgender Day of Visibility, the date when it had been celebrated since its creation in 2009, but last year fell \u8211\'20\'13 entirely coincidentally \u8211\'20\'13 on Easter Sunday.\par \par \uc2 But in a world where conspiracy theories and misinformation is rife, that sparked anger among rightwing Christians.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEaster was barely mentioned,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Brad Sherman\uc2  , an Iowa pastor and Republican now running for governor. \u8220\'20\'1CIn fact, I think it was more about some kind of LGBTQ awareness day or something, if I remember correctly, so I just feel like President Trump is standing up for Christian values.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In actual fact, Biden continued the tradition of the annual White House Easter egg roll and in a statement said: \u8220\'20\'1CAs we gather with loved ones, we remember Jesus\u8217\'20\'19s sacrifice \u8230\'20\'26 with wars and conflict taking a toll on innocent lives around the world, we renew our commitment to work for peace, security, and dignity for all people.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 This year, Trump held an Easter prayer service and dinner with Lahmeyer; prominent pastors such as \uc2 Franklin Graham\uc2  and \uc2 Robert Jeffress\uc2  ; and his personal pastor, Paula White-Cain, who now leads the White House faith office, among others.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C[Trump] preached the gospel to us pastors, and I thought that was amazing,\u8221\'20\'1D Lahmeyer said.\par \par \uc2 While most white evangelicals support Trump, there are Christian leaders, including evangelicals, who have criticized some of the president\u8217\'20\'19s policy decisions, especially to eliminate 83% of \uc2 US Agency for International Development\uc2  (USAID) programs. Among the initiatives affected was the President\u8217\'20\'19s Emergency Plan for Aids Relief (Pepfar), which has saved millions of lives from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/aids-and-hiv"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HIV/Aids }}}\uc2  and was popular with evangelicals.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe see it as really overarchingly a pro-life program in that it promotes the life-saving need for HIV treatment,\u8221\'20\'1D Emily Chambers Sharpe, the health director at World Relief, the humanitarian arm of the National Association of Evangelicals, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/mar/17/hiv-aids-pepfar-christians-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told the Guardian }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But the person behind many of the federal government cuts, \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  , head of the so-called \u8220\'20\'1Cdepartment of government efficiency\u8221\'20\'1D, called \uc2 USAID\uc2  a \u8220\'20\'1Ccriminal organization\u8221\'20\'1D and said that it was \u8220\'20\'1Ctime for it to die\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Adam Russell Taylor, the president of Sojourners, a Christian social justice group, said such remarks remind him of \u8220\'20\'1Cthe prophet Isaiah, who forewarned us that woe to you that call evil, good, and good, evil\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The administration is \u8220\'20\'1Cmaking these allegations that aren\u8217\'20\'19t backed up by evidence or proof. And they disparage this whole body of work that has created such goodwill around the world and is so aligned with our Christian values,\u8221\'20\'1D Russell Taylor said.\par \par \uc2 But many American evangelicals continue to support Trump despite such cuts, because concern for the poor \u8220\'20\'1Calways takes a back seat in evangelical politics to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  [and] control of the supreme court, which will allow them to have the religious freedom that they want\u8221\'20\'1D, said Fea, the history professor.\par \par \uc2 Tony Su\u225\'00\'E1rez, the founder of Revivalmakers Ministries, an evangelical group, said he supports Trump because he is trying to strengthen border security and is restoring \u8220\'20\'1Crespect for conservative, Judeo-Christian values\u8221\'20\'1D. <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/feb/07/trumps-executive-order-anti-christian-bias"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s taskforce order is latest in efforts to boost Christian nationalism }}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 Once the country secures the border and removes \u8220\'20\'1Cthe criminal element\u8221\'20\'1D, Su\u225\'00\'E1rez, who is also executive vice-president of the National Hispanic Christian Leadership Conference, said he would like to see a pathway to at least legal permanent residency for undocumented immigrants. He thinks that based on some of his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2018/01/09/us/politics/trump-daca-immigration.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 comments }}}\uc2  during his first term, Trump would support that too.\par \par \uc2 But Trump also wants to end birthright citizenship for the children of undocumented immigrants and foreign residents, a guarantee under the 14th amendment.\par \par \uc2 Asked for his position on this, Su\u225\'00\'E1rez said that is \u8220\'20\'1Ca little bit above me to understand what it is specifically that they are arguing\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 And on cuts to foreign aid programs, Su\u225\'00\'E1rez said he views them \u8220\'20\'1Cas difficult decisions that any organization, denomination, reformation, might have to take, and they will never be popular\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Su\u225\'00\'E1rez joked that the only thing he disagrees with Trump on is him saying that \u8220\'20\'1Cyou may even get tired of winning\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m not tired,\u8221\'20\'1D Su\u225\'00\'E1rez said. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m looking for the next win.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250428el4s001gv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
