\par\par \uc2 Television & radio\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18We\u8217\'20\'19re on a knife edge\u8217\'20\'19: Alex Gibney warns about the dangers of dark money\b0\par\par\uc2 David Smith in Washington \par \uc2 2,016 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 April 2025\par 16:59 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 In two \uc2 HBO\uc2  documentaries, the acclaimed film-maker shines a light on corrupt political spending in America\par \par \uc2 When the Rev Robert Schenck saw \uc2 Donald Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2016/jul/22/donald-trump-speech-republican-national-convention"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 secure the Republican presidential nomination}}}\uc2  in Cleveland, Ohio, in 2016, he turned to a fellow evangelical and asked: \u8220\'20\'1CAre we really going to do this? We\u8217\'20\'19re going to choose this man who\u8217\'20\'19s inimical to everything we believe?\u8221\'20\'1D The Christian leader looked at Schenck and replied: \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t care how bad he is. He\u8217\'20\'19s going to get us the court we need.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 This anecdote about the devil\u8217\'20\'19s bargain struck between Trump and the religious right is told in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.hbo.com/the-dark-money-game"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Dark Money Game}}}\uc2 , director Alex Gibney\u8217\'20\'19s new diptych of documentaries investigating how untraceable political spending has corrupted America\u8217\'20\'19s highest court, corroded its democracy and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/15/joe-biden-oval-office-trump-oligarchs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 put oligarchs in charge}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Inspired by Jane Mayer\u8217\'20\'19s book {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.penguinrandomhouse.com/books/215462/dark-money-by-jane-mayer/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dark Money}}}\uc2  : The Hidden History of the Billionaires Behind the Rise of the Radical Right, the two films examine how a supreme court decision in 2010 known as \uc2 Citizens United\uc2  enabled corporations and unions to inject unlimited funds into elections, fostering a \u8220\'20\'1Cpay-to-play\u8221\'20\'1D system.\par \par \uc2 One film, Ohio Confidential, examines {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/01/25/magazine/ohio-bribery-politics.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a vast bribery scandal}}}\uc2  in Ohio involving the lobbyist Neil Clark and the alleged manipulation of political outcomes through secret funds. Another, Wealth of the Wicked, analyses the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s role in opening the floodgates to corporate influence in politics and the subsequent weakening of democratic institutions.\par \par \uc2 Together they tell a devastating tale of how financial manipulation and legally ambiguous bribery have eroded the foundations of US democracy, empowering Trump and a class of oligarchs in ways that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2025/mar/22/trump-administration-authoritarianism"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 echo dictatorships around the world}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Speaking via \uc2 Zoom\uc2  from his home in New Harbor, Maine, Gibney warns: \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re on a knife edge now, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/audio/2025/apr/14/david-smith-is-the-us-descending-into-authoritarianism-full-story-podcast"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 teetering toward authoritarian rule}}}\uc2 . What it really is is crony capitalism and that\u8217\'20\'19s what unites this administration with [Russia\u8217\'20\'19s Vladimir] Putin, [Hungary\u8217\'20\'19s Viktor] Orb\u225\'00\'E1n, [India\u8217\'20\'19s Narendra] Modi and others.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a sense that government is nothing more than a bunch of traded favours among rich people and that\u8217\'20\'19s the terrifying part because, when you\u8217\'20\'19re only loyal to the capo di tutti capi as opposed to the constitution, suddenly the Department of Justice just becomes the Department of Vigilante Justice.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe \uc2 FBI\uc2  becomes an instrument of revenge, not law and order, and you can see that the regulatory state is being dismantled brick by brick. They\u8217\'20\'19re trying to destroy government, which is what the Powell memo effectively was trying to say way back in the day .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.senate.gov/news/speeches/the-scheme-1-the-powell-memo/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Powell memo}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D was the work of Lewis Powell, a corporate lawyer from Virginia in the 1950s and 1960s commissioned by the \uc2 US Chamber of Commerce\uc2  to devise a strategic plan for reasserting corporate power and a conservative agenda over a political domain perceived as too liberal. One section of his secret blueprint described \u8220\'20\'1Cexploiting judicial action\u8221\'20\'1D as an \u8220\'20\'1Carea of vast opportunity\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 This vision was realised with the help of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://fedsoc.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Federalist Society}}}\uc2 , which cultivated and promoted conservative legal thinkers who adhere to principles such as originalism and textualism. Led by \uc2 Leonard Leo\uc2 , the group became a \u8220\'20\'1Cpipeline\u8221\'20\'1D for placing conservative judges on the bench at all levels, including the supreme court.\par \par \uc2 Its influence was felt in 2010 with the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s 5-4 ruling in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.brennancenter.org/our-work/research-reports/citizens-united-explained"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Citizens United}}}\uc2  v Federal Elec\u173\'00\'ADtion Commis\u173\'00\'ADsion, which decided that corporations and unions have the same first amendment rights as individuals when it comes to political speech.\par \par \uc2 The ruling means that wealthy donors, corpor\u173\'00\'ADa\u173\'00\'ADtions and special interest groups can spend unlim\u173\'00\'ADited cash on any candidate or cause as long as they do not give money directly to the candidate but rather set up so-called independent entities known as super political action committees, or Super Pacs. As The Dark Money Game puts it: \u8220\'20\'1CFifteen years later, fringe groups could bundle billions in secret slush funds to frustrate popular rule.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Gibney elaborates: \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s the most bullshit kind of rationale. Anybody with common sense would know that this is a vehicle for corruption because it basically means that you\u8217\'20\'19re giving permission for people to have those kind of wink-and-nod conversations where you know how to convey the meaning, which is: \u8216\'20\'18If you give me this money, I\u8217\'20\'19ll do this for you,\u8217\'20\'19 but you don\u8217\'20\'19t have it directly, just have it in a roundabout way.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s like Japanese {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.japan-guide.com/e/e2092.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bunraku theatre}}}\uc2 , which has nearly life-size puppets, and behind the puppets are these men in black who move the puppets. You actually see them but they sort of disappear into the background.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Gibney, whose past films include {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.hbo.com/wise-guy-david-chase-and-the-sopranos"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Wise Guy: David Chase and the Sopranos}}}\uc2 , The Crime of the Century and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/tv-and-radio/2021/dec/07/the-forever-prisoner-hbo-alex-gibney-guantanamo-bay"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Forever Prisoner}}}\uc2 , also highlights the alliance that formed between big business interests seeking deregulation and social and religious conservatives, particularly on issues such \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 He explains: \u8220\'20\'1CBig business was like, how do we play the long game so that we can get what we want, which is unfettered, unregulated capitalism? Along the way they realised it\u8217\'20\'19s not very popular to say, \u8216\'20\'18We want the right to pollute in your community because it\u8217\'20\'19ll make us more money.\u8217\'20\'19 That\u8217\'20\'19s not a good political campaign slogan.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey needed a very powerful emotional issue and that was \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and so they join forces, in a way, with anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists and over time engineer a takeover of the supreme court by utilising both money and that religious fervour. \u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Gibney\u8217\'20\'19s star witness is Schenck, an evangelical minister and former anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  lobbyist who used to denounce \u8220\'20\'1Cbaby killers\u8221\'20\'1D, bring dead foetuses to demonstrations and put his body down in front of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics. He later had a crisis of conscience, changed his mind and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2019/05/30/opinion/abortion-schenck.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 came to support}}}\uc2  Roe v Wade, the 1973 supreme court ruling that enshrined \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Gibney says: \u8220\'20\'1CHe talks about how there was this unholy alliance between big business and religious conservatives such as he and they cut a deal, which is you guys need money in order to carry on your crusade and we need your help so that we can make more money and pass some of it on to you by dismantling economic regulations.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In the film, Schenck explains: \u8220\'20\'1CWhenever you talked about government regulation the argument was eventually these same characters who control my business are going to start trying to control your church. So it\u8217\'20\'19s in your best interests that we defang this monster, and that brought a lot of religious conservatives over.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have a little aphorism built on a Bible verse: \u8216\'20\'18The wealth of the wicked is laid up for the righteous.\u8217\'20\'19 So, yeah, let\u8217\'20\'19s baptise the billionaires\u8217\'20\'19 money. We can do that and it eventually brought together this alliance.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Schenck describes a carefully orchestrated \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/07/08/religious-right-supreme-court-00044739"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Operation Higher Court}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D to influence supreme court justices. This involved building relationships through social events, the use of \u8220\'20\'1Cstealth missionaries\u8221\'20\'1D (wealthy donors), and catering to their personal and ideological leanings. Religious connections, particularly conservative Catholicism and groups such as Opus Dei, appeared to play a role.\par \par \uc2 Schenck says the most successful couple he \u8220\'20\'1Cdeployed\u8221\'20\'1D were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cleveland.com/news/2022/12/ohio-couples-gifts-show-need-for-us-supreme-court-ethics-code-congressional-committee-told.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Don and Gayle Wright}}}\uc2  of Ohio, who built strong relationships with Justices \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2 , \uc2 Antonin Scalia\uc2  and \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t know all the details. To be candid, I didn\u8217\'20\'19t want to know what they were up to. Whatever it was, our donors were quite pleased. They saw the justices become bolder, more brazen, more confident and they rewarded us and the justices with whom they developed relationships for it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The biggest beneficiary has been Thomas, who received {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/06/clarence-thomas-supreme-courts-gifts-republican-megadonor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 donations, luxury gifts and holidays}}}\uc2  from the Republican mega-donor \uc2 Harlan Crow\uc2 . In 2019 Thomas and his wife flew on Crow\u8217\'20\'19s jet to Indonesia for nine days island-hopping on Crow\u8217\'20\'19s yacht, raising concerns about a potential quid pro quo.\par \par \uc2 Gibney says of the justices: \u8220\'20\'1COver time these are the friends they have. They begin to absorb the point of view of billionaires: we don\u8217\'20\'19t want rules or regulations when it comes to deploying our capital. We want to be able to do whatever it is that we want to do. Then you get to a point where, over time, the supreme court seems to be saying that there should be no rules or regulations when it comes to big money.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Wealth of the Wicked depicts {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2022/feb/22/the-scheme-senators-highlight-rightwing-influence-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the scheme}}}\uc2  to fill supreme court vacancies with conservative justices who would be willing to overturn Roe v Wade. Opponents of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights had paced their faith in past Republicans such as \uc2 Ronald Reagan\uc2  only to be constantly disappointed.\par \par \uc2 However, Leo provided a list of pre-vetted candidates to Trump, who made it public during his election campaign to successfully woo conservative Christian voters who might otherwise have recoiled from his sexual affairs, verbal insults and casual cruelty. The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/10/divided-america-roe-v-wade-supreme-court-cold-civil-war"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturning of Roe v Wade}}}\uc2  in 2022 was the ultimate victory for this decades-long effort. All the justices in the majority had been promoted by Leo and raised Catholic.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile Ohio Confidential paints a picture of deep-seated corruption within Ohio\u8217\'20\'19s state government, involving $1bn worth of bribes allegedly funneled through dark money groups that appears to have influenced legislation.\par \par \uc2 Gibney\u8217\'20\'19s film begins with Neil Clark, a powerful lobbyist known by various nicknames like \u8220\'20\'1CGodfather\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1CPrince of Darkness\u8221\'20\'1D. He was under \uc2 FBI\uc2  investigation and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/ohio-4a98679f0b1e10b47a22c21d4e6c1c49"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 found dead in Florida}}}\uc2  in 2021 with a gunshot wound to the head, ruled a suicide, and wearing a [Ohio governor] \uc2 Mike DeWine\uc2  campaign T-shirt.\par \par \uc2 Clark had been creating video diaries before his death, seemingly intending to reveal the secrets he had kept. He said: \u8220\'20\'1CNow I no longer feel the need to keep people\u8217\'20\'19s secrets. Relieved from this career-long burden, it\u8217\'20\'19s time for me to share. And share I will. A Sicilian never forgets.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 FBI\uc2  launched an investigation into Clark and others, using undercover agents posing as corrupt businessmen. Wiretaps and body wires captured conversations revealing potentially illegal activities and connections to powerful figures such as the Ohio house speaker, Larry Householder, now serving {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/bribery-investigation-ohio-speaker-householder-sentenced-7ff5163a7d1fdbbfe6570ed34c7a7f67"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 20 years in prison for racketeering}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The influx of dark money is shown to have enabled the Republican party\u8217\'20\'19s takeover of state legislatures, including Ohio\u8217\'20\'19s, in 2010. This led to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2022/jan/25/nashville-tennessee-gerrymandering-congress-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 aggressive gerrymandering}}}\uc2 , redrawing districts that made it almost impossible for Republicans to lose and incentivising politicians to cater to extremes rather than the broad public interest.\par \par \uc2 As goes Ohio, so goes the nation, Gibney argues. \u8220\'20\'1COhio is a story of where people actually got caught doing what they do every day in every state, so my presumption would be that this goes on in every state all the time. But because the Feds didn\u8217\'20\'19t happen to stumble into it, we don\u8217\'20\'19t hear about it. As the \uc2 FBI\uc2  admitted themselves, it was a case that they stumbled into by accident.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 With a convicted criminal now occupying the Oval Office, and embracing lawlessness daily, such forces can feel overwhelming. As the political consultant David Axelrod {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2025/04/12/opinion/trump-presidency-multitasking.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told the New York Times}}}\uc2  newspaper last week, \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re living in a bizarro world where heroes are being targeted and scoundrels are in a position to target them.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But a common thread running through both Gibney\u8217\'20\'19s films is bribery. He hopes that will be enough to offend a basic sense of morality. \u8220\'20\'1CIn a very essential way, most of us think bribery is a deeply immoral act where one person, by crossing somebody\u8217\'20\'19s palms with silver, can get an advantage that the rest of us don\u8217\'20\'19t have. We feel that\u8217\'20\'19s wrong and it is wrong and so now it\u8217\'20\'19s up to us to shout loudly enough so that the rule of law is restored.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Dark Money Game films air on \uc2 HBO\uc2  on 15 and 16 April in the US with a UK date to be announced\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250415el4f002e7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
