\par\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 These Tennessee lawmakers love the unborn. After birth? Not so much\b0\par\par\uc2 Arwa Mahdawi \par \uc2 1,403 \uc2 words\par \uc2 12 April 2025\par 13:31 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 A bill in the US state would allow public schools to deny undocumented children the chance to enroll\par \par \uc2 Think of the children? Nah\par \par \uc2 You\u8217\'20\'19ve probably seen {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.snopes.com/fact-check/pastor-dave-barnhart-unborn/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 this quote}}}\uc2  from an Alabama pastor called Dave Barnhart. It goes viral all the time. But I\u8217\'20\'19m resurfacing the quote because it is another day that ends with \u8220\'20\'1Cy\u8221\'20\'1D in America, which means it is relevant once again.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe unborn are a convenient group of people to advocate for,\u8221\'20\'1D Barnhart said back in 2018, remarking wryly on the movement\u8217\'20\'19s priorities. \u8220\'20\'1CThey never make demands of you \u8230\'20\'26 They don\u8217\'20\'19t need money, education or childcare \u8230\'20\'26 They allow you to feel good about yourself without any work at creating or maintaining relationships; and when they are born, you can forget about them, because they cease to be unborn.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Over in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/tennessee"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tennessee}}}\uc2 , there are a lot of lawmakers who are very proud of how much they advocate for unborn children. In 2022, as soon as Roe was overturned, the state passed one of the nation\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/feb/22/diary-doctor-navigating-total-abortion-ban-tennessee"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 strictest \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  bans}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 one without explicit exceptions to save the life of a pregnant person. The ban also made performing or attempting to perform an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://law.justia.com/codes/tennessee/2021/title-39/chapter-15/part-2/section-39-15-201/#:~:text=Criminal%20abortion%20is%20a%20Class,requirements%20of%20subsection%20(c)."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 class C felony}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 akin to aggravated assault \u8211\'20\'13 which means aiding in an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  can land you prison time and a hefty fine. That ban has been continuously {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2024/04/04/1242721479/how-narrow-can-a-medical-exception-be-in-a-state-s-abortion-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 challenged in court}}}\uc2  but the bottom line is that getting an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Tennessee is almost impossible.\par \par \uc2 Those Tennessee lawmakers who love unborn children? Surprise, surprise, they\u8217\'20\'19re not so keen on the born ones. Particularly if those kids are immigrants. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/tennessee-school-immigration-70841aef391b841321b6dc18d2eb5710"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 On Thursday}}}\uc2 , the GOP-dominated state senate approved a bill that lets public schools check the citizenship or legal immigration status of every student. Undocumented children can be denied enrollment at these public schools or forced to pay tuition. In other words: Tennessee wants to make it legal to deny undocumented kids an education. By requiring school systems to check legal immigrant status, they\u8217\'20\'19re also turning what should be safe spaces into immigration enforcement centers.\par \par \uc2 All of which, to be clear, is blatantly unconstitutional. In 1982, the supreme court decision in Plyler v Doe found states {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.americanimmigrationcouncil.org/sites/default/files/research/public_education_for_immigrant_students_understanding_plyer_v_doe.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cannot deny students}}}\uc2  a free public education over their immigration status. The Tennessee bill is not law yet, and if the Tennessee governor does sign it, it will almost certainly face legal challenges. But even if it eventually gets struck down, there is a chance it will stay on the books as a \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/opinions/2024/04/10/zombie-laws-abortion-arizona/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 zombie law\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 ready to rise again when circumstances allow.\par \par \uc2 Perhaps you are wondering why all these fierce advocates for the rights of unborn children are so keen on denying kids an education? According to lawmakers who voted for the measure, it\u8217\'20\'19s not because they\u8217\'20\'19re hateful racists who want to punish kids, it\u8217\'20\'19s because they are being fiscally responsible. Their argument is that the state simply doesn\u8217\'20\'19t have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.newschannel5.com/news/tennessee-senate-votes-yes-for-school-districts-to-ask-undocumented-kids-of-their-legal-status"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 enough money for education}}}\uc2  for undocumented kids, particularly since some will require English language learner classes.\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s a small possibility \u8211\'20\'13 just throwing it out there \u8211\'20\'13 that one of the reasons Tennessee is finding it hard to find money for education is because its regressive tax policies are heavily weighted towards extracting money from the poor rather than making the rich pay their fair share. Tennessee is one of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://theconversation.com/how-do-9-states-get-by-with-no-income-tax-a-tax-expert-explains-the-trade-offs-they-choose-230181"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 nine states}}}\uc2  in the US that doesn\u8217\'20\'19t have an income tax. It also doesn\u8217\'20\'19t have inheritance tax and has very low business tax. Residents (including undocumented immigrants) pay sales tax, property tax and a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thinktennessee.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/tax-fact-sheet_2024.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 grocery tax}}}\uc2 . Undocumented immigrants are putting money into the system and getting very little out of it. Pretending that this attack on undocumented children is about money is disingenuous. Deep down, I\u8217\'20\'19m sure even the people voting for the bill know that investing in children pays dividends to society.\par \par \uc2 Still, while it is disheartening that a bill like this got as far as it did, it\u8217\'20\'19s also important to note that it faced a lot of opposition. Nearly half of the senate\u8217\'20\'19s members spoke on the bill \u8211\'20\'13 many of them, including some Republicans, in passionate disagreement. There were tears and a lot of Bible verses quoted about {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wkrn.com/news/tennessee-politics/tennessee-senate-passes-controversial-bill-that-would-allow-school-districts-to-deny-undocumented-students/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 compassion for children}}}\uc2 . As the US becomes increasingly dystopian, it\u8217\'20\'19s important that we don\u8217\'20\'19t lose sight of just how much opposition there is to the extremist policies and legislation a hate-filled minority are pushing through. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  likes to say that winning the popular vote gave him and his cronies a mandate to do whatever they like; that all the policies getting passed have the support of the people. This simply isn\u8217\'20\'19t true. Only {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://deanobeidallah.substack.com/p/trump-did-not-get-a-mandate-he-got"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 around 32% of eligible voters}}}\uc2  actually voted for Trump.\par \par \uc2 While we must not minimize the amount of misogyny and racism there is in the US (and there is a lot!), we should also take heart from the fact that a sizable number of Americans do not want to live in an authoritarian dystopia where women have no rights and undocumented kids get no education. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/religion/fact-sheet/public-opinion-on-abortion/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sixty-three percent of Americans}}}\uc2  say \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be legal in all or most cases according to \uc2 Pew\uc2  research from 2024. Most Americans say {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/short-reads/2024/11/22/most-americans-say-undocumented-immigrants-should-be-able-to-stay-legally-under-certain-conditions/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 undocumented immigrants}}}\uc2  should have a way to stay in the country legally if certain requirements are met. Increasingly, the actions of the American government don\u8217\'20\'19t reflect the views of the American people.\par \par \uc2 Which, of course, is why the Trump administration is so obsessed with undermining education as a whole. From trying to stop undocumented immigrants from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/apr/11/los-angeles-schools-immigration-officials"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 going to school}}}\uc2 , to tightly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/apr/10/trump-columbia-consent-decree"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 controlling}}}\uc2  how Ivy League universities operate, to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/mar/21/trump-education-department-order-reactions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 attempting to eliminate}}}\uc2  the \uc2 US Department of Education\uc2 , Republicans are waging a war on critical thinking.\par \par \uc2 The US just made it harder for married women to vote\par \par \uc2 On Thursday the US House {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/apr/10/safeguard-american-voter-act-house-bill"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 approved}}}\uc2  the Safeguard American Voter Eligibility (Save) Act, which requires people to prove they are citizens when they vote. If you changed your birth name \u8211\'20\'13 as around {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/short-reads/2023/09/07/about-eight-in-ten-women-in-opposite-sex-marriages-say-they-took-their-husbands-last-name/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 80% of women}}}\uc2  in opposite-sex marriages in the US have \u8211\'20\'13 you will have to show a lot more paperwork to vote.\par \par \uc2 Mickey Rourke tells JoJo Siwa he will tie her up and make her straight\par \par \uc2 I had to look up who Rourke is because he hasn\u8217\'20\'19t been relevant for a while. Now, however, he is making headlines for being misogynistic and homophobic on Celebrity Big Brother UK. Rourke, 72, recently told JoJo Siwa (a gay singer and social media personality) that he\u8217\'20\'19d turn her straight. \u8220\'20\'1CIf I stay [in the Big Brother house] longer than four days, you won\u8217\'20\'19t be gay any more,\u8221\'20\'1D Rourke said to Siwa in a clip from Wednesday. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ll tie you up,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.teenvogue.com/story/mickey-rourkes-homophobic-comments-toward-jojo-siwa"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he added}}}\uc2 . Rourke got a warning from producers for his language but his comments were not censored. This is in stark contrast to a Big Brother \u8220\'20\'1Ccontroversy\u8221\'20\'1D last year, when \uc2 ITV\uc2 , the broadcaster, edited an episode of the show to remove shots of a T-shirt worn by one of the contestants {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://theintercept.com/2024/11/01/tv-big-brother-censor-watermelon-palestine/#:~:text=Following%20the%20initial%20broadcast%20of,regard%20it%20as%20a%20genocidal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 featuring a watermelon}}}\uc2 , which is a symbol of Palestinian solidarity.\par \par \uc2 White House says it will ignore reporters with gender pronouns in email signature\par \par \uc2 The amount of time these people spend {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2025/04/09/white-house-gender-pronouns-reporters"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 obsessing over pronouns}}}\uc2  boggles the mind. Get a hobby! Get therapy! Try thinking about literally anything else!\par \par \uc2 Student found guilty of rape goes unpunished because of promising future in gynecology\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.belganewsagency.eu/hundreds-gather-in-leuven-to-protest-against-controversial-rape-case-ruling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 criminal court}}}\uc2  in Leuven, Belgium, recently found a 24-year-old medical student, who was training as a gynaecologist, guilty of rape but {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thenewfeminist.co.uk/2025/04/rapists-sentence-gets-suspended-because-of-his-promising-future-as-a-gynaecologist/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 suspended}}}\uc2  his sentence because of his lack of prior offences and his \u8220\'20\'1Cpromising future\u8221\'20\'1D. This has sparked a lot of anger in Belgium and many commentators have drawn parallels to the Brock Turner case in the US.\par \par \uc2 Does sitting behind a screen turn you into a woman?\par \par \uc2 Fox News\u8217\'20\'19s Jesse Watters, who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.huffpost.com/entry/jesse-watters-sitting-behind-desk-makes-you-woman_n_67f50761e4b042c1f770c1a6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sits behind a screen}}}\uc2  all day, seems to think so. This profundity comes after he declared public soup consumption unmanly and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.the-independent.com/news/world/americas/us-politics/jesse-watters-fox-rules-men-b2718701.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said that real men}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cdon\u8217\'20\'19t wave simultaneously with two hands\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The week in pawtriarchy\par \par \uc2 Remember those {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/apr/03/donald-trump-tariffs-antarctica-uninhabited-heard-mcdonald-islands"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tariffs}}}\uc2  Trump imposed on Heard Island and McDonald Islands, inhabited only by penguins? Those penguins now have their {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.indy100.com/politics/trump/penguins-trump-tariffs-islands-threads"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 own social media account}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.threads.net/@penguinsagainsttrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @PenguinsAgainstTrump.}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1CWhat are you going to do, deport us?\u8221\'20\'1D one post reads. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve been dealing with ICE for centuries.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250412el4c001jm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
