\par\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 JD Vance may disagree, but this anti- \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  activist isn\u8217\'20\'19t a brutally censored dissident\b0\par\par\uc2 Catherine Bennett \par \uc2 1,101 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 April 2025\par 16:35 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The US vice-president\u8217\'20\'19s avid concern for Livia Tossici-Bolt\u8217\'20\'19s conviction is plain sinister\par \par \uc2 You know the feeling: you\u8217\'20\'19re feeling sociable, why wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t you make a sign saying \u8220\'20\'1CHere to talk, if you want to\u8221\'20\'1D, and head for a spot outside the nearest \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic? And why wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t some of its arriving patients want to pause before their appointments and satisfy your entirely innocent interest in their reproductive intentions?\par \par \uc2 This, give or take, amounted to the case by the prominent anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  campaigner, Livia Tossici-Bolt, who was on Friday found {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c4gr30z4lnlo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  guilty of twice breaching}}}\uc2  a Public Spaces Protection Order (PSPO). Her sign-holding outside a Bournemouth \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic was, she had argued, not covered by a council-imposed safe zone, being \u8220\'20\'1Ca mere invitation to speak\u8221\'20\'1D. And thus an invitation she could have happily extended to strangers just a little further from the clinic. But that did not suit Tossici-Bolt\u8217\'20\'19s purpose. Nor does anything prevent her from staging anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rallies, distributing literature, or expressing her views on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  anywhere except right in \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  patients\u8217\'20\'19 faces outside clinics. These details, although similar regulations {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/legal/us-supreme-court-rebuffs-free-speech-challenge-abortion-clinic-buffer-zone-2025-02-24/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 exist in parts of the US}}}\uc2 , routinely fail to surface in accounts by her prominent US supporters, with whose help Tossici-Bolt has been misrepresenting the illegal undermining of UK women\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a noble quest for free speech.\par \par \uc2 Joining with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/feb/16/prayer-and-prosecutions-the-us-hate-group-waging-war-over-britains-abortion-clinic-buffer-zones"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 JD Vance, and US anti-\b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  pressure group \uc2 Alliance Defending Freedom\uc2  (whose UK arm supported her legal defence), a bureau within the \uc2 US State Department\uc2  generously took time away from domestic free speech crises to send a delegation to meet Tossici-Bolt. It then tweeted what was generally understood as menacing, that it was \u8220\'20\'1Cmonitoring\u8221\'20\'1D her case. \u8220\'20\'1CIt is important that the UK respect and protect freedom of expression.\u8221\'20\'1D A similar admonition, tagging those twin objects of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s esteem, Putin and \uc2 Viktor Orb\u225\'00\'E1n\uc2 , is expected any time.\par \par \uc2 Would the State Department also be \u8220\'20\'1Cmonitoring\u8221\'20\'1D the protection from harassment of women seeking medical treatment, which is the right the \uc2 UK government\uc2  was finally, after increasing harassment outside \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics, compelled to balance with anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  campaigners\u8217\'20\'19 freedom to distress them? On the contrary. Pre-tariffs, the Telegraph attributed to some unnamed US imperialist the threatening statement \u8220\'20\'1Cno free trade without free speech\u8221\'20\'1D, as if, such is current US hubris, British women can no longer expect their reproductive choices to escape Trump\u8217\'20\'19s patriarchal reach. After Tossici-Bolt, the addition of an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  multiplier to the existing tariff formula cannot be ruled out.\par \par \uc2 British women can no longer expect their reproductive choices to escape Trump\u8217\'20\'19s patriarchal reach\par \par \uc2 Nor, now a British district judge, Orla Austin, has brazenly put domestic law before clear US instructions, can the bombing of, if not all of Dorset, at least Poole\u8217\'20\'19s unruly magistrates court. She found Tossici-Bolt had breached a buffer zone, and was ordered to pay \u163\'00\'A320,026 in costs with a two-year conditional discharge. Generously, you might think, Austin said Tossici-Bolt \u8220\'20\'1Clacked insight\u8221\'20\'1D into the impact of her actions. If so, the activist, who leads a local branch of 40 Days for Life, appears to have learned little from her years of protests, which include a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.judiciary.uk/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/Tossici-Bolt-v-Bournemouth-2023-EWHC-3229.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 failed legal}}}\uc2  challenge to the Bournemouth buffer zone and a submission against legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Northern Ireland.\par \par \uc2 That general restrictions outside \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics have, after years of disruption, finally been imposed is, of course, purely because of the distress increasingly inflicted on their clients by anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists. In the absence of safe zones, patients have been tormented with anything from abuse, spitting and challenges, to foetus pictures and activists striking attitudes indicating \u8220\'20\'1Csilent prayer\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 You might think, from outside the clinic-harassing community, that prayer location means little to an all-seeing God, but with a \uc2 What3Words\uc2  precision that might, if only theologians would investigate, account for unsatisfactory responses over thousands of years, experienced anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nuisances insist that these communications be transmitted on site. Maybe the signal is better there. Though in the case of the Bournemouth-based anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  campaigner, Adam Smith-Connor, it was more convenience that dictated silent prayer outside a clinic (the one also haunted by Tossici-Bolt) quite unrelated to the northern provider where he regretted an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  of 24 years ago. \u8220\'20\'1CIt is not practical for me to go to Leeds,\u8221\'20\'1D he told a court in 2022, \u8220\'20\'1Cso I go to a more local location to pray because my son lost his life within an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  facility.\u8221\'20\'1D He {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c4g9kp7r00vo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 received a two-year conditional discharge}}}\uc2  for breaching the PSPO with an order to pay \u163\'00\'A39,000 in costs.\par \par \uc2 In this way, Smith-Connor has also converted himself, as is evidently the way forward for anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  campaigners in predominantly \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -tolerant societies, into the more promising role of brutally censored dissident, Bournemouth\u8217\'20\'19s answer to Aleksandr Solzhenitsyn. \u8220\'20\'1CThank you VP Vance for defending western values & freedom. I salute you sir\u8221\'20\'1D, Smith-Connor tweeted after Vance had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.spectator.co.uk/article/jd-vance-what-i-worry-about-is-the-threat-from-within/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 surprised his audience}}}\uc2  at the Munich Security Conference with a speech that seemed better calculated to please anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  fanatics. Maybe the \uc2 ADF\uc2  got one about the defence legacy of the cold war?\par \par \uc2 By way of illustrating free speech in peril, Vance selected first, as the most shocking censorship, the fining of Bournemouth man Smith-Connor for breaching buffer zone regulations. Second, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thetimes.com/uk/politics/article/jd-vance-falsely-claims-uk-abortion-buffer-zones-ban-private-prayer-bvw7kv665"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lurching into fiction}}}\uc2 , he claimed Scottish residents in buffer zones had received letters warning that \u8220\'20\'1Ceven private prayer within their own homes may amount to breaking the law\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Not satisfied with this, Vance continued: \u8220\'20\'1CNaturally, the government urged readers to report any fellow citizens suspected guilty of thought crime in Britain and across Europe.\u8221\'20\'1D Eh? You gathered that even if lying is wrong, it\u8217\'20\'19s less wrong than missing the chance, as in this speech, to urge foreign opponents of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , by reinventing the intimidation of women as freedom, to go for a US-style assault on \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 And sure enough, St Livia of the harmless placards has called her conviction a \u8220\'20\'1Cdark day for freedom\u8221\'20\'1D. And to the extent that it provokes the White House into further meddling with British women\u8217\'20\'19s rights, she might, appallingly, be right.\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 Catherine Bennett is an Observer columnist\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Do you have an opinion on the issues raised in this article? If you would like to submit a letter of up to 250 words to be considered for publication, email it to us at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:observer.letters@observer.co.uk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 observer.letters@observer.co.uk}}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250409el460026l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
