\par\par \uc2 UK news\par \b \uc2 US anti- \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  group expands campaign in UK\b0\par\par\uc2 Ben Quinn \par \uc2 908 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 April 2025\par 14:38 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par 15\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Exclusive: \uc2 Alliance Defending Freedom\uc2 , which is funding case of activist Livia Tossici-Bolt, is lobbying against buffer zones around clinics\par \par \uc2 A rightwing US group backing an anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  campaigner whose case has become a new source of UK tensions with the Trump administration is significantly expanding activities and spending in Britain.\par \par \uc2 The UK branch of \uc2 Alliance Defending Freedom\uc2  (\uc2 ADF\uc2 ), which is funding the case of Livia Tossici-Bolt \u8211\'20\'13 who is being prosecuted for an alleged breach of a \u8220\'20\'1Cbuffer zone\u8221\'20\'1D outside a Bournemouth \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic \u8211\'20\'13 increased spending on campaigning and other activities in the UK to more than \u163\'00\'A31m last year.\par \par \uc2 ADF UK\u8217\'20\'19s income was more than \u163\'00\'A31.3m in the year up to June last year, according to records filed to Companies House on Friday. It included \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 ADF\uc2  support\u8221\'20\'1D of \u163\'00\'A31,119,975.\par \par \uc2 The organisation held discussions with a delegation from the US state department, which visited the UK last month before the release of a statement in which the US voiced concern about \u8220\'20\'1Cfreedom of expression in the UK\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 ADF UK, which describes itself as an advocate for \u8220\'20\'1Cthe right of Christians and others to freely associate and share their faith in public\u8221\'20\'1D, has been heavily involved in lobbying against the introduction of buffer zones around \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive health\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics.\par \par \uc2 Its cases have included that of Adam Smith-Connor, who was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/feb/14/jd-vance-stuns-munich-conference-with-blistering-attack-on-europes-leaders"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cited by the US vice-president, JD Vance}}}\uc2 , as an example of free speech being under threat in Europe, after Smith-Connor was prosecuted for breaching a public space protection order.\par \par \uc2 Tossici-Bolt, ADF UK\u8217\'20\'19s latest high-profile case, was mentioned in the US state department statement on Sunday.\par \par \uc2 A verdict on her alleged breach is expected on Friday. She denies the charges.\par \par \uc2 ADF\uc2 , which is designated a hate group by the \uc2 Southern Poverty Law Center\uc2  in the US, has close links with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s White House and has spoken of working with his administration on areas including the reversal of trans rights.\par \par \uc2 The current speaker of the \uc2 US House of Representatives\uc2 , Mike Johnson, is a former \uc2 ADF\uc2  lawyer.\par \par \uc2 Filings show that the organisation\u8217\'20\'19s British wing has a staff of nine, one earning a salary of \u163\'00\'A3100,000 a year and two others paid between \u163\'00\'A390,000 and \u163\'00\'A3100,000.\par \par \uc2 The same records give an overview of ADF UK activities in Britain, which range from briefing MPs to supporting campaigns against the assisted dying bill, and \u8220\'20\'1Cfree speech\u8221\'20\'1D cases.\par \par \uc2 The organisation is planning a big event in September in Britain as part of a plan to train law and public policy students.\par \par \uc2 ADF UK has five directors. Two, including the lawyers Robert Clarke and Paul Coleman, are based in the organisation\u8217\'20\'19s international branch headquarters in Austria.\par \par \uc2 UK reproductive healthcare providers have voiced concern about \uc2 ADF\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s role and cited the reversal of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the US and pressure exerted by rightwing campaigners.\par \par \uc2 Louise McCudden, the UK head of external affairs at \uc2 MSI Reproductive Choices\uc2 , said: \u8220\'20\'1CBefore safe access zones were implemented last year, the behaviour we saw outside our clinics included spitting, calling women \u8216\'20\'18murderers\u8217\'20\'19 and physically blocking people from entering our clinics.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn the US, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics have been bombed and burned down, and anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  campaigners have been known to gather outside clinics with guns. Doctors have been assassinated.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Heidi Stewart, the chief executive of the \uc2 British Pregnancy Advisory Service\uc2 , said: \u8220\'20\'1CIt is deeply concerning that US anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  extremists are using their significant financial resources to attempt to influence women\u8217\'20\'19s access to safe, legal reproductive healthcare here in the UK.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFollowing the overturning of Roe v Wade and the re-election of Trump as president, the anti-choice movement in this country have become emboldened in their continued attempt to strip women of their rights, dignity, and future.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 An \uc2 ADF\uc2  spokesperson said it was a registered human rights charity in the UK and was grateful to the US for bringing attention to what it described as the \u8220\'20\'1Cfree speech crisis\u8221\'20\'1D in Britain.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe advance the right to live and speak the truth for all people and are proud to support Livia\u8217\'20\'19s case and the cases of our other clients who have been victims of \u8216\'20\'18buffer zone\u8217\'20\'19 censorship,\u8221\'20\'1D they said.\par \par \uc2 ADF\uc2  was named in a \uc2 Facebook\uc2  post by the US Bureau of Democracy, Human Rights, and Labor (DRL), an office in the US state department, as being among organisations its delegation met while in the UK.\par \par \uc2 It also met officials from the \uc2 Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office\uc2  and \uc2 Ofcom\uc2 , using its talks with Britain\u8217\'20\'19s communications regulator to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2025/apr/01/us-officials-challenge-ofcoms-risk-to-free-speech-caused-by-online-safety-laws"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 challenge it on the impact of new online safety laws}}}\uc2  on freedom of expression.\par \par \uc2 The freedom of expression statement was issued after the delegation met Tossici-Bolt and ADF UK.\par \par \uc2 Among the group was Samuel D Samson, who previously worked for US conservative organisations and was pictured wearing a Make America Great Again cap. He was appointed as a senior adviser at the DRL in January. On the day of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s US election, he tweeted: \u8220\'20\'1CToday we choose God over pagan idols.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The DRL\u8217\'20\'19s interest in Britain marks a pivot by an agency set up in the 1970s to advance democracy around the world against the backdrop of the cold war.\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 This article was amended on 4 April 2025 to remove an incorrect reference that \uc2 Alliance Defending Freedom\uc2  had endorsed \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s election campaign.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250402el42002e7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
