\par\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 Despite Livia Tossici-Bolt\u8217\'20\'19s conviction, the US is not finished with making  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  a UK culture war issue\b0\par\par\uc2 Rhiannon Lucy Cosslett \par \uc2 1,044 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 April 2025\par 12:03 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 We should all be worried that the rightwing organisation \uc2 Alliance Defending Freedom\uc2  has been increasing its activities in this country\par \par \uc2 I couldn\u8217\'20\'19t sleep the other night, because I made the fatal mistake of reading about US politics directly before bed, specifically the executive order {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2025/mar/31/donald-trump-america-history-museums-smithsonian-institution"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 calling for the removal}}}\uc2  of \u8220\'20\'1Cimproper, divisive or anti-American ideology\u8221\'20\'1D from the Smithsonian museums. If US politics were a film, I\u8217\'20\'19d say we\u8217\'20\'19re somewhere in between having read aloud from the book that summons demons as a joke, and the final bloodbath.\par \par \uc2 If JD Vance rewriting history isn\u8217\'20\'19t sinister enough, then came the news that the US state department will be \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thenational.scot/news/25053003.us-state-department-monitoring-uk-womans-buffer-zone-case/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 monitoring}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D a UK woman\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  buffer zone case (why does everything they say always sound so creepy?) They are \u8220\'20\'1Cconcerned\u8221\'20\'1D, apparently, \u8220\'20\'1Cabout freedom of expression in the United Kingdom\u8221\'20\'1D. The case is that of Livia Tossici-Bolt \u8211\'20\'13 who held up a sign reading \u8220\'20\'1CHere to talk if you want\u8221\'20\'1D outside a Bournemouth \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/apr/04/abortion-campaigner-livia-tossici-bolt-buffer-zone-clinic"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was this morning convicted}}}\uc2  of breaching the buffer zone. Her case {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2025/apr/02/us-anti-abortion-group-expands-campaign-in-uk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was being funded}}}\uc2  by the UK branch of \uc2 Alliance Defending Freedom\uc2  (\uc2 ADF\uc2 ), a rightwing organisation with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/oct/05/michael-farris-amy-coney-barrett-adf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 links to the White House}}}\uc2 , which has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2025/apr/02/us-anti-abortion-group-expands-campaign-in-uk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 increased its expenditure}}}\uc2  and activities in this country of late. It has been designated a hate group by the \uc2 Southern Poverty Law Center\uc2  in the US.\par \par \uc2 Ominously, this isn\u8217\'20\'19t the first time the US has invoked the UK\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic buffer zone legislation. In a speech at the Munich Security Conference in February, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c87d9j17pjqo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Vance made the false claim}}}\uc2  that people who live within safe access zones had been sent letters by the Scottish government warning them about praying within their homes. Those comments were dangerous scaremongering, and were condemned as such, while this latest intervention {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.independent.co.uk/news/uk/politics/free-speech-uk-abortion-us-state-department-vance-b2725126.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has been blasted as}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cunjustifiable interference\u8221\'20\'1D by the former UK supreme court judge Lord Sumption. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2025/apr/01/uk-business-secretary-denies-free-speech-issue-featured-in-us-tariff-talks"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 There were reports}}}\uc2  this week that the US was intending to use these spurious concerns over free speech as leverage in trade negotiations, but the business secretary has denied this. Nevertheless, they form part of an increasingly alarming mood music regarding \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the UK.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe US state department claims that its concerns over buffer zones are around free speech, but \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not a free speech issue,\u8221\'20\'1D Sian Norris, author of Bodies Under Siege: How the Far-Right Attack on \b \highlight22\uc2 Reproductive Rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  Went Global, tells me. \u8220\'20\'1CPeople can be anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  wherever they like, but they cannot use their speech to harm others and repress women\u8217\'20\'19s human rights.\u8221\'20\'1D Norris is concerned but not surprised about the involvement of \uc2 ADF\uc2  and 40 Days for Life \u8211\'20\'13 a movement to end \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 whose Bournemouth branch is led by Tossici-Bolt.\par \par \uc2 Why so much interest by US politicians and pressure groups? I don\u8217\'20\'19t believe for a moment that the likes of Vance are truly het up about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics in the UK. Do they, like Farage, believe that there is some sort of far-right groundswell of opinion in the UK that is waiting to be exploited? I\u8217\'20\'19m not sure there\u8217\'20\'19s an appetite for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  culture war here: while I always hesitate to invoke concepts such as national character, I don\u8217\'20\'19t believe that citizens of the UK generally approve of private individuals being impeded from accessing medical treatment. It isn\u8217\'20\'19t polite, or decent, and what people do with their bodies is largely regarded as their own business. As the latest {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://natcen.ac.uk/how-are-attitudes-towards-abortion-britain-changing"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 social attitudes survey shows}}}\uc2 , support for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is at an all-time high. That isn\u8217\'20\'19t to say that the question is settled: Labour must do that by putting decriminalisation {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2024/apr/08/decriminalise-abortion-in-england-and-wales-parliament-women-stella-creasy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 back on the table}}}\uc2  as soon as possible.\par \par \uc2 Perhaps all that doesn\u8217\'20\'19t matter. Vance et al know that these comments will play well with the rightwing Christians at home. Having largely won the war in the US by depriving millions of women there of their fundamental human rights with the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-overturned-abortion-summary-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rollback of Roe v Wade}}}\uc2 , they are still not satisfied. UK \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  buffer zones are a useful issue to add to the \uc2 US government\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s main culture war \u8211\'20\'13 the idea that they are liberating people from \u8220\'20\'1Cwoke\u8221\'20\'1D and getting free speech back. Despite the fact that, as Lord Sumption noted, one of the biggest threats to free speech right now is the US, this makes it look as though it is the defender of peaceful protest both at home and abroad.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s an effective distraction tactic. \u8220\'20\'1COK, so we are literally censoring our national museums right now, but look at how we are supporting this poor woman, who simply held a sign up outside an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic!\u8221\'20\'1D Cynical leaks suggesting that \u8220\'20\'1Cthere\u8217\'20\'19s no free trade without free speech\u8221\'20\'1D add to this deliberately crafted impression of the US as a global guardian of freedom of expression. In a way it doesn\u8217\'20\'19t really matter whether UK \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  buffer zone legislation forms a part of trade negotiations: it\u8217\'20\'19s enough that the US has implied that it has and will. Whether Tossici-Bolt\u8217\'20\'19s conviction will prompt further attempts to interfere remains to be seen, but the AFD\u8217\'20\'19s increased interest in the UK is terrifying. This battle isn\u8217\'20\'19t over.\par \par \uc2 There will no doubt be those who think my fears are hysterical, but people said the same when feminists publicly feared for Roe v Wade, and women\u8217\'20\'19s bodies have been battlegrounds for so long that hypervigilance is a natural response. If you\u8217\'20\'19ll forgive me for returning to my horror movie analogy: when you live in a haunted house, you start to see threat around every corner.\par \par \uc2 As for our government \u8211\'20\'13 will it robustly defend any perceived attack on British women\u8217\'20\'19s human rights, and publicly condemn the brazen use of US cash to try to influence our laws? I\u8217\'20\'19m not holding my breath.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Rhiannon Lucy Cosslett is a Guardian columnist\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Do you have an opinion on the issues raised in this article? If you would like to submit a response of up to 300 words by email to be considered for publication in our {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/tone/letters"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  letters}}}\uc2  section, please {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:guardian.letters@theguardian.com?body=Please%20include%20your%20name,%20full%20postal%20address%20and%20phone%20number%20with%20your%20letter%20below.%20Letters%20are%20usually%20published%20with%20the%20author%27s%20name%20and%20city/town/village.%20The%20rest%20of%20the%20information%20is%20for%20verification%20only%20and%20to%20contact%20you%20where%20necessary."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 click here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250404el44001ux\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
