\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Election results released in Wisconsin judicial race \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Cecilia Nowell (now); L\u233\'00\'E9onie Chao-Fong, Coral Murphy Marcos and Tom Ambrose (earlier) \par \uc2 11,684 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 April 2025\par 03:10 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Liberal judge defeats \uc2 Brad Schimel\uc2  in the most expensive judicial election in US history, which cost a combined $80mWisconsin supreme court race: Liberal Susan Crawford beats Musk-backed candidate\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.57am BST\par \par \uc2 Summary\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 Our live coverage is ending now. In the meantime, you can find all of our live US politics coverage {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 . Here is a summary of the key developments from today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Wisconsin and Florida held special elections for a state supreme court seat and two open spots in the House of Representatives, in the first elections since \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s election in November. In Wisconsin, liberal judge Susan Crawford won her race, despite tech billionaire \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s millions in donations in support of her opponent. Meanwhile, in Florida, Republicans maintained control of the two seats vacated by national security adviser \uc2 Mike Waltz\uc2  and former congressman \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Senator \uc2 Cory Booker\uc2 , the Democrat from New Jersey, broke the record for the longest speech given on the Senate Floor after he concluded a 25 hour and 5 minute address denouncing the Trump administration and its budget cuts.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Thousands of Health and Human Services (\uc2 HHS\uc2 ) employees across the country were dismissed as the Trump administration began implementing its controversial workforce-reduction plan. The firings have included staff members who were working on the Food and Drug Administration \u8217\'20\'19s bird flu response, and shuttered at least five of Head Start \u8217\'20\'19s regional offices.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The US attorney general Pam Bondi announced that she had directed federal prosecutors to seek the death penalty for Luigi Mangione, the man accused of murdering the UnitedHealthcare CEO \uc2 Brian Thompson\uc2  outside a Manhattan hotel in December.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A group of Democratic-led states have sued the Trump administration over its decision to cut $11bn in federal funds that they were allocated during the Covid-19 pandemic.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s so-called \u8220\'20\'1Cdepartment of government efficiency\u8221\'20\'1D is finalizing its shuttering of the \uc2 US Agency for International Development\uc2 , ordering the firings of thousands of local workers, US diplomats and civil servants assigned to the agency overseas\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.44am BST\par \par \uc2 Delivering her victory speech in Madison, Judge Susan Crawford thanked Wisconsin voters for electing her to the state\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI never could have imagined that I\u8217\'20\'19d be taking on the richest man in the world,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, a nod to tech billionaire \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s significant spending on her opponent\u8217\'20\'19s campaign.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy promise to Wisconsin is clear: I will be a fair, impartial justice on the Wisconsin supreme court.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.24am BST\par \par \uc2 Democrat-backed candidate Susan Crawford has won Wisconsin\u8217\'20\'19s open seat on the state\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court, preserving the court\u8217\'20\'19s liberal majority as it prepares to hear cases that could {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/mar/31/wisconsin-abortion-state-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 determine the future of \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/wisconsin-union-supreme-court-collective-bargaining-ead7ad7e8c2187eb87197f002090755c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 collective bargaining rights}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Although state supreme court races are technically nonpartisan, Democrats had backed Crawford over her opponent, \uc2 Brad Schimel\uc2 , who\u8217\'20\'19d drawn support from Republicans including \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The election became a proxy for national debates and skyrocketed to the most expensive court race in US history, with spending approaching $99m. While Schimel received significant support from Musk, who flew to Wisconsin over the weekend and contributed more than $21 million on the race, Crawford embraced \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights supporters, including \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2 , who backed her candidacy.\par \par \uc2 Crawford\u8217\'20\'19s win will preserve the court\u8217\'20\'19s 4-3 liberal majority for another three years.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/apr/01/wisconsin-florida-voters-elections-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Wisconsin and Florida voters head to polls in test of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s popularity}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.28am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.02am BST\par \par \uc2 Cory Booker\uc2 , the Democratic senator from New Jersey, fasted and dehydrated himself ahead of his record-setting speech with the aim of breaking Strom Thurmond\u8217\'20\'19s 1957 record for the longest speech on the Senate floor.\par \par \uc2 Booker told CNN that he stopped eating days ago and dehydrated himself to avoid needing to take a break to use the restroom over the course of his 25 hour and 5 minute speech. As a result, he said, he experienced muscle spasms as he stayed on his feet throughout the address.\par \par \uc2 Booker said he was \u8220\'20\'1Cvery aware of Strom Thurmond\u8217\'20\'19s record\u8221\'20\'1D heading into the marathon speech.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSince I\u8217\'20\'19ve gotten to the Senate, I always felt it was a strange shadow hanging over this institution \u8212\'20\'14 that the longest speech, all the issues that have come up, all the noble causes that people have done, or the things that typically try to stop \u8212\'20\'14 I just found it strange that he had the record,\u8221\'20\'1D Booker told CNN. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd, as a guy who grew up with the legends of the civil rights movement, myself \u8212\'20\'14 my parents and their friends \u8212\'20\'14 it just would seem wrong to me. It always seemed wrong.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.49am BST\par \par \uc2 Wisconsin voters have elected to enshrine a voter ID law in the state constitution.\par \par \uc2 Still to come are the results from two races occurring in the state this evening, for a seat on the state\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court and to lead the state\u8217\'20\'19s education department.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.57am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.33am BST\par \par \uc2 Tallies from Wisconsin\u8217\'20\'19s hotly contested supreme court race are beginning to roll in, but it\u8217\'20\'19s not the only election happening tonight in the Badger state.\par \par \uc2 Voters will also decide at the polls who will serve as the state\u8217\'20\'19s top education officials and whether to enshrine a voter ID law in the state constitution.\par \par \uc2 In the race to lead the state\u8217\'20\'19s department of public instruction, Democrat- and union-backed Jill Underly is running against Republican-backed Brittany Kinser. Both have previously worked at public schools, but Kinser has called herself a supporter of the private school voucher program\par \par \uc2 Voters will also decide whether to amend the state constitution to include a photo ID requirement, a measure put forward by the Republican-controlled legislature. The law, one of nine such photo-ID requirements in the country, will remain in place whether voters agree to enshrine it in the constitution or not.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.56am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.18am BST\par \par \uc2 Numerous issues likely drove Wisconsin voters to the polls in \u8220\'20\'1Chistoric\u8221\'20\'1D numbers for this year\u8217\'20\'19s state supreme court race, including \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, \uc2 Guardian\uc2  reporter {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/carter-sherman"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Carter Sherman}}}\uc2  writes.\par \par \uc2 Here she is with more:\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, Wisconsin residents will decide whether to elect liberal Susan Crawford or conservative \uc2 Brad Schimel\uc2 , two county judges, to the state supreme court, which is poised to weigh in on two major \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  cases. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights advocates are trying to use the threat to the procedure to convince people to head to the polls, but, more than two years after the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  overturned {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade}}}\uc2 , it is no longer clear whether \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  can tip an election. Democratic candidates talked about outrage over Roe constantly during the 2024 election \u8211\'20\'13 and fell short, losing both the White House and the Senate.\par \par \uc2 Ben Wikler, leader of the Democratic party of Wisconsin, remains convinced that the issue can be Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 silver bullet.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is the single issue that most motivates Democratic voters and persuades independent, moderate voters to cast a ballot for Susan Crawford and against \uc2 Brad Schimel\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D Wikler said. Although the candidates are nominally non-partisan, the Democratic party is backing Crawford, while \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has endorsed Schimel. If Schimel wins, conservatives will regain control of the state supreme court.\par \par \uc2 For more, read on below:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/mar/31/wisconsin-abortion-state-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 A Wisconsin state supreme court race will test whether \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  can still tip an election}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.05am BST\par \par \uc2 Columbia University\uc2  student Mahmoud Khalil\u8217\'20\'19s deportation case should continue to play out in New Jersey, a federal judge ruled today, not Louisiana where Khalil was transfered into custody.\par \par \uc2 US District Judge Michael Farbiarz said the case should remain in New Jersey since Khalil was being held there when his lawyer filed their Habeas Corpus petition. If Khalil\u8217\'20\'19s case had been heard in Louisiana, it could have ended up before one of the nation\u8217\'20\'19s most conservative appeals courts.\par \par \uc2 Immigrations and customs enforcement (Ice) detained Khalil, a greencard holder, on March 8, citing his involvement in student protests against the war in Gaza.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/apr/01/mahmoud-khalil-case-new-jersey"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Judge rules Mahmoud Khalil\u8217\'20\'19s deportation case must continue in New Jersey}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.37am BST\par \par \uc2 With results from Florida\u8217\'20\'19s special elections already in, we\u8217\'20\'19re still waiting on news out of Wisconsin, where voters will elect a new justice to the state\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court. Conservative \uc2 Brad Schimel\uc2  and liberal Susan Crawford are locked in a race that will determine the balance of power on the state\u8217\'20\'19s court.\par \par \uc2 Turnout appears high in Wisconsin \u8211\'20\'13 so high that seven polling sites in the city of Milwaukee reported ballot shortages \u8211\'20\'13 and early voting was more than 50% ahead of levels seen in the state\u8217\'20\'19s last supreme court race.\par \par \uc2 That turnout is indicative of the attention that the Wisconsin race has garnered from across the country. According to the Brennan Center for Justice, it is now the most expensive court race on record in the US, with spending approaching $99m.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s ally and tech billionaire \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  personally contributed $3m to Schimel\u8217\'20\'19s campaign and another $1m each to three voters who signed a petition he circulated against \u8220\'20\'1Cactivist judges\u8221\'20\'1D, while groups he funded donated another $18m.\par \par \uc2 Democrats also showed support for their preferred candidate in the race, with former \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  and the billionaire \uc2 George Soros\uc2  backing Crawford.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.40am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.27am BST\par \par \uc2 Republicans maintain hold on both Florida seats\par \par \uc2 Republican \uc2 Jimmy Patronis\uc2  has won his race for Florida\u8217\'20\'19s house district 1, retaining Republican control of a seat that his predecessor \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2  won by more than 30 points last year.\par \par \uc2 Patronis\u8217\'20\'19s win came despite millions in donations in support of his competitor\u8217\'20\'19s campaign from Democrats nationwide, who\u8217\'20\'19d hoped the special election might prove an opportunity to voice their disapproval of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s agenda.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.32am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.07am BST\par \par \uc2 Cory Booker\uc2  has concluded his speech denouncing the Trump administration, 25 hours and five minutes after he began speaking Monday evening.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI believe that there is an urgent crisis in our country that we are not talking about. It\u8217\'20\'19s not a left-right crisis, it\u8217\'20\'19s a right-wrong crisis,\u8221\'20\'1D he said shortly after announcing he was winding down his remarks.\par \par \uc2 In the final minutes of his speech, Booker returned to stories he had shared over the previous day from Americans who\u8217\'20\'19d accessed veterans, Medicaid and other benefits currently under threat of cuts by Trump\u8217\'20\'19s cost-cutting measures.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t know how to solve this, I don\u8217\'20\'19t know how to stop us from going down this road,\u8221\'20\'1D Booker concluded. \u8220\'20\'1CBut I know who does have the power. The people of the United States of America. The power of the people is greater than the people in power.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLet\u8217\'20\'19s get in good trouble,\u8221\'20\'1D Booker ended, referencing his mentor the late congressman John Lewis.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.50am BST\par \par \uc2 Republicans retain key congressional seat in Florida\par \par \uc2 The Republican \uc2 Randy Fine\uc2  has won his race for Florida\u8217\'20\'19s House district six, filling the seat vacated by \uc2 Michael Waltz\uc2 , who is now \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s national security adviser.\par \par \uc2 Democrats had hoped that challenger Josh Weil might flip the long-held conservative seat, located where the president won by more than 30 points, as Weil out-raised Fine nearly tenfold.\par \par \uc2 Results are not yet available for the second special election in Florida tonight, where voters will decide who will fill the seat vacated by the former representative \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.23am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.44am BST\par \par \uc2 The former president of Costa Rica and Nobel Prize winner \u211\'00\'D3scar Arias says the United States has revoked his visa to enter the country.\par \par \uc2 Arias shared the news with Reuters, noting that the decision came just weeks after he criticized President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  on social media. In a post, Arias said Trump was behaving like \u8220\'20\'1Ca Roman emperor.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.20am BST\par \par \uc2 Cory Booker\uc2  gives longest speech in \uc2 US Senate\uc2  history\par \par \uc2 As he approached the record for longest speech given on the Senate floor, the New Jersey senator \uc2 Cory Booker\uc2  reflected on the legacy of his late colleague, the civil rights leader John Lewis.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is one of those moments when John Lewis would not sit still,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t know what John Lewis would say right now\u8221\'20\'1D but he \u8220\'20\'1Cwould say something, he would do something \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is our moral moment. This is when the most precious ideas of our country are being tested,\u8221\'20\'1D Booker continued. \u8220\'20\'1CAre we going to do something different like John Lewis would call us to do? He would call us to get into good trouble, necessary trouble.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 At the exact moment when he surpassed the previous record \u8211\'20\'13 held by the Republican senator Strom Thurmond, who gave a 24-hour-and-18-minute long speech filibustering the Civil Rights Act in 1957 \u8211\'20\'13 Booker forgave Thurmond for trying to block the protections that allowed him to be where he is today.\par \par \uc2 The Senate minority leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  then interrupted Booker to ask a question, telling him he\u8217\'20\'19d broken the record.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.22am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.01am BST\par \par \uc2 Booker's anti-Trump speech surpasses 24 hours on Senate floor\par \par \uc2 Cory Booker\uc2 , the Democratic senator from New Jersey, has surpassed 24 hours of speaking on the Senate floor.\par \par \uc2 Booker took to the floor at 7pm ET on Monday in an attempt to disrupt the normal business of the Senate to protest the \u8220\'20\'1Cgrave and urgent\u8221\'20\'1D danger of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s presidential administration.\par \par \uc2 As he approached a full day of speaking, Booker had begun to stumble slightly in his speech, but was still on his feet, making sweeping gestures as he spoke.\par \par \uc2 Over the past hour, Booker has evoked the Founding Fathers, Civil Rights leaders and lawmakers who stood up against McCarthyism in his calls for congressmembers to more assertively hold the Trump administration accountable.\par \par \uc2 Yielding to a question from Connecticut senator \uc2 Chris Murphy\uc2 , while retaining the floor, Booker rested a moment while Murphy recounted the longest speech in Senate history, given in 1957 by Republican senator Strom Thurmond to filibuster the Civil Rights Act.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat you have done here today Senator Booker couldn\u8217\'20\'19t be more different than what occurred on this floor in 1957,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CStrom Thurmond was standing in the way of inevitable progress.\u8221\'20\'1D He added, \u8220\'20\'1CToday, you are standing in the way not of progress but of retreat.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.02am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 As he approaches 24 hours of speaking on the Senate floor, the New Jersey senator \uc2 Cory Booker\uc2  has invoked nation\u8217\'20\'19s founders.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf men were angels, no government would be necessary,\u8221\'20\'1D Booker said, reading from Federalist No 51. He added: \u8220\'20\'1CBut our president is no angel.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Emphasizing the role Congress should play to hold the executive branch accountable, Booker decried his fellow congressmembers for failing to vote against the president\u8217\'20\'19s cabinet nominees and other policies.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe most powerful man in the world and the richest man in the world have taken a battle axe to the Veterans\u8217\'20\'19 Association, a battle axe to the Department of Education, a battle axe to the only agency solely focused on protecting consumers against big banks and other factors that might abuse them,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CWhat will we do in this body? What will we do in the House of Represenatitves? Right now the answer is nothing.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.07am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 Hours after the health secretary Robert F Kennedy Jr wrote on social media : \u8220\'20\'1CThe revolution begins today!\u8221\'20\'1D thousands of employees of the \uc2 Department of Health and Human Services\uc2  received layoff notices.\par \par \uc2 Those layoffs forced nearly half of the regional offices for Head Start to close Tuesday, according to the \uc2 National Head Start Association\uc2 . Five of the preschool program\u8217\'20\'19s 12 regional offices closed due to workforce reductions.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Canadian prime minister, \uc2 Mark Carney\uc2 , spoke on the phone with the Mexican president, \uc2 Claudia Sheinbaum\uc2 , today to discuss the \u8220\'20\'1Cimportance of building upon the strong trading and investment relationship between the two countries \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The North American leaders spoke about \u8220\'20\'1Cthe challenging times ahead\u8221\'20\'1D and promised to stay in \u8220\'20\'1Cclose contact\u8221\'20\'1D, according to the \uc2 Canadian government\uc2 , as they navigate efforts to secure their sovereignty and economic competitiveness amid tariffs and other threats from the United States.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Booker's speech criticizing Trump becomes second-longest in Senate history\par \par \uc2 Cory Booker\uc2 , the Democratic senator from New Jersey, has been speaking on the Senate floor for more than 23 hours.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is wrong in every way you look at it,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, speaking about the Trump administrations\u8217\'20\'19 proposed budget cuts, as he approached the 23-hour mark of his speech.\par \par \uc2 Booker began his speech yesterday at 7pm ET in protest of what he called the \u8220\'20\'1Cgrave and urgent\u8221\'20\'1D danger that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s presidential administration poses to democracy and the American people.\par \par \uc2 Booker is closing in on the longest speech ever given in Senate history. In 1957, Strom Thurmond, a Republican from South Carolina, gave an anti-civil rights speech that lasted 24 hours and 18 minutes.\par \par \uc2 In 1986, Alfonse D\u8217\'20\'19Amato, a Republican from New York, spoke about the Defense Authorization Act for 23 hours and 30 minutes. But earlier today, the Senate Historical Office corrected its list to omit D\u8217\'20\'19Amato\u8217\'20\'19s speech because the Senate adjourned for several hours during his remarks.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/apr/01/cory-booker-senate-speech-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cory Booker holds marathon Senate speech to warn of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s \u8216\'20\'18harmful\u8217\'20\'19 policies}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 During a Fox News interview this afternoon, \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  made a last-minute appeal to Wisconsin voters in support of the state supreme court candidate \uc2 Brad Schimel\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA judge race, election in Wisconsin will decide whether or not the Democrats can gerrymander Wisconsin in order to remove two House seats from Republican to Democrat,\u8221\'20\'1D Musk said. \u8220\'20\'1CIf you know people in Wisconsin, call them right now.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Republicans including Musk and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  have backed Schimel, a former state attorney general, in hopes of turning the 4-3 supreme court conservative. Musk traveled to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/wisconsin"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Wisconsin}}}\uc2  over the weekend, where he handed out $1m checks to two voters.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 A Pennsylvania man has filed a lawsuit against \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  claiming the billionaire reneged on payments promised to canvassers during the 2024 election, the \uc2 New York Times{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/live/2025/04/01/us/trump-news-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Filed as a class action against Musk and his Super Pac, the suit alleges Musk failed to pay the claimant $20,000 he was owed for collecting signatures.\par \par \uc2 Musk told Pennsylvanians he\u8217\'20\'19d pay $100 to those willing to sign petitions supporting free speech and gun ownership rights, and $47 for each signatory recruited, an amount raised to $100 in the final days of the election.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 Thousands of people are tuning in to watch \uc2 Cory Booker\uc2  hold the Senate floor as his marathon speech against the \u8220\'20\'1Cgrave and urgent\u8221\'20\'1D danger posed by the Trump administration closes in on the 22-hour mark.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/apr/01/cory-booker-senate-speech-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cory Booker holds marathon Senate speech to warn of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s \u8216\'20\'18harmful\u8217\'20\'19 policies}}}\par \par \uc2 Just before 5pm ET, more than 71,500 people were watching along from Booker\u8217\'20\'19s live feed on \uc2 YouTube\uc2 . Meanwhile, several news organizations, including AP, \uc2 PBS\uc2 , \uc2 CBS\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 and of course {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/apr/01/cory-booker-senate-speech-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Guardian}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 had feeds of their own. Others tuned in through \uc2 C-SPAN\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Booker began speaking on Monday evening, vowing to remain on the Senate floor as long as he was \u8220\'20\'1Cphysically able\u8221\'20\'1D. His speech has already become one of the longest in Senate history.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese are not normal times in our nation,\u8221\'20\'1D Booker said as he launched into his speech. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd they should not be treated as such in the \uc2 United States Senate\uc2 . The threats to the American people and American democracy are grave and urgent, and we all must do more to stand against them.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 Mike Waltz\uc2  and other national security officials using Gmail for government business - report\par \par \uc2 National security leaders, including the White House national security adviser \uc2 Mike Waltz\uc2 , conducted government business over personal Gmail accounts, the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  reports.\par \par \uc2 The Post cites documents it reviewed and interviews with three US officials that showed members of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s National Security Council had used the commercial email service, which is less secure than Signal, the service Waltz and other Trump administration officials used to coordinate a bombing attack on Yemen last week.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA senior Waltz aide used the commercial email service for highly technical conversations with colleagues at other government agencies involving sensitive military positions and powerful weapons systems relating to an ongoing conflict,\u8221\'20\'1D the Post reports. \u8220\'20\'1CWhile the NSC official used his Gmail account, his interagency colleagues used government-issued accounts, headers from the email correspondence show.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It continues: \u8220\'20\'1CWaltz has had less sensitive, but potentially exploitable information sent to his Gmail, such as his schedule and other work documents, said officials, who, like others, spoke on the condition of anonymity to describe what they viewed as problematic handling of information. The officials said Waltz would sometimes copy and paste from his schedule into Signal to coordinate meetings and discussions.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.00am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 Today so far\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ve been watching today as the New Jersey senator \uc2 Cory Booker\uc2  enters his 21st hour of speaking during a marathon address designed to \u8220\'20\'1Cdisrupt\u8221\'20\'1D the \u8220\'20\'1Cnormal business of the \uc2 United States Senate\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D for as long as he is \u8220\'20\'1Cphysically able\u8221\'20\'1D. Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is going on across the country.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Voters are casting their ballots in Wisconsin and Florida in elections that may prove a symbol of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s popularity and \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s clout.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s so-called \u8220\'20\'1Cdepartment of government efficiency\u8221\'20\'1D is finalizing its shuttering of the \uc2 US Agency for International Development\uc2 , ordering the firings of thousands of local workers, US diplomats and civil servants assigned to the agency overseas.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Thousands of Health and Human Services (\uc2 HHS\uc2 ) employees across the country are being dismissed as the Trump administration began implementing its controversial workforce-reduction plan. The plan could see 10,000 staff members removed from the department.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The firings at \uc2 HHS\uc2  have included staff members who were working on the Food and Drug Administration \u8217\'20\'19s bird flu response, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The representative \uc2 Jerry Nadler\uc2 , a New York Democrat, has issued a statement strongly condemning the Trump administration for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/mar/07/trump-administration-cancels-columbia-university-funding"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cancelling $400m in federal grants and contracts to }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/mar/07/trump-administration-cancels-columbia-university-funding"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Columbia University}}}\uc2  because of what it alleged was the college\u8217\'20\'19s repeated failure to protect students from antisemitic harassment.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The US attorney general Pam Bondi announced that she had directed federal prosecutors to seek the death penalty for Luigi Mangione, the man accused of murdering the UnitedHealthcare CEO \uc2 Brian Thompson\uc2  outside a Manhattan hotel in December.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Republican House speaker Mike Johnson failed to block a bipartisan effort to change House rules to allow new parents in Congress to vote remotely after the birth of a child. The proxy vote resolution has been led by Anna Paulina Luna of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/florida"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Florida}}}\uc2  and the Democratic representative Brittany Pettersen of Colorado.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.06am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Cory Booker\uc2 's Senate floor speech enters 21st hour\par \par \uc2 Cory Booker\uc2 , the Democratic senator from New Jersey, has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/apr/01/cory-booker-senate-speech-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 now spoken for 21 hours on the Senate floor}}}\uc2  in opposition to the Trump administration.\par \par \uc2 Booker has used his speaking slot to decry the Trump administration\u8217\'20\'19s spending cuts, its attempt to abolish the Department of Education, the president\u8217\'20\'19s attempts to bypass the judicial system and the removal of people from the US who speak out against the administration.\par \par \uc2 He began his speech at 7pm ET on Monday night and will pass the 21-hour mark at 4pm on Tuesday. Booker has had help from Democratic colleagues, who have been asking him questions that have allowed him to have a break without yielding the floor.\par \par \uc2 Booker is getting close to the all-time Senate record. In 1957, Strom Thurmond spoke for 24 hours and 18 minutes to filibuster the Civil Rights Act of the same year.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 First lady Melania Trump spoke at the International Women of Courage Award ceremony on Tuesday where she spoke about courage as \u8220\'20\'1Ca strength that is based in love\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Trump, during a rare public appearance at the state department, recognized eight women from around the world for bravery, including an Israeli woman who was held hostage by \uc2 Hamas\uc2 . She said:\par \par \uc2 I have harnessed the power of love as a source of strength during challenging times. Love has inspired me to embrace forgiveness, nurture empathy and exhibit bravery in the face of unforeseen obstacles.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 Congressman \uc2 Jerry Nadler\uc2  condemns Trump's 'authoritarian tactics' amid 'attacks' on higher education\par \par \uc2 Congressman \uc2 Jerry Nadler\uc2 , a New York Democrat, has issued a statement strongly condemning the Trump administration for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/mar/07/trump-administration-cancels-columbia-university-funding"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cancelling $400m in federal grants and contracts to }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/mar/07/trump-administration-cancels-columbia-university-funding"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Columbia University}}}\uc2  because of what it alleged was the college\u8217\'20\'19s repeated failure to protect students from antisemitic harassment.\par \par \uc2 The administration announced on Monday that a federal antisemitism taskforce is also reviewing more than $255m in contracts between \uc2 Harvard University\uc2  and the federal government, as well as $8.7bn in grant commitments to Harvard and its affiliates.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI strongly condemn former President Trump\u8217\'20\'19s latest attacks on higher education cloaked under the guise of fighting antisemitism,\u8221\'20\'1D Nadler said in his statement on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Withholding funding from Columbia and, potentially, Harvard will not make Jewish students safer \u8230\'20\'26 Make no mistake. Trump\u8217\'20\'19s actions are not rooted in genuine concern for combatting hate.\par \par \uc2 Nadler noted that the president\u8217\'20\'19s record \u8220\'20\'1Cis stained by praise for neo-Nazis, Holocaust deniers, and white nationalists\u8221\'20\'1D, adding:\par \par \uc2 I call on our nation\u8217\'20\'19s universities to reject President Trump\u8217\'20\'19s demands and to fight back against these hostile acts. If necessary, these issues must be litigated in federal court to put an end to the illegal and unconstitutional actions taken by the Trump Administration.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 From Sam Levine in New York and Ashley Spencer in Daytona Beach, Florida:\par \par \uc2 Andrew Julius, a veteran, cast his vote for Josh Weil, a Democrat, at the John Dickerson Community Center on Tuesday in a special election to determine who will replace \uc2 Mike Waltz\uc2 , the US national security adviser.\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m actually a fan of Josh Weil. I listened to him talk. I actually went to one of his town halls a couple of weeks ago at the church and I was like, all right, he seems like an educated person. He\u8217\'20\'19s a teacher, level headed, doesn\u8217\'20\'19t have those crazy conspiracy thoughts.?And so I felt comfortable saying, okay, I can vote for this guy instead of not voting at all.\par \par \uc2 A former sonar technician in the navy, Julius said he was concerned over the recent disclosure that top Trump administration officials had used Signal to communicate about sensitive bombing plans in Yemen. He said:\par \par \uc2 I had a top secret security clearance with my job in the Navy because I was a sonar tech. So we had to have a security clearance, and if I would have done just a fraction of a mistake or what was done with this whole Signal-gate fiasco, I would have been court martialed. I would have been court martialed, kicked out of the Navy, lost rank, lost pay.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s really concerning that no one has even taken responsibility like, hey, we messed up. That was a mistake. We shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t have done that,\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 The district is solidly Republican, and the GOP candidate, \uc2 Randy Fine\uc2 , is still the favorite to win. But {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2025/03/27/trump-elise-stefanik-nomination-un"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recent polling has}}}\uc2  shown that the race may be closer than expected, prompting some Republican skittishness.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 Republican House speaker Mike Johnson tried \u8211\'20\'13 and failed \u8211\'20\'13 to block a bipartisan effort to change House rules to allow new parents in Congress to vote remotely after the birth of a child.\par \par \uc2 The House, in a 206-222 procedural vote, fell short of the votes needed to adopt a rule that included language blocking a proxy vote resolution led by Republican congresswoman Anna Paulina Luna of Florida and Democratic congresswoman Brittany Pettersen of Colorado.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf we don\u8217\'20\'19t do the right thing now, it\u8217\'20\'19ll never be done,\u8221\'20\'1D said Luna, who gave birth to her son in 2023.\par \par \uc2 Pettersen, with a diaper over her shoulder and her four-month-old son in her arms, pleaded with House colleagues. \u8220\'20\'1CIt is unfathomable that in 2025 we have not modernized Congress,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re asking you to continue to stand with us.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 Musk\u8217\'20\'19s Doge to fire all local workers and US diplomats from \uc2 USAID\uc2  - report\par \par \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s cost-cutting team is finalizing the dismantlement of the \uc2 US Agency for International Development\uc2 , ordering the firings of thousands of local workers and US diplomats and civil servants assigned to the agency overseas, two former top \uc2 USAID\uc2  officials and a source with knowledge of the situation said on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 On Friday, Congress was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/world/us/state-department-notified-congress-intent-reorganize-usaid-rubio-says-2025-03-28/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 notified}}}\uc2  that almost all of \uc2 USAID\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s own employees were being fired by September, all of its overseas offices shut, and some functions absorbed into the state department.\par \par \uc2 The latest move by Musk\u8217\'20\'19s so-called \u8220\'20\'1Cdepartment of government efficiency\u8221\'20\'1D will in effect eliminate what is left of the agency\u8217\'20\'19s workforce.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/apr/01/musk-doge-usaid-firings"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Musk\u8217\'20\'19s Doge to fire all local workers and US diplomats from USAID, sources say}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Trump administration has fired staff who were working on the Food and Drug Administration \u8217\'20\'19s bird flu response as part of its {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2025/apr/01/donald-trump-elon-musk-special-elections-florida-wisconsin-texas-arizona-us-politics-live?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with%3Ablock-67ebd9538f0842b23ea4ee9b#block-67ebd9538f0842b23ea4ee9b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 mass layoffs at the }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2025/apr/01/donald-trump-elon-musk-special-elections-florida-wisconsin-texas-arizona-us-politics-live?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with%3Ablock-67ebd9538f0842b23ea4ee9b#block-67ebd9538f0842b23ea4ee9b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Department of Health and Human Services,}}}\uc2  Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 Among those fired today were leadership and administrative staff at the FDA\u8217\'20\'19s Center for Veterinary Medicine, the news agency writes, citing a source.\par \par \uc2 The center\u8217\'20\'19s Veterinary Laboratory Investigation and Response Network tests raw pet food for bird flu. In recent weeks, the \uc2 FDA\uc2  has issued several pet food recalls after detecting bird flu contamination.\par \par \uc2 The move will bring operations at the laboratory network to a halt, the source told Reuters.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 As egg prices have reached record highs, about a third of American consumers have stopped buying them in response to the rising costs, a new study suggests.\par \par \uc2 According to research from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://clarifycapital.com/the-scramble-for-eggs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Clarify Capital}}}\uc2 , 34% of Americans have stopped purchasing eggs as prices for the breakfast staple are becoming less affordable. On average, these consumers say they won\u8217\'20\'19t begin buying eggs again until costs come down to $5 or less for a carton.\par \par \uc2 The report compared the average price of eggs across all US states, observing a significant jump in 2018, when the average was $1.49. In 2025, that figure is sitting at about $5.18.\par \par \uc2 The study found that nearly 95% of Americans have noticed the significant rise in egg prices, with shoppers reporting their perceived average as $7 a dozen. The average American said they would stop buying eggs when prices hit $8 a dozen.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/apr/01/buying-eggs-cost"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 About a third of Americans stop buying eggs due to rising costs, study shows}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 A comedian whose skit for White House reporters {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/mar/30/white-house-correspondents-dinner-cancels-comedian-appearance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was canceled}}}\uc2  for fear of upsetting \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  skewered the journalists who dropped her in a biting late-night talk show routine mocking their perceived subservience to the president.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI thought when people take away your rights, erase your history and deport your friends, you\u8217\'20\'19re supposed to call it out. But I was wrong,\u8221\'20\'1D Amber Ruffin {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rUlTIeKeTVA"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said during a brief appearance}}}\uc2  Monday on NBC\u8217\'20\'19s Late Night With Seth Meyers.\par \par \uc2 Glad to find that out now, because if they had let me give that speech, ooh baby\u8230\'20\'26 I would have been so terrifically mean.\par \par \uc2 Ruffin was dropped at the weekend from the 26 April \uc2 White House Correspondents\u8217\'20\'19 Association (WHCA)\uc2  dinner when the group decided its \u8220\'20\'1Cfocus is not on the politics of division\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 As a comedy writer for Meyers and host of her own chat show on Peacock, Ruffin has frequently mocked or criticized Trump and his actions.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/apr/01/amber-ruffin-comedian-white-house-correspondents-dinner"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Comedian dropped by White House correspondents hits back: \u8216\'20\'18I would have been so terrifically mean\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 White House press secretary defends mass layoffs after health department guts staff\par \par \uc2 When asked about more possible dismissals in the federal government, White House press secretary, Karoline Leavitt, said:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe President has given the responsibility to his Cabinet secretaries to hire and fire at their respective agencies, and they reserve that right. You saw the Secretary of \uc2 Health and Human Services\uc2  announced more layoffs today. This is all part of the administration\u8217\'20\'19s effort for a mass reduction in force in the federal bureaucracy here in Washington DC, to save American taxpayers money.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 Ashley Spencer reports on the ground from Florida:\par \par \uc2 At the Church of Christ in Daytona Beach, voters lined up to vote in Florida\u8217\'20\'19s special election to replace Rep. \uc2 Mike Waltz\uc2  after he was appointed Trump\u8217\'20\'19s national security advisor. At the church, Trump bumper stickers dotted the parking lot. But the campaign for Democratic candidate Josh Weil had a more robust table set up with flyers and resources than that of Republican \uc2 Randy Fine\uc2 , who is favored to win.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CCalling all immigrants or noncitizens \u8216\'20\'18illegal\u8217\'20\'19 or calling them \u8216\'20\'18criminals\u8217\'20\'19 is insane,\u8221\'20\'1D said Victor Valentin, who volunteered for a political campaign for the first time and on behalf of Weil. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m a Hispanic man from Puerto Rico, and those are my fellow Hispanic folks also. These are great people that come here to work hard. They come here to educate their kids.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, a Fine campaign volunteer wore a shirt with Trump\u8217\'20\'19s mugshot that said Never Surrender. The former Democrat said he supported Trump and key ally \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CI want him to do what he\u8217\'20\'19s trying to do,\u8221\'20\'1D he said of Musk. \u8220\'20\'1CAnybody who\u8217\'20\'19s not happy with him is either brainwashed or a crook.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 California attorney general \uc2 Rob Bonta\uc2  sent letters to 15 insurance companies reminding them that under AB 571, they cannot deny, cancel, or increase premiums on malpractice insurance for medical providers who offer \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , contraception, or gender-affirming care in California.\par \par \uc2 The letter sent to insurers requests proof of compliance, and Bonta also issued a general industry alert.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CCalifornia has been and remains committed to protecting the right to choose and the right of individuals to access necessary medical care,\u8221\'20\'1D said Bonta. \u8220\'20\'1CLicensed providers that offer reproductive and gender-affirming care too often face significant obstacles in securing malpractice insurance \u8212\'20\'14 the California Legislature passed, and the Governor signed into law, AB 571 to tear down those barriers.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 Leavitt was asked about the error regarding a Salvadoran national with protected legal status who was deported to El Salvador last month, despite his legal protections. The Trump administration acknowledged in court that his deportation was due to an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/apr/01/ice-error-deported-maryland-man-el-salvador"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cadministrative error\u8221\'20\'1D.}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe error you\u8217\'20\'19re referring to was a clerical error,\u8221\'20\'1D Leavitt said on Tuesday. \u8220\'20\'1CIt was an administrative error. The administration maintains the position that this individual, who was deported to El Salvador and will not be returning to our country, was a member of the brutal and vicious MS-13 gang.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 White House press secretary teases Trump's Wednesday tariff announcement\par \par \uc2 In Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s press briefing, White House press secretary Karoline Leavitt addressed the deaths of four US soldiers in Lithuania, the US southern border, and a new tariffs announcement slated for tomorrow:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is obviously a very big day,\u8221\'20\'1D Leavitt said. \u8220\'20\'1CHe is with his trade and tariff team right now, perfecting it to make sure this is a perfect deal for the American people and the American worker, and you will all find out in about 24 hours from now.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump is expected to impose sweeping tariffs on US imports on Wednesday, which he has called \u8220\'20\'1Cliberation day\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Summary of the day so far\par \par \uc2 New Jersey senator \uc2 Cory Booker\uc2  is about to enter the 17th hour of his marathon overnight speech on the Senate floor to warn of what he called the \u8220\'20\'1Cgrave and urgent\u8221\'20\'1D danger that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s presidential administration poses to democracy and the American people. Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is happening today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 US voters are headed to the polls in Wisconsin and Florida in elections that some see as a test of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 s popularity and the political clout of \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 . The most closely watched contest is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/mar/29/wisconsin-supreme-court-race-elon-musk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a battle for a seat }}}\uc2  on Wisconsin\u8217\'20\'19s seven-member supreme court.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 US attorney general Pam Bondi announced that she has directed federal prosecutors to seek the death penalty for Luigi Mangione, the man accused of murdering UnitedHealthcare CEO \uc2 Brian Thompson\uc2  outside a Manhattan hotel in December.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Thousands of Health and Human Services (\uc2 HHS\uc2 ) employees across the country are being dismissed as the Trump administration began implementing its controversial workforce reduction plan, which could ultimately remove 10,000 staff from the department through forced layoffs.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A group of Democratic-led states have sued the Trump administration over its decision to cut $11bn in federal funds that they were allocated during the Covid-19 pandemic.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Republican House speaker Mike Johnson brushed off Trump\u8217\'20\'19s suggestion that he could run for a third term, adding that \u8220\'20\'1Cthe president and I have talked about this, joked about it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive health\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  said the Trump administration would cut federal family planning funding as of Tuesday, affecting birth control, cancer screenings and other services for low-income people.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 The White House said \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will deliver remarks at a \u8220\'20\'1CMake America Wealthy Again\u8221\'20\'1D event on Wednesday at 4pm ET from the White House Rose Garden.\par \par \uc2 Trump is expected to unveil a swathe of reciprocal tariffs at the event tomorrow, which he has called \u8220\'20\'1CLiberation Day\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 White House press secretary Karoline Leavitt told reporters on Monday that the goal would be to announce \u8220\'20\'1Ccountry-based tariffs\u8221\'20\'1D, although Trump has remained committed to imposing separate sector-specific charges.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 Attorney general Pam Bondi directs prosecutors to seek death penalty against Luigi Mangione\par \par \uc2 US attorney general Pam Bondi announced that she has directed federal prosecutors to seek the death penalty for Luigi Mangione, the man accused of murdering UnitedHealthcare CEO \uc2 Brian Thompson\uc2  outside a Manhattan hotel in December.\par \par \uc2 A statement by Bondi reads:\par \par \uc2 Luigi Mangione\u8217\'20\'19s murder of \uc2 Brian Thompson\uc2  \u8212\'20\'14 an innocent man and father of two young children \u8212\'20\'14 was a premeditated, cold-blooded assassination that shocked America. After careful consideration, I have directed federal prosecutors to seek the death penalty in this case as we carry out President Trump\u8217\'20\'19s agenda to stop violent crime and Make America Safe Again.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 The top Democrat on the House armed services committee says he is not confident that the defense department will get to the bottom of the Signal group chat where senior \uc2 US government\uc2  officials discussed plans to bomb Yemen in front of a journalist.\par \par \uc2 Last week, the top Democrat and Republican on the Senate armed services committee {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/mar/27/signal-investigation-bipartisan-letter"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 requested}}}\uc2  the defense department (DOD) inspector general investigate the chat.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s unclear if that inquiry has started, but Democratic congressman \uc2 Adam Smith\uc2  said he did not think the department\u8217\'20\'19s independent watchdog was up to the task.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPresident Trump fired all of the inspector generals, as we know, including the one at DOD, and I think he made it very clear what he expected out of them\u8221\'20\'1D, Smith told a press conference at the Capitol, referring to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/25/trump-fires-17-independent-watchdogs-government-agencies"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 one of the first moves}}}\uc2  the president took after being sworn in.\par \par \uc2 Is the inspector general\u8217\'20\'19s process going to be legitimate in light of the Trump administration\u8217\'20\'19s clear effort to fire people who don\u8217\'20\'19t give them the answers they want? I think the answer to that question is highly in doubt.\par \par \uc2 The inspector general\u8217\'20\'19s investigation would likely be the only one to happen anytime soon. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , along with senior officials on the group chat including defense secretary Pete Hegseth and national security adviser \uc2 Michael Waltz\uc2 , have denied any wrongdoing, and Congress\u8217\'20\'19s Republican leadership appears disinterested in pressing the matter further.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 From Jenny Peek in Madison, Wisconsin, where voting is under way {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/apr/01/wisconsin-florida-voters-elections-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  in an election}}}\uc2  that will decide majority control of the state\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court:\par \par \uc2 Voters streamed into Olbrich Botanical Gardens in Madison, Wisconsin on Tuesday morning. It\u8217\'20\'19s the state\u8217\'20\'19s capital city and a Democratic stronghold.\par \par \uc2 Jeannine Ramsey, 65, said it\u8217\'20\'19s her civic duty to vote, and she does so in every election.\par \par \uc2 The Madison resident voted for liberal-backed candidate Susan Crawford shortly before 9am. She said the \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 -supported \uc2 Brad Schimel\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t rule fairly on the issues most important to her.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think it\u8217\'20\'19s shameful that \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  can come here and spend millions of dollars and try to bribe the citizens,\u8221\'20\'1D Ramsey said.\par \par \uc2 I don\u8217\'20\'19t think it should be allowed. He doesn\u8217\'20\'19t live in our state, and I don\u8217\'20\'19t think he should be able to buy this election. It makes me angry.\par \par \uc2 Ramsey pointed to redistricting, the state\u8217\'20\'19s civil rights era \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban and collective bargaining as major issues the Wisconsin supreme court could hear in the coming months. And despite living in a liberal city, she\u8217\'20\'19s cautious about getting her hopes up.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI live in a very blue bubble and I\u8217\'20\'19ve been very disappointed in the past,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 I thought I knew what people were thinking and feeling, and I was really surprised that people would send a convicted felon back into the presidential office.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 Nearly two dozen states sue Trump administration over decision to rescind billions in health funding\par \par \uc2 A group of Democratic-led states have sued the Trump administration over its decision to cut $11bn in federal funds that they were allocated during the Covid-19 pandemic.\par \par \uc2 In the lawsuit, attorneys general and governors from 23 states and the District of Columbia argue that \uc2 Department of Health and Human Services\uc2  lacks the authority to unilaterally claw back funding the states had already built health programs around.\par \par \uc2 The \u8220\'20\'1Csudden and reckless cuts violate federal law, jeopardize public health, and will have devastating consequences for communities nationwide,\u8221\'20\'1D the lawsuit writes.\par \par \uc2 The lawsuit asks the court to immediately stop the Trump administration from rescinding the money, which was allocated by Congress during the pandemic and mostly used for Covid-related efforts such as testing and vaccination, Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 House Speaker Mike Johnson says he and Trump have 'joked' about running for third term\par \par \uc2 At a press conference in the Capitol, Republican House speaker Mike Johnson brushed off \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s suggestion that he could run for a third term.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s a constitutional path. You have to amend the constitution to do it, and that\u8217\'20\'19s a high bar,\u8221\'20\'1D Johnson said, adding that \u8220\'20\'1Cthe president and I have talked about this, joked about it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe take him at his word,\u8221\'20\'1D Johnson continued, before downplaying the possibility that any change to the constitution would succeed.\par \par \uc2 I understand why so many Americans do wish that he could run for a third term, because he\u8217\'20\'19s accomplishing so much in this first 100 days that they wish it could go on for much longer. But I think he recognizes the constitutional limitations, and I\u8217\'20\'19m not sure that there\u8217\'20\'19s a move about to amend the constitution.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 Democratic Senate minority leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  praised Senator \uc2 Cory Booker\uc2  for his \u8220\'20\'1Cstrength\u8221\'20\'1D, \u8220\'20\'1Cfortitude\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cclarity\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAll of America is paying attention to what you\u8217\'20\'19re saying,\u8221\'20\'1D Schumer said during his question to Booker, adding:\par \par \uc2 Our whole caucus is behind you. We admire your stamina, your strength, your passion, your intelligence.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 Some of Senator \uc2 Cory Booker\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s fellow Democrats have helped support him during his monologues, with several asking questions that have allowed Booker to have a break without yielding the floor.\par \par \uc2 Democratic Senate minority leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  was the first to pose a question to his New Jersey colleague, and he praised Booker for his \u8220\'20\'1Cstrength and conviction\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou\u8217\'20\'19re taking the floor tonight to bring up all these inequities that will hurt people, that will so hurt the middle class, that will so hurt poor people, that will hurt America, hurt our fiscal conditions, as you document,\u8221\'20\'1D Schumer said in his own question to Booker.\par \par \uc2 Just give us a little inkling of the strength \u8211\'20\'13 give us a little feeling for the strength and conviction that drive you to do this unusual taking of the floor for a long time to let the people know how bad these things are going to be.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 Booker's Senate floor speech stretches into 15th hour\par \par \uc2 Senator \uc2 Cory Booker\uc2 , whose marathon overnight speech on the Senate floor began at 7pm last night and is still happening, warned of what he called the \u8220\'20\'1Cgrave and urgent\u8221\'20\'1D that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s administration poses to democracy and the American people.\par \par \uc2 Booker decried the Trump administration\u8217\'20\'19s spending cuts, its attempt to abolish the Department of Education, the president\u8217\'20\'19s attempts to bypass the judicial system and the removal of people from the US who speak out against the administration.\par \par \uc2 Booker\u8217\'20\'19s speech has been supported with reams of quotes from speeches by the late American politicians \uc2 John McCain\uc2  and John Lewis, as well as excerpts from newspaper articles.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 Senator \uc2 Amy Klobuchar\uc2 , a Minnesota Democrat, said \uc2 Cory Booker\uc2  was \u8220\'20\'1Cgiving people hope\u8221\'20\'1D and that her colleague was \u8220\'20\'1Can alarm clock right now for this country\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve seen people realize this isn\u8217\'20\'19t a bunch of campaign rhetoric that\u8217\'20\'19s going on,\u8221\'20\'1D Klobuchar said as Booker yielded for a question on the Senate floor.\par \par \uc2 People are stepping up. They\u8217\'20\'19re fighting it in the courts. They\u8217\'20\'19re fighting it in Congress.\par \par \uc2 She praised Senator Booker for \u8220\'20\'1Cstanding in a snowstorm\u8221\'20\'1D. \u8220\'20\'1CYou\u8217\'20\'19re the kind of person that gives me strength,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 Senator Raphael Warnock said he was \u8220\'20\'1Cvery proud\u8221\'20\'1D of his Democratic colleague, \uc2 Cory Booker\uc2 , for his marathon speech on the Senate floor.\par \par \uc2 Warnock, speaking as Booker yielded for a question, said he had fought to expand Medicaid in his state of Georgia. The Trump administration is not working for ordinary people, he said.\par \par \uc2 The administration is working for billionaires. They\u8217\'20\'19re working for people like \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 Senator \uc2 Cory Booker\uc2  thanked his Minnesota colleague \uc2 Tina Smith{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2025/apr/01/donald-trump-elon-musk-special-elections-florida-wisconsin-texas-arizona-us-politics-live?page=with%3Ablock-67ebe3878f0842b23ea4ef2c#block-67ebe3878f0842b23ea4ef2c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  for her question,}}}\uc2  saying she \u8220\'20\'1Cwades into some difficult waters\u8221\'20\'1D. He said he had read \u8220\'20\'1Chorrible stories, painful stories\u8221\'20\'1D about people \u8220\'20\'1Ctrapped\u8221\'20\'1D in the immigration system that were a \u8220\'20\'1Cbetrayal of American values\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Booker said the Trump administration was \u8220\'20\'1Cviolating the very first words\u8221\'20\'1D of the constitution. He said:\par \par \uc2 [\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 ] wants to take power from our Congress. And the thing that is killing me, that is actually breaking my heart, is that we\u8217\'20\'19re letting him take our power.\par \par \uc2 On the subject of foreign policy, Booker said Trump had left US allies feeling \u8220\'20\'1Cabandoned\u8221\'20\'1D, \u8220\'20\'1Cdegraded\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cinsulted\u8221\'20\'1D while leaving its adversaries \u8220\'20\'1Cemboldened\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In the short time President Trump has been in office for his second term, Americans have already been put in harm\u8217\'20\'19s way because of the reckless approach of the administration.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 Senator \uc2 Tina Smith\uc2 , a Minnesota Democrat, accused \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  of using the immigration system \u8220\'20\'1Cas a tool to restrict first amendment freedoms, to subvert due process and to further weaken America\u8217\'20\'19s global standing\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Smith, speaking as Senator \uc2 Cory Booker\uc2  yielded for a question on the Senate floor, said Trump was \u8220\'20\'1Cseek(ing) to emulate the authoritarian regimes that he so openly admires\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 She noted the number of international students targeted for arrest and deportation in recent weeks because of their participation in protests in support of Palestine.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese are young people who play by all the rules,\u8221\'20\'1D Smith said.\par \par \uc2 Their views on the war in Gaza may differ sharply from mine or others, but I believe that the first amendment guarantees them the right to express those views without facing punishment or reprisal from our government.\par \par \uc2 She said the arrests had been carried out in a manner \u8220\'20\'1Cthat seems calculated to maximize fear and intimidation in immigrant and activist communities\u8221\'20\'1D. Smith said:\par \par \uc2 Does punishing people for their political speech seem consistent with American democratic values? I can\u8217\'20\'19t believe that.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 Senator \uc2 Cory Booker\uc2 , who is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2025/apr/01/donald-trump-elon-musk-special-elections-florida-wisconsin-texas-arizona-us-politics-live?page=with%3Ablock-67ebd05a8f08e27e07d376e7#block-67ebd05a8f08e27e07d376e7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 now more than 13 hours into his marathon speech}}}\uc2  on the Senate floor, accused the Trump administration and Republicans in Congress of \u8220\'20\'1Cputting profits over people\u8221\'20\'1D. Booker said:\par \par \uc2 They are trying to gut Medicaid and Medicare, programs on which nearly a third of our country rely \u8211\'20\'13 all to pay for tax cuts to billionaires and corporations.\par \par \uc2 Booker also said social security \u8220\'20\'1Cis not the government\u8217\'20\'19s money to spend\u8221\'20\'1D but the \u8220\'20\'1Chard-earned savings of working Americans that belongs to Americans,\u8221\'20\'1D adding:\par \par \uc2 [Donald] Trump and [ Elon] Musk need to keep their hands off of money that isn\u8217\'20\'19t theirs to take.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 Staff at the \uc2 US Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC)\uc2  and the Food and Drug Administration (\uc2 FDA\uc2 ) have started receiving notice that their jobs are being cut, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 The news agency, citing an \uc2 FDA\uc2  employee, reports that staff on Tuesday morning had to present their badges at the building entrance and those who had been fired were given a ticket and told to return home.\par \par \uc2 Fired staff at the CDC worked for the \uc2 National Center for Environmental Health\uc2 , \uc2 Substance Abuse and Mental Health Services Administration (SAMHSA)\uc2  and National Center for Immunization and Respiratory Diseases (NCIRD), it says.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 Mass layoffs begin at federal health agencies\par \par \uc2 Some employees at federal health agencies began receiving notices of dismissal on Tuesday morning, according to reports, days after the \uc2 US department of health\uc2  and human services (\uc2 HHS\uc2 ) announced it planned to cut 10,000 full-time jobs.\par \par \uc2 An email addressed to an employee at the \uc2 US Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC)\uc2 , obtained by CNN, reads:\par \par \uc2 This action does not reflect directly on your service, performance or conduct.\par \par \uc2 The email states that the person would be placed on administrative leave and would no longer have access to building as of Tuesday, the outlet reports.\par \par \uc2 HHS\uc2  secretary Robert F Kennedy announced the planned cuts as part of a sweeping organization of the department which, through its agencies, is responsible for tracking health trends and disease outbreaks, conducting and funding medical research, and monitoring the safety of food and medicine, as well as for administering health insurance programs for nearly half of the country, Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 The layoffs are expected to shrink \uc2 HHS\uc2  to 62,000 positions, lopping off nearly a quarter of its staff \u8211\'20\'13 10,000 jobs through layoffs and another 10,000 workers who took early retirement and voluntary separation offers, according to the news agency.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 Rightwing groups around the US are pushing legislation that would place new limits on what books are allowed in school libraries in a move that critics decry as censorship often focused on LGBTQ+ issues, race or imposing conservative social values.\par \par \uc2 Caught up in the attempts at suppressing books are classics like The Color Purple and Slaughterhouse-Five.\par \par \uc2 Opponents of such bills argue that they would actually hinder individual rights because the proponents would be imposing their beliefs on parents and children who do not share their views. Those campaigning for the restrictions say it would prevent children from being exposed to what they label {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2025/03/22/us/alabama-library-defunded-book-bans-hnk/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sexually explicit}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.heraldtribune.com/story/news/politics/2025/03/24/florida-book-bans-bill-defines-nudity-sexual-content-porniography-harmful-minors/82632778007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 obscene content}}}\uc2  and increase parental rights.\par \par \uc2 There are at least 112 proposed state bills concerning school \u8211\'20\'13 and public \u8211\'20\'13 libraries that seek to expand the definition of what is deemed obscene or \u8220\'20\'1Charmful to minors\u8221\'20\'1D and to limit librarian staff\u8217\'20\'19s ability to determine which books are in their collections, according to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ala.org/advocacy/adverse-legislation-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 American Library Association}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/apr/01/new-book-bans-library-schools"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Rightwing groups across US push new bans to limit \u8216\'20\'18obscene\u8217\'20\'19 books in libraries}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 Democratic senator \uc2 Cory Booker\uc2  holds marathon speech to highlight 'recklessness' of Trump policies\par \par \uc2 Senator \uc2 Cory Booker\uc2  has been giving a marathon speech on the Senate floor that has lasted into the early hours of Tuesday morning, highlighting what he described as the \u8220\'20\'1Crecklessness\u8221\'20\'1D of the Trump administration.\par \par \uc2 The New Jersey Democrat began his address on Monday night and said he would continue to speak for as long as he could \u8220\'20\'1Cphysically endure\u8221\'20\'1D. By 7.30am ET, Booker was still going.\par \par \uc2 The focus of his remarks are concerns over president Trump\u8217\'20\'19s proposed cuts to programs like Medicaid.\par \par \uc2 At the start of his speech, Booker said:\par \par \uc2 I rise with the intention of disrupting the normal business of the \uc2 United States Senate\uc2  for as long as I am physically able. I rise tonight because I believe sincerely that our nation is in crisis.\par \par \uc2 He went on:\par \par \uc2 In just 71 days, the president of the United States has inflicted so much harm on Americans\u8217\'20\'19 safety, financial stability, the core foundations of our democracy and even our aspirations as a people for \u8211\'20\'13 from our highest offices \u8211\'20\'13 a sense of common decency.\par \par \uc2 These are not normal times in America, and they should not be treated as such.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 US voters are headed to the polls on Tuesday in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/wisconsin"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Wisconsin}}}\uc2  and Florida in elections that some see as a test of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s popularity and the political clout of his billionaire ally \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The most closely watched contest is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/mar/29/wisconsin-supreme-court-race-elon-musk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a battle for a seat }}}\uc2  on Wisconsin\u8217\'20\'19s seven-member supreme court. Conservatives are trying to flip ideological control of the court, which currently has a 4-3 liberal majority. The contest, which features liberal judge Susan Crawford facing off against conservative \uc2 Brad Schimel\uc2 , will have huge consequences in the state.\par \par \uc2 The supreme court is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/mar/31/wisconsin-abortion-state-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 set to determine the future of \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/wisconsin-union-supreme-court-collective-bargaining-ead7ad7e8c2187eb87197f002090755c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 collective bargaining rights}}}\uc2 . The court could also ultimately require the state legislature to redraw the state\u8217\'20\'19s eight congressional districts, which are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://planscore.org/plan.html?20220307T032625.619130097Z"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 heavily distorted}}}\uc2  in favor of Republicans, who control six of them.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/apr/01/wisconsin-florida-voters-elections-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Wisconsin and Florida voters head to polls in test of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s popularity}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 A \uc2 Cornell University\uc2  student who participated in pro-Palestinian protests and was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/mar/21/ice-cornell-university-student-sued-trump-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 asked to surrender by United States immigration officials}}}\uc2  has said he is leaving the US, citing fear of detention and threats to his personal safety.\par \par \uc2 Momodou Taal, a doctoral candidate in Africana studies and dual citizen of the UK and the Gambia, has participated in pro-Palestinian protests against Israel\u8217\'20\'19s war in Gaza after the October 2023 \uc2 Hamas\uc2  attack. His attorneys said last month that he was asked to turn himself in and that his student visa was being revoked.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has pledged to deport foreign pro-Palestinian protesters and accused them of supporting the militant group \uc2 Hamas\uc2 , being antisemitic and posing foreign policy hurdles.\par \par \uc2 Protesters, including some Jewish groups, say the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/trump-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump administration}}}\uc2  wrongly conflates their criticism of Israel and support for Palestinian rights with antisemitism and support for \uc2 Hamas\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Last year, Taal was in a group of activists who disrupted a career fair on campus that featured weapons manufacturers and the university thereafter ordered him to study remotely. He previously posted online that \u8220\'20\'1Ccolonised peoples have the right to resist by any means necessary\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Taal filed a lawsuit in mid-March to block deportations of protesters, a bid that was denied by a judge last week.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/apr/01/momodou-taal-pro-palestine-cornell-student-leaving-us-detention-fears"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pro-Palestinian British Cornell student says he will leave US citing fear of detention}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive health\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  said the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/trump-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump administration}}}\uc2  would cut federal family planning funding as of Tuesday, affecting birth control, cancer screenings and other services for low-income people.\par \par \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  said that nine of its affiliates received notice that funding would be withheld under a program known as Title X, which has supported healthcare services for poor people since 1970.\par \par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal reported last week the US Department of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/health"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Health}}}\uc2  and Human Services planned an immediate freeze of $27.5m in family planning grants for groups including \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  says more than 300 health centers are in the Title X network and Title X-funded centers received more than 1.5m visits in 2023. It did not say how much funding would be halted by the Trump administration.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/mar/31/trump-planned-parenthood"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump officials to cut Planned Parenthood family planning funds}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Large majority of Europeans support retaliatory tariffs against US, poll finds\par \par \uc2 A large majority of western Europeans support retaliatory tariffs against the US, a survey has shown, if {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  introduces sweeping import duties for major trading partners as expected this week.\par \par \uc2 The US president appears likely to unleash a range of tariffs, varying from country to country, on Wednesday, which he has called Liberation Day. He also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/mar/26/trump-new-car-tariffs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said last week}}}\uc2  that a 25% levy on cars shipped to the US would come into force the next day.\par \par \uc2 Many European firms are likely to be hit hard. Some, including Germany\u8217\'20\'19s car manufacturers and France\u8217\'20\'19s luxury goods firms and wine, champagne and spirits makers, rely on exports to the US for up to 20% of their income.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 EU\uc2  has already pledged a \u8220\'20\'1Ctimely, robust and calibrated\u8221\'20\'1D response to Washington\u8217\'20\'19s plans, which experts predict are likely to depress output, drive up prices and fuel a trade war. Global markets and the dollar {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/live/2025/mar/31/world-markets-us-dollar-worst-month-2022-trump-trade-war-tariffs-investors-business-live-news"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fell on Monday}}}\uc2  after Trump crushed hopes that what he calls \u8220\'20\'1Creciprocal tariffs\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 arguing that trading partners are cheating the US \u8211\'20\'13 would only target countries with the largest trade imbalances.\par \par \uc2 A \uc2 YouGov\uc2  survey carried out in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/denmark"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Denmark}}}\uc2 , France, Germany, Italy, Spain, Sweden and the UK found that if the US tariffs went ahead, large majorities \u8211\'20\'13 ranging from 79% of respondents in Denmark to 56% in Italy \u8211\'20\'13 favoured retaliatory levies on US imports.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/apr/01/large-majority-of-europeans-support-retaliatory-tariffs-against-us-poll-finds"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Large majority of Europeans support retaliatory tariffs against US, poll finds}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.42am BST\par \par \uc2 As \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  prepared to unveil a swathe of reciprocal tariffs, global markets braced and some Republican senators voiced their opposition to a strategy that critics warn risks a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2025/mar/17/donald-trump-trade-wars-global-growth-inflation-oecd-uk-tariffs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 global trade war,}}}\uc2  provoking retaliation by major trading partners such as China, Canada and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/mar/29/italian-pm-calls-for-reasoned-approach-to-escalating-tariff-war-between-eu-and-us"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the European Union}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The US president said on Monday he would be \u8220\'20\'1Cvery kind\u8221\'20\'1D to trading partners when he unveils further tariffs this week, potentially as early as Tuesday night.\par \par \uc2 The Republican billionaire insists that reciprocal action is needed because the world\u8217\'20\'19s biggest economy has been \u8220\'20\'1Cripped off by every country in the world\u8221\'20\'1D, promising \u8220\'20\'1CLiberation Day\u8221\'20\'1D for the US.\par \par \uc2 He could also unveil more sector-specific levies.\par \par \uc2 Asked for details, he told reporters on Monday: \u8220\'20\'1CYou\u8217\'20\'19re going to see in two days, which is maybe tomorrow night or probably Wednesday.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But he added: \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re going to be very nice, relatively speaking, we\u8217\'20\'19re going to be very kind.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/apr/01/donald-trump-us-reciprocal-tariffs-trading-partners"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump prepares to unveil reciprocal tariffs as markets brace amid trade war fears}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.29am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump aides draft proposal for at least 20% tariffs on most imports to US, \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  reports\par \par \uc2 White House aides have drafted a proposal to impose tariffs of about 20% on most imports to the United States, the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  reported on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s team is mulling using trillions of dollars in new import revenue for a tax dividend or refund, the report said, citing sources.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.18am BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s executive order seeking to overhaul the nation\u8217\'20\'19s elections faced its first legal challenges on Monday as the \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2  and a pair of non-profits filed two separate lawsuits calling it unconstitutional.\par \par \uc2 The Campaign Legal Center and the State Democracy Defenders Fund brought the first lawsuit Monday afternoon. The DNC, the Democratic Governors Association and Senate and House Democratic leaders followed soon after with a complaint of their own.\par \par \uc2 Both lawsuits filed in the US district court for the District of Columbia ask the court to block Trump\u8217\'20\'19s order and declare it illegal.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe president\u8217\'20\'19s executive order is an unlawful action that threatens to uproot our tried-and-tested election systems and silence potentially millions of Americans,\u8221\'20\'1D said Danielle Lang, senior director of voting rights at the DC-based Campaign Legal Center.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is simply not within the president\u8217\'20\'19s authority to set election rules by executive decree, especially when they would restrict access to voting in this way.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The White House did not respond to a request for comment.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/mar/31/democrats-sue-trump-elections"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats sue Trump over \u8216\'20\'18unlawful\u8217\'20\'19 plan to overhaul US elections}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.06am BST\par \par \uc2 Control of the Wisconsin supreme court at stake in race that broke records for spending\par \par \uc2 Majority control of the Wisconsin supreme court will be decided on Tuesday in a race that broke records for spending and has become a proxy battle for the nation\u8217\'20\'19s political fights, pitting a candidate backed by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  against a Democratic-aligned challenger.\par \par \uc2 Republicans including Trump and the world\u8217\'20\'19s wealthiest person, \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 , lined up behind \uc2 Brad Schimel\uc2 , a former state attorney general. Democrats like \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  and billionaire megadonor \uc2 George Soros\uc2  backed Susan Crawford, a Dane County judge who led legal fights to protect union power and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and to oppose voter ID.\par \par \uc2 The first major election in the country since November is seen as a litmus test of how voters feel about Trump\u8217\'20\'19s first months back in office and the role played by Musk, whose \u8220\'20\'1Cdepartment of government efficiency\u8221\'20\'1D has torn through federal agencies and laid off thousands of workers, AP reported. Musk traveled to Wisconsin on Sunday to make a pitch for Schimel and personally hand out $1m checks to two voters.\par \par \uc2 On Monday, Trump hinted as to why the outcome of the race was important. The court can decide election-related laws and settle disputes over future election outcomes.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWisconsin\u8217\'20\'19s a big state politically, and the supreme court has a lot to do with elections in Wisconsin,\u8221\'20\'1D he told reporters in the Oval Office. \u8220\'20\'1CWinning Wisconsin\u8217\'20\'19s a big deal, so therefore the supreme court choice \u8211\'20\'13 it\u8217\'20\'19s a big race.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Crawford embraced the backing of \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  and other \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights advocates, running ads that highlighted Schimel\u8217\'20\'19s opposition to the procedure. She also attacked Schimel for his ties to Trump and Musk, referring to \u8220\'20\'1CElon Schimel\u8221\'20\'1D during a debate.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.51am BST\par \par \uc2 Oliver Stone to testify at \uc2 John F Kennedy\uc2  assassination hearing\par \par \uc2 Film director Oliver Stone will testify at a US {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/house-of-representatives"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 House of Representatives}}}\uc2  hearing on Tuesday that is considering thousands of pages of documents related to the 1963 assassination of \uc2 John F Kennedy\uc2  released this month at \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s direction .\par \par \uc2 Representative Anna Paulina Luna, chair of the Task Force on the Declassification of Federal Secrets, said that lawmakers will hear from witnesses about the value of the documents.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBy investigating the newly released JFK files, consulting experts, and tracking down surviving staff of various investigative committees, our task force will get to the bottom of this mystery and share our findings with the American people,\u8221\'20\'1D Luna said.\par \par \uc2 Shortly after taking office for his second term in January, Trump signed an executive order directing national intelligence and other officials to quickly come up with a plan for the full and complete release of all records relating to President Kennedy\u8217\'20\'19s assassination.\par \par \uc2 The archives\u8217\'20\'19 Kennedy assassination collection has more than 6m pages of records, the vast majority of which had been declassified and made public before Trump\u8217\'20\'19s order. Kennedy\u8217\'20\'19s murder has been attributed to lone gunman Lee Harvey Oswald.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/film/2025/mar/31/oliver-stone-testify-john-f-kennedy-assassination-hearing-jfk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Oliver Stone to testify at John F Kennedy assassination hearing}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.43am BST\par \par \uc2 Special elections to deliver voters\u8217\'20\'19 verdict on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s chaotic first months\par \par \uc2 Good morning and welcome to the US politics live blog. I\u8217\'20\'19m Tom Ambrose and I will be bringing you all the latest news lines over the next few hours.\par \par \uc2 We start with news that several elections today will be a crucial test of the popularity of the chaotic and extremist first two months of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s second term and the clout of his close ally, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/elon-musk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Elon Musk}}}\uc2 , the world\u8217\'20\'19s richest man who has been tasked with radically reforming the \uc2 US federal government\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 They could also offer a glimmer of hope to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 fresh off a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/mar/26/james-malone-democrat-pennsylvania-state-senate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 surprise upset win}}}\uc2  in a local race in Pennsylvania last week \u8211\'20\'13 that their divided political party could be seeing a resurgence in its fortunes.\par \par \uc2 Or, if they fail to land further blows on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans}}}\uc2 , it will be yet another sign that the party is destined for a long period in the wilderness amid {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nationalreview.com/corner/democrats-are-more-unpopular-than-ever/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 historic lows}}}\uc2  of its popularity in recent polls.\par \par \uc2 Many eyes are focused on two previously Republican-held congressional seats in Florida, where its sixth and first congressional districts are vacant and up for grabs.\par \par \uc2 Mike Waltz\uc2  left to take up a cabinet job for Trump and \uc2 Matt Gaetz{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/13/trump-matt-gaetz-attorney-general"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 resigned}}}\uc2  to pursue a failed bid to become attorney general. House Republicans currently hold a razor-thin majority over Democrats, 218 to 213, with four seats vacant, in the lower chamber of Congress.\par \par \uc2 Republican nerves about how tight the House could become were emphasized last week after Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/mar/27/trump-withdraws-elise-stefanik-nomination-gop-house-majority"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pulled the nomination}}}\uc2  of New York congresswoman \uc2 Elise Stefanik\uc2  to be United Nations ambassador \u8211\'20\'13 a move widely seen as admitting that marginal Republican districts are at risk of being lost.\par \par \uc2 It is the old district of Waltz, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/mar/27/trump-fire-waltz-signal-atlantic-leak"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 embattled national security adviser}}}\uc2 , that is most at risk. State senator \uc2 Randy Fine\uc2  has lagged behind his Democratic opponent, Josh Weil, in fundraising amid {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2025/03/26/fine-weil-florida-special-election-00249679"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 concerns that he could lose the district}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 though such a defeat is far from certain.\par \par \uc2 Read my colleague Richard Luscombe\u8217\'20\'19s full report on the elections here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/mar/30/special-elections-trump-test"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Special elections to deliver voters\u8217\'20\'19 verdict on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s chaotic first months}}}\par \par \uc2 In other news:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump said Wednesday will be \u8220\'20\'1CLiberation Day\u8221\'20\'1D when he announces reciprocal tariffs on nearly all US trading partners. Global stock markets were a sea of red on Monday and investors fled to gold amid recession fears.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/trump-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump administration}}}\uc2  has announced a review of federal contracts and grants at \uc2 Harvard University\uc2  over allegations of antisemitism.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Senate majority leader \uc2 John Thune\uc2  said he believes \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is \u8220\'20\'1Cprobably messing with you\u8221\'20\'1D with his remarks on Sunday that there are \u8220\'20\'1Cmethods\u8221\'20\'1D by which he could run for a third term.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A coalition of civil rights groups filed a lawsuit on Monday seeking to block portions of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/mar/25/trump-executive-order-voter-registration-immigration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump\u8217\'20\'19s executive order}}}\uc2  that would require voters to prove their citizenship in order to vote.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump took aim at ticket scalping in a new executive order signed today, which directs the Department of Justice and the \uc2 FTC\uc2  to crack down on ticket resellers who price-gouge.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Tens of millions of dollars is being withheld from \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  chapters across the US in an attempt by the Trump administration to force the clinics to change their operations.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A federal judge has put the Trump administration plans to deport hundreds of thousands of Venezuelan immigrants on pause, ruling Monday that protections struck down by officials should be reinstated while lawsuits continue.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250401el410018k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
