\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Wisconsin supreme court race a litmus test for \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s political power\b0\par\par\uc2 Sam Levine \par \uc2 1,593 \uc2 words\par \uc2 31 March 2025\par 13:49 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The high-stakes race will determine which party will control a court that will rule on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and voting rights\par \par \uc2 A race to determine control of the Wisconsin supreme court that has profound stakes for voting, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and labor rights in the state, is also shaping up to be a litmus test of \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s political power, making it one of the most consequential elections of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s second term.\par \par \uc2 Liberals currently hold a 4-3 majority on the state supreme court, but the liberal justice Ann Walsh Bradley is retiring. Susan Crawford, a liberal judge, is facing off on Tuesday against the conservative judge \uc2 Brad Schimel\uc2  for the seat. The winner will determine which party has control of a court that is set to rule on the future of the state\u8217\'20\'19s 1849 \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/wisconsin-union-supreme-court-collective-bargaining-ead7ad7e8c2187eb87197f002090755c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 collective bargaining rights}}}\uc2  and the makeup of the state\u8217\'20\'19s eight congressional districts.\par \par \uc2 The election has become the most expensive judicial election in American history, with more than $80m spent on both sides so far. Musk began spending in the race earlier this year, shortly after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/tesla-musk-wisconsin-supreme-court-dealerships-101d7608d69dda61aeaf6ebee7903d2b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tesla filed a lawsuit}}}\uc2  challenging a Wisconsin law that blocks the company from opening car dealerships in the state.\par \par \uc2 The billionaire\u8217\'20\'19s Super Pac is offering $100 to those who sign a petition in opposition to \u8220\'20\'1Cactivist judges\u8221\'20\'1D. So far, Musk and groups he funds have spent more than $20m in the race. On Friday, he posted on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 /X and said he would campaign in Wisconsin this weekend and give away $1m as part of a sweepstakes-like contest to people who had voted. He later deleted the post after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://electionlawblog.org/?p=149196"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 experts pointed out}}}\uc2  such a program could be illegal under state law. He posted a revised tweet saying he would distribute the money to people {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/elonmusk/status/1905673297439666486"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to act as spokespeople}}}\uc2  for the petition. The Wisconsin attorney general, \uc2 Josh Kaul\uc2 , a Democrat, also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wisdoj.gov/PressReleases/kaul-v-musk-summons-complaint.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sued Musk}}}\uc2  and his Pac on Friday to stop the giveaway, though an appeals court reportedly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.jsonline.com/story/news/politics/elections/2025/03/29/wisconsin-court-rejects-effort-to-block-elon-musk-voter-payments/82721261007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 declined}}}\uc2  to immediately step in and stop it.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is kind of a test case for \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D Crawford, a former prosecutor, said in an interview. \u8220\'20\'1CHe wants to make sure that nothing stands in the way of what he\u8217\'20\'19s doing to try to dismantle the federal government.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Schimel\u8217\'20\'19s campaign did not respond to an interview request.\par \par \uc2 Musk\u8217\'20\'19s entrance in the race comes as he has railed against federal judges who have threatened to halt Trump\u8217\'20\'19s agenda, calling for the impeachment of some and backing Republicans who have heeded the call.\par \par \uc2 So much money being spent in a state supreme court election would have been unthinkable even a decade ago. Wisconsin supreme court justices are elected to 10 year terms, and until recently the candidates had low profiles and few paid attention to the races. In a 2020 state supreme court race, both candidates spent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wisdc.org/news/press-releases/131-press-release-2020/6658-2020-supreme-court-race-cost-record-shattering-10m"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a combined $10m}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But in recent years, awareness has grown of the powerful role state supreme courts can play in defining major issues, bringing more money and hard-nosed politics to these races. In North Carolina, a Republican candidate is seeking to overturn a supreme court election he lost to a Democratic candidate {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/08/north-carolina-supreme-court-blocks-certification-allison-riggs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 by 734 votes}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat we\u8217\'20\'19ve really seen in recent years is just how important state courts are in determining election law and how elections are run,\u8221\'20\'1D said Bryna Godar, a staff attorney at the state democracy research initiative at the \uc2 University of Wisconsin\uc2  law school. She noted that Trump carried the state by just 30,000 votes in 2024 and Biden by even less in 2020.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CReally what we\u8217\'20\'19re seeing is state courts are playing a huge role not just in determining issues for the state, but in determining rules for elections that can have impacts at a national level when you\u8217\'20\'19re looking at a swing state like Wisconsin,\u8221\'20\'1D she added.\par \par \uc2 Schimel, a former Republican state attorney general, has made no secret that there would be little daylight between him and Trump, praising the president and talking about the need for a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politifact.com/factchecks/2025/mar/28/susan-crawford/in-wisconsin-supreme-court-race-crawford-claims-sc/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Csupport network\u8221\'20\'1D }}}\uc2  for him. He has also posed with a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wispolitics.com/2025/crawford-campaign-schimel-a-50ft-trump-inflatable-seriously/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 large inflatable}}}\uc2  Trump and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2025/03/03/wisconsin-supreme-court-trump-musk/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said the justices }}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cscrewed [Trump] over\u8221\'20\'1D by keeping a Green party candidate off the ballot in 2020 (Trump narrowly lost the state to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  that year). He has also called one of the female justices on the state supreme court \u8220\'20\'1Cdumb as a sack of hammers\u8221\'20\'1D and another female justice \u8220\'20\'1Ccrazy\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2025/03/21/us/politics/trump-schimel-wisconsin-supreme-court.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  endorsed}}}\uc2  Schimel on 21 March.\par \par \uc2 State Democrats have made the race a referendum on Musk, putting up \u8220\'20\'1Cpeople v Musk\u8221\'20\'1D billboards across the state and holding town halls. When the party tested messaging, it showed ads highlighting Musk\u8217\'20\'19s connections to Schimel to \u8220\'20\'1Cmotivate Democrats who otherwise want to tune out politics entirely to come out, cast a ballot, and recruit their friends\u8221\'20\'1D, said Ben Wikler, chairman of the state Democratic party.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf \uc2 Brad Schimel\uc2  loses this race and Susan Crawford wins, it\u8217\'20\'19ll become clear to Democrats that they can fight back against Musk and win,\u8221\'20\'1D said Wikler. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd it\u8217\'20\'19ll be clear to Republicans that Musk may not be able to save their bacon if they keep going along with his attacks on our country. That could have a profound impact on the whole arc of American politics in this era.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The race has energized Democrats. \u8220\'20\'1CBack in November and December, I think a lot of people I was talking to were pretty discouraged by some of the results that they saw in the November election after having put a lot of time and energy into some of those campaigns,\u8221\'20\'1D Crawford said. \u8220\'20\'1CThat has dramatically changed in the last couple of months as the administration has taken a lot of actions in a hurry that have made people really worried and concerned about the direction our country is heading.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In the weeks after Musk got involved in race, Wikler said, he saw Democrats \u8220\'20\'1Cget up off the mat and lean into the fightback\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 \u8226\'20\'22 \u8226\'20\'22\par \par \uc2 Even before Musk\u8217\'20\'19s involvement, the high stakes of the race were clear. The court heard oral arguments in a case challenging the state\u8217\'20\'19s 1849 \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban last year and is set to consider another one dealing with whether the state constitution protects the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In 2020, the state supreme court narrowly voted 4-3 to turn away a Trump lawsuit challenging his loss in the state and seeking to overturn the results.\par \par \uc2 In 2023, Democrats won a major victory when the liberal candidate Janet Protasiewicz won a seat on the court and flipped its ideological balance. Last year, the new state supreme court struck down state legislative maps, getting rid of Republican districts that were so distorted they gave Democrats no chance of ever winning a majority. Republicans went from having a near two-thirds supermajority to a slim majority in the statehouse.\par \par \uc2 The next court could hear a challenge to Wisconsin\u8217\'20\'19s congressional maps, in which Republicans hold six of eight seats. That balance is also considered severely askew in favor of Republicans and could ultimately help determine control of the US House, where Republicans hold a majority of just a few seats.\par \par \uc2 The spending in the race has shattered the more than $50m spent in the 2023 race. Musk has spent more than $18m through America Pac and Building America\u8217\'20\'19s future. The Republican mega-donor \uc2 Richard Uihlein\uc2  has gotten somewhat less attention, but Uihlein-aligned groups have spent at least $5.3m in favor of Schimel, funneling it through various entities, according to campaign finance records.\par \par \uc2 Lynde Uihlein, a cousin of \uc2 Richard Uihlein\uc2  has also been a major donor to the group A Better Wisconsin Together, which has spent more than $6m in the race supporting Crawford. The family members were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/feb/21/wisconsin-supreme-court-primary-election-uihlein-family-campaign-finance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 also on separate sides}}}\uc2  of the 2023 state supreme court race.\par \par \uc2 Robert Yablon, a law professor at the \uc2 University of Wisconsin-Madison\uc2 , noted that the huge spending in the race was only possible because of the state\u8217\'20\'19s loose campaign finance laws. People in Wisconsin can donate unlimited amounts to state parties, which can pass that money on to candidates. There are also very weak anti-coordination laws between independent expenditure groups and campaigns.\par \par \uc2 The race, Yablon said, was a \u8220\'20\'1Ctest for judicial independence\u8221\'20\'1D. If Musk succeeds in winning and ultimately gets rulings favorable to him, it could undermine that perception.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou would hope that in a judicial race, you might have different candidates \u8211\'20\'13 maybe they have different ideologies or philosophies, different ways that they talk about the law, but it\u8217\'20\'19s shared ground that they believe that the judiciary ought to operate independently from other branches, ought to check those branches,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 The turnout in Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s election is expected to be much lower than the turnout in the November presidential election, making it difficult to make firm conclusions about the voter reaction to Trump so far. But there still may be signals to take away from Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s contest.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf there is a strong win for Crawford, it will at least be evidence of the energy of liberals and the extent to which opposition to the Trump administration, to \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 , has been effectively activated,\u8221\'20\'1D Yablon said. If Schimel wins, he said it \u8220\'20\'1Cwill probably be quite disheartening for liberals, for the Democratic party that\u8217\'20\'19s invested so much in this race, and they may then really have to go back to the drawing board\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250329el3t001b9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
