\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 New York clerk refuses to enforce Texas effort to punish  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  provider\b0\par\par\uc2 Carter Sherman \par \uc2 544 \uc2 words\par \uc2 27 March 2025\par 21:15 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Texas suit alleging Dr Margaret Carpenter mailed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills to \uc2 Lone Star\uc2  state will likely go to \uc2 US supreme court\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/new-york"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York}}}\uc2  county clerk on Thursday refused to enforce a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/texas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas}}}\uc2  court fineagainst a New York doctor accused of mailing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  pills across state lines \u8211\'20\'13 a move that tees up a dramatic showdown between states that protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and those that have banned the procedure. The clash will probably end up in front of the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In December, the Texas attorney general, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/dec/13/texas-abortion-pills-lawsuit-ken-paxton"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ken Paxton, sued}}}\uc2  Dr Margaret Carpenter in a Texas court for allegedly mailing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills to the Lone Star state, which bans virtually all abortions. After Carpenter did not show up to a court hearing earlier this year, a Texas judge ruled against her, ordering her to pay a $113,000 penalty and stop sending \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills to Texas.\par \par \uc2 New York has, however, enacted a \u8220\'20\'1Cshield law\u8221\'20\'1D that forbids state officials from extraditing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers to other states or complying with out-of-state court orders. In his statement refusing to enforce the Texas fine, the acting Ulster county clerk Taylor Bruck cited the law.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn accordance with the New York State Shield Law, I have refused this filing and will refuse any similar filings that may come to our office. Since this decision is likely to result in further litigation, I must refrain from discussing specific details about the situation,\u8221\'20\'1D Bruck said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 Paxton\u8217\'20\'19s office did not immediately respond to a request for comment, but Texas may challenge New York\u8217\'20\'19s shield law through a lawsuit. Although a number of blue states have passed shield laws since the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  overturned {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade}}}\uc2  in 2022, they have never been put to the legal test.\par \par \uc2 The case will also probably serve as a bellwether for the future of interstate relations between anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  states and pro-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights states. In the years since Roe fell, anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists have grown increasingly frustrated over people\u8217\'20\'19s ability to travel across state lines for the procedure and to undergo medication abortions through telehealth. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/mar/05/alabama-court-hearing-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Alabama has threatened to prosecute people}}}\uc2  who help others travel for out-of-state abortions, while {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/31/new-york-louisiana-abortion-pill-charges"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Louisiana has issued a criminal indictment}}}\uc2  against Carpenter for allegedly prescribing an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill to someone in that state.\par \par \uc2 New York\u8217\'20\'19s governor, \uc2 Kathy Hochul\uc2 , refused Louisiana\u8217\'20\'19s call for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/feb/13/texas-abortion-pills-shield-laws-new-york-doctor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  extradition}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CI will not be signing an extradition order that came from the governor of Louisiana \u8211\'20\'13 not now, not ever,\u8221\'20\'1D she said last month.\par \par \uc2 Carpenter has not publicly commented on the case. However, a group she co-founded, \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Coalition for Telemedicine Access, has accused Paxton of \u8220\'20\'1Cputting women directly in harm\u8217\'20\'19s way\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSince Roe v Wade was overturned, we have seen attempts to further impede and erode a person\u8217\'20\'19s right to make decisions about their own bodies,\u8221\'20\'1D the organization said in a statement after news of Paxton\u8217\'20\'19s lawsuit against Carpenter broke.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CShield laws are essential in safeguarding and enabling \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care regardless of a patient\u8217\'20\'19s zip code or ability to pay. They are fundamental to ensuring everyone can access reproductive healthcare as a human right.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250327el3r002jv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
FF
