\par\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 Arrested at gunpoint, charged as a felon: a midwife\u8217\'20\'19s lot in anti- \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  Texas\b0\par\par\uc2 Arwa Mahdawi \par \uc2 1,490 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 March 2025\par 13:03 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The state with the most radical \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law is seeking to make an example of Maria Margarita Rojas\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  arrests have started\par \par \uc2 Texas is a fairly decent place to be an armadillo (they\u8217\'20\'19re the official state small mammal) and an increasingly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.motherjones.com/politics/2025/02/report-sepsis-maternal-deaths-surged-in-texas-following-abortion-bans/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dire place}}}\uc2  to be a woman. In 2021, it implemented a near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban: the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/01/texas-abortion-law-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 most radical \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  law}}}\uc2  in the US. Now it\u8217\'20\'19s going even further in its crusade to outlaw \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . On Monday, the Texas attorney general, \uc2 Ken Paxton\uc2 , announced the first criminal charges under Texas\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban. Maria Margarita Rojas, a licensed midwife, was charged with the illegal performance of an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and with practicing medicine without a license, according to a press release {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/mar/17/texas-midwife-abortion-state-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 from Paxton\u8217\'20\'19s office}}}\uc2 . Her employee Jose Ley was also charged.\par \par \uc2 There are still a lot of details that are unclear or unverified when it comes to this case, which apparently caught officials\u8217\'20\'19 eyes after an anonymous tip-off. But I\u8217\'20\'19ll tell you what is glaringly apparent: Texas wants to make an example of Rojas. They want Rojas, who primarily served a low-income Spanish-speaking community, to be a cautionary tale. One that ensures people are too terrified to even think about helping a woman obtain an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Rojas isn\u8217\'20\'19t getting some sort of slap on the wrist; the full force of the state is coming after her. She was reportedly pulled over by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://truthout.org/articles/texas-files-criminal-charges-against-midwife-who-allegedly-offered-abortion-care/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 police at gunpoint}}}\uc2  while on her way to a clinic and the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  charge is a second-degree felony, which comes with up to 20 years in prison. Meanwhile, according to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.texastribune.org/2025/03/17/texas-abortion-midwife-arrested/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas Tribune}}}\uc2 , the state recommended Rojas and Ley each be held on a million-dollar bond. A million dollars! (In the end, a judge ordered their bonds each be set at $500,000 for the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related charges and $200,000 for the medical license charges.) To put this in perspective, a Texas elementary school teacher arrested earlier this month after a \u8220\'20\'1Clarge quantity\u8221\'20\'1D of child sexual abuse materials was reportedly found on his devices, is being held in jail on a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.kvue.com/article/news/crime/austin-elementary-school-teacher-arrested-child-porn-carl-innmon/269-2dd9714b-2093-4624-9d7a-53825f75fd14"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $75,000 bond}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Locking up doctors isn\u8217\'20\'19t a popular policy platform \u8211\'20\'13 according to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/sections/health-shots/2024/03/07/1236344392/abortion-politics-poll-miscarriage-pregnancy-emergencies-kff"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 2024 KFF poll}}}\uc2 , eight in 10 Democrats, two-thirds of independents and about half of Republicans want to protect doctors who perform abortions from facing either fines or prison time. Which seems to be why Paxton went after a midwife. Mary Ziegler, a law professor and leading authority on the legal history of the American \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  debate, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://slate.com/news-and-politics/2025/03/texas-midwife-first-abortion-prosecution-maria-rojas.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 notes in Slate}}}\uc2  that \u8220\'20\'1Cthis is almost certainly not the first prosecution that Paxton could have brought\u8221\'20\'1D. No, it looks like Paxton was trying to find the perfect victim: someone he could easily smear.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe fact that Rojas is not a physician is central to Paxton\u8217\'20\'19s strategy,\u8221\'20\'1D Ziegler writes. \u8220\'20\'1CHe claims that the prosecution will protect women from unlicensed and presumably unsafe providers \u8230\'20\'26 [he wants] to signal that midwives who provide abortions are unsafe, unqualified, and dishonest.\u8221\'20\'1D This attack on the credibility of midwives \u8211\'20\'13 particularly non-white midwives \u8211\'20\'13 isn\u8217\'20\'19t new. The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/mar/17/texas-midwife-abortion-state-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Guardian notes that}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CAs \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans spread across the country in the 19th century, midwives were often driven out of work or faced criminal consequences, which in turn led white, male doctors to siphon up their patients and dominate the medical field.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Some observers believe that the timing of all this is also strategic. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activist Jessica Valenti (who used to write this newsletter and now {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://jessica.substack.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 writes \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22 , Every Day}}}\uc2  ) has noted that Rojas was arrested weeks ago. Why did Paxton wait until now to send out a press release? Valenti reckons he is trying to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.instagram.com/jessicavalenti/reel/DHY8-qHJ8iR/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 distract from the fact}}}\uc2  that Texas Republicans are trying to push through {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://legiscan.com/TX/bill/SB2880/2025"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SB 2880}}}\uc2 , which she characterizes as the biggest piece of anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  legislation since Roe was overturned. This bill targets Texans\u8217\'20\'19 access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills and makes it easier to sue people and companies involved in a person\u8217\'20\'19s medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.lonestarlive.com/news/2025/03/texas-bill-targets-people-involved-in-medication-abortions-excluding-rapists.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The bill also protects}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cany person who impregnated the woman who used \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -inducing drugs through conduct constituting sexual assault\u8221\'20\'1D from being sued.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFlooding the zone\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2025/02/07/nx-s1-5289315/trump-week-in-review"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 strategy put forward}}}\uc2  by Steve Bannon to describe the process of overwhelming the media by creating more news than anyone can possibly follow \u8211\'20\'13 is very much part of the Republican playbook. But, at this point, I don\u8217\'20\'19t know whether anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists really care about distracting us from all the dystopian schemes they\u8217\'20\'19ve got up their sleeves. On the contrary, they seem eager to rub their cruelty in our faces. Still, amid the unceasing torrent of news, it is true that we must stay focused. We must remember that the arrest of Rojas and Ley isn\u8217\'20\'19t some sort of one-off isolated to Texas but part of a much broader attack on \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Don\u8217\'20\'19t listen to Donald Trump\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Creassurances\u8221\'20\'1D that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights should be {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://kffhealthnews.org/news/article/the-week-in-brief-trump-abortion-states/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 left to the states}}}\uc2  to decide: the eventual goal is to end \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access entirely.\par \par \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s dad says his son was friendly with their Black servants growing up\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  recently did a deep dive into why Elon has become obsessed with anti-DEI efforts. While Musk, who is busy dismantling the country, didn\u8217\'20\'19t speak to the Post, his estranged dad, Errol (the one who has two children with his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://people.com/elon-musks-dad-told-him-fathers-day-2022-fathered-second-child-with-former-stepdaughter-book-7967981"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 former stepdaughter}}}\uc2  ), did send an email where he provided some information on Elon and his younger brother\u8217\'20\'19s childhood. \u8220\'20\'1CWe had several black servants who were their friends,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2025/03/20/elon-musk-race-dei-doge/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Errol noted}}}\uc2  in defence of his fascist-salute-enthusiast son. Can\u8217\'20\'19t possibly be racist then.\par \par \uc2 Republican who introduced Trump derangement syndrome bill arrested for soliciting a minor\par \par \uc2 You can\u8217\'20\'19t {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/mar/18/minnesota-justin-eichorn-arrested-soliciting-minor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 make this stuff up}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Gis\u232\'00\'E8le Pelicot will publish a memoir\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s called A Hymn to Life and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/books/2025/mar/20/gisele-pelicot-memoir-a-hymn-to-life"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 it\u8217\'20\'19ll be out next year}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The radical vision of Dona Ann McAdams \u8211\'20\'13 in pictures\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI was fascinated by how women presented themselves in public,\u8221\'20\'1D McAdams writes in a reflection accompanying one of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/artanddesign/gallery/2025/mar/20/the-female-gaze-interested-me-more-the-radical-vision-of-dona-ann-mcadams-in-pictures"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 photos in this amazing collection}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CEveryone knew about the male gaze, but the female gaze interested me more.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Israel has killed more than 200 children in Gaza in just a few days\par \par \uc2 A \uc2 Unicef\uc2  spokesperson {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2025/3/21/live-israeli-attacks-kill-almost-600-as-troops-invade-south-north-gaza"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told Al Jazeera}}}\uc2  that at least 200 children had been killed in Gaza since Israel shattered the ceasefire. Friday was Mother\u8217\'20\'19s Day in the Middle East, making this even more harrowing. Meanwhile, everyone in Gaza is traumatized. Please watch {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2025/03/19/world/video/palestinian-children-trauma-israel-war-intldsk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 this heartbreaking video}}}\uc2  from CNN where eight-year-old Sama Tubail, who has lost all her hair from stress, says: \u8220\'20\'1CI want to die and have my hair grow in paradise.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2025/03/19/world/video/palestinian-children-trauma-israel-war-intldsk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The UN has said}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Ca generation has been traumatized\u8221\'20\'1D, and that nearly all of Gaza\u8217\'20\'19s 1.2 million children need psychological support. If you\u8217\'20\'19re American, your taxpayer dollars are funding this, your lawmakers are enabling this, large swathes of the media are justifying this, and you can lose your job for speaking up about this.\par \par \uc2 Ella Keidar Greenberg sentenced to 30 days in prison for refusing to join the Israeli army\par \par \uc2 Greenberg is a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pressenza.com/2025/03/trans-israeli-refuser-ella-keidar-greenberg-sentenced-to-30-days-in-prison/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 trans woman}}}\uc2  who has protested with Palestinian activists against land theft. She\u8217\'20\'19s risking being sent to male military prison in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tiktok.com/@the_andrey_x/video/7483507615243291912?_r=1&_t=ZT-8upFb8KCR8l&fbclid=IwY2xjawJKeYNleHRuA2FlbQIxMQABHQpuxpBHEYxIEGlq3OXChXzllfd-gq-PYA-Svog_G0tgFY9juMPUaC0wSA_aem_H3CONpqe3mjCX9__ChrTSA"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 order to stand against}}}\uc2  the genocide. An enormously brave woman \u8211\'20\'13 it\u8217\'20\'19s a shame people like her aren\u8217\'20\'19t getting more media attention.\par \par \uc2 US women\u8217\'20\'19s justice group launches campaign to get Andrew Tate extradited\par \par \uc2 The group, UltraViolet, has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/mar/20/andrew-tate-deported-campaign-ultraviolet"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 criticized the Trump administration}}}\uc2  for reportedly pressuring Romanian officials to allow Tate to fly to Florida last month.\par \par \uc2 Iranian authorities have escalated their crackdown on women\u8217\'20\'19s rights defenders\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSince International Women\u8217\'20\'19s Day (IWD) on 8 March, the Iranian authorities have arbitrarily arrested at least five women\u8217\'20\'19s rights activists,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.amnesty.org/en/latest/news/2025/03/iran-authorities-target-womens-rights-activists-with-arbitrary-arrest-flogging-and-death-penalty/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Amnesty International reports}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CThese arrests come amid an intensified crackdown \u8230\'20\'26 In the lead up to IWD, the authorities flogged a male singer 74 times for performing a protest song against Iran\u8217\'20\'19s discriminatory compulsory veiling laws and, in February 2025, sentenced a women\u8217\'20\'19s rights activist to death.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Bird research has a bro\par \par \uc2 bias\par \par \uc2 You can\u8217\'20\'19t even escape sexism {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nationalgeographic.com/animals/article/female-bird-research-sex-bias"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 when you\u8217\'20\'19re a pigeon}}}\uc2 , apparently.\par \par \uc2 The week in pawtriarchy\par \par \uc2 Technically, the blobfish does not have any paws. (Nor does it have a swim bladder, a full skeleton, muscles or scales.) Still, it gets an honourable mention this week after being crowned {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/mar/18/once-named-worlds-ugliest-animal-blobfish-wins-new-zealands-fish-of-the-year"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New Zealand\u8217\'20\'19s fish of the year}}}\uc2 . This is quite a result for the blobfish (which a spokesperson for the competition described as looking like \u8220\'20\'1Ca failed medical experiment\u8221\'20\'1D when it\u8217\'20\'19s out of the water), which was once voted the \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2013/sep/12/blobfish-world-ugliest-animal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 world\u8217\'20\'19s ugliest animal}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D. Another fun fact about the blobfish? They don\u8217\'20\'19t have many bones, but still have more of a spine than the Democrats.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250322el3m001gt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
