\par\par \uc2 Global development\par \b \uc2 A tale of two conferences: women against women as \u8216\'20\'18poison of patriarchy\u8217\'20\'19 returns and  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  fight intensifies\b0\par\par\uc2 Isabel Choat in New York \par \uc2 1,717 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 March 2025\par 05:02 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Last week, anti-choice campaigners emboldened by current US politics met in New York at the same time as \uc2 UN\uc2  delegates gathered to address the widespread inequalities women face. The battle to protect rights has never felt more urgent\par \par \uc2 In a meeting room on the 27th floor of a swish Manhattan hotel, Denise Mountenay is telling the audience that the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is \u8220\'20\'1CNazi thinking.\u8221\'20\'1D Mountenay regrets her own abortions, and says she has been called by God to spread the word that she and other women \u8220\'20\'1Cwere lied to, deceived, pressured into making the most horrible choice: to choose death instead of life\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 She goes on to list reasons why \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is \u8220\'20\'1Cnot a safe procedure. [That\u8217\'20\'19s what] they want woman to think \u8211\'20\'13 that is a lie.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Many of her claims, including that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  leads to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cancer.org/cancer/risk-prevention/medical-treatments/abortion-and-breast-cancer-risk.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 breast cancer}}}\uc2 , have been thoroughly disproved by scientific studies. Other claims, such as that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  causes {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ucsf.edu/news/2022/06/423161/ucsf-turnaway-study-shows-impact-abortion-access"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lifelong mental health problems}}}\uc2  and infertility also have been shown to be untrue when access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is safe and legal. Studies show that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  denial {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.scirp.org/journal/paperinformation?paperid=138846"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 increases the risk}}}\uc2  of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.apa.org/news/press/releases/2022/05/restricting-abortion-mental-health-harms"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 both}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The backlash is a pre-emptive strike in case feminists win, it\u8217\'20\'19s a deliberate organised effort because we were so close\par \par \uc2 Marta Lempart, Polish pro-choice activist\par \par \uc2 Mountenay, from the Christian, anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Endeavour Forum, is one of many speakers, mostly women, to address the Conference on the State of Women and Family (CSWF) in New York. Over two days they speak repeatedly of love and respect for women, yet decry global efforts to empower women and expand their rights. They reiterate their stance against \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in any circumstances, including gang-rape, and hail motherhood as the ultimate role for women.\par \par \uc2 Sponsored by four leading US, rightwing organisations, including \uc2 the Heritage Foundation\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/nov/04/what-is-project-2025-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  architect of Project 2025}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2019/may/16/cfam-rightwing-white-house-anti-abortion-un"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 C-Fam}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 designated a hate group by the The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.splcenter.org/resources/hate-watch/could-austin-ruses-violent-rhetoric-endanger-c-fams-status-un/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Southern Poverty Law Center}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 CSWF is an opportunity for conservative heavyweights and anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  campaigners to reassert their opposition to \u8220\'20\'1Cgender ideology\u8221\'20\'1D and air their grievances about the perceived attack on conservative values. LGBTQ rights, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/article/2024/may/29/global-pandemic-treaty-could-be-more-than-a-year-away-after-deadline-missed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pandemic treaty}}}\uc2 , comprehensive sex education and \u8220\'20\'1Cleftish insanity\u8221\'20\'1D on US college campuses are held up as examples of corrupting secular ideologies.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s blizzard of executive orders, including the assertion that \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/20/trump-executive-order-gender-sex"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 there are only two genders}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D, felt like \u8220\'20\'1CChristmas multiple days in a row,\u8221\'20\'1D says Jay W Richards, director of the Richard and \uc2 Helen DeVos\uc2  Centre for Life, and a fellow at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.heritage.org/staff/jay-w-richards-phd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Heritage Foundation}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CSuddenly it\u8217\'20\'19s a new day \u8211\'20\'13 that\u8217\'20\'19s the good news; the bad news is the fight is not over.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par \uc2 Anti-rights actors are nothing new. But the ferociousness of the attack on \u8211\'20\'13 and scale of the current backlash against \u8211\'20\'13 women\u8217\'20\'19s rights is sending a chill through rights defenders, giving an urgency to calls for a united response.\par \par \uc2 A minute\u8217\'20\'19s walk from the CSWF gathering, the 69th Commission on the Status of Women ( {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.un.org/en/story/2025/03/1160941"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CSW}}}\uc2  ) is taking place at the same time at the \uc2 UN\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s headquarters. This annual meeting aims to address the widespread inequalities, violence and discrimination women continue to face around the world.\par \par \uc2 UN\uc2  secretary general \uc2 Ant\u243\'00\'F3nio Guterres\uc2  opens the conference with a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.unwomen.org/en/news-stories/speech/2025/03/remarks-of-the-un-secretary-general-at-the-opening-of-the-69th-session-of-the-commission-on-the-status-of-women#:~:text=The%20Pact%20for%20the%20Future%20commits%20to%20integrate%20women%20in,and%20all%20walks%20of%20life."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 red alert}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CThe poison of patriarchy is back \u8211\'20\'13 and it is back with a vengeance: slamming the brakes on action; tearing up progress; and mutating into new and dangerous forms.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 His warning that hard-won gains are being thrown into reverse follows a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.unwomen.org/en/news-stories/press-release/2025/03/one-in-four-countries-report-backlash-on-womens-rights-in-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 UN report}}}\uc2  revealing that one in four countries reported a backlash on gender equality in 2024. Based on a review of progress by 159 member states, the report attributes the rollback to crises including a weakening of democratic institutions, Covid, climate breakdown and conflict. But it notes the key role of anti-rights actors who \u8220\'20\'1Care actively undermining longstanding consensus on key women\u8217\'20\'19s rights issues. Where they cannot roll back legal and policy gains altogether, they seek to block or slow their implementation.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Earlier this month, \uc2 Oxfam\uc2  published its own {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://policy-practice.oxfam.org/resources/personal-to-powerful-holding-the-line-for-gender-justice-in-the-face-of-growing-621683/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 assessment}}}\uc2  of the damage being wreaked by anti-rights groups: \u8220\'20\'1CA range of rightwing, religious, and conservative actors around the world are capitalising on persistent crises, to reorient state power towards a reassertion of racist and sexist profit-driven systems that favours the wealthy, privileges men, and harms and disadvantages women and LGBTQIA+ people in the name of \u8216\'20\'18traditional\u8217\'20\'19 family values.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 I wasn\u8217\'20\'19t scared, and then it hit me that this movement is more daring, bolder and is doing anything they can do to convey their message\par \par \uc2 Nelly Munyasia, \b \highlight22\uc2 Reproductive Health\b0 \highlight\uc2  Network Kenya\par \par \uc2 Many of the events taking place at \uc2 UN\uc2  event address the threat posed by anti-rights groups. In a session called Feminism for the Win: Strategies to Defy and Defeat Anti-feminist Movements, panellists speak of the rise of \u8220\'20\'1Cchainsaw masculinity\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Crapid authoritarian transformation\u8221\'20\'1D. Marta Lempart, the activist who led Poland\u8217\'20\'19s pro-choice women\u8217\'20\'19s strikes, notes grimly \u8220\'20\'1Cthe alpha male is back in town,\u8221\'20\'1D adding: \u8220\'20\'1CThe backlash is a pre-emptive strike in case feminists win, it\u8217\'20\'19s a deliberate organised effort because we were so close.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The anti-rights movement is also present at the \uc2 UN\uc2 . In one Q&A Liana Gordon, a youth delegate from the Canadian anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  organisation Campaign Life Coalition, asks the panel: \u8220\'20\'1CYou talk of women\u8217\'20\'19s rights but what about the rights of the unborn child?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The question infuriates Lempart. \u8220\'20\'1CWhenever someone says \u8216\'20\'18women\u8217\'20\'19s rights but \u8230\'20\'26 or human rights but \u8230\'20\'26\u8217\'20\'19 it\u8217\'20\'19s bullshit \u8230\'20\'26 I hate these guys and I\u8217\'20\'19m saying that out loud. You have to fight, insult them, do all the things you should\u8217\'20\'19t be doing. You have to speak how you feel.\u8221\'20\'1D It is a response that delights Gordon who later relays it to her fellow anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists. \u8220\'20\'1CLast year I did not see this type of emotional response at least not at this level. It confirmed to me that we are winning,\u8221\'20\'1D says Gordon. \u8220\'20\'1CI have a message for Marta: you may hate me but we love you.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Challenging participants and taking up oxygen in discussions is a key {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.internationalyouthcoalition.com/unweekly/r9715vaymta47lw4uhmle55ke8yxlb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 strategy }}}\uc2  for anti-rights groups at CSW. After taking part in one panel discussion, Nelly Munyasia from the \b \highlight22\uc2 Reproductive Health\b0 \highlight\uc2  Network Kenya, recalls being handed a flyer incorrectly stating that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not legal in any country. \u8220\'20\'1CInitially I wasn\u8217\'20\'19t scared, and then it hit me that this [anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ] movement is more daring, bolder and is doing anything they can do to convey their message.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par \uc2 On the first day of CSW, member states adopt a political declaration reaffirming their commitment to respect, protect and champion the rights, equality, and empowerment of women and girls. Sima Bahous, executive director of \uc2 UN Women\uc2  calls the declaration \u8220\'20\'1Ca show of unity for all women and girls, everywhere \u8230\'20\'26 at a time when hard-fought gains for gender equality are under attack.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US government{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://usun.usmission.gov/explanation-of-position-on-the-commission-on-the-status-of-women-csw-political-declaration-location-of-remarks/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 refuses to endorse}}}\uc2  it, but it is welcomed by leading health and rights groups such as the \uc2 International Planned Parenthood Federation\uc2  (\uc2 IPPF\uc2 ) as a sign of international solidarity and support for the human rights of women and girls.\par \par \uc2 But the declaration has a glaring omission: while sexual and \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive health\b0 \highlight\uc2  and rights (SRHR) was part of a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.unwomen.org/sites/default/files/2025-02/csw69-political-declaration-draft-en.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 draft declaration}}}\uc2  published in January, there is no mention in the final agreement. \uc2 IPPF\uc2  believes the absence of SRHR, a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thelancet.com/journals/lancet/article/PIIS0140-6736(18)30293-9/fulltext"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cornerstone of women\u8217\'20\'19s equality and sustainable development}}}\uc2 , significantly weakens the text\u8217\'20\'19s scope.\par \par \uc2 Thirty years ago SRHR was included in the 12 critical areas covered by the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2025/mar/03/we-had-all-this-energy-the-landmark-gathering-of-women-that-unnerved-the-chinese-government"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 historic Beijing declaration in 1995}}}\uc2 , a policy framework still regarded as the blueprint for gender equality and justice. Since then, it has often been a point of contention in international forums, but the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.un.org/en/E/CN.6/2024/L.3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 2024 agreement acknowledged}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cthe need for ensuring universal access to sexual and reproductive healthcare services, including for family planning, information and education\u8221\'20\'1D. The omission this year is seen by global advocacy groups and research centres as another effect of the increasingly hostile environment.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis year negotiators didn\u8217\'20\'19t feel they could continue to fight for [those rights] so they let it go \u8211\'20\'13 because [otherwise] it would crash the negotiations. Many of us find that profoundly disappointing,\u8221\'20\'1D says Beth Schlachter, senior director of US external relations at \uc2 MSI Reproductive Choices\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Schlachter\u8217\'20\'19s colleague, Bethan Cobley, director of external affairs and partnerships, adds that the absence of language around SRHR has global ramifications, \u8220\'20\'1CThese words set the global normative framework in the countries where we operate; countries take this language and use it to inform their national policies \u8211\'20\'13 it is hugely important.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The environment of extreme hostility is having numerous detrimental effects on healthcare providers attempting to deliver services to communities across Kenya, says Munyasia. \u8220\'20\'1CWe come from a continent where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  continues to be regarded as a taboo \u8211\'20\'13 you can imagine the work we have done to show women [they can have a safe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ]. Now we are seeing disinformation which contributes to stigma and instils fear in women who will be termed murderers.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Munyasia has been harassed on social media and has had to remove signs from \b \highlight22\uc2 Reproductive Health\b0 \highlight\uc2  Network Kenya offices, and even move offices; the call centre it runs has been reported to the authorities. The organisation has also recorded a rise in police targeting healthcare providers \u8211\'20\'13 it has documented 28 arrests of healthcare providers and their patients in the last two years.\par \par \uc2 She is alarmed at the prospect of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://acpf.africa/2024/10/26/2nd-pan-african-conference-on-family-values/#:~:text=The%20focus%20will%20be%20on,series%20of%20virtual%20pre%2Dconferences."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pan-African Conference on Family Values}}}\uc2  taking place in Nairobi in May adding to the atmosphere of fear and distrust among women who use reproductive healthcare services.\par \par \uc2 The worst part of it, says Munyisia, is that relentless attacks combined with aid cuts will prevent women and girls accessing contraceptives and safe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  leading to unplanned, unwanted pregnancies, a rise in HIV infections and maternal deaths.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s going to be messy unless we have funders that can step up to mitigate this,\u8221\'20\'1D she says. \u8220\'20\'1CWhat breaks my heart is that vulnerable women and girls will suffer in global south.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Back at CSWF, a delegate from Liberia asks a panel how she could support young women who have been gang-raped.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPray,\u8221\'20\'1D comes the reply.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250322el3m000dx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
