\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Texas midwife arrested for allegedly providing abortions amid state\u8217\'20\'19s near-total ban\b0\par\par\uc2 Carter Sherman \par \uc2 463 \uc2 words\par \uc2 17 March 2025\par 22:19 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Maria Margarita Rojas charged with illegal performance of procedure, considered a second-degree felony in the state\par \par \uc2 A Texas midwife has been arrested over accusations that she performed abortions in defiance of the state\u8217\'20\'19s near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, the Texas attorney general, \uc2 Ken Paxton\uc2 , announced on Monday.\par \par \uc2 Maria Margarita Rojas has been charged with the illegal performance of an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and with practicing medicine without a license, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.oag.state.tx.us/news/releases/attorney-general-ken-paxton-announces-arrest-houston-area-abortionist-and-crackdown-clinics"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a press release}}}\uc2  from Paxton\u8217\'20\'19s office. Under Texas law, the illegal performance of an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is considered a second-degree felony. If convicted, Rojas could face decades in prison.\par \par \uc2 Rojas\u8217\'20\'19s arrest is believed to be the first criminal arrest under Texas\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban. Last year, Paxton\u8217\'20\'19s office {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/dec/13/texas-abortion-pills-lawsuit-ken-paxton"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sued Dr Margaret Carpenter}}}\uc2 , a New York-based \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider, for allegedly mailing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills to a Texan.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn Texas, life is sacred. I will always do everything in my power to protect the unborn, defend our state\u8217\'20\'19s pro-life laws, and work to ensure that unlicensed individuals endangering the lives of women by performing illegal abortions are fully prosecuted,\u8221\'20\'1D Paxton said in a statement accompanying the news of Rojas\u8217\'20\'19s arrest. \u8220\'20\'1CTexas law protecting life is clear, and we will hold those who violate it accountable.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In the years since the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  overturned Roe v Wade, enabling Texas and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/jul/29/abortion-laws-bans-by-state"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more than a dozen other states}}}\uc2  to ban almost all abortions, anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists have grown increasingly fed up with the lack of prosecutions of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers. In Texas, advocates have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/investigations/2025/01/17/texas-abortion-pills-lawsuit/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 increasingly encouraged men}}}\uc2  whose partners have had abortions to strike back with legal action.\par \par \uc2 Rojas, 48, operated a network of three clinics in the Houston area, according to Paxton\u8217\'20\'19s office. These clinics, his office said, \u8220\'20\'1Cunlawfully employed unlicensed individuals who falsely presented themselves as licensed medical professionals to provide medical treatment\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Requests for comment from Rojas\u8217\'20\'19s clinics were not immediately returned. However, Holly Shearman, a midwife who runs a birthing center where Rojas sometimes worked, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.texastribune.org/2025/03/17/texas-abortion-midwife-arrested/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told the Texas Tribune}}}\uc2  that she did not believe the allegations.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve known her for eight years and I\u8217\'20\'19ve never heard her talk about anything like that,\u8221\'20\'1D said Shearman, who said Rojas is a devout Catholic who often works with Spanish-speaking, low-income individuals. \u8220\'20\'1CI just can\u8217\'20\'19t picture Maria being involved in something like this.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Midwives \u8211\'20\'13 in particular, midwives of color \u8211\'20\'13 have long been a target of US anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activism. As \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans spread across the country in the 19th century, midwives were often driven out of work or faced criminal consequences, which in turn led white, male doctors to siphon up their patients and dominate the medical field.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250317el3h003ea\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
