\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Fate of Wyoming\u8217\'20\'19s last  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  clinic in balance as Republicans take aim\b0\par\par\uc2 Cy Neff in Cheyenne \par \uc2 1,111 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 March 2025\par 11:04 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Wellspring center in Casper pauses services after conservative legislature passes tough new restrictions\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s a small, unremarkable beige building in downtown Casper, the heart of Wyoming\u8217\'20\'19s oil country, tucked between a Sinclair gas station and a local dry cleaner. Most days of the week, the building attracts a small throng of protesters.\par \par \uc2 In May 2022, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://wyofile.com/casper-abortion-clinic-arsonist-sentenced-to-five-years-in-prison/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 it was burned down}}}\uc2  just three weeks before a new business was set to open in the building. Since it finally opened in 2023, Wyoming lawmakers have passed a number of laws designed specifically to shut it down.\par \par \uc2 Wyoming\u8217\'20\'19s 2025 legislative session, which has just ended, has brought them closer than ever to succeeding in obstructing the work of Wellspring Health Access, the state\u8217\'20\'19s only full-service \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic.\par \par \uc2 Near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans went into effect in Wyoming after the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  overturned Roe v Wade in 2022, but a Wyoming district court judge {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/politics/elections/2024/11/19/wyoming-abortion-ban-blocked/76425067007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturned the bans last year}}}\uc2  citing the state\u8217\'20\'19s constitutionally guaranteed right to healthcare access. The case \u8211\'20\'13 brought by Wellspring \u8211\'20\'13 is currently in the hands of the Wyoming supreme court.\par \par \uc2 Due to an injunction, Wellspring was able to operate during the prolonged legal battle. That changed last week, when the conservative legislature passed a law requiring facilities providing in-clinic abortions meet the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://wyofile.com/wyoming-enacts-new-abortion-clinic-rules-raising-questions-about-casper-facilitys-future/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 regulatory requirements of ambulatory surgical centers}}}\uc2 , which have entirely different building codes and regulations, requiring a prohibitively expensive relocation. The law would also require doctors to have admitting privileges at a hospital within 10 miles, which is more stringent than its codes for ambulatory surgical centers.\par \par \uc2 Another law mandates a transvaginal ultrasound and 48-hour waiting period for women seeking abortions, and was passed after the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://wyofile.com/senate-overrides-gordons-veto-of-abortion-bill-requiring-transvaginal-ultrasounds-in-wyoming/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 legislature overrode the governor\u8217\'20\'19s veto}}}\uc2  on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 In the meantime, the clinic has paused services for all patients.\par \par \uc2 Wellspring is back in familiar territory \u8211\'20\'13 the Wyoming courts \u8211\'20\'13 and has filed a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://wyofile.com/abortion-clinic-files-lawsuit-to-block-new-wyoming-laws/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lawsuit against both bills}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re quite disappointed in the legislature. We saw it coming, but it\u8217\'20\'19s still disappointing,\u8221\'20\'1D said Julie Burkhart, Wellspring\u8217\'20\'19s president.\par \par \uc2 The laws are designated by reproductive law experts as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.plannedparenthoodaction.org/issues/abortion/types-attacks/trap-laws"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trap laws}}}\uc2 , anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies to chip away at \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access when a full ban is out of reach. The \uc2 American College of Obstetricians and Gynecologists\uc2  has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.acog.org/news/news-articles/2020/11/hospital-admitting-privilege-mandates-undermine-physician-practice-and-unduly-burden-womens-access-to-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 opposed legislation identical to Wyoming\u8217\'20\'19s ambulatory surgical center bill}}}\uc2 , and opposes {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.acog.org/clinical/clinical-guidance/committee-statement/articles/2025/02/increasing-access-to-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ultrasound requirements}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Republican speaker of the house Chip Neiman was the main sponsor of this session\u8217\'20\'19s ultrasound bill. While Neiman insists the reasoning behind the bill is medical, he admitted {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://wyofile.com/house-speaker-senate-bound-abortion-restrictions-are-about-more-than-safety/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 during a floor debate this session}}}\uc2  that his bill also intended to make women \u8220\'20\'1Creconsider\u8221\'20\'1D their abortions.\par \par \uc2 When asked by the Guardian how he reached a medical position opposed by major medical associations, Neiman opened by talking about the sanctity of life.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s a human being,\u8221\'20\'1D Neiman said.\par \par \uc2 Neiman continued his answer on his medical position by talking about {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://wyofile.com/felony-animal-cruelty-probe-still-active-one-year-after-wyoming-wolfs-torture-prosecutor-says/#:~:text=The%20signed%20act%20creates%20the,have%20been%20taken%20into%20possession."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 anti animal-cruelty legislation}}}\uc2 , an anecdote about a fellow legislator who knew two women who had abortions 40 years ago and said they were severely distraught afterwards, and his belief in \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans without exceptions, saying that he favors the death penalty for men who rape women.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s more to it than just getting rid of an inconvenience, you know, or something that\u8217\'20\'19s going to impact, your financial, or through rape or incest or whatever,\u8221\'20\'1D Neiman said. \u8220\'20\'1CI get that that\u8217\'20\'19s traumatic. I believe anybody that perpetrates that on a woman, to me, the death penalty is the best answer.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The new laws would require Wellspring to completely restructure the clinic\u8217\'20\'19s operations. At the moment, people seeking abortions are largely being referred to Colorado, and Burkhart is working out solutions for those that come for its other services, including IUDs, family planning, oral contraceptives, and general gynecological services.\par \par \uc2 Wyoming residents may still choose to receive medication abortions from out of state through the mail, thanks to shield laws that offer protections to providers who prescribe pills to people in states with bans. (A doctor in Jackson, Wyoming, previously prescribed the pills but did not respond to questions from the \uc2 Guardian\uc2  asking if this is still the case.)\par \par \uc2 But the loss of the services frozen at Wellspring \u8211\'20\'13 which was the only facility in the state providing surgical abortions \u8211\'20\'13 will reverberate beyond Casper, the state\u8217\'20\'19s second largest city with a population of under 60,000. Burkhart says the clinic has served people from over 19 states, many coming from states with similarly harsh \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have a commitment to bringing \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive health\b0 \highlight\uc2  services to under-served and under-resourced areas,\u8221\'20\'1D Burkhart said. \u8220\'20\'1CI come from an agricultural family in Oklahoma, and so for me, that\u8217\'20\'19s very personal, because no matter where you live in the United States, you deserve access to quality healthcare.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Burkhart is no stranger to hostile political conditions, having been an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2019/may/30/he-gave-so-much-the-woman-fighting-the-abortion-wars-begun-by-george-tiller"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 adviser for Kansas doctor George Tiller}}}\uc2 , who was assassinated in 2009 by an anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  extremist. She worries about the protesters outside, who she says are increasingly emboldened by national politics.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have a bomb-threat policy. We have an active-shooter policy. These are things that in other businesses, people do not have to think about day to day,\u8221\'20\'1D Burkhart said. \u8220\'20\'1CStaff have to be alert when they\u8217\'20\'19re out in public. You know, are they being followed? This does not make living life easy.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 While the atmosphere in Wyoming\u8217\'20\'19s legislature is hostile to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , data suggests that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://wyofile.com/wyoming-abortion-views-hold-steady-as-lawmakers-pursue-more-restrictions/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 voters in the Cowboy State feel differently}}}\uc2 . Polling from the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://wysac.uwyo.edu/wysac/projects/weys24/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 University of Wyoming}}}\uc2  shows that only 11% of residents believe \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should never be permitted\u8221\'20\'1D. Another 20% support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in cases where \u8220\'20\'1Cthe need has been clearly established\u8221\'20\'1D, and nearly 40% believe \u8220\'20\'1Cwomen should always have access to abortions as a matter of personal choice\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Lawmakers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wyoleg.gov/Legislation/2025/HB0042"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 filed}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wyoleg.gov/Legislation/2025/HB0064"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 five}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wyoleg.gov/Legislation/2025/HB0159"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bills}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wyoleg.gov/Legislation/2025/HB0250"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 targeting}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wyoleg.gov/Legislation/2025/SF0125"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  at the outset of the 2025 legislative session. Some of the more ambitious measures failed, such as a bill that would have regulated \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill chemicals in wastewater by making {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cowboystatedaily.com/2025/01/24/bill-to-keep-abortion-drugs-out-of-water-supply-passes-house-committee/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 women bag the remains of their miscarriages}}}\uc2  and a first-of-its kind effort to exempt \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the state\u8217\'20\'19s definition of healthcare, that, in its original draft, would have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/feb/02/wyoming-republicans-anti-abortion-bill"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 exempted chemotherapy as well}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Burkhart says that her and her staff plan to stay in the fight. After trial by fire with the 2022 arson, she says many people expected her to give up.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think people thought, and rightfully so, \u8216\'20\'18They\u8217\'20\'19re gonna pack up and go home and call it a day here,\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D Burkhart said. \u8220\'20\'1CBut we dug our heels in even deeper.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250308el3800106\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
