\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 Arizona court permanently blocks 15-week  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  ban\b0\par\par\uc2 Carter Sherman \par \uc2 437 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 March 2025\par 16:06 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The ruling marks a victory for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights months after a ballot measure added protections to the state constitution\par \par \uc2 A court permanently blocked Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s 15-week {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ban from taking effect on Wednesday, months after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/arizona"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Arizona}}}\uc2  residents voted to pass a ballot measure adding \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights into the state constitution.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFor two years, I\u8217\'20\'19ve seen firsthand how our state\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban has harmed my patients, with countless lives and futures changed because politicians thought their views of the right healthcare was more important than pregnant people and their medical providers,\u8221\'20\'1D Dr Eric M Reuss, one of the healthcare providers who brought the lawsuit over Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s 15-week ban, said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 The 15-week ban had already been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/dec/03/arizona-abortion-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 paused since December}}}\uc2 , when Reuss and other providers filed their lawsuit, which argued that the ballot measure, which adds constitutional protections for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  until about 24 weeks, meant the ban was now unconstitutional. Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s attorney general, Democrat Kris Mayes, had agreed not to enforce the ban while litigation played out.\par \par \uc2 The short ruling on Wednesday, from Judge Frank Moskowitz of Maricopa county superior court, agreed that the 15-week ban was unconstitutional and forbade Arizona officials from enforcing it.\par \par \uc2 Arizona spent much of 2024 at the center of the contentious US \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  wars, after a state supreme court agreed to let a near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban take effect. The threat of that ban \u8211\'20\'13 which dated back to 1864, before Arizona had become a state \u8211\'20\'13 unleashed nationwide outrage. State legislators, including Republicans, quickly scrambled to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/02/arizona-1864-abortion-ban-repealed-governor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 repeal the 1864 ban}}}\uc2  and let the 15-week ban, which was already on the books, stand in its place.\par \par \uc2 Arizona then became one of seven states to pass {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/nov/05/abortion-ballot-results-tracker-ban-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pro-\b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights ballot measures}}}\uc2  in the 2024 elections. However, these measures did not immediately restore or strengthen access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 rather, activists have had to push for litigation or legislation to make good on the ballots\u8217\'20\'19 promises. After a lengthy court battle, Missouri, which banned virtually all abortions before its residents voted in favor of a pro-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights measure, has also now {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/feb/15/judge-strikes-down-licensing-requirement-abortion-providers-missouri"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 restored access to the procedure}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In a statement on Wednesday, \uc2 Nancy Northup\uc2 , president and CEO of the \uc2 Center for \b \highlight22\uc2 Reproductive Rights\b0 \highlight\uc2 , vowed to continue trying to topple other barriers to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in Arizona.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBurdensome and pointless requirements leveled at \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers and mandatory waiting periods for patients continue to undermine the voters\u8217\'20\'19 will,\u8221\'20\'1D Northup said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe will keep fighting to ensure that Arizonans get all the freedoms they voted for and rightfully expect.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250305el35002h5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
