\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Trump launches fresh attacks on US  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  rights\b0\par\par\uc2 Carter Sherman and agencies \par \uc2 954 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 March 2025\par 13:52 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Administration to drop Idaho emergency \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  lawsuit and back South Carolina in Planned Parenthood funds case\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/trump-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump administration}}}\uc2  fired off a series of dramatic attacks on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights on Tuesday, as it signaled its plan to drop out of a case defending access to emergency abortions while asking the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  for permission to join a case against the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The justice department said it would move to dismiss the case over emergency abortions, which had been originally filed by the Biden administration, according to court papers filed by the largest hospital network in Idaho. The Biden administration had sued Idaho over its near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, which it accused of running afoul of a federal law that protects patients\u8217\'20\'19 right to health care in emergencies.\par \par \uc2 The dismissal could come as soon as Wednesday, St Luke\u8217\'20\'19s Health System wrote in a court filing. The hospital has previously said that Idaho\u8217\'20\'19s ban forced its providers to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/23/supreme-court-verdict-emergency-abortions-patients-doctors"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fly women out of state}}}\uc2  for emergency care.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the Trump administration has filed paperwork asking the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  to let it join the upcoming oral arguments in a case over South Carolina\u8217\'20\'19s attempt to eradicate Medicaid funding for medical services offered by \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Although it is already illegal to use federal dollars to pay for abortions, South Carolina\u8217\'20\'19s Republican governor, \uc2 Henry McMaster\uc2 , ordered the state department of health to block \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  from Medicaid because, McMaster said: \u8220\'20\'1Cpayment of taxpayer funds to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics, for any purpose, results in the subsidy of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the denial of the right to life\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The Trump administration hopes to help defend South Carolina\u8217\'20\'19s actions, asking for 10 minutes of the April oral arguments\u8217\'20\'19 running time. South Carolina is being represented by \uc2 Alliance Defending Freedom\uc2 , a powerhouse Christian legal group that was the architect of much of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/feb/01/anti-abortion-activists-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 conservative attack}}}\uc2  on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and LGBTQ+ rights.\par \par \uc2 Under Medicaid rules, patients may choose to see any provider who is qualified to treat them. \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  typically provides an array of reproductive and sexual health services, such as STI testing and birth control. South Carolina also bans abortions past six weeks of pregnancy \u8211\'20\'13 before many women even realize they are pregnant.\par \par \uc2 These moves appear to mark some of the administration\u8217\'20\'19s first major actions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . In his first term, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  appointed many of the supreme court justices who voted to overturn the nationwide right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 2022.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Trump administration has made clear they would let women die rather than get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D Deirdre Schifeling, chief political and advocacy officer at the \uc2 ACLU\uc2 , said in a statement after news of the Idaho filing broke.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COn the campaign trail, President Trump repeatedly promised not to interfere with women\u8217\'20\'19s ability to access \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and patients\u8217\'20\'19 ability to get the care they need. His failure to keep that promise, six weeks into his administration, goes against the will of the vast majority of people in this country who want and expect their loved ones to be able to get the care they need at a hospital.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Tuesday filing from St Luke\u8217\'20\'19s came as the hospital seeks a court order allowing doctors to continue providing abortions in emergency situations as they deem necessary. Complaints that pregnant women were turned away from US emergency rooms spiked after the overturning of Roe v Wade amid questions about what care they could legally provide, federal records showed.\par \par \uc2 The supreme court stepped into the Idaho case last year and ultimately handed down a narrow ruling that allowed hospitals to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/jun/27/supreme-court-allows-emergency-abortions-idaho"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 continue performing emergency abortions}}}\uc2  as doctors deemed necessary.\par \par \uc2 The high court did not, however, resolve key legal questions in the case, and it was argued before the ninth US circuit court of appeals in December. The appeals court has not yet ruled, but Idaho has argued that its state law allows for abortions in life-threatening situations and that the Biden administration was trying to improperly expand its exceptions.\par \par \uc2 A justice department spokesperson did not immediately respond to requests for comment. Idaho officials also did not immediately reply to requests for comment.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis case is about preserving South Carolina\u8217\'20\'19s authority to govern itself in a way that aligns with the law and our state\u8217\'20\'19s values,\u8221\'20\'1D Brandon Charochak, a spokesperson for McMaster, said in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1CGovernor McMaster thanks the Trump administration for defending our ability to protect life.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CGovernor McMaster welcomes and appreciates the Trump administration\u8217\'20\'19s support in Medina v \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2 . This case is about preserving South Carolina\u8217\'20\'19s authority to govern itself in a way that aligns with the law and our state\u8217\'20\'19s values. Governor McMaster thanks the Trump administration for defending our ability to protect life.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 About 50,000 people in the US develop life-threatening pregnancy complications each year, including major blood loss, sepsis or the loss of reproductive organs. In rare cases, doctors might need to terminate a pregnancy to protect the health of the pregnant person, especially in cases where there is no chance for a fetus to survive.\par \par \uc2 Before the court blocked the state from enforcing the ban in health-threatening emergencies, some Idaho doctors reported that pregnant women were facing delays in care and in some cases being flown to out-of-state hospitals for treatment they would have previously been able to get at home.\par \par \uc2 Most Republican-controlled states have started enforcing new bans or restrictions since 2022. Currently, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/jul/29/abortion-laws-bans-by-state"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 12 states are enforcing bans on \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  at all stages of pregnancy, with limited exceptions, and four have bans that kick in at or about six weeks into pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250305el35001b9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
