\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  rejects anti- \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  challenges to clinic \u8216\'20\'18buffer zones\u8217\'20\'19\b0\par\par\uc2 Carter Sherman \par \uc2 699 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 February 2025\par 19:10 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Conservative-dominated court declined to hear two cases opposing ordinances limiting protests near \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics\par \par \uc2 In a loss for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  opponents, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US supreme court}}}\uc2  on Monday declined to take up two cases involving \u8220\'20\'1Cbuffer zone\u8221\'20\'1D ordinances, which limit protests around \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics and which anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists have spent years trying to dismantle.\par \par \uc2 The two cases dealt with buffer zone ordinances passed by the cities of Carbondale, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/illinois"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Illinois}}}\uc2 , and Englewood, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/new-jersey"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New Jersey}}}\uc2 . In filings to the supreme court, which is dominated 6-3 by conservatives, anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists argued that these ordinances ran afoul of the first amendment\u8217\'20\'19s guarantees of free speech. They also asked the justices to overturn a 2000 ruling called Hill v Colorado, which upheld a buffer zone law in Colorado.\par \par \uc2 The justices didn\u8217\'20\'19t explain why they declined to hear arguments in the cases, but the far-right justices {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/samuel-alito"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Samuel Alito}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/clarence-thomas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Clarence Thomas}}}\uc2  said they would have preferred to take them up. In a dissent outlining his desire to take the Carbondale case, Thomas wrote that he believed Hill \u8220\'20\'1Clacks continuing force\u8221\'20\'1D, in part due to recent rulings such as Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization, which overturned {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade}}}\uc2  and abolished the federal right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI would have taken this opportunity to explicitly overrule Hill,\u8221\'20\'1D he wrote. \u8220\'20\'1CFollowing our repudiation in Dobbs, I do not see what is left of Hill. Yet, lower courts continue to feel bound by it. The court today declines an invitation to set the record straight on Hill\u8217\'20\'19s defunct status.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Illinois case involved a 2023 ordinance that limited people from getting within 8ft of another individual if that individual is within 100ft of a healthcare facility, such as Carbondale\u8217\'20\'19s multiple \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics. In the wake of Roe\u8217\'20\'19s demise, Carbondale\u8217\'20\'19s clinics had become a haven for people fleeing the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans that now blanket much of the US south and midwest.\par \par \uc2 The anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  group Coalition Life sued over the ordinance, vowing to keep up the court fight even after Carbondale repealed it. The \u8220\'20\'1Cgamesmanship\u8221\'20\'1D over the ordinance, the group argued, only proved that \u8220\'20\'1CHill will continue to distort both the first amendment and public debates about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  unless and until it is overruled\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The New Jersey case, meanwhile, was brought by an anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protester named Jeryl Turco, who asked the justices to strike down a 2014 ordinance. That ordinance bans people from coming within 8ft of the entrances of certain healthcare facilities in Englewood \u8211\'20\'13 including \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics \u8211\'20\'13 unless they are patients, employees or passersby.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers and their supporters have spent years defending the idea of buffer zones, pointing to the high rates of violence and harassment that occur in and around US \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics. Over the last half-century, clinics have weathered more than 40 bombings, 200 arsons and 300 burglaries, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://prochoice.org/wp-content/uploads/2022-VD-Report-FINAL.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to the National \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Federation}}}\uc2 . Anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists have also killed at least 11 people.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics have also long relied on the protections of the Freedom of Access to Clinic Entrances Act, or Face, a federal law that is meant to penalize people who vandalize \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive health\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics or who threaten, obstruct or injure the individuals trying to enter those clinics. But after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  took office in January, his justice department vowed to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/jan/26/us-anti-abortion-movement-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 significantly curtail investigations}}}\uc2  into alleged Face violations. Trump also pardoned several anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists who had been recently convicted for violating Face.\par \par \uc2 In the years since it overturned Roe, the supreme court has shown hesitation around newer \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  cases. In 2024, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/jun/13/supreme-court-abortion-pill-access"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the justices rejected an attempt}}}\uc2  to limit access to mifepristone, a common \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill \u8211\'20\'13 but {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/jun/13/supreme-court-abortion-pill-mifepristone#:~:text=In%20a%209%2D0%20unanimous,in%20a%20US%20medication%20abortion."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 left the door open}}}\uc2  for a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/17/abortion-pill-mifepristone-lawsuit-texas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lower court to continue the case}}}\uc2 . The justices also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/jun/27/supreme-court-allows-emergency-abortions-idaho"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 punted on a case}}}\uc2  that questioned whether federal law requires hospitals to provide emergency abortions. That case is also continuing in a lower court.\par \par \uc2 Still, the supreme court is set to rule in at least one \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  case this term. In April, the high court will hear arguments in a case over whether South Carolina can cut the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  out of Medicaid funding.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250224el2o0030e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
