\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Missouri lawmaker proposes registry of pregnant women \u8216\'20\'18at risk\u8217\'20\'19 for abortions\b0\par\par\uc2 Carter Sherman \par \uc2 735 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 February 2025\par 12:02 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Dubbed \u8216\'20\'18eHarmony for babies\u8217\'20\'19, bill would create connected databases for pregnant women and those looking to adopt\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republican}}}\uc2  lawmaker in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/missouri"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Missouri}}}\uc2  has introduced legislation to create a registry of pregnant women who are \u8220\'20\'1Cat risk\u8221\'20\'1D of having an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 a proposal the bill\u8217\'20\'19s author characterized as an \u8220\'20\'1CeHarmony for babies\u8221\'20\'1D that could also help match adoptive parents with babies.\par \par \uc2 If passed, the bill would create two registries: one for people \u8220\'20\'1Cat risk\u8221\'20\'1D of abortions and one for people looking to adopt. Members of each registry could access the other, while Missouri government officials would be tasked with helping members meet each other and facilitating adoptions. The bill\u8217\'20\'19s goal is to \u8220\'20\'1Creduce the number of preventable abortions in Missouri\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMothers who choose to put their children up for adoption need to match with prospective adoptive parents,\u8221\'20\'1D Gerard Harms, an adoption attorney and the author of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://documents.house.mo.gov/billtracking/bills251/sumpdf/HB0807I.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Save MO Babies Act}}}\uc2 , testified in a Missouri state legislative committee hearing on Tuesday. \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s what this database is.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The bill does not define what puts someone \u8220\'20\'1Cat risk\u8221\'20\'1D of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Save MO Babies Act is the latest in a series of anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  efforts to expand government tracking of pregnant women and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  patients. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/project-2025"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Project 2025}}}\uc2 , the famous conservative policy playbook, suggested that the \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/05/project-2025-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 expand its \u8220\'20\'1Csurveillance\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  to force states to turn over data on \u8220\'20\'1Cexactly how many abortions take place within its borders, at what gestational age of the child, for what reason, the mother\u8217\'20\'19s state of residence, and by what method\u8221\'20\'1D, as well as information on miscarriages, stillbirths, and \u8220\'20\'1Ctreatments that incidentally result in the death of a child (such as chemotherapy)\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Project 2025 also proposes rolling back Joe Biden-era guidance that uses the Health Insurance Portability and Accountability Act (Hipaa), the US law governing patient privacy, to narrow the circumstances under which healthcare providers can talk to law enforcement about patients who may have undergone abortions. While still a senator, JD Vance signed on to a letter condemning the guidance. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/feb/01/anti-abortion-activists-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Alliance Defending Freedom}}}\uc2 , a conservative legal group that has spearheaded much of the rightwing attack on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and LGBTQ+ rights, has also sued over it.\par \par \uc2 In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://time.com/6972022/donald-trump-transcript-2024-election/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an interview with Time}}}\uc2  last year, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  signaled that he would be open to letting states monitor women\u8217\'20\'19s pregnancies to ascertain whether they had undergone abortions. \u8220\'20\'1CI think they might do that,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, adding: \u8220\'20\'1CThe states are going to say. It\u8217\'20\'19s irrelevant whether I\u8217\'20\'19m comfortable or not.\u8221\'20\'1D (He later tried to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.msnbc.com/the-reidout/reidout-blog/trump-time-interview-abortion-surveillance-rcna150914"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 walk that statement back}}}\uc2 .)\par \par \uc2 At the state level, Indiana is embroiled in a legal battle over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  patients\u8217\'20\'19 records, as the state\u8217\'20\'19s Republican governor and a local anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  group {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://indianacapitalchronicle.com/briefs/abortion-providers-sue-to-keep-state-records-private/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have sought to access records}}}\uc2  about the few people who have managed to recently undergo the procedure in Indiana. (The state {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/jul/29/abortion-laws-bans-by-state"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 only permits abortions}}}\uc2  in cases of rape, incest or medical emergency.) A judge {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://lawyeringproject.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/2025.02.19_Temporary-Restraining-Order.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ruled this week}}}\uc2  to block the records\u8217\'20\'19 release.\par \par \uc2 If the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  group obtains the records, the judge wrote, \u8220\'20\'1Cit will be free to publicize those medical records further, including by posting them on the Internet, depriving patients of their privacy, which cannot be adequately remedied through money damages\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, Harms suggested that people had misunderstood his intentions in writing the bill. The proposed Missouri registry, he said, was not an attempt \u8220\'20\'1Cto go out and data-mine\u8221\'20\'1D. Instead, he suggested that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics could provide patients with information about the registry so they could join it on their own.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a completely voluntary program as it comes to the parents of these children,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 The bill, Harms added, was \u8220\'20\'1Cinartfully drafted\u8221\'20\'1D and suggested that lawmakers should fine-tune the legislation.\par \par \uc2 It is not clear whether the bill will move forward. But Missouri Republican state lawmakers have introduced a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/dec/06/missouri-abortion-rights-amendment"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 barrage of other \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  restrictions}}}\uc2 , including legislation to roll back a November ballot measure that added \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights to the state constitution.\par \par \uc2 Missouri has moved to the epicenter of the national war over the procedure over the last few months. After the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/nov/05/abortion-ballot-results-tracker-ban-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 passage}}}\uc2  of the November ballot measure, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers sued to strike down the state\u8217\'20\'19s near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban and a raft of other restrictions on the procedure. Abortions finally {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/feb/15/judge-strikes-down-licensing-requirement-abortion-providers-missouri"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 resumed in the state this week}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250222el2m001e6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
