\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Trump signs executive order expanding access to IVF, says White House\b0\par\par\uc2 L\u233\'00\'E9onie Chao-Fong and Carter Sherman \par \uc2 405 \uc2 words\par \uc2 18 February 2025\par 22:44 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Order directs domestic policy council to suggest ways to \u8216\'20\'18aggressively\u8217\'20\'19 reduce cost of accessing in vitro fertilization\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  has signed an executive order to expand access to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/ivf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in vitro fertilization}}}\uc2  (IVF).\par \par \uc2 The order directs the domestic policy council to make recommendations to \u8220\'20\'1Caggressively\u8221\'20\'1D reduce the costs for accessing IVF, according to a White House fact sheet. Karoline Leavitt, the White House press secretary, said on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 /X that the order was evidence of the president\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cpromises kept\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 even though {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/fact-sheets/2025/02/fact-sheet-president-donald-j-trump-expands-access-to-in-vitro-fertilization-ivf/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the order}}}\uc2  does not directly change any policy and does not, on its own, fulfill Trump\u8217\'20\'19s campaign pledge to make the government or insurance companies cover IVF.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAmericans need reliable access to IVF and more affordable treatment options, as the cost per cycle can range from $12,000 to $25,000,\u8221\'20\'1D the fact sheet reads.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is the policy of my Administration to ensure reliable access to IVF treatment, including by easing unnecessary statutory or regulatory burdens to make IVF treatment drastically more affordable.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 During the 2024 presidential election, Trump recast his position on IVF as a strong supporter of the treatment, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2024/sep/21/trump-ivf-republicans-blocking-access"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 declaring himself the \u8220\'20\'1Cfather of IVF\u8221\'20\'1D }}}\uc2  while at the same time admitting he only recently discovered what the procedure involved.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s campaign promise to in effect make IVF freewas criticized by Democrats who accused him of softening his stance only after voters signaled broad support for \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 After the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  overturned Roe v Wade in a decision backed by three justices that Trump appointed, Republicans tried to distance themselves from the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement as pro-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights supporters repeatedly won ballot measures even in red states.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Tuesday order may now drive a further wedge between the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/trump-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump administration}}}\uc2  and the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement. The news of the order unleashed a torrent of complaints from anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists, who are largely opposed to IVF because it can create unused embryos (which they consider to be people).\par \par \uc2 Kristan Hawkins\uc2 , the president of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/feb/18/trump-ivf-executive-order"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Students for Life of America}}}\uc2 , tweeted that the news was \u8220\'20\'1Ctragic\u8221\'20\'1D and compared IVF with eugenics.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIVF turns children into a product to be created, sold, and discarded \u8211\'20\'13 violating their basic human rights,\u8221\'20\'1D tweeted \uc2 Lila Rose\uc2 , the leader of the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  group Live Action. In another tweet, she added: \u8220\'20\'1CIVF is NOT pro-life.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250218el2i00338\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
