\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Judge strikes down license requirement for  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  providers in Missouri\b0\par\par\uc2 Carter Sherman \par \uc2 398 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 February 2025\par 18:21 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Ruling enables providers to offer procedure, which voters enshrined in state constitution after fall of Roe in 2022\par \par \uc2 In a massive victory for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights supporters, a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/dec/06/missouri-abortion-rights-amendment"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Missouri}}}\uc2  judge on Friday blocked a licensing requirement for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics that providers said prevented them from offering the procedure.\par \par \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  announced shortly after the judge\u8217\'20\'19s ruling that its clinics would once again perform abortions in Missouri.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services are resuming in Missouri!\u8221\'20\'1D Planned Parenthood Great Plains, an affiliate that operates in Missouri, announced on \uc2 Facebook\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CWe are excited to soon offer care at select Missouri health centers, ensuring safe, compassionate and essential reproductive healthcare for those who need it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Margot Riphagen, president and CEO of Planned Parenthood Great Rivers, another Missouri affiliate, added in a statement: \u8220\'20\'1COur health center staff are quickly readying to restart this critical care in the coming days.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Abortions have been virtually banned in Missouri since 2022, when the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  overturned Roe v Wade and permitted much of the nation\u8217\'20\'19s south and midwest regions to outlaw the procedure. But in November, Missouri residents voted to pass a ballot measure adding \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights to the state constitution.\par \par \uc2 The ACLU of Missouri, Planned Parenthood Great Plains and Planned Parenthood Great Rivers then sued Missouri to strike down a bevy of anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws.\par \par \uc2 The Jackson county circuit court judge Jerri Zhang agreed to halt a number of those laws in December. But Zhang left in place a requirement that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics be licensed by the Missouri department of health and senior services \u8211\'20\'13 a policy that \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  said in court papers was \u8220\'20\'1Cmedically unnecessary\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 While that requirement was in place, the reproductive healthcare giant said its clinics could not perform abortions in Missouri.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt was so weaponized when we had to get licensure from the state. The state would delay,\u8221\'20\'1D Emily Wales, president and CEO of Planned Parenthood Great Plains, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/dec/23/missouri-abortion-rights-ruling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told the Guardian in December}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CThey would force us to litigate to get a license.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  asked Zhang to reconsider the ruling. In her Friday order, Zhang declared that the licensing requirement was \u8220\'20\'1Cdiscriminatory\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt does not treat services provided in \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  facilities the same as other types of similarly situated healthcare, including miscarriage care,\u8221\'20\'1D Zhang wrote.\par \par \uc2 The Missouri attorney general is likely to appeal Zhang\u8217\'20\'19s ruling.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250215el2f001e3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
