\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 JD Vance decried as extremist over attack on UK  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  clinic safe zones\b0\par\par\uc2 Alexandra Topping \par \uc2 712 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 February 2025\par 13:20 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 US vice-president\u8217\'20\'19s comments, part of a wide-ranging tirade against Europe, called inaccurate and misogynistic\par \par \uc2 JD Vance has been labelled an \u8220\'20\'1Cextremist\u8221\'20\'1D after he launched a broadside against the UK\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to protect women seeking an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The US vice-president\u8217\'20\'19s criticisms of UK and Scottish policies on safe access zones around \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics \u8211\'20\'13 part of a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/feb/14/jd-vance-stuns-munich-conference-with-blistering-attack-on-europes-leaders"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wide-ranging tirade against Europe on Friday}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 were derided as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/feb/14/thought-and-cancelled-elections-how-do-jd-vances-europe-claims-stand-up"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 inaccurate}}}\uc2  and misogynistic by a number of groups, politicians and governments.\par \par \uc2 Heidi Stewart, the chief executive of Bpas, the UK\u8217\'20\'19s leading provider of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services, said safe zones \u8211\'20\'13 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/oct/18/mps-back-plans-for-abortion-clinic-buffer-zones-in-england-and-wales"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 buffer areas}}}\uc2  of 150 metres around \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics designed to stop women being harassed with leaflets, shown pictures of foetuses, or having to pass by vigils \u8211\'20\'13 were vital to protect women\u8217\'20\'19s access to essential healthcare in an \u8220\'20\'1Coverwhelmingly pro-choice country\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBpas... will always remain proud to stand against misogynistic and anti-democratic interference with British women\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  by foreign extremists, whether they are the vice-president of the US or not,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 The Labour MP \uc2 Stella Creasy\uc2 , who campaigned for the safe zones which were introduced last year, posted a picture of a scene from the dystopian television series The Handmaid\u8217\'20\'19s Tale alongside with the words: \u8220\'20\'1CAnd so it begins \u8230\'20\'26 \u8221\'20\'1D She accused Vance of calling \u8220\'20\'1Cfor the right to harass women having an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D because \u8220\'20\'1Cour bodies are their battleground, our human rights their target\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In Vance\u8217\'20\'19s speech at the Munich security conference, he said the UK had \u8220\'20\'1Cplaced the basic liberties of religious Britons \u8230\'20\'26 in the crosshairs\u8221\'20\'1D, citing the prosecution of Adam Smith-Connor, a physiotherapist and army veteran. Vance said he had been charged with the \u8220\'20\'1Cheinous crime of standing 50 metres from an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic and silently praying for three minutes, not obstructing anyone, not interacting with anyone, just silently praying on his own\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Smith-Connor, who is receiving {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://adfinternational.org/en-gb/campaign/support-adam"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 legal support from Alliance Defending Freedom International}}}\uc2 , a conservative Christian legal advocacy group in the US, was convicted of breaching a safe zone in October last year after refusing repeated requests to move away from outside an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic in Bournemouth in November 2022.\par \par \uc2 A community officer spoke to him for an hour and 40 minutes and asked him to leave, but he refused. Smith-Connor was handed a two-year conditional discharge and ordered to pay more than \u163\'00\'A39,000 costs after the case brought by Bournemouth, Christchurch and \uc2 Poole council\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Vance also claimed the Scottish government had distributed letters to citizens whose houses lay \u8220\'20\'1Cwithin so-called safe access zones, warning them that even private prayer within their own homes may amount to breaking the law\u8221\'20\'1D. Shortly after his statement, a Scottish government spokesperson said: \u8220\'20\'1CThe vice-president\u8217\'20\'19s claim is incorrect. Private prayer at home is not prohibited within safe access zones and no letter has ever suggested it was.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.parliament.scot/bills-and-laws/bills/s6/abortion-services-safe-access-zones-scotland-bill"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Services (Safe Access Zones) (Scotland) Act}}}\uc2 , introduced last year, banned \u8220\'20\'1Csilent prayer\u8221\'20\'1D to prevent mass silent vigils that have been used by large groups of US pro-life protesters {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.marchforlife.co.uk/40-days-for-life-uk-vigils/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 such as 40 Days for Life}}}\uc2 . The law states that the actions are only banned if they are likely to cause alarm or distress to someone accessing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services.\par \par \uc2 The Scottish Green MSP Gillian Mackay, who pushed for the introduction of safe zones, said Vance was spreading \u8220\'20\'1Cshocking and shameless misinformation\u8221\'20\'1D. She said: \u8220\'20\'1CHe is one of the most powerful people in the world but he is peddling total nonsense and dangerous scaremongering.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The managing director for the \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Support Network, Camille Kumar, accused him of \u8220\'20\'1Cdog-whistle messaging\u8221\'20\'1D and an attack on \u8220\'20\'1Cfragile\u8221\'20\'1D women\u8217\'20\'19s rights. \u8220\'20\'1CIt is deeply concerning that within days of pardoning [protesters] in the US for their harassment of women and pregnant people outside \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics, JD Vance is now trying to stir up anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rhetoric in the UK.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The director of the End Violence, Andrea Simon, said: \u8220\'20\'1CSafe access buffer zones were introduced to ensure that women can safely access \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services without fear of harassment. That is vital, because \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a fundamental healthcare right for women in the UK, which must be protected.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250215el2f0015q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
