\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 Texas judge fines New York doctor for mailing  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  pills to patient in Texas\b0\par\par\uc2 Cecilia Nowell \par \uc2 801 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 February 2025\par 18:07 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Judge Bryan Gantt orders doctor to stop prescribing and sending pills to state, setting up challenge to \u8216\'20\'18shield laws\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 A Texas judge has ordered a New York doctor to immediately stop prescribing and mailing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills to patients in Texas, setting up a challenge to state \u8220\'20\'1Cshield laws\u8221\'20\'1D that could reach the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In his order Thursday, Judge Bryan Gantt of Collin county district court ordered Dr Margaret Daley Carpenter of New Paltz, who uses telemedicine to see patients across the country, to cease her work and pay a penalty of more than $100,000. The lawsuit was filed by Texas attorney general \uc2 Ken Paxton\uc2 , a close ally of Donald Trump, in December.\par \par \uc2 The case, which challenges the strength of \u8220\'20\'1Cshield laws\u8221\'20\'1D established to protect physicians offering \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care, is widely believed to be headed for the supreme court. Such laws emerged after the court overturned Roe v Wade in 2022 \u8211\'20\'13 and signify a growing divide among states since then.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, New York\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic governor, \uc2 Kathy Hochul\uc2 , said the state would not cooperate with an extradition request for Carpenter, filed by Louisiana officials in a separate case.\par \par \uc2 The Texas lawsuit alleges that Carpenter provided a 20-year-old woman with the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills mifepristone and misoprostol. After the woman sought follow-up care at her local emergency room, the \u8220\'20\'1Cbiological father of her unborn child\u8221\'20\'1D filed a complaint with the attorney general, according to court records. The anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  group Texas Right to Life has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/14/texas-anti-abortion-bills-filed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 encouraged men}}}\uc2  to report instances when they believe their partners may have received such \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care, and file wrongful death lawsuits against the physicians and friends who provided assistance.\par \par \uc2 A separate Louisiana lawsuit, the first criminal indictment of its kind, accuses Carpenter of sending the same pills to a pregnant teenager in that state.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI will not be signing an extradition order that came from the governor of Louisiana \u8211\'20\'13 not now, not ever,\u8221\'20\'1D Hochul said on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Carpenter has not commented directly on either case, but an organization she leads, called the \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Coalition for Telemedicine, released a statement on Thursday, saying: \u8220\'20\'1CToday\u8217\'20\'19s extradition order from a prosecutor with an anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  agenda is the latest escalation in Louisiana\u8217\'20\'19s ongoing state-sponsored effort to prosecute safe and effective healthcare.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It added: \u8220\'20\'1COngoing attempts by anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  state officials to restrict access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care are inconsistent with New York state law.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Louisiana\u8217\'20\'19s Republican governor, \uc2 Jeff Landry\uc2 , who signed the warrant for Carpenter to appear in court there, posted about the case on social media on Thursday: \u8220\'20\'1CThere is only one right answer in this situation: the doctor must face extradition to Louisiana where justice will be served.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Shield laws\par \par \uc2 Over the last five months of 2023, medical providers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/may/14/abortion-bans-shield-laws-telehealth-pills"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shipped \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  pills to more than 40,000 people}}}\uc2  living in states that forbid abortions via \u8220\'20\'1Cshield laws\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Since 2022, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://law.ucla.edu/academics/centers/center-reproductive-health-law-and-policy/shield-laws-reproductive-and-gender-affirming-health-care-state-law-guide"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 23 states and Washington DC}}}\uc2  have enacted such laws to protect providers offering reproductive healthcare, according to the \uc2 University of California, Los Angeles\uc2 . The laws represent a departure from previous interstate legal agreements.\par \par \uc2 The laws vary in scope state-to-state, with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://williamsinstitute.law.ucla.edu/wp-content/uploads/Shield-Law-NY-Sep-2024.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York\u8217\'20\'19s declaring}}}\uc2  that state and local entities may not cooperate with, or provide information or use resources in furtherance of, an out-of-state investigation of any \u8220\'20\'1Clegally protected \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive health\b0 \highlight\uc2  activity\u8221\'20\'1D. It also prohibits the state\u8217\'20\'19s governor from recognizing any extradition requests.\par \par \uc2 As a result of that wording, Carpenter and her attorneys did not respond to the Texas lawsuit or appear in court on Wednesday for a hearing before the judge, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2025/02/13/health/texas-new-york-abortion-pills-lawsuit.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the New York Times}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In a previous statement, Carpenter\u8217\'20\'19s organization said: \u8220\'20\'1CShield laws are essential in safeguarding and enabling \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care regardless of a patient\u8217\'20\'19s ZIP code or ability to pay.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 At a press conference regarding Louisiana\u8217\'20\'19s extradition order on Thursday, Hochul told reporters: \u8220\'20\'1CWe have put in place strict shield laws that anticipate this very situation.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Texas was the first state to initiate such legal action challenging shield laws, and the Louisiana case against Carpenter is the first such criminal indictment.\par \par \uc2 Such laws could end up before the supreme court if Texas files a petition in New York state court to collect the financial penalty it ordered Carpenter to pay. Alongside a $100,000 fine and about $13,000 in attorneys\u8217\'20\'19 fees and court costs, the Texas judge also ordered Carpenter to immediately cease prescribing and mailing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills. Violating an injunction can result in a contempt order that may carry additional financial penalties.\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 The last paragraph of this article was amended on 14 February 2025. The judge is from Texas and not New York, as an earlier version said.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250214el2e000b5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
