\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 First Thing: Zelenskyy and Vance to meet after Macron warns not to \u8216\'20\'18capitulate\u8217\'20\'19 to Russia\b0\par\par\uc2 Clea Skopeliti \par \uc2 1,066 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 February 2025\par 12:49 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 European leaders to put pressure on US vice-president to involve them in talks over Ukraine. Plus, Texas judge fines New York doctor for mailing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills\par \par \uc2 Good morning.\par \par \uc2 The US vice-president, JD Vance, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/feb/14/vance-zelenskyy-europe-ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is to meet the Ukrainian president, Volodymyr Zelenskyy, and other European leaders}}}\uc2  in Munich, after widespread criticism of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s statements on Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Following a phone call with \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  on Wednesday, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/feb/12/trump-putin-ukraine-ceasefire"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump said he believed it was \u8220\'20\'1Cunlikely\u8221\'20\'1D Ukraine would be able}}}\uc2  to regain much of its territory and he was \u8220\'20\'1COK\u8221\'20\'1D with it not joining \uc2 Nato\uc2 . In an interview with the Wall Street Journal on Friday, Vance tried to stymie condemnation of Trump for what appeared to be premature and unilateral concessions, saying the US would be willing to impose sanctions on Russia if Moscow did not accept a satisfactory deal and that the option of sending US troops remained on the table.\par \par \uc2 European leaders will put pressure on Vance to involve them in talks over Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s fate when they meet, stressing that their security is bound to Kyiv\u8217\'20\'19s. The French president, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/feb/14/ukraine-war-macron-warns-of-risk-of-capitulation-as-trump-suggests-russia-may-not-make-any-concessions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Emmanuel Macron, has been among those demanding}}}\uc2  the US be more cautious, saying: \u8220\'20\'1C A peace that is a capitulation is bad news for everyone.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What\u8217\'20\'19s the reaction\par \par \uc2 in Ukraine?\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/feb/13/i-feel-angry-and-betrayed-ukrainians-react-to-donald-trumps-call-to-putin"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Anger and betrayal were common emotions}}}\uc2  among those the Guardian spoke to in Kyiv. Zelenskyy called the Putin-Trump call \u8220\'20\'1Cunpleasant\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 but clearly cognizant of being unable to burn bridges, said the subsequent call he had with Trump was \u8220\'20\'1Ca very good conversation\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Hamas\uc2  expected to name Israeli hostages it will free this weekend\par \par \uc2 Hamas\uc2  is expected on Friday to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2025/feb/14/israel-gaza-war-hostages-ceasefire-middle-east-latest-news?page=with:block-67aef0878f085b5f5c28c232#block-67aef0878f085b5f5c28c232"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 name three hostages it will release this weekend}}}\uc2  under the terms of the ceasefire agreement, according to local media, while the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2025/feb/14/israel-gaza-war-hostages-ceasefire-middle-east-latest-news?page=with:block-67af12d98f085b5f5c28c32c#block-67af12d98f085b5f5c28c32c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Israeli government has signalled it will also stick the deal}}}\uc2 , after the fragile peace appeared to be close to breaking point this week.\par \par \uc2 The Israeli prime minister\u8217\'20\'19s office on Thursday issued a statement clarifying its expectation for the continuation of the ceasefire. \u8220\'20\'1CThere is a framework in place for the release of our hostages,\u8221\'20\'1D the spokesperson David Mencer said. \u8220\'20\'1CThat framework makes clear that three live hostages must be released by \uc2 Hamas\uc2  terrorists on Saturday.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The statement follows nearly three days of confusion after Trump declared that Israel should demand \uc2 Hamas\uc2  release all the remaining hostages by Saturday or resume its war. It also comes after \uc2 Hamas\uc2  suggested it could delay the release of hostages due to what it said were violations by the Israeli army, before walking back the threat on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 How many hostages remain with \uc2 Hamas\uc2 ? There are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/feb/13/israel-stick-to-hostage-release-plan-if-hamas-honours-schedule-gaza"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 76 people, though it is unclear}}}\uc2  how many are still alive.\par \par \uc2 Texas judge fines New York doctor for mailing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills to patient in Texas\par \par \uc2 A Texas judge has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/feb/13/texas-abortion-pills-shield-laws-new-york-doctor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ordered a New York doctor to stop mailing \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  pills}}}\uc2  to patients in Texas and fined her more than $100,000, in a case expected to go to the supreme court.\par \par \uc2 Judge Bryan Gantt of Collin county district court on Thursday ordered Dr Margaret Daley Carpenter of the town of New Paltz in New York state to cease prescribing and mailing the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills.\par \par \uc2 The case, which follows a lawsuit filed by the Texas attorney general, \uc2 Ken Paxton\uc2 , an ally of Trump, challenges the limits of \u8220\'20\'1Cshield laws\u8221\'20\'1D, which were established after the fall of Roe v Wade to protect physicians offering abortions.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 How did the case come to be? The \u8220\'20\'1Cbiological father of an unborn child\u8221\'20\'1D of an alleged patient of Carpenter filed a complaint with the attorney general \u8211\'20\'13 a tactic encouraged by anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups.\par \par \uc2 In other news \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Mexico\u8217\'20\'19s president has accused the US of harboring drug cartels and working with Mexican organized crime,\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/feb/13/claudia-sheinbaum-us-drug-cartel"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 responding to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s claim}}}\uc2  that her government was in an \u8220\'20\'1Cintolerable alliance\u8221\'20\'1D with traffickers.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A federal judge has temporarily halted\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s executive order to limit gender-affirming healthcare for trans youth,\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/feb/13/trump-trans-youth-healthcare-order"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 putting the directive on hold}}}\uc2  for 14 days.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The\par \par \uc2 National Park Service\par \par \uc2 culled all references to trans people from its website for the Stonewall national monument on Thursday,\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/feb/13/stonewall-website-transgender"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 despite the 1969 riot there, which sparked the contemporary gay rights movement}}}\uc2 , being led by trans women.\par \par \uc2 Stat of the day: $1tn of investment in AI has already been announced in 2025\par \par \uc2 We are not even two months into the year, but {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2025/feb/14/ai-godfathers-paris-industry-dangers-future"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  about $1tn of fresh investment in AI}}}\uc2  has already been announced, notes the columnist Alexander Hurst in a dispatch from a conference in the lead-up to the Paris AI summit. This is despite the colossal amounts of energy the datacenters use to train and run systems \u8211\'20\'13 and the threats that the technology\u8217\'20\'19s godfathers told Hurst they believe it may pose in the near future.\par \par \uc2 Don\u8217\'20\'19t miss this: De La Soul on grief, Gorillaz and never giving up\par \par \uc2 If the trio now known as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/music/2025/feb/14/hip-hop-de-la-soul-grief-gorillaz-trugoy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 De La Soul hadn\u8217\'20\'19t failed an English exam in 1985}}}\uc2 , the world might never have heard 3 Feet High and Rising, as the three met that summer when they were stuck inside studying at their Long Island high school. Ahead of the release of their new album, Kelvin \u8220\'20\'1CPosdnuos\u8221\'20\'1D Mercer and Vincent \u8220\'20\'1CMaseo\u8221\'20\'1D Mason talk about losing their bandmate Dave \u8220\'20\'1CTrugoy the Dove\u8221\'20\'1D Jolicoeur two years ago and how their creative, warm sound brought hip-hop to new audiences.\par \par \uc2 Climate check: Richest nations\u8217\'20\'19 demand for beef, palm oil and timber driving extinction\par \par \uc2 The world\u8217\'20\'19s richest {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2025/feb/14/richest-nations-exporting-extinction-with-demand-for-beef-palm-oil-and-timber-aoe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 countries are eliminating 15 times more biodiversity abroad}}}\uc2  than within their own borders, research shows, driven by their demand for products including beef, palm oil, and timber. The US was responsible for 3% of the world\u8217\'20\'19s non-US forest habitat destruction, with wealthy countries behind 13% of such damage.\par \par \uc2 Last Thing: Scientists sniff ancient mummies\par \par \uc2 Science has moved on from using samples to date ancient remains: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/science/2025/feb/14/smell-like-an-egyptian-researchers-sniff-ancient-mummies-to-study-preservation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 researchers are now relying on the human nose}}}\uc2  (well, alongside scientific instruments) to tell how well-preserved an Egyptian mummy is. What does it smell like? \u8220\'20\'1CSpicy, woody and sweet\u8221\'20\'1D, apparently.\par \par \uc2 Sign up\par \par \uc2 First Thing is delivered to thousands of inboxes every weekday. If you\u8217\'20\'19re not already signed up, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/info/2018/sep/17/guardian-us-morning-briefing-sign-up-to-stay-informed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 subscribe now}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Get in touch\par \par \uc2 If you have any questions or comments about any of our newsletters please email {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:newsletters@theguardian.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 newsletters@theguardian.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250214el2e00231\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
