\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Meta\uc2  accused of \u8216\'20\'18bowing\u8217\'20\'19 to Trump by making  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  content harder to find\b0\par\par\uc2 Jessica Glenza \par \uc2 438 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 February 2025\par 22:15 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Democratic senator concerned after company is accused of \u8216\'20\'18shadow-banning\u8217\'20\'19 non-profits offering medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 Senator Ruben Gallego has accused social media giant \uc2 Meta\uc2  of \u8220\'20\'1Cpresumptively bowing\u8221\'20\'1D to the Trump administration by making \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related content more difficult to find.\par \par \uc2 Meta\uc2 , the parent company of \uc2 Facebook\uc2  and \uc2 Instagram\uc2 , was accused of \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/jan/29/abortion-pills-instagram-shadow-banning"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shadow-banning}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D several non-profits who provide medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to women in the US.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am deeply concerned at the chilling effect that suppressing content related to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has towards women,\u8221\'20\'1D Gallego wrote in a letter sent to the company on Friday. \u8220\'20\'1CWomen around the country rely on medicated \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as safe and effective way to address deeply personal health decisions.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A dozen states across the south-east and midwest {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/jul/29/abortion-laws-bans-by-state"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ban \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 . Four states ban the procedure past six weeks of gestation, before most women know they are pregnant.\par \par \uc2 Non-profits, such as Aid Access, have responded by providing medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to women in all 50 states using \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.kff.org/other/state-indicator/shield-laws/?currentTimeframe=0&sortModel=%7B%22colId%22:%22Location%22,%22sort%22:%22asc%22%7D"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shield laws}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 protections passed by states friendly to \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  that prevent healthcare providers from legal consequences in \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -ban states.\par \par \uc2 In Gallego\u8217\'20\'19s letter, the senator describes how Aid Access had posts removed from \uc2 Facebook\uc2  and blurred on \uc2 Instagram\uc2 . The organization was also locked out of \uc2 Facebook\uc2  and briefly suspended from \uc2 Instagram\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The experience mirrors that of other medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  organizations, such as telehealth clinic Hey Jane, whose spokesperson {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/jan/29/abortion-pills-instagram-shadow-banning"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told the Guardian}}}\uc2  that \uc2 Instagram\uc2  made its posts harder to find. Other groups, Women Help Women and Just the Pill, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2025/01/23/technology/instagram-facebook-abortion-pill-providers.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told the New York Times}}}\uc2  their accounts were suspended and restored.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am also troubled by the timing of these events,\u8221\'20\'1D said Gallego, in the letter. \u8220\'20\'1CTaken together, \uc2 Meta\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s decision to end fact-checking, while simultaneously restricting access to content related to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , looks like a calculated move to avoid the ire of President Trump, a well-known opponent of both \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and attempts to limit mis- and disinformation.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Gallego asks \uc2 Meta\uc2  for its \u8220\'20\'1Crationale\u8221\'20\'1D for removing content related to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ; why it was removed \u8220\'20\'1Cspecifically in the weeks\u8221\'20\'1D following Trump\u8217\'20\'19s election victory, and whether the removals were in \u8220\'20\'1Cspecific states\u8221\'20\'1D or nationally.\par \par \uc2 In a statement, a \uc2 Meta\uc2  spokesperson told the Guardian when the removals were first reported: \u8220\'20\'1CThese groups encountered both correct enforcement and a variety of issues, including over enforcement and a technical bug, that resulted in the blurring of some posts. But we\u8217\'20\'19ve been quite clear in recent weeks that we want to allow more speech and reduce enforcement mistakes \u8211\'20\'13 and we\u8217\'20\'19re committed to doing that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250203el230038u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
