\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Wyoming Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 anti- \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  bill inadvertently targets chemotherapy and surgeries\b0\par\par\uc2 Cy Neff \par \uc2 1,041 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 February 2025\par 17:21 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Senate File 125 could limit access to any treatment that \u8216\'20\'18causes harm\u8217\'20\'19 to the heart, lungs, brain and other organs\par \par \uc2 In an effort to restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/wyoming"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Wyoming}}}\uc2  Republicans authored a bill that could choke access to a host of life-saving medical procedures, from chemotherapy to heart surgery.\par \par \uc2 State judge Melissa Owens {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/politics/elections/2024/11/19/wyoming-abortion-ban-blocked/76425067007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturned Wyoming\u8217\'20\'19s \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  bans}}}\uc2  in November 2024, citing the state\u8217\'20\'19s constitutionally guaranteed right to healthcare. The Republican state senator Cheri Steinmetz and the bill\u8217\'20\'19s eight co-sponsors took issue with the ruling, and sought to draw up a definition of healthcare that excludes \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe intent of [Senate File] 125 is to do no harm and go back to that Hippocratic oath and look at healthcare through that lens,\u8221\'20\'1D Steinmeitz told the Guardian.\par \par \uc2 Steinmetz says {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wyoleg.gov/Legislation/2025/SF0125"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Senate File 125}}}\uc2  offers a new definition of healthcare in Wyoming: \u8220\'20\'1CNo act, treatment or procedure that causes harm to the heart, respiratory system, central nervous system, brain, skeletal system, jointed or muscled appendages or organ function shall be construed as healthcare.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The bill carves out exceptions \u8211\'20\'13 for example, when such a procedure is required to save the life of a pregnant woman, or if \u8220\'20\'1Ca person has no chance of meaningful recovery\u8221\'20\'1D without it. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/23/trump-executive-order-fetal-personhood"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fetal personhood}}}\uc2  is still on the books in Wyoming from 2023\u8217\'20\'19s overturned \u8220\'20\'1CLife Is a Human Right Act\u8221\'20\'1D, but experts interviewed said that the murkiness of the bill\u8217\'20\'19s language made it unclear if it would succeed at restricting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access \u8211\'20\'13 its intended purpose.\par \par \uc2 But Wyoming attorneys and healthcare law professionals at \uc2 Boston University\uc2 , \uc2 George Washington University\uc2 , Johns Hopkins and Pittsburgh University, say the problem is that a broad swath of healthcare procedures can be considered to cause \u8220\'20\'1Charm \u8221\'20\'1D by design.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s a slew of medical procedures, surgeries, treatments that can have potentially positive outcomes but may also cause harm in the short period or as an unintended consequence,\u8221\'20\'1D the Wyoming attorney Abigail Fournier said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s scary to me, because I think it could be interpreted to be very limiting in terms of what healthcare providers can do.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Wyoming\u8217\'20\'19s constitutional right to healthcare stems from a 2012, voter-ratified constitutional amendment stating that \u8220\'20\'1Cthe right to make healthcare decisions is reserved to the citizens of the state of Wyoming\u8221\'20\'1D. Tom Lubnau, Wyoming attorney and former Republican speaker of the state house, helped author the amendment. He sees much of the current legislature as having \u8220\'20\'1Ctunnel vision\u8221\'20\'1D, and a fixation on passing social issue legislation that ignores constitutionality.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHealthcare decisions are the individual\u8217\'20\'19s in Wyoming. And that\u8217\'20\'19s what the freedom amendment says,\u8221\'20\'1D Lubnau said. \u8220\'20\'1CButt out of my decisions, and let me take care of myself.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Lubnau sits on one side of Wyoming\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/politics/elections/2024/11/05/wyoming-election-republican-conservative-changes/75962807007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 gaping Republican divide}}}\uc2 , which pits an older class of more moderate, establishment Republicans against the state\u8217\'20\'19s further-right Freedom Caucus, who, this past election cycle, became the first Freedom Caucus chapter to take {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/14/wyoming-freedom-caucus"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 control of a state house}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Freedom Caucus has wasted no time in pushing a mass of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://wyofile.com/wyoming-freedom-caucus-five-and-dime-flies-through-house/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 social issue bills}}}\uc2  that line up neatly with national conservative talking points. Among the focuses are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wyoleg.gov/Legislation/2025/HB0147"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dismantling DEI programming}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://wyofile.com/wyoming-lawmakers-double-down-on-protecting-female-spaces-with-bills-to-police-gender-in-bathrooms-sports/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 strict definitions of gender}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://wyofile.com/trumps-deportation-agenda-taking-hold-with-wyoming-legislature-some-sheriffs/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 immigration restrictions}}}\uc2  and a glut of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://wyofile.com/abortion-restrictions-pass-through-house-panel-with-no-questions-from-members-on-public-testimony/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  restrictions}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Boston University\uc2  healthcare law professor Nicole Huberfeld has seen plenty of crafty attempts to restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, such as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2019/dec/09/supreme-court-kentucky-abortion-law-doctors-ultrasound"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 transvaginal ultrasound requirements}}}\uc2 , or laws mandating \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics meet the licensing requirements of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/politics/2024/03/04/wyoming-approve-abortion-restrictions/72790394007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ambulatory surgical centers}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But Huberfeld and other experts interviewed said that they had yet to encounter a bill looking to redefine healthcare entirely.\par \par \uc2 Huberfeld will not be surprised if other states follow Wyoming\u8217\'20\'19s lead, particularly those that have constitutional rights to healthcare.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf they don\u8217\'20\'19t have bills like this, I expect that they will take a page from Wyoming\u8217\'20\'19s book and try the same thing,\u8221\'20\'1D Huberfeld said.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 George Washington University\uc2  law professor Sonia Suter said the bill fit into a broader trend of taking away authority from medical professionals and putting it into the hands of politicians.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s a lot less faith in professional expertise, scientists, medicine,\u8221\'20\'1D Suter said. \u8220\'20\'1CLegislators are coming in and trying to pass laws that are less about healthcare and more about some kind of moral agenda, religious agenda. This is a way to sort of give the legislature more power.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 When asked if any doctors or medical professionals were consulted in the authoring of the bill, Steinmetz said that she received the bill from an attorney, and was not sure who the attorney sourced input from. She said that the bills\u8217\'20\'19 sponsors were aware of concerns about chemotherapy and other procedures \u8211\'20\'13 and that they would sort it out if the bill moved forward.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have the best of intentions, and sometimes bills start out a little rockier than others,\u8221\'20\'1D Steinmetz said.\par \par \uc2 Joanne Rosen, health law professor at \uc2 Johns Hopkins University\uc2 , is less worried with the intentions behind the bill, and more so with the effects of bills that seek to carve out \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 and end up affecting less \u8220\'20\'1Ccontroversial\u8221\'20\'1D forms of healthcare.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt has the effect of chilling physicians from administering medical treatment because they worry they may be in violation of the law. That\u8217\'20\'19s a significant concern,\u8221\'20\'1D Rosen said.\par \par \uc2 While attorneys interviewed confirmed that voter referendums are necessary to make changes to Wyoming\u8217\'20\'19s constitution, Steinmetz said that the bill did not seek to change the constitution \u8211\'20\'13 just a definition.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CObviously it\u8217\'20\'19s not spelled out in the constitution that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is healthcare, and so we can put limitations on that,\u8221\'20\'1D Steinmeitz said.\par \par \uc2 Still, Clark Stith, Wyoming attorney and former Republican state speaker pro tempore, is not sold.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis bill, which purports to provide rules of construction of the Wyoming constitution, simply can\u8217\'20\'19t do that,\u8221\'20\'1D Stith said. \u8220\'20\'1CA statute cannot change the meaning of words in the constitution. Period. End of story.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Stith also wondered why, if \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is such a central priority, politicians put the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  question in the hands of Wyoming\u8217\'20\'19s voters.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhy aren\u8217\'20\'19t you bringing it as a proposed constitutional amendment?\u8221\'20\'1D Stith asked. \u8220\'20\'1CWhy aren\u8217\'20\'19t you bringing it as a joining resolution to get placed on the ballot?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250202el22001p7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
