\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 This anti- \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  leader is building on \u8216\'20\'18the ultimate victory from the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19\b0\par\par\uc2 Carter Sherman \par \uc2 1,245 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 February 2025\par 20:12 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Erik Baptist, with \uc2 Alliance Defending Freedom\uc2 , has his sights set on mifepristone after the fall of Roe v Wade\par \par \uc2 Dozens of anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists streamed into the conference room of a Washington DC hotel. They jostled for seats as speakers, dotted throughout the room, blasted a song about the need to be \u8220\'20\'1Ca little more like Jesus, a little less like me\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 By the time a trio of advocates, assembled on a dais at the front of the room, started to talk about the \u8220\'20\'1CFuture of Chemical \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in America\u8221\'20\'1D, the title of one of the first seminars at the National Pro-Life Summit, it was standing room only.\par \par \uc2 When it was Erik Baptist\u8217\'20\'19s turn to address the crowd, he said: \u8220\'20\'1CChemical \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is the No 1 priority and issue of our time, for the life movement,\u8221\'20\'1D using the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement\u8217\'20\'19s lingo for medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which is performed with pills.\par \par \uc2 Baptist is in a rare position to do something about it.\par \par \uc2 Since July, Baptist has led the Center for Life at the Christian legal group {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/jun/19/alliance-defending-freedom-lgbtq-rights-america"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Alliance Defending Freedom}}}\uc2  (\uc2 ADF\uc2 ), one of the foremost conservative advocacy organizations in the US.\par \par \uc2 Formed in 1994, the \uc2 ADF\uc2  is today the rightwing answer to \uc2 the American Civil Liberties Union\uc2 . The legal group\u8217\'20\'19s attorneys are at the forefront of virtually every conservative cause du jour, such as campus free speech, access to gender-affirming care and, of course, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 ADF\uc2  played a critical role in demolishing Roe v Wade, as it helped craft the model bill that became the Mississippi \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban that overturned Roe. But its lawyers have also been a part of recent supreme court cases over access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills and emergency abortions.\par \par \uc2 As the Center for Life\u8217\'20\'19s director, these kinds of efforts are now within Baptist\u8217\'20\'19s purview.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe do have a comprehensive approach to lawsuits and what we\u8217\'20\'19re trying to do. We\u8217\'20\'19re obviously trying to win in courts and try to protect as many unborn lives as we can and support mothers who [are] in unplanned pregnancies. And how we execute that manifests itself in multiple ways,\u8221\'20\'1D said Baptist, who is also senior counsel at the \uc2 ADF\uc2  and served as one of the \uc2 Environmental Protection Agency\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s top lawyers during Donald Trump\u8217\'20\'19s first term.\par \par \uc2 He added: \u8220\'20\'1CWe have brought cases on behalf of pregnant centers, sidewalk counselors, pro-life doctors, and we\u8217\'20\'19ll continue to do that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In an interview a few days after the summit, Baptist laid out many of the \uc2 ADF\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s priorities for 2025 \u8211\'20\'13 and the organization is poised to have a big year.\par \par \uc2 In December 2024, a petition by \uc2 ADF\uc2  attorneys convinced the supreme court to hear oral arguments in Kerr v Planned Parenthood South Atlantic, a case that could determine whether states can refuse to send Medicaid funds to \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2 . Defunding Planned Parenthood, the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement\u8217\'20\'19s arch-nemesis, has long been one of the movement\u8217\'20\'19s most cherished goals.\par \par \uc2 Then there\u8217\'20\'19s the fight over the federal Emergency Medical Treatment and Labor Act, known as Emtala, which requires hospitals to stabilize patients who arrive at their doors in emergencies. The Biden administration said that Emtala also covers emergency abortions, but \uc2 ADF\uc2  attorneys have joined Idaho \u8211\'20\'13 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/oct/21/idaho-abortion-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 home to one of the nation\u8217\'20\'19s strictest \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  bans}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 in fighting that interpretation. That case went all the way up to the supreme court last year but, like the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills case, is now continuing in a lower court. The \uc2 ADF\uc2  is also involved in at least two other cases over Emtala.\par \par \uc2 Baptist walked summit attendees through the \u8220\'20\'1Cfuture of chemical \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  litigation\u8221\'20\'1D, which, he predicted, will be divided between two lines of lawsuits. One line follows a case, originally filed by the \uc2 ADF\uc2  on behalf of anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  doctors, that targets the Food and Drug Administration\u8217\'20\'19s regulation of the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill mifepristone.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 ADF\uc2  argued the case all the way to the supreme court \u8211\'20\'13 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/jun/13/supreme-court-abortion-pill-access"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 only for the high court to rule 9-0}}}\uc2  that the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  plaintiffs lacked the legal standing needed to bring the case. Earlier this month, however, a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/17/abortion-pill-mifepristone-lawsuit-texas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas federal judge agreed to let three states}}}\uc2  resurrect the case.\par \par \uc2 That judge, Matthew Kacsmaryk, offers a keyhole glimpse into \uc2 ADF\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s far-reaching network. A Trump appointee, Kacsmaryk {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.newyorker.com/magazine/2023/10/09/alliance-defending-freedoms-legal-crusade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 once worked for a Christian advocacy group}}}\uc2  that received grants from the \uc2 ADF\uc2 . Graduates of an \uc2 ADF\uc2  program for law students have interned and clerked for his chambers. Graduates from the same program have also clerked for supreme court justices \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  and \uc2 Amy Coney Barrett\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 the latter of whom, prior to her ascension to the supreme court, had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/coney-barrett-christian-law-fellowship-blackstone/2020/09/27/7ae41892-fdc5-11ea-b555-4d71a9254f4b_story.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 spoken five times at an ADF program}}}\uc2  designed in service of a \u8220\'20\'1Cdistinctly Christian worldview in every area of law\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Baptist told attendees at the summit, who included many high school and college students, that the future of the mifepristone case looks rosy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI frankly think the supreme court will be annoyed with those blue states, such as California and New York, trying to undermine the promise of Dobbs,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, in a reference to Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health, the case that overturned Roe. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m looking forward to the future of that litigation.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 ADF\uc2 , Baptist added in an interview, is \u8220\'20\'1Cno longer involved\u8221\'20\'1D with the case. \u8220\'20\'1CBut we do support those efforts,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 The second line of litigation will focus on efforts to take down blue-state shield laws, which are intended to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers who mail \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills across state lines. Between April and June of last year, providers offered nearly 10,000 abortions each month through shield laws, according to data from #WeCount, a research project by the Society of Family Planning.\par \par \uc2 Texas, Baptist noted at the Summit, recently sued a New York doctor for allegedly prescribing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills to a Texan. On Friday, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/31/new-york-louisiana-abortion-pill-charges"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a Louisiana grand jury indicted}}}\uc2  the same doctor for allegedly prescribing an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill in the southern state.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey need to be taken down, too,\u8221\'20\'1D Baptist told summit attendees of shield laws. The divide between states like New York and Texas will, he said, \u8220\'20\'1Cprobably, again, create a constitutional crisis. And again, I think the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s not going to be happy.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In 2023, the first full year after Roe fell, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/27/post-roe-abortion-rate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the US saw more than 1m abortions}}}\uc2 , according to the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2 , which tracks abortions and restrictions on the procedure. It was the largest number recorded in more than a decade \u8211\'20\'13 which has infuriated anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists and led them to heavily target \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills, which account for roughly two-thirds of US abortions.\par \par \uc2 With Trump now in office, Baptist believes that lawsuits may not be necessary to implement anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  aims.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe executive branch, on its own accord, without litigation, can do the right thing as well,\u8221\'20\'1D he said in an interview. Under Trump, he indicated, the Food and Drug Administration could roll back its own approval of mifepristone, yanking it from the market.\par \par \uc2 But if the \uc2 ADF\uc2  has to sue, it will.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSince 2011, we have won 15 times at the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 , and ultimately a lot of our lawsuits end up there,\u8221\'20\'1D Baptist said. \u8220\'20\'1CSo you may have losses along the way, but when you have the ultimate victory from the supreme court \u8211\'20\'13 that\u8217\'20\'19s the most important one to judge our cases by.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250201el21001gt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
