\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 At least five senior \uc2 FBI\uc2  leaders reportedly demoted or moved as Trump\u8217\'20\'19s nominee is grilled by senators \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Robert Mackey (now); L\u233\'00\'E9onie Chao-Fong, Alice Herman and Christy Cooney (earlier) \par \uc2 13,114 \uc2 words\par \uc2 31 January 2025\par 03:22 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This liveblog is now closed.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.14am GMT\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 As attention in Washington turns to the tragic loss of life near Reagan National airport, we are wrapping up this politics live blog, but will return to chronicle new developments on Friday. Here is an overview of the day:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  pre-empted the federal investigation by experts into the air disaster by speculating, in line with the prevailing views on Fox News, that somehow a push for diversity had lowered standards in the nation\u8217\'20\'19s air traffic controller ranks. His comments, at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/30/trump-washington-dc-plane-crash"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a news conference}}}\uc2  that reminded many of his deeply partisan 2020 Covid briefings, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2025/jan/30/donald-trump-guantanamo-bay-rfk-jr-tulsi-gabbard-fbi-kash-patel-us-politics-latest-news?page=with:block-679bfb1c8f08a29ab875704a#block-679bfb1c8f08a29ab875704a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 prompted outrage}}}\uc2  from the Congressional Black caucus and other Democrats.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kash Patel, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s nominee to lead the \uc2 FBI\uc2 , was accused of being {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2025/jan/30/donald-trump-guantanamo-bay-rfk-jr-tulsi-gabbard-fbi-kash-patel-us-politics-latest-news?page=with:block-679bdb818f084dac099e35d8#block-679bdb818f084dac099e35d8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 happy to lie for Trump}}}\uc2  at his senate confirmation hearing.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Robert F Kennedy won\u8217\'20\'19t commit to keeping \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill mifepristone on market. Kennedy, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2025/jan/30/donald-trump-guantanamo-bay-rfk-jr-tulsi-gabbard-fbi-kash-patel-us-politics-latest-news?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with%3Ablock-679ba6938f08a29ab8756bce#block-679ba6938f08a29ab8756bce"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pressed}}}\uc2  to answer whether he would keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill on the market, refused to say that he would.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 At least five senior \uc2 FBI\uc2  leaders who were promoted by the bureau\u8217\'20\'19s former director, \uc2 Christopher Wray\uc2 , have been notified they are being {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2025/jan/30/donald-trump-guantanamo-bay-rfk-jr-tulsi-gabbard-fbi-kash-patel-us-politics-latest-news?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with%3Ablock-679bd61e8f084dac099e3589#block-679bd61e8f084dac099e3589"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 demoted or reassigned}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Tulsi Gabbard\uc2 , in her opening remarks at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2025/jan/30/donald-trump-guantanamo-bay-rfk-jr-tulsi-gabbard-fbi-kash-patel-us-politics-latest-news?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with%3Ablock-679ba1e68f088478fa0ca1c7#block-679ba1e68f088478fa0ca1c7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 her confirmation hearing}}}\uc2  for national intelligence chief, said that she has \u8220\'20\'1Cno love for Assad, Gaddafi, or any dictator, I just hate al-Qaida\u8221\'20\'1D. Gabbard was pushing back against criticism for her 2017 meeting with the then Syrian dictator \uc2 Bashar al-Assad\uc2 , during a visit to Damascus, Syria, that will become a focal point of questioning during the hearing.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Brendan Carr\uc2 , the new, pro-Trump chairman of the \uc2 Federal Communications Commission\uc2  has opened an investigation into corporate sponsorship of public media. Carr {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2025/jan/30/donald-trump-guantanamo-bay-rfk-jr-tulsi-gabbard-fbi-kash-patel-us-politics-latest-news?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with%3Ablock-679c235e8f084dac099e3810#block-679c235e8f084dac099e3810"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 warned}}}\uc2  the heads of NPR and \uc2 PBS\uc2  that his findings could be used by Republicans in Congress to end all funding for the networks.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump administration froze $45m of aid, most of it for Gaza, none of it for condoms. A United Nations agency that promotes sexual and \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive health\b0 \highlight{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2025/jan/30/donald-trump-guantanamo-bay-rfk-jr-tulsi-gabbard-fbi-kash-patel-us-politics-latest-news?page=with:block-679bea2d8f088478fa0ca5f3#block-679bea2d8f088478fa0ca5f3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 confirmed to the Guardian}}}\uc2  that it did have state department funding for its in work Gaza and the West Bank frozen by the Trump administration, but none of that funding was for condoms.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.22am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.32am GMT\par \par \uc2 US funding freeze imperils health of millions of vulnerable women and girls\par \par \uc2 The peals of laughter coming from rightwing precincts of the internet and cable news this week, after the White House claimed that \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cdepartment of government efficiency\u8221\'20\'1D had stopped payment on a $50m shipment of condoms to Gaza \u8211\'20\'13 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2025/jan/30/donald-trump-guantanamo-bay-rfk-jr-tulsi-gabbard-fbi-kash-patel-us-politics-latest-news?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with%3Ablock-679bea2d8f088478fa0ca5f3#block-679bea2d8f088478fa0ca5f3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 which appears to be untrue}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 echo a little hollow when the real costs of the blanket funding freeze for humanitarian assistance come into focus.\par \par \uc2 Eddie Wright, a spokesperson for the \uc2 United Nations Population Fund\uc2 , known by its old acronym, \uc2 UNFPA\uc2 , has shared with the Guardian some examples of the terrible impact the US funding freeze will have on millions of \u8220\'20\'1Cvulnerable women and girls in some of the world\u8217\'20\'19s most difficult settings\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US government\uc2  contributed nearly half of the \uc2 UN\uc2  agency\u8217\'20\'19s funding for humanitarian aid in 2024. In response to the funding freeze, Wright says, \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 UNFPA\uc2  has currently issued a moratorium on all spending and payments related to active awards, which will have immediate and widespread effects across regions, both programmatically and operationally.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Here are some examples provided by Wright of the impact of that US funding being frozen this week, apparently because someone in the administration mistakenly guessed that the funds were being used to send condoms to Gaza:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 In Afghanistan, over 9 million beneficiaries will not receive services and over 1,700 female health workers will no longer be employed.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 In Gaza, 50,000 pregnant women will lose critical care as \uc2 UNFPA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s mobile health teams are forced to halt operations. These teams provide care through home and shelter visits, especially in the hardest-hit northern areas.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 In Bangladesh, nearly 600,000 beneficiaries will be at risk of losing sexual and \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive health\b0 \highlight\uc2  and gender-based violence prevention and response services.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 In Ukraine, around 400,000 women and girls will be affected by cuts to psychosocial support, gender-based violence prevention and response services, safe spaces, and economic empowerment programs provided by 45 mobile teams and 21 safe spaces.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 In Pakistan, 1.7 million people (including 1.2 million Afghan refugees) will lose the life-saving sexual and \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive health\b0 \highlight\uc2  services provided by 62 health facilities.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 In Yemen, more than 220,000 people displaced by conflict or natural disasters will lose access to lifesaving emergency relief deliveries of essential items.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 In Sudan and its surrounding countries, thousands of displaced people will lose emergency sexual and \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive health\b0 \highlight\uc2  services and gender-based violence prevention and response services.\par \par \uc2 According to Wright: \u8220\'20\'1CWe are currently seeking a humanitarian waiver so that our life-saving assistance can continue, and look forward to engaging with the new US administration to support vulnerable women and girls in some of the world\u8217\'20\'19s most difficult settings.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.51am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.01am GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump's \uc2 FCC\uc2  chair says his investigation of NPR and \uc2 PBS\uc2  could end funding\par \par \uc2 Brendan Carr\uc2 , the new, pro-Trump chairman of the \uc2 Federal Communications Commission\uc2  has opened an investigation into corporate sponsorship of public media and warned the heads of NPR and \uc2 PBS\uc2  that his findings could be used by Republicans in Congress to end all funding for the networks.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am concerned that NPR and \uc2 PBS\uc2  broadcasts could be violating federal law by airing commercials,\u8221\'20\'1D Carr wrote on Wednesday in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://static01.nyt.com/newsgraphics/documenttools/340343f285781674/6da3eb69-full.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a letter}}}\uc2  to the presidents of both broadcasters obtained by the \uc2 New York Times\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CIn particular, it is possible that NPR and \uc2 PBS\uc2  member stations are broadcasting underwriting announcements that cross the line into prohibited commercial advertisements.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 As NPR\u8217\'20\'19s media correspondent, David Folkenflik, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2025/01/30/nx-s1-5281162/fcc-npr-pbs-investigation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2  the \uc2 FCC\uc2  does not have direct oversight of the networks, but it does regulate the roughly 1,500 public broadcasting stations across the country, which hold licenses granted by the \uc2 FCC\uc2  for use of public airwaves for radio and television.\par \par \uc2 Katherine Maher, the president of NPR and former chief executive of the nonprofit \uc2 Wikimedia Foundation\uc2 , said in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2025/01/30/g-s1-45619/statement-from-npr-president-and-ceo-katherine-maher"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a statement}}}\uc2  that the use of corporate underwriting spots, in place of ads, \u8220\'20\'1Ccomplies with federal regulations, including the \uc2 FCC\uc2  guidelines on underwriting messages for noncommercial educational broadcasters\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Two Democrats on bipartisan commission issued statements condemning the investigations. \u8220\'20\'1CThis appears to be yet another Administration effort to weaponize the power of the \uc2 FCC\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D commissioner Anna M Gomez {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.fcc.gov/public/attachments/DOC-409227A1.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CThe \uc2 FCC\uc2  has no business intimidating and silencing broadcast media.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPublic television and radio stations play a significant role in our media ecosystem\u8221\'20\'1D commissioner \uc2 Geoffrey Starks\uc2 , who was initially nominated by Trump in 2018, added. \u8220\'20\'1CAny attempt to intimidate these local media outlets is a threat to the free flow of information and the marketplace of ideas. The announcement of this investigation gives me serious concern.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Proposals to defund public media have already been introduced by Republicans in the House and Senate.\par \par \uc2 Defunding the public broadcasters, which provide high-quality, nonpartisan news reporting, has been on the wishlist of the American right for decades.\par \par \uc2 In 2012, for instance, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://archive.nytimes.com/thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/10/05/romneys-attack-on-big-bird-sows-confusion-abroad-and-feeds-it-at-home/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mitt Romney promised}}}\uc2 , during a debate with \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 , to end the federal subsidy for public broadcasting even though, as he told the \uc2 PBS\uc2  moderator Jim Lehrer, \u8220\'20\'1CI like \uc2 PBS\uc2 , I love Big Bird, I actually like you too.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Critics point out that Republicans appear to vastly overestimate how much Americans actually spend on public broadcasting. A 2021 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://journals.sagepub.com/doi/10.1177/19401612211060255"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 study}}}\uc2  from scholars at the \uc2 University of Pennsylvania\uc2  found that while Germans pay $142.42 each for a year of public media, Norwegians pay $110.73, Britons pay $81.30, Spaniards pay $58.25, Americans pay just $3.16.\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://i2.cdn.turner.com/cnn/2011/images/03/31/rel4m.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 poll conducted for CNN}}}\uc2  in 2011 showed that, after years of conservative complaints about taxpayer dollars funding public broadcasting, most Americans thought NPR and \uc2 PBS\uc2  got a much larger share of the federal budget than they actually do.\par \par \uc2 That survey, which asked respondents to estimate what share of the federal budget was spent on certain government programs, found that just 27% of Americans knew that the money for \uc2 PBS\uc2  and NPR was less than 1% of government spending. Almost half of respondents guessed that the share was between 1% and 5% of the federal budget, and nearly a third of those surveyed said the funding for \uc2 PBS\uc2  and NPR was in excess of 5% of all federal spending.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.45am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.28am GMT\par \par \uc2 The Senate voted {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/cspan/status/1885119702910812566"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 79-18}}}\uc2  to confirm North Dakota billionaire \uc2 Doug Burgum\uc2  as interior secretary.\par \par \uc2 More than half of Senate Democrats joined all 53 Republicans in voting for Burgum, who served two terms as governor of the oil-rich state and ran for president in 2023, bbefore dropping out and endorsing Trump.\par \par \uc2 Burgum, 68, is a software industry entrepreneur who grew up in a small North Dakota farming community.\par \par \uc2 Trump wants Burgum to be the first interior secretary on the National Security Council, and named him chair of a new National Energy Council tasked with achieving American \u8220\'20\'1Cenergy dominance\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Records obtained by the Associated Press {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/trump-oil-gas-industry-burgum-interior-ally-3ebe90d0207c99866365d72e74eda371?taid=679c14dce33576000173e5cf&utm_campaign=TrueAnthem&utm_medium=AP&utm_source=Twitter"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reveal}}}\uc2  that Burgum \u8220\'20\'1Ceagerly assisted\u8221\'20\'1D the oil industry while in elected office, \u8220\'20\'1Ceven as the governor was profiting from the lease of family land to oil companies\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.11am GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump administration froze $45m of aid, most of it for Gaza, none of it for condoms\par \par \uc2 As speculation continued over what, exactly, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was talking about when he claimed, on Wednesday, to have blocked a $50m grant \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/29/trump-condoms-gaza"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to buy condoms to Hamas}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D, a United Nations agency that promotes sexual and \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive health\b0 \highlight\uc2  has confirmed to the Guardian that it did have $45m in state department funding for its in work Gaza and the West Bank frozen by the Trump administration.\par \par \uc2 After reporting from the \uc2 Guardian{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2025/jan/28/donald-trump-executive-orders-transgender-troops-dei-covid-us-politics-live?page=with:block-679977268f086189f840e07b#block-679977268f086189f840e07b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 revealed}}}\uc2  that not a penny of the $60.8m in contraceptive and condom shipments funded by the \uc2 US Agency for International Development\uc2  (\uc2 USAid\uc2 ) in the past year went to Gaza, and the administration declined to provide evidence for the claim, Trump supporters have engaged in a desperate scramble to prove that Trump, and his press secretary, Karoline Leavitt, were not lying about the planned funding.\par \par \uc2 One straw grasped at by Trump supporters was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/DataRepublican/status/1884689831051354264"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the theory}}}\uc2  that someone in the administration had come across funding for \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive health\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a province of Mozambique named Gaza, and gotten confused.\par \par \uc2 Another, discovered by a Trump supporter scouring a public database of \uc2 US government\uc2  spending on Thursday, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/RandoLand_us/status/1884960913423282539"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 identified}}}\uc2  a $45m grant to the \uc2 United Nations Population Fund\uc2 , known by its old acronym, \uc2 UNFPA\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.usaspending.gov/award/ASST_NON_SPRMCO24VC0339_1900/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 made in September}}}\uc2  to support its work, including in the occupied Palestinian territories.\par \par \uc2 Eddie Wright, a spokesperson for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.unfpa.org/about-us"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the UN agency}}}\uc2 , confirmed that the grant was frozen in emails from \uc2 USAid\uc2  to various \uc2 UNFPA\uc2  offices since 26 January, all of which were backdated to 24 January. But Wright stressed that none of the funding was used to provide condoms in Gaza.\par \par \uc2 According to Wright \u8220\'20\'1Capproximately 70%\u8221\'20\'1D of the $45m \u8220\'20\'1Cwas earmarked for Gaza and the rest for West Bank\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The agency did provide $100,000 worth of male condoms to Gaza last year, Wright said, \u8220\'20\'1Cbut none of it was funded by the United States\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 So what was the money for? Wright says that it was used to equip \u8220\'20\'1Csix maternity units for normal deliveries; 3 units for C-Sections; Caravans/prefabs for 40 safe spaces\u8221\'20\'1D, where survivors of sexual violence can receive medical referrals and counselling.\par \par \uc2 The grant was also intended to \u8220\'20\'1Csupport the expansion of mental health and psychosocial support services, as well as the prevention of sexual exploitation and abuse\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In addition, Wright explained, the US funds were intended to pay for \u8220\'20\'1Clife-saving medicine and supplies to prevent maternal mortality, as well as 500,000 dignity kits with key hygiene and sanitation items; 30,000 Mama and Baby kits with essentials for new mothers and newborns, and menstrual health supplies\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The agency is currently hoping to receive a humanitarian waiver from the state department to unfreeze the funds, \u8220\'20\'1Cto enable us to continue our lifesaving work\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.19am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.29pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Senator \uc2 Susan Collins\uc2 , a Republican from Maine, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/ChadPergram/status/1885074710397874431"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told}}}\uc2  the Fox congressional correspondent Chad Pergram that she has \u8220\'20\'1Cnot made a final decision\u8221\'20\'1D on whether to vote for \uc2 Tulsi Gabbard\uc2  or \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2  but plans to watch video highlights of the confirmation hearings to inform her decisions. \u8220\'20\'1CI need to get the clips of both hearings of the parts that I missed\u8221\'20\'1D Collins said.\par \par \uc2 Given the great length of the hearings, many supporters and opponents of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s cabinet picks are doing the same. But reactions to the clips on social media are a political Rorschach test.\par \par \uc2 To take one example, video of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://youtu.be/29tu5nr7_-s?si=1Ii_o9xFDeuk3JXs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a fiery exchange}}}\uc2  between Kennedy and Bernie Sanders during a tense Senate health committee hearing on Thursday has been widely seen online, but with sharply different assessments of who won out.\par \par \uc2 Bernie Sanders questioned \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2  during a Senate health committee hearing on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn many ways, President Trump and Mr Kennedy have asked some of the right questions,\u8221\'20\'1D Sanders began. \u8220\'20\'1CProblem is their answer will only make a bad situation worse.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The senator then pressed Kennedy to promise that, as health secretary, he would fight to guarantee health care to every American.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m going to make America healthier than other countries in the world right now \u8212\'20\'14 we\u8217\'20\'19re the sickest\u8221\'20\'1D Kennedy said, before Sanders cut in to repeat his question.\par \par \uc2 Kennedy then pivoted, and addressing the senator as \u8220\'20\'1CBernie\u8221\'20\'1D, accused him of \u8220\'20\'1Ccorruption\u8221\'20\'1D for supposedly \u8220\'20\'1Caccepting millions of dollars from the pharmaceutical industry\u8221\'20\'1D. Before Kennedy had even finished the prepared attack, his supporters in the room applauded.\par \par \uc2 Sanders, however, replied that the charge was false. \u8220\'20\'1COh no, no, no\u8221\'20\'1D, he said. \u8220\'20\'1CI ran for president, like you. I got millions and millions of contributions. They did not come from the executives; not one nickel of PAC money from the pharmaceutical industry. They came from workers\u8221\'20\'1D. Sanders supporters in the room clapped.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn 2020,\u8221\'20\'1D Kennedy insisted, \u8220\'20\'1Cyou were the single largest receiver of pharmaceutical money\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBecause I had small contributions from workers\u8221\'20\'1D employed by drug companies, Sanders interjected.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBernie, you were the single largest receiver of pharmaceutical dollars\u8221\'20\'1D Kennedy insisted.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNo, from workers in the industry\u8221\'20\'1D Sanders explained.\par \par \uc2 Video of the exchange, captioned, \u8220\'20\'1CRFK Jr. calls out Bernie Sanders direct to his face!\u8221\'20\'1D was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/elonmusk/status/1885057952953897469"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 enthusiastically shared by}}}\uc2  Kennedy supporter \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  on his social media platform, racking up over 10 million views.\par \par \uc2 Supporters of Sanders on the same platform pointed out that he was correct that taking small-dollar donations from workers employed by drug companies was not the same as taking money \u8220\'20\'1Cfrom the pharmaceutical industry\u8221\'20\'1D, but their comments were far less seen on the platform controlled by Musk.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.32pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.32pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The Congressional Black Caucus has denounced \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cracist\u8221\'20\'1D attempt to blame diversity for the midair collision between a US military helicopter and an \uc2 American Airlines\uc2  jet approaching Reagan National airport near Washington D C on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 After expressing sympathy for the victims, and confidence in the ability of federal investigators to determine the cause of the accident, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cbc.house.gov/news/documentsingle.aspx?DocumentID=2771"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a statement}}}\uc2  from the caucus strongly criticized Trump\u8217\'20\'19s response:\par \par \uc2 However, the opportunity to fully focus our sympathies on those who are in mourning and who may not have even retrieved their dearly departed was marred by a truly disgusting and disgraceful display of racist political prognostication. President Trump, without evidence or regard for the gravity and solemnity of this incident in which American lives were lost, held a press conference to falsely blame the diversity initiatives of past administrations for the cause of this incident. Not only are the President\u8217\'20\'19s claims untrue, they also speak to the Republican Party\u8217\'20\'19s desire to divide us as a country.\par \par \uc2 To be clear, diversity, equity, and inclusion are American values. Diversity policies work to benefit all Americans who have traditionally been kept out of opportunities, including white women, veterans, and aging Americans, not just the Black and minority communities that Trump and Republicans want to scapegoat and villainize for political gain. We are not going back!\par \par \uc2 Caucus chair Congresswoman Yvette D Clarke, a Democrat from Brooklyn, shared video of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s remarks {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://bsky.app/profile/repyvetteclarke.bsky.social/post/3lgy4b6wg5k2l"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 on Bluesky}}}\uc2 , with the comment: \u8220\'20\'1CWhile families grieve and our nation mourns the 67 victims of last night\u8217\'20\'19s heartbreaking crash, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his cronies are already abusing this tragedy to further their racist, repugnant agenda\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.35pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.41pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Speaking to reporters in the Oval Office, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  just insisted that Egypt and Jordan, which have refused to cooperate with his proposal to \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/26/trump-resumes-sending-2000-pound-bombs-to-israel-undoing-biden-pause"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 just clean out}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D the entire population of the besieged Gaza Strip, by resettling Palestinians in their countries, will eventually agree.\par \par \uc2 Asked if there is \u8220\'20\'1Canything you can do to make\u8221\'20\'1D President \uc2 Abdel Fattah\uc2  el-Sisi of Egypt and King Abdullah II of Jordan accept that population transfer, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/Acyn/status/1885072749879844939"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump replied}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CThey will do it. They will do it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat makes you say that?\u8221\'20\'1D the reporter asked.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re going to do it, OK?\u8221\'20\'1D Trump replied. \u8220\'20\'1CWe do a lot for them, and they\u8217\'20\'19re going to do it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump did not elaborate on what kind of pressure he plans to exert, but the recent freeze of US foreign aid made exceptions for military assistance to Israel \u8211\'20\'13 whose longstanding major arms packages from the US have expanded further since the Gaza war \u8211\'20\'13 and Egypt, which has received generous US defense funding since it signed a peace treaty with Israel in 1979.\par \par \uc2 Jordan, which also has a peace deal with Israel, and controlled the West Bank and East Jerusalem until they were seized by Israeli forces in 1967, is also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.foreignassistance.gov/cd/jordan/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a major recipient of US aid}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s first impeachment was over his demand that Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s president, \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskyy\uc2 , \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2019/sep/25/trumps-phone-call-with-ukraines-president-read-the-full-transcript"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 do us a favor}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D in return for military assistance.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.49pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.01pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has said the US will put a 25% tariff on imports from Mexico and Canada, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 Trump, speaking to reporters in the Oval Office, reportedly said he would decide probably by tonight whether or not those tariffs would apply to oil.\par \par \uc2 Trump has previously pledged to sign an executive order imposing a 25% tariff on all products coming in to the US from Mexico and Canada, two of the country\u8217\'20\'19s biggest trading partners.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.44pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Joining Democratic congressional leaders at the press conference, Altadena resident Jackie Jacobs described the moment she realized it was time to evacuate.\par \par \uc2 The 88-year-old said she received a message telling her and her husband to \u8220\'20\'1Cget out\u8221\'20\'1D and they did just that, carrying with them only the clothes that they were wearing.\par \par \uc2 The Eaton fire tore through Altadena, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/18/altadena-fire-black-families"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a historically Black town}}}\uc2  in the San Gabriel Valley, claiming nearly every house on their street, including their home.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEverything now is in ashes,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. The houses on their block were only identifiable by their chimneys.\par \par \uc2 Officials say nearly 9,500 structures have been burned and at least 17 people lost their lives in the fire, which is 99% contained. A new study published by UCLA found that Black residents in Altadena were 1.3 times more likely to have experienced destruction or major damage than non-Black households.\par \par \uc2 Jacob\u8217\'20\'19s husband, David, said the couple is staying in an \uc2 Airbnb\uc2 . They have had friends and family urge them to move back to Alabama. But they want to stay in their beloved Altadena.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re just asking God to guide us,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/19/altadena-displacement-black-families"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18I want to preserve our legacy\u8217\'20\'19: Black families in Altadena fear displacement after fire }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.54pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.30pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Hearings conclude today for Trump's nominees\par \par \uc2 The Senate judiciary committee has concluded the confirmation hearing of Kash Patel, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s nominee to lead the \uc2 FBI\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 That concludes today\u8217\'20\'19s Senate confirmation hearings, which also saw \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2  and \uc2 Tulsi Gabbard\uc2  face questions over their nominations.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/30/tulsi-gabbard-confirmation-hearing"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tulsi Gabbard grilled on Snowden, Assad and Putin in tense Senate hearing}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/30/rfk-hhs-confirmation-hearing"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 RFK Jr dodges clear answers on vaccines as Senate grilling enters second day}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.43pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.17pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Democrat alleges Patel is happy to 'lie' for Trump in tense questioning\par \par \uc2 Hours into Kash Patel\u8217\'20\'19s confirmation hearing to be \uc2 FBI\uc2  director, we are getting into his witness testimony before a grand jury in the Trump classified documents case \u8211\'20\'13 and it has become awkward for Patel.\par \par \uc2 During the documents investigation, Patel was subpoenaed to testify before a federal grand jury about whether \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  declassified the documents he had retained at his Mar-a-Lago club, after he publicly represented that Trump was authorized to have those documents because he had declassified them before leaving office.\par \par \uc2 Patel initially declined to appear, citing his fifth amendment right against self-incrimination, the Guardian reported at the time. He later testified after the chief US district judge in Washington authorized Patel to have limited immunity from prosecution, which forced his testimony.\par \par \uc2 Under oath and under close questioning from Senator \uc2 Cory Booker\uc2 , Patel clarified that while he had heard and witnessed Trump issue a declassification order for some documents, he did not actually know whether they applied to the documents the \uc2 FBI\uc2  seized at Mar-a-Lago.\par \par \uc2 Booker is seizing on this to say Patel is happy to \u8220\'20\'1Clie\u8221\'20\'1D on behalf of Trump in public to support him, which he said was disqualifying. \u8220\'20\'1CHe is refusing the transparency he claims to adhere to,\u8221\'20\'1D Booker adds.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.42pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.00pm GMT\par \par \uc2 House Democratic leaders on Thursday came to Altadena to survey the damage from the Eaton fire that burned through historically Black neighborhoods, vowing to fight for more federal aid without conditions.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s no Democratic way or Republican way to respond to a crisis in an extreme weather event like these horrific wildfires, there is an American way,\u8221\'20\'1D House leader \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2  of New York said at a press conference after touring the devastation. \u8220\'20\'1CWe want to make sure that Congress and the American people stand with the people of this amazing community.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and Republicans have threatened to impose conditions on federal disaster aid for Los Angeles to rebuild after the wildfires, though on a visit to the region last week he told residents and officials: \u8220\'20\'1CWe have to work together to get this really worked out.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Led by congresswoman Judy Chu, who represents the fire victims of Altadena, Jeffries toured the area with House Democratic whip Katherine Clark of Massachusetts and House Democratic caucus chair Pete Aguilar of California.\par \par \uc2 enltrHouse Democratic leaders are in Altadena today to tour the devastation from the fire.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe cannot condition any assistance to the people of Altadena, the people of Pasadena, the people of Los Angeles County, the people of California,\u8221\'20\'1D Jeffries said. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Me1IJbS0em"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Me1IJbS0em}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Lauren Gambino (@laurenegambino) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/laurenegambino/status/1885016946212823237?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 30, 2025}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere is enough Fema money to last us up until March but we will need supplemental money, as has happened in every major disaster in this country,\u8221\'20\'1D Chu said, adding that it is unprecedented for Congress to attach partisan conditions to federal disaster aid.\par \par \uc2 Chu and Jeffries also warned that the Trump administration\u8217\'20\'19s now-paused freeze on federal grant and loan funding threatened to impact communities like Altadena as they recover from disaster.\par \par \uc2 Jeffries added: \u8220\'20\'1CCalifornia has sent more money to the federal government year after year after year than they ever get back in return. The people of California are simply asking for some of those tax dollars to come back to the state to help the people in need.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.06pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.48pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Several senior \uc2 FBI\uc2  leaders demoted or reassigned \u8211\'20\'13 report\par \par \uc2 At least five senior \uc2 FBI\uc2  leaders who were promoted by the bureau\u8217\'20\'19s former director, \uc2 Christopher Wray\uc2 , have been notified they are being demoted or reassigned, CNN reports.\par \par \uc2 The senior officials are at the executive assistant director level and include those who oversee cyber, national security and criminal investigations, the outlet writes, citing sources.\par \par \uc2 The report comes after the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/27/trump-fires-justice-department-officials-jack-smith"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 firing of more than a dozen federal prosecutors}}}\uc2  at the justice department, across the street from the \uc2 FBI\uc2  headquarters, earlier this week.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.06pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.38pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Transgender women incarcerated in federal prisons have been placed in isolation, told they will be transferred to men\u8217\'20\'19s prisons and advised they will lose access to gender-affirming medical treatments in response to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s executive order \u8220\'20\'1Cdefending women from gender ideology extremism\u8221\'20\'1D, according to civil rights advocates and people behind bars.\par \par \uc2 The executive order on \u8220\'20\'1Cgender ideology\u8221\'20\'1D was announced on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s first day in office, and is part of a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/28/trump-executive-order-transgender-transition"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 flurry}}}\uc2  of executive actions {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/nbc-out/out-politics-and-policy/trump-executive-order-transgender-military-dei-rcna189470"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 targeting trans rights}}}\uc2  and LGBTQ+ {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abcnews.go.com/Politics/trumps-executive-order-restrict-education-topics/story?id=118239458"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 education}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Staff at \uc2 Federal Medical Center\uc2  (\uc2 FMC\uc2 ) Carswell, a US women\u8217\'20\'19s prison in Texas that houses people with special medical needs, took actions within days of the order, according to attorneys and one resident. Officers went to trans women\u8217\'20\'19s cells one by one and ordered them out, according to one incarcerated resident, a trans man housed with the women.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe officers yelled at these women: \u8216\'20\'18Come right now, leave your things. You don\u8217\'20\'19t have time to pack,\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D the man said in Spanish. \u8220\'20\'1CThe officials were degrading them and saying disgusting things, like: \u8216\'20\'18We don\u8217\'20\'19t have to call you women anymore. Where you\u8217\'20\'19re going, you\u8217\'20\'19re going to be a man.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 As one trans woman was trying to pack her bra, an official laughed at her and said: \u8220\'20\'1CYou won\u8217\'20\'19t need that where you\u8217\'20\'19re going,\u8221\'20\'1D he recalled. \u8220\'20\'1CThe women were screaming and crying, saying: \u8216\'20\'18Where are you taking us?\u8217\'20\'19 It was so humiliating.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 LGBTQ+-rights lawyers say the moves will have major consequences for the health and safety of trans people in federal custody, and blatantly violate federal laws and a range of constitutional protections.\par \par \uc2 Read the full story here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/30/trans-people-federal-prisons"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trans people in US federal prisons face brutal crackdown under Trump order}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.52pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.20pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Democrats on the Senate budget committee boycotted Thursday\u8217\'20\'19s vote to advance Russell Vought\u8217\'20\'19s nomination to head the office of management and budget.\par \par \uc2 Calling Vought a threat to democracy, Senate Democrats on the committee said they refused to \u8220\'20\'1Cvote for someone so clearly unfit for office\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Senate Democrats had urged a delay on Vought\u8217\'20\'19s confirmation hearings after the office \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  nominated him to lead ordered a freeze on federal grant funding.\par \par \uc2 Issued on Monday by the acting director of the office of management and budget and rescinded on Wednesday, the order would have potentially impacted critical programs that receive federal aid, including Head Start and Meals on Wheels.\par \par \uc2 But Republican lawmakers have plowed ahead with Vought\u8217\'20\'19s confirmation, and Republican members of the Senate budget committee held the vote anyway on Thursday without any Democrats present.\par \par \uc2 Vought\u8217\'20\'19s confirmation will move to the full Senate after the 11-0 committee vote.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/30/trump-russell-vought-budget-vote"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats refuse to vote on Trump budget pick: \u8216\'20\'18So clearly unfit for office\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.15pm GMT\par \par \uc2 'Leading not lying': ex-transportation secretary Buttigieg slams Trump\par \par \uc2 Pete Buttigieg\uc2 , the former transportation secretary, has condemned \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cdespicable\u8221\'20\'1D comments during a Thursday press conference on the deadly mid-air collision near Washington DC.\par \par \uc2 Trump, at a White House briefing, took aim at Buttigieg and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/30/trump-washington-dc-plane-crash-dei"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 claimed Democrats were responsible}}}\uc2  for declining standards in air traffic control and that the disaster \u8220\'20\'1Ccould have been\u8221\'20\'1D caused by diversity, equity and inclusion (DEI) policies at the \uc2 Federal Aviation Administration\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe was a disaster,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said of Buttigieg. \u8220\'20\'1CHe was a disaster as a mayor, he ran his city into the ground, and he\u8217\'20\'19s a disaster now. He\u8217\'20\'19s just got a good line of bullshit.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump also said Buttigieg, who is gay, ran the transportation department into the ground \u8220\'20\'1Cwith his diversity\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs families grieve, Trump should be leading, not lying,\u8221\'20\'1D Buttigieg {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/PeteButtigieg/status/1885013865676562491"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  on X.\par \par \uc2 We put safety first, drove down close calls, grew Air Traffic Control, and had zero commercial airline crash fatalities out of millions of flights on our watch.\par \par \uc2 He said one of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s first acts as president was to \u8220\'20\'1Cfire and suspend some of the key personnel who helped keep our skies safe,\u8221\'20\'1D adding:\par \par \uc2 Time for the President to show actual leadership and explain what he will do to prevent this from happening again.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.42pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.42pm GMT\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLook at them, I want you to look at them if you have the courage,\u8221\'20\'1D Democratic senator Adam Schiff declared, asking Trump\u8217\'20\'19s nominee to head the \uc2 Federal Bureau of Investigation\uc2 , Kash Patel, to look at \uc2 Capitol police\uc2  officers in the room during his Senate confirmation hearing.\par \par \uc2 During the hearing, Patel decried violence against law enforcement that occurred at the Capitol riot on 6 January 2021.\par \par \uc2 Schiff questioned him about his comments on an episode of \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s War Room podcast apparently claiming partial credit for producing Justice for All, a recording of January 6 defendants singing the national anthem from prison.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.57pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.35pm GMT\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere have been, as I understand it, dozens of studies done all over the world that make it very clear that vaccines do not cause autism,\u8221\'20\'1D said Senator Bernie Sanders during \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Senate confirmation hearing to lead the \uc2 Department of Health and Human Services\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe evidence is there, that\u8217\'20\'19s it \u8211\'20\'13 vaccines do not cause autism. Do you agree with that?\u8221\'20\'1D asked Sanders. \u8220\'20\'1CI asked you a simple question, Bobby.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.36pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.30pm GMT\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEverybody\u8217\'20\'19s entitled to their opinion,\u8221\'20\'1D said Kash Patel in response to a question from Vermont senator Peter Welch about whether the nominee to lead the \uc2 Federal Bureau of Investigation\uc2  believed that former joint chiefs of staff chair \uc2 Mark Milley\uc2  should be tried for treason.\par \par \uc2 The Trump administration has stripped Milley \u8211\'20\'13 who clashed with Trump during his first term and rejected his attempts to overturn the 2020 election \u8211\'20\'13 of his security detail.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.32pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.55pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 Some of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s most controversial picks for his cabinet and key administration roles are facing Senate confirmation hearings today. Here\u8217\'20\'19s a recap of the latest developments:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2 ,Trump\u8217\'20\'19s pick to lead the country\u8217\'20\'19s top health agency, attending a second straight day of bruising hearings on Capitol Hill. Appearing before the Senate health committee, Kennedy dodged direct questions about whether he still believes vaccines cause autism and whether Covid-19 vaccines saved the lives of millions. He pledged to hire \u8220\'20\'1Cpro-life\u8221\'20\'1D deputies in his office, if he is confirmed. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/29/rfk-jr-senate-confirmation-hearing"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kennedy faced tough questions from Democrats before the Senate finance committee on Wednesday.}}}\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kash Patel,Trump\u8217\'20\'19s pick to lead the \uc2 Federal Bureau of Investigation\uc2  (\uc2 FBI\uc2 ), insisted he did not have an \u8220\'20\'1Cenemies list\u8221\'20\'1D and that the bureau under his leadership would not seek retribution against the president\u8217\'20\'19s adversaries. Patel, appearing before the Senate judiciary committee, said he did not agree with shortening sentences for people who assault law enforcement, a week after Trump\u8217\'20\'19s sweeping pardons for people charged in the January 6 attack on the Capitol.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Tulsi Gabbard\uc2 , Trump\u8217\'20\'19s pick to be director of national intelligence, faced sharp criticism over past comments sympathetic to Russia, her meeting with Syria\u8217\'20\'19s now-deposed leader, \uc2 Bashar al-Assad\uc2 , and her past support for government leaker Edward Snowden. Appearing before the Senate intelligence committee, Gabbard said Snowden had broke the law but refused to answer whether the whistleblower was a traitor.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump said there were no survivors in the midair collision of an \uc2 American Airlines\uc2  jet and a military Black Hawk helicopter near Washington DC. At a briefing in the White House, Trump questioned the role of the helicopter pilot and air traffic control, as well as faulted \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  as he injected politics into his crash response.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.02pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.41pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Mass deportation \u8211\'20\'13 at least in theory \u8211\'20\'13 is apparently popular among the American people.\par \par \uc2 So over and over again, Trump and his allies have loudly touted {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ipsos.com/en-us/majority-americans-support-deporting-immigrants-who-are-us-illegally"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 their plans}}}\uc2  to detain and deport undocumented immigrants, initially focusing on those with criminal records. In doing so, they\u8217\'20\'19ve redirected the US public\u8217\'20\'19s attention toward their \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2025/01/17/us/politics/trump-immigration-raids-chicago.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shock and awe}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D tactics that led to thousands of arrests {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2025/01/26/politics/chicago-immigration-trump-ice/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 across the country}}}\uc2  in less than a week.\par \par \uc2 But as all eyes turn to these high-profile enforcement efforts, the new administration from its very first moments has also been relentlessly, if more quietly, targeting people trying to come to the US legally, systematically dismantling safety nets meant to protect the world\u8217\'20\'19s most vulnerable individuals and families, who are already suffering because of it.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/30/trump-immigration-deportation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s immigration crackdown also targets legal pathways to enter US}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.27pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is still historically unpopular compared with other new US presidents, a new poll {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.gallup.com/poll/655955/trump-inaugural-approval-rating-historically-low-again.aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 showed}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAt 47%, President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s initial job approval rating for his second term is similar to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.gallup.com/poll/202811/trump-sets-new-low-point-inaugural-approval-rating.aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 inaugural 45% reading}}}\uc2  during his first term, again placing him below all other elected presidents dating back to 1953,\u8221\'20\'1D wrote Megan Brenan, a senior editor for Gallup, which carried out the poll.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTrump remains the only elected president with sub-50% initial approval ratings, and his latest disapproval rating (48%) is three percentage points higher than in 2017.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 John F Kennedy\uc2  remains the most popular modern president at the start of his term, according to Gallup polling. In the first month of his presidency, in 1961, the Democrat enjoyed 72% approval and just 6% disapproval.\par \par \uc2 Dwight Eisenhower\uc2  (1953) and \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  (2009) enjoyed the next-highest approval ratings, at 68%. \uc2 Jimmy Carter\uc2 , who died last month aged 100, scored 66% approval in February 1977, at the start of his single term in office.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/30/trump-low-approval-rating"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump begins term with historically low approval rating, poll shows}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.19pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2  was asked if he would rescind a Biden administration rule requiring physicians who receive federal funding to perform gender-affirming care.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYes, I will,\u8221\'20\'1D Kennedy said in response to a question by \uc2 Josh Hawley\uc2 , a Republican senator from Missouri. \u8220\'20\'1CThat rule is anti-science.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Kennedy added:\par \par \uc2 Do you really want somebody performing surgery on you who is morally opposed to that surgery? It doesn\u8217\'20\'19t make any sense.\par \par \uc2 Kennedy said that \u8220\'20\'1Cwe need to embrace diversity in this country\u8221\'20\'1D and not \u8220\'20\'1Cforce people to do things that are against their conscience\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.26pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.59pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump, without evidence, appears to blame DEI for plane crash\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  continued to turn what might have been a sombre briefing into a baseless rant against DEI (diversity, equity and inclusion) programs despite no evidence of a link with Wednesday night\u8217\'20\'19s plane crash.\par \par \uc2 The president was backed to the hilt by his transportation secretary, Sean Duffy, who said \u8220\'20\'1Cwe can only accept the best and the brightest\u8221\'20\'1D in positions affecting passenger safety, and his defense secretary, Pete Hegseth, who echoed: \u8220\'20\'1CThe era of DEI is gone at the defense department and we need the best and brightest.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Then came Vice-President \uc2 JD Vance\uc2 , who claimed \u8220\'20\'1Cwe want to hire the best people\u8221\'20\'1D who are \u8220\'20\'1Cactually competent enough to do the job\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Trump returned to the lectern to claim that \u8220\'20\'1Cvery powerful tests\u8221\'20\'1D for competence in air traffic control were \u8220\'20\'1Cterminated\u8221\'20\'1D by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 CNN\u8217\'20\'19s Kaitlin Collins asked: \u8220\'20\'1CAren\u8217\'20\'19t you getting ahead of the investigation?\u8221\'20\'1D Trump replied: \u8220\'20\'1CNo, I don\u8217\'20\'19t think so at all \u8230\'20\'26 I don\u8217\'20\'19t think that\u8217\'20\'19s a smart question. I\u8217\'20\'19m surprised, coming from you.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Another reporter asked why Trump believes DEI is responsible. He said: \u8220\'20\'1CBecause I have common sense and unfortunately a lot of people don\u8217\'20\'19t. We want brilliant people doing this. This is a major chess game at the highest level.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.35pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.57pm GMT\par \par \uc2 RFK Jr says he would hire 'pro-life' people in his office\par \par \uc2 Tim Scott, the Republican senator from South Carolina, said that he and \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2  had some \u8220\'20\'1Cserious conversations about the importance of life\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou assured me that your deputies were going to be pro life. Is that still the case?\u8221\'20\'1D Scott asked Kennedy. Kennedy replied:\par \par \uc2 I will implement President Trump\u8217\'20\'19s policies. I serve at his pleasure, but I share President Trump\u8217\'20\'19s [belief] that every \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a tragedy.\par \par \uc2 Pressed on whether he will hire deputies within his \uc2 Department of Health and Human Services\uc2  who will be pro-life, Kennedy said: \u8220\'20\'1CI am.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.52pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Tulsi Gabbard\uc2  is avoiding answering a question on whether or not Edward Snowden should be considered a traitor to the United States.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIs Edward Snowden a traitor: yes or no?\u8221\'20\'1D she is asked by successive senators.\par \par \uc2 Edward Snowden broke the law. He released information about the United States. If I may just finish my thought, senator \u8230\'20\'26 In this role that I\u8217\'20\'19ve been nominated for, confirmed as director of national intelligence, I will be responsible for protecting our nation\u8217\'20\'19s secrets, and I have more immediate steps that I would take to prevent another Snowden.\par \par \uc2 That has not satisfied senator Michael Bennet from Colorado, a Democrat. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is when the rubber hits the road,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 This is not a moment for social media. It\u8217\'20\'19s not a moment to propagate conspiracy theories \u8230\'20\'26 This is when you need to answer questions of the people whose votes you\u8217\'20\'19re asking for.\par \par \uc2 He continues:\par \par \uc2 Obviously we didn\u8217\'20\'19t select this nominee. But can\u8217\'20\'19t we do better than somebody who doesn\u8217\'20\'19t believe in [Fisa law] 702? Can we believe that somebody who can\u8217\'20\'19t answer whether Snowden was a traitor five times today, who made excuses for \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s invasion of Ukraine? The first time that I\u8217\'20\'19m aware of any American official has done that, I\u8217\'20\'19m questioning her judgment. That\u8217\'20\'19s the issue that\u8217\'20\'19s at stake here.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.54pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.47pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Kash Patel, the nominee to be the \uc2 FBI\uc2  director, evades a hypothetical from Senator \uc2 Chris Coons\uc2  about whether he would open an investigation into a political opponent if requested by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , or would stop a legitimate investigation into a Trump ally.\par \par \uc2 Patel says he will simply obey the law.\par \par \uc2 The questions touch on issues that came up during Trump\u8217\'20\'19s first term: when the president asked then \uc2 FBI\uc2  director \uc2 Jim Comey\uc2  to end the investigation into his national security adviser. Comey declined \u8211\'20\'13 and was later fired by Trump.\par \par \uc2 But Patel also told Coons that the \uc2 FBI\uc2  would not engage in retribution against Trump\u8217\'20\'19s political opponents, backpedaling from his past claims that even former \uc2 FBI\uc2  director \uc2 Chris Wray\uc2  should be prosecuted in part for his role in allowing the criminal investigation of Trump for his mishandling of classified documents. Patel said the \uc2 FBI\uc2  \u8216\'20\'18will not go backwards\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.50pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.39pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Kash Patel, the nominee to be the \uc2 FBI\uc2  director, attempts to distance himself from verbatim quotes being read back at him by Senator Amy Klobuchar that don\u8217\'20\'19t portray Patel as a nonpartisan official.\par \par \uc2 Klobuchar ticks through various remarks he has made on a number of podcasts, including that he would shut down the \uc2 FBI\uc2  headquarters and turn it into a museum of the so-called \u8220\'20\'1Cdeep state\u8217\'20\'19.\par \par \uc2 Patel said her quotations were a \u8220\'20\'1Cgrotesque\u8221\'20\'1D mischaracterization, and at other times claimed not to remember the remarks being read back to him.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am quoting his own words,\u8221\'20\'1D Klobuchar said.\par \par \uc2 Patel says the \uc2 FBI\uc2  works for the justice department, and adds that the justice department reports to the White House.\par \par \uc2 Democratic senator \uc2 Chris Coons\uc2  notes that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s attorney general nominee, Pam Bondi, gave a different response in her hearing: that the justice department reports to the constitution and the American people. It\u8217\'20\'19s a notable difference.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.42pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.37pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Wearing a dark blue suit, white shirt and red tie, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  entered the White House briefing room at 11.21am, accompanied by his defence secretary, Pete Hegseth, and the transportation secretary, Sean Duffy, both new to their jobs.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19d like to request a moment of silence for the victims and their families, please,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said.\par \par \uc2 After the pause, and in softer, graver tones than usual, he resumed: \u8220\'20\'1CI speak to you this morning in an hour of anguish for our nation.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump provided a description of the incident, noting: \u8220\'20\'1CSadly, there are no survivors.\u8221\'20\'1D He described it as \u8220\'20\'1Ca tragedy of terrible proportions\u8221\'20\'1D that has \u8220\'20\'1Creally shaken a lot of people\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The president added: \u8220\'20\'1CWe are all heartbroken, we are all searching for answers. That icy, icy Potomac \u8230\'20\'26 cold water.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump said \u8220\'20\'1Cwe have very strong opinions and ideas\u8221\'20\'1D about how the accident happened then reverted to taking political swipes at Barack Obama and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  over air traffic controller standards. \u8220\'20\'1CThe word \u8220\'20\'1Ctalented\u8221\'20\'1D. You have to be naturally talented geniuses.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In a harsher tone than before, he then complained about diversity and inclusion in \uc2 FAA\uc2  programs and described former transportation secretary \uc2 Pete Buttigieg\uc2  as a \u8220\'20\'1Cdisaster\u8221\'20\'1D who has a \u8220\'20\'1Cgood line in bullshit\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.44pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.28pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Kash Patel, the nominee to be the \uc2 FBI\uc2  director, is indignant at Democrats raising the list of deep-state actors that he considered to be \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s political opponents.\par \par \uc2 Democrats have referred to the list, which appears as an appendix in his book Government Gangsters, as an enemies list.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s not an enemies list,\u8221\'20\'1D Patel said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a total mischaracterization.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But the list does effectively name anyone and everyone who Patel has viewed as disloyal to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s agenda.\par \par \uc2 It includes people like the \uc2 FBI\uc2  agents who led the Russia investigation, and former attorney generals, \uc2 FBI\uc2  directors and CIA directors \u8211\'20\'13 but only those Trump has personally clashed with and has mused at various times about wanting to investigate.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.32pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.27pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is delivering remarks from the White House briefing room on last night\u8217\'20\'19s midair collision at Reagan National airport near Washington DC.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe work has now shifted to a recovery mission. Sadly, there are no survivors,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said.\par \par \uc2 This was a dark and excruciating night in our nation\u8217\'20\'19s capital and in our nation\u8217\'20\'19s history, and a tragedy of terrible proportions.\par \par \uc2 He said authorities have \u8220\'20\'1Csome pretty good ideas\u8221\'20\'1D about what led to the crash.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2025/jan/30/plane-crashes-near-washington-dc-after-mid-air-collision-with-military-helicopter-follow-live"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Washington DC plane crash: Trump holds briefing after officials say no survivors expected to be found \u8211\'20\'13 latest}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.31pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.24pm GMT\par \par \uc2 RFK Jr won't commit to keeping \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill mifepristone on market\par \par \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2  was pressed to answer whether he would keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill mifepristone on the market.\par \par \uc2 Tammy Baldwin\uc2 , a Democratic senator from Wisconsin, noted that more than 100 peer-reviewed studies for the medication have confirmed that 99% of patients who took the pill had no complications.\par \par \uc2 Kennedy refused to commit to keeping mifepristone on the market and available to women, and said he would not get ahead of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  on the issue.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPresident Trump has not chosen a policy,\u8221\'20\'1D Kennedy said. \u8220\'20\'1CI will implement his policy.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.31pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.16pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Tulsi Gabbard\uc2  has said that if she is nominated she won\u8217\'20\'19t advocate for a pardon for Edward Snowden.\par \par \uc2 In response to a question by Senator \uc2 Susan Collins\uc2 , Gabbard said:\par \par \uc2 If confirmed as the director of national intelligence, my responsibility would be to ensure the security of our nation\u8217\'20\'19s secrets, and would not take actions to advocate for any actions related to Snowden. So the answer is no.\par \par \uc2 \u8221\'20\'1DI would work to make sure that we don\u8217\'20\'19t have any disclosures or vigilantes taking it upon themselves [to disclose intelligence],\u8221\'20\'1D she continued, pointing to \u8220\'20\'1Clegal routes\u8221\'20\'1D for whistleblowers to raise complaints.\par \par \uc2 She also denied reports in the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  that she had met with a senior member of \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2 , the Iran-backed militant group in Lebanon, calling it an \u8220\'20\'1Cabsurd accusation\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.19pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.14pm GMT\par \par \uc2 RFK Jr avoids saying Covid vaccines were successful as Bernie Sanders grills him\par \par \uc2 Bernie Sanders, the independent senator of Vermont, asked \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2  if he agreed that Covid-19 vaccines were successful in saving millions of lives.\par \par \uc2 Kennedy refused to be pinned down, saying there is no good surveillance system.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf you show me science that shows that,\u8221\'20\'1D Kennedy said. Sanders replied:\par \par \uc2 You\u8217\'20\'19re applying for the job \u8211\'20\'13 clearly you should know this. And the scientific community has established that Covid vaccines saved millions of lives and you\u8217\'20\'19re casting doubt.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.32pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.05pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Tulsi Gabbard\uc2 : 'no love for Assad, Gaddafi, or any dictator'\par \par \uc2 Tulsi Gabbard\uc2 , in her opening remarks at her confirmation hearing for national intelligence chief, said that she has \u8220\'20\'1Cno love for Assad, Gaddafi, or any dictator, I just hate al-Qaida\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Gabbard was pushing back against criticism for her 2017 meeting with the then Syrian dictator Bashar al-Assad during a visit to Damascus, Syria, that will become a focal point of questioning during the hearing.\par \par \uc2 \u8221\'20\'1DI hate that we have leaders who cozy up to Islamist extremists, minimizing them to so called rebels,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, indicating the former national security adviser Jake Sullivan.\par \par \uc2 Gabbard has come under attack for her public remarks saying that Syria did not use chemical weapons against civilians and that Russia was provoked into invading Ukraine, and for her defense of Edward Snowden.\par \par \uc2 If confirmed, Gabbard has said that she will \u8220\'20\'1Ccheck my own personal views at the door\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In her opening remarks, she attacked Biden-era intelligence officials for leading to a crisis of confidence in the US intelligence community. Gabbard said she was \u8220\'20\'1Ccommitted to delivering intelligence that is collected, analyzed and reported without bias, prejudice or political influence\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Gabbard said her military service and work in Congress on the homeland security, foreign affairs and armed services committee means that \u8220\'20\'1CI know first-hand how essential accurate, unbiased, timely intelligence is to the president, to Congress, to our war fighters. I also know the heavy costs of intelligence failures and abuses.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Gabbard also attacked those who raised concerns about her ties to the Science of Identity Foundation, which some critics have said is a cult.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CUnfortunately, they\u8217\'20\'19re once again using the religious bigotry card, but this time, trying to foment religious bigotry against Hindus and Hinduism,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 If anyone is sincerely interested in knowing more about my own personal spiritual path, Hinduism, I welcome you to go to my account on X, where I\u8217\'20\'19ll share more on this topic.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.19pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.58pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2 , in his opening statement on Thursday before the Senate health committee, said he was \u8220\'20\'1Chumbled\u8221\'20\'1D to be \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s nominee to see the \uc2 Department of Health and Human Services\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The overall health of Americans is in \u8220\'20\'1Cgrievous condition\u8221\'20\'1D, Kennedy said, noting that more than 70% of adults and a third of children are overweight or obese.\par \par \uc2 The United States has worse health than any other developed nation. We spend more on healthcare, sometimes double, sometimes triple, as other nations.\par \par \uc2 Kennedy said that if he is confirmed, he will do \u8220\'20\'1Ceverything in my power to put the health of America on track.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.03pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.48pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Kash Patel, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s pick to be the next \uc2 FBI\uc2  director, distances himself from criticism relating to the January 6 Capitol attack under questioning from Dick Durbin, the top Democrat on the Senate judiciary committee.\par \par \uc2 Patel says he has always rejected violence against law enforcement officers, including on January 6, and that he did not agree with any commutations for people who attacked police.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI have repeatedly, often publicly and privately, said there can never be a tolerance for violence against law enforcement,\u8221\'20\'1D Patel said.\par \par \uc2 But he sidestepped entirely Durbin\u8217\'20\'19s question about whether he thought \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  made the country safer by pardoning 1,600 January 6 rioters, including many who were convicted of assault against law enforcement.\par \par \uc2 And he distanced himself from his involvement in the jailhouse recording of the so-called \u8220\'20\'1CJanuary 6 choir\u8221\'20\'1D singing the national anthem that was repeatedly played at Trump rallies during the election campaign.\par \par \uc2 Multiple members of the choir had been in custody specifically for violently attacking police during the riot.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.53pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.46pm GMT\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m in a crowded White House press briefing room where \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is expected to hold a briefing at 11am about last night\u8217\'20\'19s plane crash at Reagan Washington National airport.\par \par \uc2 A presidential seal has been added to the briefing room lectern and there are two flags on the podium.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  made only one appearance here during his four years in office, whereas Trump regularly held briefings during the Covid-19 pandemic, most notoriously when he speculated on the merits of bleach as a cure.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s the first test of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s second term in the role of consoler-in-chief, one that \uc2 Ronald Reagan\uc2  played after the Space Shuttle Challenger disaster, \uc2 Bill Clinton\uc2  often performed with aplomb and Biden delivered with characteristic empathy. What could go wrong?\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.52pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.39pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Bernie Sanders, the independent senator of Vermont, congratulated \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2  for the phrase \u8220\'20\'1CMake America healthy again\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Speaking at Kennedy\u8217\'20\'19s confirmation hearing in front of the Senate health committee, Sanders asked if the nominee would work to lower the cost of prescription drugs and guarantee family leave if confirmed.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m not quite sure how we can move to making America healthy again unless we have the guts to take on the insurance companies and drug companies and guarantee healthcare for all people,\u8221\'20\'1D Sanders said.\par \par \uc2 How do you have a healthy country when women are forced to go back [to work after having babies]? That\u8217\'20\'19s not making America healthy again.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.45pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.35pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Dick Durbin, the top Democrat on the Senate judiciary committee, notes that Kash Patel has complained that he was hamstrung by bad-faith actors at every position he has held \u8211\'20\'13 including in the first Trump White House, at the justice department and at the defense department.\par \par \uc2 Durbin says that this is conspiratorial thinking and that he \u8220\'20\'1Cdoes not meet the standard\u8221\'20\'1D to lead the \uc2 FBI\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.37pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.32pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Senator Mark Warner, a Democrat and the vice-chair of the Senate intelligence committee, said that he \u8220\'20\'1Ccontinues to have significant concerns about [Tulsi] Gabbard\u8217\'20\'19s qualifications \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Warner, one of Gabbard\u8217\'20\'19s most vocal critics, has said that Gabbard\u8217\'20\'19s public questioning of Syria\u8217\'20\'19s use of chemical weapons and her position that Russia was provoked into launching its invasion of Ukraine \u8220\'20\'1Craises serious questions about your judgment\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt also leads me to question whether you can develop the trust necessary to give our allies confidence that they can share their most sensitive intelligence,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Make no mistake about if they stop sharing that intelligence, the United States will be less safe.\par \par \uc2 He said that intelligence sharing between the United States and Australia helped prevent a terrorist attack at a Taylor Swift concert.\par \par \uc2 Warner also attacked Gabbard for her support of the NSA whistleblower Edward Snowden, who leaked files from the intelligence agency and then fled to Russia, where he has remained a fugitive since 2013.\par \par \uc2 Her support for Snowden gave him \u8220\'20\'1Cserious concerns about confirming\u8221\'20\'1D Gabbard.\par \par \uc2 He also attacked her for her opposition FISA Section 702, a law that gives the US sweeping powers to collect intelligence of non-Americans outside the United States.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.37pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.30pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Republican chair of Senate committee has 'some reservations' on RFK Jr vaccine positions\par \par \uc2 Bill Cassidy\uc2 , the Republican chair of the Senate health committee, opened the confirming hearing of \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2  by saying that he had \u8220\'20\'1Csome reservations\u8221\'20\'1D on Kennedy\u8217\'20\'19s past positions on vaccines.\par \par \uc2 Cassidy spoke about his experience as a doctor, and told a story about a patient he treated who needed an emergency liver transplant.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI thought $50 of vaccines could have prevented this all. And that was an inflection point in my career,\u8221\'20\'1D Cassidy said.\par \par \uc2 He said vaccines \u8220\'20\'1Csave lives. I know they\u8217\'20\'19re a crucial part of keeping our nation healthy.\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He noted that Kennedy has an \u8220\'20\'1Ctremendous\u8221\'20\'1D following, and that there are people who trust him more than their own doctors.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe question is, what will you do with that trust?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.17pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.18pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Tom Cotton, the Republican chair of the Senate intelligence committee and a vocal supporter of \uc2 Tulsi Gabbard\uc2 , begins by telling a packed room that the nomination has \u8220\'20\'1Cgenerated a bit more interest and attention than do most nominees before this committee \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 But I want to stress Miss Gabbard has been and will be treated with the exact same respect, consideration and professionalism that were extended to every nominee, no more, no less, no better, no worse.\par \par \uc2 Cotton said that Gabbard had undergone five \uc2 FBI\uc2  background checks and that he had spent two hours reviewing the report, which comes to 300 pages. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s clean as a whistle,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 He also defended Gabbard\u8217\'20\'19s military record and loyalty to the US, saying he was \u8220\'20\'1Cdismayed\u8221\'20\'1D by attacks against Gabbard, saying that \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  had \u8220\'20\'1Csmeared\u8221\'20\'1D her by calling her an \u8220\'20\'1Casset of a foreign nation\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.20pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.16pm GMT\par \par \uc2 RFK Jr's second day of confirmation hearings begins\par \par \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 s Senate confirmation hearing to become America\u8217\'20\'19s top health official has also started at the health committee.\par \par \uc2 The independent senator Bernie Sanders, who on Wednesday confronted Kennedy over anti-vaccine merchandise sold by his former organization Children\u8217\'20\'19s Health Defense, is expected to continue probing the nominee\u8217\'20\'19s controversial vaccine statements that have drawn fierce opposition from the medical community.\par \par \uc2 Kennedy\u8217\'20\'19s nomination to lead the \uc2 Department of Health and Human Services\uc2  has sparked unprecedented pushback, with more than 15,000 medical professionals and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/dec/10/fk-hhs-nomination-nobel-laureates-letter"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 75 Nobel laureates}}}\uc2  mobilizing against his confirmation.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.21pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.12pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Tulsi Gabbard\uc2  hearing begins for intelligence chief\par \par \uc2 Tulsi Gabbard\uc2  has arrived at the Dirksen Senate building for a confirmation hearing as director of national intelligence that is expected to be one of the most contested of the early Trump administration.\par \par \uc2 She was accompanied by her family, as well as supporters including the recently confirmed attorney general, Pam Bondi.\par \par \uc2 Supporters began to chant \u8220\'20\'1CUSA! USA! USA!\u8221\'20\'1D before the hearing began.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.19pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.09pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Top Democrat expresses doubt on Patel's 'experience' and 'judgment' to lead \uc2 FBI\par \par \uc2 Richard Durbin\uc2 , the top Democrat on the Senate judiciary committee, said he does not believe that Kash Patel has the \u8220\'20\'1Cexperience\u8221\'20\'1D, \u8220\'20\'1Ctemperament\u8221\'20\'1D or \u8220\'20\'1Cjudgment\u8221\'20\'1D to lead the \uc2 FBI\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAfter meeting with Mr Patel and reviewing his record, I do not believe you meet the standard,\u8221\'20\'1D Durbin said.\par \par \uc2 Durbin described Patel as \u8220\'20\'1Csomeone who\u8217\'20\'19s left behind a trail of grievances throughout his life, lashing out at anyone who disrespects him or doesn\u8217\'20\'19t agree with him.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He noted that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  had fired his first \uc2 FBI\uc2  director, \uc2 James Comey\uc2 , and forced out his second \uc2 FBI\uc2  director, \uc2 Christopher Wray\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWith Mr Patel, however, obviously, the president has found a loyalist,\u8221\'20\'1D Durbin said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.17pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.02pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump to speak after fatal mid-air collision near Washington DC\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will appear in the White House briefing room at 11am ET to speak about Wednesday\u8217\'20\'19s deadly mid air collision near Washington DC.\par \par \uc2 The bodies of 28 people have been retrieved from the Potomac River and no survivors are expected to be found following a midair collision of an \uc2 American Airlines\uc2  jet and a military Black Hawk helicopter at Reagan National airport.\par \par \uc2 You can follow our updates on the plane crash {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2025/jan/30/plane-crashes-near-washington-dc-after-mid-air-collision-with-military-helicopter-follow-live"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 on our live blog.}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2025/jan/30/plane-crashes-near-washington-dc-after-mid-air-collision-with-military-helicopter-follow-live"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Washington DC officials believe there are no survivors after jet carrying 64 people collided with military helicopter \u8211\'20\'13 latest}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.16pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.54pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Tulsi Gabbard\uc2  faces Senate intelligence committee for confirmation hearing\par \par \uc2 Tulsi Gabbard\uc2 , \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s choice to be director of national intelligence, will begin her confirmation hearing with the Senate intelligence committee at 10am ET.\par \par \uc2 Senator Tom Cotton, the Republican chair of the Senate intelligence committee, said he supported Gabbard\u8217\'20\'19s nomination even before his committee began the hearing.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI support \uc2 Tulsi Gabbard\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s nomination,\u8221\'20\'1D Cotton told Fox News.\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19ve been working with her to move towards confirmation, and I look forward to working with her for four years.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.15pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.49pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Chuck Grassley\uc2 , the Senate judiciary committee chair, began the confirmation hearing for Kash Patel by recognizing the victims of Wednesday night\u8217\'20\'19s plane crash in Washington DC.\par \par \uc2 Grassley then said that the \uc2 FBI\uc2  has the \u8220\'20\'1Clowest rating in a century\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s no surprise that public trust has declined in an institution that has been plagued by abuse, lack of transparency and weaponization of law enforcement,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Nevertheless, the \uc2 FBI\uc2  remains an \u8220\'20\'1Cimportant, even indispensable\u8221\'20\'1D institution for law and order in the country, he said.\par \par \uc2 Addressing Patel, he said the job of \uc2 FBI\uc2  director is to restore the public trust and return the institution to its core mission of \u8220\'20\'1Cfighting crime\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.51pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.42pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Kash Patel, nominated by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to be the next \uc2 FBI\uc2  director, has entered the Senate judiciary room to begin his confirmation hearing.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.45pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.31pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Analysis: RFK Jr testimony offers 'through the looking glass' moment for Democrats\par \par \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s testimony was a \u8220\'20\'1Cthrough the looking glass\u8221\'20\'1D moment for some senators, as lawmakers questioned one of the nation\u8217\'20\'19s most influential vaccine critics for a job as the top US health official.\par \par \uc2 The hearing was a testament to how quickly Republicans have integrated \u8220\'20\'1CMake America Healthy Again\u8221\'20\'1D rhetoric into their own, lauding Kennedy, who was called a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/28/caroline-kennedy-rfk-letter"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cpredator\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  only hours earlier in a letter by his own cousin, as the correct man to head the \uc2 Department of Health and Human Services\uc2  (\uc2 HHS\uc2 ).\par \par \uc2 That letter alone, which described how Kennedy put baby chicks and mice into a blender for the birds of prey he keeps as pets, might have been disqualifying in earlier political eras.\par \par \uc2 But as the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/trump-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump administration}}}\uc2  dominates headlines with nominees, executive orders and new laws, Kennedy\u8217\'20\'19s hearing on Wednesday was one more spectacle where thunderous Democrats attempted to hold a mirror to the nominee, only for him to step right through.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/30/rfk-jr-testimony-confirmation-hearing"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 RFK Jr\u8217\'20\'19s testimony offers a \u8216\'20\'18through the looking glass\u8217\'20\'19 moment for Democratic senators}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.14pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.24pm GMT\par \par \uc2 RFK Jr to face Senate health committee on second day of hearings\par \par \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2 , \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s pick to head the \uc2 Department of Health and Human Services\uc2 , will face the Senate health committee from 10am ET.\par \par \uc2 Kennedy\u8217\'20\'19s appearance in front of the health committee comes a day after a bruising performance in a heated three-and-a-half-hour hearing before the finance committee.\par \par \uc2 During the combative confirming hearing on Wednesday, Democrats confronted one of the US\u8217\'20\'19s most prominent vaccine skeptics, who will possibly be handed the reins of America\u8217\'20\'19s public health system.\par \par \uc2 The Senate finance committee\u8217\'20\'19s ranking member, \uc2 Ron Wyden\uc2 , challenged the 71-year-old Kennedy over seemingly contradictory statements, reading quotes from podcasts in which Kennedy had claimed \u8220\'20\'1Cno vaccine is safe and effective\u8221\'20\'1D while testifying under oath that he supports vaccines. He read another quote from 2020 how Kennedy claimed he regretted vaccinating his children.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAll of these things cannot be true,\u8221\'20\'1D Wyden said. \u8220\'20\'1CSo are you lying to Congress today when you say you are pro-vaccine, or did you lie on all those podcasts?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Colorado senator Michael Bennet accused Kennedy of \u8220\'20\'1Cpeddling half-truths\u8221\'20\'1D throughout his career, demanding yes or no answers about past controversial statements. When asked if he had called Lyme disease a \u8220\'20\'1Chighly likely\u8221\'20\'1D military bioweapon, Kennedy said, \u8220\'20\'1CI probably did say that,\u8221\'20\'1D although he disputed other claims.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/29/rfk-jr-senate-confirmation-hearing"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 RFK Jr and Democrats clash over his vaccine history in confirmation hearing}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.13pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.07pm GMT\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA lot of people say he\u8217\'20\'19s crazy,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is reported to have once said of his pick to be the next \uc2 FBI\uc2  director, Kash Patel. \u8220\'20\'1C I think he\u8217\'20\'19s kind of crazy. But sometimes you need a little crazy.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 If Trump gets his way, crazy will now be coming to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/fbi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 FBI}}}\uc2 , the 116-year-old national security and law enforcement agency charged with protecting the US from terrorism, cybercrime and other threats.\par \par \uc2 Kashyap \u8220\'20\'1CKash\u8221\'20\'1D Patel is the son of Indian immigrants. His parents, of Gujarati ancestry, moved to the US in the 1970s after his father, Pramod, fled the oppressive regime of \uc2 Idi Amin\uc2  in Uganda. Pramod became a financial officer for an aviation company.\par \par \uc2 Patel was born and raised in Garden City, a well-to-do village on Long Island, New York, living in a home that included his father\u8217\'20\'19s eight siblings. In his memoir, he writes of an extended family setting off for Disney World every year in a 15-car convoy and watching the \uc2 New York Islanders\uc2  play ice hockey. His {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.defense.gov/About/Biographies/Biography/Article/2418491/kashyap-p-patel/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 official biography}}}\uc2  on the Pentagon website notes: \u8220\'20\'1CKash is a life-long ice hockey player, coach, and fan.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Raised Hindu, he was one of the few students of colour at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.gardencity.k12.ny.us/o/gchs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Garden City high school}}}\uc2 . His senior yearbook quotation, taken from the Jewish theologian Abraham Joshua Heschel, was: \u8220\'20\'1CRacism is man\u8217\'20\'19s gravest threat \u8211\'20\'13 the maximum of hatred for a minimum reason.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/dec/07/who-is-kash-patel-fbi-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kash Patel: how Trump\u8217\'20\'19s FBI pick went from public defender to provocateur}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.23pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.56pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Kash Patel, nominated by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to be the next \uc2 FBI\uc2  director, is expected to face scrutiny on Thursday about whether his loyalty to the president would end the independence of the nation\u8217\'20\'19s premier law-enforcement agency from White House political pressure.\par \par \uc2 The Senate confirmation hearing comes at a fraught moment for the \uc2 FBI\uc2  as its parent agency, the justice department, has been roiled by the demotion of scores of top officials and prosecutors deemed to be insufficiently trustworthy to carry out Trump\u8217\'20\'19s agenda.\par \par \uc2 The greatest challenge for \uc2 FBI\uc2  directors in the Trump era has been the delicate balance of retaining the confidence of Trump while resisting overtures to make public proclamations that are untrue or to open politically motivated lines of inquiry that personally benefit the president.\par \par \uc2 Patel is unlikely to have such difficulties, such is his ideological alignment with Trump on a range of issues including the need to pursue retribution against any perceived enemies like special counsel Jack Smith and others who investigated him during his first term.\par \par \uc2 That so-called list of enemies also stretches to senior \uc2 FBI\uc2  officials in Washington, whom Trump has criticized for allowing agents to obtain a search warrant to search his Mar-a-Lago club for classified documents after he left office and Trump ignored a grand-jury subpoena for their return.\par \par \uc2 Patel\u8217\'20\'19s dramatic views to reshape the \uc2 FBI\uc2  added to broader concerns about his fitness for the role after he was accused of lying about obtaining proper clearances that nearly botched a high-stakes hostage rescue operation by Seal Team Six during the first {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/trump-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump administration}}}\uc2  in 2020.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/30/trump-nominee-fbi-kash-patel-scrutiny"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 FBI pick Kash Patel to face scrutiny over Trump loyalty at Senate hearing}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.52pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Kash Patel to face Senate confirmation hearing for \uc2 FBI\uc2  director\par \par \uc2 Kash Patel, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s pick to lead the \uc2 FBI\uc2 , faces what could be a contentious confirmation hearing before the Senate judiciary committee on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Patel is expected to face scrutiny over his close relationship with Trump, which allowed him to become the frontrunner for the position, and his overall competence to lead the \uc2 FBI\uc2  at a time when it has weathered sustained attacks not just from Trump but Patel himself.\par \par \uc2 The Senate confirmation hearing is scheduled to begin at 9.30am ET.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.17pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.38pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s some more reaction to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s executive order instructing the military to prepare to house 30,000 immigrants at the US naval base in Cuba.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CGuant\u225\'00\'E1namo is a stain on our nation\u8217\'20\'19s honor,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Jerry Nadler\uc2 , a Democratic congressman from New York, said.\par \par \uc2 For years, I have advocated for its closure, condemning the abuses and glaring lack of accountability that persist there. This massive expansion into a mass detention camp is morally indefensible & raises significant civil liberties concerns.\par \par \uc2 This is horrific,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Rashida Tlaib\uc2 , a Democratic congresswoman from Michigan, said.\par \par \uc2 We cannot allow this level of dehumanization to become normalized. We need to shut down Guant\u225\'00\'E1namo once and for all.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.51pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.31pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has signed an executive order to prepare a huge detention facility at Guant\u225\'00\'E1namo Bay that he said could be used to hold up to 30,000 immigrants deported from the US.\par \par \uc2 Known primarily for holding suspects accused of terrorism-related offences, Trump ordered the preparation of a \u8220\'20\'1Cmigrant facility\u8221\'20\'1D that he said would be used to \u8220\'20\'1Cdetain the worst criminal illegal aliens threatening the American people\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s our explainer on the detention facility in the US-run military enclave.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/30/donald-trump-guantanamo-bay-cuban-detention-camp-illegal-migrants"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Guant\u225\'00\'E1namo Bay: the US prison camp in Cuba Trump is eyeing for illegal migrants}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.51pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.23pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Rights groups condemn Trump Guant\u225\'00\'E1namo Bay order as 'disastrous' and 'indefensible'\par \par \uc2 Rights groups were swift to condemn \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s announcement that he would order the construction of a migrant detention facility in Guant\u225\'00\'E1namo Bay.\par \par \uc2 Amnesty International{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/amnestyusa/status/1884725762927817048"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  Guant\u225\'00\'E1namo has been a \u8220\'20\'1Csite of torture, indefinite detention without charge or trial and other unlawful practices\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 It argued that Trump should be using his authority to close the prison and not repurposing it for offshore immigration detention.\par \par \uc2 The American Civil Liberties Union\uc2  said building a huge detention facility at Guant\u225\'00\'E1namo would be a \u8220\'20\'1Cdisastrous mistake\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Sending scores of immigrants to an inaccessible military base in Cuba could enable the government to deprive them of basic human rights, far from lawyers, the press, and Congressional oversight. Unfortunately, that appears to be the point.\par \par \uc2 The International Refugee Assistance Project said Wednesday\u8217\'20\'19s announcement marked \u8220\'20\'1Cyet another grave and indefensible act by the Trump administration\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In a statement it said that Guant\u225\'00\'E1namo is \u8220\'20\'1Cnotorious for torture and other egregious, illegal \uc2 US government\uc2  action\u8221\'20\'1D and that \u8220\'20\'1Ceven during the Biden administration, when only dozens of people were held there typically, rights violations were rampant.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 If that\u8217\'20\'19s what conditions at Guant\u225\'00\'E1namo were like under Biden, what will it be like when Trump requires the military to detain tens of thousands?\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.29pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.12pm GMT\par \par \uc2 As part of his administration\u8217\'20\'19s crackdown on illegal immigration, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has announced that the US will hold migrants at the notorious Guant\u225\'00\'E1namo military detention facility in Cuba.\par \par \uc2 The US naval base outpost in Guant\u225\'00\'E1namo Bay already has a facility used to house migrants picked up at sea, which is separate from the high-security prison for foreign terrorism suspects established in the aftermath of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/september11"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 11}}}\uc2  attacks by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/al-qaida"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Al-Qaida}}}\uc2  on the US.\par \par \uc2 A relatively small number of migrants have been detained at the facility \u8211\'20\'13 the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  reported that just 37 migrants were held there from 2020 to 2023 \u8211\'20\'13 but that could increase dramatically following Trump\u8217\'20\'19s announcement.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, Trump said the facility would hold up to 30,000 immigrants. \u8220\'20\'1CWe have 30,000 beds in Guant\u225\'00\'E1namo to detain the worst criminal illegal aliens threatening the American people. This will double our capacity immediately,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 But a US official told CNN that the facilities at Guantanamo Bay are far from prepared to house up to 30,000 migrants. \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s no way there\u8217\'20\'19s 30,000 beds any more,\u8221\'20\'1D the US official said, adding that in order to care for that number of people, the US would have to bring \u8220\'20\'1Ca lot of military staff\u8221\'20\'1D in.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.57pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Facebook\uc2  owner Meta has agreed to pay $25m to settle a lawsuit brought by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  over the platform\u8217\'20\'19s decision to suspend his accounts in the wake of the January 6 attack on the US Capitol.\par \par \uc2 The majority of the settlement \u8211\'20\'13 $22m \u8211\'20\'13 will go toward a fund to pay for Trump\u8217\'20\'19s presidential library, according to the Wall Street Journal. The rest will pay for legal fees and go to other plaintiffs listed in the case.\par \par \uc2 Following the January 6 attack, \uc2 Facebook\uc2  gave Trump the maximum penalty under its rules, suspending his \uc2 Facebook\uc2  and \uc2 Instagram\uc2  accounts indefinitely.\par \par \uc2 At the time, CEO \uc2 Mark Zuckerberg\uc2  justified the decision by saying: \u8220\'20\'1CWe believe the risks of allowing the president to continue to use our service during this period are simply too great.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump responded: \u8220\'20\'1CThey shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be allowed to get away with this censoring and silencing, and ultimately, we will win. Our Country can\u8217\'20\'19t take this abuse anymore!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Read the full story here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2025/jan/29/meta-trump-settlement-25-million"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Meta agrees to pay Trump $25m for suspending accounts over Capitol riots}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.09pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.39pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s abrupt decision to pause all US foreign aid programmes could exacerbate violence in Latin America, driving more migration from a region already struggling with the rise of organised crime, experts have warned.\par \par \uc2 The US disbursed $1.5bn (\u163\'00\'A31.2bn) in humanitarian, military, environmental, and economic aid to South American countries in the 2023 financial year, but Trump has suspended almost all US foreign aid for at least 90 days to review whether it is \u8220\'20\'1Caligned\u8221\'20\'1D with the interests of his administration.\par \par \uc2 Already, at least three humanitarian organisations have suspended support operations for more than 41,000 people displaced by a recent outbreak of guerrilla violence in Colombia.\par \par \uc2 Another programme aimed at finding jobs to integrate hundreds of thousands of Venezuelan migrants into Colombian society was also paralysed. In Brazil, two organisations working to assist Venezuelans fleeing Nicol\u225\'00\'E1s Maduro\u8217\'20\'19s dictatorship shut down their operations and a programme aimed at tackling the commercial sexual exploitation of children was ordered to stop.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COrganized gang violence has been a tragic burden for the region, as well as non-state armed groups,\u8221\'20\'1D said Marcia Wong, former deputy assistant administrator at the \uc2 US Agency for International Development\uc2  (\uc2 USAid\uc2 ) Bureau for Humanitarian Assistance.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWithout assistance, vacuums can develop \u8211\'20\'13 allowing exploitation and violence.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Read the full story here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/30/trump-aid-freeze-latin-america"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s US aid freeze will drive migration from Latin America, experts warn}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.05pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.21pm GMT\par \par \uc2 RFK and Gabbard to face confirmation hearings\par \par \uc2 Some of President Trump\u8217\'20\'19s most controversial cabinet picks are set to appear before Senate committees as part of their confirmation process today.\par \par \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2 , the nominee to head the \uc2 Department of Health and Human Services\uc2 , will face the health committee from 10am EST (3pm GMT).\par \par \uc2 Kennedy {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/30/rfk-hhs-confirmation-hearing"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appeared before the finance committee}}}\uc2  on Wednesday and, during a three-and-a-half-hour hearing, was grilled over past comments about the efficacy of vaccines as well as his grasp of the workings of the US healthcare system.\par \par \uc2 Also appearing at 10am ET, this time before the intelligence committee, will be \uc2 Tulsi Gabbard\uc2 , Trump\u8217\'20\'19s nominee for director of national intelligence.\par \par \uc2 A Democratic congresswoman until 2021, Gabbard gradually moved away from her old party and last year endorsed Trump, joining him on the campaign trail at several rallies.\par \par \uc2 Gabbard has faced opposition for comments on topics including Edward Snowden, the Russia-Ukraine War, and the Syrian civil war.\par \par \uc2 In January 2017, she revealed she had travelled to Syria to meet its now-deposed president, \uc2 Bashar al-Assad\uc2 , whose regime had been responsible for the deaths of hundreds of thousands of people. A few months later, she said she was \u8220\'20\'1Cskeptical\u8221\'20\'1D about whether the regime had been behind chemical weapons attacks that targeted civilians during the war.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.07pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.48am GMT\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s the full text of that post from the president of Cuba, \uc2 Miguel D\u237\'00\'EDaz-Canel\uc2 , condemning \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s announcement of plans for a migrant detention facility at Guant\u225\'00\'E1namo Bay.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn an act of brutality, the new \uc2 US government\uc2  announces that it will imprison thousands of migrants at the Guantanamo Naval Base, located in illegally occupied #Cuba territory, and forcibly expel them, placing them next to the well-known prisons of torture and illegal detention,\u8221\'20\'1D he wrote on X.\par \par \uc2 The country\u8217\'20\'19s foreign minister, \uc2 Bruno Rodr\u237\'00\'EDguez Parrilla\uc2 , said the base was in \u8220\'20\'1Cillegally occupied #Cuba territory outside the jurisdiction of US courts\u8221\'20\'1D and showed \u8220\'20\'1Ccontempt for the human condition and international law\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 esltrEn acto de brutalidad, nuevo gobierno de EEUU anuncia encarcelamiento en Base Naval en Guant\u225\'00\'E1namo, ubicada en territorio de {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Cuba?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Cuba}}}\uc2  ilegalmente ocupado, de miles de migrantes que expulsa forzosamente, a los que ubicar\u225\'00\'E1 junto a las conocidas c\u225\'00\'E1rceles de tortura y detenci\u243\'00\'F3n ilegal.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Miguel D\u237\'00\'EDaz-Canel Berm\u250\'00\'FAdez\uc2  (@DiazCanelB) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DiazCanelB/status/1884705081901130038?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 29, 2025}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.07pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.37am GMT\par \par \uc2 What has Trump announced about Guant\u225\'00\'E1namo Bay?\par \par \uc2 As part of his plans to reduce illegal immigration to the US, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has ordered the creation of a new detention facility capable of holding 30,000 people at Guant\u225\'00\'E1namo Bay.\par \par \uc2 He said the centre would be used to \u8220\'20\'1Cdetain the worst criminal illegal aliens threatening the American people\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSome of them are so bad, we don\u8217\'20\'19t even trust the countries [of origin] to hold them because we don\u8217\'20\'19t want them coming back,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CSo we\u8217\'20\'19re going to send them out to Guant\u225\'00\'E1namo.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Guant\u225\'00\'E1namo Bay is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/30/donald-trump-guantanamo-bay-cuban-detention-camp-illegal-migrants"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 best-known as the site}}}\uc2  of a US naval base on a coastal strip of land in southeastern Cuba that was leased by the US under a treaty in 1903.\par \par \uc2 A military prison set up on the base in the wake of the September 11 attacks has since been used to hold suspects accused of terrorism-related offences, with few ever charged or convicted.\par \par \uc2 Democratic presidents \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  both tried to close the prison but were stopped by Congress.\par \par \uc2 An existing facility, separate from the prison, is already used by the US to detain migrants intercepted at sea, although it does not appear in public government records and details have only recently surfaced.\par \par \uc2 As of February 2024, four people were being held at the facility, the \uc2 New York Times{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/09/19/us/politics/migrants-guantanamo-bay-cuba-detention.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2 , citing the department of homeland security.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.08pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.12am GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump plan to open migrant detention centre at Guant\u225\'00\'E1namo Bay an \u8216\'20\'18act of brutality\u8217\'20\'19, Cuban president says\par \par \uc2 Good morning and welcome to our live coverage of the latest news from US politics.\par \par \uc2 First up, the Cuban president has described \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s announcement of plans for a migrant detention facility at Guant\u225\'00\'E1namo Bay as an \u8220\'20\'1Cact of brutality\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Writing on X, \uc2 Miguel D\u237\'00\'EDaz-Canel\uc2  said the move would place people deported from the US \u8220\'20\'1Cnext to well-known prisons of torture and illegal detention\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, Trump signed an executive order instructing officials to prepare a facility capable of holding 30,000 people at the naval base, which over the past two decades has been used primarily to hold suspects accused of terrorism-related offences, with few ever charged or convicted.\par \par \uc2 Trump said the new facility would be used to \u8220\'20\'1Cdetain the worst criminal illegal aliens threatening the American people\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Stay with us for more on that announcement and all the day\u8217\'20\'19s developments.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.08pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250130el1u001jr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
