\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 Groups helping Americans find  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  pills report \uc2 Instagram\uc2  \u8216\'20\'18shadow-banning\u8217\'20\'19\b0\par\par\uc2 Carter Sherman \par \uc2 1,029 \uc2 words\par \uc2 30 January 2025\par 15:25 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Organizations find posts censored, removed or made difficult to find in days after Trump return to White House\par \par \uc2 Over the last week, the accounts of some major organizations that help Americans find \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills had their \uc2 Instagram\uc2  posts censored or removed, and at least one group said its account became difficult to find through searching \u8211\'20\'13 a practice known as \u8220\'20\'1Cshadow-banning\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Censorship of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related content on social media is a longstanding issue. In the days and weeks after the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  overturned Roe v Wade in June 2022, several \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights groups had their \uc2 Instagram\uc2  and TikTok posts removed or accounts suspended, while \uc2 Instagram\uc2  and \uc2 Facebook{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2022/jun/28/facebook-instagram-meta-abortion-pills-posts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 deleted the posts of users who mentioned \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  pills}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But the recent erasure and submerging of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related content, so soon after \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s return to power, has caused fear among some \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights supporters that a bigger crackdown could be on the horizon \u8211\'20\'13 and concerns that the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2025/jan/07/meta-facebook-instagram-threads-mark-zuckerberg-remove-fact-checkers-recommend-political-content"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Meta founder Mark Zuckerberg\u8217\'20\'19s promise}}}\uc2  to protect \u8220\'20\'1Cfree expression\u8221\'20\'1D may not apply to all speech.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s been this narrative of first amendment rights and free speech and we hope that that applies to all forms of speech,\u8221\'20\'1D said Rebecca Davis, head of marketing at Hey Jane, a telehealth clinic that provides \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills, emergency contraception and birth control.\par \par \uc2 Since last week, an \uc2 Instagram\uc2  search for the words \u8220\'20\'1Chey jane\u8221\'20\'1D will not surface the organization\u8217\'20\'19s account. Instead, users can only find it if they type in the word \u8220\'20\'1Chey jane health\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 the account\u8217\'20\'19s full name. This, Davis said, constitutes a shadow ban.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFor someone who\u8217\'20\'19s not following us but is seeking out care, there\u8217\'20\'19s really no way for them to be able to know that the only way to find us is to type \u8216\'20\'18hey jane health\u8217\'20\'19,\u8221\'20\'1D Davis said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt really does limit people\u8217\'20\'19s ability to find accurate information when they\u8217\'20\'19re seeking out this very timely, essential healthcare.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 On Friday, \uc2 Instagram\uc2  removed a Hey Jane post entitled \u8220\'20\'1C5 \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Facts You Need to Know in 2025\u8221\'20\'1D, alleging: \u8220\'20\'1CThe post may buy, sell, or exchange drugs that require a prescription from a doctor or pharmacist,\u8221\'20\'1D in violation of the platform\u8217\'20\'19s community guidelines. Hey Jane has been verified by LegitScript, which certifies online pharmacies. \uc2 Meta\uc2  can grant authorization to LegitScript-certified entities to run prescription drug ads.\par \par \uc2 The New York Times\uc2 , which {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2025/01/23/technology/instagram-facebook-abortion-pill-providers.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported on the changes}}}\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related content and accounts on Friday morning, said that two other organizations that help women access \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills, Just the Pill and Women Help Women, had their accounts restored.\par \par \uc2 But, at least by Friday evening, the Women Help Women account was unavailable and was not restored until late on Monday night, according to a screenshot viewed by the Guardian.\par \par \uc2 Jessica Valenti, author of a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://jessica.substack.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 popular newsletter}}}\uc2  that tracks developments in \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and restrictions, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://bsky.app/profile/jessicavalenti.bsky.social/post/3lgedi3ghp22l"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 flagged last week}}}\uc2  that multiple posts from the organization Aid Access, which mails \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills, were blurred out. As of Tuesday, at least two pinned posts on the account remained partially obscured; while the captions were available, the images were blurred or removed entirely. In a post last week, the group said that its account had recently been suspended for more than a week.\par \par \uc2 In a statement, a \uc2 Meta\uc2  spokesperson said the company\u8217\'20\'19s policies around the sale of pharmaceutical drugs had not changed.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe prohibit the sale of pharmaceutical drugs on our platforms without proper certification,\u8221\'20\'1D the spokesperson\u8217\'20\'19s statement said. \u8220\'20\'1CThese groups encountered both correct enforcement and a variety of issues, including overenforcement and a technical bug, that resulted in the blurring of some posts. But we\u8217\'20\'19ve been quite clear in recent weeks that we want to allow more speech and reduce enforcement mistakes \u8211\'20\'13 and we\u8217\'20\'19re committed to doing that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The blurs on the Aid Access account were the result of a glitch, as those posts had been cross posted to \uc2 Facebook\uc2  and removed on that platform on the suspicion that they had violated \uc2 Facebook\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s policies, according to \uc2 Meta\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Some of those removed posts were restored after the company decided they did not, in fact, violate any policies. The Women Help Women account was suspended in error.\par \par \uc2 The Hey Jane post, \uc2 Meta\uc2  said, was deleted because it did not meet the requirements for content around prescription drugs. Accounts and content may also not be \u8220\'20\'1Crecommended\u8221\'20\'1D by \uc2 Instagram\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s algorithm \u8211\'20\'13 and thus harder to find through search \u8211\'20\'13 if they deals with pharmaceutical drugs or have recently violated \uc2 Instagram\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s guidelines.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThroughout the years, the process of getting the accounts back or just communicating with big tech has been harder,\u8221\'20\'1D said Martha Dimitratou, digital strategist for the group Plan C, which provides information about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills, and a co-founder of Repro Uncensored, a coalition that works to protect access to information about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Medical experts widely agree that, in the first trimester of pregnancy, it is safe to \u8220\'20\'1Cself-manage\u8221\'20\'1D your own \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  using pills.\par \par \uc2 Plan C\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Instagram\uc2  account, Dimitratou estimated, had been taken down \u8220\'20\'1Csix, seven times at least\u8221\'20\'1D. \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s not at all institutional memory or understanding that this is something that keeps happening to this account,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEvery time we have a new instance of censorship, we have to prove that we are a non-profit. We have to go again from square one.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related content is often taken down when the procedure is in the headlines, said Jane Eklund, lead researcher with Repro Uncensored. The organizations that post the content are frequently told they are violating platforms\u8217\'20\'19 regulations around selling or providing goods online \u8211\'20\'13 even when their accounts have nothing to do with selling or providing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills, according to Eklund, who worked on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.amnestyusa.org/reports/obstacles-to-autonomy-post-roe-removal-of-abortion-information-online/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a 2024 Amnesty International report}}}\uc2  about the removal of online info about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSo many organizations are left in the dark. They would do what they need to do to avoid having their content taken down if they actually knew what that is,\u8221\'20\'1D Eklund continued.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey just don\u8217\'20\'19t really have that transparency from the platform.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 This story has been updated to reflect comments from \uc2 Meta\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250129el1t002pf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
