\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Trump order to turn Guant\u225\'00\'E1namo Bay into migrant detention center prompts outcry \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Robert Mackey, Lauren Gambino, Joan E Greve and Christy Cooney \par \uc2 11,945 \uc2 words\par \uc2 30 January 2025\par 03:20 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This blog has now closed. Read our latest story here\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.08am GMT\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 Another very full day of news from the Trump restoration draws to a close, but your \uc2 Guardian\uc2  livebloggers will be back on Thursday to chronicle events as they unfold. Here are some of the main developments from the past few hours:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2025/jan/29/donald-trump-democrats-freeze-federal-funding-us-politics-live?page=with:block-679aa57a8f082bd5ac0ee58e#block-679aa57a8f082bd5ac0ee58e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ordered}}}\uc2  the US military to detain up to 30,000 undocumented immigrants at Guant\u225\'00\'E1namo Bay, prompting widespread backlash from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2025/jan/29/donald-trump-democrats-freeze-federal-funding-us-politics-live?page=with:block-679abb498f08d7cb6f3003b7#block-679abb498f08d7cb6f3003b7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rights groups, Democrats}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2025/jan/29/donald-trump-democrats-freeze-federal-funding-us-politics-live?page=with:block-679aa4158f08d7cb6f3002f6#block-679aa4158f08d7cb6f3002f6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Cuban government}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Office of Personnel Management sent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2025/jan/29/donald-trump-democrats-freeze-federal-funding-us-politics-live?page=with:block-679ab36b8f08d7cb6f300380#block-679ab36b8f08d7cb6f300380"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a memo }}}\uc2  to federal agencies instructing them to take immediate and far-reaching steps to comply with Trump\u8217\'20\'19s executive order to crack down on \u8220\'20\'1CGender Ideology Extremism\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A federal judge agreed to issue a temporary restraining order blocking Trump\u8217\'20\'19s freeze on federal spending after the White House press secretary {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2025/jan/29/donald-trump-democrats-freeze-federal-funding-us-politics-live?page=with:block-679ac9908f083fa6b3a7bc9a#block-679ac9908f083fa6b3a7bc9a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 undermined}}}\uc2  the administration\u8217\'20\'19s argument in a tweet.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Department of Government Efficiency celebrated the end of what it called \u8220\'20\'1CDEI scholarships in Burma\u8221\'20\'1D, which {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2025/jan/29/donald-trump-democrats-freeze-federal-funding-us-politics-live?page=with:block-679adb5b8f082bd5ac0ee720#block-679adb5b8f082bd5ac0ee720"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a former diplomat explained}}}\uc2  was really a bipartisan program to help young people struggling for an end to that country\u8217\'20\'19s sectarian military dictatorship.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s executive order \u8220\'20\'1Cto combat antisemitism\u8221\'20\'1D asks federal agencies to explore ways {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2025/jan/29/donald-trump-democrats-freeze-federal-funding-us-politics-live?page=with:block-679ac1918f083fa6b3a7bc51#block-679ac1918f083fa6b3a7bc51"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to deport pro-Palestinian activists}}}\uc2 , including student protesters.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Former New Jersey senator \uc2 Bob Menendez{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2025/jan/29/donald-trump-democrats-freeze-federal-funding-us-politics-live?page=with:block-679aaa178f082bd5ac0ee5ba#block-679aaa178f082bd5ac0ee5ba"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 added his name }}}\uc2  to the list of officials accused or convicted of public corruption hoping for Trump to show them mercy.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.10am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.47am GMT\par \par \uc2 Why is \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Doge picking on young people hoping to end Myanmar\u8217\'20\'19s nightmare autocracy?\par \par \uc2 The headlong rush to cut government funding for anything that sounds too much like \u8220\'20\'1Cdiversity, equity and inclusion\u8221\'20\'1D to the new administration\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wired.com/story/elon-musk-lackeys-office-personnel-management-opm-neuralink-x-boring-stalin/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shockingly young shock troops}}}\uc2  appears to have brought an abrupt halt to a program that supported young leaders struggling for a better future for Myanmar, the country formerly known as Burma, which is now ruled by a military dictatorship engaged in ethnic conflict.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Department of Government Efficiency {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/DOGE/status/1884612616347066536"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 boasted }}}\uc2  on his social media platform that a program to provide what it called \u8220\'20\'1C$45m in DEI scholarships in Burma\u8221\'20\'1D had been cancelled.\par \par \uc2 But as the former congressman and veteran diplomat \uc2 Tom Malinowski{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/Malinowski/status/1884733902620668363"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pointed out}}}\uc2 , the funding was for \uc2 USAid\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.iie.org/programs/usaid-lincoln-scholarship-program/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lincoln scholarships}}}\uc2 , \u8220\'20\'1Cwhich help young people struggling for freedom in Burma\u8217\'20\'19s dictatorship \u8211\'20\'13 a cause America has supported under Republican & Democratic presidents\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat could be \u8216\'20\'18woke\u8217\'20\'19 or \u8216\'20\'18DEI\u8217\'20\'19 about these scholarships?\u8221\'20\'1D Malinowksi asks. \u8220\'20\'1CThe only clue is that \uc2 USAID\uc2  says they\u8217\'20\'19re for students \u8216\'20\'18of diverse backgrounds\u8217\'20\'19 (oh no, diversity!). This is essential for Burma, where the military has exploited ethnic and religious divisions to stay in power.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The program description on the \uc2 USAid\uc2  website does indeed say that the aim of investing in \u8220\'20\'1C135 young Myanmar leaders from diverse backgrounds\u8221\'20\'1D is to help \u8220\'20\'1Cthe next generation of leaders to guide Myanmar along a path of inclusive socio-economic development\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Given the new administration\u8217\'20\'19s horror at the prospect of young people fleeing conflict zones to build better lives in the United States, wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t a modest investment in helping young people carve out a common future in a country divided by sectarian violence make sense?\par \par \uc2 Malinowksi added that, in his career as a senator, the new secretary of state, \uc2 Marco Rubio\uc2 , supported human rights in Burma and urged the Biden administration to do even more to help the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/jan/22/rohingya-refugees-bangladesh-border-myanmar-human-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 persecuted}}}\uc2  Rohingya ethnic minority.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt looks like these geniuses are just going through grant awards and killing anything that uses words like \u8216\'20\'18diversity\u8217\'20\'19 and \u8216\'20\'18inclusion,\u8217\'20\'19 even though in countries where ethnic and religious minorities are murdered and persecuted, these have long been American goals,\u8221\'20\'1D Malinowski concluded.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.09am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.34am GMT\par \par \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 , the former House speaker, has endorsed Ben Wikler for \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2  chair, just days before the party elects a new leader.\par \par \uc2 Wikler, who leads the Wisconsin Democrats and is the only former writer for the Onion in the race, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://bsky.app/profile/benwikler.bsky.social/post/3lgw3jgcmts2p"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shared}}}\uc2  Pelosi\u8217\'20\'19s endorsement on Bluesky.\par \par \uc2 The DNC will elect a new chair on Saturday.\par \par \uc2 While Pelosi remains a powerful force in Democratic party politics, Wikler\u8217\'20\'19s main rival for the leadership of the DNC, Ken Martin of Minnesota, touted the endorsement of a much younger party leader, Tennessee state representative {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/12/tennessee-justin-pearson-vote-reinstate-memphis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Justin Pearson}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.46am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.08am GMT\par \par \uc2 A federal judge in Rhode Island agreed to issue a temporary restraining order blocking \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s freeze on federal spending after the White House press secretary undermined the Trump administration\u8217\'20\'19s argument that it had rescinded the memo from the White House budget office that ordered a freeze.\par \par \uc2 As Mattathias Schwartz {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2025/01/29/us/politics/trump-anti-woke-funding.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2  for the \uc2 New York Times\uc2 , lawyers for 22 states and the District of Columbia, which had filed suit, introduced as evidence {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/PressSec/status/1884672871944901034"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a social media post}}}\uc2  from the White House press secretary, Karoline Leavitt, in which she insisted that, despite the memo, \u8220\'20\'1Cthe federal funding freeze\u8221\'20\'1D was still in effect.\par \par \uc2 US district court judge James McConnell Jr agreed that the harm caused by Trump\u8217\'20\'19s freeze was ongoing, in part because, \u8220\'20\'1Cbased on comments by the president\u8217\'20\'19s press secretary\u8221\'20\'1D, the impact of the withdrawal of the budget office memo was \u8220\'20\'1Chugely ambiguous\u8221\'20\'1D. The judge also pointed to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://storage.courtlistener.com/recap/gov.uscourts.rid.58912/gov.uscourts.rid.58912.28.0_1.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 extensive testimony}}}\uc2  from state officials that they had been locked out of systems that provide reimbursements for Medicaid and other government programs.\par \par \uc2 Congresswoman \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/AOC/status/1884733641139405132"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 mocked Leavitt}}}\uc2  in a post on the platform formerly known as \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , noting that her \u8220\'20\'1Ctweets were so bad today she earned the entire administration a federal restraining order. Keep talking and tweeting, girl! You\u8217\'20\'19re doing great!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.11am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.31am GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump order on antisemitism targets pro-Palestinian protesters\par \par \uc2 A new {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/presidential-actions/2025/01/additional-measures-to-combat-anti-semitism/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 executive order}}}\uc2  signed by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  on Wednesday \u8220\'20\'1Cto combat antisemitism\u8221\'20\'1D asks federal agencies to explore ways to deport pro-Palestinian activists, including student protesters, who are found to have broken the law during protests.\par \par \uc2 As our colleague {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/29/trump-executive-order-pro-palestinian-activists"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Marina Dunbar reports}}}\uc2 , the order appears to target students and other activists who engaged in demonstrations against the Israeli war in Gaza following the \uc2 Hamas\uc2  attack on Israel on 7 October 2023.\par \par \uc2 The text of the order says that action is necessary because the \uc2 Hamas\uc2  attack on Israel on \u8220\'20\'1Cunleashed an unprecedented wave of vile anti-Semitic discrimination, vandalism, and violence against our citizens, especially in our schools and on our campuses\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 If Not Now, an organization of American Jews \u8220\'20\'1Corganizing our community to end US support for Israel\u8217\'20\'19s apartheid system\u8221\'20\'1D, denounced the order.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are disgusted that Trump and his antisemitic, neo-Nazi allies are planning to deport students and other immigrants for protesting [against] the Israeli military\u8217\'20\'19s assault on Gaza, while gutting academic freedom by threatening to withhold billions in federal funding for universities,\u8221\'20\'1D the group said in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/IfNotNowOrg/status/1884713368524906602"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a statement}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CThis attack \u8211\'20\'13 fueled by anti-Palestinian racism \u8211\'20\'13 is all part of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s broad-based attack on immigrants, our education system, and our democracy.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Layla Saliba, a Palestinian American graduate student at \uc2 Columbia University\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/itslaylas/status/1884750943234732049"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  on social media that student protesters there were being monitored by the police as they rallied on Wednesday evening.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CJust outside the \uc2 Columbia University\uc2  gates, students are hosting a vigil in honor of Hind Rajab,\u8221\'20\'1D Saliba wrote on X. \u8220\'20\'1CHind was a six-year-old Palestinian girl killed by the Israeli military. [The] \uc2 NYPD\uc2  is monitoring and filming students as they read poetry.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.44am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.57pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump order to turn Guant\u225\'00\'E1namo Bay into migrant detention center sparks outcry\par \par \uc2 There has been a wave of criticism from across the country and around the globe to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s executive order instructing the military to prepare to house 30,000 immigrants at the US naval base in Cuba.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CGuant\u225\'00\'E1namo Bay has been the site of torture, indefinite detention without charge or trial and other unlawful practices by the \uc2 US government\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Amnesty International\uc2  said in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/amnestyusa/status/1884725762927817048"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a statement}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CPresident Trump should be using his authority to finally close the prison there, not re-purposing the facility for offshore immigration detention.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CGuant\u225\'00\'E1namo is a stain on our nation\u8217\'20\'19s honor,\u8221\'20\'1D Representative \uc2 Jerry Nadler\uc2 , a New York Democrat, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/RepJerryNadler/status/1884709160912105567"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote}}}\uc2  in response to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s comments on the order. \u8220\'20\'1CFor years, I have advocated for its closure, condemning the abuses and glaring lack of accountability that persist there. This massive expansion into a mass detention camp is morally indefensible & raises significant civil liberties concerns.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis darkly harkens back to why Guant\u225\'00\'E1namo was chosen to hold \u8216\'20\'18war on terror\u8217\'20\'19 detainees in the first place,\u8221\'20\'1D the historian of Cuba Andr\u233\'00\'E9s Pertierra {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/ASPertierra/status/1884714628560662975"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 observed}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CThe US sent Haitian refugees fleeing in the early 90s to Guant\u225\'00\'E1namo because it existed in a legal grey area in international law, limiting their rights and US obligations.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is horrific,\u8221\'20\'1D Congresswoman \uc2 Rashida Tlaib{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/RepRashida/status/1884738892504457287"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1C We cannot allow this level of dehumanization to become normalized. We need to shut down Guant\u225\'00\'E1namo once and for all.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHours after Holocaust Memorial Day, Trump opens a prison for immigrants at Guant\u225\'00\'E1namo,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Guy Verhofstadt\uc2 , the former prime minister of Belgium, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/guyverhofstadt/status/1884717012875907386"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote on X}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.44am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.28pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  has ramped up his spat with Florida\u8217\'20\'19s Republican-dominated legislature over who has the most extreme immigration policies by promising to veto {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sun-sentinel.com/2025/01/28/florida-lawmakers-beef-up-immigration-plan-with-trump-administration-help/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a bill they passed on Tuesday night}}}\uc2  called the Trump Act in deference to the new president.\par \par \uc2 The Republican governor has been fuming since lawmakers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/27/desantis-immigration-proposal-florida-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 abruptly shut down a special session}}}\uc2  he summoned them to on Monday to advance his anti-immigration agenda, then moved ahead with their own plans instead.\par \par \uc2 The humiliated DeSantis, in a flurry of posts to X, appearances on Fox News, and even a hastily convened \u8220\'20\'1Croundtable\u8221\'20\'1D on Wednesday morning, denounced the Tackling and Reforming Unlawful Migration Policy (Trump) Act as \u8220\'20\'1Cweak\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Ctoothless\u8221\'20\'1D, even though it was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sun-sentinel.com/2025/01/28/florida-lawmakers-beef-up-immigration-plan-with-trump-administration-help/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 written with White House}}}\uc2  help to support the president\u8217\'20\'19s deportation plans, according to the Sun-Sentinel.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, the governor posted to X that his \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/GovRonDeSantis/status/1884598402648096895"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 veto pen is ready}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D, in part because it would removed authority for immigration enforcement from his oversight and place it in the hands of a cabinet member with whom he has been feuding.\par \par \uc2 Agriculture commissioner \uc2 Wilton Simpson\uc2 , among those tipped to succeed DeSantis as governor when his term ends in 2027, hit back in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/WiltonSimpson/status/1884272725780488202"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a post}}}\uc2  of his own.\par \par \uc2 He highlighted the support of \u8220\'20\'1CFlorida\u8217\'20\'19s conservative legislature\u8221\'20\'1D to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s agenda of raids, arrests and deportations of undocumented migrants, and reminded DeSantis: \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m not the one who opposed and ran against President Trump\u8221\'20\'1D, a reference to his disastrous challenge for last year\u8217\'20\'19s Republican presidential nomination.\par \par \uc2 Student groups and immigration advocates protested across the state Tuesday against a measure included in the Trump Act and DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s proposals to charge undocumented people out-of-state tuition rates to attend Florida colleges and universities.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Florida\u8217\'20\'19s Democrats appear to be enjoying DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s squirming. In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/FlaDems/status/1884433059144999253?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a post}}}\uc2  to X, the party condemned the act it says \u8220\'20\'1Ckicks Dreamers out of college and gives police bonuses for working with Ice [\uc2 Immigration and Customs Enforcement\uc2 ]\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWill our lame duck Governor veto this bill or go home with egg on his face?\u8221\'20\'1D it asked.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.11am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.25pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Federal agencies ordered to change email settings to remove prompts for pronouns\par \par \uc2 Chuck Ezell, the acting director of the Office of Personnel Management, sent a memo to federal agencies on Wednesday instructing them to take immediate and far-reaching steps to comply with Trump\u8217\'20\'19s executive order, \u8220\'20\'1CDefending Women From Gender Ideology Extremism\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The memo, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/USOPM/status/1884730384799220124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 posted on X}}}\uc2 , orders agencies to go to great lengths to remove anything that might be defined as promoting \u8220\'20\'1Cgender ideology\u8221\'20\'1D from public websites and social media accounts, and even to make sure that internal email systems, like Outlook, are set to turn off prompts that ask users for their pronouns.\par \par \uc2 Agency leaders are required to notify employees to abide by the order, and undertake a review of programs, contracts and grants by 5pm on Friday, and \u8220\'20\'1Cterminate any that promote or inculcate gender ideology\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 They are also instructed to report back to the OPM by no later than noon on 7 February with a complete list of all steps taken to comply with the order and the guidance in the memo.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.46pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.50pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Add the name of former New Jersey senator \uc2 Bob Menendez\uc2  to the list of Democrats in legal trouble angling for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to do them a favor.\par \par \uc2 Speaking to reporters outside federal court in New York, where he was just sentenced to 11 years in prison for taking bribes, including 13 gold bars found in his New Jersey home during {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/01/bob-menendez-new-jersey-bribery-charges"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a 2022 raid by the FBI}}}\uc2 , Menendez unsubtly invoked Trump in his remarks.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWelcome to the southern district of New York, the wild west of political prosecutions,\u8221\'20\'1D Menendez said. \u8220\'20\'1CPresident Trump is right: this process is political and it\u8217\'20\'19s corrupted to the core. I hope President Trump cleans up the cesspool, and restores the integrity to the system.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Former New Jersey senator \uc2 Bob Menendez\uc2  praised \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  after his sentencing on corruption charges.\par \par \uc2 Like New York\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic mayor, \uc2 Eric Adams\uc2 , if Menendez wants Trump to intervene on his behalf, he will have to walk back previous comments denouncing the president. The former senator\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 YouTube\uc2  channel, for instance, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/live/2y6Z0F9jMTk?si=n9Q5GMoBoMstyodv"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 still features}}}\uc2  video of him raising, on the Senate floor in 2019, what he called then, \u8220\'20\'1Cthe entirely legitimate question of whether \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  could be compromised by the Russian government\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 If Menendez and Adams hold out hope, it could be because Trump has a track record of throwing a life line to former officials charged with public corruption.\par \par \uc2 In 2020, Trump commuted the 14-year sentence \uc2 Rod Blagojevich\uc2 , the former governor of Illinois and Celebrity Apprentice contestant, was serving after being convicted on corruption charges.\par \par \uc2 Trump called Blagojevich\u8217\'20\'19s punishment \u8220\'20\'1Ca tremendously powerful ridiculous sentence in my opinion\u8221\'20\'1D and Blagojevich emerged from prison {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.newyorker.com/magazine/2024/06/17/rod-blagojevichs-tips-for-prison-survival-just-in-time-for-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 calling himself}}}\uc2  a \u8220\'20\'1CTrumpocrat\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.46pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.11pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump orders officials to expand migrant detention facility at Guant\u225\'00\'E1namo\par \par \uc2 A memo sent to reporters by the White House communications team directs the new the secretary of defense, Pete Hegseth, and the secretary of homeland security, \uc2 Kristi Noem\uc2 , to act on his executive order to prepare a huge detention facility at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/guantanamo-bay"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Guant\u225\'00\'E1namo Bay}}}\uc2  that could be used to hold up to 30,000 immigrants deported from the US.\par \par \uc2 Here is the full text of the memo from Trump:\par \par \uc2 I hereby direct the Secretary of Defense and the Secretary of Homeland Security to take all appropriate actions to expand the Migrant Operations Center at Naval Station Guantanamo Bay to full capacity to provide additional detention space for high-priority criminal aliens unlawfully present in the United States, and to address attendant immigration enforcement needs identified by the \uc2 Department of Defense\uc2  and the \uc2 Department of Homeland Security\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 This memorandum is issued in order to halt the border invasion, dismantle criminal cartels, and restore national sovereignty.\par \par \uc2 This memorandum is not intended to, and does not, create any right or benefit, substantive or procedural, enforceable at law or in equity by any party against the United States, its departments, agencies, or entities, its officers, employees, or agents, or any other person.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.47pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.00pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Cuba denounces Trump plan to detain migrants at Guant\u225\'00\'E1namo Bay\par \par \uc2 Cuba has responded to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/29/trump-guantanamo-detention-center"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announcement}}}\uc2  that he plans to open a detention center for migrants at Guant\u225\'00\'E1namo Bay, with the foreign minister claiming the idea \u8220\'20\'1Cshows contempt towards the human condition and international law\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Writing on X, the US social media site owned by Trump backer \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 , \uc2 Bruno Rodr\u237\'00\'EDguez Parrilla{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/BrunoRguezP/status/1884706810625478887"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 condemned}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cthe \uc2 US government\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s decision to imprison migrants at the Guant\u225\'00\'E1namo naval base, in an enclave where it created torture centers and indefinite detention\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Also writing on X, Cuba\u8217\'20\'19s president, \uc2 Miguel D\u237\'00\'EDaz-Canel Berm\u250\'00\'FAdez\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/DiazCanelB/status/1884705081901130038"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called the plan}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Can act of brutality\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.21pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.47pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The Senate just voted, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.senate.gov/legislative/LIS/roll_call_votes/vote1191/vote_119_1_00023.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 56-42}}}\uc2 , to confirm \uc2 Lee Zeldin\uc2 , a former Republican congressman from New York, to be the administrator of the \uc2 Environmental Protection Agency\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Zeldin, who is expected to carry out Trump\u8217\'20\'19s orders to reverse Biden administration climate rules aimed at slashing emissions from vehicles, power plants and factories, will lead an agency newly staffed by lawyers and lobbyists for the oil and chemical industries.\par \par \uc2 Three Democratic senators joined every Republican in voting to put Zeldin in charge of the \uc2 EPA\uc2 : \uc2 Ruben Gallego\uc2  and \uc2 Mark Kelly\uc2  of Arizona, and \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2  of Pennsylvania. Senators \uc2 Cory Booker\uc2 , of New Jersey, and \uc2 Jon Ossoff\uc2 , of Georgia, did not vote.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.34pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s justice department has spoken with federal prosecutors in Manhattan about possibly dropping the corruption case against Mayor \uc2 Eric Adams\uc2  of New York, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2025/01/29/us/politics/justice-department-trump-charges-eric-adams.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the New York Times reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Adams, as Eric Berger {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/25/eric-adams-trump-new-york?CMP=Share_iOSApp_Other"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported for the Guardian}}}\uc2  last week, is a Democrat \u8220\'20\'1Cwho faces a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/26/eric-adams-charges-indictment"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 federal indictment}}}\uc2  for allegedly accepting bribes and illegal campaign contributions from foreign sources, met with Trump at his Mar-a-Lago resort in Florida shortly before the president-elect took office; went to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s inauguration, rather than attend scheduled events in the city for \uc2 Martin Luther King\uc2  Day; and did an interview with [Tucker] Carlson, a former Fox News host who frequently criticizes Democrats and has promoted conspiracy theories about immigration\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 All of these moves have been widely interpreted by critics of the mayor as a concerted effort to win Trump\u8217\'20\'19s favor, and a get-out-of-jail-free card.\par \par \uc2 Trump and Adams, the newspaper reports, citing several people close to the mayor, \u8220\'20\'1Chave been in direct communication for weeks, speaking on the phone\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.12pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.26pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Today so far\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s nearly 4.30pm in Washington DC. Here\u8217\'20\'19s a round-up of key US politics news so far:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 White House Office of Management and Budget\uc2  has rescinded its memo regarding the pause in federal grants and loans. The news comes a day after a federal judge temporarily halted the policy, which had prompted mass confusion and concern across the country.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 But the White House has created further confusion over the announcement with a cryptic statement. White House press secretary Karoline Leavitt{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/i/web/status/1884671760638853388"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told NBC News}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CIn light of the injunction, OMB has rescinded the memo to end any confusion on federal policy created by the court ruling and the dishonest media coverage. The executive orders issued by the president on funding reviews remain in full force and effect and will be rigorously implemented by all agencies and departments.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has signed the Laken Riley Act \u8211\'20\'13 named after a murdered nursing student \u8211\'20\'13 the first legislation to receive his signature since taking office last week. At a desk in the White House\u8217\'20\'19s East Room, Trump was surrounded by legislative sponsors of the bill as well as members of Riley\u8217\'20\'19s family. The bill directs authorities to detain and deport immigrants who are accused, though not convicted, of theft-related crimes if they are unlawfully present in the US.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 During the speech, Trump also said he was planning to sign an executive order opening a detention center at Guant\u225\'00\'E1namo Bay that would hold up to 30,000 people in the US illegally. Trump said the camp would be used \u8220\'20\'1Cto detain the worst criminal illegal aliens threatening the American people\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2  defended his record in a contentious hearing before the Senate finance committee. Kennedy, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s pick for secretary of health and human services, faced pointed questions from Democrats about his past comments criticizing vaccines and his reversal on supporting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The top Democrat on the finance committee accused Kennedy of having \u8220\'20\'1Cembraced conspiracy theories\u8221\'20\'1D. \u8220\'20\'1CThe receipts show that Mr Kennedy has embraced conspiracy theories, quacks, and charlatans, especially when it comes to the safety and efficacy of vaccines,\u8221\'20\'1D Senator \uc2 Ron Wyden\uc2  of Oregon said. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is the profile of somebody who chases money and influence wherever they lead, even if that means the deaths of children and other vulnerable people.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Republicans voiced support for Kennedy, but his path to confirmation remains unclear. Senator \uc2 Mike Crapo\uc2 , the Republican chair of the finance committe, told Kennedy: \u8220\'20\'1CI think you have come through well and deserve to be confirmed.\u8221\'20\'1D But Kennedy\u8217\'20\'19s habit of flip-flopping on crucial health-related issues could jeopardize his confirmation.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A judge sentenced former New Jersey senator \uc2 Bob Menendez\uc2  to 11 years in prison on Wednesday on federal bribery and corruption charges. Menendez, 70, a three-term Democratic senator, was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/16/bob-menendez-bribery-verdict"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 found guilty}}}\uc2  last year by a jury in a Manhattan courtroom of 16 counts of corruption, including bribery, extortion and acting as a foreign agent. He resigned from the Senate shortly after the conviction.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.29pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.11pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Chris Stein has been reporting on the reaction to a separate Trump administration effort to encourage federal workers to resign en masse.\par \par \uc2 For context, the US office of personnel management (OPM) sent nearly all of its 3 million employees {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.opm.gov/fork"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an email}}}\uc2  offering them deferred resignations and warning that, if they choose to stay, they may be laid off or reassigned.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s obvious that this is a scam built on a Musk template,\u8221\'20\'1D a federal employee told the Guardian on condition of anonymity. \u8220\'20\'1CTaking this buyout \u8211\'20\'13 a voluntary separation \u8211\'20\'13 would mean forfeiting benefits like the pensions many of us are building toward, or reduced pensions for those who would be eligible. It\u8217\'20\'19s a cruel joke and the various mocking lines about thanking people for their service are salt in the wound.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/29/trump-federal-workers-resignation-offer-reaction"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Federal workers decry Trump attempt to force mass resignations as \u8216\'20\'18cruel joke\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.45pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Former US senator \uc2 Bob Menendez\uc2  sentenced to 11 years in prison on corruption conviction\par \par \uc2 A judge sentenced former New Jersey senator \uc2 Bob Menendez\uc2  to 11 years in prison on Wednesday on federal bribery and corruption charges.\par \par \uc2 Menendez, 70, a three-term Democratic senator, was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/16/bob-menendez-bribery-verdict"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 found guilty}}}\uc2  last year by a jury in a Manhattan courtroom of 16 counts of corruption, including bribery, extortion and acting as a foreign agent. He resigned from the Senate shortly after the conviction.\par \par \uc2 A years-long investigation found Menendez had accepted bribes in the form of cash and gold bars in exchange for helping the governments of Qatar and Egypt.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.51pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.37pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The White House has not released further details about the Guant\u225\'00\'E1namo Bay order beyond what was previewed by the president during the bill signing.\par \par \uc2 One of the major logistical challenges of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s mass deportation plans is detention space. Despite the president\u8217\'20\'19s desire to deport millions of people living in the US unlawfully, the process of arresting and removing people can take weeks, months or even longer.\par \par \uc2 Congress has given Ice the money for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.house.gov/billsthisweek/20240318/Division%20C%20Homeland.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 41,500 }}}\uc2  detention beds in the 2024 fiscal year. Building additional facilities will take time and resources.\par \par \uc2 The US military {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/29/colorado-aurora-military-base-immigration-detention"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2  on Tuesday it would allow Ice to use Buckley space force base in Colorado to \u8220\'20\'1Cstage and process criminal aliens within the US\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.38pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.00pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump says he will open migrant detention center at Guant\u225\'00\'E1namo Bay\par \par \uc2 In his bill signing remarks, Trump said he was planning to sign an executive order opening a detention center at Guant\u225\'00\'E1namo Bay that would hold up to 30,000 people in the US illegally.\par \par \uc2 Trump said the camp would be used \u8220\'20\'1Cto detain the worst criminal illegal aliens threatening the American people\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSome of them are so bad, we don\u8217\'20\'19t even trust the countries to hold them because we don\u8217\'20\'19t want them coming back,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CSo we\u8217\'20\'19re going to send them out to Guant\u225\'00\'E1namo. This will double our capacity immediately.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Of the camp in Cuba, used to hold terrorism suspects, Trump said: \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s a tough place to get out of.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.23pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.48pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump signs Laken Riley Act\par \par \uc2 Trump has signed the Laken Riley Act, the first legislation to receive his signature since taking office last week. At a desk in the White House\u8217\'20\'19s East Room, Trump was surrounded by legislative sponsors of the bill as well as members of Riley\u8217\'20\'19s family.\par \par \uc2 The controversial measure was approved over the concerns of legal experts and immigration advocates who warned that the measure tramples immigrants\u8217\'20\'19 right to due process while failing to address very real problems with the country\u8217\'20\'19s overwhelmed immigration system. The bill directs authorities to detain and deport immigrants who are accused, though not convicted, of theft-related crimes if they are unlawfully present in the US.\par \par \uc2 It does not include additional funding for implementation, a concern raised in a memo from the \uc2 US Immigration and Customs Enforcement\uc2  (ICE).\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/29/laken-riley-act-us-immigration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump notches legislative win with Laken Riley Act signed into law}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.09am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.47pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump asked the newly confirmed DHS secretary \uc2 Kristi Noem\uc2  to stand for applause. He seemed to acknowledge that commenting on her gender and appearance was \u8220\'20\'1Cprobably not complimentary\u8221\'20\'1D but did so anyway.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CShe is a woman, but she is tough,\u8221\'20\'1D he said of Noem, adding: \u8220\'20\'1CDon\u8217\'20\'19t let that look fool you. That look is tough.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.48pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.44pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump said fury over Biden\u8217\'20\'19s border policy \u8211\'20\'13 and support for his immigration plans \u8211\'20\'13 was responsible for his victory in November.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s why I\u8217\'20\'19m here and not somebody else,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.50pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.42pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump is recounting \u8211\'20\'13 in gruesome detail \u8211\'20\'13 the murder of Laken Riley, a 22-year-old nursing student from Georgia who was murdered in 2023 by Jose Ibarra, an undocumented immigrant from Venezuela.\par \par \uc2 Trump said the bill \u8211\'20\'13 which would allow the arrest and detention of undocumented immigrants charged with theft-related crimes \u8211\'20\'13 was a \u8220\'20\'1Ctremendous tribute\u8221\'20\'1D to Riley.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWith today\u8217\'20\'19s action, her name will also live for ever in the laws of our land,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, acknowledging her parents and family members who are in the office.\par \par \uc2 He also touted the bipartisan nature of the bill, which attracted notable Democratic support in both chambers.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.45pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.34pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump speaks before signing Laken Riley Act\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is speaking at the White House, where he is expected to sign the immigration detention bill, the Laken Riley Act.\par \par \uc2 But first he is taking a victory lap, touting the size of his electoral (and popular vote) win as well as his administration\u8217\'20\'19s blitz of executive actions. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve broken decades of failed Washington policies and restored common sense and sanity to our government,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump declared.\par \par \uc2 He said his administration has informed federal workers that \u8220\'20\'1Cthey must show up to the office on time and on schedule\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CShow up or be terminated,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Trump also made a number of claims about the border, rescinding Biden administration policies on energy and DEI. He added that the \u8220\'20\'1Cwater has now begun flowing in California\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Trump has claimed that the US military entered the state and \u8220\'20\'1Cturned on the water\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 which the California department of water resources {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/CA_DWR/status/1884122000232444407"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 clarified}}}\uc2 , explaining that the military did not enter the state and that federal pumps had been temporarily offline for maintenance.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.55pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.20pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Robert Tait has chronicled the echos between Trump\u8217\'20\'19s attempt to freeze trillions of dollars of federal funds and the \u8220\'20\'1Cdarkest days of Watergate\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Monday\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://bsky.app/profile/marisakabas.bsky.social/post/3lgr2gf5uzk27"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 memo}}}\uc2  from the White House office of management and budget (OMB) ordering a \u8220\'20\'1Ctemporary pause\u8221\'20\'1D on a vast array of spending activities across the \uc2 US federal government\uc2  convulsed official Washington in a manner arguably unseen since the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.history.com/news/what-was-the-saturday-night-massacre"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Saturday Night Massacre}}}\uc2  of 1973.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/richard-nixon"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Richard Nixon}}}\uc2  sparked frenzied accusations of a presidential coup and assaulting the rule of law when he tried to fire Archibald Cox, the special prosecutor appointed to investigate Watergate, before dispensing with the attorney general and his deputy after both declined to follow his order to carry out the sacking.\par \par \uc2 But he notes there are important distinctions.\par \par \uc2 Yet where Nixon\u8217\'20\'19s \u8211\'20\'13 counterproductive and ultimately doomed \u8211\'20\'13 attempt at halting the Watergate inquiry was unrehearsed and born of desperation, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s assault on spending programmes has been thought through and was months in the planning.\par \par \uc2 Its brainchild is \uc2 Russ Vought\uc2 , who headed the OMB in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s first presidency and has been nominated to the post again. Vought, founder of the rightwing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://americarenewing.com/about/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Center for Renewing America }}}\uc2  thinktank has commissioned a series of policy papers arguing, in effect, that the president is empowered to seize funds authorised by Congress for different spending priorities, even though the law states differently.\par \par \uc2 In Vought\u8217\'20\'19s crosshairs is the Impoundment Control Act of 1974, passed, weeks before Nixon resigned, in response to the president\u8217\'20\'19s aggressive practice of impounding funds appropriated by Congress. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.congress.gov/93/statute/STATUTE-88/STATUTE-88-Pg297.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The law}}}\uc2  has been in place since and \u8220\'20\'1Cestablish[es] a procedure providing congressional control over the impoundment of funds by the executive branch\u8221\'20\'1D. But Vought\u8217\'20\'19s thinktank has called it \u8220\'20\'1Cnorm-breaking, unprecedented, and unconstitutional\u8221\'20\'1D, and argues there is nothing illegitimate about such impoundments.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/29/trump-funding-freeze-evokes-watergate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Why Trump\u8217\'20\'19s order to freeze funding evokes the darkest days of Watergate}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.00pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Today so far\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s where the day stands so far:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 White House Office of Management and Budget\uc2  has rescinded its memo regarding the pause in federal grants and loans. The news comes a day after a federal judge temporarily halted the policy, which had prompted mass confusion and concern across the country.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 But the White House has created further confusion over the announcement with a cryptic statement. White House press secretary Karoline Leavitt{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/i/web/status/1884671760638853388"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told NBC News}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CIn light of the injunction, OMB has rescinded the memo to end any confusion on federal policy created by the court ruling and the dishonest media coverage. The executive orders issued by the president on funding reviews remain in full force and effect and will be rigorously implemented by all agencies and departments.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2  defended his record in a contentious hearing before the Senate finance committee. Kennedy, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s pick for secretary of health and human services, faced pointed questions from Democrats about his past comments criticizing vaccines and his reversal on supporting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The top Democrat on the finance committee accused Kennedy of having \u8220\'20\'1Cembraced conspiracy theories\u8221\'20\'1D. \u8220\'20\'1CThe receipts show that Mr Kennedy has embraced conspiracy theories, quacks, and charlatans, especially when it comes to the safety and efficacy of vaccines,\u8221\'20\'1D Senator \uc2 Ron Wyden\uc2  of Oregon said. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is the profile of somebody who chases money and influence wherever they lead, even if that means the deaths of children and other vulnerable people.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Republicans voiced support for Kennedy, but his path to confirmation remains unclear. Senator \uc2 Mike Crapo\uc2 , the Republican chair of the finance committe, told Kennedy: \u8220\'20\'1CI think you have come through well and deserve to be confirmed.\u8221\'20\'1D But Kennedy\u8217\'20\'19s habit of flip-flopping on crucial health-related issues could jeopardize his confirmation.\par \par \uc2 The blog will have more coming up, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.21pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.56pm GMT\par \par \uc2 White House statement sparks confusion over funding freeze\par \par \uc2 The White House is sending mixed messages about the implications of the announcement from the Office of Management and Budget that it was rescinding its memo freezing federal funding.\par \par \uc2 White House press secretary Karoline Leavitt {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/PeterAlexander/status/1884671760638853388"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told NBC News}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CIn light of the injunction, OMB has rescinded the memo to end any confusion on federal policy created by the court ruling and the dishonest media coverage.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe executive orders issued by the president on funding reviews remain in full force and effect and will be rigorously implemented by all agencies and departments. This action should effectively end the court case and allow the government to focus on enforcing the president\u8217\'20\'19s orders on controlling federal spending. In the coming weeks and months, more executive action will continue to end the egregious waste of federal funding.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The statement will almost certainly spark even more confusion about the status of federal grants and loans. Stay tuned for updates.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.20pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.47pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Senate Republican applauds reversal of federal funding pause\par \par \uc2 Senator \uc2 Susan Collins\uc2 , a Republican of Maine and the chair of the Senate appropriations committee, celebrated the \uc2 White House Office of Management and Budget\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s decision to rescind its order pausing federal grants and loans.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am pleased that OMB is rescinding the memo imposing sweeping pauses in federal programs,\u8221\'20\'1D Collins said in a new statement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhile it is not unusual for incoming administrations to review federal programs and policies, this memo was overreaching and created unnecessary confusion and consternation.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.36pm GMT\par \par \uc2 RFK Jr confirmation hearing concludes\par \par \uc2 The Senate finance commitee\u8217\'20\'19s confirmation hearing for \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2 , \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s pick for secretary of health and human services, has concluded.\par \par \uc2 Mike Crapo\uc2 , the Republican chair of the committee, told Kennedy: \u8220\'20\'1CI think you have come through well and deserve to be confirmed.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But it remains unclear whether Kennedy will have the necessary support for confirmation, particularly after Democrats pressed the nominee on his past comments criticizing vaccines and his long history of support for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access.\par \par \uc2 As Kennedy left the hearing room, his supporters cheered for him, with one yelling: \u8220\'20\'1CMake America healthy again!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.23pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.24pm GMT\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/JonLemire/status/1884665527143907821"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 screenshot}}}\uc2  shared on social media shows the announcement from the \uc2 White House Office of Management and Budget\uc2  that the order pausing federal grants and loans had been rescinded.\par \par \uc2 It states simply: \u8220\'20\'1COMB Memorandum M-25-13 is rescinded. If you have questions about implementing the President\u8217\'20\'19s Executive Orders, please contact your agency General Counsel.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.23pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.15pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump rescinds order pausing federal grants and loans\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 White House Office of Management and Budget\uc2  has rescinded \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s order that put a pause on federal grants and loans, which sparked confusion and concern across the country.\par \par \uc2 According to Reuters, a White House official confirmed the order had been rescinded. The news comes one day after the federal judge temporarily halted the funding pause.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.05pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Senator Bernie Sanders went on to mock \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2  over his flip-flopping on the issue of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, as the cabinet nominee has embraced \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  stance in recent weeks.\par \par \uc2 Echoing other Democrats on the finance committee, Sanders quoted Kennedy\u8217\'20\'19s own words from 2023, when he said that the government should not interfere with a woman\u8217\'20\'19s bodily autonomy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI have never seen any major politician flip on that issue quite as quickly as you did when Trump asked you to become \uc2 HHS\uc2  secretary,\u8221\'20\'1D Sanders said. \u8220\'20\'1CTell me why you think people should have confidence in your consistency and in your word when you really made a major U-turn on an issue of that importance in such a short time.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Kennedy replied: \u8220\'20\'1CSenator, I believe, and I\u8217\'20\'19ve always believed, that every \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a tragedy.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It is a line that Kennedy has returned to over and over again as Democrats hammer the cabinet nominee on his long record of support for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.24pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.54pm GMT\par \par \uc2 RFK Jr dodges Sanders' question on healthcare being a human right\par \par \uc2 Senator Bernie Sanders attempted to place \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2  on the record about whether he believed that healthcare is a human right, but the cabinet nominee repeatedly dodged the question.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDo you agree with me that the United States should join every other major country on earth and guarantee healthcare to all people as a human right? Yes, no?\u8221\'20\'1D Sanders asked.\par \par \uc2 Kennedy replied: \u8220\'20\'1CSenator, I can\u8217\'20\'19t give you a yes or no answer to that question.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.25pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.42pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Warren raises ethical concerns about Kennedy's nomination\par \par \uc2 Senator Elizabeth Warren, a Democrat of Massachusetts, highligted Kennedy\u8217\'20\'19s pledge to keep corruption and corporate influence out of the department of health and human services and asked him about his post-government plans.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHere\u8217\'20\'19s an easy question. Will you commit that when you leave this job, you will not accept compensation from a drug company, a medical device company, a hospital system or a health insurer for at least four years, including as a lobbyist or a board member?\u8221\'20\'1D Warren asked.\par \par \uc2 Kennedy asked Warren to repeat the question before asking: \u8220\'20\'1CWho? Me?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYes, you,\u8221\'20\'1D Warren said, as some laughs broke out in the hearing room.\par \par \uc2 Kennedy then said that he would commit to that pledge, prompting Warren to ask: \u8220\'20\'1CWill you also agree that you won\u8217\'20\'19t take any compensation from any lawsuits against drug companies while you are secretary and for four years afterwards?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ll certainly commit to that while I\u8217\'20\'19m secretary,\u8221\'20\'1D Kennedy said, before launching into a defense of his record without addressing his post-government plans.\par \par \uc2 Warren again pressed Kennedy on not taking compensation from lawsuits, and he continued to quibble with her questioning, avoiding a concrete answer to her queries.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf you get confirmed, you could influence every single one of those lawsuits,\u8221\'20\'1D Warren said. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd I am asking you to commit right now that you will not take a financial stake in every one of those lawsuits so that what you do as secretary will also benefit you financially down the line.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ll comply with all of the ethical guidelines,\u8221\'20\'1D Kennedy said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat is not the question,\u8221\'20\'1D Warren shot back. \u8220\'20\'1CNo one should be fooled here.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.26pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.16pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Senator \uc2 Catherine Cortez Masto\uc2 , a Democrat of Nevada, pressed Kennedy on whether he, as a lawyer, believed that pregnant women in life-threatening situations should be allowed to have emergency abortions even in states where the procedure is banned.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou would agree also as an attorney that federal law protects her right to that emergency care, correct?\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Cortez Masto\uc2  asked.\par \par \uc2 Kennedy replied: \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t know.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.27pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.06pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Senator \uc2 Maggie Hassan\uc2 , a Democrat of New Hampshire, suggested that she and \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2  actually agree on the issue of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, citing his many past comments in support of \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 As she questioned Kennedy, Hassan\u8217\'20\'19s staff displayed posters highlighting Kennedy\u8217\'20\'19s past remarks in support of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access. One poster quoting Kennedy read, \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m pro-choice \u8230\'20\'26 I don\u8217\'20\'19t think the government has any business telling people what they can or cannot do with their body.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou said that, right?\u8221\'20\'1D Hassan asked.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYes,\u8221\'20\'1D Kennedy tersely replied.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is remarkable that you have such a long record of fighting for women\u8217\'20\'19s reproductive freedom and really great that my Republican colleagues are so open to voting for a pro-choice \uc2 HHS\uc2  secretary,\u8221\'20\'1D Hassan said.\par \par \uc2 She then asked Kennedy, \u8220\'20\'1CYou have clearly stated in the past that bodily autonomy is one of your core values. The question is: do you stand for that value or not? When was it that you decided to sell out the values you\u8217\'20\'19ve had your whole life in order to be given power by President Trump?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Kennedy reiterated, \u8220\'20\'1CSenator, I agree with President Trump that every \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a tragedy.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.57pm GMT\par \par \uc2 RFK Jr echoes Trump on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and pledges to study 'safety issues' of mifepristone\par \par \uc2 Although \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2  has previously identified as \u8220\'20\'1Cpro-choice,\u8221\'20\'1D he fully backed \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s view on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  during his Senate confirmation hearing.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI agree with President Trump that every \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a tragedy. I agree with him that we cannot be a moral nation if we have 1.2 million abortions a year. I agree with him that the states should control \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D Kennedy told Republican senator \uc2 James Lankford\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 He added: \u8220\'20\'1CI serve at the pleasure of the president. I\u8217\'20\'19m going to implement his policies.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Asked about access to the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication Mifepristone, Kennedy suggested that federal agencies should examine potential \u8220\'20\'1Csafety issues\u8221\'20\'1D related to the drug.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe need to understand the safety of every drug \u8211\'20\'13 Mifepristone and every other drug,\u8221\'20\'1D Kennedy said. \u8220\'20\'1C[Trump] is not taking a position yet on Mifepristone, a detailed position, but he\u8217\'20\'19s made it clear to me that he wants me to look at the safety issues, and I\u8217\'20\'19ll ask \uc2 NIH\uc2  [the \uc2 National Institutes of Health\uc2 ] and \uc2 FDA\uc2  [the Food and Drug Administration] to do that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.27pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.46pm GMT\par \par \uc2 RFK Jr suggests \uc2 HHS\uc2  personnel decisions will be 'based upon my opinion'\par \par \uc2 Senator Mark Warner, a Democrat of Virginia, pressed \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2  on whether he would move to dismiss longtime staffers at the \uc2 Department of Health and Human Services\uc2 , as \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s other cabinet picks have already started doing at other agencies.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI will commit to not firing anybody who is doing their job,\u8221\'20\'1D Kennedy said.\par \par \uc2 Warner asked, \u8220\'20\'1CBased upon your opinion, or your political agenda, or Mr Trump\u8217\'20\'19s political agenda?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBased upon my opinion,\u8221\'20\'1D Kennedy replied.\par \par \uc2 Warner remarked, \u8220\'20\'1CSo I guess that means a lot of the folks who have had any type of views on vaccines will be out of work.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.53pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.31pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Senator Michael Bennet, a Democrat of Colorado, continued his rapid-fire questioning of Robert F Kennedy with more quotes from Kennedy\u8217\'20\'19s past writings and interviews.\par \par \uc2 Bennet asked: \u8220\'20\'1CDid you say that Lyme disease is highly likely a materially engineered bioweapon?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Kennedy replied: \u8220\'20\'1CI probably did say that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Bennet asked: \u8220\'20\'1CDid you say that exposure to pesticides causes children to become transgender?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Kennedy replied: \u8220\'20\'1CNo, I never said that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Bennet challenged that claim, saying he would submit the record to the committee chair. He then asked: \u8220\'20\'1CDid you write in your book, and I quote, \u8216\'20\'18it\u8217\'20\'19s undeniable that African Aids is an entirely different disease from western Aids\u8217\'20\'19?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Kennedy replied: \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m not sure.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Bennet concluded his questioning by reminding Kennedy of the importance of the job he is seeking, noting that Americans rely on the \uc2 Department of Health and Human Services\uc2  to provide accurate medical information.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis matters. It doesn\u8217\'20\'19t matter what you come here and say that isn\u8217\'20\'19t true, that\u8217\'20\'19s not reflective of what you really believe,\u8221\'20\'1D Bennet said. \u8220\'20\'1CUnlike other jobs that we\u8217\'20\'19re confirming around this place, this is a job where it is life and death.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.32pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.29pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Democrat's rapid-fire questioning puts RFK Jr on defense\par \par \uc2 Senator Michael Bennet, a Democrat of Colorado, said that he agreed with \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2  on some of his criticism of the US healthcare system, but he painted Kennedy as woefully unqualified to lead the department of health and human services.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat is so disturbing to me is that out of 330 million Americans, we\u8217\'20\'19re being asked to put somebody in this job who has spent 50 years of his life not honoring the tradition that he talked about at the beginning of this conversation, but peddling in half-truths, peddling in false statements, peddling in theories that create doubt about whether or not things we know are safe are unsafe,\u8221\'20\'1D Bennet said.\par \par \uc2 Bennet then launched into a series of damning, rapid-fire questions about Kennedy\u8217\'20\'19s past comments on a range of healthcare topics, including the coronavirus pandemic and Aids.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDid you say that Covid-19 was a genetically engineered bioweapon that targets Black and white people, but spared Ashkenazi Jews and Chinese people?\u8221\'20\'1D Bennet said.\par \par \uc2 Kennedy replied: \u8220\'20\'1CI didn\u8217\'20\'19t say it was deliberately targeted. I just quoted an \uc2 NIH\uc2 -funded and \uc2 NIH\uc2 -published study.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.29pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.14pm GMT\par \par \uc2 As Democrat \uc2 Ron Wyden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s questioning time ran out, \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2  attempted to clean up his record on vaccines, saying: \u8220\'20\'1CSenator, I support the measles vaccine. I support the polio vaccine. I will do nothing as \uc2 HHS\uc2  secretary that makes it difficult or discourages people from taking either of those vaccines.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Wyden shot back: \u8220\'20\'1CAnybody who believes that ought to look at the measles book you wrote saying parents have been misled into believing that measles is a deadly vaccine. That is not true.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.28pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.10pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Ron Wyden\uc2 , the top Democrat on the Senate finance committee, also pressed \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2  on his role in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/rfk-jr-samoa-measles-outbreak/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 deadly measles outbreak}}}\uc2  that struck Samoa in 2019.\par \par \uc2 The measles outbreak in Samoa \u8211\'20\'13 which claimed the lives of 83 people, most of them young children \u8211\'20\'13 came just months after Kennedy visited the island nation.\par \par \uc2 Quoting Kennedy\u8217\'20\'19s book that raised doubts about the potential lethality of measles, Wyden said: \u8220\'20\'1CThe reality is measles are in fact deadly and highly contagious \u8211\'20\'13 something that you should\u8217\'20\'19ve learned after your lies contributed to the deaths of 83 people, most of them children, in a measles outbreak in Samoa. So my question here is: Mr Kennedy, is measles deadly, yes or no?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Kennedy replied that the death rate from measles has historically been quite low, and he again denied any role in the Samoa outbreak.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI went there nothing to do with vaccines. I went there to introduce a medical and thematic system that would digitalize records in Samoa,\u8221\'20\'1D Kennedy said. \u8220\'20\'1CI never taught or gave any public statement about vaccines. You cannot find a single Samoan who will say, \u8216\'20\'18I didn\u8217\'20\'19t get a vaccine because of \uc2 Bobby Kennedy\uc2 .\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He concluded: \u8220\'20\'1CI went in June of 2019. The measles outbreak started in August. So, clearly I had nothing to do with the measles.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 That final comment seemed curious given that reports have pointed to the timeline of Kennedy\u8217\'20\'19s visit as potentially incriminating, considering the outbreak followed just a couple of months later.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.28pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.54pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Kennedy clashes with Democrat over past vaccine comments\par \par \uc2 Ron Wyden\uc2 , the top Democrat on the Senate finance committee, criticized \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2  for having \u8220\'20\'1Cspent years pushing conflicting stories about vaccines\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 As he began his questioning, Wyden quoted some of Kennedy\u8217\'20\'19s podcast interviews in which he claimed that \u8220\'20\'1Cno vaccine is safe and effective\u8221\'20\'1D and that he regretted vaccinating his own children. But in his opening statement, Kennedy denied being anti-vaccine.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMr Kennedy, all of these things cannot be true,\u8221\'20\'1D Wyden said. \u8220\'20\'1CSo, are you lying to Congress today when you say you are pro-vaccine, or did you lie on all of those podcasts? We have all of this on tape.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Kennedy replied that his previous comment about vaccines\u8217\'20\'19 safety had been truncated and had since been corrected, telling Wyden, \u8220\'20\'1CYou know about this, Senator Wyden, so bringing this up right now is dishonest.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Wyden retorted that Kennedy has \u8220\'20\'1Ca history of trying to take vaccines away from people,\u8221\'20\'1D citing his signature on a 2021 petition calling for the Food and Drug Administration to block access to coronavirus vaccines. Kennedy suggested that the \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2  had mishandled the recommendation process for those vaccines.\par \par \uc2 Another protester then interrupted the hearing.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.55pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.43pm GMT\par \par \uc2 In response to questioning from Republican chair \uc2 Mike Crapo\uc2 , \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2  said he was not looking to place restrictions on food options, even though he has consistently expresssed alarm over Americans\u8217\'20\'19 diets.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t want to take food away from anybody,\u8221\'20\'1D Kennedy said. \u8220\'20\'1CIf you like a McDonald\u8217\'20\'19s cheeseburger and a Diet Coke, which my boss loves, you should be able to get them.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The comment, an acknowledgment of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s long-documented {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://time.com/7095424/donald-trump-mcdonalds-love-campaign-kamala-harris-work-history/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 embrace of fast food}}}\uc2 , was met with chuckles in the hearing room.\par \par \uc2 Kennedy continued, \u8220\'20\'1CIf you want to eat Hostess Twinkies, you should be able to do that, but you should know what the impacts are on your family and on your health.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.38pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Protester disrupts Kennedy's opening comments on vaccines\par \par \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2  dedicated most of his opening statement to detailing his vision for addressing \u8220\'20\'1Cchronic disease\u8221\'20\'1D if confirmed as the secretary of health and human services, but he took a moment to address his past comments attacking vaccines.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNews reports have claimed that I am anti-vaccine or anti-industry. I am neither,\u8221\'20\'1D Kennedy said.\par \par \uc2 He was disrupted by a protester who appeared to yell in response: \u8220\'20\'1CYou lie!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The protester was escorted out of the hearing room, and then Kennedy was then able to continue his opening statement, saying, \u8220\'20\'1CI am pro-safety.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.10am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.31pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Before \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2  delivered his opening statement, the Republican chair and Democratic ranking member of the Senate finance committee shared a tense exchange on the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/28/trump-federal-funding-freeze-medicaid"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Medicaid portal outage}}}\uc2  that occurred yesterday.\par \par \uc2 Medicaid payment portals were down across the country yesterday following \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s announcement of a federal funding freeze, but multiple states reported that the portals were back online last night.\par \par \uc2 In his opening statement, Democrat \uc2 Ron Wyden\uc2  of Oregon pointed to the outage as a sign of what may be to come if Kennedy is confirmed to lead the department of health and human services.\par \par \uc2 The chair of the committee, Republican \uc2 Mike Crapo\uc2  of Idaho, criticized Wyden\u8217\'20\'19s comments as a \u8220\'20\'1Cfalse attack,\u8221\'20\'1D noting that the portals are now operational, but Wyden retorted that the outage had created \u8220\'20\'1Cbedlam across the country\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.22pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Democrat excoriates Kennedy for having 'embraced conspiracy theories'\par \par \uc2 The top Democrat on the Senate finance committee, \uc2 Ron Wyden\uc2  of Oregon, delivered a scathing rebuke of \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2  in his opening statement at the cabinet nominee\u8217\'20\'19s confirmation hearing.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe receipts show that Mr. Kennedy has embraced conspiracy theories, quacks, and charlatans, especially when it comes to the safety and efficacy of vaccines,\u8221\'20\'1D Wyden said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s made it his life\u8217\'20\'19s work to sow doubt and discourage parents from getting their kids life-saving vaccines. It\u8217\'20\'19s been lucrative for him and put him on the verge of real power. This is the profile of somebody who chases money and influence wherever they lead, even if that means the deaths of children and other vulnerable people.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Wyden noted that, if confirmed as the next secretary of health and human services, Kennedy would play a key role in issuing medical recommendations for the nation, and the Democrat expressed fear that Kennedy might use his authority to restrict access to the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication Mifepristone.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWomen deserve to know if Mr Kennedy will abuse his power as our country\u8217\'20\'19s chief health officer to essentially implement a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban by restricting access to this safe and legal medication,\u8221\'20\'1D Wyden said.\par \par \uc2 He concluded, \u8220\'20\'1CAfter a careful review of \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s statements, actions, associations and views, I have reached the conclusion that he should not be entrusted with the health and well-being of the American people. When he\u8217\'20\'19s taken every side of every issue, how can this committee and the American public believe anything he has to say?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.16pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The Republican chair of the Senate finance committee, \uc2 Mike Crapo\uc2  of Idaho, praised \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2  as \u8220\'20\'1Ca voice for an inspiring coalition of Americans who are deeply committed to improving the health and wellbeing of our nation\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In his opening statement, Crapo lamented that the US healthcare system has become a \u8220\'20\'1Cdyfunctional maze\u8221\'20\'1D for many Americans, and he framed Kennedy\u8217\'20\'19s potential confirmation as an \u8220\'20\'1Copportunity to deliver bold, transformative solutions\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRegardless of political party, everyone in this room shares a common recognition that our current system has fallen short, as well as a common desire to make our country healthier,\u8221\'20\'1D Crapo said. \u8220\'20\'1CI look forward to today\u8217\'20\'19s conversation as well as your testimony, Mr Kennedy.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.18pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.03pm GMT\par \par \uc2 RFK Jr confirmation hearing begins\par \par \uc2 The chair of the Senate finance committee, Republican \uc2 Mike Crapo\uc2  of Idaho, has kicked off the confirmation hearing for \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2 , \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s nominee for secretary of health and human services.\par \par \uc2 After Kennedy entered the hearing room, he walked up toward the dais to shake the hands of committee members while photographers swirled around him to capture the scene.\par \par \uc2 The hearing will begin with opening statements before senators have the opportunity to question Kennedy, who has faced intense criticism over allegations of sexual harassment and his shifting stance on vaccines.\par \par \uc2 Stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.52pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Anti-vaccine rhetoric and lawsuits were a lucrative enterprise for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/robert-f-kennedy-jr"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr}}}\uc2 , leading up to his nomination to be secretary of health \u8211\'20\'13 one he is seeking to distance himself from as he enters confirmation hearings this week.\par \par \uc2 Last week, he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://extapps2.oge.gov/201/Presiden.nsf/PAS+Index/F3C8425ED335BB5685258C1A00565D57/$FILE/Kennedy%2C%20Jr.%2C%20Robert%20F.%20%20finalEA.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 promised to resign}}}\uc2  from his consultancies and chairmanship of Children\u8217\'20\'19s Health Defense, a leading anti-vaccine nonprofit, if he is confirmed. That is cold comfort to public health experts anxiously eyeing his confirmation.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe plain truth is that vaccines have saved hundreds of millions of lives,\u8221\'20\'1D said Dr \uc2 Tom Frieden\uc2 , former director of the \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2  (CDC) under \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 , and now CEO of Resolve to Save Lives, a public health-focused non-profit.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen Mr Kennedy says things like autism does come from vaccines\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 a false claim \u8211\'20\'13 \u8220\'20\'1Cthat\u8217\'20\'19s very problematic\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Frieden continued: \u8220\'20\'1CThat was a fraudulent claim from someone who was aiming to profit from it, and false claims like that not only undermine our confidence in safe and effective vaccines they also divert attention from finding the real cause of things like autism that affect so many people.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Read Jessica\u8217\'20\'19s full report:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/29/rfk-jr-confirmation-hearing"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 RFK Jr\u8217\'20\'19s shifting vaccines stance worries experts ahead of confirmation hearing}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.41pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Robert F Kennedy \u8217\'20\'19s confirmation hearing comes one day after his cousin, Caroline Kennedy, shared {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/JBKSchlossberg/status/1884294384474046900"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a video}}}\uc2  on social media describing him as a \u8220\'20\'1Cpredator\u8221\'20\'1D who \u8220\'20\'1Cpreys on the desperation of parents of sick children\u8221\'20\'1D by peddling misinformation on vaccines.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI have known Bobby my whole life; we grew up together. It\u8217\'20\'19s no surprise that he keeps birds of prey as pets because he himself is a predator,\u8221\'20\'1D Caroline Kennedy said in the video.\par \par \uc2 Her remarks were also shared in a letter to senators, as she implored them not to confirm RFK Jr as the next secretary of health and human services.\par \par \uc2 She went on to say that her father, President \uc2 John F Kennedy\uc2 , and her uncle, former US attorney general Robert F Kennedy, would be \u8220\'20\'1Cdisgusted\u8221\'20\'1D by the actions of her cousin.\par \par \uc2 More on Caroline Kennedy\u8217\'20\'19s comments here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/28/caroline-kennedy-rfk-letter"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Caroline Kennedy calls cousin RFK Jr a predator ahead of confirmation hearing}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.28pm GMT\par \par \uc2 RFK Jr confirmation hearing getting under way soon\par \par \uc2 The Senate confirmation hearing for Robert F Kennedy, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s nominee for secretary of health and human services, will get underway in about 30 minutes, and Democrats are expected to grill Kennedy on allegations of sexual harassment and his shifting stance on vaccines.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Joseph Gedeon reports: \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2 , the environmental lawyer turned anti-vaccine activist, faces a watershed moment this week as the Senate confirmation hearings begin on his nomination as the US\u8217\'20\'19s top health official, setting up what could be the most contentious cabinet battle of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s second administration.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe 71-year-old Kennedy, whose nomination has sparked fierce resistance from the scientific establishment, would take control of a sprawling $1.8tn healthcare apparatus at a time when public trust in medical institutions remains deeply fractured along partisan lines.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs health and human services secretary, Kennedy would oversee everything from vaccine policy to food safety, wielding enormous influence over public health decisions affecting millions of Americans. His controversial views \u8211\'20\'13 including debunked claims about vaccines and autism, fluoride safety and raw milk regulations \u8211\'20\'13 have put him at odds with mainstream medical consensus.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CKennedy told NPR in December that as a member of the administration, he is \u8216\'20\'18not going to take vaccines away from anybody\u8217\'20\'19, but he also added he wanted people to make \u8216\'20\'18informed choices\u8217\'20\'19.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Read Joseph\u8217\'20\'19s full report:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/29/rfk-jr-senate-confirmation-hearing"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Confirmation hearings begin for RFK Jr\u8217\'20\'19s nomination to be US health secretary}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.25am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.07pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , the Minnesota governor and former Democratic vice-presidential nominee, argued that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s federal funding freeze closely mirrors many of the proposals included in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/28/federal-grants-paused-project-2025"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Project 2025}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe were preparing for it. They wrote it out. If you go back and look at that now, you\u8217\'20\'19ll see this go step by step,\u8221\'20\'1D Walz told MSNBC on Tuesday night.\par \par \uc2 Walz described the funding freeze, which was paused by a federal judge on Tuesday, as \u8220\'20\'1Ccruel\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Csomewhat buffoonish,\u8221\'20\'1D but he expressed concern that Trump may be using it as a trial balloon to see how far he can go with his agenda.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s like you caught someone and they stole everything out of your house. You caught them and you told them to put it back,\u8221\'20\'1D Walz said. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd when you start looking, some of it\u8217\'20\'19s still gone. What they\u8217\'20\'19re going to see is, oh, they didn\u8217\'20\'19t raise a stink about meteorologists or our folks who are monitoring PFAS [per- and polyfluoroalkyl substances] in our water, so let\u8217\'20\'19s just go on with that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Walz acknowledged that many Americans are fatigued after a grueling presidential election, but he implored them to not give up the fight in the face of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s return to the White House.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI would tell people, stay focused. Don\u8217\'20\'19t take the bait on the distractions,\u8221\'20\'1D Walz said. \u8220\'20\'1CSurround yourself with people who understand this and recognize the things they went after today are basically a big chunk of what society does. People like to have clean water and hospitals and safety and roads and airports, all the things they\u8217\'20\'19re going after.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He concluded: \u8220\'20\'1CI think we have to find that voice. We have to push back.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.27am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.47pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Ramon Antonio Vargas reports:\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/film/selena-gomez"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Selena Gomez}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 the Texas-born pop star and actor whose paternal grandparents are from Mexico \u8211\'20\'13 has laughed off a failed Republican US Senate hopeful\u8217\'20\'19s call for her to be deported from the country after she recorded a video of herself expressing sympathy for people affected by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s immigration crackdown.\par \par \uc2 Responding to a comment from the former candidate that she should be \u8220\'20\'1Cdeported\u8221\'20\'1D over her video, Gomez took to social media and wrote in part: \u8220\'20\'1CThanks for the laugh.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Gomez nonetheless deleted the video amid a social media pile-on primarily driven by conservatives in favor of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/27/trump-immigration-dr-phil-chicago-raids"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 deportation raids}}}\uc2  that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s administration has been carrying out early in his second presidency, which began on 20 January.\par \par \uc2 The clip in question showed the 32-year-old Gomez wiping away tears as she remarked: \u8220\'20\'1CI just wanted to say that I\u8217\'20\'19m so sorry. All my people are getting attacked, the children. I don\u8217\'20\'19t understand.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI wish I could do something, but I can\u8217\'20\'19t. I\u8217\'20\'19ll try everything. I promise.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Read the full report:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/29/selena-gomez-ice-raids-response"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Selena Gomez laughs off Republican calling to \u8216\'20\'18deport\u8217\'20\'19 her over Ice raid video}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.26am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.32pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Democrats have expressed outrage over reports that Pete Hegseth, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s new secretary of defense, has removed the security detail and clearance of \uc2 Mark Milley\uc2 , the former chair of the joint chiefs of staff who has fiercely criticized Trump in the past.\par \par \uc2 According to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.foxnews.com/politics/white-house-pulling-gen-milleys-security-detail-clearance-panel-may-face-demotion-retirement"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fox News}}}\uc2 , Hegseth has also instructed the acting inspector general to investigate whether Milley should be stripped of one of his stars for allegedly undermining the chain of command during Trump\u8217\'20\'19s first term.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPete Hegseth pledged to the Senate that he\u8217\'20\'19d protect the independence of the \uc2 Department of Defense\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s watchdog for waste, fraud, and abuse,\u8221\'20\'1D Senator Elizabeth Warren, a Democrat of Massachusetts, said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBut after President Trump illegally fired the Pentagon\u8217\'20\'19s Inspector General, the Defense Secretary is going back on his word and weaponizing government investigations to go after Trump\u8217\'20\'19s perceived political enemies. It\u8217\'20\'19s a clear warning sign that Secretary Hegseth is focused more on political retribution than national security.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.18pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Over on Capitol Hill, Republicans are struggling to cobble together a plan to pass a major bill that is expected to include provisions on taxes, immigration and spending cuts.\par \par \uc2 Congressional Republicans have debated for weeks about whether the legislation \u8211\'20\'13 which they plan to pass using a process called reconciliation to avoid the Senate filibuster \u8211\'20\'13 should be split into one bill or two bills. After a two-day House Republican retreat, lawmakers are no closer to finding a path forward, one member reported.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have only been presented with the same policy and budget cut proposals that we have been presented with for a month now at all our meetings and at a full Saturday conference meeting earlier this month,\u8221\'20\'1D representative \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2 , a Republican of Georgia, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/repmtg/status/1884579123470757912?s=46"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote}}}\uc2  on social media.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNext time we meet, I hope to know a framework of our plan and I hope this doesn\u8217\'20\'19t turn into another bill with thousands of pages dumped on us with less than 72 hours to read it all before we have to vote on the eve of another government shutdown. But why would I expect different?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 House Republicans are working with a razor-thin majority, so they have no room for error as they work to get their bill across the finish line.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.54pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Executive order restricts gender transition for under-19s\par \par \uc2 President Trump has issued an executive order restricting gender transition treatment for people under 19.\par \par \uc2 The order said medical professionals across the country were \u8220\'20\'1Cmaiming and sterilizing a growing number of impressionable children under the radical and false claim that adults can change a child\u8217\'20\'19s sex through a series of irreversible medical interventions\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CCountless children soon regret that they have been mutilated and begin to grasp the horrifying tragedy that they will never be able to conceive children of their own or nurture their children through breastfeeding,\u8221\'20\'1D it said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMoreover, these vulnerable youths\u8217\'20\'19 medical bills may rise throughout their lifetimes, as they are often trapped with lifelong medical complications, a losing war with their own bodies, and, tragically, sterilization.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAccordingly, it is the policy of the United States that it will not fund, sponsor, promote, assist, or support the so-called \u8216\'20\'18transition\u8217\'20\'19 of a child from one sex to another, and it will rigorously enforce all laws that prohibit or limit these destructive and life-altering procedures.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The order also directed the US health secretary to \u8220\'20\'1Ctake all appropriate actions to end the chemical and surgical mutilation of children, including regulatory and sub-regulatory actions\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.54pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.26pm GMT\par \par \uc2 An overwhelming majority of people in Greenland do not want the island to become part of the US, according to a poll.\par \par \uc2 President Trump has repeatedly said he wants the US to control Greenland, which is strategically located and believed to have significant untapped resources. Trump has refused to rule out using tariffs or force to acquire the territory from Denmark.\par \par \uc2 In a poll published by Denmark\u8217\'20\'19s Berlingske and Greenland\u8217\'20\'19s Sermitsiaq newspapers, 85% of residents of the island said they would not back the move, while 6% were in favour and 9% were undecided.\par \par \uc2 Some 45% saw Trump\u8217\'20\'19s interest as a \u8220\'20\'1Cthreat\u8221\'20\'1D, 43% saw it as an \u8220\'20\'1Copportunity\u8221\'20\'1D, and 13% were undecided.\par \par \uc2 A day after Trump\u8217\'20\'19s inauguration this month, Greenland\u8217\'20\'19s Prime Minister Mute Egede insisted that Greenlanders \u8220\'20\'1Cdon\u8217\'20\'19t want to be American\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.34pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.59am GMT\par \par \uc2 UN\uc2  agencies have begun cutting their global aid operations following the 90-day suspension of all foreign assistance ordered by President Trump.\par \par \uc2 Filippo Grandi, the head of the organisation\u8217\'20\'19s refugee agency, \uc2 UNHCR\uc2 , sent out an overnight email to employees ordering an immediate clampdown on expenditure, including a 90-day delay in ordering new supplies except for emergencies, a hiring and contract freeze, and a halt to all international air travel.\par \par \uc2 UNHCR\uc2  is responsible for providing life-saving assistance to the 122 million people currently displaced from their homes across 136 countries.\par \par \uc2 The new US secretary of state, \uc2 Marco Rubio\uc2 , previously claimed the freeze would not affect life-saving aid, which he defined as \u8220\'20\'1Ccore lifesaving medicine, medical services, food, shelter, and subsistence assistance, as well as supplies and reasonable administrative costs as necessary to deliver such assistance\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He said its targets were aid programmes involving \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , family planning, and \u8220\'20\'1Cgender ideology\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The US provided \u163\'00\'A32bn ($2.49bn) in funding to the \uc2 UNHCR\uc2 , according to the latest figures for 2024 \u8211\'20\'13 a fifth of the agency\u8217\'20\'19s total budget.\par \par \uc2 Read the full story here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/jan/28/un-aid-cuts-trump-funding"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 UN aid agencies cut back operations after Trump\u8217\'20\'19s 90-day funding suspension}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.33pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.46am GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump offers US federal workers buyouts to resign\par \par \uc2 In another part of its efforts to reshape the \uc2 US government\uc2 , the Trump administration has offered federal workers buyouts worth more than seven months\u8217\'20\'19 salary to leave their jobs.\par \par \uc2 A memo circulated on Tuesday evening set out four mandatory directives, including a full-time return to the office for most employees. It also said that the federal workforce would be subjected to \u8220\'20\'1Cenhanced standards of suitability and conduct\u8221\'20\'1D and warned that most agencies would be downsized.\par \par \uc2 It said the offer to leave would remain open until 6 February.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US government\uc2  is roughly the nation\u8217\'20\'19s 15th-largest workforce, with more than 3 million employees. Project 2025, the conservative manifesto that has guided much of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s policy goals, calls for mass firings of federal workers and suggests replacing many with political appointees.\par \par \uc2 Denouncing the offer, the president of the \uc2 American Federation of Government Employees\uc2  union, \uc2 Everett Kelley\uc2 , said it was part of an attempt to pressure workers not considered loyal to the new administration to leave their jobs.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPurging the federal government of dedicated career federal employees will have vast, unintended consequences that will cause chaos for the Americans who depend on a functioning federal government,\u8221\'20\'1D a statement read.\par \par \uc2 Read the full story here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/28/trump-federal-workers-buyouts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump offers US federal workers buyouts to resign}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.33pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.28am GMT\par \par \uc2 What we know about the block on Trump's funding freeze\par \par \uc2 More now on the news that a federal judge has blocked a move by President Trump to pause trillions of dollars in federal loans, grants, and other financial assistance.\par \par \uc2 Federal grants and loans reach into virtually every corner of Americans\u8217\'20\'19 lives, with hundreds of billions of dollars flowing into education, healthcare and anti-poverty programmes, housing assistance, disaster relief, infrastructure, and a host of other initiatives.\par \par \uc2 A two-page internal memo which had been due to take effect at 5pm eastern time on Tuesday told all federal agencies to \u8220\'20\'1Ctemporarily pause all activities related to obligations or disbursement of all federal financial assistance\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The memo was met with widespread confusion in Washington, where civil servants struggled to understand its full extent scope and application.\par \par \uc2 The US constitution gives Congress control over spending matters, but Trump has said he believes the president has the power to withhold money for programmes he dislikes.\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://democrats-appropriations.house.gov/sites/evo-subsites/democrats-appropriations.house.gov/files/evo-media-document/1.27.25%20DeLauro%20Murray%20to%20Vaeth.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 letter from senior Democrats}}}\uc2  on the \uc2 House Committee on Appropriations\uc2  expressed \u8220\'20\'1Cextreme alarm about the Administration\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to undermine Congress\u8217\'20\'19s power of the purse\u8221\'20\'1D, adding that this and other directives had \u8220\'20\'1Csown immense confusion across the country, with some reports indicating that they could immediately halt all federal funding for any grant or loan\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 US district judge Loren AliKhan granted the temporary halt after several advocacy groups argued the freeze would devastate programmes ranging from healthcare to road construction. The court will revisit the issue on Monday.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/29/donald-trump-federal-aid-freeze-blocked-medicaid-fafsa"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s funding freeze temporarily blocked by court \u8211\'20\'13 what we know so far }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.34am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.05am GMT\par \par \uc2 Opening summary\par \par \uc2 Good morning and welcome to our live coverage of all the latest developments from US politics.\par \par \uc2 We start with the news that a federal judge has temporarily blocked a move by President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/28/trump-pauses-grants-loans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pause trillions of dollars in federal loans, grants, and other financial assistance}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A two-page internal memo had told all federal agencies to \u8220\'20\'1Ctemporarily pause all activities related to obligations or disbursement of all federal financial assistance\u8221\'20\'1D and that \u8220\'20\'1Cthe use of Federal resources to advance Marxist equity, transgenderism, and green new deal social engineering policies is a waste of taxpayer dollars\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The directive was seen as part of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s desire to end programs related to diversity, equity, and inclusion ( DEI ). The court order came moments before it was due to take effect and will prevent it from being implemented until at least next Monday, 3 February.\par \par \uc2 The administrative stay came in response to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://storage.courtlistener.com/recap/gov.uscourts.dcd.276842/gov.uscourts.dcd.276842.1.0.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lawsuit}}}\uc2  filed by four groups representing non-profits, public health professionals and small businesses in which they said the directive was illegal and would have a \u8220\'20\'1Cdevastating impact on hundreds of thousands of grant recipients who depend on the inflow of grant money\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Stay with us for more on that and all the latest updates throughout the day.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.32pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250129el1t001p6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
