\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 RFK Jr faces questions about U-turn on  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  in \uc2 US Senate\uc2  hearing\b0\par\par\uc2 Anna Betts \par \uc2 687 \uc2 words\par \uc2 29 January 2025\par 22:23 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Health secretary nominee once identified as \u8216\'20\'18pro-choice\u8217\'20\'19 but said he agrees with Trump \u8216\'20\'18every \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a tragedy\u8217\'20\'19RFK Jr and Democrats clash over his vaccine history in confirmation hearing\par \par \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2 , \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s nominee for health secretary, faced questions about his flip-flopping on \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a \uc2 US Senate\uc2  confirmation hearing on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Kennedy identified as \u8220\'20\'1Cpro-choice\u8221\'20\'1D during his presidential campaign as a Democrat, but said repeatedly in Wednesday\u8217\'20\'19s hearing for secretary of health and human services (\uc2 HHS\uc2 ) that he agreed with Trump that \u8220\'20\'1Cevery \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a tragedy\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI agree with him that we cannot be a moral nation if we have 1.2 million abortions a year. I agree with him that the states should control \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D Kennedy said in response to questions from Senator \uc2 James Lankford\uc2 , a Republican from Oklahoma, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/jul/29/abortion-laws-bans-by-state"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 where \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  is banned}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI serve at the pleasure of the president. I\u8217\'20\'19m going to implement his policies,\u8221\'20\'1D he continued.\par \par \uc2 Kennedy also reassured Republicans in private conversations that he had changed his position on the issue. In December, \uc2 Josh Hawley\uc2 , a Republican senator of Missouri, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/HawleyMO/status/1869135780607869235"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said that Kennedy had told him}}}\uc2  he would \u8220\'20\'1Creinstate President Trump\u8217\'20\'19s pro-life policies at \uc2 HHS\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Key to Kennedy\u8217\'20\'19s testimony was the pledge to investigate the safety of mifepristone, one drug in a so-called medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The drug has been the focus of attacks by anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  campaigners since the fall of Roe v Wade, and is now the most common way to end a pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 The drug has been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2023/04/01/health/abortion-pill-safety.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 extensively investigated}}}\uc2  for safety, and it is found to have fewer adverse outcomes {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.aafp.org/pubs/afp/issues/2022/0100/p5.html#:~:text=These%20rates%20of%20complications%20are,year%20in%20the%20United%20States."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 than acetaminophen}}}\uc2  (paracetamol), a common over-the-counter pain reliever. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/apr/28/junk-science-papers-abortion-cases"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Key studies}}}\uc2  that supported a recent supreme court case over mifepristone\u8217\'20\'19s approval in the early 2000s have been retracted.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe need to understand the safety of every drug \u8211\'20\'13 mifepristone and every other drug,\u8221\'20\'1D Kennedy said, adding that Trump had not yet taken a position on the medication, but that he had made it clear to Kennedy that he \u8220\'20\'1Cwants me to look at the safety issues\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Democrats produced placards of Kennedy\u8217\'20\'19s past pro-choice statements, including one campaign statement reported by the Hill that read: \u8220\'20\'1CMr Kennedy\u8217\'20\'19s position on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is that it is always a woman\u8217\'20\'19s right to choose. He does not support legislation banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI have never seen any major politician flip on that issue quite as quickly as you did when Trump asked you to become \uc2 HHS\uc2  secretary,\u8221\'20\'1D Bernie Sanders, an independent senator from Vermont who caucuses with Democrats, told Kennedy.\par \par \uc2 Sanders asked, rhetorically: \u8220\'20\'1CTell me why you think people should have confidence in your consistency and in your work when you really made a major U-turn on an issue of that importance?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Maggie Hassan\uc2 , a Democratic senator of New Hampshire, suggested she and Kennedy actually agreed on the issue of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, citing and referencing his many past comments in support of \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2 . As she questioned Kennedy, Hassan\u8217\'20\'19s staff displayed posters that highlighted his previous remarks in support of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access.\par \par \uc2 One poster quoted Kennedy saying: \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m pro-choice \u8230\'20\'26 I don\u8217\'20\'19t think the government has any business telling people what they can or cannot do with their body.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou said that, right?\u8221\'20\'1D Hassan asked Kennedy, to which he replied: \u8220\'20\'1CYes.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is remarkable that you have such a long record of fighting for women\u8217\'20\'19s reproductive freedom and really great that my Republican colleagues are so open to voting for a pro-choice \uc2 HHS\uc2  secretary,\u8221\'20\'1D Hassan said.\par \par \uc2 She then asked Kennedy: \u8220\'20\'1CYou have clearly stated in the past that bodily autonomy is one of your core values. The question is: do you stand for that value or not? When was it that you decided to sell out the values you\u8217\'20\'19ve had your whole life in order to be given power by President Trump?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Kennedy reiterated: \u8220\'20\'1CSenator, I agree with President Trump that every \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a tragedy.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Jessica Glenza and Joanie Greve contributed reporting\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250129el1t0038v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
