\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 The anti- \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  movement weighs its next move: \u8216\'20\'18We haven\u8217\'20\'19t gone away\u8217\'20\'19\b0\par\par\uc2 Carter Sherman \par \uc2 1,050 \uc2 words\par \uc2 27 January 2025\par 17:22 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The movement is on the upswing thanks to Trump but a question lingers: what is their role in his administration?\par \par \uc2 Minutes into the National Pro-Life Summit, \uc2 Kristan Hawkins\uc2 , president of Students for Life of America, had convinced its more than 1,000 attendees to leap to their feet. She was recording a video, and she had a message she wanted them to send to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTHANK YOU MISTER PRESIDENT!\u8221\'20\'1D the crowd in the ballroom thundered, before bursting into raucous applause \u8211\'20\'13 complete with wolf whistles.\par \par \uc2 Every January, anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists from across the country gather in Washington for the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/24/trump-vance-march-for-life"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March for Life}}}\uc2 , the largest anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  gathering in the US. In recent years, the march has been followed by the National Pro-Life Summit, which seeks to take the raw energy of the march and channel it towards specific organizations and policy aims. The summit, which is organized by the powerful Students for Life of America, held seminars on efforts to halt access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills, protect campus free speech and defend marriage as the union between one man and one woman. There was a pro-life job fair, where young people could learn about working for \uc2 the Heritage Foundation\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 the architects of the famous Project 2025 policy playbook \u8211\'20\'13 as well as a huge room where they could pick up T-shirts with slogans such as \u8220\'20\'1CDEFUND PLANNED PARENTHOOD\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 There was one overarching theme that knit the summit together: thanks to Trump, the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement is on the upswing.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFor those of you that were advocating for an America that isn\u8217\'20\'19t weak and pathetic, but instead one that has borders, one that defends the unborn, one that believes in liberty and freedom \u8211\'20\'13 it is amazing to see how quick America can get back on pace,\u8221\'20\'1D the Turning Point USA founder Charlie Kirk told the cheering crowd assembled in the ballroom. He continued: \u8220\'20\'1CYou guys have an amazing ally in the White House in the fight for life. Both President Trump and JD Vance.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In his first few days in office, Trump has already notched a few victories for the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement, as he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/24/trump-order-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reinstated the Mexico City policy}}}\uc2  limiting funding for overseas groups that perform or advocate for abortions, issued an executive order that declared that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/23/trump-executive-order-fetal-personhood"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 gender begins \u8220\'20\'1Cat conception\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  and pardoned several anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists who had been convicted of illegally blocking an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic. His Department of Justice also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/justice-department-reproductive-care-clinics-prosecutions-5f693b186d0dd62fc693474aab7b5f3f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 promised to significantly curtail prosecutions}}}\uc2  against people accused of violating the Freedom of Access to Clinic Entrances Act, or Face, which has been used to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics from violence.\par \par \uc2 But he has not implemented more sweeping anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  measures, such as using the 19th-century anti-vice law the Comstock Act to in effect ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide. As thrilled as anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists may now be, there\u8217\'20\'19s still work to be done \u8211\'20\'13 and a question lingering over the movement: what exactly is their role in his administration?\par \par \uc2 When he ran for president in 2016, Trump was powered by a coalition of anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists who agreed to throw their weight behind him if he appointed \u8220\'20\'1Cpro-life\u8221\'20\'1D justices to the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 . He kept that promise and, thanks in large part to his nominees, the supreme court overturned Roe v Wade in 2022. But by 2024, after \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights supporters won multiple red-state ballot measures, Trump was a far less reliable ally to the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement. He repeatedly flip-flopped on the issue, prompting criticism from prominent anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists, including Hawkins.\par \par \uc2 Trump won the presidential election anyway. Not necessarily because people oppose \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 several states that Trump won also voted in favor of measures preserving access to the procedure \u8211\'20\'13 but because Trump\u8217\'20\'19s popularity may exceed that of the movement that once propelled him to the White House.\par \par \uc2 In an interview, Hawkins rejected the idea that Trump is more popular than the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  cause. (Fifty-four per cent of Americans identify as \u8220\'20\'1Cpro-choice\u8221\'20\'1D, while 41% say they are \u8220\'20\'1Cpro-life\u8221\'20\'1D, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.gallup.com/poll/1576/abortion.aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to recent Gallup polling}}}\uc2 .) While Trump has objected to signing a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, Hawkins wants him to commit to defunding \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2 . She also hopes that \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2 , who has been tapped to head the \uc2 Department of Health and Human Services\uc2 , will be open to rolling back the FDA\u8217\'20\'19s approval of the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill mifepristone, given Kennedy\u8217\'20\'19s skepticism toward pharmaceutical companies.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI have a whole lot of damn bodies,\u8221\'20\'1D Hawkins said. \u8220\'20\'1CYou can think we\u8217\'20\'19re annoying all you want, but we have a lot of people and we haven\u8217\'20\'19t gone away.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In making a deal with Trump, Hawkins suggested that her group\u8217\'20\'19s strongest asset was their organizing. She pointed to the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement\u8217\'20\'19s recent electoral successes at the state level, such as the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/01/south-carolina-female-senators"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 defeat of multiple South Carolina Republicans}}}\uc2  who blocked a total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve been around for 52 years,\u8221\'20\'1D Hawkins said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re not novices at this.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Even if Trump isn\u8217\'20\'19t the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement\u8217\'20\'19s most devoted champion, much of the movement appears ready to embrace Trumpism anyway. Some of the biggest speakers at the summit \u8211\'20\'13 such as Kirk, the former housing and urban development secretary Ben Carson and Fox News host \uc2 Kayleigh McEnany\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 are less known for their involvement in the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement than for their proximity to Maga. Several attenders donned Maga hats; one couple wore a pair in his-and-hers blue and pink. Tributes to Trump and Vance regularly punctuated speakers\u8217\'20\'19 talks.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI have never in my life seen a more important message \u8211\'20\'13 not just for the March for Life but for the future of our movement \u8211\'20\'13 than the one that Vice-President \uc2 JD Vance\uc2  gave,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 the Heritage Foundation\uc2  president, Kevin Roberts, told the summit attendees. \u8220\'20\'1CIn particular, the vice-president put his finger on something that is necessary \u8211\'20\'13 just definitionally \u8211\'20\'13 for the survival of the American republic: we need more babies!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The crowd burst into applause. \u8220\'20\'1CWoo!\u8221\'20\'1D someone cheered.\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 This article was amended on 27 January 2025 to correct an editing error omitting the number of Students for Life of America attenders at the National Pro-Life Summit.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250126el1q001e1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
