\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Trump signs executive orders targeting  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  rights \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Aben\u233\'00\'E9 Clayton, L\u233\'00\'E9onie Chao-Fong,Chris Stein and Daniel Lavelle \par \uc2 12,001 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 January 2025\par 02:47 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This blog has now closed. Read our latest story here\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.29am GMT\par \par \uc2 Thank you for following the Guardian US live blog. Here are some of the top moments of the day:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has arrived in Los Angeles and was greeted by Governor \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2 . Trump was accompanied by the first lady and held an impromptu press conference as soon as he stepped off the plane.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump said that he would waive federal permits so people who lost their homes in the Los Angeles wildfires could begin to rebuild as soon as possible. Trump said this on Friday after a tour of the fire-ravaged Palisades community.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Mexico denied a military plane carrying people who were deported from the US access to land in the country on Thursday, NBC News has reported.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 While aboard Air Force One en route to tour the devastation from the wildfires in Los Angeles, Trump signed two executive orders targeting abortions. The first would reinstate the Mexico City policy, which prevents international non-governmental organizations that perform or promote abortions from receiving federal funding. The second was an order affirming a longstanding federal policy that the US does not use federal funds to pay for abortions.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The justice department chief of staff, Chad Mizelle, has issued an order to curtail prosecutions against people accused of blocking \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  facilities. In a memo on Friday, Mizelle wrote that prosecutions and civil actions under the Freedom of Access to Clinic Entrances (Face) Act will now be permitted only in \u8220\'20\'1Cextraordinary circumstances\u8221\'20\'1D or in cases presenting \u8221\'20\'1Dsignificant aggravating factors\u8221\'20\'1D, AP reports.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has suggested paring back or even dismantling the federal response to major disasters, a move that would cut off aid that has largely helped support {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republican}}}\uc2  -leaning states that voted for him in last year\u8217\'20\'19s US presidential election.\par \par \uc2 Thanks for reading. Have a good weekend.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/24/trump-order-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump signs order to reinstate \u8216\'20\'18global gag rule\u8217\'20\'19 on \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  aid}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.30am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.31am GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  said that he would waive federal permits so people who lost their homes in the Los Angeles wildfires could begin to rebuild as soon as possible. Trump said this on Friday after a tour of the fire-ravaged Palisades community.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19d ask that the local permitting process be the same. Some of the people were saying they\u8217\'20\'19ll be forced to wait 18 months for their permits \u8230\'20\'26I\u8217\'20\'19m sure you can get it down to not even 18 days,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said as he sat at a table with LA mayor Karen Bass during a roundtable briefing.\par \par \uc2 This announcement followed the announcement of a $2.5bn aid package signed by \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  on Thursday that is meant to expedite the cleanup, inspection and permitting processes so that residents affected by the Eaton and Palisades fires.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.49am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.01am GMT\par \par \uc2 Mexico denied a military plane carrying people who were deported from the US access to land in the country on Thursday, NBC News reported on Friday. According to the outlet:\par \par \uc2 It was not immediately clear why Mexico blocked the flight, but tensions between the US and Mexico, neighbors and longtime allies, have risen since \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  won the November election. Trump has threatened to slap 25% across-the-board tariffs on Mexico in retaliation for migrants crossing the border the countries share. But he has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/white-house/trump-tariffs-day-1-rcna188640"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 not yet put them in effect}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Issues between the Trump administration and Mexico have been high since the president\u8217\'20\'19s first administration and these {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/21/trump-remain-in-mexico-program"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tensions have only grown}}}\uc2 , with Trump and his allies blaming Mexican and Central American migrants for crime in the US and have vowed to ramp up deportations.\par \par \uc2 Read the entirety of the NBC News report on the rejected flights {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/immigration/mexico-refuses-accept-us-deportation-flight-rcna189182"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.07am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.49am GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump signs executive orders targeting abortions\par \par \uc2 While aboard Air Force One en route to tour the devastation from the wildfires in Los Angeles, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  signed two executive orders targeting abortions.\par \par \uc2 The first would reinstate the Mexico City policy, which prevents international non-governmental organizations that perform or promote abortions from receiving federal funding. This policy, which \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights supporters call the \u8220\'20\'1Cglobal gag rule\u8221\'20\'1D, dates back to the 1980s and is typically implemented whenever Republicans take control of the White House.\par \par \uc2 The second was an order affirming a longstanding federal policy that the US does not use federal funds to pay for abortions.\par \par \uc2 The actions come just after he addressed a crowd of thousands of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents in Washington on Friday to mark the 52nd anniversary of the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s 1973 decision in Roe v Wade. The decision created a national right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  but was overturned by the court in 2022.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.15am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.48am GMT\par \par \uc2 Officials identify 18 of 28 people killed in LA wildfires\par \par \uc2 The Los Angeles county medical examiner has identified 18 of the 28 people who died in the still-burning Eaton and Palisades fire, the medical examiner\u8217\'20\'19s office announced on Friday.\par \par \uc2 The deceased people whose names have been released range in age from their late 50s to early 90s. Most died in their homes from smoke inhalation and \u8220\'20\'1Cthermal injuries\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 These names were released as \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  visited the area to tour the fire-ravaged neighborhoods where the deaths occurred.\par \par \uc2 The names of those who died can be {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://me.lacounty.gov/2025/press-releases/wildfire-update-18-victims-identified-by-medical-examiner/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 found here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.59am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.50pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump is taking an aerial tour of the Pacific Palisades area of Los Angeles to see the devastation from the Palisades fire.\par \par \uc2 The Palisades fire, which began on 7 January and has killed at least 11 people, has burned more than 23,000 acres and destroyed nearly 7,000 structures so far. That blaze is still not completely contained.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.41pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump lands at Los Angeles airport\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has arrived in Los Angeles and was greeted by Governor \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2 . Trump was accompanied by the first lady and held an impromptu press conference as soon as he stepped off the plane.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re going to do a lot of work and I think you\u8217\'20\'19re going to see a lot of progress,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said, referring to the damage from the wildfires.\par \par \uc2 Newsom asked for Trump\u8217\'20\'19s support in the recovery effort and emphasized, \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s not just the folks in Palisades but the folks in Altadena that were devastated.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.47pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.01pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Summary of the day so far\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a recap of the latest developments:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  said he would consider signing an executive order to \u8220\'20\'1Cfundamentally reform\u8221\'20\'1D or potentially eliminate the \uc2 Federal Emergency Management Agency\uc2  (Fema). Trump, during a visit to Asheville, criticized the agency\u8217\'20\'19s disaster response during a tour of hurricane-damaged areas in western North Carolina. He proposed giving governors more direct responsibility for disaster response, indicating he wants to redirect federal funding straight to states rather than through the federal agency.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Senate will vote tonight on the nomination of Pete Hegseth, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s controversial pick for US secretary of defense. Hegseth, a former Fox News host and army veteran, cleared a key procedural hurdle on Thursday but two Senate Republicans, Susan Collins of Maine and \uc2 Lisa Murkowski\uc2  of Alaska, voted against his nomination amid mounting concerns over his personal history and inexperience.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The state department ordered a sweeping freeze on almost all US foreign aid programs, making exceptions for only aid to Israel and humanitarian food crises. The exceptions did not include life-saving health programs, such as clinics and immunization programs. Suspending funding \u8220\'20\'1Ccould have life or death consequences\u8221\'20\'1D for children and families around the world, \uc2 Oxfam\uc2  warned.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The interior department said it has officially changed the change of the Gulf of Mexico to the Gulf of America. Alaska\u8217\'20\'19s mountain Denali, the highest peak in North America, has officially been renamed Mount McKinley \u8211\'20\'13 the name it was called before \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  changed it in 2015, the department said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Trump administration issued a new round of heavy-handed measures that could rapidly deport immigrants who entered the US through recently established legal pathways, according to an internal \uc2 Department of Homeland Security\uc2  memo obtained the \uc2 New York Times\uc2 . In no waste of time, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s press secretary, Karoline Leavitt, posted on X on Friday that \u8220\'20\'1CDeportation flights have begun\u8221\'20\'1D with official pictures of people boarding a military-style aircraft.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A federal judge banned Stewart Rhodes, the former leader of the far-right Oath Keepers group, and some other January 6 defendants from entering Washington DC, as well as the US Capitol, as a condition of their release from prison. The acting US attorney for the District of Columbia, Ed Martin, intervened on behalf of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/24/trump-pardon-proud-boys-enrique-tarrio"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Rhodes }}}\uc2  and other members of the militia group, asking US district court judge \uc2 Amit Mehta\uc2  to reverse the ban. Rhodes was among 1,500 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/20/trump-executive-orders-jan-6-pardons"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 controversially given}}}\uc2  blanket pardons or commutations by Trump soon after he was sworn in on Monday.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump and his vice-president, JD Vance, indicated that the justice department would no longer prosecute anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists in separate addresses to the March for Life rally. \u8220\'20\'1CNo longer will our government throw pro-life protesters and activists \u8211\'20\'13 elderly, grandparents, or anybody else \u8211\'20\'13 in prison,\u8221\'20\'1D Vance told the thousands-strong crowd that gathered on the National Mall, which included members of the white nationalist group Patriot Front. Meanwhile, the justice department\u8217\'20\'19s chief of staff issued an order to curtail prosecutions against people accused of blocking \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  facilities.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The supreme court has agreed to consider whether the country\u8217\'20\'19s first publicly funded religious charter school should be allowed to open in Oklahoma. The case, led by two Catholic dioceses, could open the door to allowing public funds to directly flow to religious schools and transform the line between church and state in education.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump held a call with the Danish prime minister, \uc2 Mette Frederiksen\uc2 , last week in which he insisted he was serious in his determination to take over Greenland, according to a \uc2 Financial Times\uc2  report. The call was described by senior European officials as \u8220\'20\'1Cfiery\u8221\'20\'1D with Trump being aggressive and confrontational. Denmark\u8217\'20\'19s foreign minister, \uc2 Lars L\u248\'00\'F8kke Rasmussen\uc2 , said his country had agreed to discuss the question of Greenland after his first call with the US secretary of state , \uc2 Marco Rubio\uc2 , on Friday.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Marco Rubio\uc2  also spoke with China\u8217\'20\'19s foreign minister, Wang Yi, on Friday in the first publicly disclosed contact between an official in the second Trump administration and a Chinese counterpart. A US readout of the call said Rubio \u8220\'20\'1Cemphasized that the Trump Administration will pursue a US-PRC relationship that advances US interests and puts the American people first.\u8221\'20\'1D A Chinese readout said the two also discussed Taiwan, with Wang reportedly telling Rubio that Beijing will never allow Taiwan to be separated from mainland China.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Trump administration withdrew a Biden administration proposal to ban menthol cigarettes in the US, according to a filing by the office of information and regulatory affairs. Menthol cigarettes have also faced scrutiny for their disproportionate impact on the health of Black communities, and for their role in luring young people to smoking.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump said he had pulled federal security protection for the former top US health official \uc2 Anthony Fauci\uc2 , who served as the nation\u8217\'20\'19s top infectious disease official during the Covid-19 pandemic and had served seven US presidents. Trump said he would \u8220\'20\'1Ccertainly not take responsibility\u8221\'20\'1D if something was to happen to Fauci or \uc2 John Bolton\uc2 , his former national security adviser whose security detail he has also terminated.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.40pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The supreme court has agreed to consider whether the country\u8217\'20\'19s first publicly funded religious charter school should be allowed to open in Oklahoma.\par \par \uc2 The case, led by two Catholic dioceses, could open the door to allowing public funds to directly flow to religious schools and transform the line between church and state in education.\par \par \uc2 A lower court blocked the establishment of St Isidore of Seville Catholic virtual school, ruling that its funding arrangement violated the constitution\u8217\'20\'19s first amendment limits on government endorsement of religion.\par \par \uc2 The online school had planned to start classes for its first enrollees last fall, with part of its mission to evangelize its students in the Catholic faith.\par \par \uc2 Charter schools in Oklahoma are considered public schools under state law and draw funding from the state government.\par \par \uc2 Justice \uc2 Amy Coney Barrett\uc2  has recused herself from the case but did not explain why.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.28am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.26pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  ordered the Gulf of Mexico to be renamed the Gulf of America and Alaska\u8217\'20\'19s Mount Denali as Mount McKinley on Monday, something he promised earlier this month at a press conference.\par \par \uc2 In his inaugural address on Monday, Trump said the former Republican president William McKinley \u8220\'20\'1Cmade our country very rich through tariffs and through talent \u8211\'20\'13 he was a natural businessman\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 While Trump can direct the US geological survey to change how it denotes the Gulf of Mexico, such a name change would be unlikely to be recognized internationally.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/20/trump-gulf-mexico-executive-order"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Can Trump really rename the Gulf of Mexico the Gulf of America?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.29am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.05pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Interior department says Gulf of Mexico officially renamed Gulf of America\par \par \uc2 The Trump administration\u8217\'20\'19s interior department said it has officially changed the change of the Gulf of Mexico to the Gulf of America.\par \par \uc2 Alaska\u8217\'20\'19s mountain Denali, the highest peak in North America, has officially been renamed Mount McKinley \u8211\'20\'13 the name it was called before \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  changed it in 2015, the department said in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.doi.gov/pressreleases/interior-department-advances-restoration-historic-names-honoring-american-greatness"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  statement.}}}\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , on his first day in office on Monday, signed an order to rename the 617,800 sq mile Gulf of Mexico and Alaska\u8217\'20\'19s 20,000ft mountain Denali. The interior department said:\par \par \uc2 In accordance with President \uc2 Donald J Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s recent executive order, the Department of the Interior is proud to announce the implementation of name restorations that honor the legacy of American greatness, with efforts already under way. As directed by the president, the Gulf of Mexico will now officially be known as the Gulf of America and North America\u8217\'20\'19s highest peak will once again bear the name Mount McKinley.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.19pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.48pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The justice department chief of staff, Chad Mizelle, has issued an order to curtail prosecutions against people accused of blocking \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  facilities.\par \par \uc2 In a memo on Friday, Mizelle wrote that prosecutions and civil actions under the Freedom of Access to Clinic Entrances (Face) Act will now be permitted only in \u8220\'20\'1Cextraordinary circumstances\u8221\'20\'1D or in cases presenting \u8221\'20\'1Dsignificant aggravating factors\u8221\'20\'1D, AP reports. He said:\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  campaigned on the promise of ending the weaponization of the federal government and has recently directed all federal departments and agencies to identify and correct the past weaponization of law enforcement.\par \par \uc2 Mizelle also ordered the immediate dismissal of three civil Face Act cases related to blockades of clinics in Tennessee, Pennsylvania and Ohio.\par \par \uc2 It comes a day after Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/23/trump-pardons-anti-abortion-activists"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced he would pardon anti-\b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  activists }}}\uc2  convicted of blockading \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic entrances.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.18pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.36pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s pledge to rename the highest mountain in North America has sparked backlash among some Indigenous Alaskans and Alaskan lawmakers, including Republicans.\par \par \uc2 Trump reiterated his intentions to rename Denali back to Mount McKinley during his inaugural address. \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  had dubbed the mountain Denali during his presidency, undoing the 1917 designation made in honor of the 25th president, William McKinley.\par \par \uc2 The declaration of renaming has proved to be highly controversial. The Koyukon, an Alaska Indigenous Athabascan group, referred to the mountain as Denali for centuries before McKinley took office or Alaska became a US state.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.alaskasnewssource.com/2025/01/22/executive-order-rename-denali-signed-by-president-trump/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Alaska News Source}}}\uc2  reported research that suggested that Alaskans are against changing the name back to McKinley by about a two-to-one margin, despite Alaska being a state that is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.270towin.com/states/Alaska"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overwhelmingly supportive}}}\uc2  of Republicans.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/24/trump-denali-rename-reaction"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Indigenous Alaskans and Republicans dismayed by Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Denali renaming}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.15pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will sign an executive order on Friday to create a taskforce to review the \uc2 Federal Emergency Management Agency\uc2  (Fema) and recommend changes, according to a report.\par \par \uc2 The order establishes a group called the Fema Review Council, Semafor reports, who will be directed to issue a report on how the federal disaster response agency currently functions and ultimately recommend changes, including reorganizing or getting rid of the agency altogether.\par \par \uc2 Trump, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2025/jan/24/us-politics-donald-trump-tariffs-china-birthright-citizenship-latest-news-updates?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with%3Ablock-6793c5e38f081abff9bef697#block-6793c5e38f081abff9bef697"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  in comments earlier today,}}}\uc2  said he would consider signing an executive order to \u8220\'20\'1Cfundamentally reform\u8221\'20\'1D or potentially eliminate Fema, calling the agency \u8220\'20\'1Cnot good\u8221\'20\'1D and a \u8220\'20\'1Cdisaster\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think we\u8217\'20\'19re going to recommend that Fema go away,\u8221\'20\'1D the president told reporters in Asheville, North Carolina.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.17pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.54pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The acting secretary of homeland security, Benjamine Huffman, has invoked a seldom-used provision of federal law to make it easier to deputize state and local police to carry out immigration enforcement, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 In a memo seen by Reuters, Huffman, who took over leadership of the department after \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was inaugurated, cited a \u8220\'20\'1Cmass influx\u8221\'20\'1D of migrants to the United States, though aspects of his order remains unclear.\par \par \uc2 Enforcement of immigration law is the job of the federal government, though some Republican-led states have passed laws to allow state and local police to check the paperwork of suspected undocumented migrants.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.17pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.35pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Acting US attorney for Washington DC Ed Martin has released a statement comparing \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s commutations of the Oath Keeper\u8217\'20\'19s militia members\u8217\'20\'19 sentences to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s last-minute pardons of his family members Trump\u8217\'20\'19s political enemies.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf a judge decided that Jim Biden, General \uc2 Mark Milley\uc2 , or another individual were forbidden to visit America\u8217\'20\'19s capital-even after receiving a last-minute, preemptive pardon from the former President \u8211\'20\'13 I believe most Americans would object. The individuals referenced in our motion have had their sentences commuted \u8211\'20\'13 period, end of sentence,\u8221\'20\'1D Martin said in a statement obtained by Politico.\par \par \uc2 Martin has argued against a judge\u8217\'20\'19s order that prevents several members of the militia, including founder Stewart Rhodes from being in Washington DC or the Capitol building.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.16pm GMT\par \par \uc2 State department halts all new aid funding after Trump order\par \par \uc2 The state department has ordered a halt to funding for almost all aid programs, citing an executive order \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  signed on Monday, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 Only aid to Israel and humanitarian food crises are excluded under the policy, with all other US aid programs told to keep running only until they exhaust the funding they currently have.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more, from the AP:\par \par \uc2 The sweeping order threatened a quick halt to countless projects globally aiding health, education, development, job training and other efforts by the United States, the largest provider of foreign aid. It appears to begin enforcement of a pledge to eliminate aid programs that President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  judges not to be in U.S. interests.\par \par \uc2 The order \u8212\'20\'14 sent in a cable to U.S. embassies worldwide and obtained by The Associated Press \u8212\'20\'14 prohibits new government spending, which appears to limit programs to running only as long as they have cash on hand.\par \par \uc2 Some leading aid organizations on Friday were interpreting the directive as an immediate stop-work order for U.S.-funded aid work globally, a senior aid organization official said. Many would likely cease operations immediately so as not to incur more costs, the official said.\par \par \uc2 The official was not authorized to speak publicly and spoke on condition of anonymity.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.59pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Justice department asks judge to drop ban on Oath Keepers militia members entering US Capitol - report\par \par \uc2 Acting US attorney for Washington DC Ed Martin has intervened on behalf of Oath Keepers founder Stewart Rhodes and other members of the militia group, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/kyledcheney/status/1882876942938231271"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Politico reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In a just-filed motion, Martin asked federal judge \uc2 Amit Mehta\uc2  to reverse a ban he imposed on the militia members that prevents them from entering the US Capitol or Washington DC.\par \par \uc2 Martin argues that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s commutation of the group\u8217\'20\'19s sentences preclude any such ban from being enforced, according to a filing. We\u8217\'20\'19ll see how Mehta responds.\par \par \uc2 This post has been corrected to note that Martin is the acting US attorney for Washington DC, not the acting attorney general.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.32pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.46pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Another reason for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to be cautious when it comes to unraveling the \uc2 Federal Emergency Management Agency\uc2  (Fema): his Republican predecessor \uc2 George W Bush\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s experience with the botched response to Hurricane Katrina.\par \par \uc2 The storm 20 years ago inundated New Orleans in one of the worst natural disasters of its time, and Bush\u8217\'20\'19s administration was widely seen as botching the federal response. His administration\u8217\'20\'19s Fema chief, Michael Brown, wound up {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2005/sep/10/hurricanekatrina.usa3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 being relieved of his role}}}\uc2  coordinating the response to the disaster and later resigned.\par \par \uc2 The storm struck just less a year after Bush had won a second term in the 2004 election, and majorities in both houses of Congress. Coupled with dissatisfaction over Bush\u8217\'20\'19s handling of the Iraq war, voters handed control of Congress back to the Democrats in the 2006 midterms \u8211\'20\'13 exactly the sort of scenario Trump would surely like to avoid.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.23pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Federal Emergency Management Agency\uc2  is the latest part of the federal government in \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s crosshairs. But as the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/oliver-milman"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Oliver Milman}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/dharna-noor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dharna Noor}}}\uc2  report, the president may want to tread carefully:\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has suggested paring back or even dismantling the federal response to major disasters, a move that would cut off aid that has largely helped support {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republican}}}\uc2  -leaning states that voted for him in last year\u8217\'20\'19s US presidential election.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump}}}\uc2  said that the \uc2 Federal Emergency Management Agency\uc2  (Fema) had \u8220\'20\'1Cnot done their job for the last four years\u8221\'20\'1D and that there would be \u8220\'20\'1Ca whole big discussion very shortly, because I\u8217\'20\'19d rather see the states take care of their own problems\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In an interview {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.foxnews.com/politics/trump-warns-fema-faces-reckoning-after-biden-admin-not-done-job"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 with Fox News}}}\uc2 , the US president said of Fema that \u8220\'20\'1Call it does is complicate everything\u8221\'20\'1D and that even states who resoundingly backed him, such as Oklahoma, should be primarily left to deal with the aftermath of major storms, floods and fires.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI love Oklahoma, but you know what? If they get hit with a tornado or something, let Oklahoma fix it,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd then the federal government can help them out with the money. Fema is getting in the way of everything.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Shifting the burden of disaster aid to the states, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/08/trump-project-2025-hurricanes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an idea outlined by the rightwing Project 2025 manifesto before the election}}}\uc2 , would hit Republican-leaning states hardest, federal spending figures suggest.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/23/trump-fema-natural-disasters"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Setting us up for catastrophe\u8217\'20\'19: alarm at Trump attack on federal disaster agency}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.08pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  said he was \u8220\'20\'1Cproud to be a participant\u8221\'20\'1D in the overturning of Roe v Wade as he addressed anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists at the March for Life rally in Washington DC.\par \par \uc2 Trump, in a prerecorded video address, said he would \u8220\'20\'1Cagain stand proudly for families and for life\u8221\'20\'1D in his second term.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSix courageous justices of the \uc2 Supreme Court of the United States\uc2  returned the issue to the state legislatures and to the people where it belongs,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Also addressing the crowds on Friday vice-president \uc2 JD Vance\uc2  said Trump had \u8220\'20\'1Cdelivered on his promise of ending Roe\u8221\'20\'1D, describing him as the most pro-family, most pro-life American president of our lifetimes\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAmerica is fundamentally a pro-baby, a pro-family and a pro-life country,\u8221\'20\'1D Vance added.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.58pm GMT\par \par \uc2 In their speeches to the March for Life on Friday, the largest anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  gathering in the US, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and vice-president \uc2 JD Vance\uc2  avoided making sweeping policy announcements about limiting access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 However, both men indicated that the Department of Justice would no longer enforce the federal Freedom of Access to Clinic Entrances Act, or the Face Act, against anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protests.\par \par \uc2 That law, passed in the 1990s amid a spate of high-profile anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  violence, penalizes individuals who threaten, obstruct or injure someone who is trying to access a \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive health\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic, or who vandalize a clinic.\par \par \uc2 Anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists, Vance told a roaring crowd, \u8220\'20\'1Cshould never have the government go after them again.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, Trump pardoned a number of anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists convicted of blockading a clinic in defiance of the Face Act. Those convictions had fueled demands by activists to repeal the act entirely.\par \par \uc2 Vance and Trump \u8211\'20\'13 who spoke remotely, via a recorded message \u8211\'20\'13 garnered the biggest cheers by far from the thousands of people who rallied on the National Mall.\par \par \uc2 Although Trump repeatedly flip-flopped on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights during the 2024 campaign, angering the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  leaders who supported him during his first time, the movement\u8217\'20\'19s enthusiasm for the new president was clearly undiminished.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.59pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.53pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Denmark in 'crisis mode' after Trump's 'fiery call' over Greenland - report\par \par \uc2 We {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2025/jan/24/us-politics-donald-trump-tariffs-china-birthright-citizenship-latest-news-updates?page=with:block-6793d84e8f081abff9bef7df#block-6793d84e8f081abff9bef7df"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported earlier }}}\uc2  that Denmark has agreed to discuss the question of Greenland with Washington, according to Danish foreign minister \uc2 Lars L\u248\'00\'F8kke Rasmussen\uc2  after his first call with the US secretary of state, \uc2 Marco Rubio\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Trump also spoke to the Danish prime minister, \uc2 Mette Frederiksen\uc2 , last week in which he insisted he was serious in his determination to take over Greenland, the \uc2 Financial Times\uc2  reports.\par \par \uc2 Trump spoke to Frederiksen for about 45 minutes in a call that was described as \u8220\'20\'1Cfiery\u8221\'20\'1D, the paper writes, citing senior European officials.\par \par \uc2 The conversation between the two went very badly, the officials said, adding that Trump had been aggressive and confrontational. \u8220\'20\'1CIt was horrendous,\u8221\'20\'1D a source told FT.\par \par \uc2 One person said the Danes \u8220\'20\'1Care utterly freaked out\u8221\'20\'1D by Trump\u8217\'20\'19s call with Frederiksen. Another told the paper:\par \par \uc2 The intent was very clear. They want it. The Danes are now in crisis mode.\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for Frederiksen told the FT they did \u8220\'20\'1Cnot recognize the interpretation of the conversation given by anonymous sources\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.25pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.39pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The Trump administration has withdrawn a Biden administration proposal to ban menthol cigarettes in the US, according to a filing by the office of information and regulatory affairs.\par \par \uc2 The Food and Drug Administration\uc2  proposed a ban on the sale of flavored cigars and menthol cigarettes in 2022 after several health advocacy groups said they were highly addictive, and played a role in luring young people to smoking.\par \par \uc2 Menthol cigarettes have also faced scrutiny for their disproportionate impact on the health of Black communities, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 The news agency quotes Yolonda Richardson, CEO of \uc2 Campaign for Tobacco-Free Kids\uc2 , as saying:\par \par \uc2 It is deeply disappointing that a final rule was not issued in a timely manner.... it is more critical than ever that states and cities step up their efforts to end the sale of menthol cigarettes and other flavored tobacco products.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.27pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Susie Wiles, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s chief of staff, has denied \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  a permanent office in the West Wing of the White House, according to a Times {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thetimes.com/us/american-politics/article/susie-wiles-chief-of-staff-elon-musk-wp0pfkxrx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report.}}}\par \par \uc2 Wiles, whose role as gatekeeper to the president wields great influence, has made it clear that she does not welcome \u8220\'20\'1Cpeople who want to work solo or be a star\u8221\'20\'1D, the paper writes.\par \par \uc2 Musk, who has been put in charge of the \u8220\'20\'1Cdepartment of government efficiency\u8221\'20\'1D (Doge), had been angling for his own office within yards of the Oval Office, it says.\par \par \uc2 But his senior leadership team will be based in the Eisenhower executive office building, which is in the White House grounds but a short walk away from the main complex, it says.\par \par \uc2 Asked if Musk would be getting an office in the West Wing, Trump said earlier this week: \u8220\'20\'1CNo. He\u8217\'20\'19s getting an office for about 20 people that we\u8217\'20\'19re hiring to make sure that these [savings] get implemented.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.20pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Denmark\u8217\'20\'19s foreign minister \uc2 Lars L\u248\'00\'F8kke Rasmussen\uc2  agreed with his US counterpart, \uc2 Marco Rubio\uc2 , to discuss the question of Greenland at a later time, the country\u8217\'20\'19s foreign ministry said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 The two spoke for 20 minutes on Friday, discussing Ukraine, European security, and the Middle East.\par \par \uc2 The statement {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://um.dk/#/embedded/release/14235993/samtale-med-usas-nye-udenrigsminister?publisherId=2012662&lang=da&widget=true"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in Danish}}}\uc2  said that while \u8220\'20\'1CArctic security was not on the agenda,\u8221\'20\'1D the two agreed it would be discussed on another occasion, and Greenland would also be involved in talks.\par \par \uc2 Denmark has been on high alert about the US administration\u8217\'20\'19s intentions towards Greenland since \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s comments suggesting he would want to take control over the territory.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this week, he again said it was \u8220\'20\'1Ca wonderful place,\u8221\'20\'1D that the US \u8220\'20\'1Cneeds for international security\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.06pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Members of the white nationalist group Patriot Front have gathered in Washington DC for the annual anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  March for Life rally.\par \par \uc2 A white supremacist and neo-fascist hate group, Patriot Front emerged as a rebrand of the neo-Nazi organization Vanguard America in the aftermath of the 2017 Unite the Right rally in Charlottesville, Virginia.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.splcenter.org/hatewatch/2022/02/01/one-five-patriot-front-applicants-claim-military-ties"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 According to}}}\uc2  the \uc2 SPLC\uc2 , the Patriot Front \u8220\'20\'1Crepresents one of the most prominent white supremacist groups in the country\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.00pm GMT\par \par \uc2 A slew of big-name conservative men are addressing March for Life, the largest anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rally in the US.\par \par \uc2 Senate majority leader \uc2 John Thune\uc2 , House speaker Mike Johnson and Florida\u8217\'20\'19s governor, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , are all amping up the thousands of marchers who gathered on the National Mall on Friday.\par \par \uc2 But the name to get the biggest cheers so far belongs to a man who isn\u8217\'20\'19t there: \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is a new golden age in America, now we have President \uc2 Donald J Trump\uc2  back in the White House \u8212\'20\'14\u8220\'20\'1C Johnson started to say, only to be interrupted by rapturous cheers from the crowd.\par \par \uc2 Johnson praised Trump for pardoning and freeing anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists who were convicted of illegally blockading clinics. He also flagged one of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s new executive orders, which declares that there are only two genders and incorporates the language of fetal personhood, a legal doctrine that holds that embryos and fetuses deserve full legal rights and protections.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t know if you saw his executive order \u8212\'20\'14 it defines life as beginning at conception rather than birth,\u8221\'20\'1D Johnson said, to immense cheers.\par \par \uc2 Friday marks the first time that both the \uc2 US Senate\uc2  majority leader and the House speaker have spoken to the March, which has gathered annually for more than 50 years. Vice-president JD Vance is expected to address the crowd in person, while Trump is set to deliver a video message.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.48pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The US secretary of state, \uc2 Marco Rubio\uc2 , spoke with China\u8217\'20\'19s foreign minister, Wang Yi, on Friday in the first publicly disclosed contact between an official in the second Trump administration and a Chinese counterpart.\par \par \uc2 Wang told Rubio that Beijing and Washington should implement the \u8220\'20\'1Cimportant consensus\u8221\'20\'1D reached between the Chinese president, Xi Jinping, and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , according to a readout of the call by the \uc2 Chinese foreign ministry\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI hope you would conduct yourself well and play a constructive role in the future of the Chinese and American people and in world peace and stability,\u8221\'20\'1D Wang reportedly told Rubio.\par \par \uc2 Wang also said that China has \u8220\'20\'1Cno intention of surpassing or replacing anyone, but we must defend our legitimate right to development,\u8221\'20\'1D the Chinese ministry said.\par \par \uc2 The two also discussed Taiwan, it said. Wang reiterated that Beijing will never allow Taiwan to be separated from mainland China, and warned the US to handle related matters carefully, the ministry said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.33pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The Trump administration is issuing a new round of heavy-handed measures that could rapidly deport immigrants who entered the US through recently established legal pathways, according to an internal \uc2 Department of Homeland Security\uc2  memo obtained the \uc2 New York Times\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The directive, signed by the acting homeland security secretary Benjamine Huffman, grants \uc2 Immigration and Customs Enforcement\uc2  (Ice) officials unprecedented authority to expedite deportations for immigrants who entered the country with government authorization through two key Biden-era programs.\par \par \uc2 The newly reported memo instructs Ice officials to identify and potentially deport immigrants who have been in the country for over a year and have not yet applied for asylum, in effect sidestepping traditional immigration court proceedings.\par \par \uc2 In no waste of time, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s press secretary, Karoline Leavitt, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/PressSec/status/1882759560613527770"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 posted on X}}}\uc2  on Friday that \u8220\'20\'1CDeportation flights have begun\u8221\'20\'1D with official pictures of people boarding a military-style aircraft.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/24/legal-immigrant-deportation-trump-ice"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump gives Ice power to deport immigrants who came legally under Biden}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.37pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.18pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Dr \uc2 Anthony Fauci\uc2  did not have Secret Service protection, but his security detail \u8211\'20\'13 which \uc2 Donald Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2025/jan/24/us-politics-donald-trump-tariffs-china-birthright-citizenship-latest-news-updates?page=with:block-6793c79e8f081abff9bef6c5#block-6793c79e8f081abff9bef6c5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ended last night}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 was being provided and paid for by the \uc2 National Institutes of Health\uc2 , CNN reports.\par \par \uc2 Fauci, who served as the nation\u8217\'20\'19s top infectious disease official, has continued to face ongoing threats due to his role during the Covid-19 pandemic.\par \par \uc2 He has previously spoken about the need for round-the-clock security protection after receiving \u8220\'20\'1Ccredible death threats\u8221\'20\'1D that included his wife and daughters.\par \par \uc2 In 2022, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/05/anthony-fauci-west-virginia-men-three-years-prison"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a West Virgina man was sentenced to prison }}}\uc2  for sending emails threatening Fauci and his family would be \u8220\'20\'1Cdragged into the street, beaten to death, and set on fire\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The Republican senator \uc2 Rand Paul\uc2  had publicly called for Fauci\u8217\'20\'19s security detail to be terminated. In a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/RandPaul/status/1882596448904290515"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 post}}}\uc2  on X on Thursday, Paul wrote:\par \par \uc2 Today I sent supporting information to end the 24 hr a day limo and security detail for Fauci. I wish him nothing but peace but he needs to pay for his own limos.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.21pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.09pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump, taking questions from reporters in Asheville, was asked about reports that he terminated Dr \uc2 Anthony Fauci\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s security detail last night.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen you work for government, at some point your security detail comes off. You can\u8217\'20\'19t have it forever,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump replied.\par \par \uc2 Asked if he would feel responsible if something was to happen to Fauci or \uc2 John Bolton\uc2 , his former national security adviser whose security detail he also ended earlier this week, Trump said:\par \par \uc2 No. They all made a lot of money. They can hire their own security too \u8230\'20\'26 I can give them some good numbers of very good security people.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CCertainly I would not take responsibility,\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.13pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.00pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump says he will sign executive order to 'fundamentally overhaul' or 'get rid' of Fema\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  said he will sign an executive order to begin the process of \u8220\'20\'1Cfundamentally reforming and overhauling\u8221\'20\'1D or \u8220\'20\'1Cmaybe getting rid of\u8221\'20\'1D the \uc2 Federal Emergency Management Agency\uc2  (Fema).\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think, frankly, that Fema is not good,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump told reporters in Asheville, North Carolina.\par \par \uc2 I think when you have a problem like this, I think you want to use your state to fix it and not waste time calling Fema \u8230\'20\'26 I think we\u8217\'20\'19re going to recommend that Fema go away.\par \par \uc2 He went on describe Fema as a \u8220\'20\'1Cbig disappointment\u8221\'20\'1D. \u8220\'20\'1CThey cost a tremendous amount of money. It\u8217\'20\'19s very bureaucratic, and it\u8217\'20\'19s very slow,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.54pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump terminates security detail for Dr \uc2 Anthony Fauci\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has terminated security detail for Dr \uc2 Anthony Fauci\uc2 , the former director of the \uc2 National Institute of Allergy and Infectious Disease\uc2 , CNN reports.\par \par \uc2 Fauci had his security protections revoked on Thursday night, the outlet writes, citing a source.\par \par \uc2 He has since hired his own private security that he will have to pay for himself, it says.\par \par \uc2 Since returning to the White House, Trump has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/23/mike-pompeo-brian-hook-john-bolton-security"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ended security details for several of his former administration officials,}}}\uc2  including his former secretary of state, \uc2 Mike Pompeo\uc2 , former top aide \uc2 Brian Hook\uc2 , and \uc2 John Bolton\uc2 , his former national security adviser.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.01pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.46pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  reiterated his call for the \uc2 Organization of the Petroleum Exporting Countries\uc2  (Opec) to cut oil prices, claiming that it would help bring an end to the war in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Speaking to reporters in Asheville, North Carolina, Trump said:\par \par \uc2 We want to see \uc2 Opec\uc2  cut the price of oil, and that will automatically stop the tragedy that\u8217\'20\'19s taking place in Ukraine. It\u8217\'20\'19s a butchering tragedy for both sides.\par \par \uc2 Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/23/donald-trump-imports-to-us-tariffs-davos-economic-policy-nato-spending"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 made similar comments during an online address to the World Economic Forum in Davos }}}\uc2  on Thursday, where he called on \uc2 Opec\uc2  to cut the cost of oil, in order to choke off revenues to Russia and halt the conflict in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.56pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.34pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Asked about LA fires, Trump says he wants voter ID and changed water policies from California\par \par \uc2 Trump, speaking to reporters in Asheville, North Carolina, also said he wanted to secure two things from California in exchange for wildfire aid : voter identification laws and changes to water policy in the wake of the wildfires.\par \par \uc2 I want to see two things in Los Angeles. Voter ID, so that the people have a chance to vote, and I want to see the water be released and come down into Los Angeles and throughout the state.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAfter that, I will be the greatest president that California has ever seen,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Trump has repeatedly claimed falsely that the California governor, \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2 , and other officials have refused to provide water from the northern part of the state to fight the fires.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.13pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.22pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump says he wants to see states 'take care' of disasters themselves\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  said he would like to see states take care of disasters themselves as he made his first presidential trip of his second administration to hurricane-battered North Carolina on Friday.\par \par \uc2 Trump, speaking to reporters, accused the \uc2 Federal Emergency Management Agency\uc2  (Fema) of having \u8220\'20\'1Creally let the country down\u8221\'20\'1D as he prepared to meet with emergency responders and tour the \u8220\'20\'1Cmassive amount of damage\u8221\'20\'1D left by Hurricane Helene. He said:\par \par \uc2 I like the concept [of] when North Carolina gets hit, the governor takes care of it. When Florida gets hit, the governor takes care of it. Meaning the states take care of it.\par \par \uc2 He continued:\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19d like to see states take care of disasters, let the state take care of the tornadoes and the hurricanes and all of the other things that happen.\par \par \uc2 Asked if he expected to ask Congress for additional aid for North Carolina and California, Trump claimed that the aid will go through his administration instead of Fema.\par \par \uc2 The aid will go through us. So rather than going through Fema, it will go through us.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.26pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.09pm GMT\par \par \uc2 In his first interview after his release from prison, \uc2 Enrique Tarrio\uc2  thanked \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for pardoning him for his role in planning the January 6 riot, saying he \u8220\'20\'1Cliterally gave me my life back\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Now that he is out, the Proud Boys leader wants revenge, he told Alex Jones, the conspiracy theorist host of Info Wars. He said:\par \par \uc2 The people who did this, they need to feel the heat, they need to be put behind bars, and they need to be prosecuted.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSuccess is going to be retribution,\u8221\'20\'1D he added. \u8220\'20\'1CWe gotta do everything in our power to make sure that the next four years sets us up for the next 100 years.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In the days since the leaders of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/05/january-6-capitol-attackers-trump-pardons"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 far-right militia groups were freed }}}\uc2  from prison, they and their organizations are regrouping and figuring out how to build back momentum now that Trump is back in office. They are emboldened by the mass pardons for the insurrectionists and are planning their next moves.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/24/trump-pardon-proud-boys-enrique-tarrio"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Proud Boys leader thanks Trump for January 6 pardon and vows revenge}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.58pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Judge bars Oath Keepers founder from entering Washington DC after prison release\par \par \uc2 A federal judge has barred the former leader of the far-right Oath Keepers militia group, Stewart Rhodes, and several other January 6 defendants from going into Washington DC or the US Capitol without the court\u8217\'20\'19s approval.\par \par \uc2 US district judge \uc2 Amit Mehta\uc2  issued the order after Rhodes visited the Capitol on Wednesday, a day after he was released from prison as part of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s sweeping clemency order.\par \par \uc2 Rhodes was convicted of seditious conspiracy for his role in the attack on the Capitol and sentenced to 18 years in prison.\par \par \uc2 The judge\u8217\'20\'19s order today also applies to other members of the Oath Keepers group who were convicted of charges that they participated in a violent plot to attack the Capitol.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/21/enrique-tarrio-stewart-rhodes-pardon-january-6-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Who are Enrique Tarrio and Stewart Rhodes, and what were their roles in January 6?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.38pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.36pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is heading to Los Angeles today to survey fire damage, and reportedly invited along California\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic senator Adam Schiff, a leading antagonist who he has insulted repeatedly.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/ccadelago/status/1882639352565756248"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Politico broke the news yesterday}}}\uc2 , along with Trump\u8217\'20\'19s invitation to the state\u8217\'20\'19s other senator, Democrat Alex Padilla. Both declined, with their offices saying they needed to remain in Washington to vote.\par \par \uc2 As he departed the White House this morning for the trip that will also take him to hurricane-ravaged areas of North Carolina, a reporter asked Trump why he invited Schiff, given their bad blood. Trump replied:\par \par \uc2 I don\u8217\'20\'19t know. Is he going? Is he going? I don\u8217\'20\'19t know. I mean, I really don\u8217\'20\'19t know. You know, if he\u8217\'20\'19s going to be there it would be cheaper but I didn\u8217\'20\'19t invite him. Somebody did.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.39pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.19pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Congresswoman Melanie Stansbury is the top Democrat on a subcommittee that will support the \u8220\'20\'1CDepartment of government efficiency\u8221\'20\'1D (Doge), the \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 -backed initiative to streamline the federal government.\par \par \uc2 In an interview with CNN today, Stansbury said she believes the quasi-governmental department is less interested in efficiency, and more interested in policies that will benefit Musk and other wealthy businesses:\par \par \uc2 We believe that they\u8217\'20\'19re going to use the Doge subcommittee to eviscerate the federal workforce. We think they\u8217\'20\'19re going to go after federal departments, agency heads. We think they\u8217\'20\'19re going to go after the retirement benefits and use it also to restructure the government as a way to be essentially a personal piggy bank for \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 . I mean, I think none of us really understand why \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  is even interested in restructuring the government, except for that he has billions of dollars in federal contracts. And I think it\u8217\'20\'19s notable that up until the inauguration, he was operating his arm of DOGE out of \uc2 SpaceX\uc2 , which is the company that he has billions of dollars in front of the federal government with.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.20pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.58pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump weighing deploying up to 10,000 troops to US-Mexico border - report\par \par \uc2 The Trump administration may deploy as many as 10,000 troops to the US-Mexico border and construct detention facilities for migrants on military bases, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/trump-troops-us-mexico-border/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CBS News reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The president earlier this week sent 1,500 active-duty troops to the border, adding to a preexisting deployment authorized under \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . The memo circulating in government says Trump may dramatically expand the troop presence to make good on his campaign promise of stopping border crossers. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more, from \uc2 CBS\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 The internal Customs and Border Protection memo dated Jan. 21 indicates there\u8217\'20\'19s a plan to dispatch \u8220\'20\'1C~10,000 soldiers\u8221\'20\'1D to help the agency\u8217\'20\'19s mission at the southern border. The Trump administration, according to the document, has submitted an \u8220\'20\'1C[u]nrestrained request\u8221\'20\'1D for the Pentagon to surge resources and personnel to assist CBP with technology and infrastructure.\par \par \uc2 The memo also says the \uc2 Defense Department\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cmay\u8221\'20\'1D convert its bases into \u8220\'20\'1Cholding facilities,\u8221\'20\'1D presumably to help CBP detain migrants who crossed into the U.S. illegally.\par \par \uc2 Additionally, the memo shows the Trump administration is planning to dramatically expand detention capacity at \uc2 Immigration and Customs Enforcement\uc2 , which is expected to be at the center of Mr. Trump\u8217\'20\'19s promised mass deportations.\par \par \uc2 According to the document, ICE officials want 14 new detention facilities with the capacity to hold up to 1,000 migrants each and another four able to accommodate as many as 10,000 immigrant detainees each.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.39pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Chicago was said to be an initial target of the mass deportations \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  promised on his first day in office.\par \par \uc2 But the promised raids did not wind up taking place, and it\u8217\'20\'19s unclear if and when they will. Politico reports that the word in the Illinois state government is that Trump is interested more in spectacle than substance when it comes to immigration enforcement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s not like anyone with the Trump administration is picking up the phone and calling us and saying \u8216\'20\'18Here\u8217\'20\'19s the plan,\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D an Illinois state official told Politico.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re looking for a PR stunt.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.19pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s threats to carry out mass arrests in cities that have curtailed cooperation with immigration authorities have spread fear throughout communities, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/maanvi-singh"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Maanvi Singh}}}\uc2  reports:\par \par \uc2 Chicago\u8217\'20\'19s Lower West Side felt uneasily quiet this week.\par \par \uc2 Christina Alejandra, a dancer and local business owner in the city\u8217\'20\'19s artsy, majority Mexican American neighborhood, wondered whether it was because of the freezing temperatures, or the impending threat of immigration raids.\par \par \uc2 The city has been preparing for weeks for a crackdown, after \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s new administration made clear that so-called sanctuary cities \u8211\'20\'13 communities like Chicago that refuse to hand over immigrants to federal authorities \u8211\'20\'13 would be the first targets of its mass-deportation program.\par \par \uc2 But the fear didn\u8217\'20\'19t really hit Alejandra, who\u8217\'20\'19s 26 and undocumented, until Monday, inauguration day, as Trump began unleashing a barrage of new immigration restrictions. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve never been scared like this before,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  is not publishing Alejandra\u8217\'20\'19s full name to protect her and her family from immigration enforcement.\par \par \uc2 Chicago and surrounding areas have seen raids before, including during the first {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/trump-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump administration}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CBut this feels different,\u8221\'20\'1D Alejandra said. \u8220\'20\'1CThe way he and his supporters are riled up. There\u8217\'20\'19s a shift happening.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Such worries have been stirred up in immigrant communities across the US in recent days, amid a flood of new executive orders setting strict limits on who can enter the US, who can stay here and who can call themselves an American, setting off unprecedented waves of panic within the country and at its borders.\par \par \uc2 Moments after the president was sworn into office, asylum seekers waiting to enter the country learned that their appointments to meet with Customs and Border Protection had been cancelled \u8211\'20\'13 and images of devastated and desperate people at the border made a stark diptych with the inaugural ceremonies.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/24/trump-immigration-crackdown"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump immigration crackdown begins: \u8216\'20\'18I\u8217\'20\'19ve never been scared like this before\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.56pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Republican lawmaker proposes constitutional amendment allowing Trump third term\par \par \uc2 Republican congressman Andy Ogles has proposed a constitutional amendment that would allow \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to serve a third term in office.\par \par \uc2 The Tennessee lawmaker said he was making the proposal because he thinks Trump has done such a great job over the past few days:\par \par \uc2 President Trump\u8217\'20\'19s decisive leadership stands in stark contrast to the chaos, suffering, and economic decline Americans have endured over the past four years. He has proven himself to be the only figure in modern history capable of reversing our nation\u8217\'20\'19s decay and restoring America to greatness, and he must be given the time necessary to accomplish that goal. To that end, I am proposing an amendment to the Constitution to revise the limitations imposed by the 22nd Amendment on presidential terms. This amendment would allow President Trump to serve three terms, ensuring that we can sustain the bold leadership our nation so desperately needs.\par \par \uc2 The amendment {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ogles.house.gov/media/press-releases/rep-ogles-proposes-amending-22nd-amendment-allow-trump-serve-third-term"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is written}}}\uc2  in such a way that the three other living presidents who have served two terms \u8211\'20\'13 \uc2 Bill Clinton\uc2 , \uc2 George W Bush\uc2  and \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 would not be eligible to run again.\par \par \uc2 It is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2015/may/06/amending-consitution-politics-trend"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 very difficult}}}\uc2  to amend the US constitution, and it remains to be seen if Ogles\u8217\'20\'19s idea is to be taken seriously.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.34pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s press secretary, Karoline Leavitt, has announced that \u8220\'20\'1Cdeportation flights have begun,\u8221\'20\'1D and shared photos of people lining up to board a military aircraft.\par \par \uc2 enltrDeportation flights have begun.\par \par \uc2 President Trump is sending a strong and clear message to the entire world: if you illegally enter the United States of America, you will face severe consequences. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/CTlG8MRcY1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/CTlG8MRcY1}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Karoline Leavitt (@PressSec) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PressSec/status/1882759560613527770?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 24, 2025}}}\par \par \uc2 Leavitt\u8217\'20\'19s comment was light on details, but perhaps she means they have begun under Trump administration, as there was plenty of deporting going on during \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s just-concluded presidency:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/dec/19/deportations-biden-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US deportations under Biden rose to decade high, outpacing Trump years}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.57pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.12pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Senate may vote on confirming Hegseth to lead defense department this evening\par \par \uc2 The Senate may take a final vote on confirming Pete Hegseth to lead the Pentagon this evening.\par \par \uc2 Yesterday, the Republican-controlled chamber narrowly voted to begin debate on the former Fox News host\u8217\'20\'19s nomination, which has been dogged by a sexual assault allegation and other reports of poor behavior. Two Republican senators and all Democrats voted against confirming Hegseth, but that wasn\u8217\'20\'19t enough to stop the nomination from proceeding.\par \par \uc2 A vote on his final confirmation could take place at 9pm ET. Here\u8217\'20\'19s the latest on his nomination:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/23/lisa-murkowski-pete-hegseth-nomination"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Key Republican senators to vote against Pete Hegseth for US defense secretary}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.51pm GMT\par \par \uc2 US health agency employees are now banned from nearly all travel and certain agencies and programs have been ordered to stop issuing new contracts and grants until further notice.\par \par \uc2 The limits on travel and spending, announced internally on Wednesday, add to previous indefinite halts on external communications, including publishing new reports or even posting to social media, and on reviewing and approving new medical research, a nearly $50bn industry in the US.\par \par \uc2 Employees of the 13 agencies overseen by US Health and Human Services (\uc2 HHS\uc2 ) may only travel to return from assignments or to escape life-threatening situations. That means regular meetings with state and local health officials, training sessions and grant reviews are now on hold.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/24/us-health-agencies-funding-cuts-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Travel, grant and funding cuts \u8216\'20\'18stifling\u8217\'20\'19 US health agencies in new Trump era}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.53pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.32pm GMT\par \par \uc2 70% of Americans do not approve of Musk in government\par \par \uc2 Many Americans agree that the federal government is beset by inefficiency, corruption and needless bureaucracy, but they are less sure about whether aspiring trillionaire \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  is the right person to tackle it.\par \par \uc2 An Associated Press-NORC Centre for Public Affairs Research poll shows only 30% adults in the USA strongly or somewhat approve of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1CDepartment of Government Efficiency\u8221\'20\'1D (Doge), which Musk leads.\par \par \uc2 The poll also shows, despite prevailing wisdom on some social media sites, that Americans aren\u8217\'20\'19t particularly worried about \u8220\'20\'1Cdeep state\u8221\'20\'1D actors undermining Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Republican agenda. They\u8217\'20\'19re also unmoved about cuts to large numbers of federal jobs and moving federal agencies outside Washington.\par \par \uc2 Only one-third of US adults have a favourable view of Musk, the world\u8217\'20\'19s richest person. Approximately half of Americans think of Musk and Trump in unfavourable terms. US adults broadly think it\u8217\'20\'19s a bad thing if the president relies on billionaires for advice about government policy, according to the poll.\par \par \uc2 About 60% of those polled say this would be a \u8220\'20\'1Cvery\u8221\'20\'1D or \u8220\'20\'1Csomewhat\u8221\'20\'1D bad thing, while only about one in 10 call it a very or somewhat good thing, three in 10 are neutral.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.49pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.31pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The United Nations says the right to seek asylum is \u8220\'20\'1Cuniversally recognised\u8221\'20\'1D after Trump suspended all refugee admissions and halted the US asylum programme.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAll states are entitled to exercise their jurisdiction along their international borders, [but] they need to do so in line with their human rights obligations,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 UN\uc2  rights office spokeswoman \uc2 Ravina Shamdasani\uc2  says, according to AFP news agency.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe right to seek asylum is a universally recognised human right,\u8221\'20\'1D she adds.\par \par \uc2 On Monday, Trump signed an executive order suspending the Refugee Admissions Program, saying the US \u8220\'20\'1Clacks the ability to absorb large numbers of migrants, and in particular, refugees, into its communities\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The move blocked 1,600 approved Afghan refugees from moving to the States, while over 3,000 others are waiting in Albania to be resettled.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 UNHCR\uc2  said yesterday that \u8220\'20\'1Crefugee resettlement is a life-saving measure\u8221\'20\'1D, and they are \u8220\'20\'1Cready to continue our work with the new administration to find solutions for refugees\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.15pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Unity, in this sense, is the threshold requirement for people to live together in a free society, it is the solid rock, as Jesus said, in this case upon which to build a nation. It is not conformity. It is not a victory of one over another. It is not weary politeness nor passivity born of exhaustion. Unity is not partisan.\par \par \uc2 Rather, unity is a way of being with one another that encompasses and respects differences, that teaches us to hold multiple perspectives and life experiences as valid and worthy of respect; that enables us, in our communities and in the halls of power, to genuinely care for one another even when we disagree. Those across our country who dedicate their lives, or who volunteer, to help others in times of natural disaster, often at great risk to themselves, never ask those they are helping for whom they voted in the past election or what positions they hold on a particular issue. We are at our best when we follow their example\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2025/jan/24/bishop-mariann-edgar-budde-sermon-that-enraged-donald-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Contempt is a dangerous way to lead a country\u8217\'20\'19: here is the sermon that enraged Donald Trump | Mariann Edgar Budde}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.13pm GMT\par \par \uc2 German politician suggests Canada joins the EU\par \par \uc2 Germany\u8217\'20\'19s former foreign minister has suggested that Canada be invited to join the \uc2 European Union\uc2 , giving voice to an unlikely proposition that has quietly circulated since \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  began {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/dec/06/trump-fox-news-patriot-award"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 floating the idea}}}\uc2  of Canada becoming the US\u8217\'20\'19s 51st state.\par \par \uc2 Speaking to Germany\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thepioneer.de/originals/others/articles/sigmar-gabriel-will-kanada-in-die-eu-aufnehmen"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pioneer Media,}}}\uc2  Sigmar Gabriel pointed to the shifting geopolitics ushered in by Trump\u8217\'20\'19s second term. \u8220\'20\'1CWe should invite Canada to become a member of the \uc2 European Union\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D said Gabriel, adding: \u8220\'20\'1CThey are more European than some European member states anyway.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Gabriel, who was also Germany\u8217\'20\'19s vice-chancellor from 2013 to 2018, said it was an idea worth pursuing, even if Canada is not geographically located in Europe. \u8220\'20\'1CI would give it a try. Canada is an enormously important country. It is, by the way, a strategic Arctic border state \u8230\'20\'26 We need to gather allies. That also applies to our free trade agreements.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 His suggestion echoed an opinion column published earlier this year in The Economist and which argued that the union would be beneficial for both as \u8220\'20\'1CCanada is vast and blessed with natural resources but relatively few people, while the EU is small, cramped and mineral-poor\u8217\'20\'19.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbc.ca/news/world/trump-davos-canada-1.7440118"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 again called}}}\uc2  on Canada to join the US as he addressed the Davos economic forum in Switzerland by video link: \u8220\'20\'1CAs you probably know, I say, \u8216\'20\'18You can always become a state, and if you\u8217\'20\'19re a state, we won\u8217\'20\'19t have a deficit. We won\u8217\'20\'19t have to tariff you.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Canadian officials have repeatedly slammed any such suggestion, with one minister {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbc.ca/news/world/trump-davos-canada-1.7440118"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 describing it}}}\uc2  as something out of a \u8220\'20\'1CSouthpark episode.\u8221\'20\'1D Polls {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbc.ca/news/canada/canada-join-u-s-poll-1.7434317"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 carried out in recent weeks}}}\uc2  on both sides of the border have suggested that the vast majority of Canadians and many Americans disapprove of the idea.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.22pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.59am GMT\par \par \uc2 Moscow rejects president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s suggestion that a settlement in Ukraine can be achieved by falling oil prices\par \par \uc2 In an address to the annual \uc2 World Economic Forum\uc2  on Thursday, Trump said that the OPEC+ alliance of oil exporting countries shares responsibility for the ongoing Ukrainian War due to keeping oil prices too high. Trump said that \u8220\'20\'1Cif the price came down, the Russia-Ukraine war would end immediately\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Asked about Trump\u8217\'20\'19s comments, Kremlin spokesperson Dmitry Peskov said: \u8220\'20\'1CThe conflict doesn\u8217\'20\'19t depend on oil prices,\u8221\'20\'1D Peskov said in a conference call with reporters. \u8220\'20\'1CThe conflict is ongoing because of the threat to Russia\u8217\'20\'19s national security, the threat to Russians living on those territories and the refusal by the Americans and the Europeans to listen to Russia\u8217\'20\'19s security concerns. It\u8217\'20\'19s not linked to oil prices.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Asked to comment on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s claim that Ukrainian president \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskyy\uc2  is ready for a deal, Peskov said: \u8220\'20\'1CZelenskyy can\u8217\'20\'19t be ready for a deal.\u8221\'20\'1D He added: \u8220\'20\'1CIn order to reach a settlement it\u8217\'20\'19s necessary to conduct talks, and Zelenskyy forbade himself to hold talks by his own decree.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, Trump threatened Russia with more tariffs, taxes and sanctions if they don\u8217\'20\'19t end the war.\par \par \uc2 Peskov said that the Kremlin was paying close attention to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s statements, insisting Moscow \u8220\'20\'1Cremains ready for an equal dialogue, for a mutually respectful dialogue\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis dialogue took place between the two presidents during Trump\u8217\'20\'19s first presidency. And we are waiting for signals that we have not received yet,\u8221\'20\'1D Peskov said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.01pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.42am GMT\par \par \uc2 Spare a thought for the grifters. Those sad Brits who have spent years toadying up to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  in the belief they had been admitted into his gilded inner circle. Those men and women who bravely posted selfies on X as they arrived in Washington in the belief they would be attending the inauguration of The Donald.\par \par \uc2 There was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/liz-truss"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Liz Truss}}}\uc2  looking like a cheap Paddington Bear in a blue coat and red Maga hat announcing her arrival in DC. Only to go mysteriously silent when she discovered she hadn\u8217\'20\'19t made the cut. Not just to the Rotunda where the main action was being staged but also not to the overspill area in the Capitol where guests could follow proceedings on TV. Presumably Lizzie was left to watch the action on her phone in a McDonald\u8217\'20\'19s somewhere downtown\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/24/digested-week-desperado-brits-realise-trump-need-of-them"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Digested week: Desperado Brits come to finally realise Trump has no need of them }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.27am GMT\par \par \uc2 Russia open to nuclear talks\par \par \uc2 Russia says it is open to negotiating nuclear disarmament, the BBC reports.\par \par \uc2 The Russian government will work with Washington, but only if the nuclear weapons of the UK and France are on the negotiation table, Kremlin spokesperson Dmitry Peskov said.\par \par \uc2 Peskov\u8217\'20\'19s comments come in the aftermath of US president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s announcement on Thursday that he wanted to work towards reducing nuclear arms.\par \par \uc2 Trump indicated that Russia and China could possibly support reducing their own nuclear arsenals.\par \par \uc2 Peskov said: \u8220\'20\'1CWe are certainly interested in starting the negotiation process as soon as possible.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But he also added: \u8220\'20\'1CIn the current situation, all nuclear capacities need to be taken into account. In particular, it\u8217\'20\'19s impossible to hold a conversation without taking into consideration the nuclear capacities of France and the United Kingdom. The current realities make it necessary.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.37am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.27am GMT\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/lifeandstyle/picture/2025/jan/24/not-sure-about-elon-musks-salute-lets-run-it-through-normalize-the-stephen-collins-cartoon"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Not sure about Elon Musk\u8217\'20\'19s salute? Let\u8217\'20\'19s run it through Normalize \u8230\'20\'26 the Stephen Collins cartoon}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.13am GMT\par \par \uc2 In a series of newly unearthed podcasts, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/pete-hegseth"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pete Hegseth}}}\uc2 , \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s pick for defense secretary, appears to endorse the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/15348423.2024.2408124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 theocratic and authoritarian}}}\uc2  doctrine of \u8220\'20\'1Csphere sovereignty\u8221\'20\'1D, a worldview derived from the extremist beliefs of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Christian_reconstructionism"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Christian reconstructionism}}}\uc2  (CR) and espoused by churches aligned with far-right Idaho pastor Douglas Wilson.\par \par \uc2 In the recordings, Hegeth rails against \u8220\'20\'1Ccultural Marxism\u8221\'20\'1D, feminism, \u8220\'20\'1Ccritical race theory\u8221\'20\'1D, and even democracy itself, which he says \u8220\'20\'1Cour founders blatantly rejected as being completely dangerous\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 For much of the over five hours of recordings, which were published over February and March 2024, Hegseth also castigates public schools, which he characterizes as implementing an \u8220\'20\'1Cegalitarian, dystopian LGBT nightmare\u8221\'20\'1D, and which podcast host Joshua Haymes describes as \u8220\'20\'1Cone of Satan\u8217\'20\'19s greatest tools for excising Christ from not just our classrooms but our country\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/24/trump-pete-hegseth-extremism"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump Pentagon nominee endorses extremist Christian doctrine}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.33am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.54am GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump to address America\u8217\'20\'19s largest anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rally\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is due to make a speech via video link to the March for Life rally, America\u8217\'20\'19s largest annual anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rally later on Friday.\par \par \uc2 The president pardoned 23 anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists a day before the March for Life in Washington DC.\par \par \uc2 Trump is not the first president to address the rally. Previous Republican presidents, including \uc2 George W Bush\uc2  and \uc2 Ronald Reagan\uc2 , have addressed the group remotely. However, in 2020, Trump became the first US president to attend the rally in person.\par \par \uc2 The annual rally began in 1974 after the legalisation of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  established in Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.04am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.35am GMT\par \par \uc2 While some have praised {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  for issuing \u8220\'20\'1Cfull, complete and unconditional\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/20/trump-executive-orders-jan-6-pardons"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pardons for the 1,500 individuals}}}\uc2  involved in the January 6 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-capitol-breach"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 attack on the US Capitol}}}\uc2 , Pamela Hemphill has pushed back.\par \par \uc2 Hemphill, who was also arrested on January 6, has refused to accept Trump\u8217\'20\'19s pardon, instead deciding to take responsibility for the role she played in trying to overturn the 2020 election results which made \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  victorious over Trump.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAbsolutely not,\u8221\'20\'1D Hemphill, 71, told the Guardian on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s an insult to the \uc2 Capitol police\uc2  officers and to the rule of law and to the nation. It contributes to the propaganda that it was a peaceful protest, that the DoJ is weaponized against them and against Trump.\u8221\'20\'1D\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/23/maga-granny-trump-pardon"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Former \u8216\'20\'18Maga Granny\u8217\'20\'19 refuses to accept Trump\u8217\'20\'19s pardon for actions on January 6}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.14am GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump prepares to tour wildfire damage in Los Angeles after criticising California\u8217\'20\'19s water policy\par \par \uc2 Trump has erroneously claimed that California could have mitigated the wildfires sooner if it hadn\u8217\'20\'19t been for redirecting water to the Pacific Ocean. The president was referring to the water federally managed by the Central Valley Project.\par \par \uc2 However, the agency mostly supplies farms and doesn\u8217\'20\'19t carry water to Los Angeles. Meanwhile, The \uc2 Metropolitan Water District of Southern California\uc2  says it has ample storage to meet the region\u8217\'20\'19s water needs.\par \par \uc2 In the first hours of his second term, Trump encouraged federal officials to route more water to the crop-rich Central Valley and densely populated cities in the southern part of the state, even threatening to withhold federal disaster aid unless state leaders change their approach on water.\par \par \uc2 He has continued to question how California\u8217\'20\'19s water managed. Last year on his Truth Social platform, he criticized the \u8220\'20\'1Crerouting of MILLIONS OF GALLONS OF WATER A DAY FROM THE NORTH OUT INTO THE PACIFIC OCEAN, rather than using it, free of charge, for the towns, cities, & farms dotted all throughout California\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Trump has suggested that state officials \u8220\'20\'1C turn the valve \u8221\'20\'1D to send more water to the city. But state water supplies are not to blame for hydrants running dry and a key reservoir near Pacific Palisades that was not filled\par \par \uc2 California\u8217\'20\'19s water system is complicated.\par \par \uc2 Most of the region\u8217\'20\'19s water is in the north, while the bulk of the state\u8217\'20\'19s population is in the drier south. Los Angeles is the second driest city in America and relies on water from elsewhere. As does the dry Central Valley, where most of California\u8217\'20\'19s produce is grown.\par \par \uc2 Two complex systems of dams and canals move rain and melted snow from the mountainous north to the south. One is managed by the federal government, the Central Valley Project, while the other is operated by the state of California and known as the State Water Project. Both systems channel water through the Sacramento-San Joaquin River Delta, an estuary supporting wildlife, including salmon and the delta smelt.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Los Angeles Department of Water and Power\uc2  also manages its own aqueducts that draw water from the eastern Sierra Nevada. The Federal government decides how much water is routed to the delta to protect threatened species and how much goes to Central Valley Project users, mostly farms. That project does not supply water to Los Angeles.\par \par \uc2 However, Trump insists the state lets too much water go to the ocean rather than cities and farms.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.20pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.02am GMT\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US Department of State\uc2  has banned consular posts from flying any flags other than that of the US as part of the Trump administration\u8217\'20\'19s pledge to crack down on diversity efforts in government institutions.\par \par \uc2 A cable seen by the Guardian titled \u8220\'20\'1COne flag policy\u8221\'20\'1D appears to target several instances during the Biden administration when gay pride and Black Lives Matters flags were flown at embassies abroad.\par \par \uc2 Gay pride flags were also on display at the White House during a 2023 Pride month celebration held on the south lawn, sparking a backlash from conservatives\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/23/trump-administration-bans-non-us-flags-from-being-flown-at-embassies"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump administration bans non-US flags from being flown at embassies}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.08am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.45am GMT\par \par \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  signs $2.5bn relief package as \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  set to visit LA\par \par \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  has signed a $2.5bn relief package to help areas of Los Angeles recover from the devastating fires that have been burning for nearly two weeks. The funds were announced during a press conference on Thursday in Pasadena, just outside Altadena, the town hit hardest by the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2025/jan/07/southern-california-wildfire-windstorm-live-updates?page=with:block-677e809e8f087292f9af754a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Eaton fire, which ignited on 7 January}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The signing of the bipartisan aid package comes a day before \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is set to visit the fire-torn areas and amid continued criticism of the California governor and other state officials\u8217\'20\'19 management of the state\u8217\'20\'19s water supply. It also follows a new blaze, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fire.ca.gov/incidents/2025/1/22/hughes-fire"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Hughes fire}}}\uc2 , which sparked on Wednesday morning and quickly grew. It is now 36% contained and has burned nearly 10,400 acres (4,209 hectares), according to \uc2 Cal Fire\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The largest of the recent Los Angeles-area blazes ignited on 7 January, ripping through the Pacific Palisades neighborhood in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/los-angeles"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Los Angeles}}}\uc2  and killing 11 people. The Eaton fire, which broke out the same day near Altadena, killed 17 people.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.54am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.29am GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump gives \uc2 Immigration and Customs Enforcement\uc2  officials powers to quickly deport migrants allowed into the country temporarily by Biden\par \par \uc2 According to an internal government memo obtained by the \uc2 New York Times\uc2 , \uc2 Immigration and Customs Enforcement (ICE)\uc2  officials will have powers normally reserved for encounters at America\u8217\'20\'19s border with Mexico to quickly remove migrants.\par \par \uc2 Stephen Miller\uc2 , a White House deputy chief of staff and the architect of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s hard-line immigration policies, has made clear that he opposed both programs.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHere\u8217\'20\'19s an idea: Don\u8217\'20\'19t fly millions of illegal aliens from failed states thousands of miles away into small towns across the American Heartland,\u8221\'20\'1D Miller said on social media in September.\par \par \uc2 Reacting to the memo, Tom Jawetz, a senior lawyer in the \uc2 Homeland Security Department\uc2  in the Biden administration, said: \u8220\'20\'1CIn addition to raising serious legal concerns, subjecting people who played by the rules to a summary deportation process is an outrageous and unprecedented betrayal.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Karen Tumlin, the director of the Justice Action Center, an immigrant advocacy group, said the decision was a mistake: \u8220\'20\'1CAmerican communities have opened their hearts and homes for people from Cuba, Haiti, Nicaragua, Venezuela, Afghanistan and Ukraine,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CPunishing people who did everything the government asked, and many of whom had US-based sponsors, to this summary deportation procedure is appalling.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.30am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.11am GMT\par \par \uc2 Nick Brown, the Washington state attorney general, spoke outside after a federal judge temporarily blocked \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s executive order redefining birthright citizenship.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe came to the courthouse today to defend the United States constitution. To defend democracy in America and to defend what it means to be an American citizen,\u8221\'20\'1D Brown said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.12am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.59am GMT\par \par \uc2 In the first few days of his presidency, people tried to challenge and reason with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 suing his administration, questioning his decisions to reporters and pleading to him for mercy. But does Trump care what his critics think? Jonathan Freedland speaks to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.newyorker.com/contributors/susan-b-glasser"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Susan Glasser of the New Yorker}}}\uc2  about what we can expect from a leader who goes it alone\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/audio/2025/jan/24/can-anyone-hold-back-donald-trump-podcast"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Can anyone hold back Donald Trump? \u8211\'20\'13 podcast}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.53am GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump says he\u8217\'20\'19d 'rather not\u8217\'20\'19 impose tariffs on China\par \par \uc2 US president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  says he would \u8220\'20\'1Crather not\u8221\'20\'1D impose tariffs on China, after repeatedly pledging to hit the nation with hefty import levies.\par \par \uc2 Trump said he could make a deal with America\u8217\'20\'19s biggest economic rival because \u8220\'20\'1Cwe have something that they want, we have a pot of gold\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have one very big power over China, and that\u8217\'20\'19s tariffs, and they don\u8217\'20\'19t want them, and I\u8217\'20\'19d rather not have to use it. But it\u8217\'20\'19s a tremendous power over China,\u8221\'20\'1D he said in an interview with Fox News which aired on Thursday in the United States.\par \par \uc2 When Trump took office he said 10% tariffs on all Chinese imports could kick in by 1 February \u8211\'20\'13 and on the campaign trail touted a levy as high as 60%.\par \par \uc2 On Friday Beijing called for the US and China to resolve their differences through \u8220\'20\'1Cdialogue and consultation\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CChina-US economic and trade cooperation is mutually beneficial,\u8221\'20\'1D foreign ministry spokesperson Mao Ning said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTrade wars and tariff wars have no winners and don\u8217\'20\'19t serve anyone\u8217\'20\'19s interests or the world\u8217\'20\'19s interests,\u8221\'20\'1D she added.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250124el1o0015u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
