\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Trump signs order to reinstate \u8216\'20\'18global gag rule\u8217\'20\'19 on  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  aid\b0\par\par\uc2 Carter Sherman \par \uc2 577 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 January 2025\par 01:46 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Federal rule also known as \u8216\'20\'18Mexico City policy\u8217\'20\'19 halts US funds to overseas groups that provide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  on Friday signed an executive order reinstating a federal rule known as the \u8220\'20\'1CMexico City policy\u8221\'20\'1D which halts US aid from flowing to groups that provide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services, counsel people about the procedure or advocate for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights overseas.\par \par \uc2 The policy, which was first instituted by \uc2 Ronald Reagan\uc2  in 1984, is typically implemented whenever a Republican president wins the White House and rescinded whenever a Democrat wins. But this whiplash has major implications for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and reproductive healthcare around the world.\par \par \uc2 Historically, the revival of the Mexico City policy affects up to about $600m of international aid. During his first term, however, Trump dramatically expanded the scope of the Mexico city policy, which \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights supporters call a \u8220\'20\'1Cglobal gag rule\u8221\'20\'1D. Rather than applying the policy only to family planning assistance, as was typical, the Trump administration applied to it to assistance for organizations that offer a range of health services around the globe \u8211\'20\'13 leading the policy to affect billions of dollars\u8217\'20\'19 worth of aid.\par \par \uc2 According to the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2 , which tracks \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions and their impact, the policy can cut off access to contraception, lead women to seek out unsafe abortions and cause tumult within the non-governmental groups that depend on US aid to keep their programs going.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CReinstating the Mexico City policy will have deadly consequences for people across the globe,\u8221\'20\'1D Rebecca Hart Holder, president of Reproductive Equity Now, said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe United States is a vital partner to healthcare providers and organizations around the world, and robbing those frontline providers of their ability to provide the full spectrum of reproductive healthcare, and even information about people\u8217\'20\'19s options, will result in people losing their lives to pregnancy complications.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump also signed a second executive order affirming a longstanding US policy that prohibits the use of federal funds to pay for abortions. That order also rolled back two executive orders penned by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , which sought to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in the wake of the 2022 overturning of Roe v Wade. The fall of Roe led a wave of states to ban the procedure.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s executive orders arrived hours after he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/24/trump-vance-march-for-life"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sent a pre-recorded message}}}\uc2  to the protesters who attended the March for Life, the nation\u8217\'20\'19s largest anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  gathering, in Washington on Friday afternoon. His vice president, JD Vance, addressed the March in person.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWith the inauguration on Monday, our country faces the return of the most pro-family, most pro-life American president of our lifetimes,\u8221\'20\'1D Vance told the crowd, to massive cheers.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights supporters had anticipated the return of the Mexico City policy, but are still awaiting news on whether Trump will allow widespread enforcement of the Comstock Act, a 19th-century anti-vice law that could be used to effectively ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide.\par \par \uc2 Although \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights remain extremely popular in the US, Vance and Trump\u8217\'20\'19s appearances at the March are a sign of the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement\u8217\'20\'19s political firepower and diehard grip on the GOP.\par \par \uc2 The Senate majority leader, \uc2 John Thune\uc2 , and speaker of the House, Mike Johnson, also spoke at the March \u8211\'20\'13 marking the first time in the March\u8217\'20\'19s 50-year-plus history that the leaders of both chambers of Congress had ever done so.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250125el1p0005l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
