\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Trump and Vance back anti- \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  activists in March for Life speeches\b0\par\par\uc2 Carter Sherman in Washington \par \uc2 867 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 January 2025\par 22:39 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Both president and vice-president indicate US justice department will no longer prosecute anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists\par \par \uc2 In addresses to the March for Life, the nation\u8217\'20\'19s largest anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rally, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  and his vice-president, JD Vance, both indicated on Friday that the US justice department would no longer prosecute anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNo longer will our government throw pro-life protesters and activists \u8211\'20\'13 elderly, grandparents, or anybody else \u8211\'20\'13 in prison,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/jd-vance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Vance}}}\uc2  told the thousands-strong crowd that gathered on the National Mall, in the shadow of the Washington Monument. \u8220\'20\'1CIt stopped on Monday, and we\u8217\'20\'19re not gonna let it come back to this country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Vance trumpeted the president\u8217\'20\'19s decision to, on Thursday, pardon several anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists who had been convicted of violating the federal Free Access to Clinic Entrances Act, or the Face Act, by blockading an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic. That law penalizes people who threaten, obstruct or injure someone who is trying to access a \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive health\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic \u8211\'20\'13 or who vandalize a clinic. Anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists have, for years, attempted to strike it down or convince the federal government to stop enforcing it.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m releasing the Christians and pro-life activists who were persecuted by the Biden regime for praying and living out their faith,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said in his own address, which the president pre-recorded and broadcast to the crowd on two giant screens. He added: \u8220\'20\'1CNever again will religious persecution be allowed to happen in America.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 However, neither Trump nor Vance talked about any of the sweeping policies that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights activists are now bracing for, such as the enforcement of a 19th-century anti-vice law that could effectively ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide. They did not even mention the Mexico City policy, which is also known as the \u8220\'20\'1Cglobal gag rule\u8221\'20\'1D and which blocks foreign non-governmental organizations (NGOs) from receiving assistance if they refer people for abortions, counsel them on the procedure or advocate for its access.\par \par \uc2 Every Republican president since \uc2 Ronald Reagan\uc2  has enforced this rule. And every Democratic one has rescinded it, although Trump \u8211\'20\'13 during his first presidency \u8211\'20\'13 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2019/mar/26/trump-global-gag-rule-us-aid-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dramatically expanded the rule\u8217\'20\'19s scope}}}\uc2  so that it affected some $6bn in aid. The lack of immediate action from the new Trump administration on the policy has puzzled \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights supporters.\par \par \uc2 In recent years, the March for Life has at times doubled as a Trump rally. This year\u8217\'20\'19s iteration was no different. Vendors sold marchers red hats with Trump\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1CMake America Great Again\u8221\'20\'1D (Maga) slogan and T-shirts bearing the words \u8220\'20\'1CFIGHT \u8230\'20\'26 FIGHT \u8230\'20\'26 FIGHT!\u8221\'20\'1D above an image of Trump holding his fist in the air (which was taken shortly after his attempted assassination in July).\par \par \uc2 Trump and Vance\u8217\'20\'19s appearances also seemingly garnered the biggest roars from the crowd \u8211\'20\'13 far more than any anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  talking point or the appearances of the \uc2 US Senate\uc2  majority leader, John Thune, the House speaker, Mike Johnson, or Florida\u8217\'20\'19s governor, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Johnson did win big cheers from the marchers, though, when he mentioned {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/23/trump-executive-order-fetal-personhood"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a recent executive order}}}\uc2  that declared that people are divided into male and female \u8220\'20\'1Cat conception\u8221\'20\'1D. That language evokes the doctrine of fetal personhood, which holds that embryos and fetuses should be granted full legal rights and protections \u8211\'20\'13 and which, if fully enacted, would totally outlaw \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as well as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/jan/23/abortion-homicide-bills"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 potentially criminalize \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  patients}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur country has got to get back to God,\u8221\'20\'1D said Marie Summergren, 64, of Pennsylvania. \u8220\'20\'1CNeither one \u8211\'20\'13 our president or our vice-president \u8211\'20\'13 has any problem saying that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She added: \u8220\'20\'1CIt feels as though the tide is turning. It\u8217\'20\'19s OK to talk about God again.\u8221\'20\'1D (\uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , the previous president, was a devout Catholic.)\par \par \uc2 The marchers struck an ebullient tone, convinced that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s return to the White House signaled their own return to power after a series of electoral defeats. After Vance spoke, the crowd chanted: \u8220\'20\'1CJD! JD! JD!\u8221\'20\'1D Then, as they marched towards the National Mall and the US Capitol building, cheers like \u8220\'20\'1CWe love babies! Yes we do!\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1CYour mom! Chose life!\u8221\'20\'1D sprang up. They also carried signs that declared \u8220\'20\'1CLife Wins,\u8221\'20\'1D \u8220\'20\'1CDefund Planned Parenthood\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1CMake More Babies.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Many did not seem convinced that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans should contain any exceptions.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHuman life starts at conception,\u8221\'20\'1D said Henry Cooper, an 18-year-old march attender from California. \u8220\'20\'1CAn \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is never medically necessary. Ectopic pregnancy is something else. That\u8217\'20\'19s not considered an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . There\u8217\'20\'19s always something you can do.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBesides ectopic pregnancies, there are no cases where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  improves the likelihood of the mother surviving other than a non-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  way would,\u8221\'20\'1D agreed Luc Lessard, 18, of Colorado. \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s no real cause for it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 (The \uc2 American College of Obstetricians and Gynecologists\uc2 , the pre-eminent membership organization for US ob-gyns, has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.acog.org/advocacy/abortion-is-essential/come-prepared/abortion-access-fact-sheet"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  repeatedly emphasized the medical need}}}\uc2  for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access. At least five women have reportedly died after \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans affected their medical care.)\par \par \uc2 Both Cooper and Lessard voted for Trump. The duo bought a pair of red Maga hats for $30 at the march.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m excited for the next four years,\u8221\'20\'1D Cooper said.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250124el1o003h2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
