\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s executive order on gender uses language pointing to \u8216\'20\'18fetal personhood\u8217\'20\'19\b0\par\par\uc2 Carter Sherman \par \uc2 578 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 January 2025\par 01:58 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par 15\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Words \u8216\'20\'18at conception\u8217\'20\'19 in order gesture to push by anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement to give embryos and fetuses legal rights\par \par \uc2 One of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/20/trump-executive-order-gender-sex"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new executive orders}}}\uc2 , which claims there are only two genders, quietly incorporates tenets of fetal personhood \u8211\'20\'13 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2024/mar/20/states-fetal-personhood-bill"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the legal doctrine}}}\uc2 , pushed by the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement, that life begins at conception and that embryos and fetuses therefore deserve full legal rights and protections.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\u8216\'20\'18Female\u8217\'20\'19 means a person belonging, at conception, to the sex that produces the large reproductive cell,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/presidential-actions/2025/01/defending-women-from-gender-ideology-extremism-and-restoring-biological-truth-to-the-federal-government/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reads the order}}}\uc2 , which was issued just hours after Trump took office on Monday. \u8220\'20\'1C\u8216\'20\'18Male\u8217\'20\'19 means a person belonging, at conception, to the sex that produces the small reproductive cell.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The words \u8220\'20\'1Cat conception\u8221\'20\'1D have set off alarm bells among \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights supporters. If fully enacted, fetal personhood would have sweeping repercussions for all US law; not only would it outlaw \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide, but it could even lead governments to treat \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as murder and treat people who undergo the procedure as murderers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t think it was a mistake. I don\u8217\'20\'19t think it was a coincidence. I think this was an intentional way to continue to normalize the idea that embryos are people,\u8221\'20\'1D said Dana Sussman, senior vice-president of Pregnancy Justice, a reproductive justice group that tracks efforts to enshrine fetal personhood into law.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is yet another attempt to codify it in one form or another.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 During the campaign, Trump veered between taking credit for engineering the supreme court conservative majority that overturned Roe v Wade and claiming that he didn\u8217\'20\'19t want to implement a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban. But {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/09/republican-abortion-ban-policy-platform-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the 2024 Republican platform}}}\uc2  evoked fetal personhood, stressing Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 commitment to \u8220\'20\'1Cthe issue of life\u8221\'20\'1D and suggesting that fetuses are included in the 14th amendment\u8217\'20\'19s guarantee that \u8220\'20\'1Cno person can be denied life or liberty without due process\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Advocates of fetal personhood hope to ultimately bring a case to the supreme court that will lead the justices to declare that the 14th amendment applies from the moment of conception. (The 14th amendment also protects birthright citizenship, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jan/21/birthright-citizenship-explained-trump-executive-order"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 which Trump is now attempting to end}}}\uc2 .)\par \par \uc2 Mary Ziegler, a \uc2 University of California, Davis\uc2 , School of Law professor who studies the legal history of reproduction, stressed that the executive order did not establish new protections or legal status for embryos and fetuses.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s unclear if this is Trump starting down a road towards much bolder steps on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  or IVF or if this is just Trump throwing anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  insiders a bone that most readers wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t necessarily understand,\u8221\'20\'1D said Ziegler, who studies the legal history of reproduction.\par \par \uc2 But, she added: \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s always a big deal when you have something, a seed like that, planted in federal law that someone could maybe make something out of later.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In the weeks and days leading up to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s return to the White House, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights supporters feared that the new president {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/05/project-2025-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 would take steps to cut off access}}}\uc2  to the procedure, such as by using a 19th-century anti-vice law to ban the mailing of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related equipment or ordering the FDA to roll back its approval of a common \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill.\par \par \uc2 So far, Trump has not yet taken decisive action on the issue. However, his administration did seemingly dispose of the website reproductiverights.gov, which included information about access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  coverage.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250123el1n001xh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
