\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Texas lawmakers take aim at  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  pills in new legislative session\b0\par\par\uc2 Mary Tuma in Austin \par \uc2 929 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 January 2025\par 18:53 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bills crafted to stop what is widely viewed a loophole as \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills have helped mitigate bans dotting the US\par \par \uc2 As the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://capitol.texas.gov/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas legislature}}}\uc2  convenes in Austin on Tuesday for the first day of its 2025 session, a number of anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bills have already been filed, largely aimed at halting the flow of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills into the state.\par \par \uc2 The bills were crafted to stop what is widely viewed as a loophole in \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans across the country, as pills have helped mitigate the impact of the bans now dotting the US. Texas Right to Life, the state\u8217\'20\'19s largest anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  advocacy group, has had a hand in drafting a number of the bills, and is encouraging men to sue people who have supported their partners\u8217\'20\'19 abortions.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere hasn\u8217\'20\'19t been any real accountability when it comes to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill access, so we are going to try several different approaches to give Texans more tools to end this deadly trend,\u8221\'20\'1D said John Seago, president of Texas Right to Life.\par \par \uc2 Texas was the first state in the US to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/01/texas-abortion-law-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ban most abortions}}}\uc2  in recent years, passing a six-week ban that went into effect months before the fall of Roe v Wade. Following the Dobbs decision that overturned Roe, the state enacted a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://capitol.texas.gov/BillLookup/History.aspx?LegSess=87R&Bill=HB1280"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 total ban}}}\uc2  that threatens doctors with up to life in prison. Texas often serves as a laboratory for anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bills and strategies that other Republican-led states {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://reproductivefreedomforall.org/news/twelve-states-and-counting-poised-to-copy-texas-abortion-ban/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 later replicate}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 While a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://capitol.texas.gov/BillLookup/History.aspx?LegSess=871&Bill=SB4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas law}}}\uc2  already criminalizes sending \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills to its residents by mail, it has been difficult to enforce. An average of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://societyfp.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/10/WeCount-Report-8-June-2024-data.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 2,800 abortions}}}\uc2  a month are still obtained in Texas through so-called shield laws that were passed in a number of blue states to offer protection to providers who prescribe to women in states with bans. Other abortions are self-managed with help from pills supplied through underground networks. These channels have been sources of ongoing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://texasrighttolife.com/30000-lives-lost-the-hidden-reality-of-abortions-in-texas/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 frustration}}}\uc2  for anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists who see the mail-order route as a final loophole that needs closing.\par \par \uc2 Texas Republicans pre-filed several bills to target pills. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://capitol.texas.gov/BillLookup/History.aspx?LegSess=89R&Bill=HB1651"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 One}}}\uc2  would make it a \u8220\'20\'1Cdeceptive trade practice\u8221\'20\'1D to send pills via mail without a prescription from an in-state doctor after an in-person exam. Similar to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/14/louisiana-abortion-pills-dangerous-substances-list"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 measure in Louisiana}}}\uc2  that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/01/louisiana-abortion-pills"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 doctors warn}}}\uc2  will delay life-saving care, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://capitol.texas.gov/BillLookup/History.aspx?LegSess=89R&Bill=HB1339"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 another}}}\uc2  would reclassify \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  drugs as dangerous \u8220\'20\'1Ccontrolled substances\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Yet {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://capitol.texas.gov/BillLookup/History.aspx?LegSess=89R&Bill=HB991"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 another bill}}}\uc2  would allow citizens to file lawsuits that force internet service providers to block websites that host \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  funds \u8211\'20\'13 organizations that help people seeking \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  travel out of state \u8211\'20\'13 or provide information about obtaining \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills. The bill specifically names groups that offer \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication through the mail, including Aid Access, Plan C and Hey Jane.\par \par \uc2 That bill seeks to use a novel enforcement mechanism written into the 2021 ban \u8211\'20\'13 termed a \u8220\'20\'1Cprivate bounty-hunter scheme\u8221\'20\'1D by the supreme court justice \uc2 Sonia Sotomayor\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 which allowed citizens to sue anyone they suspected of facilitating an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CIt also brings up the issue of Texas potentially projecting its power outside of state lines to regulate speech about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and that could get very complicated,\u8221\'20\'1D said Mary Ziegler, law professor at \uc2 University of California-Davis\uc2  and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law historian.\par \par \uc2 Emboldened by the incoming Trump administration, Texas anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  advocates feel optimistic that their plans will come to fruition following a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.texastribune.org/2023/05/11/texas-legislature-abortion/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 relatively quiet}}}\uc2  session on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 2023. But even if some of the bills pass, they will probably be met with court challenges.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWith some of these efforts to block out-of-state \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills by mail the courts will need to first resolve the question of cross-border legal conflicts,\u8221\'20\'1D Ziegler said. \u8220\'20\'1CWhose state laws are going to apply in these scenarios? And that\u8217\'20\'19s going to be messy.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par \uc2 Texas Right to Life says blocking residents from receiving \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -inducing medication is the group\u8217\'20\'19s top priority this year. The influential group is also encouraging men to file wrongful death lawsuits against organizations and doctors that help facilitate their partners\u8217\'20\'19 abortions. Such a suit was filed in March 2023 by Texas resident Marcus Silva {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/mar/11/texas-women-sued-wrongful-death-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 against}}}\uc2  his ex-wife\u8217\'20\'19s friends for allegedly assisting in her medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Silva {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/11/texas-abortion-pills-lawsuit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 quietly dropped}}}\uc2  the case in October.\par \par \uc2 The group says it is working with ministries, \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  recovery groups\u8221\'20\'1D and crisis pregnancy centers around the state to find plaintiffs and that it hopes to file the first such lawsuit by February.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSeveral men around Texas who are fathers of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  victims are very, very interested in holding these individuals accountable. And we are working to enable that,\u8221\'20\'1D said Seago. \u8220\'20\'1CThe ultimate goal is to expose these activists and send a message that they will be held responsible to deter them from operating.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In December, the Texas attorney general, \uc2 Ken Paxton\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/dec/13/texas-abortion-pills-lawsuit-ken-paxton"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sued a New York doctor}}}\uc2  for allegedly mailing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills to a Texas woman, setting up a battle that tests the endurance of shield laws.\par \par \uc2 This session, Paxton could get a boost in his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/dec/12/texas-abortion-ken-paxton-kate-cox"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 crusade to criminalize}}}\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  with another bill, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://capitol.texas.gov/BillLookup/History.aspx?LegSess=89R&Bill=HB1004"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HB 1004}}}\uc2 , which would empower the AG to unilaterally prosecute \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related offenses.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Democrats have filed bills to help doctors navigate the law by clarifying the medical exceptions to the state\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans and allowing them to use their {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://capitol.texas.gov/BillLookup/History.aspx?LegSess=89R&Bill=HB257"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 best medical judgment}}}\uc2  when treating patients. They have also suggested measures to carve out {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://capitol.texas.gov/BillLookup/History.aspx?LegSess=89R&Bill=HB395"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rape and incest exceptions}}}\uc2  in Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law.\par \par \uc2 Neither bill is expected to pass as the legislature is under Republican control.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250114el1e0020h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
