\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 New Mexico supreme court strikes down local  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  pill restrictions\b0\par\par\uc2 Guardian staff and agencies \par \uc2 759 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 January 2025\par 15:52 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Justice rules against ordinances in counties and towns on Texas border that sought to limit access to mifepristone\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/newmexico"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New Mexico}}}\uc2  supreme court late on Thursday ruled against several local ordinances in the state that aim to restrict distribution of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  pill.\par \par \uc2 In a unanimous opinion, the court said the ordinances invaded the legislature\u8217\'20\'19s authority to regulate reproductive care.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur legislature granted to counties and municipalities all powers and duties not inconsistent with the laws of New Mexico. The ordinances violate this core precept and invade the legislature\u8217\'20\'19s authority to regulate access to and provision of reproductive healthcare,\u8221\'20\'1D the court wrote in its opinion by the justice Shannon Bacon.\par \par \uc2 It declined to address whether the ordinances violated the state\u8217\'20\'19s constitutional protections.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is legal in New Mexico, which has become a destination for women seeking abortions from Texas, especially, and other states that have banned the procedure following the \uc2 US supreme court{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-overturned-abortion-summary-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ruling in 2022}}}\uc2  ending a woman\u8217\'20\'19s constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and handing powers over the issue to individual states.\par \par \uc2 Following that ruling, leaders of New Mexico\u8217\'20\'19s Roosevelt and Lea counties and the towns of Clovis and Hobbs, all on the Texas border, passed ordinances seeking to stop \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics from receiving or sending mifepristone, a pill taken with another drug to perform a medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and other \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related materials in the mail. Medication abortions account for more than half of all US abortions. Last June the supreme court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/jun/13/supreme-court-abortion-pill-access"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 upheld access}}}\uc2  to the drugs.\par \par \uc2 The ordinances invoked the federal {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/jun/20/comstock-act-democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Comstock Act}}}\uc2 , a 19th-century \u8220\'20\'1Canti-vice\u8221\'20\'1D law against mailing abortifacients, which are drugs that induce \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and said that clinics must comply with the law.\par \par \uc2 Under Roosevelt county\u8217\'20\'19s ordinance, any person other than a government employee could bring a civil lawsuit and seek damages of at least $100,000 for each violation of the Comstock Act.\par \par \uc2 The New Mexico supreme court admonished this, saying that creating a private right of action and damages award was \u8220\'20\'1Cclearly intended to punish protected conduct\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The state attorney general, Ra\u250\'00\'FAl Torrez, praised the court\u8217\'20\'19s ruling on Thursday, saying that the core of the argument was that state laws pre-empted any action by local governments to engage in activities that would infringe on the constitutional rights of citizens.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe bottom line is simply this: \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access is safe and secure in New Mexico,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s enshrined in law by the recent ruling by the New Mexico supreme court and thanks to the work of the New Mexico legislature.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The New Mexico house speaker, Javier Mart\u237\'00\'EDnez, called access to healthcare a basic fundamental right in New Mexico.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt doesn\u8217\'20\'19t take a genius to understand the statutory framework that we have. Local governments don\u8217\'20\'19t regulate healthcare in New Mexico. It is up to the state,\u8221\'20\'1D the Albuquerque Democrat said.\par \par \uc2 Opposition to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  runs deep in New Mexico communities along the border with Texas, however, which has one of the most restrictive bans in the US.\par \par \uc2 But Democrats, who control every statewide elected office in New Mexico and hold majorities in the state house and senate, have moved to shore up access to the service.\par \par \uc2 In 2021, the New Mexico legislature repealed a dormant 1969 statute that outlawed most \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  procedures as felonies, ensuring access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  even after the Roe v Wade reversal.\par \par \uc2 And in 2023, the Democratic New Mexico governor, \uc2 Michelle Lujan Grisham\uc2 , signed a bill that overrides local ordinances aimed at limiting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access and enacted a shield law that protects \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers from investigations by other states.\par \par \uc2 In September, construction began on a state-funded \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive health\b0 \highlight\uc2  and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic in southern New Mexico that will cater to local residents and people who travel from neighboring states.\par \par \uc2 The new clinic should open in 2026 to provide services ranging from medical and procedural abortions to contraception, cervical cancer screenings and education about adoptions.\par \par \uc2 It was not immediately clear whether the ruling can be appealed in federal court. The New Mexico supreme court opinion explicitly declined to address conflicts with federal law, basing its decision solely on state provisions.\par \par \uc2 The Texas-based attorney Jonathan Mitchell, a former Texas solicitor general and architect of that state\u8217\'20\'19s strict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, said he looked forward \u8220\'20\'1Cto litigating these issues in other states and bringing the meaning of the federal Comstock Act to the supreme court of the United States\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Reuters and the Associated Press contributed reporting\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250110el1a0028p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
