\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s appointments signal which Project 2025 goals he might advance first\b0\par\par\uc2 Rachel Leingang \par \uc2 1,570 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 January 2025\par 12:03 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Plans to stretch the law to favor Trump and drive out dissenting voices are expected to begin immediately\par \par \uc2 Despite {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/nov/04/what-is-project-2025-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 disavowing}}}\uc2  Project 2025 on the campaign trail and the people involved with creating it, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has now {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/22/project-2025-trump-picks"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tapped numerous people}}}\uc2  tied to the project for key roles in his administration as he prepares to advance some of its main goals.\par \par \uc2 He acknowledged in December that he agreed with some parts of the project, but didn\u8217\'20\'19t say which, claiming he didn\u8217\'20\'19t read it and didn\u8217\'20\'19t have any part in it. \u8220\'20\'1CThey have some things that are very conservative and very good. They have other things that I don\u8217\'20\'19t like,\u8221\'20\'1D he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://time.com/7201565/person-of-the-year-2024-donald-trump-transcript/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told Time magazine}}}\uc2 . He also said he thought it was \u8220\'20\'1Cinappropriate\u8221\'20\'1D that the project was released ahead of the election and could have derailed his win because \u8220\'20\'1Cthey had some pretty ridiculous things in there\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 A lot of it\u8217\'20\'19s going to be Trump daring Congress and the courts to stop him\par \par \uc2 Christopher Bosso\par \par \uc2 The project is an effort by \uc2 the Heritage Foundation\uc2 , a prominent rightwing thinktank, and more than 100 other conservative organizations. It constitutes a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/14/project-2025-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 900-plus page manifesto}}}\uc2  that details how an incoming president should dismantle features of the government it believes conflict with conservative ideology. The people behind it also put together a database of thousands of potential employees who could staff the next Trump administration and a training program that taught these staffers how to work in the federal government.\par \par \uc2 The first steps of the plan involve amassing more power for the top executive, driving out dissenting voices and stretching the law to favor Trump. Those plans are expected to begin immediately and Trump will also use the justice department to go after his enemies soon after taking office.\par \par \uc2 That power shift enables the other {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/01/project-2025-key-proposals"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 elements of the project}}}\uc2 , which calls for policies that overhaul immigration, restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, remove LGTBQ+ and diversity protections, end climate work, alter employment practices and ramp up deregulation.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA lot of it\u8217\'20\'19s going to be Trump daring Congress and the courts to stop him,\u8221\'20\'1D said Christopher Bosso, a professor of public policy and politics at \uc2 Northeastern University\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The extensive planning by \uc2 the Heritage Foundation\uc2  and other conservative groups for a second Trump administration stands in contrast to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s first win, when the president wasn\u8217\'20\'19t as ready to quickly install his loyalists and launch his policies. This time, the conservative movement is poised to pounce immediately on a pent-up demand of rightwing dreams \u8211\'20\'13 and so is Trump.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CProject 2025 said the quiet parts out loud,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Ben Olinsky\uc2 , senior vice-president of structural reform and governance at the \uc2 Center for American Progress\uc2 , a left-leaning thinktank.\par \par \uc2 The project didn\u8217\'20\'19t just say what it wanted to do, but how it wanted to achieve its goals, he said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt lays out a path to either ignore or flout the law, or to bend the law through its will, and change how things work so that they can get all of these things done. And that\u8217\'20\'19s what makes it even scarier.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 What\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s appointments signal\par \par \uc2 Trump nominated \uc2 Russell Vought\uc2 , an architect of the project and the founder of the Center for Renewing America, as the director of the US office of management and budget, the same role Vought had in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s first administration.\par \par \uc2 Vought wrote a chapter for the project that talks about how the president can consolidate power and use the budget process to make agencies fall in line with his agenda. Both he and Trump rail against the so-called \u8220\'20\'1Cdeep state\u8221\'20\'1D and federal civil servants who staff much of the government.\par \par \uc2 That goal is a major part of Project 2025 and a top priority for Trump: making more federal jobs political appointments. Only about 4,000 federal employees are now political appointees. The rest of the more than 2 million civil servants hold their jobs regardless of party control and develop expertise that keeps critical services functioning. \u8220\'20\'1CSchedule F\u8221\'20\'1D would classify far more roles as policy-related \u8211\'20\'13 about 50,000 more \u8211\'20\'13 giving Trump a huge amount of power to roll out his agenda.\par \par \uc2 Vought attacked the civil service as overly liberal and unaccountable to the people, saying that \u8220\'20\'1Ca President today assumes office to find a sprawling federal bureaucracy that all too often is carrying out its own policy plans and preferences \u8212\'20\'14 or, worse yet, the policy plans and preferences of a radical, supposedly \u8216\'20\'18woke\u8217\'20\'19 faction of the country\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He has also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.vox.com/politics/388393/donald-trump-congress-impoundment-budget-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 advocated for}}}\uc2  using a process called \u8220\'20\'1Cimpoundment\u8221\'20\'1D to withhold funds from agencies or programs even if Congress has appropriated those funds, a practice that would probably draw legal scrutiny but would give Trump more direct budget power to defund things he doesn\u8217\'20\'19t like.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTrump has appointed somebody who he knows is going to carry out Project 2025,\u8221\'20\'1D Bosso said of Vought.\par \par \uc2 Other appointees have direct ties to the project as well. \uc2 Peter Navarro\uc2 , who Trump tapped as a senior counselor on trade and manufacturing, authored a section of the project that makes a case for trade restrictions, part of a dueling chapter on trade plans that includes both free and fair trade positions. By choosing Navarro, Trump doubled down on his plans to use tariffs and trade to get other countries to go along with his ideas.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe stark lesson of this chapter is that America gets fleeced every day in the global marketplace,\u8221\'20\'1D Navarro wrote in the project.\par \par \uc2 The choice speaks to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cgeneral antipathy to free trade, which goes back to his first time around in office\u8221\'20\'1D, and his desire to use \u8220\'20\'1Ctrade as a weapon, even if it has rebound effects on the US economy\u8221\'20\'1D, Bosso said.\par \par \uc2 The first dominoes\par \par \uc2 Expanding political appointments will be an early step for the Trump administration, a key way that will allow him to carry out the rest of his plans.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe ones to watch are the second tier, the ones right below the cabinet-grade people,\u8221\'20\'1D Bosso said. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd if you get a bunch of folks who are competent, who know what they\u8217\'20\'19re doing, and they\u8217\'20\'19re ready to go, and they believe in the project, that\u8217\'20\'19s what\u8217\'20\'19s going to be important.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump will also seek to end or undermine the independence of independent agencies. With the \uc2 FCC\uc2 , for example, he could try to bully them to go after broadcasters\u8217\'20\'19 licenses because he doesn\u8217\'20\'19t like their coverage, Olinsky said. \uc2 Brendan Carr\uc2 , Trump\u8217\'20\'19s nominee to chair the \uc2 Federal Communications Commission\uc2 , wrote the Project 2025 chapter suggesting ways to change the \uc2 FCC\uc2 , including by reining in big tech.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think they plan to run a hardball effort that, I would argue, just ignores or breaks the law, and then forces others to challenge them in the courts,\u8221\'20\'1D Olinsky said.\par \par \uc2 While the justice department isn\u8217\'20\'19t an independent agency, it has in effect been able to independently undertake investigations \u8211\'20\'13 which Trump could stop. Kevin Roberts, \uc2 the Heritage Foundation\uc2  president, has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/01/21/magazine/heritage-foundation-kevin-roberts.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cwe just disagree wholly that the Department of Justice is independent of the president or the executive branch\u8221\'20\'1D. Project 2025 suggests stocking the department with far more political appointees because it has been \u8220\'20\'1Ccaptured by an unaccountable bureaucratic managerial class and radical Left ideologues\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Immigration is a day-one priority for Trump, who has vowed a campaign of mass deportation and a raft of policy changes to block people from entering the country. Project 2025 doesn\u8217\'20\'19t detail how a mass deportation would work, but it does call for stopping migration, halting waitlists for visa programs, ending some visas altogether, raiding worksites and going after cities and states that don\u8217\'20\'19t play along.\par \par \uc2 Presidents have a lot of latitude on immigration policy, Olinsky said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe should expect that Trump will exercise every lever at his disposal to limit legal immigration, to deport folks who have been here for years and to try to end birthright citizenship,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Culture-war policy areas, like protections for LGBTQ+ people and efforts to improve diversity, will probably be reversed quickly once Trump takes office. Project 2025 makes suggestions in nearly every chapter of programs to get rid of these goals, some of which can be done away with by the internal directives.\par \par \uc2 Deregulating industry is another key feature of the project where Trump aligns. Project 2025 includes a raft of deregulation plans and ways government functions can be privatized. This includes minimizing overtime pay for companies, making it harder to regulate toxic chemicals and weakening unions.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe real point is to neuter the federal government in areas of the regulatory state, environmental regulations, health regulations \u8211\'20\'13 the stuff that people don\u8217\'20\'19t think they want until they want it,\u8221\'20\'1D Bosso said.\par \par \uc2 In some areas, it\u8217\'20\'19s not clear if Trump will follow what Project 2025 wants because his own comments conflict with their proposals. On \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , for instance, Trump has largely sidestepped the debate over further restrictions after Roe fell, while the project provides a host of ways to curtail access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medications, add regulatory hoops and increase monitoring of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNotwithstanding the comments that Trump made when it was politically helpful for him to make them, I do think that we\u8217\'20\'19re going to see attacks on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and reproductive care in this administration,\u8221\'20\'1D Olinsky said.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250108el18001jn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
