\par\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 The year in patriarchy: coconut trees, \u8216\'20\'18childless cat ladies\u8217\'20\'19 and crimes against humanity\b0\par\par\uc2 Arwa Mahdawi \par \uc2 1,261 \uc2 words\par \uc2 28 December 2024\par 14:02 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s now time to \u8216\'20\'18hold space\u8217\'20\'19 for everything that happened in 2024 with a list \u8211\'20\'13 so here are 10 of the biggest stories from the year in patriarchy\par \par \uc2 2024 was a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/article/2024/aug/16/demure-tiktok-trend"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 very demure, very mindful}}}\uc2 , very dystopian sort of year. I started {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2023/dec/30/memorable-moments-patriarchy-abortion-taylor-swift"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 last year\u8217\'20\'19s}}}\uc2  annual roundup by noting that it had been the hottest year on record and \u8230\'20\'26 guess what? 2024 has now surpassed 2023 as the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/business/environment/2024-will-be-hottest-year-record-eu-scientists-say-2024-12-09/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hottest year ever}}}\uc2 . Many of the same extreme themes from last year have also persisted: anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists are still trying to roll back \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the US and the horrific situation for women in Iran and Afghanistan has only got worse.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile Gaza is still being destroyed, and \u8211\'20\'13 despite the fact that an increasing number of experts are terming the bombardment a \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.amnesty.org/en/latest/news/2024/12/amnesty-international-concludes-israel-is-committing-genocide-against-palestinians-in-gaza/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 genocide}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 the US is continuing to enable the destruction and much of the world is still continuing to look away. The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2024/mar/22/what-caused-the-civil-war-in-sudan-and-how-has-it-become-one-of-the-worlds-worst-humanitarian-crises"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 civil war in Sudan}}}\uc2 , which started last April, has also spread catastrophically, with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.unwomen.org/en/news-stories/statement/2024/04/a-year-of-suffering-for-sudanese-women-and-girls"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 women and girls}}}\uc2  bearing the brunt of the humanitarian crisis.\par \par \uc2 It wasn\u8217\'20\'19t a bad year for women everywhere. In pop culture, it was (once again) the year of Taylor Swift. The pop sensation\u8217\'20\'19s epic Eras tour finally came to an end in December after a record-breaking {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/music/2024/dec/09/taylor-swifts-eras-tour-smashes-touring-revenue-record-with-more-than-2bn-in-ticket-sales"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $2bn in ticket sales}}}\uc2 . Charli xcx also had a major year and brought us a much-needed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/lifeandstyle/article/2024/jul/16/brat-summer-is-the-long-era-of-clean-living-finally-over"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 slime green Brat summer}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Even the combined star power of Swift (who endorsed her) and Charli xcx (who declared that \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/23/kamala-harris-charli-xcx-brat"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 kamala IS brat}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D), couldn\u8217\'20\'19t help \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  become the first female president of the US, however. Nor could a million {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/culture/article/2024/jul/22/kamala-harris-coconut-tree-meme"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 coconut tree memes}}}\uc2 . But while the US still seems averse to voting for a woman, Mexico\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Claudia Sheinbaum\uc2  became the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/jun/02/mexico-elections-first-female-president-violence"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 country\u8217\'20\'19s first female president}}}\uc2  in a landslide victory. And Haliey Welch (better known {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/03/hawk-tuah-girl-podcast-interview"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 as \u8220\'20\'1Chawk tuah\u8221\'20\'1D girl}}}\uc2  ), became the first woman to parlay a viral joke about oral sex into a lucrative brand empire, including a podcast and merchandising deal, only to get embroiled in a $440mn {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/tech/tech-news/hawk-tuah-girl-says-s-cooperating-lawyers-suit-related-crash-meme-cryp-rcna185049"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cryptocurrency scandal}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 To invoke one of the most memorable phrases of the year: it\u8217\'20\'19s now time to \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/film/2024/nov/28/holding-space-wicked-has-made-the-term-famous-but-what-does-it-mean"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hold space}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D for everything that happened with a list. To round off 2024, here are 10 of the biggest \u8211\'20\'13 and most absurd \u8211\'20\'13 stories from the year in patriarchy:\par \par \uc2 1. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , a legally defined sexual predator, won the US presidency again\par \par \uc2 More {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/15/trump-win-sexual-assault-victims"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 than 27 women}}}\uc2  have accused the incoming president of sexual misconduct, and a jury in a civil case last year found Trump liable for sexually abusing the writer E Jean Carroll. None of that seems to matter to a large percentage of the American public who enthusiastically voted Trump in for his \u8220\'20\'1Crevenge term\u8221\'20\'1D. The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2024/feb/16/donald-trump-organization-legal-woes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 adjudicated fraudster}}}\uc2  is already busy {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/24/trump-cabinet-alleged-sexual-abusers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 filling the White House}}}\uc2  with other people accused of sexual misconduct. Meanwhile his vice-president, JD Vance, can\u8217\'20\'19t stop talking about \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/06/jd-vance-childless-cat-ladies-tim-walz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 childless cat ladies}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D. And Trump\u8217\'20\'19s right-hand man, Elon Musk, is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2024/nov/19/he-has-already-fathered-many-children-now-musk-wants-all-of-the-us-to-embrace-extreme-breeding"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 obsessed}}}\uc2  with Americans having as many children as possible and seems intrigued by the idea that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/article/2024/sep/07/elon-musk-women-testosterone"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 women can\u8217\'20\'19t think freely because of \u8220\'20\'1Clow T\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 . What a time to be alive.\par \par \uc2 2. Access to the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill came under attack in the US\par \par \uc2 Medication abortions now make up {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/19/abortion-increase-2023-data"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more than 60%}}}\uc2  of all US abortions. This has made the common \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill, mifepristone (generally used as part of a two-drug regimen in medication abortions) a major target for anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists. In June the \uc2 US supreme court{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/jun/13/supreme-court-abortion-pill-mifepristone"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rejected an attempt}}}\uc2  to roll back access to the medication, but individual states are still doing their best to make getting hold of the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill difficult. Louisiana, for example, has reclassified mifepristone and misoprostol as \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/01/louisiana-abortion-pills"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 controlled substances}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 3. France enshrined \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a constitutional right\par \par \uc2 The French looked at everything that has happened in the US and, in a historic vote, vowed to give the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/mar/04/france-to-hold-final-vote-on-enshrining-abortion-as-a-constitutional-right"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 full constitutional protection}}}\uc2 . Tr\u232\'00\'E8s bon.\par \par \uc2 4. The \uc2 Taliban\uc2  continued its war on Afghan women\par \par \uc2 Women are being systematically erased from every facet of public life in Afghanistan. This year, among other restrictions, the \uc2 Taliban{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2024/dec/06/taliban-afghanistan-ban-women-training-nurses-midwives-outrageous-act-ignorance-human-rights-healthcare"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 made a move}}}\uc2  to ban women from training as nurses and midwives; banned women from speaking or showing their faces {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/article/2024/aug/26/taliban-bar-on-afghan-women-speaking-in-public-un-afghanistan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 outside their homes}}}\uc2  ; and decided to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2024/mar/28/taliban-edict-to-resume-stoning-women-to-death-met-with-horror"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 resume publicly stoning women}}}\uc2  to death. \uc2 UN\uc2  experts have called the \uc2 Taliban\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s system of discrimination a \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.hrw.org/news/2024/06/11/un-expert-slams-taliban-crimes-against-afghan-women-girls"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 crime against humanity}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19 and, in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/sep/25/taliban-to-be-taken-to-international-court-over-gender-discrimination"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 groundbreaking move}}}\uc2 , the \uc2 Taliban\uc2  will be taken to the international court of justice for gender discrimination.\par \par \uc2 5. Gis\u232\'00\'E8le Pelicot showed the world that \u8216\'20\'18shame must change sides\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 After discovering that her (now ex) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/dec/11/a-rapist-can-be-in-the-family-how-dominique-pelicot-became-one-of-the-worst-sexual-predators-in-history"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 husband of 50 years}}}\uc2  had been drugging her and inviting at least 50, and possibly more than 80, strangers to rape her for almost a decade, Gis\u232\'00\'E8le Pelicot waived her right to anonymity and invited the world into her trial. She was determined, she said, \u8220\'20\'1Cthat things change\u8221\'20\'1D in this \u8220\'20\'1Cmacho, patriarchal society that trivialises rape\u8221\'20\'1D. Dominique Pelicot, 72, was given the maximum 20-year sentence and the French court found all 50 co-accused guilty of sexual offences. Gis\u232\'00\'E8le has become a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2024/dec/19/gisele-pelicot-trial-verdict-france"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 feminist icon}}}\uc2 , inspired millions, and sparked a reckoning with rape culture.\par \par \uc2 6. Paris 2024 was the first Olympics to achieve gender parity\par \par \uc2 When Paris hosted the Olympics in 1924 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/are-the-2024-paris-olympics-gender-equal-that-depends-how-you-measure-it"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 less than 5%}}}\uc2  of the participants were women and they were only allowed to compete in \u8220\'20\'1Cladylike\u8221\'20\'1D sports. A century later the \uc2 International Olympic Committee (IOC)\uc2  declared the 2024 Paris Games the #GenderEqualOlympics. Calling it {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/are-the-2024-paris-olympics-gender-equal-that-depends-how-you-measure-it"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 equal}}}\uc2  is a bit of a stretch, but there was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcolympics.com/news/paris-2024-sets-milestone-first-olympics-achieve-full-gender-parity"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 numerical gender parity}}}\uc2  on the playing field. And there were also a lot of memorable moments: who can forget {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/article/2024/aug/12/raygun-rachael-gunn-paris-olympics-breaking-viral-kangaroo-hop-video"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Raygun\u8217\'20\'19s kangaroo hop}}}\uc2  ?\par \par \uc2 7. Iran announced a \u8216\'20\'18treatment clinic\u8217\'20\'19 for women who defy strict hijab laws\par \par \uc2 The opening of a \u8220\'20\'1Chijab removal treatment clinic\u8221\'20\'1D was announced in November amid a crackdown on women who are considered to be in breach of Iran\u8217\'20\'19s mandatory dress code and will offer \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2024/nov/14/iran-announces-treatment-clinic-for-women-who-defy-strict-hijab-laws"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 scientific and psychological treatment for hijab removal}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D. In other words, it\u8217\'20\'19ll be a prison.\par \par \uc2 8. More women and children killed in Gaza than any other recent conflict\par \par \uc2 An \uc2 Oxfam\uc2  analysis published in September found that more women and children have been killed in Gaza by the Israeli military over the past year than the equivalent period of any other conflict over the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.oxfam.org/en/press-releases/more-women-and-children-killed-gaza-israeli-military-any-other-recent-conflict"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 past two decades}}}\uc2 . According to one estimate, a child is killed every 10 minutes in Gaza and death feels imminent for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/dec/11/death-feels-imminent-for-96-of-children-in-gaza-study-finds"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 96% of children}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 9. Women in Sudan faced systematic sexual violence\par \par \uc2 The civil war in Sudan, which appears to have been significantly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://theconversation.com/sudan-is-burning-and-foreign-powers-are-benefiting-whats-in-it-for-the-uae-238695"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 enabled by the UAE}}}\uc2 , has led to a catastrophic humanitarian crisis and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.un.org/en/story/2024/12/1158511"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 widening famine}}}\uc2 . \uc2 UN\uc2  experts have documented \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2024/10/sudan-un-fact-finding-mission-documents-large-scale-sexual-violence-and"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 staggering}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D amounts of sexual and gender-based violence against girls and women. Men and boys have also been targeted while in detention with sexual violence.\par \par \uc2 10. Moo Deng waddled her way into our hearts\par \par \uc2 Adorable, ungovernable and incredibly moist: the baby pygmy hippo {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/lifeandstyle/2024/dec/26/the-peoples-pygmy-princess-how-moo-deng-captured-the-worlds-hearts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 became a viral sensation}}}\uc2 . She got her own {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.billboard.com/music/pop/moo-deng-hippo-theme-song-listen-1235828572/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dance anthem}}}\uc2  (\u8220\'20\'1CMoodeng boing boing / Boing boing boing boing\u8221\'20\'1D); correctly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/nation/2024/11/05/moo-deng-pygmy-hippo-election-trump-harris-cake/76065982007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 predicted}}}\uc2  the US election; launched a million memes; {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.today.com/popculture/tv/bowen-yang-moo-deng-snl-rcna173165?"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 featured}}}\uc2  on Saturday Night Live; and inspired an enormous amount of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.today.com/shop/moo-deng-best-gifts-rcna173060"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 merchandise}}}\uc2 . Because it\u8217\'20\'19s 2024, her story also got an obligatory crypto twist: the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.yahoo.com/lifestyle/moo-deng-just-got-adoptive-084013927.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ethereum co-founder}}}\uc2 Vitalik Buterin\uc2  donated nearly $294,000 to Moo Deng\u8217\'20\'19s zoo, describing himself as the hippo\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cadoptive father\u8221\'20\'1D. May the little hippo continue to flourish in 2025.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241228ekcs001gv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
