\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Why speech could be a target for the anti- \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  movement in 2025\b0\par\par\uc2 Carter Sherman \par \uc2 916 \uc2 words\par \uc2 27 December 2024\par 14:59 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement is looking at ways to control information about how and where to obtain abortions\par \par \uc2 The next front in the US \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  wars may be what people are allowed to say about it.\par \par \uc2 More than two years after the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  overturned Roe v Wade in the case Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization, US abortions are on the rise, thanks in large part to the spread of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills and travel across state lines. This has infuriated anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  advocates, who have proposed policies to help the incoming Trump administration {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/17/anti-abortion-groups-trump-2025"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 curtail the mailing of \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  pills}}}\uc2  and targeted {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/sep/28/texas-lawyer-abortion-ban-procedure-patient-information"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 individuals and groups}}}\uc2  that help women get out-of-state abortions . In a sign of how the issue is pitting states against one another, Texas earlier this month sued {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/dec/13/texas-abortion-pills-lawsuit-ken-paxton"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a New York-based doctor}}}\uc2  who allegedly provided a telehealth \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to a Texan woman.\par \par \uc2 In an effort to cut off the avenues remaining to people in states with bans, the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement is looking at ways to control information about how and where to obtain abortions. State lawmakers have filed at least two bills for the 2025 legislative session that target \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related speech.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat now matters in a country where a third of the country bans \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and other states do not is the flow of people, the flow of pills and the flow of information,\u8221\'20\'1D said Rachel Rebouch\u233\'00\'E9, an expert in \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive health\b0 \highlight\uc2  law and the dean of \uc2 Temple University\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s law school. \u8220\'20\'1CControlling what people can find out about services that are not legal in their state but are legal somewhere else is part of this larger conversation post-Dobbs.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 One of the 2025 bills, pre-filed in Texas, would make it illegal to \u8220\'20\'1Cprovide information on how to obtain an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -inducing drug\u8221\'20\'1D and to maintain a website that \u8220\'20\'1Cassists or facilitates a person\u8217\'20\'19s effort in obtaining an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -inducing drug\u8221\'20\'1D. It would also force internet service providers to block people from accessing websites run by Aid Access, Plan C and other groups that help people obtain medication abortions, even when they\u8217\'20\'19re doing so through the healthcare system.\par \par \uc2 The second bill, which was pre-filed in New Hampshire, would ban \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  trafficking\u8221\'20\'1D, or the practice of transporting minors for abortions without their parents\u8217\'20\'19 permission, as well as forbid people from \u8220\'20\'1Crecruiting\u8221\'20\'1D minors for having abortions. This kind of language, which appears in model legislation written by the prominent anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  group National Right to Life, has left \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights activists fearful \u8211\'20\'13 especially since two states, Idaho and Tennessee, have already passed laws to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  trafficking and \u8220\'20\'1Crecruiting\u8221\'20\'1D. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is legal in New Hampshire until 24 weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 The language in the bills could have far-reaching consequences. \u8220\'20\'1CThere is no specific meaning to what \u8216\'20\'18recruiting\u8217\'20\'19 is in the law. It could be anything \u8211\'20\'13 like having a conversation with someone, sharing general information, persuading,\u8221\'20\'1D said Kylee Sunderlin, director of legal services at If/When/How, which runs a helpline for people looking for information about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , miscarriage and birth. Sunderlin continued: \u8220\'20\'1CIf totally factual information that I provide to someone through the Repro Legal Helpline in some way persuades them toward the decision to have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , then, yeah, that could definitely be seen as \u8216\'20\'18recruiting\u8217\'20\'19.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Earlier this month, the San Francisco-based ninth US circuit court of appeals {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/dec/02/idaho-abortion-trafficking-law"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ruled to let most of Idaho\u8217\'20\'19s \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  trafficking ban take effect}}}\uc2  but froze the \u8220\'20\'1Crecruiting\u8221\'20\'1D provision, which the judge M Margaret McKeown said would likely curtail speech protected by the first amendment.\par \par \uc2 Elisabeth Smith, director of state policy and advocacy at the \uc2 Center for \b \highlight22\uc2 Reproductive Rights\b0 \highlight\uc2 , believes the attempt to restrict \u8220\'20\'1Crecruiting\u8221\'20\'1D young people is likely a trial balloon for future laws that target people of all ages. \u8220\'20\'1CEvery ban that we have seen on adult access to care started with a ban on youth access to care,\u8221\'20\'1D Smith said.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents have also experimented with recategorizing specific kinds of talk. In 2024, lawmakers in Idaho, Mississippi, Oklahoma and West Virginia introduced bills to limit \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related speech. Three of those bills would have restricted advertising around \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , such as billboards that let people know about out-of-state options. Under US constitutional law, commercial speech \u8211\'20\'13 such as advertising \u8211\'20\'13 is often easier to regulate than political speech.\par \par \uc2 Although the 1975 supreme court case Bigelow v Virginia has protected advertising around \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Harvard Law School lecturer Dessie Otachliska isn\u8217\'20\'19t convinced that it would survive a return to the modern-day, hyper-conservative supreme court.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat opinion is a little bit shaky. There\u8217\'20\'19s ways to overturn it,\u8221\'20\'1D said Otachliska, who has written about {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nyujlpp.org/quorum/otachliska-free-speech-post-dobbs/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 post-Roe threats to \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 -related speech}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CIt could be that there is a pathway where certain advocates are hoping or thinking that if Bigelow goes back in front of the supreme court, that precedent will fall.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A federal court has also temporarily blocked Tennessee\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  trafficking ban. The state has appealed that ruling. Especially if the outcome is different from the appeals court ruling in the Idaho case, the supreme court may decide to step in and rule on the contours of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related speech and what it means to \u8220\'20\'1Crecruit\u8221\'20\'1D a young person for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBecause these are novel laws that are being passed by more and more states, it signals that the issue is not going away,\u8221\'20\'1D Rebouch\u233\'00\'E9 said.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241227ekcr001gt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
