\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Mixed ruling leaves Missouri  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  rights in limbo despite ballot measure\b0\par\par\uc2 Carter Sherman \par \uc2 613 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 December 2024\par 18:06 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Judge said state\u8217\'20\'19s ban \u8216\'20\'18clearly contrary\u8217\'20\'19 to recently passed constitutional amendment but left other laws in place\par \par \uc2 More than two months after Missouri residents voted to add \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights into their state constitution and overturn the state\u8217\'20\'19s ban on the procedure, abortions have not yet resumed in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/missouri"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Missouri}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 and it\u8217\'20\'19s not clear when they will, according to a key \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  official in the region.\par \par \uc2 The day after the election, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/dec/06/missouri-abortion-rights-amendment"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Missouri Planned Parenthood affiliates filed a lawsuit}}}\uc2  asking the court to eliminate a slew of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions that, the affiliates said, made it impossible to perform the procedure. On Friday evening, the Jackson county circuit court judge Jerri Zhang ruled that several restrictions, including the state\u8217\'20\'19s near-total ban, were \u8220\'20\'1Cclearly contrary\u8221\'20\'1D to the state\u8217\'20\'19s new constitutional amendment and could not be enforced.\par \par \uc2 However, Zhang left other laws in place, including a requirement that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics be licensed by the Missouri department of health and senior services. In order to obtain that license, clinics must have extra-large hallways and rooms. \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  called those rules \u8220\'20\'1Cmedically unnecessary\u8221\'20\'1D in court papers and said that many of its facilities do not meet those standards.\par \par \uc2 As long as they are in place, Emily Wales, president of Planned Parenthood Great Plains, which operates in Missouri, is not sure when her clinics will be able to start performing abortions. The organization is now weighing its legal options \u8211\'20\'13 as it may ask Zhang to re-examine her ruling, go to a higher court seeking relief or attempt to apply for a license from the state.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe misperception people may have now is that we could just apply and reopen our doors,\u8221\'20\'1D Wales said. But, she added: \u8220\'20\'1CIt was so weaponized when we had to get licensure from the state. The state would delay. They would force us to litigate to get a license.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Two \uc2 Planned Parenthood\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics had to stop providing the procedure back in 2018 \u8211\'20\'13 years before the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  overturned Roe v Wade in 2022 and allowed Missouri to ban almost all abortions \u8211\'20\'13 because the clinics could not come to licensing agreements with the Missouri state government.\par \par \uc2 Voters in seven states passed pro-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights ballot measures in November, but \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights activists are now in the process of making those measures\u8217\'20\'19 promises real. Because the measures do not automatically strike down \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions, advocates are now hoping that lawsuits or new legislation may be used to do so. In Arizona, the state\u8217\'20\'19s attorney general, Kris Mayes, a Democrat, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/dec/03/arizona-abortion-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has agreed not to enforce}}}\uc2  the state\u8217\'20\'19s 15-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban while litigation over Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s pro-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights ballot measure plays out.\par \par \uc2 Unlike Arizona, however, Missouri\u8217\'20\'19s state government is dominated by Republicans. Despite voters\u8217\'20\'19 support for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, state lawmakers have already {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.kansascity.com/news/politics-government/article296568974.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 filed at least 11 anti-\b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  bills}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI would have been more surprised if they hadn\u8217\'20\'19t,\u8221\'20\'1D Mallory Schwarz, executive director of \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Action Missouri, told the Guardian ahead of Friday\u8217\'20\'19s ruling. \u8220\'20\'1CBut we have an opportunity to look forward. A big goal will be making sure people have access to accurate information, because part of what they\u8217\'20\'19re doing with all of these new attacks is trying to scare people. We know that fear and confusion itself is a barrier to care.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Zhang\u8217\'20\'19s mixed ruling has already left patients confused, according to Wales. After the judge issued her decision, over the weekend, some patients called to ask for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  appointments in Missouri, only to be told that they had to instead go to Kansas, Wales said.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241223ekcn0030e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
