\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Texas sues New York doctor accused of mailing  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  pills across state lines\b0\par\par\uc2 Carter Sherman \par \uc2 760 \uc2 words\par \uc2 16 December 2024\par 17:50 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Lawsuit filed by state attorney general \uc2 Ken Paxton\uc2  against Dr Margaret Carpenter will be first to test power of shield laws\par \par \uc2 The Texas attorney general, \uc2 Ken Paxton\uc2 , has sued a New York doctor over accusations that she mailed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills to a Texas woman in defiance of the state\u8217\'20\'19s ban on the procedure .\par \par \uc2 The lawsuit will test the power of \u8220\'20\'1Cshield laws\u8221\'20\'1D, a post- {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade}}}\uc2  strategy designed to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers and enable access to pills for women in states that have banned \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Filed in Collin county, Texas, and announced on Friday, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.texasattorneygeneral.gov/news/releases/attorney-general-ken-paxton-sues-activist-new-york-doctor-illegally-providing-abortion-drugs-across"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the lawsuit }}}\uc2  alleges that Dr Margaret Carpenter sent \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills to a 20-year-old Texas woman through telemedicine. After the woman sought medical attention for severe bleeding in July, the \u8220\'20\'1Cbiological father of the unborn child\u8221\'20\'1D suspected that she had sought to end her pregnancy without informing him and found the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills, according to the lawsuit.\par \par \uc2 Because Carpenter is based in New York, Paxton\u8217\'20\'19s lawsuit will come up against New York\u8217\'20\'19s shield law, which dictates that officials in the state not cooperate with attempts by other states to sue or prosecute providers who send \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills to people in states that ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Seven other states have passed similar shield laws since the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  overturned Roe.\par \par \uc2 These laws have proven critical to maintaining post-Roe access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . On average, in every month between April and June of 2024, shield laws helped providers send pills to more than 9,700 people who live in states with near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans, six-week bans or restrictions on telemedicine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://societyfp.org/research/wecount/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #WeCount}}}\uc2 , a research project by the Society of Family Planning.\par \par \uc2 This lawsuit will mark the first time shield laws are tested in court, pitting the laws of two states against one another.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis was inevitable,\u8221\'20\'1D said Mary Ziegler, a \uc2 University of California, Davis\uc2 , school of law professor who studies the legal history of reproduction. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is going to be a state-to-state conflict.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Ziegler added: \u8220\'20\'1CThe goal, I think in part, is to intimidate physicians by saying: \u8216\'20\'18We\u8217\'20\'19re coming for you personally.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Mifepristone and misoprostol, the two drugs that the lawsuit accuses Carpenter of mailing, are commonly utilized in US abortions and are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fda.gov/drugs/postmarket-drug-safety-information-patients-and-providers/questions-and-answers-mifepristone-medical-termination-pregnancy-through-ten-weeks-gestation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 safe and effective}}}\uc2  when used to end pregnancies in the first trimester. The lawsuit indicates that the woman\u8217\'20\'19s pregnancy ended at around nine weeks, but it is not clear whether she suffered long-term health consequences.\par \par \uc2 The woman\u8217\'20\'19s degree of involvement in the lawsuit is also not clear. Paxton\u8217\'20\'19s office did not immediately return a request for comment.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn Texas, we treasure the health and lives of mothers and babies, and this is why out-of-state doctors may not illegally and dangerously prescribe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -inducing drugs to Texas residents,\u8221\'20\'1D Paxton said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 Paxton\u8217\'20\'19s lawsuit is asking for a temporary injunction against Carpenter that would stop her from prescribing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills to Texas residents and from practicing telemedicine in Texas, where Carpenter allegedly does not hold a medical license. The lawsuit also asks that Carpenter be fined $100,000 for each violation of Texas law, as well as cover any attorneys\u8217\'20\'19 fees that Texas incurs.\par \par \uc2 Ziegler said that it is not clear whether New York law would protect Carpenter from having to pay those fines if Paxton prevails.\par \par \uc2 New York law also enables Carpenter to argue that Paxton\u8217\'20\'19s lawsuit constitutes \u8220\'20\'1Cunlawful interference with protected rights\u8221\'20\'1D, meaning she could potentially file a lawsuit of her own. If Texas or Carpenter win money through a lawsuit but their respective state courts refuse to force them to pay, the litigation could end in front of the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 , Ziegler said.\par \par \uc2 Carpenter is a founder and co-medical director of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Coalition for Telemedicine, which works to expand access to shield laws and help doctors navigate them. The organization did not immediately reply to requests for comment.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs other states move to attack those who provide or obtain \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care, New York is proud to be a safe haven for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access,\u8221\'20\'1D the New York attorney general, Letitia James, said in a statement after news of Paxton\u8217\'20\'19s lawsuit broke.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe will always protect our providers from unjust attempts to punish them for doing their job and we will never cower in the face of intimidation or threats.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 This article was amended on 16 December 2024 to correct a misspelled name.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241213ekcd002jp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
