\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 As funding dries up, private  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  clinics across the US are closing\b0\par\par\uc2 Carter Sherman \par \uc2 961 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 December 2024\par 17:02 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Since the fall of Roe in 2022, 76 clinics have shuttered and the initial surge of donations is now falling short\par \par \uc2 Providing abortions rarely paid the bills for Kwajelyn Jackson in 2024.\par \par \uc2 As the executive director of Feminist Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Center, an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic in Atlanta, Georgia, Jackson spent the year navigating Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, dwindling financial support for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  patients and soaring inflation. The clinic spent more money than it brought in from providing abortions, especially as Jackson strove to pay her staffers a decent wage and the clinic often subsidized the abortions of patients who could not afford to pay.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEssentially, we are charging about half of what it costs to provide the care,\u8221\'20\'1D Jackson said. \u8220\'20\'1COur ability to maintain payroll and our operating expenses on an ongoing basis was really strained for a portion of 2024. We were sort of living paycheck to paycheck.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Feminist Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Center is still open, but it\u8217\'20\'19s one of the lucky ones. Over the last year, 11 independent \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics closed, bringing the nationwide total of brick-and-mortar indie clinics in the US to 363, according to a report released on Tuesday morning by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Care Network (ACN), a network of independent providers. That\u8217\'20\'19s down from more than 500 in 2012.\par \par \uc2 In the US, \u8220\'20\'1Cindependent\u8221\'20\'1D \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics are those not linked to a hospital or run by \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2 . Their closures can have an outsize impact on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, since independent clinics provide almost 60% of all US abortions, according to the ACN report. More than 60% of the clinics that provide abortions after the first trimester of pregnancy are independently run, as are all of the clinics that perform abortions after 26 weeks. If the US network of independent clinics shrinks further, untold numbers of would-be \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  patients will probably be unable to end their pregnancies.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhether it\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans or extremists outside of the clinic or the financial challenges that come along with having to shift services, move a clinic, comply with new regulations \u8211\'20\'13 clinics have been under an enormous amount of financial pressure,\u8221\'20\'1D said Jay Thibodeau, communications director for the \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Care Network. \u8220\'20\'1CThe relief that they need is not coming right now.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In total, 76 independent \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics have closed since the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  overturned Roe v Wade in 2022 and permitted more than a dozen states to ban almost all abortions.But the closures aren\u8217\'20\'19t limited to states with restrictive laws. Of the 11 clinics that shuttered in the last year, eight were located in states with strong \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections.\par \par \uc2 After Roe fell, millions of dollars in donations gushed into the coffers of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights organizations. But in the years since, much of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/sep/22/us-abortion-funds-run-out-of-money-demand-surges"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 that money has dried up }}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 especially funds going to independent clinics and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  funds, which help patients pay for the procedure and logistical expenses that may surround it, such as travel and lodging.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, patients\u8217\'20\'19 needs have increased. Despite the clinic closures, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/27/post-roe-abortion-rate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rates have risen }}}\uc2  over the last two years, largely because people have traveled across state lines for the procedure or accessed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills through tele-health. Medication abortions \u8211\'20\'13 which now account for roughly two-thirds of US abortions \u8211\'20\'13 require fewer resources to administer and can also be sent through the mail, alleviating the burden on brick-and-mortar clinics.\par \par \uc2 Still, there is no real replacement for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics, which provide surgical abortions when medication is not an option, and other services like ultrasounds and counseling.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs a provider that provides both medication and procedural \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , we know that people need multiple options,\u8221\'20\'1D Jackson said. \u8220\'20\'1CMedication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not for everyone.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Over the summer, as donations slumped, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/newsletters/2024-06-26/abortion-hotline-cuts-services-due-to-lack-of-funds"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the National \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Federation (NAF) announced }}}\uc2  that it was cutting the financial assistance it offered to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  patients. Rather than covering 50% of the cost of an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in most states \u8211\'20\'13 and 100% in some states, including Georgia \u8211\'20\'13 NAF started covering only 30%.\par \par \uc2 A few weeks later, an organization called Resources for \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Delivery ended The Access Fund (TAF), another program that helped pay for abortions, providing about $1m in funding each month, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thenation.com/article/society/perfect-storm-abortion-access/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to the Nation }}}\uc2 . A Resources for \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Delivery staffer declined the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s request for comment on why the organization ended the program. \u8220\'20\'1CAs a policy, we do not provide comments to the press,\u8221\'20\'1D the staffer said in an email.\par \par \uc2 For Feminist Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Center, these policy changes dramatically affected their work.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur patients were basically getting free care,\u8221\'20\'1D Jackson said. \u8220\'20\'1CNow most patients are getting about 30% of the cost of their care covered by NAF funding and then other \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  funds are trying their best to fill in some more of that gap.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Economic forces have made things worse. In part because about half of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  patients live below the federal poverty line, providers have kept the cost of abortions relatively low. But inflation has led the cost of everything else to surge. If Jackson were to charge patients the true cost of performing an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 including the cost of equipment and labor \u8211\'20\'13 she says she would probably have to double the clinic\u8217\'20\'19s prices.\par \par \uc2 Another source of strain is fatigue among would-be donors, more than two years after the fall of Roe . The \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Care Network has, for several years, run a fundraising campaign called Keep Our Clinics, which helps clinics pay for rent, security, legal costs and other services. In 2022, the campaign raised $5m. In 2023, it raised $3m.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe can\u8217\'20\'19t sustain an entire system of healthcare on people donating a little bit at a time,\u8221\'20\'1D Thibodeau said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe need enormous system change.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241211ekcb002pg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
