\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Missouri  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  rights in legal limbo after constitutional protections take effect\b0\par\par\uc2 Carter Sherman \par \uc2 759 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 December 2024\par 19:01 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  affiliates ask for strike down of near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban and other limiting statutes in lawsuit\par \par \uc2 An amendment to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/missouri"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Missouri }}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s constitution protecting the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  took effect late on Thursday, two years after the state banned the procedure \u8211\'20\'13 but abortions have not yet resumed in the state.\par \par \uc2 The day after Missouri voters supported the measure to amend the constitution, \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  affiliates in the state filed a lawsuit asking the court to strike down the state\u8217\'20\'19s near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban as well as a raft of other restrictions that, \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  said, make it impossible to perform the procedure. In a hearing on Wednesday, the groups asked the Jackson county circuit judge Jerri Zhang to quickly issue an order to freeze the restrictions and allow abortions in the state to resume on Friday.\par \par \uc2 However, the judge has not acted, and Missouri \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers remain in legal limbo, caught between contradictory provisions in the state\u8217\'20\'19s constitution and its statutes. Under the new amendment 3, Missouri residents possess a \u8220\'20\'1Cfundamental {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/07/missouri-abortion-rights-ballot-measure-ruled-invalid"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 right to reproductive freedom }}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D, including access to abortions until fetal viability.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think it\u8217\'20\'19s a simple case. I don\u8217\'20\'19t think we are asking for something particularly extraordinary,\u8221\'20\'1D said Emily Wales, president of Planned Parenthood Great Plains in Missouri. \u8220\'20\'1CWe have Missouri providers who travel to Kansas currently to provide care. It\u8217\'20\'19s absolutely their hope to provide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services in their home state. So as soon as we get notice, we will rearrange our plans to ensure that Missourians have access to care.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Even before the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  overturned Roe v Wade in 2022, paving the way for Missouri to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  outright, abortions in Missouri had dwindled dramatically. One Planned Parenthood affiliate had stopped offering the procedure altogether, while the other could only do so at a single clinic, according to \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s lawsuit. This decline was due, the lawsuit alleges, to a series of \u8220\'20\'1Cimpenetrable, onerous and medically unnecessary restrictions\u8221\'20\'1D that are still technically in place \u8211\'20\'13 such as requiring medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  patients to undergo a vaginal exam or mandating that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  patients visit a clinic for counseling, wait 72 hours and then return for the procedure.\par \par \uc2 Without a favorable court order from Zhang, Wales said: \u8220\'20\'1CThere will be too many restrictions on the books that we just can\u8217\'20\'19t actually comply with.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Andrew Bailey, Missouri attorney general, has said that amendment 3 means its near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban is unenforceable. However, other restrictions can remain in place, including the requirement of a \u8220\'20\'1C72-hour reflection period\u8221\'20\'1D, Bailey argued in a recent court filing. Removing those requirements would infringe on women\u8217\'20\'19s right to choose childbirth, he said, which is also included in amendment 3\u8217\'20\'19s guarantee of \u8220\'20\'1Creproductive freedom\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRegulations that ensure individuals have adequate time to choose between options \u8211\'20\'13 and will not be racked by regret \u8211\'20\'13 do not \u8216\'20\'18delay\u8217\'20\'19 rights under amendment 3; those regulations foster those decisions,\u8221\'20\'1D he wrote.\par \par \uc2 Bailey argued that, rather than issuing a court order that would impact numerous \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions, Zhang should instead let these restrictions\u8217\'20\'19 futures be decided over the course of litigation.\par \par \uc2 With amendment 3\u8217\'20\'19s impact in question, Missouri state legislators this week proposed a number of potential new restrictions. Lawmakers pre-filed at least 11 anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bills, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.kansascity.com/news/politics-government/article296568974.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a tally by the Kansas City Star }}}\uc2 . The state legislature may take up these bills when it reconvenes in January 2025. Republicans will control the state house, senate and governor\u8217\'20\'19s mansion.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.senate.mo.gov/25info/BTS_Web/Bill.aspx?SessionType=R&BillID=445"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 One pre-filed bill }}}\uc2  would once again ask Missouri voters to amend the state constitution \u8211\'20\'13 this time to outlaw all abortions except in medical emergencies or in cases of rape. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://house.mo.gov/bill.aspx?bill=HB111&year=2025&code=R"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Another }}}\uc2  would endow embryos and fetuses with full rights and protections \u8211\'20\'13 a measure that, if enacted, would grant them a status known as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2024/mar/20/states-fetal-personhood-bill"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cfetal personhood\u8221\'20\'1D }}}\uc2  and in effect ban all \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Yet {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://documents.house.mo.gov/billtracking/bills251/hlrbillspdf/0748H.02I.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 another }}}\uc2  would ask voters to amend the Missouri constitution to, in the future, make it more difficult to pass ballot measures. Under that proposal, ballot measures would have to win both a simple majority of voters and win a majority of voters in more than half of the state\u8217\'20\'19s congressional districts. (Right now, Missouri ballot measures must only win most voters in the state.)\par \par \uc2 Mallory Schwarz, executive director of \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Action Missouri, remains committed to fighting these new efforts.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think these attacks are only going to further enrage voters who just made a very clear decision,\u8221\'20\'1D Schwarz said.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241206ekc6002se\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
