\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Trump team signs agreement on background checks for nominees; lawyers push for hush-money case dismissal \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Maanvi Singh (now); Chris Stein, Erum Salam and Kirsty McEwen (earlier) \par \uc2 9,943 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 December 2024\par 02:00 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This blog has now closed. You can read our Trump hush-money story here\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.59am GMT\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re closing this blog down now. Thanks for reading. You can read the latest story here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/dec/03/trump-team-background-checks"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump team agrees to DoJ background checks for nominees }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.57pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Today's recap\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s transition team belated signed a memorandum of understanding with the \uc2 US Department of Justice\uc2 , which will allow the \uc2 FBI\uc2  to conduct background checks on the president-elect\u8217\'20\'19s nominees. But it remains unclear whether Trump will send all his picks for vetting, given that his team had indicated it would avoid or delay complete background checks, relying instead on internal vetting.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers have asked for a dismissal of the hush-money case, in which he was convicted on 34 felony counts, invoking \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s decision to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/dec/01/joe-biden-pardons-hunter"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pardon his son }}}\uc2 , Hunter, in their argument\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/dec/03/white-house-joe-biden-hunter-pardon-donald-trump-jan-6-rioters-clemency-us-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-674f40918f08e41b41d662df#block-674f40918f08e41b41d662df"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reportedly }}}\uc2  offered the job of deputy secretary of defense to \uc2 Stephen Feinberg\uc2 , a billionaire investor whose firm has taken stakes in companies that do business with the Pentagon.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Pete Hegseth, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s pick to lead the defense department, had multiple affairs while married to his first wife, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.vanityfair.com/news/story/pete-hegseth-first-marriage"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Vanity Fair }}}\uc2  reported. Such behavior could have violated military rules governing Hegseth, who served in the army national guard, and also strike another blow to his reputation as Republican senators consider whether he should lead the Pentagon.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Hegseth is also facing sexual misconduct allegations, as well as allegations of financial mismanagement and aggressive drunkeness at previous workplaces. Republican senator Lindsay Graham said these allegations were \u8220\'20\'1Cdisturbing\u8221\'20\'1D and would be hard to defend.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s pick to lead the \uc2 Drug Enforcement Administration\uc2 , Florida sheriff Chad Chronister, has withdrawn from consideration just two days after being nominated. The sheriff had three decades of experience in law enforcement but was little known outside Florida.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Fallout from Biden\u8217\'20\'19s pardon of his son \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  continues. A Delaware federal judge {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/dec/03/white-house-joe-biden-hunter-pardon-donald-trump-jan-6-rioters-clemency-us-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-674f35da8f08230422ca20b1#block-674f35da8f08230422ca20b1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cited the pardon }}}\uc2  in ending \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s prosecution on charges related to lying to buy a gun, while a top Trump adviser {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/dec/03/white-house-joe-biden-hunter-pardon-donald-trump-jan-6-rioters-clemency-us-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-674f0ee68f08230422ca1e15#block-674f0ee68f08230422ca1e15"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 refused to say }}}\uc2  if the incoming president would opt to pardon himself of recently dismissed charges over allegedly hiding classified documents and plotting to overturn the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Chuck Schumer{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/dec/03/white-house-joe-biden-hunter-pardon-donald-trump-jan-6-rioters-clemency-us-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-674f2ba28f08282fa897eb67#block-674f2ba28f08282fa897eb67"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will continue }}}\uc2  to lead Democrats in the Senate after a closed-door election by his colleagues. He will be the minority leader starting next year, when Republicans take control of the chamber.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Traveling in Angola, Biden was asked about his decision to pardon his son. He {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/dec/03/white-house-joe-biden-hunter-pardon-donald-trump-jan-6-rioters-clemency-us-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-674f23258f08e41b41d6608b#block-674f23258f08e41b41d6608b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 refused to answer }}}\uc2 , and has not said anything else about the decision since making it public on Sunday evening.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Democrats who might seek the presidency in 2028 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/dec/03/white-house-joe-biden-hunter-pardon-donald-trump-jan-6-rioters-clemency-us-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-674f1dd58f08230422ca1f1a#block-674f1dd58f08230422ca1f1a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 did not want to share }}}\uc2  with Politico their views on \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s pardon. Party officials seeking to lead the \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2  were more talkative.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.03pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.52pm GMT\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/mark-zuckerberg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mark Zuckerberg }}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump }}}\uc2 , who have previously engaged in bitter public feuds, are now warming to each other as Zuckerberg seeks to influence tech policy in the incoming administration, Emily Swanson reports:\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Meta\uc2  CEO {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2024/nov/28/mark-zuckerberg-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dined at the president-elect\u8217\'20\'19s Mar-a-Lago club }}}\uc2  in Florida last week, talking technology and demonstrating the company\u8217\'20\'19s camera-equipped sunglasses, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.foxnews.com/video/6365439469112"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fox News }}}\uc2  reported.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C \uc2 Mark Zuckerberg\uc2  has been very clear about his desire to be a supporter of and a participant in this change that we\u8217\'20\'19re seeing all around America,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Stephen Miller\uc2 , a top Trump deputy, told Fox.\par \par \uc2 Meta\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s president of global affairs, \uc2 Nick Clegg\uc2 , agreed with Miller. Clegg said in a recent press call that Zuckerberg wanted to play an \u8220\'20\'1Cactive role\u8221\'20\'1D in the administration\u8217\'20\'19s tech policy decisions and wanted to participate in \u8220\'20\'1Cthe debate that any administration needs to have about maintaining America\u8217\'20\'19s leadership in the technological sphere\u8221\'20\'1D, particularly on artificial intelligence. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/meta"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Meta }}}\uc2  declined to provide further comment.\par \par \uc2 The weeks since the election have seen something of a give-and-take developing between Trump and Zuckerberg, who previously banned the president-elect from \uc2 Instagram\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/facebook"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Facebook }}}\uc2  for using the platforms to incite political violence on 6 January 2021. In a move that appears in deference to Trump \u8211\'20\'13 who has long accused \uc2 Meta\uc2  of censoring conservative views \u8211\'20\'13 the company now says its content moderation has at times been too heavy-handed.\par \par \uc2 Clegg said hindsight showed that \uc2 Meta\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Coverdid it a bit\u8221\'20\'1D in removing content during the Covid-19 pandemic, which Zuckerberg {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2024/08/27/business/mark-zuckerberg-meta-biden-censor-covid-2021/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recently blamed }}}\uc2  on pressure from the Biden administration.\par \par \uc2 Read the full story here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/dec/03/trump-administration-mark-zuckerberg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mark Zuckerberg seeks \u8216\'20\'18active role\u8217\'20\'19 in Trump tech policy  }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.56pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.37pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Even more details are emerging about Pete Hegseth \u8217\'20\'19s alcohol use, with NBC building on earlier reports that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s pick to lead the defense department had issues with drinking excessively in professional environments.\par \par \uc2 NBC reports:\par \par \uc2 Pete Hegseth, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/donald-trump/trump-picks-fox-news-host-pete-hegseth-defense-secretary-rcna179895"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 President-elect Donald Trump\u8217\'20\'19s pick for defense secretary }}}\uc2 , drank in ways that concerned his colleagues at Fox News, according to 10 current and former Fox employees who spoke with NBC News.\par \par \uc2 Two of those people said that on more than a dozen occasions during Hegseth\u8217\'20\'19s time as a co-host of \u8216\'20\'18Fox & Friends Weekend,\u8217\'20\'19 which began in 2017, they smelled alcohol on him before he went on air. Those same two people, plus another, said that during his time there he appeared on television after they\u8217\'20\'19d heard him talk about being hungover as he was getting ready or on set.\par \par \uc2 An earlier report from the New Yorker detailed whistleblower accusations that Hegseth was forced out of leadership roles at two military veterans organizations after allegations of financial mismanagement, aggressive drunkenness and sexist behavior.\par \par \uc2 Earlier today Republican senator \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2  told reporters that allegations of Hegseth\u8217\'20\'19s misconduct were \u8220\'20\'1Cdisturbing\u8221\'20\'1D and would be hard to defend.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSome of these articles are very disturbing. He obviously has a chance to defend himself here. But some of this stuff is going to be difficult. Time will tell,\u8221\'20\'1D Graham said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.50pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.28pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump's pick to lead DEA \u8211\'20\'13 Florida sheriff Chad Chronister \u8211\'20\'13 withdraws\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s nominee to lead the \uc2 Drug Enforcement Administration\uc2 , Florida sheriff Chad Chronister, has withdrawn from consideration.\par \par \uc2 He wrote in a statement:\par \par \uc2 To serve as Administrator of the \uc2 Drug Enforcement Administration\uc2  is the honor of a lifetime. Over the past several days, as the gravity of this very important responsibility set in, I\u8217\'20\'19ve concluded that I must respectfully withdraw from consideration. There is more work to be done for the citizens of Hillsborough County and a lot of initiatives I am committed to fulfilling. I sincerely appreciate the nomination, outpouring of support by the American people, and look forward to continuing my service as Sheriff of Hillsborough County.\par \par \uc2 Chronister, 56, had worked in the sheriff\u8217\'20\'19s office that the Tampa area for more than 30 years, but was little known outside of Florida.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.29pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.17pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Arizona says it will not enforce \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban until related lawsuit plays out\par \par \uc2 Weeks after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/arizona"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Arizona }}}\uc2  voters overwhelmingly passed a ballot measure to enshrine {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  rights into the state constitution, Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s attorney general, Kris Mayes, has agreed that the state will not enforce its 15-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban while a new lawsuit over the law plays out.\par \par \uc2 The lawsuit, filed on Tuesday in Maricopa county superior court on behalf of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/arizona"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Arizona }}}\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers, argues that Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s 15-week ban is now unconstitutional and should be overturned.\par \par \uc2 In legal documents signed by Mayes and that will be filed alongside the lawsuit after the court formally accepts the case, Arizona agreed with providers not to prosecute people under the ban until 30 days after the litigation has wrapped up \u8211\'20\'13 a move that permits \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers in the state to resume performing abortions past 15 weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFor two years, physicians\u8217\'20\'19 hands have been tied when a patient needs to end a pregnancy after 15 weeks, including when they face serious pregnancy complications. But today we can once again provide care to people who want to end their pregnancy,\u8221\'20\'1D Dr Eric Reuss, one of the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers who filed the lawsuit, said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe hope the courts will quickly recognize the harms of Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s ban and strike it down once and for all.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The lawsuit marks the latest effort by advocates to make good on the pro-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights ballot measures {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/nov/05/abortion-ballot-results-tracker-ban-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 passed by seven states }}}\uc2  in the November elections. While these measures amended states\u8217\'20\'19 constitutions to protect or expand \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, they did not actually rewrite pre-existing state laws.\par \par \uc2 Read the full story here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/dec/03/arizona-abortion-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Arizona says it will not enforce \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban until related lawsuit plays out }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.26pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.35pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers had noted that the US justice department was poised to abandon Trump\u8217\'20\'19s federal cases and referred to a departmental memo that bars prosecution of sitting presidents.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs in those cases, dismissal is necessary here,\u8221\'20\'1D their filing argued. \u8220\'20\'1CJust as a sitting president is completely immune from any criminal process, so too is President Trump as president-elect.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Special counsel prosecutors who were pursuing the federal cases against Trump indeed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/25/trump-criminal-case-dismissed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 filed paperwork  }}}\uc2  on 25 November asking for their dismissal \u8211\'20\'13 citing justice department policy that his team has repeatedly invoked.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt has long been the position of the Department of Justice that the United States constitution forbids the federal indictment and subsequent criminal prosecution of a sitting president,\u8221\'20\'1D wrote Molly Gaston, the top deputy for special counsel Jack Smith.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat prohibition is categorical and does not turn on the gravity of the crimes charged, the strength of the government\u8217\'20\'19s proof, or the merits of the prosecution, which the government stands fully behind.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Manhattan prosecutors have argued against dismissal in prior court papers and have suggested a solution that would obviate any concerns about interrupting his presidency \u8211\'20\'13 including \u8220\'20\'1Cdeferral of all remaining criminal proceedings until after the end of defendant\u8217\'20\'19s upcoming presidential term\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.35pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The dismissal pitch came after Judge Juan Merchan\u8217\'20\'19s decision on 22 November to indefinitely postpone the president-elect\u8217\'20\'19s sentencing so lawyers on both sides can argue over its future, given Trump\u8217\'20\'19s victory in the recent presidential election.\par \par \uc2 While Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers have repeatedly pushed for dismissal to no avail, his impending return to the presidency has presented an opportunity for them to make their case once again.\par \par \uc2 Merchan said in his postponement decision that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers had a 2 December deadline to file their argument for dismissal. Prosecutors had a week to submit their response.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers have been calling on Merchan to toss the case outright after he defeated {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris }}}\uc2  on 5 November. In previous papers seeking permission to file a formal dismissal request, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s attorneys said that dismissal was required \u8220\'20\'1Cin order to facilitate the orderly transition of executive power\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Todd Blanche, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s main attorney and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/15/trump-doj-todd-blanche-emil-bove"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  selection for deputy US attorney general }}}\uc2 , as well as Emil Bove, his choice for principal associate deputy attorney general, said that Manhattan district attorney \uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s office \u8220\'20\'1Cappears to not yet be ready to dismiss this politically motivated and fatally flawed case, which is what is mandated by the law and will happen as justice takes its course\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.33pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump lawyers request dismissal of hush-money case\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s lawyers have asked a New York state judge to dismiss the criminal case against him, in which he was convicted of 34 felony counts involving hush money.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers have argued that sentencing in the case would cause \u8220\'20\'1Cunconstitutional impediments\u8221\'20\'1D to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s ability to govern.\par \par \uc2 The lawyers also cited \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s sweeping pardon of his son \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  in their argument. The filing reads:\par \par \uc2 Yesterday, in issuing a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/joe-biden/joe-biden-issue-pardon-son-hunter-biden-rcna182369"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 10-year pardon to Hunter Biden }}}\uc2  that covers any and all crimes whether charged or uncharged, President Biden asserted that his son was \u8216\'20\'18selectively, and unfairly, prosecuted,\u8217\'20\'19 and \u8216\'20\'18treated differently.\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 President Biden argued that \u8216\'20\'18raw politics has infected this process and it led to a miscarriage of justice.\u8217\'20\'19 These comments amounted to an extraordinary condemnation of President Biden\u8217\'20\'19s own DOJ.\par \par \uc2 Already, Judge {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/donald-trump/know-juan-merchan-judge-trump-indictment-case-rcna77611"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Juan Merchan  }}}\uc2  has indefinitely {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/donald-trump/judge-trump-hush-money-case-postpones-sentencing-consider-whether-case-rcna180861"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 postponed }}}\uc2  Trump\u8217\'20\'19s sentencing.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.40pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.25pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump team signs agreement on background checks for nominees\par \par \uc2 The Trump transition team said it has entered a memorandum of understanding with the \uc2 US Department of Justice\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is the next step in the ongoing preparation of senior administration officials for the purpose of serving in President Trump\u8217\'20\'19s administration,\u8221\'20\'1D the statement said. \u8220\'20\'1CThis allows the transition team to submit names for background checks and security clearances.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The brief statement didn\u8217\'20\'19t make clear whether the transition has given up on delaying or privatizing background checks for its cabinet nominees.\par \par \uc2 Earlier, those familiar with the tram\u8217\'20\'19s plans had indicated that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s appointees would skirt full \uc2 FBI\uc2  vetting and delay receiving classified briefings until after Trump was sworn in.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.46pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.52pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump defense secretary nominee admitted to multiple affairs during failed first marriage \u8211\'20\'13 report\par \par \uc2 Pete Hegseth, whom \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  named as his pick to lead the defense department, had multiple affairs while married to his first wife, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.vanityfair.com/news/story/pete-hegseth-first-marriage"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Vanity Fair reports }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Such behavior could have violated military rules governing Hegseth, who served in the army national guard, and also strike another blow to his reputation as Republican senators consider whether he should lead the Pentagon. Other media outlets in recent days {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/dec/02/pete-hegseth-non-profit-allegations"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have reported }}}\uc2  on an accusation of sexual assault against Hegseth, which he denies, as well as claims that he abuses alcohol, mismanaged finances at two charities he was involved in and created a hostile environment for women.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more, from Vanity Fair\u8217\'20\'19s story:\par \par \uc2 Hegseth and Schwarz\u8217\'20\'19s young marriage was short-lived. In December 2008, Schwarz filed for divorce after Hegseth admitted that he cheated on her, according to four sources close to the couple. (APM Reports previously revealed that the infidelity was listed as grounds in the couple\u8217\'20\'19s divorce proceedings.) The sources told me that Hegseth\u8217\'20\'19s infidelity left Schwarz emotionally and psychologically scarred. \u8216\'20\'18She was gaslighted by him heavily throughout their relationship,\u8217\'20\'19 one of the sources told me. \u8216\'20\'18As far as everyone else was concerned, they were viewed by many as this all-American power couple that were making big things for themselves.\u8217\'20\'19 (Schwarz declined to comment. Hegseth\u8217\'20\'19s lawyer, Timothy Parlatore, did not respond to a detailed list of questions for this story, and instead provided a statement that impugned my record as a reporter.)\par \par \uc2 At the time Schwarz filed for divorce, Hegseth was dating Samantha Deering, whom he met while working in Washington, DC, at Vets for Freedom, a group that lobbied to maintain the military\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Ccounterinsurgency\u8221\'20\'1D strategy in Iraq and Afghanistan. In 2010, Hegseth married Deering, with whom he has three kids. In 2017, Deering filed for divorce after Hegseth fathered a child with his Fox News producer Jennifer Rauchet. Hegseth and Rauchet married in 2019 at Trump\u8217\'20\'19s golf course in Colts Neck, New Jersey.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.56pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.31pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Speaking of \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theatlantic.com/politics/archive/2024/12/harris-team-election/680844/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Atlantic published }}}\uc2  a lengthy interview with four top players in the vice-president\u8217\'20\'19s failed campaign for the White House, in which they discuss what went wrong.\par \par \uc2 The general conclusion of the piece is that it would have been difficult for any Democrat to win, given how unhappy much of the United States was with \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s leadership. But the president\u8217\'20\'19s decision to end his bid for a second term just over three months before election day made it unlikely that Harris would be able to turn the situation around \u8211\'20\'13 and indeed, she was not able to.\par \par \uc2 It also underscores that Democrats have work to do to win back voting blocs that once supported the party but appear to be defecting in increasing numbers to the GOP.\par \par \uc2 From the piece:\par \par \uc2 In a race shaped so profoundly by fundamental forces of disaffection with the country\u8217\'20\'19s direction, could anything have changed the outcome? As the Democratic strategist Mike Podhorzer {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.weekendreading.net/p/is-this-what-democracy-looks-like"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has argued }}}\uc2 , more voters might have ranked their hesitations about Trump higher if the Republican-appointed majority on the Supreme Court had not blocked any chance that the former president would face a criminal trial before this election on the charges that he tried to subvert the previous one. Plouffe pointed to another what-if potentially big enough to have changed the result: Biden\u8217\'20\'19s withdrawal from the race much earlier rather than only after his disastrous debate performance in June. If Biden had dropped out last winter, Plouffe argued to me, Democrats could have held a full-fledged primary that would have either produced a nominee more distant from his administration or strengthened Harris by requiring her to establish her independence. Looking back at what contributed to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s victory, Plouffe said pointedly, Biden\u8217\'20\'19s choice not to step aside sooner was \u8216\'20\'18the cardinal sin.\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Even so, Plouffe acknowledged, \u8216\'20\'18I\u8217\'20\'19m not sure, given the headwinds, any Democrat could have won.\u8217\'20\'19 For all the difficulties that the atmosphere created for Harris, the election unquestionably raised warning signs for Democrats that extend beyond dissatisfaction with current conditions. It continued an erosion that is ominous for the party in its support among working-class nonwhite voters, particularly Latino men. And as Flaherty, the deputy campaign manager, told me, the Republican Party\u8217\'20\'19s win powerfully demonstrated that it \u8211\'20\'13 or at least Trump himself \u8211\'20\'13 has built more effective mechanisms for communicating with infrequent voters, especially young men who don\u8217\'20\'19t consume much conventional political news.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.46pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.11pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Something \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  might do once he takes office is pardon people convicted over the January 6 insurrection.\par \par \uc2 Despite that, the justice department is continuing those prosecutions, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.justice.gov/usao-dc/pr/kentucky-man-pleads-guilty-felony-civil-disorder-during-jan-6-capitol-breach"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 just announced }}}\uc2  that Matthew Brent Carver of Kentucky had pleaded guilty to a charge of \u8220\'20\'1Cfelony offense of obstruction of law enforcement during a civil disorder\u8221\'20\'1D in the attack that occurred nearly four years ago. Here\u8217\'20\'19s what the department says Carver did:\par \par \uc2 Around approximately 2:45 pm, law enforcement officers, including members of the U.S. Capitol Police and D.C. Metropolitan Police Department (MPD)\u8212\'20\'14who were performing their official duties at the Capitol on January 6\u8212\'20\'14gathered and formed a police line towards the southern end of the Upper West Terrace. Several minutes later, around 2:47 pm, these officers moved in tandem towards the northern end of the Upper West Terrace in an effort to clear and secure the Upper West Terrace.\par \par \uc2 As the officers advanced, they ordered protesters to \u8220\'20\'1CMove Back! Move Back!\u8221\'20\'1D while they attempted to secure the Upper West Terrace. Around 2:48 pm, as the police line approached the northern end of the Upper West Terrace, Carver emerged from the crowd, assumed an aggressive stance towards the approaching officers, and yelled, \u8220\'20\'1CCome on! Bring it!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Seconds later, Carver approached an MPD officer, grabbed the officer\u8217\'20\'19s baton, and attempted to pull the baton away from the officer and, in doing so, also pulled the officer out of the police line and into the crowd of rioters. Carver was then pulled back into the crowd. Shortly afterward, the police line reformed and continued to push the protesters out of the Upper West Terrace, and Carver eventually made his way out of restricted permitter.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 FBI\uc2  arrested Carver on Jan. 30, 2024, in Kentucky.\par \par \uc2 And a look at how many people have faced charges over the attack:\par \par \uc2 In the 46 months since Jan. 6, 2021, more than 1,561 individuals have been charged in nearly all 50 states for crimes related to the breach of the U.S. Capitol, including more than 590 individuals charged with assaulting or impeding law enforcement, a felony. The investigation remains ongoing.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.18pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.57pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and other top Democrats spent the past four years arguing to voters, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/06/how-trump-won-us-election-president"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 unsuccessfully }}}\uc2 , that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  represents a unique threat to democracy and must never be put in power again.\par \par \uc2 Speaking to \uc2 Newsmax\uc2 , Trump adviser \uc2 Jason Miller\uc2  turned their rhetoric on its head, by arguing that the incoming president will be good for democracy worldwide:\par \par \uc2 Democracy is going to be in such better standing around the world, because you have to have a strong American presidency if you want to have strong democracy around the world, where you see peace in the Middle East, where you get the Russia-Ukraine conflict resolved. And finally, we\u8217\'20\'19re going to get back to where we have peace and prosperity \u8230\'20\'26 for everybody.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.37pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Top adviser says Trump will take 'nonstop' action in first 100 days of new administration\par \par \uc2 Speaking to the conservative \uc2 Newsmax\uc2  network, top \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  adviser \uc2 Jason Miller\uc2  said that the incoming president will take aggressive actions over his first 100 days in office, including cracking down on migrants and spurring more oil and gas drilling.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPresident Trump is \u8230\'20\'26 moving really fast here. I mean, even by Thanksgiving, he had his entire cabinet picked,\u8221\'20\'1D Miller said. He said several top advisers including incoming White House chief of staff Susie Wiles and \u8220\'20\'1Cborder czar\u8221\'20\'1D Tom Homan \u8220\'20\'1Care putting together the executive orders and the policies. As President Trump said, we\u8217\'20\'19re going to drill, baby, drill and secure the border \u8211\'20\'13 those will be day one priorities.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Miller continued:\par \par \uc2 This first 100 days is going to be nonstop. There\u8217\'20\'19s so many things that he\u8217\'20\'19s ready to do. Because, again, we\u8217\'20\'19ve never had a second-term president step in that is ready to go. In fact, we\u8217\'20\'19ve never had a first-term president, never had president in history who\u8217\'20\'19s so ready to go on day one, who knows exactly what they want to do. So, if you voted for President Trump, [you] should be pretty enthused that we\u8217\'20\'19re gonna have the country back on track.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.40pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.20pm GMT\par \par \uc2 As he wrapped up his speech on the outskirts of Angola\u8217\'20\'19s capital, Luanda, a reporter asked \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  for his comment on the declaration of martial law in South Korea.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m just getting briefed on it,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden replied.\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for the national security council {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/dec/03/white-house-joe-biden-hunter-pardon-donald-trump-jan-6-rioters-clemency-us-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-674f4c198f086e00842ca322#block-674f4c198f086e00842ca322"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said earlier }}}\uc2  that they were \u8220\'20\'1Cseriously concerned\u8221\'20\'1D by the declaration, but Biden has not yet commented.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.30pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.01pm GMT\par \par \uc2 As South Korea\u8217\'20\'19s surprise martial law announcement sends shock waves across the country and beyond, another war abroad is also commanding the US\u8217\'20\'19s attention, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/roth-andrew"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Andrew Roth }}}\uc2  reports. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is scrambling to \u8220\'20\'1Cput Ukrainian forces in the strongest possible position\u8221\'20\'1D before \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who has threatened to cut off all aid to Ukraine, assumes the highest level of office in the nation.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/biden-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden administration }}}\uc2  is rushing military equipment to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ukraine }}}\uc2  in a last-ditch effort to shore up the country\u8217\'20\'19s defenses against the Russian invasion before {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump }}}\uc2  assumes the US presidency in January.\par \par \uc2 The newly announced $725m in assistance will include Stinger anti-air missiles, anti-drone weapons, artillery shells and long-range Himars rocket munitions, and anti-armour missiles, as well as spare parts and other assistance to repair damaged equipment from US stocks, the state department said.\par \par \uc2 The new shipments of weapons come as Ukraine is desperately seeking to stabilise its frontlines in both the east of the country, where {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/sep/21/russians-pokrovsk-ukrainian-city-families-agonise-residents-leave"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Russia has made grinding progress toward the crucial logistics town of Pokrovsk }}}\uc2 , as well in the Kursk region of Russia, where {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/sep/13/the-game-continues-evacuating-casualties-and-bombing-bridges-in-kursk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ukrainian forces are bracing themselves for an assault }}}\uc2  by Russian and North Korean troops.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/dec/03/biden-ukraine-russia-trump-military-assistance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden administration announces additional $725m in military assistance to Ukraine }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.10pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.31pm GMT\par \par \uc2 South Korea\u8217\'20\'19s president, \uc2 Yoon Suk Yeol\uc2 , declared martial law today, and accused the country\u8217\'20\'19s main opposition party of being anti-state, North Korea sympathizers.\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for the US national security council told CNN that the US was not given a warning from the South Korean president before he declared martial law.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are seriously concerned by the developments we are seeing on the ground in the ROK [Republic of Korea].\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The US state department\u8217\'20\'19s principal deputy spokesperson Vedant Patel said in a press conference today: \u8220\'20\'1CWe are watching the recent developments in the ROK with grave concern. We are seeking to engage with our Republic of Korea counterparts at every level \u8230\'20\'26 This is an incredibly fluid situation.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 You can read more about this development on our South Korea blog {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2024/dec/03/south-korea-declares-emergency-martial-law-yoon-suk-yeol-north-korea-latest-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2024/dec/03/south-korea-declares-emergency-martial-law-yoon-suk-yeol-north-korea-latest-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Martial law will stay in place until South Korean president lifts it, military officials say \u8211\'20\'13 live }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.37pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.55pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/dec/03/white-house-joe-biden-hunter-pardon-donald-trump-jan-6-rioters-clemency-us-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-674f40918f08e41b41d662df#block-674f40918f08e41b41d662df"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reportedly }}}\uc2  offered the job of deputy secretary of defense to a billionaire investor whose firm has taken stakes in companies that do business with the Pentagon. Should \uc2 Stephen Feinberg\uc2  accept the nomination, it will be the latest to stir controversy, particularly among Democrats concerned that his nominees lack experience, have conflicts of interest or will pursue dangerous policies. Meanwhile, the fallout from \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s pardon of his son \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  continues. A Delaware federal judge {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/dec/03/white-house-joe-biden-hunter-pardon-donald-trump-jan-6-rioters-clemency-us-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-674f35da8f08230422ca20b1#block-674f35da8f08230422ca20b1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cited the pardon }}}\uc2  in ending \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s prosecution on charges related to lying to buy a gun, while a top Trump adviser {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/dec/03/white-house-joe-biden-hunter-pardon-donald-trump-jan-6-rioters-clemency-us-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-674f0ee68f08230422ca1e15#block-674f0ee68f08230422ca1e15"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 refused to say }}}\uc2  if the incoming president would opt to pardon himself of recently dismissed charges over allegedly hiding classified documents and plotting to overturn the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else has happened today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Chuck Schumer{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/dec/03/white-house-joe-biden-hunter-pardon-donald-trump-jan-6-rioters-clemency-us-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-674f2ba28f08282fa897eb67#block-674f2ba28f08282fa897eb67"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will continue }}}\uc2  to lead Democrats in the Senate after a close-door election by his colleagues. He will be the minority leader starting next year, when Republicans take control of the chamber.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Traveling in Angola, Biden was asked about his decision to pardon his son. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/dec/03/white-house-joe-biden-hunter-pardon-donald-trump-jan-6-rioters-clemency-us-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-674f23258f08e41b41d6608b#block-674f23258f08e41b41d6608b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 He refused to answer }}}\uc2 , and has not said anything else about the decision since making it public on Sunday evening.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Democrats who might seek the presidency in 2028 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/dec/03/white-house-joe-biden-hunter-pardon-donald-trump-jan-6-rioters-clemency-us-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-674f1dd58f08230422ca1f1a#block-674f1dd58f08230422ca1f1a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 did not want to share with Politico }}}\uc2  their views on \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s pardon. Party officials seeking to lead the \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2  were more talkative.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.18pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.39pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump offered deputy defense secretary job to billionaire investor in Pentagon-linked firms \u8211\'20\'13 report\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has offered the post of deputy secretary of defense to \uc2 Stephen Feinberg\uc2 , the billionaire co-founder and CEO of investment firm \uc2 Cerberus Capital Management\uc2 , which has stakes in companies that do business with the military, the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  reports.\par \par \uc2 It is not clear if Feinberg accepted the job, the Post reports, and Trump has not yet publicly announced the nomination.\par \par \uc2 Cerberus\uc2  this year {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cerberus.com/media/cerberus-acquires-controlling-interest-in-leading-government-aviation-services-provider-m1/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 disclosed }}}\uc2  an investment in M1 Support Services, which provides military aircraft training and maintenance services. In 2018, \uc2 Cerberus{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cerberus.com/media/cerberus-to-acquire-majority-interest-in-navistar-defense/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 took a majority stake }}}\uc2  in \uc2 Navistar Defense\uc2 , which manufactures military vehicles.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.41pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.14pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Defense secretary nominee Pete Hegseth will be back on Capitol Hill today, meeting with Republican senators who will consider his appointment.\par \par \uc2 Politico reports that he is scheduled to meet \uc2 Eric Schmitt\uc2  of Missouri, \uc2 Ted Budd\uc2  of North Carolina and James Risch of Idaho. Hegseth will also probably run into plenty of reporters who will be asking about his drinking, treatment of women and financial management of two veterans non-profits he reportedly was forced out of.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.16pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.52pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Judge ends gun case against \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  after pardon\par \par \uc2 A judge has ordered an end to \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s prosecution on charges of lying about his drug use when buying a gun, after \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  pardoned him on Sunday.\par \par \uc2 Delaware federal judge Maryellen Noreika terminated the case against \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  in a decision issued today, after a jury found him guilty of three gun-related charges earlier this year. Biden was also pardoned of tax fraud charges leveled against him in California, which he pleaded guilty to. He was awaiting sentencing in both cases before the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/dec/02/joe-biden-hunter-pardon-reaction"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 controversial }}}\uc2  presidential pardon.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more about the gun case:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/11/hunter-biden-gun-charges-verdict"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Hunter Biden found guilty on all three charges in federal gun case }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.31pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s pick for defense secretary, Pete Hegseth, was on Capitol Hill yesterday to meet with senators ahead of his confirmation. He also encountered many reporters who asked him about reports that he drank excessively, and was involved in financial mismanagement. As the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/roberttait"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Robert Tait }}}\uc2  reports, Hegseth did not have much to say to them:\par \par \uc2 Questions continued to dog {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump }}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s nominee to lead the Pentagon, Pete Hegseth, on Monday following reports he was twice ousted from previous organisations he led over financial mismanagement and improper behavior, with reporters asking him directly if he had an alcohol problem.\par \par \uc2 Hegseth, 44, who was visiting Capitol Hill to drum up support for his troubled nomination, did not respond when a journalist {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/jamiedupree/status/1863681372457488860?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw%7Ctwcamp%5Etweetembed%7Ctwterm%5E1863681372457488860%7Ctwgr%5E9d102206ce12377f3e87e4e73b86c8ddc7320fb2%7Ctwcon%5Es1_&ref_url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.thedailybeast.com%2Fpete-hegseth-faces-reporters-on-capitol-hill-asking-if-hes-a-drunk%2F"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 asked }}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1CDo you have an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/alcohol"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 alcohol }}}\uc2  problem?\u8221\'20\'1D as he arrived for a meeting with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republican }}}\uc2  senators.\par \par \uc2 Later, another reporter, from \uc2 CBS\uc2 , buttonholed him in a corridor and asked him: \u8220\'20\'1CWere you ever drunk while traveling on the job?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m not gonna dignify that with a response,\u8221\'20\'1D Hegseth, until recently a Fox News host, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thedailybeast.com/pete-hegseth-faces-reporters-on-capitol-hill-asking-if-hes-a-drunk/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 answered }}}\uc2 , adding: \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m talking to all the senators and I look forward to their discussions.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The New Yorker magazine recently reported whistleblower accusations that Hegseth was forced out of leadership roles in two military veterans organisations following allegations of financial mismanagement, aggressive drunkenness and sexist behaviour.\par \par \uc2 The disclosures have further complicated Hegseth\u8217\'20\'19s chances of winning over Republican senators at confirmation hearings after an earlier revelation that police in California investigated a sexual assault allegation made against him in 2017. The investigation did not result in criminal charges and Hegseth later reached a financial settlement with the woman who made the complaint.\par \par \uc2 The magazine reported that Hegseth had to be carried to his room at a Memorial Day veterans event in Virginia Beach in 2014 after getting \u8220\'20\'1Ctotally sloshed\u8221\'20\'1D, and on another occasion reportedly had to be restrained from joining female dancers on stage at a Louisiana strip club.\par \par \uc2 One witness recounted him shouting \u8220\'20\'1CKill all Muslim, kill all Muslims\u8221\'20\'1D at a bar in Cuyahoga Falls, Ohio, in 2015. The episode was the subject of a written complaint to the Koch-backed group Concerned Veterans for America (CVA), of which Hegseth was then chief executive officer.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/dec/03/pete-hegseth-defense-department-alcohol-use"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Defense head pick Pete Hegseth now dogged by questions over alcohol use }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.32pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.09pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Senate Democrats stick with \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  to lead party\par \par \uc2 Senate Democrats have voted to keep New York\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  as their leader, putting him in a position to steer the opposition to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s policies in Congress\u8217\'20\'19s upper chamber.\par \par \uc2 Schumer has led the Senate since Democrats retook the majority in 2021, but will serve as minority leader beginning next year, after the GOP won back control in the November elections. He will nonetheless remain a powerful figure in the chamber thanks to its filibuster, which blocks the passage of legislation that does not receive at least 60 votes, and will surely be invoked by Democrats to cripple much of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s legislative agenda.\par \par \uc2 Nonetheless, Republicans are expected to attempt to pass legislation addressing taxation, spending and other economic matters using the Senate\u8217\'20\'19s reconciliation procedure, in which bills only require majority support to pass.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what Schumer {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/SenSchumer/status/1863975893670015292"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 had to say }}}\uc2  after Democrats selected him as their leader today in a closed-door election:\par \par \uc2 I am honored and humbled to be chosen by my colleagues to continue leading Senate Democrats during this crucial period for our country. Our caucus has led the way in passing historic legislation that has improved the lives of millions of Americans and we remain laser focused on addressing the most pressing challenges facing our country.\par \par \uc2 As I have long said, our preference is to secure bipartisan solutions wherever possible and look for ways to collaborate with our Republican colleagues to help working families. However, our Republican colleagues should make no mistake about it, we will always stand up for our values.\par \par \uc2 We have a lot of work ahead \u8211\'20\'13 in the Senate and as a country \u8211\'20\'13 and in this upcoming Congress, our caucus will continue to fight for what\u8217\'20\'19s best for America\u8217\'20\'19s working class. Senate Democrats are ready to get to work for you, the American people.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.31pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.51pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The GOP seems set to hold the House of Representatives with a tiny three-seat majority, thanks, in part, to congressional maps drawn to make it easier for Republicans to win.\par \par \uc2 One of the states that played a big role in making that happen was North Carolina, where the GOP used its dominance of state government to enact maps that made it next to impossible for several sitting Democratic members of Congress to win their seats again. One of those Democrats whose districts were gerrymandered out from under them, Wiley Nickel, wrote {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.newsobserver.com/opinion/article296319684.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an op-ed in the Raleigh News & Observer }}}\uc2  in which he reflected on how the state played a major role in handing Republicans the House majority again \u8211\'20\'13 and with it, full control of Congress to enact \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s policies.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what Nickel had to say:\par \par \uc2 Now, with Adam Gray\u8217\'20\'19s apparent victory in California\u8217\'20\'19s 13th District giving Republicans a bare three-seat majority in the US House, it\u8217\'20\'19s clear that gerrymandering in North Carolina tipped the scales in their favor and cost Democrats control of the \uc2 US House of Representatives\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 My district along with the districts of Jeff Jackson and Kathy Manning were turned into safe Republican seats where Democrats had zero chance to win. Had North Carolina sent the three of us back to Washington, under fair maps, then New York Rep \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2  would be our next Speaker of the House with a one seat Democratic majority at 218-217.\par \par \uc2 Let\u8217\'20\'19s be clear. This wasn\u8217\'20\'19t an accident. This was by design. Republicans in Congress can give North Carolina Speaker Tim Moore a big wet kiss when he gets to Washington. Not only did he draw himself a safe Republican seat, but he gave Republicans the three House seats that became the difference in control of Congress.\par \par \uc2 The MAGA Republicans in Raleigh who drew these maps didn\u8217\'20\'19t care about reflecting the will of the people. They cared about power. They used the redistricting process to rig the system, taking advantage of their supermajority to draw lines that would give them three more seats \u8211\'20\'13 no matter what the voters wanted.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.34pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.29pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Reporters traveling with \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in Angola asked him to comment on his decision to pardon \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 , and whether he thought \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  would keep up his outreach to the southern African nation.\par \par \uc2 Biden responded to neither question. He has yet to elaborate on his decision to pardon Hunter, other than the announcement he issued on Sunday evening.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.33pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.07pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Politico wanted to know what leading Democrats who might run for president in 2028 thought of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s decision to pardon his son Hunter.\par \par \uc2 But they would not say. From {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2024/12/02/democrats-hunter-biden-pardon-reaction-00192247"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Politico\u8217\'20\'19s story }}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Govs \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  of California, \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2  of Michigan, Josh Shapiro of Pennsylvania, \uc2 Andy Beshear\uc2  of Kentucky and JB Pritzker of Illinois declined to weigh in or did not respond to requests for comment on the pardon when asked by POLITICO. Neither did Sens Raphael Warnock of Georgia, Amy Klobuchar of Minnesota or \uc2 Cory Booker\uc2  of New Jersey.\par \par \uc2 Contenders to lead the \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2 , which is shaping up to be a major decision for the party as it looks to lead the opposition to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and take back the White House four years from now, were more forthcoming:\par \par \uc2 Several of the Democrats running to lead the national party defended Biden or supported his pardon.\par \par \uc2 Former Gov Martin O\u8217\'20\'19Malley, who is campaigning to head the DNC, said, \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t blame the president for protecting his son from a man who has vowed to persecute his political enemies and their family members. I would do the same for my children.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Ben Wikler, the Wisconsin Democratic Party chair who is also running for the post, suggested that he agreed with Biden\u8217\'20\'19s move, saying that \u8220\'20\'1Cthe president\u8217\'20\'19s statement speaks for itself\u8221\'20\'1D and that \u8220\'20\'1CTrump\u8217\'20\'19s plan to wield federal power through extremists like Kash Patel to attack his political enemies and their families is a frightening reality that the whole country needs to prepare for.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Ken Martin, chair of the Minnesota Democratic-Farmer-Labor Party and another DNC chair candidate, said that he understands Biden\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cinstinct to be a protective father\u8221\'20\'1D as a dad himself and argued that the pardon system should be \u8220\'20\'1Creformed\u8221\'20\'1D so it can\u8217\'20\'19t be used for personal reasons by anyone.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAny Republicans who are expressing outrage today but didn\u8217\'20\'19t blink when \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  pardoned his son-in-law\u8217\'20\'19s father are hypocrites,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Chuck Rocha, a strategist who is considering running for DNC chair, said, \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m very pro-Biden pardon. I\u8217\'20\'19m very anti-lying about it. As somebody who has run a presidential campaign, it would\u8217\'20\'19ve been easy to dodge this.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.12pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.45pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Miller also confirmed to CNN that Trump was sticking by his nominee for defense secretary, Pete Hegseth, despite mounting reports of his poor financial management and history of alcohol abuse.\par \par \uc2 Over the weekend, the New Yorker reported that Hegseth was forced out of his leadership roles at two veteran-focused non-profits amid allegations that he mismanaged finances, showed up for events drunk and created a hostile environment for female staffers.\par \par \uc2 Asked about the reporting on CNN, Miller attacked the New Yorker, and said the president-elect continued to support Hegseth:\par \par \uc2 When it comes to Pete Hegseth, there aren\u8217\'20\'19t any concerns. And we feel very good about his positioning for being confirmed by the Senate\par \par \uc2 \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 Now, with regard to Pete, family conversations sometimes are very tough. And in the case with his mother, his mother did go and take that back and say that she was sorry for that. And right \u8211\'20\'13 I believe that Pete Hegseth is ultimately, when he has a chance to present his case, it\u8217\'20\'19s going to come across very clearly that he\u8217\'20\'19s going to be a great person to lead the DOD, and that he didn\u8217\'20\'19t do anything wrong. Now, again, the letter in \u8220\'20\'1CThe New Yorker,\u8221\'20\'1D or the \u8211\'20\'13 the \u8211\'20\'13 whatever they called it in \u8220\'20\'1CThe New Yorker\u8221\'20\'1D with their piece that they ran, that was basically just innuendo and gossip.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on the latest stories about Hegseth\u8217\'20\'19s conduct:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/dec/02/pete-hegseth-non-profit-allegations"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pete Hegseth forced out of non-profit leadership roles for misconduct \u8211\'20\'13 report }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.23pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Miller was also asked on CNN about Trump\u8217\'20\'19s comments concerning the pardoning of January 6 insurrectionists.\par \par \uc2 On the campaign trail, Trump repeatedly said he would pardon some of those who faced charges or were convicted over the violent attack on the Capitol. After \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  announced he would pardon his son \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 , Trump wrote on Truth Social: \u8220\'20\'1CDoes the Pardon given by Joe to Hunter include the J-6 Hostages, who have now been imprisoned for years? Such an abuse and miscarriage of Justice!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Responding to that comment, Miller told CNN:\par \par \uc2 I want to be careful here and make sure I\u8217\'20\'19m being very direct with you. President Trump has said a number of times on the campaign trail that he\u8217\'20\'19s going to look at each of these cases individually, full stop. That\u8217\'20\'19s what he said. There\u8217\'20\'19s never been a declaration of some \u8211\'20\'13 something bigger, broader. And again, that\u8217\'20\'19s for something for the Department of Justice to go deal with when President Trump takes office again, not for someone who\u8217\'20\'19s a spokesperson from the campaign or transition team.\par \par \uc2 Because, again, the whole point here is, we have to get politics out of the justice system. Justice should apply to everybody equally.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.05pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Top Trump adviser stays mum on if incoming president will pardon himself\par \par \uc2 Jason Miller\uc2 , a top adviser to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , was asked on CNN this morning if the president-elect would pardon himself of federal charges he faced, once he takes office.\par \par \uc2 Trump was indicted last year for allegedly trying to overturn the 2020 election, and for possessing and hiding classified documents. The justice department special counsel leading the prosecution, Jack Smith, last week dropped those charges, thought kept open the possibility that they could be reinstated at a future time.\par \par \uc2 Once he is inaugurated, Trump has the power to issue himself a pardon that could end his legal trouble for good. CNN asked Miller if Trump would do that, and he responded:\par \par \uc2 That would never be something that I would weigh in on. That would be something for the legal team to discuss. And again, President Trump did nothing wrong.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on the quiet ending the to the two high-profile prosecutions of the former-turned-incoming president:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/25/trump-criminal-case-dismissed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Prosecutors drop election interference and documents cases against Trump }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.11pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.45pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  successfully campaigned for the presidency on a promise to stop illegal border crossings, and has leaned heavily on Mexico to prevent US-bound migrants from traversing their territory. From Tapachula, Mexico, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/thomas-graham"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Thomas Graham }}}\uc2  has a look at what that means for migrants:\par \par \uc2 Outside the migration office, Tito subtly pointed out the watchful human smugglers leaning against a wall.\par \par \uc2 They had already tried to sell their services to Tito, who was on his way to the US but, like everyone else there, found himself stuck in Tapachula, a town in southern {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/mexico"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mexico }}}\uc2  that has become a global way station.\par \par \uc2 Tito, who only gave his first name, left Haiti for Chile in 2019, where he set up a company selling wooden pallets and met a Haitian woman, with whom he had a daughter, but the pandemic put him of business. He set out for the US, promising his family he would send money home.\par \par \uc2 That was two years ago.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt hurts me to see these people with their children,\u8221\'20\'1D said Tito, gesturing to a nearby campsite, where grubby little legs poked out of tent flaps. \u8220\'20\'1CI couldn\u8217\'20\'19t bear to have my kid do this with me.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 By the border with Guatemala, Tapachula is where Mexico has strived to contain people heading north, acting as the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/mar/12/mexico-migrants-us-immigration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US\u8217\'20\'19s immigration enforcer }}}\uc2 . Yet president-elect \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is now demanding Mexico do more \u8211\'20\'13 with the threat of a day-one 25% tax on all imports if it fails.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis Tariff will remain in effect until such time as Drugs, in particular Fentanyl, and all Illegal Aliens stop this Invasion of our Country!\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/nov/26/mexico-trump-tariffs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump  }}}\uc2  blustered last week.\par \par \uc2 After a phone call with Mexico\u8217\'20\'19s president, \uc2 Claudia Sheinbaum\uc2 , Trump claimed she had \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/nov/28/donald-trump-mexican-president-meeting-claudia-sheinbaum-tariffs-immigration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 agreed to stop migration through Mexico }}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D and that this was \u8220\'20\'1Ceffectively closing our southern border\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2024/dec/03/trump-mexico-migrants-border-closure"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump threat and mounting dangers in Mexico drive migrant rush towards US }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.20pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s recently announced nominee to lead the \uc2 FBI\uc2 , Kash Patel, has proposed downsizing its Washington headquarters and using its investigative powers to target journalists and enemies of the incoming president.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/playbook"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Politico reports }}}\uc2  that to the Republican senators who will vote on confirming him for the role, none of those promises are disqualifying, at least not yet. Here\u8217\'20\'19s a few of the thoughts they shared with Politico about Patel:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joni Ernst\uc2  of Iowa: \u8220\'20\'1CI do know Kash, and that\u8217\'20\'19s why I think he\u8217\'20\'19s going to be great. We really do need people that will go in and shake up some of these organizations \u8230\'20\'26 I do think he will be able to get confirmed, absolutely.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Susan Collins\uc2  of Maine: \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t know Kash Patel. I had heard his name, but I don\u8217\'20\'19t know his background, and I\u8217\'20\'19m going to have to do a lot of work before reaching a decision on him. In general, I\u8217\'20\'19ve found it\u8217\'20\'19s important to review the background check, the committee work and the public hearing.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Thom Tillis\uc2  of North Carolina: \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m in a presumptive positive position right now. Everybody says what they want to say about him seeking retribution, or have the office of retribution set up and all that. I just don\u8217\'20\'19t see it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.08pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.55pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump to attend ceremony for Notre Dame reopening in Paris\par \par \uc2 Notre Dame Cathedral will reopen in Paris on Saturday with incoming US president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  set to attend the ceremony marking the resurrection of the Gothic masterpiece five years after a devastating fire.\par \par \uc2 The Republican confirmed Monday he had accepted an invitation from French president \uc2 Emmanuel Macron\uc2  to attend the grand re-opening of the 850-year-old edifice which was nearly lost to flames in April 2019.\par \par \uc2 It will be Trump\u8217\'20\'19s first foreign trip since his re-election last month in a political comeback that has set off alarm bells in much of Europe, including in France where Macron regularly tussled with the New York real estate tycoon during his first term.\par \par \uc2 Trump posted on his Truth Social website that Macron had \u8220\'20\'1Cdone a wonderful job ensuring that Notre Dame has been restored to its full level of glory, and even more so. It will be a very special day for all!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The presence of Trump is likely to encourage other world political leaders to attend as they seek to build relations and head off possible disputes over trade and defence before his 20 January inauguration.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.03pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.38pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Angola welcomes Biden\par \par \uc2 Angola wants to expand its collaboration with the United States on security and military initiatives, its president, \uc2 Jo\u227\'00\'E3o Louren\u231\'00\'E7o\uc2 , said on Tuesday, during a visit by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.10pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.38pm GMT\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ve created a visual guide for what could be at stake during the Trump presidency here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/dec/03/what-stake-second-trump-presidency-charts-maps"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 What\u8217\'20\'19s at stake with a second Trump presidency \u8211\'20\'13 in charts and maps }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.05pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Roughly a month after election losses that left Republicans in charge of the White House and both houses of Congress, and saw once-core working class, Latino and female voters slip away, some Democratic officials are trying to explain what happened.\par \par \uc2 Republican \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s victory over Democrat \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  on Nov. 5 was part of a global pattern that saw 80% of incumbent parties lose seats or vote share in 2024, outgoing \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2  chair \uc2 Jaime Harrison\uc2  wrote in a 3 December memo to \u8220\'20\'1Cinterested parties\u8221\'20\'1D obtained by Reuters.\par \par \uc2 Despite falling short, the party\u8217\'20\'19s historic investments in every US state and territory helped prevent \u8220\'20\'1Cwhat could have been a larger red wave\u8221\'20\'1D, Harrison wrote.\par \par \uc2 Democrats raised \u8211\'20\'13 and spent \u8211\'20\'13 more than $1bn just since vice-president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  took over for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  as the candidate in late July. Nonetheless, the campaign finished the election in the red, financially and politically.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAlthough Democrats did not achieve what we set out to do, Trump wasn\u8217\'20\'19t able to capture the support of more than 50% of the electorate and Democrats beat back global headwinds that could\u8217\'20\'19ve turned this squeaker into a landslide,\u8221\'20\'1D Harrison, who has said he will leave his post next year, wrote in the memo. \u8220\'20\'1CTrump\u8217\'20\'19s election is far from a mandate,\u8221\'20\'1D he wrote.\par \par \uc2 Far-right parties have gained ground in Europe, especially with younger voters, and are questioning climate change and pro-immigration policies. In the US, the political right\u8217\'20\'19s gains shocked many Democratic voters and activists who thought a flood of volunteers, fundraising and fresh momentum would help Harris win.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s second presidency could lead to big changes in everything from U.S. health policy to education to oil drilling rules.\par \par \uc2 Some Democrats blamed Biden for not stepping aside earlier. Top Harris advisers, including her campaign chair \uc2 Jen O\u8217\'20\'19Malley Dillon\uc2 , deputy campaign manager \uc2 Quentin Fulks\uc2 , and advisers Stephanie Cutter and David Plouffe pointed to other factors, too, in a recent interview. Americans\u8217\'20\'19 post-Covid economic woes, the short 107-day span of the campaign, and the two hurricanes diverted attention from the whirlwind campaign, they said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.37am GMT\par \par \uc2 Republican senator Ted Cruz has urged US officials to investigate whether European governments have tried to unduly influence the country\u8217\'20\'19s laws around artificial intelligence.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2023/nov/02/five-takeaways-uk-ai-safety-summit-bletchley-park-rishi-sunak"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Britain hosted the world\u8217\'20\'19s first global AI safety summit }}}\uc2  last year, bringing tech executives, world leaders and academics together to discuss a coordinated approach on regulation. Some countries have since set up their own AI safety institutes, which have continued to share expertise across borders.\par \par \uc2 Cruz, who ran against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in the Republican Party\u8217\'20\'19s 2016 race for presidential nominee, is among the party\u8217\'20\'19s most influential senators. He has been a vocal critic of president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s approach to tech regulation, reports Reuters.\par \par \uc2 In a letter addressed to US attorney general \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2 , dated 21 November but only made public on Monday, Cruz said European governments had imposed heavy-handed regulations on American AI companies abroad, and were now trying to steer the direction of AI regulations at home.\par \par \uc2 Cruz described these regulations as \u8220\'20\'1Conerous\u8221\'20\'1D and a product of the \u8220\'20\'1Cradical left\u8221\'20\'1D. \u8220\'20\'1CWhile the Biden-Harris administration may not want to inform the American people of just how closely they are collaborating with foreign governments, at the very least, the American people have a right to know what foreign actors are trying to impose these radical regulations on American companies,\u8221\'20\'1D Cruz wrote.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 European Union\uc2  has led the global charge for regulations tailored to AI technology, having this {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2024/mar/14/what-will-eu-proposed-regulation-ai-mean-consumers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 year passed the AI act }}}\uc2 , the world\u8217\'20\'19s first sweeping set of laws governing the technology.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.38am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.25am GMT\par \par \uc2 My colleague Rachel Savage has more on \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s visit to Angola here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/dec/03/us-history-of-enslavement-in-spotlight-joe-biden-angola"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden to address \u8216\'20\'18horrific history\u8217\'20\'19 of enslavement in America on Angola visit }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.23am GMT\par \par \uc2 Beijing said Tuesday it would restrict exports to the United States of some key components in making semiconductors, after Washington announced curbs targeting China\u8217\'20\'19s ability to make advanced chips.\par \par \uc2 Among the materials banned from export are metals gallium, antimony and germanium, Beijing\u8217\'20\'19s commerce ministry said in a statement that cited \u8220\'20\'1Cnational security\u8221\'20\'1D concerns, reports AFP.\par \par \uc2 Exports of graphite, another key component, will also be subject to \u8220\'20\'1Cstricter reviews of end-users and end-uses\u8221\'20\'1D, the ministry said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTo safeguard national security interests and fulfil international obligations such as non-proliferation, China has decided to strengthen export controls on relevant dual-use items to the United States,\u8221\'20\'1D Beijing said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAny organisation or individual in any country or region violating the relevant regulations will be held accountable according to the law,\u8221\'20\'1D it added.\par \par \uc2 In its own latest curbs, Washington on Monday announced restrictions on sales to 140 companies, including Chinese chip firms Piotech and SiCarrier, without additional permission.\par \par \uc2 They also impact \uc2 Naura Technology Group\uc2 , which makes chip production equipment, according to the \uc2 US Commerce Department\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The move expands Washington\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to curb exports of state-of-the-art chips to China, which can be used in advanced weapons systems and artificial intelligence.\par \par \uc2 The new US rules also include controls on two dozen types of chip-making equipment and three kinds of software tools for developing or producing semiconductors.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.07am GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  announced on Monday he has picked investment banker and Republican mega-donor \uc2 Warren Stephens\uc2  to serve as ambassador to the UK, reports my colleague Alice Herman.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWarren has always dreamed of serving the United States full-time,\u8221\'20\'1D wrote Trump in a social media post. \u8220\'20\'1CI am thrilled that he will now have that opportunity as the top Diplomat, representing the U.S.A. to one of America\u8217\'20\'19s most cherished and beloved Allies.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Stephens is chair, president and CEO of \uc2 Stephens Inc\uc2 , a privately owned financial services firm headquartered in Little Rock, Arkansas, according to the firm\u8217\'20\'19s website.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/dec/02/trump-uk-ambassador-warren-stephens"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump picks Republican mega-donor Warren Stephens as ambassador to UK }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.55am GMT\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  to address history of enslavement in US on Angola visit\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is using the first visit to Angola by a US president to promote Washington\u8217\'20\'19s investments in the country and see a slavery museum where he\u8217\'20\'19ll acknowledge the trafficking of human beings that once linked the two nations\u8217\'20\'19 economies.\par \par \uc2 A centerpiece of his trip is showcasing a US commitment of $3bn for the Lobito Corridor, a railway redevelopment linking Zambia, Congo and Angola that is meant to make it far easier to move raw materials in the continent and for export. The project also has drawn financing from the \uc2 European Union\uc2 , the \uc2 Group of Seven\uc2  leading industrialized nations, a western-led private consortium and African banks, reports Associated Press.\par \par \uc2 The project aims to advance the US presence in a region rich in critical minerals used in batteries for electric vehicles, electronic devices and clean energy technologies and to counter China\u8217\'20\'19s heavy investments in mining and processing African minerals.\par \par \uc2 The US has for years built relations in Africa through trade, security and humanitarian aid. The 800-mile (1,300-kilometer) railway upgrade is a different move and has shades of China\u8217\'20\'19s Belt and Road infrastructure strategy in Africa and other parts of the world.\par \par \uc2 Biden is to fly to the Angolan coastal city of Lobito on Wednesday for a first-hand look at a port terminal that is the Atlantic Ocean outlet for the corridor.\par \par \uc2 White House national security spokesperson John Kirby said the Biden administration \u8220\'20\'1Chas absolutely transformed\u8221\'20\'1D US-Africa relations and that the corridor\u8217\'20\'19s completion is \u8220\'20\'1Cgoing to take years but there\u8217\'20\'19s already been a lot of work put in\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 That means much of it may fall to Biden\u8217\'20\'19s successor, Republican \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who takes office on 20 January. Asked whether the project could proceed without future support from Trump, Kirby said it was \u8220\'20\'1Cour fervent hope that as the new team comes in and takes a look at this that they see the value too, that they see how it will help drive a more secure, more prosperous, more economically stable continent\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.44pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.41am GMT\par \par \uc2 White House: Biden pardoned Hunter to protect him from political opponents\par \par \uc2 The White House said on Monday that president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  pardoned his son \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  in part to protect him from future persecution from political opponents, but his move drew fierce criticism, with some Democrats saying it undermined public trust in the rule of law.\par \par \uc2 Biden, a Democrat whose term ends on 20 January when Republican president-elect \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  takes office, signed an unconditional pardon for \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  on Sunday and said he believed his son had been selectively prosecuted and targeted unfairly by the president\u8217\'20\'19s political opponents.\par \par \uc2 His surprise move was panned by his Republican political opposition, but also by Democrats who said it eroded trust in the judicial system, a concept Biden and his party had used to criticize Trump, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 Hunter was prosecuted for tax offenses and charges related to possession of a firearm after being targeted for years by Republicans in Congress who accused him of making business deals using his father\u8217\'20\'19s name but failed to establish any clear connections.\par \par \uc2 White House spokesperson \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  on Monday defended the president\u8217\'20\'19s action and said Biden believed Hunter faced further grief from his adversaries, who she did not name. Jean-Pierre was among the White House officials who had repeatedly said in the past Biden would not pardon his son.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COne of the reasons the president did the pardon is because they didn\u8217\'20\'19t seem like \u8211\'20\'13 his political \u8230\'20\'26 opponents \u8211\'20\'13 would let go of it. It didn\u8217\'20\'19t seem like they would move on,\u8221\'20\'1D she told reporters on Air Force One during a trip to Angola. \u8220\'20\'1CThey would continue to go after his son. That\u8217\'20\'19s what he believed.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Jean-Pierre stressed this was not the first time a president had pardoned a family member. \uc2 Bill Clinton\uc2  pardoned his half-brother Roger before he left office, and Trump his daughter\u8217\'20\'19s father-in-law, \uc2 Charles Kushner\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  hinted that the pardon would pave the way for clemency for the January 6 rioters. My colleague Robert Tait writes:\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump }}}\uc2  seized on \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/dec/02/joe-biden-hunter-pardon-statement"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pardon }}}\uc2  to drop one of his strongest hints yet that he intends to grant clemency to at least some of the instigators and participants of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-capitol-breach"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 6 attack }}}\uc2  on the US Capitol by a mob trying to overturn his 2020 election defeat.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDoes the Pardon given by Joe to Hunter include the J-6 Hostages, who have now been imprisoned for years? Such an abuse and miscarriage of Justice!\u8221\'20\'1D the US president-elect posted on his Truth Social platform.\par \par \uc2 It was the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/17/trump-pardon-january-6-rioters"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 latest in a series of supportive comments }}}\uc2  by Trump on behalf of those convicted for their part in the onslaught, which resulted in the deaths of five people at the time. Additionally, four police officers involved in trying to beat back the rioters killed themselves in the days and months after the attack.\par \par \uc2 Now the granting of a pardon by the sitting president, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/joebiden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden }}}\uc2 , to his son appears to have been taken by Trump as a fresh justification.\par \par \uc2 The 2021 assault spawned one of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/17/trump-pardon-january-6-rioters"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 biggest criminal investigations }}}\uc2  in US history, resulting in federal charges being filed against nearly 1,500 people. About 1,000 have either been found guilty or pleaded guilty.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/dec/02/hunter-biden-pardon-trump-jan-6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump uses Hunter Biden pardon to hint potential clemency for January 6 insurrectionists }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.13pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241203ekc30013l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
