\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Arizona says it will not enforce  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  ban until related lawsuit plays out\b0\par\par\uc2 Carter Sherman \par \uc2 693 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 December 2024\par 19:37 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Lawsuit filed on behalf of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers argues state\u8217\'20\'19s 15-week ban is unconstitutional\par \par \uc2 Weeks after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/arizona"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Arizona }}}\uc2  voters overwhelmingly passed a ballot measure to enshrine {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  rights into the state constitution, Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s attorney general, Kris Mayes, has agreed that the state will not enforce its 15-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban while a new lawsuit over the law plays out.\par \par \uc2 The lawsuit, filed on Tuesday in Maricopa county superior court on behalf of Arizona \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers, argues that Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s 15-week ban is now unconstitutional and should be overturned.\par \par \uc2 In legal documents signed by Mayes and that will be filed alongside the lawsuit after the court formally accepts the case, Arizona agreed with providers not to prosecute people under the ban until 30 days after the litigation has wrapped up \u8211\'20\'13 a move that permits \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers in the state to resume performing abortions past 15 weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFor two years, physicians\u8217\'20\'19 hands have been tied when a patient needs to end a pregnancy after 15 weeks, including when they face serious pregnancy complications. But today we can once again provide care to people who want to end their pregnancy,\u8221\'20\'1D Dr Eric Reuss, one of the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers who filed the lawsuit, said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe hope the courts will quickly recognize the harms of Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s ban and strike it down once and for all.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The lawsuit marks the latest effort by advocates to make good on the pro-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights ballot measures {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/nov/05/abortion-ballot-results-tracker-ban-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 passed by seven states in the November elections }}}\uc2 . While these measures amended states\u8217\'20\'19 constitutions to protect or expand \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, they did not actually rewrite pre-existing state laws.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions must now be knocked down through litigation or legislation \u8211\'20\'13 processes that take time and whose outcomes are far from guaranteed.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s up to other state actors to do the work of going back and making sure that Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s laws are in line with the really strong protections that are now in place in the constitution,\u8221\'20\'1D Rebecca Chan, staff attorney with the \uc2 American Civil Liberties Union (ACLU)\uc2  Reproductive Freedom Project, said in an interview.\par \par \uc2 The national \uc2 ACLU\uc2 , the ACLU of Arizona, the \uc2 Planned Parenthood Federation of America\uc2 , the Center for \b \highlight22\uc2 Reproductive Rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the law firm \uc2 Perkins Coie\uc2  are representing the plaintiffs in the Arizona lawsuit.\par \par \uc2 Chan continued: \u8220\'20\'1CChallenging the 15-week ban is really the first step to fulfilling the promise of that amendment and we\u8217\'20\'19re really excited to see that ban gone.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Over the last year, Arizona has been at the epicenter of numerous disputes over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. Last spring, the Arizona state supreme court agreed to let a 19th-century near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban \u8211\'20\'13 which dates back to before Arizona became a state \u8211\'20\'13 take effect. That decision unleashed nationwide outrage and led the Republican-controlled state legislature to scramble to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/02/arizona-1864-abortion-ban-repealed-governor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 repeal the 19th-century law }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Outside Arizona, voters also passed pro-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights ballot measures in Colorado, Maryland, Missouri, Montana, Nevada and New York state. \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  affiliates that operate in Missouri have already filed a lawsuit challenging the state\u8217\'20\'19s near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban as well as a slew of other restrictions on the procedure.\par \par \uc2 A hearing in that case is scheduled for Wednesday. If all goes well for \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2 , the reproductive healthcare giant is expected to resume performing abortions in Missouri as soon as this week.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\u8217\'20\'19s incoming administration may undermine the success of these ballot measures, since federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions could override state-level protections. Although Trump has flip-flopped on whether to implement a nationwide ban, activists have already started {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/17/anti-abortion-groups-trump-2025"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 drawing up wishlists of stringent anti-\b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  policies }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere is absolutely the risk of a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban and there are many ways they may try to accomplish that,\u8221\'20\'1D Chan said. \u8220\'20\'1CBut in this present moment, when that has not yet happened \u8211\'20\'13 and at this moment it is not yet guaranteed that it will happen \u8211\'20\'13 we do have this incredible opportunity to really effectuate this very, very strong protection that Arizona voters were emphatic that they wanted.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241203ekc3002jr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
