\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 What\u8217\'20\'19s at stake with a second Trump presidency \u8211\'20\'13 in charts and maps\b0\par\par\uc2 Pamela Duncan, Will Craft, Oliver Milman, Lucy Swan and Heidi Wilson \par \uc2 1,580 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 December 2024\par 17:55 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Conflicts around the globe and domestic policies on immigration and vaccinations are likely to face upheaval\par \par \uc2 The second \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  administration is expected to have a vast impact both domestically and around the world, potentially reshaping everything from the very private \u8211\'20\'13 such as \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in the US \u8211\'20\'13 right through to something as public as the health of the planet itself.\par \par \uc2 While Trump\u8217\'20\'19s policies and their effects will take time to emerge, we can tell a lot about where things are heading by comparing the status quo to current data trends in six key areas, from migration and war through to climate and vaccine uptake.\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Drill, baby, drill\par \par \uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 for fossil fuels\par \par \uc2 Trump is planning a full reversal of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s climate policies, via a swift withdrawal of the US from the Paris climate deal, the downplaying or burying of climate science and the championing of fossil fuel interests.\par \par \uc2 A primary goal will be to unpick the Inflation Reduction Act, Biden\u8217\'20\'19s signature climate bill that Trump has called the \u8220\'20\'1Cgreatest scam in the history of any country\u8221\'20\'1D. A rebate for people to buy electric cars will probably be axed, although as most of the bill\u8217\'20\'19s clean energy spending {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2023/feb/22/climate-spending-republican-states-clean-energy-funding"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 flows to Republican-held districts }}}\uc2  Trump may find resistance in Congress to a full repeal of the IRA.\par \par \uc2 An easier target will be pollution regulations on cars, power plants and factories. Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2024/nov/11/environmental-protection-agency-staff-react-trump-second-term"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is set to shrink the Environmental Protection Agency }}}\uc2 , usher in industry-friendly policies and replace nonpartisan civil servants with political apparatchiks.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDrill, baby drill\u8221\'20\'1D was a repeated Trump mantra on the campaign trail and \uc2 Doug Burgum\uc2 , who will oversee 20% of the US landmass if confirmed as interior secretary, will be tasked with throwing open as much federal land as possible for oil and gas production, including sensitive areas of the Arctic put off-limits by the Biden administration.\par \par \uc2 No country {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/article/2024/jul/24/fossil-fuel-liquified-natural-gas-louisiana"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has extracted as much oil and gas as the US under Biden }}}\uc2 , yet Trump thinks even more should be done. Alternatives such as wind energy, dismissed as \u8220\'20\'1Cdisgusting\u8221\'20\'1D by Trump, will be sidelined and support for communities at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/09/marathon-oil-fire-louisiana-cancer-alley"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 home }}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2024/nov/24/cop29-climate-finance-deal-criticised-travesty-justice-stage-managed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 abroad }}}\uc2  dealing with climate-driven disasters and air pollution will be demolished.\par \par \uc2 All of this will result in more greenhouse gases, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.carbonbrief.org/analysis-trump-election-win-could-add-4bn-tonnes-to-us-emissions-by-2030/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 as much as 4bn tonnes more }}}\uc2 , than if Trump were not president. The US, and the world, will still move towards cleaner forms of energy and chip away at its emissions, but at a slower pace at a time when urgency is crucial.\par \par \uc2 Conflict in\par \par \uc2 Ukraine and the Middle East\par \par \uc2 Trump, who is known for his isolationist tendencies, has claimed he will end the war in Ukraine in \u8220\'20\'1Cone day\u8221\'20\'1D and has repeatedly attempted to block aid packages in Congress.\par \par \uc2 He has given few details of how such a peace would be achieved, although his vice-president, JD Vance, has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/09/13/us/politics/vance-trump-ukraine-russia-war.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 set out a plan }}}\uc2  that critics describe as tantamount to a Russian victory, with Moscow keeping de facto control over Ukrainian territory it occupies now and Ukraine left outside Nato.\par \par \uc2 The Russian-controlled areas of Ukraine are in the south-east, and include partial control of four regions it illegally \u8220\'20\'1Cannexed\u8221\'20\'1D in 2022, the year of its full-scale invasion.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/02/zelenskiy-trump-risks-being-loser-president-if-he-imposes-bad-deal-on-ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 In an interview with the Guardian in May }}}\uc2  the Ukrainian president, Volodymr Zelesnkyy, told Trump that he risked being tagged as a \u8220\'20\'1Closer president\u8221\'20\'1D if he allowed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/russia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Russia }}}\uc2  to win the war. Zelenskyy added that \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s track record suggested Moscow would eventually violate any ceasefire deal and push further into Ukraine, making the US president look \u8220\'20\'1Cvery weak\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Regarding the Middle East, Trump has said he wants the Gaza war to end and has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.timesofisrael.com/trump-told-netanyahu-he-wants-gaza-war-over-by-time-he-enters-office-sources/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reportedly told }}}\uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  it should be concluded before he takes office. But the terms on which he would press for an end to the war and what that would mean for Palestinians in Gaza and the West Bank are unclear. At other times Trump has also said Israel should be allowed to \u8220\'20\'1Cfinish the job\u8221\'20\'1D in Gaza.\par \par \uc2 The most immediate consequence of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s win could be the boost given to the annexationist wing of the Israeli far right, with the installation of figures such as the incoming Israeli ambassador, \uc2 Mike Huckabee\uc2 , who have been vocal about their beliefs \u8211\'20\'13 in defiance of international law \u8211\'20\'13 that the occupied West Bank belongs to Israel.\par \par \uc2 Vaccine collapse\par \par \uc2 With Trump having nominated the outspoken vaccine sceptic \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2  as the secretary of health and human services, and the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/26/nih-trump-bhattacharya-covid"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Covid \u8220\'20\'1Cherd immunity\u8221\'20\'1D proponent Jay Bhattacharya }}}\uc2  to head the \uc2 National Institutes of Health\uc2  (\uc2 NIH\uc2 ) biomedical research institution, there are fears that vaccine coverage could continue to erode. Kindergartners in the US are required to receive four vaccines to prevent against communicable disease, but the proportion of immunised children fell again in the last academic year, to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cdc.gov/schoolvaxview/data/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 below 93% }}}\uc2  for all reported vaccines. By way of example, the \uc2 World Health Organization\uc2  says 95% vaccination coverage for MMR is needed to prevent measles from breaking out.\par \par \uc2 Vaccine uptake in the US has been following a worrying trend among this age group: rates slid in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/vaccinations-kindergarten-exemptions-cdc-1c0f9a196a70491fccf48b9125090de0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 30 states in the last academic year }}}\uc2 , while in 40 states (and DC) exemptions grew. In 14 states, exemptions exceeded 5%: in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.idahoednews.org/top-news/analysis-a-long-troubling-immunization-trend-just-gets-worse/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Idaho }}}\uc2 , for example, where exemption rates have almost doubled in five years, one in seven kindergarteners started school without proof of vaccination.\par \par \uc2 Inflation\par \par \uc2 The cost of eggs and other consumer staples soared during the Biden administration, with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.huffpost.com/entry/trump-price-of-groceries_l_6734c1f5e4b0958bad3dc73b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cegg-flation\u8221\'20\'1D }}}\uc2  cited as a key factor in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s election victory \u8211\'20\'13 though as in other countries, much of the inflation was caused by disruptions to global supply chains caused by Covid lockdowns.\par \par \uc2 Three-quarters of voters interviewed in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2024-elections/exit-polls"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 exit polls }}}\uc2  across 10 key states (Arizona, Florida, Georgia, Michigan, Nevada, North Carolina, Ohio, Pennsylvania, Texas and Wisconsin) said inflation had caused them either \u8220\'20\'1Csevere\u8221\'20\'1D or \u8220\'20\'1Cmoderate\u8221\'20\'1D hardship over the past year: 74% of the former and 51% of the latter voted for Trump.\par \par \uc2 Although he has pledged to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/15/trump-economy-inflation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cquickly\u8221\'20\'1D lower prices }}}\uc2  if elected, experts have said that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s campaign promise to impose tariffs on all foreign goods entering the US could push up inflation {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2024/nov/06/inflation-looks-to-have-secured-trump-win-but-his-policies-mean-higher-prices"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in the short term }}}\uc2  while {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://taxfoundation.org/blog/trump-tariffs-impact-economy/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shrinking the size of the economy }}}\uc2  by reducing work and investment in the longer term.\par \par \uc2 Many other countries, from competitors such as China to allies such as the UK and EU, are nervously assessing the possible impact of these proposed tariffs, which may result in tit-for-tat retaliatory price hikes on US exports.\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Mass deportation\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Though the Biden administration was a high point for the number of deportations over the last decade, Trump has vowed to conduct the largest mass deportation operation in US history \u8211\'20\'13 not by returning people who have recently crossed the border to claim asylum, but by kicking out millions of people who have built entire lives in the US.\par \par \uc2 According to a report from the \uc2 American Immigration Council\uc2 , there are about 11 million people living in the US without legal documentation. To deport them all would come with significant humanitarian and fiscal costs, and cost at least $315bn, the organisation wrote.\par \par \uc2 The scale of such a programme would vastly exceed the combined total of removals (deportations made under a formal court order) and returns (such as when an individual voluntarily leaves when apprehended at the border) that took place under the Obama, Biden or first Trump eras.\par \par \uc2 There were 5m deportations under Obama, from 2009-16; and 2m deportations from 2017-20 under Trump. The Biden administration has deported nearly 5 million people, most through a public health order known as Title 42, which allowed the US to deny people from seeking asylum.\par \par \uc2 But mass deportation as Trump imagines it would involve not just refusing asylum seekers, but kicking out people who have lived in the country for years, even decades \u8211\'20\'13 and in the case of some children their whole lives. It would require forcibly separating people from their families and communities. And operationally it would mean growing the government bureaucracy, not shrinking it \u8211\'20\'13 by hiring more personnel, leasing or acquiring facilities to house people, and expanding the immigration court system.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access\par \par \uc2 In the recent election, 10 states held referendums on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 : seven of them chose to enshrine the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the state constitution, while three \u8211\'20\'13 Nebraska, Florida and South Dakota \u8211\'20\'13 left \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans in place. Somewhat paradoxically, millions of voters engaged in \u8220\'20\'1Csplitting\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 choosing to expand local \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access while also voting for politicians who oppose it.\par \par \uc2 One of them is Trump himself, who proudly takes credit for overturning Roe v Wade by installing three conservative justices on the supreme court. Although he has claimed many different things about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including sometimes saying he would veto any national ban that Congress may pass, many of his closest people are very clear that they intend to restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  even further.\par \par \uc2 Project 2025, the controversial policy manifesto \u8211\'20\'13 many authors of which are current and former Trump officials \u8211\'20\'13 advocates for the federal government to use a 1873 law called the Comstock Act to go after \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related medications such as mifepristone. Project 2025 has also called for the government to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/05/project-2025-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 conduct surveillance on states that allow \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 . The fight over access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related care will only grow over the next four years, including through legal challenges.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241203ekc30018u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
