\par\par \uc2 Global development\par \b \uc2 Beatriz v El Salvador: the  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  case that could set a precedent across Latin America\b0\par\par\uc2 Sarah Johnson \par \uc2 1,190 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 December 2024\par 12:02 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Activists targeted as US-linked hard-right campaigns sow disinformation ahead of inter-American court of human rights ruling on case of woman who was denied \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 2013\par \par \uc2 Earlier this year, Morena Herrera woke up to find that a video about her had been posted on social media. It claimed that the 64-year-old campaigner for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in El Salvador had \u8220\'20\'1Cchased down\u8221\'20\'1D a young woman in hospital and \u8220\'20\'1Cterrorised\u8221\'20\'1D her into seeking an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The young woman was Beatriz, who had been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2023/mar/24/historic-moment-as-el-salvador-abortion-case-fuels-hopes-for-expanded-access-across-latin-america"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 denied an \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  in 2013 }}}\uc2 , even though she was seriously ill and the foetus would not have survived outside the uterus.\par \par \uc2 Beatriz died after being involved in a traffic accident in 2017, but her case is before judges at the inter-American court of human rights {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://jurisprudencia.corteidh.or.cr/en/vid/916956246"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 (IACHR) }}}\uc2 , based in Costa Rica, and could open the way for El Salvador to decriminalise \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It could also set an important precedent in the region: across the Caribbean, South and Central America, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not permitted for any reason {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://reproductiverights.org/maps/worlds-abortion-laws/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in seven countries }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In El Salvador, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  can be punished by up to eight years in prison, and women can even be {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bbc.com/news/world-61798330.amp"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 charged with aggravated homicide }}}\uc2 , which carries a sentence of up to 50 years in prison. Women have been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/10/el-salvador-woman-sentenced-prison-after-miscarriage"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 jailed for miscarriages }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 This is not the first time Herrera has been subjected to such an attack. \u8220\'20\'1CThere have been videos of me on several occasions which tell the government to prosecute me,\u8221\'20\'1D she says. \u8220\'20\'1CThere had already been a campaign saying that I traded in foetal organs \u8211\'20\'13 an absurd thing.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In a video posted last year, Herrera was called an \u8220\'20\'1Cenemy of the state\u8221\'20\'1D, a \u8220\'20\'1Ccolleague of terrorists\u8221\'20\'1D and a \u8220\'20\'1Cfeminazi\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The videos are part of a slew of attacks that activists say has picked up pace in the lead-up to the judgment in the Beatriz case, which is expected soon. In 2023, IM-Defensoras, an organisation that supports female, transgender and non-binary human rights defender human rights defenders in Mexico, Guatemala, Honduras, El Salvador and Nicaragua, documented {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://im-defensoras.org/en/public/ypv383dte60cfbeqap3zfbdt1phn/IM-INFORMEEJECUTIVO24-INGweb.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 188 attacks }}}\uc2  on activists in El Salvador, 78% of which were digital.\par \par \uc2 Almost two-thirds (62%) targeted women campaigning for sexual and \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The majority occurred around the time Beatriz\u8217\'20\'19s case was being heard at the \uc2 IACHR\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA lot of the attacks are aimed at stigmatisation,\u8221\'20\'1D says Lydia Alpizar, co- director of IM-Defensoras. \u8220\'20\'1C[They are] slandering campaigns, fake news, manipulation and question or doubt [activists\u8217\'20\'19] ethical or moral qualities.\par \par \uc2 The attacks are aimed at stigmatisation \u8230\'20\'26 slandering campaigns, fake news, manipulation\par \par \uc2 Lydia Alpizar\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s very clear that anti-rights and anti-gender groups that have affinity with the government are attacking and questioning the point of view of feminists and defenders, and also trying to put pressure on the inter-American court to avoid any kind of advancement.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 On {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://casobeatriz.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 one website }}}\uc2  set up to discredit the case of Beatriz, there are photos of the judges of the \uc2 IACHR\uc2  at the top alongside a heading in white and red capital letters that reads: \u8220\'20\'1CThey want to legalise \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  with a fake case.\u8221\'20\'1D Below is a link to a petition asking the judges not to \u8220\'20\'1Csell out\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The website was created by the Global Center for Human Rights, a US-based {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://slate.com/news-and-politics/2022/06/adopt-your-baby-meme-abortion-protest-roe.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 anti-\b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  organisation }}}\uc2  linked to conservative evangelical groups that opposes what it calls \u8220\'20\'1Cideological colonisation [of] countries rooted in Christian values\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 According to the organisation\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.instagram.com/globalcenterforhumanrights/p/CvN9s1prYfH/?locale=ko&img_index=1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 social media }}}\uc2 , it hosted an event in July 2023 with \uc2 the Heritage Foundation\uc2 , a conservative Washington thinktank, \u8220\'20\'1Chighlighting the use of US taxpayer funds to finance the undermining of fundamental freedoms in Latin America and the Caribbean\u8221\'20\'1D. \uc2 The Heritage Foundation\uc2  is the creator of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/26/what-is-project-2025-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Project 2025 }}}\uc2 , a roadmap for the second Trump presidency that aims to further {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/05/project-2025-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 curb \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights }}}\uc2 , among other things.\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=goTUrKq7GgU"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 video claiming the Beatriz case is \u8220\'20\'1Cfake\u8221\'20\'1D }}}\uc2 , co-produced by the Global Center for Human Rights, was posted in August on the \uc2 YouTube\uc2  channel of Ciudadanos Argentina. This political group is linked to La Libertad Avanza (Freedom Advances), the far-right coalition led by Argentina\u8217\'20\'19s president, \uc2 Javier Milei\uc2 , who wants to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/nov/20/argentina-milei-abortion-womens-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reverse the country\u8217\'20\'19s landmark legalisation of \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  in 2020.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is about to be legalised across all of the American continent if we don\u8217\'20\'19t act urgently,\u8221\'20\'1D it states, and lists various human rights organisations and philanthropic foundations as donors of the \uc2 IACHR\uc2 , questioning its independence. There is a clip in the video of the president of the court, Nancy Hern\u225\'00\'E1ndez, rejecting such claims as \u8220\'20\'1Cabsolutely false\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Back in El Salvador, Mariana Moisa, a women\u8217\'20\'19s rights activist and founder of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://agrupacionciudadana.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Citizens\u8217\'20\'19 Coalition for the Decriminalisation of \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 , which campaigns for women convicted over premature births and obstetric emergencies, says she is subjected to an increasing torrent of abuse every time she posts on X.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI have received a lot of threats and hate speech on social networks, especially on X,\u8221\'20\'1D she says. \u8220\'20\'1CA post can lead to a wave of comments where I\u8217\'20\'19m called a murderer; people accuse me of promoting a crime and there are requests that the attorney general investigate me.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 There is a political interest of the extreme right to oppose women\u8217\'20\'19s rights \u8230\'20\'26 a way to maintain the social order is by oppressing women and girls\par \par \uc2 Mariana Moisa\par \par \uc2 Anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups often gather outside her office to pray, which she sees as an act of intimidation. Her organisation\u8217\'20\'19s website was the target of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://im-defensoras.org/2020/05/alerta-defensoras-sv-la-pagina-web-de-la-agrupacion-ciudadana-por-la-despenalizacion-del-aborto-el-salvador-tuvo-mas-de-13000-intentos-de-sabotaje-para-dar-de-baja-al-sitio/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 13,000 cyber-attacks }}}\uc2  during the hearing of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://reproductiverights.org/case/manuela-v-el-salvador-inter-american-court-of-human-rights/#:~:text=The%20Court%20heard%20oral%20arguments,reproductive%20health%20care%2C%20including%20abortion."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 landmark case }}}\uc2  of Manuela v El Salvador at the \uc2 IACHR\uc2  in 2021.\par \par \uc2 The court ruled that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2021/dec/02/el-salvador-responsible-for-death-of-woman-jailed-after-miscarriage"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 El Salvador violated the human rights of Manuela }}}\uc2 , a woman who was accused of having an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after suffering a miscarriage and sentenced to 30 years in prison. She died two years later, still in detention.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe can clearly see there is a political interest of the extreme right to oppose women\u8217\'20\'19s rights,\u8221\'20\'1D says Moisa. \u8220\'20\'1CNo politician wants their citizens to be truly free, especially not those of the extreme right, so a way to maintain the social order is by oppressing women and girls.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Both Moisa and Herrera worry about the impact of such attacks in the future. They are taking place against a backdrop in El Salvador where a state of emergency to tackle gangs declared by the authoritarian president, \uc2 Nayib Bukele\uc2 , in March 2022 has led to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/article/2024/jul/16/el-salvador-children-detentions-human-rights-watch"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 arbitrary detention of more than 80,000 people }}}\uc2 , ill treatment, torture and deaths in custody.\par \par \uc2 Herrera says: \u8220\'20\'1CI am not going to say that [these attacks do] not affect me \u8230\'20\'26 I worry that at a given moment [authorities] will translate these invented accusations into legal proceedings.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Moisa is also concerned. \u8220\'20\'1CI do not want to be in jail,\u8221\'20\'1D she says. \u8220\'20\'1CBut I know that it is a risk that we run as human rights activists in this context.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe believe this fight is urgent and necessary. If we do not fight, there will be more girls who will continue to be forced to give birth.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241202ekc2001p9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
