\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Number of US abortions fell by only 2% after wave of state bans, CDC report reveals\b0\par\par\uc2 Carter Sherman \par \uc2 928 \uc2 words\par \uc2 27 November 2024\par 20:28 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 First major report from the \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2  tallies \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provision in the post-Roe US\par \par \uc2 Despite the wave of state {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  bans that took effect after the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US supreme court }}}\uc2  overturned {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade }}}\uc2  in June 2022, the number of abortions performed in the US fell by only 2% that year, according to the first major report from the \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2  (CDC) to tally \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provision in the post-Roe United States.\par \par \uc2 The findings in the report, released Wednesday, echo other research that has uncovered that US \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates have surprisingly risen in the years since Roe\u8217\'20\'19s demise. In 2023, the US saw more than 1m abortions, according to the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2 , which tracks abortions and restrictions on the procedure \u8211\'20\'13 the highest number recorded in more than a decade.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt really speaks to a bifurcation of access,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Isaac Maddow-Zimet\uc2 , a \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2  data scientist. \u8220\'20\'1COn one hand, you have many states where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has gotten incredibly difficult to access \u8211\'20\'13 states with total bans, states with six-week bans. Access has gotten much more difficult for people living in those states. And then, on the other hand, you have states with more protective laws where a lot of the things that people have been doing to ameliorate the effects of bans have also increased access to residents of those states.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The CDC report found that US providers performed more than 613,000 abortions in 2022, only a slight drop from the nearly 626,000 abortions performed in 2021. Other metrics of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provision also remained similar to past years. Like in the Roe era, the vast majority of abortions took place at or before nine weeks of pregnancy, according to the CDC. Just over 6% of abortions took place 14 to 20 weeks into pregnancy, and about 1% took place at or after 21 weeks of pregnancy. Women in their 20s accounted for the bulk of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  patients. Almost 60% of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  patients had also previously given birth.\par \par \uc2 However, the CDC report arrives with a number of asterisks. Its data is not comprehensive, since four states \u8211\'20\'13 California, Maryland, New Hampshire and New Jersey \u8211\'20\'13 do not supply the agency with data about the abortions performed in their jurisdictions. (The \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2  research does include these states.) Some states also do not provide the CDC with demographic data on their \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  patients.\par \par \uc2 The CDC report also does not include data on abortions performed outside of the US healthcare system. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/mar/25/self-managed-abortions-avoid-bans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Past research has indicated }}}\uc2  that, in the six months after Roe fell, roughly 26,000 more Americans used pills to induce their own at-home abortions than would have done so if Roe had not collapsed. (Medical experts widely agree that it is safe to self-manage your own \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  using pills early on in pregnancy.)\par \par \uc2 The holes in the CDC data have infuriated some \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/project-2025"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Project 2025 }}}\uc2 , the infamous playbook of conservative policies, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/05/project-2025-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 suggests that }}}\uc2  states lose federal funding if they do not supply the CDC with data on \u8220\'20\'1Cexactly how many abortions take place within its borders, at what gestational age of the child, for what reason, the mother\u8217\'20\'19s state of residence, and by what method\u8221\'20\'1D. It also suggests that the CDC capture data on miscarriages, stillbirths, and \u8220\'20\'1Ctreatments that incidentally result in the death of a child (such as chemotherapy)\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The increased availability of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills almost certainly helps explain why the numbers haven\u8217\'20\'19t fallen. Eight states have enacted \u8220\'20\'1Cshield laws\u8221\'20\'1D that legally protect providers who use telemedicine to mail \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills to people living in states with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans. Between April and June 2024, shield laws enabled providers to offer a monthly average of 7,700 telehealth abortions to people in states with total or six-week bans, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://societyfp.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/10/WeCount-Report-8-June-2024-data.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 data from #WeCount }}}\uc2 , a research project by the Society of Family Planning.\par \par \uc2 Despite the national picture, the number of abortions performed in several states that enacted near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans after Roe fell dropped precipitously, the CDC found. The number of abortions performed in Alabama, which outlawed almost all abortions midway through 2022, dropped by more than half between 2021 and 2022. Meanwhile, states that have become \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  havens started performing far more abortions. Kansas, which borders multiple anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  states, performed almost 5,000 more abortions in 2022 than it did in 2021 \u8211\'20\'13 indicating that women in states with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans are traveling for the procedure.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe estimate that, in 2023, around 168,000 people traveled across state lines to access \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care, which is more than double the number of people who traveled in 2019 or 2020,\u8221\'20\'1D Maddow-Zimet said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt speaks to the way that people are going to really great lengths \u8211\'20\'13 often with a lot of support from a lot of other organizations \u8211\'20\'13 in order to be able to access \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care when they need it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Organizations such as \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  funds have long helped \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  patients pay for travel. However, as outrage over Roe\u8217\'20\'19s demise has died down, many of those funds have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/sep/22/us-abortion-funds-run-out-of-money-demand-surges"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 begun to }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://rewirenewsgroup.com/2024/08/13/following-national-funding-cuts-july-was-pure-hell-for-abortion-funds/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 run out }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thenation.com/article/society/perfect-storm-abortion-access/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 of money }}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 which could, in turn, lead \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provision overall to fall.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have a system right now that\u8217\'20\'19s really reliant on people donating large amounts of money, people working overtime \u8211\'20\'13 both providers and support organizations \u8211\'20\'13 to get people access,\u8221\'20\'1D Maddow-Zimet said. \u8220\'20\'1CWhether that is something that can be sustained in the long run, I think is a big question.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241127ekbr002s2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
