\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 California prepares to fortify state\u8217\'20\'19s  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  access: \u8216\'20\'18Fight for what\u8217\'20\'19s right\u8217\'20\'19\b0\par\par\uc2 Sam Levin in Los Angeles \par \uc2 1,063 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 November 2024\par 13:02 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Lawmaker Mia Bonta outlines new bills package to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  in interview with the Guardian\par \par \uc2 As \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  returns to the White House, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/17/anti-abortion-groups-trump-2025"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 anti-\b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  groups }}}\uc2  are hoping this is their moment.\par \par \uc2 With Republicans controlling both chambers of Congress and the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  governed by a conservative supermajority, activists are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/nov/07/abortion-donald-trump-return-to-white-house"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pushing }}}\uc2  an extreme agenda, including a nationwide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, a prohibition on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills, a \u8220\'20\'1Cfetal personhood\u8221\'20\'1D doctrine that could restrict in vitro fertilization and attacks on contraception.\par \par \uc2 Rights groups are looking to states to safeguard reproductive care, perhaps none more so than California, the most populous and among the bluest in the US.\par \par \uc2 California lawmakers are already preparing. Mia Bonta, a Democratic assemblymember, who chairs the state assembly\u8217\'20\'19s health committee, said she will be introducing a package of bills next month that seeks to expand access to birth control pills, protect emergency \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care at hospitals and enhance maternal health in the state.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen the federal government and president is moving to a motto of \u8216\'20\'18 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2024/nov/13/your-body-my-choice-maga-men"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 your body, my choice }}}\uc2 ,\u8217\'20\'19 I think it\u8217\'20\'19s very important we clarify in the state of California what our bottom line is,\u8221\'20\'1D Bonta said in an interview on Tuesday. \u8220\'20\'1CCalifornia will continue to be a sanctuary state, to push for the recognition of women\u8217\'20\'19s autonomy and our bodily autonomy and to prioritize through our healthcare policy, access to full reproductive care.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Bonta will put her bills forward on 2 December, the start of the \u8220\'20\'1CTrump-proofing\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/07/california-resistance-state-trump-federal-government"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 emergency legislative session }}}\uc2  called by the state\u8217\'20\'19s governor, \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Since 2022, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights are enshrined in California\u8217\'20\'19s constitution and the state in recent years has established itself as a sanctuary for women from other states seeking the procedure. Bonta\u8217\'20\'19s proposals seek to further that trend, she said. Since the supreme court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-overturned-abortion-summary-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturned }}}\uc2  the constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in its 2022 Dobbs decision, states have been free to set policy, with 21 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/jul/29/abortion-laws-bans-by-state"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 banning }}}\uc2  or restricting the procedure. Californians in 2022 passed a measure enshrining \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the state constitution.\par \par \uc2 A first bill is meant to ensure access to emergency reproductive healthcare. It\u8217\'20\'19s a response to a law passed last year in Idaho, which established that abortions in the state are only allowed when the life of the patient is in danger. Advocates fear that under Trump, Idaho\u8217\'20\'19s interpretation could be expanded nationwide, threatening \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care in emergencies.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe wanted to ensure that in California you do not have to go through a heartbreak and health emergency \u8230\'20\'26 should you need access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in emergency rooms,\u8221\'20\'1D Bonta said.\par \par \uc2 Her second bill aims to increase access to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/04/opill-birth-control-pill"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 over-the-counter birth control }}}\uc2  for recipients of Medi-Cal, the state\u8217\'20\'19s Medicaid program.\par \par \uc2 Her third bill seeks to streamline the licensing process for alternative birthing centers, as the number of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://calmatters.org/health/2023/11/california-hospitals-close-maternity-wards/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 labor and delivery wards in some parts of the state has dwindled in recent years }}}\uc2 . In some regions, Bonta said, women in labor could have to travel up to two hours to get care: \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m just blown away that in the United States, in this day and age, that that is the case.\u8221\'20\'1D. Birthing centers are linked to better health outcomes for lower-income women, the lawmaker noted, adding she was looking for ways to make the centers more financially sustainable.\par \par \uc2 While Trump on the campaign trail has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2024/04/08/politics/donald-trump-abortion-2024/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said }}}\uc2  legislation should be left to states and that he would {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/donald-trump-says-he-would-veto-federal-abortion-ban/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 veto }}}\uc2  a national ban, he has repeatedly flip-flopped on the issue. And there are many other ways his administration could unravel rights and access, even in blue states. Project 2025, the rightwing manifesto crafted by his allies, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/nov/07/abortion-donald-trump-return-to-white-house"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 calls for the president }}}\uc2  to roll back the \uc2 FDA\uc2  approval of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills, increase CDC \u8220\'20\'1Csurveillance\u8221\'20\'1D of pregnancy loss and erode federal funding for family planning programs that provide contraception.\par \par \uc2 Bonta said it was important to recognize that access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a right supported by a majority of voters, including many in states that voted for Trump. Missouri, Montana, Arizona and Nevada all {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/nov/05/abortion-ballot-results-tracker-ban-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 favored }}}\uc2  Trump and passed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights measures this month.\par \par \uc2 Safeguarding Californians\u8217\'20\'19 access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is personal for Bonta. In 2022, she revealed she {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/abortion-california-reproductive-rights-da48d0d0b85b5c734c6071498cd29274"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 had an \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  at the age of 21. \u8220\'20\'1CI chose to own my body,\u8221\'20\'1D she said at the time. It\u8217\'20\'19s a decision that helped her break the \u8220\'20\'1Ccycle of poverty in my family\u8221\'20\'1D, she said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt was important to me to be very open about my own health journey,\u8221\'20\'1D she said this week. \u8220\'20\'1CIn this moment when women in other parts of the country are having to go back to considering engaging in a practice that will put their lives at risk, it\u8217\'20\'19s important to be a beacon \u8230\'20\'26 and fight to make sure [they] have the same kind of care that I was afforded. I want to be able to look my daughters in the eye and tell them I\u8217\'20\'19m fighting for their health, their quality of life and that of their children.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Bonta is married to California\u8217\'20\'19s attorney general, \uc2 Rob Bonta\uc2 , who is readying the state\u8217\'20\'19s department of justice to fight a range of possible Trump administration efforts that would restrict civil rights and impede other progressive initiatives in the state. The attorney general has said he is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/08/trump-proof-california-ag"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 prepared to take on those policies }}}\uc2  with litigation and has draft legal briefs ready, including to challenge a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 Trump is expected to push back hard. Bonta said she hoped legislators wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be distracted by culture war rhetoric, and would focus on \u8220\'20\'1Csound policy that can stand up against federal intervention\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 While the conservative leanings of the courts have made that challenge more difficult, she said, \u8220\'20\'1Cour job is to fight for what\u8217\'20\'19s right and and hope the court system \u8230\'20\'26 will not try to legislate through legal rulings and that there will be some modicum of decency in the judiciary.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s hard not to feel like we\u8217\'20\'19re heading into a dystopian state,\u8221\'20\'1D said Bonta. \u8220\'20\'1CThere are a lot of people who are just as scared as I am in this moment \u8230\'20\'26 As a legislator, I have the privilege of being in the halls of power in the state of California. I\u8217\'20\'19m thankful I have the ability to fight.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241122ekbm001xi\par }\par \b \uc2 Search Summary\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9360\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 rst=grdn AND (abortion OR "reproductive rights" OR "reproductive health") AND (atleast5(abortion) OR atleast3("reproductive rights"))\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9360\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9360\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Date\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 01/01/2021 to 06/30/2026\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9360\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\c